{"parentUuid":"018ad4e3-8589-4ab3-a98a-9ccfcd1aed39","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce8b8wPaBN8XWCf4sorNW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MfTLAGWz1mQHw7MG9hjiD2","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Verify Track 1 spec grounding","subagent_type":"canon:verifier","prompt":"Verify the draft spec@1 at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track1-draft.json (id SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS, for the callisto Rust monorepo at /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto) against its source requirement@1 below. For each of the spec's 13 acceptance criteria, classify as supported (requirement/research evidence exists with direct citation), unsupported (no basis in source), or overfitted (narrower than source supports, excluding valid cases).\n\nSource requirement@1:\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"REQ-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"statement\": \"Fix three independent, confirmed-live correctness bugs in callisto's fixed-group version engine: (1) fixed-group siblings are bumped independently from their own base version instead of a shared group-aligned target, (2) a fully-implemented divergence/napi-drift pre-mutation check function is never called from any command, and (3) a declared error variant for detecting same-target-different-spelling group membership conflicts is never constructed.\",\n  \"stakeholder\": \"Callisto maintainers and any user with a fixed-group release configuration (napi-rs platform packages, monorepo packages that must always release in lockstep)\",\n  \"why\": \"All three bugs were confirmed live via direct code inspection this session, not just documentation drift. Bug 1 causes silent, permanent version divergence within a group the user explicitly configured to stay in lockstep. Bugs 2 and 3 are complete, unit-tested implementations sitting completely disconnected from any real command.\",\n  \"done_when\": [\n    \"Given a Fixed group with two Package members, one already released (has a prior tag) at version 2.0.0 and one never-released at version 0.1.0, and a cascade run that assigns both a Minor severity bump, both siblings' computed target version is the SAME group-aligned version (derived from the released sibling's tag-based version per the existing fixed_group_target function in groups.rs), not two independently-bumped versions computed from each sibling's own divergent base.\",\n    \"This holds through the real, live call path: crate::cascade::run_cascade -> raise() -> the per-sibling fixed-group loop -> bump_target, not just in a unit test of fixed_group_target called directly.\",\n    \"CascadeInput gains a `tags: &TagIndex` field since fixed_group_target requires it. Both real construction sites are updated: crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:70 and crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs:53.\",\n    \"Explicit decision, stated in the spec (not left ambiguous): whether commands/snapshot.rs's fixed-group target computation is brought into scope by this same fix or is explicitly out of scope with a stated reason.\",\n    \"crate::groups::pre_mutation_checks is called from commands/version.rs's real orchestration path, before run_cascade executes.\",\n    \"pre_mutation_checks's return value is actually consumed: diagnostics merged into real output, divergence errors actually abort the command.\",\n    \"GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership is constructed by new detection logic in GroupTable::resolve or an equivalent post-resolution check for the two-differently-spelled-groups-same-resolved-package case, and must NOT fire for the ordinary single-group-membership case.\",\n    \"Given a workspace config with no group spelling conflicts, GroupTable::resolve behaves exactly as it does today (regression: existing tests pass unmodified).\",\n    \"All three fixes are covered by tests that exercise the REAL call path, not just isolated unit tests of the already-existing helper functions.\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"Track 2 (platform-manifest / optionalDependencies writes) -- separate track, depends on this one.\",\n    \"Track 9 (cascade_action peer-escalation severity bug, dependency-spec rewrite key bug) -- separate, scoped track sharing cascade.rs.\",\n    \"Any change to fixed_group_target's or pre_mutation_checks's own internal logic/signature beyond what's needed to call them from real code.\",\n    \"GroupTable::resolve's other existing responsibilities and error paths beyond the new ConflictingGroupMembership detection.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nRead the full spec@1 JSON from the file path above for the complete acceptance criteria text (my summary of AC-001 through AC-013 topics: shared group-aligned target computed via the real call path; CascadeInput gains tags field and both construction sites updated; snapshot.rs's in-scope/out-of-scope handling explicitly decided; pre_mutation_checks wired into version.rs with diagnostics merged and divergence errors aborting; TagIndex/NapiTargetsIndex newly bound locally in plan_version; ConflictingGroupMembership detection added to GroupTable::resolve without breaking the ordinary single-membership case; regression coverage for unmodified config; real-call-path test coverage for all three bugs).\n\nNo research-report@1 exists for this spec — the requirement's done_when criteria and the drafting agent's own code-verification (noted in its report: it corrected two inaccuracies in the requirement, confirmed exact line numbers and the ConflictingGroupMembership error shape) are the only source evidence available. Output a structured evidence report with supported, unsupported, and overfitted arrays plus a reasoning scratchpad."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1278,"cache_read_input_tokens":353848,"output_tokens":2028,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1278,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2028,"cache_read_input_tokens":353848,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1278,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1278},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8b8rQvj3V55Da8iPw5r","type":"assistant","uuid":"b67bf904-e189-4183-a00d-67c7f5c82770","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:53:05.217Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
