om the released sibling's tag-based version per the existing fixed_group_target function...), not two independently-bumped versions computed from each sibling's own divergent base.'\", \"source\": \"requirement@1\" },\n    { \"criterion_id\": \"AC-002\", \"evidence\": \"done_when[1]: 'This holds through the real, live call path: crate::cascade::run_cascade -&gt; raise() -&gt; the per-sibling fixed-group loop -&gt; bump_target, not just in a unit test of fixed_group_target called directly.'\", \"source\": \"requirement@1\" },\n    { \"criterion_id\": \"AC-003\", \"evidence\": \"done_when[2]: 'CascadeInput gains a tags: &amp;TagIndex field... Both real construction sites are updated: crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:70 and crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs:53.'\", \"source\": \"requirement@1\" },\n    { \"criterion_id\": \"AC-004\", \"evidence\": \"done_when[3] requires an explicit, stated decision on whether snapshot.rs's fixed-group *target computation* is brought into scope by the same fix; combined with done_when[1]'s generic (command-agnostic) real-call-path requirement, testing that the cascade-stage fix also reaches plan_snapshot's path is the testable expression of that required decision.\", \"source\": \"requirement@1\" },\n    { \"criterion_id\": \"AC-005\", \"evidence\": \"done_when[3]'s demand that the snapshot.rs scope decision be explicit and testable ('not left ambiguous') supports asserting what does/does not change in plan_snapshot's observable output as the concrete, falsifiable form of that decision.\", \"source\": \"requirement@1\" },\n    { \"criterion_id\": \"AC-007\", \"evidence\": \"done_when[4]: 'pre_mutation_checks is called from commands/version.rs's real orchestration path, before run_cascade executes' and done_when[5]: 'divergence errors actually abort the command.'\", \"source\": \"requirement@1\" },\n    { \"criterion_id\": \"AC-008\", \"evidence\": \"done_when[5]: 'pre_mutation_checks's return value is actually