aim\": \"Requires plan_version to construct the TagIndex 'via a newly-bound local variable, distinct from the existing inline, unbound ws.tags()? call passed directly as an argument to aggregate()' and a NapiTargetsIndex via a specific construction pattern — i.e., it tests a particular implementation shape (variable-binding structure), not just an outcome.\",\n      \"source_scope\": \"done_when[4] only requires that pre_mutation_checks be called from the real orchestration path with the correct inputs before run_cascade; it says nothing about how those inputs must be bound (new local vs. inline expression). AC-009 excludes valid implementations that satisfy the requirement's actual behavioral demand without introducing a distinctly-named local binding.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"reasoning\": \"Nine of thirteen criteria trace cleanly to specific done_when items (AC-001/002/003/007/008/010/011/012/013), each with essentially a paraphrase-level match to a single done_when bullet — high confidence supported. AC-004 and AC-005 required more inference: they test the *consequences* of the explicit snapshot.rs-scope decision that done_when[3] mandates be made and stated, rather than restating a done_when bullet directly, but done_when[3]'s own language ('not left ambiguous') implies the decision must be testable, which is exactly what AC-004/AC-005 operationalize — I judged this close enough to direct citation rather than inferred plausibility. AC-006 is flagged unsupported primarily because its literal text is self-contradictory against both the requirement and the rest of the spec, not merely under-cited; I did not attempt to silently 'fix' the apparent typo and grade the corrected version, since the instructions say to evaluate the criterion as it stands. AC-009 is the clearest case of overfitting: the underlying need (correct TagIndex/NapiTargetsIndex supplied to pre_mutation_checks) is grounded, but the criterion bakes in an implementation-structural constraint (distinct newly-bound local variable) that the requirement never specifies and that would fail a functionally-correct alternative implementation. No criterion was found to have zero plausible connection to any done_when item — the unsupported/overfitted findings are about missing or contradictory citation and over-narrow implementation-detail testing, not about criteria invented from nothing.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>45344</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>1</tool_uses><duration_ms>105646</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"c8f5cd3b-332a-4d08-bd09-a858d1d35fe2","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:54:59.565Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
