{"parentUuid":"d301f8ff-feda-452e-bbc7-fddd6c946638","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"34c76b23-b9a9-48c0-b471-5ab1f3b9cb2d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NRAQyRTUeyU35owsnbgw5A","type":"tool_result","content":"api_surface keys: <class 'list'>\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CascadeInput.tags\",\n    \"signature\": \"pub tags: &'a TagIndex\",\n    \"description\": \"New field added to the CascadeInput struct (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs, currently 8 fields: graph, groups, cfg, seed, reasons, named_by, base, pre \\u2014 none named tags). Required so that raise()'s per-sibling fixed-group loop can call fixed_group_target(sib, tags, ...) instead of calling bump_target independently on each sibling. Both real construction sites must supply it: commands/version.rs:70 (plan_version) and commands/snapshot.rs:53 (plan_snapshot). TagIndex is defined in crates/callisto-graph/src/tags.rs and exposes last_tag(&self, id: &PackageId) -> Option<&LastTag> and an empty() constructor for tests.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cascade::raise (internal, per-sibling fixed-group loop)\",\n    \"signature\": \"fn raise<D: DependencyResolver>(input: &CascadeInput<D>, ...) -> ... (signature unchanged; internal logic changes only)\",\n    \"description\": \"The fixed-group loop at lines 464-478 currently computes each sibling's target by calling bump_target(sib, sev, input) directly against that sibling's own base version. This spec changes that loop to compute the shared group-aligned target once (via crate::groups::fixed_group_target, using input.tags) and assign that same target to every sibling in the group, instead of bumping each sibling independently. raise() is shared by both run_cascade call paths (version.rs and snapshot.rs via solve_cascade), so this fix applies to both commands mechanically \\u2014 see AC-004/AC-005.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"commands::version::plan_version (internal orchestration change; external signature unchanged)\",\n    \"signature\": \"pub fn plan_version(...) -> Result<VersionPlan, GraphError>\",\n    \"description\": \"External signature and return type are unchanged. Internally, plan_version gains: (a) a local `tags` binding capturing the TagIndex currently only produced inline as an unbound argument to aggregate() at line 43 (e.g. `let ta","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6190b4a5-ab98-459c-80b3-1eb30a50a0d1","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:01:40.805Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"api_surface keys: <class 'list'>\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CascadeInput.tags\",\n    \"signature\": \"pub tags: &'a TagIndex\",\n    \"description\": \"New field added to the CascadeInput struct (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs, currently 8 fields: graph, groups, cfg, seed, reasons, named_by, base, pre \\u2014 none named tags). Required so that raise()'s per-sibling fixed-group loop can call fixed_group_target(sib, tags, ...) instead of calling bump_target independently on each sibling. Both real construction sites must supply it: commands/version.rs:70 (plan_version) and commands/snapshot.rs:53 (plan_snapshot). TagIndex is defined in crates/callisto-graph/src/tags.rs and exposes last_tag(&self, id: &PackageId) -> Option<&LastTag> and an empty() constructor for tests.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cascade::raise (internal, per-sibling fixed-group loop)\",\n    \"signature\": \"fn raise<D: DependencyResolver>(input: &CascadeInput<D>, ...) -> ... (signature unchanged; internal logic changes only)\",\n    \"description\": \"The fixed-group loop at lines 464-478 currently computes each sibling's target by calling bump_target(sib, sev, input) directly against that sibling's own base version. This spec changes that loop to compute the shared group-aligned target once (via crate::groups::fixed_group_target, using input.tags) and assign that same target to every sibling in the group, instead of bumping each sibling independently. raise() is shared by both run_cascade call paths (version.rs and snapshot.rs v