{"parentUuid":"9a6df802-b131-46ae-a117-c6ab1ad012a6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce8ckZzaJwzYtx4tJzevw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Structure looks intact. Now re-running verify → audit → exit-gate on the corrected spec."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":821,"cache_read_input_tokens":388429,"output_tokens":1736,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":821,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1736,"cache_read_input_tokens":388429,"cache_creation_input_tokens":821,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":821},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8ckUdN4xSNXEi2VJton","type":"assistant","uuid":"c7594fe2-1daa-48da-901a-cc03f0c823d2","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:13:59.087Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"c7594fe2-1daa-48da-901a-cc03f0c823d2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce8ckZzaJwzYtx4tJzevw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Yb4bfdTWR4PoHsPunpdcJJ","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Re-verify Track 1 spec after redraft","subagent_type":"canon:verifier","prompt":"Verify the revised spec@1 at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track1-draft.json (id SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS, callisto Rust monorepo at /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto) against its source requirement@1 below. This is a re-verification after a substantial redraft — the spec was fully rewritten in response to a canon-exit-gate FAIL that found 7 blockers, most critically that bug 1's fix was originally scoped to the wrong function (raise()'s sibling loop, which cannot fire for the seeded-severity scenario the requirement describes) and has now been rescoped to a NEW Fixed-group convergence block inside solve_cascade, mirroring an existing Linked-group block at cascade.rs:314-379. Read the spec's own `revision_note` field for the full list of what changed.\n\nFor each of the spec's 16 acceptance criteria, classify as supported, unsupported, or overfitted against the source requirement.\n\nSource requirement@1:\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"REQ-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"statement\": \"Fix three independent, confirmed-live correctness bugs in callisto's fixed-group version engine: (1) fixed-group siblings are bumped independently from their own base version instead of a shared group-aligned target, (2) a fully-implemented divergence/napi-drift pre-mutation check function is never called from any command, and (3) a declared error variant for detecting same-target-different-spelling group membership conflicts is never constructed.\",\n  \"stakeholder\": \"Callisto maintainers and any user with a fixed-group release configuration\",\n  \"why\": \"All three bugs were confirmed live via direct code inspection. Bug 1 causes silent, permanent version divergence within a group the user explicitly configured to stay in lockstep. Bugs 2 and 3 are complete, unit-tested implementations sitting completely disconnected from any real command.\",\n  \"done_when\": [\n    \"Given a Fixed group with two Package members, one already released (has a prior tag) at version 2.0.0 and one never-released at version 0.1.0, and a cascade run that assigns both a Minor severity bump, both siblings' computed target version is the SAME group-aligned version (derived from the released sibling's base version per the existing fixed_group_target function in groups.rs), not two independently-bumped versions computed from each sibling's own divergent base.\",\n    \"This holds through the real, live cascade call path (crate::cascade::run_cascade / solve_cascade), not just in a unit test of fixed_group_target called directly.\",\n    \"CascadeInput gains a tags: &TagIndex field. Both real construction sites are updated: commands/version.rs:70 and commands/snapshot.rs:53.\",\n    \"Explicit decision, stated in the spec: whether commands/snapshot.rs's fixed-group target computation is brought into scope by this same fix or is explicitly out of scope with a stated reason.\",\n    \"crate::groups::pre_mutation_checks is called from commands/version.rs's real orchestration path, before run_cascade executes.\",\n    \"pre_mutation_checks's return value is actually consumed: diagnostics merged into real output, divergence errors actually abort the command.\",\n    \"GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership is constructed by new detection logic in GroupTable::resolve for the two-differently-spelled-groups-same-resolved-package case, and must NOT fire for the ordinary single-group-membership case.\",\n    \"Given a workspace config with no group spelling conflicts, GroupTable::resolve behaves exactly as it does today (regression: existing tests pass unmodified).\",\n    \"All three fixes are covered by tests that exercise the REAL call path, not just isolated unit tests of the already-existing helper functions.\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"Track 2 (platform-manifest / optionalDependencies writes).\",\n    \"Track 9 (cascade_action peer-escalation severity bug, dependency-spec rewrite key bug).\",\n    \"Any change to fixed_group_target's or pre_mutation_checks's own internal logic/signature beyond what's needed to call them from real code.\",\n    \"GroupTable::resolve's other existing responsibilities and error paths beyond the new ConflictingGroupMembership detection.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nRead the full spec@1 JSON from disk for complete acceptance criteria text. Output a structured evidence report with supported, unsupported, and overfitted arrays plus a reasoning scratchpad."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":821,"cache_read_input_tokens":388429,"output_tokens":1736,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":821,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1736,"cache_read_input_tokens":388429,"cache_creation_input_tokens":821,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":821},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8ckUdN4xSNXEi2VJton","type":"assistant","uuid":"f86208ab-b206-4403-b99c-e460ee14698e","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:14:12.174Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slu