{"parentUuid":"8cbac767-4fc9-4fcf-bf2e-59df393605af","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce8e7yrUST8BuZ2m4ZrhZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Quick status check-in:\n\n**Track 3a & 3b1**: fully complete and committed. Clean baseline confirmed (`just ci` passes).\n\n**Track 2**: confirmed to be only ~20% done (consumption wired, planning logic never built, two dormant bugs found by audit). You chose to fix Track 1 first since Track 2 depends on it.\n\n**Track 1** (fixed-group cascade correctness — currently in progress): this has been a genuinely rigorous back-and-forth —\n1. Drafted the spec, verified, audited, fixed 7 issues from those two passes.\n2. First exit-gate attempt **failed** — it caught something important: the spec had targeted the wrong function for bug 1's fix entirely. The real fix needed a new Fixed-group convergence block inside `solve_cascade` (mirroring an existing Linked-group block), not a tweak to `raise()`'s sibling loop, plus 6 smaller issues.\n3. Redrafted addressing all 7 blockers.\n4. Re-verified — surfaced a legitimate tension worth double-checking (whether one new criterion, a member-dedup requirement, is real scope creep or a necessary correctness precondition for the other criteria).\n5. **Currently running**: re-audit, explicitly weighing that tension against the actual code before rendering a verdict.\n\nOnce the audit comes back, next is the exit-gate again, then (assuming pass) writing the spec to disk, committing it, and moving to vector-planner for the implementation plan. I'll report back with the audit result shortly."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":80,"cache_read_input_tokens":400454,"output_tokens":545,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":30},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ep