{"parentUuid":"4c7f12e8-c93c-4b0c-acf6-10d0710e1b05","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"daa78fe3-695a-438e-aed6-d41775edc067","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UM8mR8n1L1JXbTuMrqPvFX","type":"tool_result","content":"=== keys ===\n['id', 'purpose', 'scope', 'non_goals', 'api_surface', 'acceptance_criteria', 'linked_requirement', 'revision_note', 'reasoning']\n\n=== reasoning (if present) ===\nRead cascade.rs's full solve_cascade, bump_target, and raise() functions plus groups.rs's fixed_group_target and pre_mutation_checks, config/groups.rs's resolve(), and commands/version.rs and commands/snapshot.rs in full before making any edit, per the correction instructions. Confirmed every line number and signature cited in the blocker list against the live source rather than trusting the paraphrase. Key structural decision: rather than inventing a new free function, the Fixed-group fix is expressed as a second block inside solve_cascade's existing `while changed` fixpoint loop, exactly mirroring the pattern already proven correct for Linked groups at lines 314-379 -- this keeps the fix minimal, keeps it participating in the same convergence/worklist machinery, and naturally supersedes raise()'s independent per-sibling bump_target calls without requiring raise() itself to change (since the new block re-reads and overwrites out.targets from the shared fixed_group_target result on every outer-loop pass, regardless of how a member's severity got there). Chose to add explicit non_goals for both the raise()-loop-left-unmodified point and the fixed_group_target SemVer/PEP440 gap rather than silently omitting them, since the correction instructions and this spec's own judgment standard require every known-but-unaddressed gap to be stated rather than glossed. For AC-010c's dedup fix, chose `Vec::dedup()` (which only removes consecutive duplicates) specifically because it composes correctly with the pre-existing `.sort()` immediately before it -- GroupMember's derived Ord sorts by resolved PackageId first for Package variants, so two different spellings of the same PackageId become adjacent after sort and are then correctly collapsed by dedup, without needing a new data structure or a full refactor of resolve()'s member-collection logic.\n=== cascade_tests.rs CascadeInput sites ===\n48:    let input = CascadeInput {\n141:    let input = CascadeInput {\n196:    let input = CascadeInput {\n258:    let input = CascadeInput {\n324:    let input = CascadeInput {\n411:    let input = CascadeInput {","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"84837d07-d5dd-4e1d-a95c-e906aa616560","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:46:37.534Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== keys ===\n['id', 'purpose', 'scope', 'non_goals', 'api_surface', 'acceptance_criteria', 'linked_requirement', 'revision_note', 'reasoning']\n\n=== reasoning (if present) ===\nRead cascade.rs's full solve_cascade, bump_target, and raise() functions plus groups.rs's fixed_group_target and pre_mutation_checks, config/groups.rs's resolve(), and commands/version.rs and commands/snapshot.rs in full before making any edit, per the correction instructions. Confirmed every line number and signature cited in the blocker list against the live source rather than trusting the paraphrase. Key structural decision: rather than inventing a new free function, the Fixed-group fix is expressed as a second block inside solve_cascade's existing `while changed` fixpoint loop, exactly mirroring the pattern already proven correct for Linked groups at lines 314-379 -- this keeps the fix minimal, keeps it participating in the same convergence/worklist machinery, and naturally supersedes raise()'s independent per-sibling bump_target calls without requiring raise() itself to change (since the new block re-reads and overwrites out.targets from the shared fixed_group_target result on every outer-loop pass, regardless of how a member's severity got there). Chose to add explicit non_goals for both the raise()-loop-left-unmodified point and the fixed_group_target SemVer/PEP440 gap rather than silently omitting them, since the correction instructions and this spec's own judgment standard require every known-but-unaddressed gap to be stated rather than glossed. For AC-010c's dedup fix, chose `Vec::dedup()` (which only removes consecutive duplicates) specifically because it composes correctly with the pre-existing `.sort()` immediately before it -- GroupMember's derived Ord sorts by resolved PackageId first for Package variants, so two different spellings of the same PackageId become adjacent after sort and are then correctly collapsed by dedup, without needing a new data structure or a full refactor of resolve()'s member-collection logic.\n=== cascade_tests.rs CascadeInput sites ===\n48:    let input = CascadeInput {\n141:    let input = CascadeInput {\n196:    let input = CascadeInput {\n258:    let input = CascadeInput {\n324:    let input = CascadeInput {\n411:    let input = CascadeInput {","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4c7f12e8-c93c-4b0c-acf6-10d0710e1b05","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
