ming no red phase was possible or expected (implementation already existed). No production code was touched, matching the plan's explicit \"no production code changes\" step.\n\nRan `cargo fmt -p callisto-graph`, `cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings` (clean), and the full `cargo test -p callisto-graph` suite (all passing, no regressions) before committing.\n\nCommit: `88755f1` — \"test(graph): pin AC-007 grammar-mismatch fixed-group divergence via plan_version\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"T07\",\n  \"status\": \"done\",\n  \"steps_completed\": [\n    \"Read AC-007 from spec file on disk\",\n    \"Added sibling test to existing mod tests block in version.rs\",\n    \"Ran test once to confirm fixture correctness (passed immediately, confirming pre-existing implementation coverage, not a red-phase violation)\",\n    \"Confirmed no production code changes needed per task instructions\",\n    \"Ran cargo fmt -p callisto-graph\",\n    \"Ran cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings (clean)\",\n    \"Ran full cargo test -p callisto-graph suite (all green)\",\n    \"Committed\"\n  ],\n  \"test_result\": \"pass\",\n  \"commit_sha\": \"88755f1\",\n  \"concerns\": \"This task was a regression-pin for already-implemented logic (per T06 wiring pre_mutation_checks into plan_version), so no red phase was observed for new implementation code — the test passed on first run as the plan itself predicted. This matches the task's explicit instructions and was verified empirically rather than assumed.\",\n  \"criteria_evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-007\",\n      \"test_file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n      \"test_line\": 399,\n      \"implementation_file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs\",\n      \"implementation_line\": 67\n    }\n  ],\n  \"reasoning\": \"AC-007 covers both divergence sub-cases; T06 already proved the values-divergence branch. This task proves the grammar-mismatch branch specifically, via the real plan_version call path (wired at version.rs:84 -&gt; groups::pre_mutation_checks -&gt; groups.rs:67 GroupGrammarMismatch).\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>55099</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>20</tool_uses><duration_ms>379284</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
