{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:21:43.820Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a8e3e0fd1fc8512f6</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a8e3e0fd1fc8512f6.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Exit-gate Track 2 spec (retry 3)\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result># Verdict: PASS (retry_count 3, confidence high)\n\nVerdict written to `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/verdict-track2-retry3.json` (schema-valid, zero blockers).\n\n**No escalation needed.** The spec is cleared for planning.\n\n## The three retry-2 fixes — all genuinely landed\n\nI verified each against live code rather than the summary:\n\n1. **AC-002b now asserts at the public entry point.** It requires `plan_version` to return `Ok(..)` with `PlatformWrite.from == \"3.2.1\"`. The behavior is confirmed achievable, not speculative — `cargo.rs:178-189` returns `Ok(inherited version)` when inheritance is present and only falls through to `Err(WorkspaceInherited)` when it is absent, and an **existing test at `cargo.rs:1749-1779` already proves exactly this shape** (asserts `current_version() == \"4.5.6\"` with a resolver supplied).\n2. **AC-002's headline is now literally true** for both the direct-declaration and workspace-inherited cases. The prior false universal is gone.\n3. **AC-002b's path is corrected and both line ranges are exact** — `crates/callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs:47-52` is precisely the `inherited_version` detection; `580-587` is precisely the version resolution inside `inheritance()`.\n\n## The cross-check that mattered most\n\nAC-002 and AC-002b are not merely non-contradictory — they are **jointly load-bearing**. `cargo.rs:80-87` hard-errors on open when `uses_inheritance &amp;&amp; ctx.cargo_workspace.is_none()`. Without AC-002's mandated `OpenContext` derivation, AC-002b's maturin scenario would fail at open. And AC-002's unconditional `ManifestRole::Canonical` is required because `package.rs:104-106` rejects `Platform` role + `CargoToml` format. Both anchors verified verbatim.\n\n## Retry-1 blockers 1-4 — no regression\n\nI re-read the retry-1 verdict from disk and checked each against current text. All four remain resolved: the false npm-refresh claim (confirmed — `apply.rs:354-408` has only Cargo and Pypi branches, no Npm), the `ManifestDecl::new`-vs-`open` conflation, AC-005's unobservable per-group scoping, and AC-011's assertion on function-local `active_ecosystems` (now on `ApplyOutcome.staged`, confirmed public and assigned at `apply.rs:469`).\n\nAll four gate conditions hold: 16 testable criteria, zero TBDs (the sole \"TBD\" string is the phrase \"No TBDs remain\" in the private reasoning field), error cases AC-008 and AC-012 correctly flagged `is_error_case: true` with AC-012b correctly flagged `false` as a success path, and scope confined to one cycle behind seven non-goals.\n\n## One non-gating observation to relay\n\nThe `purpose` field opens *\"Make callisto-cli's plan_version()...\"* — but `plan_version` is defined only at `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:22`; callisto-cli merely calls it at `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/version.rs:25`.\n\nI deliberately did **not** gate on this, and want to be explicit about why rather than bury it: it sits in framing prose, touches none of the four pass conditions, and every actionable pointer — the `scope` field, both `api_surface` entries, and all 16 criteria — correctly names `callisto-graph`. A developer implements from scope and the criteria, which answer \"which crate\" unambiguously three separate ways. Forcing a fourth cycle and a human escalation over a noun in a summary sentence, while all sixteen criteria and every file/line reference verify clean, would be gate theater. Worth a one-word cleanup on any future touch.\n\nThis is a genuine pass — no condition was relaxed and no criterion was waved through as close enough.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>70183</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>26</tool_uses><duration_ms>318974</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
