{"parentUuid":"fecf8b39-6550-47e3-bca9-8e94859b08c8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce92MLRuJXcbSBXghkSYx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017p2JhZh96DonfZGiAmdHcf","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Plan Track 2 implementation","subagent_type":"vector:planner","prompt":"Produce a plan@1 for the spec at .claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json (workspace root /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto, read spec_file_path from disk — it's already set correctly in the file). This spec passed canon-exit-gate on its 3rd attempt after unusually heavy adversarial review; it is precisely grounded in the actual current code (exact line numbers, function signatures, and call sites were independently re-verified multiple times) — trust its api_surface section's mechanism descriptions as accurate, but still verify against the live code yourself before writing each task's failing test, since specs and code can still drift.\n\nKey implementation shape from the spec's api_surface (for your own orientation, not a substitute for reading the spec/code yourself): (1) PlatformWrite gains a `from: Version` field (crates/callisto-graph/src/plan.rs) — a breaking change to any code constructing it directly; (2) commands::version::plan_version (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs) becomes the real producer of VersionPlan.platform_writes/optional_dep_updates for Fixed groups with GroupMember::PlatformManifest members — reads each platform manifest's current version via callisto_manifests::open with an OpenContext derived the same way apply_version_plan already derives it (crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs:118-130), uses ManifestRole::Canonical unconditionally regardless of the GroupMember's own role field; (3) apply::apply_version_plan (crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs) gets two fixes: Fix 1 extends active_ecosystems (currently derived only from plan.bumps, apply.rs:325-349) to also derive from platform_writes/optional_dep_updates manifest paths so npm lockfile staging (not refresh — npm has none) works when a plan contains only these two fields; Fix 2 adds a precondition check to the platform_writes dispatch loop (apply.rs:244-252) mirroring the sibling bump loops' current==from/current==target/else three-way branch, using the new `from` field, returning GraphError::UnexpectedManifestVersion on drift but treating current==target as an idempotent-retry success (not an error).\n\nSequence tasks by dependency: PlatformWrite's `from` field addition (and its call-site fixups, including apply.rs's existing dispatch loop and any test fixtures) must land before Fix 2 can be built on top of it; the plan_version producer logic and the apply.rs Fix 1/Fix 2 fixes are otherwise fairly independent of each other (different files) and can be sequenced in either order relative to each other, though Fix 2 depends on the `from` field existing. No task should exceed 15 minutes for a competent developer — this will likely mean the field addition is its own task, the OpenContext/ManifestRole::Canonical read-and-populate logic in plan_version is split from the optionalDependencies detection logic, and apply.rs's two fixes are separate tasks. Every acceptance criterion in the spec (16 total: AC-001 through AC-013 plus AC-002b, AC-007b, AC-012b) must appear in at least one task's covers_criteria.\n\nOutput the plan@1 to your own returned object (the calling process will persist it to .claude/plans/ and pass it through vector-challenger before implementation begins)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1076,"cache_read_input_tokens":620997,"output_tokens":1266,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1076,"ephemeral_