{"parentUuid":"078c6b0d-dc69-43c3-9a01-80cbe4f39479","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce93Lju8Br2nQmcnfqLLX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VqCv4K1e5hB4kyMa5NWxRi","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans/ACTIVE.md","old_string":"Exit-gate: PASS. Full `cargo test -p callisto-graph` suite green (361+ tests). Mutation testing (cargo-mutants, scoped to the 4 touched files, 105 mutants) completed after the exit-gate: 41 caught, 56 missed/timed-out. Nearly all survivors are in pre-existing, untouched decision logic outside this track's scope (`cascade_action`, `caret_covers`, `coverage()` in `cascade.rs`, `GroupTable::validate_syntactic` in `config/groups.rs` — none touched by any Track 1 task) — a genuine, long-standing coverage gap, not something this track introduced. The one survivor genuinely inside Track 1's new code (the Fixed-group convergence block's idempotency guard, `cascade.rs:404/407`) exactly mirrors a pre-existing, already-accepted gap in the Linked-group block it deliberately copies (`cascade.rs:333/336`) — consistent with, not worse than, the existing pattern. 25 precision tests were specified by the mutator; deferred as backlog (see Track 11/12-adjacent follow-up), not blocking, since fixing the pre-existing gaps is out of this track's scope and the one in-scope gap matches accepted precedent.","new_string":"Exit-gate: PASS (correction below supersedes an earlier premature reading of the same run). Full workspace suite green: 975 tests across 54 suites, clippy/fmt/doc/wasm all clean. Mutation testing (cargo-mutants, scoped to the 4 touched files, 113 mutants) ran to full completion: 42 caught, 32 timeout, 10 unviable, 28 survivors — **zero survivors in Track 1's own new/touched code**. All 28 survivors are in pre-existing, untouched decision logic (`cascade_action`, `caret_covers`, `coverage()` in `cascade.rs`, plus pre-existing `solve_cascade` regions) — a genuine, long-standing coverage gap predating this track, not introduced by it. Verified non-vacuous: 8 mutants were generated inside the new Fixed-group convergence block (lines 384-434) and all 8 were caught — notably, the exact structural analogues of two of those mutants in the pre-existing Linked-group block (`cascade.rs:333/336`) *did* survive, while the new mirrored guards (`404/407`) did not, meaning the new tests are strictly stronger than the code they were modeled on. (An earlier note in this entry, based on a mid-run snapshot before cargo-mutants finished, mischaracterized this as one in-scope survivor — corrected here.) 25 precision tests targeting the pre-existing survivors were specified by the mutator; deferred as backlog, out of this track's scope."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2036,"cache_read_input_tokens":667343,"output_tokens":1076,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2036,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1076,"cache_read_input_tokens":667343,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2036,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2036},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce93LfwztFmErKWuFVTb5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b39b4364-acbb-4975-bb05-24cfafc2d9a7","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:36:33.381Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
