{"parentUuid":"c9b0e4b5-90c8-479d-9e91-2b128a2f371d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans/PLAN-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json","snippet":"1\t{\n2\t  \"schema\": \"plan@1\",\n3\t  \"id\": \"PLAN-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES\",\n4\t  \"spec_file_path\": \".claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json\",\n5\t  \"spec_hash\": \"sha256:a8d8b1914557f3af4197f9cfa39333cf6303215d2d28ef4c4a0b092eb6f0785e\",\n6\t  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES\",\n7\t  \"reasoning\": \"Verified live code before decomposing: PlatformWrite/OptionalDepUpdate are 2-field structs at plan.rs:45-55; plan_version hardcodes both to Vec::new() at version.rs:262-263; apply.rs's platform_writes loop (244-252) has no precondition and active_ecosystems (325-349) only reads plan.bumps. GroupMember::PlatformManifest{owner,role,path,name} lives at config/groups.rs:26-33 and is only populated via IdentityIndex.platform, itself populated in walk.rs:190-216 by detecting npm package.json files with non-empty os+cpu arrays (detect_npm_role, walk.rs:590+) during the walk -- so a realistic test fixture for a Fixed group with a PlatformManifest member is: an owner Cargo crate + a sibling npm package.json declaring os/cpu arrays, referenced by its own npm name in [[fixed-group]] members. Manifest reads go through callisto_manifests::open(&ManifestDecl::new(path, ManifestRole::Canonical, fmt), &OpenContext) exactly as apply.rs already does at 118-136/244-262 -- OpenContext derivation is duplicated verbatim into plan_version rather than extracted into a shared helper, since the spec's api_surface explicitly describes plan_version deriving it itself and extracting a helper is an unrequested refactor. AC-008's 'manifest doesn't exist / can't be parsed' is only reachable at plan_version's read time (not at walk/group-resolution time, since IdentityIndex only ever registers manifests that walked successfully) -- so its test loads a valid workspace first, then removes the platform manifest from disk before calling plan_version, exercising the same code path a real deleted-file race would hit. Tasks are ordered so PlatformWrite's `from` field (Task 1) lands before apply.rs's Fix 2 precondition (Task 8), which is the only cross-file ordering constraint the spec's api_surface calls out; the two commands/version.rs producer sub-features (platform_writes in Tasks 2-4, optional_dep_updates in Tasks 5-6) and the two apply.rs fixes (Tasks 7-8) are otherwise independent of each other by file. Every task's covers_criteria was cross-checked against all 16 IDs (AC-001..AC-013 + AC-002b, AC-007b, AC-012b) at the end -- all 16 present.\",\n8\t  \"tasks\": [\n9\t    {\n10\t      \"id\": \"TASK-1\",\n11\t      \"title\": \"Add `from: Version` field to PlatformWrite\",\n12\t      \"depends_on\": [],\n13\t      \"files\": [\n14\t        \"crates/callisto-graph/src/plan.rs\",\n15\t        \"crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs\"\n16\t      ],\n17\t      \"reasoning\": \"PlatformWrite is currently a 2-field struct (manifest, version) at plan.rs:45-49. This is a breaking type change that every other task in this plan (Task 2's producer, Task 8's precondition check) depends on. The one existing call site that constructs PlatformWrite directly is the test at apply.rs:2260 (apply_version_plan_executes_platform_writes_and_optional_dep_updates) -- it will fail to compile once the field is added, so it must be fixed in this same task to keep the crate compiling.\",\n18\t      \"test\": {\n19\t        \"description\": \"New unit test in plan.rs asserting PlatformWrite has a `from` field. This test does not compile against the current 2-field struct, which is the required RED state for a struct-field addition.\",\n20\t        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/plan.rs\",\n21\t        \"code\": \"#[cfg(test)]\\nmod platform_write_from_field_tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n    use callisto_model::VersionGrammar;\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn platform_write_carries_from_field_distinct_from_version() {\\n        let pw = PlatformWrite {\\n            manifest: PathBuf::from(\\\"platform/package.json\\\"),\\n            version: Version::parse(\\\"1.1.0\\\", VersionGrammar::SemVer).unwrap(),\\n            from: Version::parse(\\\"1.0.0\\\", VersionGrammar::SemVer).unwrap(),\\n        };\\n        assert_eq!(pw.from.render(), \\\"1.0.0\\\");\\n        assert_eq!(pw.version.render(), \\\"1.1.0\\\");\\n    }\\n}\",\n22\t        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib plan::platform_write_from_field_tests\",\n23\t        \"expected_failure\": \"error[E0560] or E0609: struct `PlatformWrite` has no field named `from` -- compile error, crate fails to build\"\n24\t      },\n25\t      \"implementation\": {\n26\t        \"description\": \"Add the `from` field to PlatformWrite, then fix the one pre-existing direct constructor at apply.rs:2260 so the crate compiles.\",\n27\t        \"steps\": [\n28\t          \"In crates/callisto-graph/src/plan.rs, change `pub struct PlatformWrite { pub manifest: PathBuf, pub version: Version }` to `pub struct PlatformWrite { pub manifest: PathBuf, pub version: Version, pub from: Version }`.\",\n29\t          \"In crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs, in the test `apply_version_plan_executes_platform_writes_and_optional_dep_updates` (around line 2260), change the `PlatformWrite` literal from `crate::plan::PlatformWrite { manifest: PathBuf::from(\\\"platform/package.json\\\"), version: cargo_version(\\\"1.1.0\\\") }` to `crate::plan::PlatformWrite { manifest: PathBuf::from(\\\"platform/package.json\\\"), version: cargo_version(\\\"1.1.0\\\"), from: cargo_version(\\\"1.0.0\\\") }` -- 1.0.0 matches the fixture's on-disk platform/package.json version, so this remains the non-drifted, non-precondition-failing case.\"\n30\t        ]\n31\t      },\n32\t      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n33\t      \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass, including plan::platform_write_from_field_tests::platform_write_carries_from_field_distinct_from_version and apply::tests::apply_version_plan_executes_platform_writes_and_optional_dep_updates\",\n34\t      \"commit_message\": \"feat(graph): add `from` field to PlatformWrite\\n\\nCaptures the platform manifest's on-disk version at plan time so apply_version_plan can precondition-check it before writing, mirroring PlannedBump.from's role in the sibling bump loops.\",\n35\t      \"covers_criteria\": []\n36\t    },\n37\t    {\n38\t      \"id\": \"TASK-2\",\n39\t      \"title\": \"plan_version: OpenContext derivation + core platform_writes producer (single platform member, happy path)\",\n40\t      \"depends_on\": [\n41\t        \"TASK-1\"\n42\t      ],\n43\t      \"files\": [\n44\t        \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\"\n45\t      ],\n46\t      \"reasoning\": \"This is the core producer logic: for each Fixed group's GroupMember::PlatformManifest whose owner received a real PlannedBump this run, open the platform manifest (ManifestRole::Canonical unconditionally, OpenContext derived exactly as apply.rs:118-130 does) and emit a PlatformWrite with from=on-disk current_version, version=owner's bump target. Also covers the two 'no write should happen' regressions (AC-005: no platform members anywhere; AC-006: owner not bumped) since they exercise the same new code path with zero/no-match inputs and share the test fixture helpers already in this file's `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` (git_init_with_commit, tag, commit_all).\",\n47\t      \"test\": {\n48\t        \"description\": \"Three tests added to commands/version.rs's existing test module, reusing its git_init_with_commit/tag/commit_all helpers. Platform manifest fixtures use a Cargo owner package plus a sibling npm package.json with non-empty os/cpu arrays (the only mechanism, per walk.rs:590-630, that causes IdentityIndex to register a GroupMember::PlatformManifest), referenced in [[fixed-group]] members by its own npm package name.\",\n49\t        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n50\t        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_emits_platform_write_for_bumped_owner_with_platform_sibling commands::version::tests::plan_version_platform_writes_empty_when_no_platform_members_exist commands::version::tests::plan_version_no_platform_write_when_owner_not_bumped\",\n\n... [255 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d9435741-0cae-4ca4-a990-be3577adfd1f","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:39:32.649Z","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
