{"parentUuid":"974728aa-ecc1-4c4c-935b-d88d3e84e021","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce95DGU9yR2dh4UznffYP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ssk455DhhEJx6nchcAJHAG","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Correct Track 2 spec AC-002b contradiction (retry)","subagent_type":"canon:drafter","prompt":"Run canon/correct (correction mode) on the spec at .claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json (workspace root /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto, spec_file_path already set correctly in the file). Do the correction work yourself in this invocation and return the full corrected spec@1 JSON object as your final output — do not describe a plan to do it or delegate further.\n\nA lambda-implementer working task TASK-3 (from /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans/PLAN-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json) reported a confirmed contradiction between criterion AC-002b and observed system behavior:\n\n**criterion_id**: AC-002b\n\n**spec_claim**: AC-002b requires that a maturin-style platform manifest (a Cargo.toml with `version.workspace = true`) can be declared as a `GroupMember::PlatformManifest` sibling of a Fixed-group owner (the same real-workspace-discovery pattern as AC-001's npm case), such that calling `plan_version` through its real, disk-discovered call path resolves the workspace-inherited version and emits a `PlatformWrite` with `from` equal to that resolved version.\n\n**observed_behavior**: `crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs:199` — the ONLY code site that registers a manifest into `IdentityIndex.platform` (which is what causes `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs`'s `resolve()` to classify a config member as `GroupMember::PlatformManifest` rather than an ordinary `GroupMember::Package`) is gated by `if *eco == Ecosystem::Npm`, with no equivalent branch for `Ecosystem::Cargo`. I independently verified this by reading walk.rs:185-221 myself. The implementer also empirically verified it with a real workspace fixture through the real `Workspace::load` -> `plan_version` pipeline: a Cargo.toml platform sibling with `version.workspace = true` resolved as an ordinary `GroupMember::Package`, not `GroupMember::PlatformManifest`, producing its own independent `PlannedBump` and leaving `plan.platform_writes` empty. No Cargo-format manifest can currently become a `GroupMember::PlatformManifest` through the real discovery pipeline. The spec's own non_goals item 6 assumes \"group config already passed that validation\" (i.e., that discovery correctly produces PlatformManifest members) — but for the Cargo ecosystem, it doesn't; that assumption is false for this specific case.\n\nSibling criterion AC-007 (npm multi-sibling platform writes) is unaffected and fully satisfiable today with zero new implementation — TASK-2's already-landed code (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:264-302) already loops over every PlatformManifest member and handles this correctly.\n\n**Your correction task**: revise AC-002b (and any other criterion/non_goals/api_surface text that assumes Cargo-format platform-manifest discovery already works) to be honest about current system capability, in one of two ways -- pick whichever is more appropriate and state your reasoning:\n\n(a) Narrow AC-002b to explicitly scope it to the OpenContext/cargo_workspace-inheritance-handling CODE that TASK-2 already correctly implements (i.e., IF a Cargo-format manifest were ever classified as a PlatformManifest member, the OpenContext derivation would correctly resolve its workspace-inherited version) — proven via a more targeted test that doesn't require the full real-discovery pipeline to already support Cargo platform manifests, OR\n\n(b) Convert AC-002b into an explicit non_goal, stating clearly that Cargo/maturin-format platform-manifest DISCOVERY (extending walk.rs's Ecosystem::Npm-gated detection to also handle Ecosystem::Cargo) is a separate, out-of-scope feature this track does not build, and that this track's OpenContext/ManifestRole::Canonical machinery is written generically (format-agnostic) so it will work correctly once that separate discovery feature ships -- but proving that end-to-end is deferred to whichever future track adds Cargo platform-manifest discovery.\n\nRead the full current spec from disk before deciding. Return the full corrected spec@1 object with `revision_note` set describing exactly what changed and why, per the standard canon/correct contract. Output the complete JSON directly in your response."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":398,"cache_read_input_tokens":710830,"output_tokens":1744,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":65},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":398,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1744,"cache_read_input_tokens":710830,"cache_creation_input_tokens":398,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":398},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce95DDPs4DXJcQ4WVQoP9","type":"assistant","uuid":"46463c22-216c-4d6a-84cd-69f022726bad","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:01:11.495Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
