{"parentUuid":"15cf3297-6fe0-4606-ab5e-69c113281542","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce95MzkMEi2DZkyZCFGa5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NNwoCrWkmKpX7KtXHyAVKv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\ngit diff .claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json | head -5\necho \"---\"\ngit status --short\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\nwith open('.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json') as f:\n    d = json.load(f)\nfor c in d['acceptance_criteria']:\n    if c['id'] == 'AC-002b':\n        print(c['criterion'])\nprint()\nprint('revision_note present:', 'revision_note' in d)\nprint('non_goals count:', len(d['non_goals']))\n\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1209,"cache_read_input_tokens":713389,"output_tokens":505,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":206},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1209,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":505,"cache_read_input_tokens":713389,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1209,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1209},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce95MuXaCrMx7c1ZtnVkS","type":"assistant","uuid":"3d440821-dd28-4773-b469-cc463a6aefb7","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:03:00.809Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"3d440821-dd28-4773-b469-cc463a6aefb7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f2b6282f-30f5-4394-9324-af4eeca1ec63","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NNwoCrWkmKpX7KtXHyAVKv","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json b/.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json\nindex c3d0cfb7..d3a9ba73 100644\n--- a/.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json\n+++ b/.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json\n@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@\n---\n M .claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json\n M crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\nScoped to the OpenContext/workspace-inheritance resolution logic this track builds (AC-002), NOT to real-workspace discovery of a Cargo platform manifest -- as of this spec, crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs:199 (the only site that registers a manifest into IdentityIndex.platform, which is what allows config/groups.rs::resolve() to classify a member as GroupMember::PlatformManifest) is gated by `if *eco == Ecosystem::Npm` with no Ecosystem::Cargo branch, so no Cargo.toml can become a GroupMember::PlatformManifest through the real, disk-discovered call path today (see non_goals for the deferred discovery-extension work). This criterion instead verifies the resolution logic directly: given a Fixed group constructed with a GroupMember::PlatformManifest member whose path P points at a Cargo.toml with `version.workspace = true` (a maturin platform crate inheriting its version from the workspace root, per crates/callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs:47-52's inherited_version detection) -- that member constructed directly in the test's group/workspace fixture rather than produced by walk.rs discovery -- and the workspace's root Cargo.toml declares a `[workspace.package] version` (e.g. \"3.2.1\", resolved via WorkspaceInheritance per crates/callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs:580-587), calling commands::version::plan_version on that group succeeds (returns Ok(..)) and the resulting VersionPlan's PlatformWrite entry for P has `from` equal to that resolved workspace version (\"3.2.1\") -- not an Err(ManifestError::WorkspaceInherited). This confirms plan_version's OpenContext derivation correctly resolves Cargo workspace-inherited versions for any manifest already classified as GroupMember::PlatformManifest, regardless of how that classification arose, and that the AC-002 machinery is format-agnostic. It does NOT confirm that plan_version works end-to-end starting from a real, disk-discovered Cargo platform manifest -- that requires the walk.rs discovery extension described in non_goals, which this track does not build.\n\nrevision_note present: True\nnon_goals count: 9","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6cf34260-8a22-4951-8055-d537fe3ac645","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:03:03.105Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"diff --git a/.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json b/.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json\nindex c3d0cfb7..d3a9ba73 100644\n--- a/.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json\n+++ b/.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json\n@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@\n---\n M .claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json\n M crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\nScoped to the OpenContext/workspace-inheritance resolution logic this track builds (AC-002), NOT to real-workspace discovery of a Cargo platform manifest -- as of this spec, crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs:199 (the only site that registers a manifest into IdentityIndex.platform, which is what allows config/groups.rs::resolve() to classify a member as GroupMember::PlatformManifest) is gated by `if *eco == Ecosystem::Npm` with no Ecosystem::Cargo branch, so no Cargo.toml can become a GroupMember::PlatformManifest through the real, disk-discovered call path today (see non_goals for the deferred discovery-extension work). This criterion instead verifies the resolution logic directly: given a Fixed group constructed with a GroupMember::PlatformManifest member whose path P points at a Cargo.toml with `version.workspace = true` (a maturin platform crate inheriting its version from the workspace root, per crates/callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs:47-52's inherited_version detection) -- that member constructed directly in the test's group/workspace fixture rather than produced by walk.rs discovery -- and the workspace's root Cargo.toml declares a `[workspace.package] version` (e.g. \"3.2.1\", resolved via WorkspaceInheritance per crates/callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs:580-587), calling commands::version::plan_version on that group succeeds (returns Ok(..)) and the resulting VersionPlan's PlatformWrite entry for P has `from` equal to that resolved workspace version (\"3.2.1\") -- not an Err(ManifestError::WorkspaceInherited). This confirms plan_version's OpenContext derivation correctly resolves Cargo workspace-inherited versions for any manifest already classified as GroupMember::PlatformManifest, regardless of how that classification arose, and that the AC-002 machinery is format-agnostic. It does NOT confirm that plan_version works end-to-end starting from a real, disk-discovered Cargo platform manifest -- that requires the walk.rs discovery extension described in non_goals, which this track does not build.\n\nrevision_note present: True\nnon_goals count: 9","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3d440821-dd28-4773-b469-cc463a6aefb7","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
