{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:05:14.109Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ac9f7c744ace9c035</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01CztDYCwU2yQoDGPLPwvA6M</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/ac9f7c744ace9c035.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement TASK-4 (AC-008 error propagation)\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Committed successfully as `b5a9123`. The pre-existing modified spec file (from the parallel TASK-3 canon-correction workflow) was correctly left untouched and unstaged.\n\n## Summary\n\n**TASK-4**: plan_version platform_writes: AC-008 error propagation on unreadable platform manifest\n\n- Read AC-008 directly from `.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json` on disk — confirmed it has two disjuncts: missing-file and malformed-content, both requiring `Err(GraphError)`, no panic, no partial `VersionPlan`.\n- Confirmed tree was clean and TASK-2 (`431feb9`) was HEAD-1 for `commands/version.rs` before starting.\n- Wrote both tests required by the review-extended `test.description`: `plan_version_returns_err_when_platform_manifest_missing_from_disk_at_plan_time` and `plan_version_returns_err_when_platform_manifest_content_is_malformed`, using the Case D hybrid-root fixture convention from TASK-2's landed tests.\n- Since TASK-2 already implements full `?`-based propagation, the tests passed immediately on first run — this is a test-only regression-pinning task by design (no `implementation.steps` in the plan). To verify this wasn't a vacuous pass, I temporarily swallowed the error at each propagation point (`ManifestFormat::from_path`, `ManifestDecl::new`, `open`, `current_version`) and confirmed both tests genuinely fail (red), then restored the real implementation byte-for-byte and confirmed green again.\n- `cargo fmt -p callisto-graph`, `cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n- Full suite: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib` → 371 passed, 0 failed.\n- Committed as `b5a9123`.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"TASK-4\",\n  \"status\": \"done\",\n  \"steps_completed\": [\n    \"confirmed clean tree at TASK-2 HEAD (431feb9) via git log/status\",\n    \"read AC-008 acceptance criterion text directly from spec file on disk\",\n    \"reviewed TASK-2's landed Case D hybrid-root fixture convention for consistency\",\n    \"wrote plan_version_returns_err_when_platform_manifest_missing_from_disk_at_plan_time\",\n    \"wrote plan_version_returns_err_when_platform_manifest_content_is_malformed (per review-extended test.description)\",\n    \"verified red: temporarily swallowed each ?-propagation site, confirmed both tests fail\",\n    \"restored real implementation byte-for-byte, confirmed both tests green\",\n    \"ran cargo fmt -p callisto-graph\",\n    \"ran cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings (clean)\",\n    \"ran full cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib (371 passed, 0 failed)\",\n    \"committed\"\n  ],\n  \"test_result\": \"pass\",\n  \"commit_sha\": \"b5a9123\",\n  \"criteria_evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-008\",\n      \"test_file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n      \"test_line\": 853,\n      \"implementation_file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n      \"implementation_line\": 291\n    }\n  ],\n  \"concerns\": \"This task adds no new implementation code by design (depends_on TASK-2, which already implements the full ?-based propagation chain). Genuine red/green TDD was demonstrated indirectly: instead of a red phase preceding implementation, I temporarily broke each error-propagation site to confirm the new tests would fail if the propagation regressed, then restored the shipped implementation unchanged. This matches the plan's own expected_failure note for this task.\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Verified via manual mutation that both tests are non-vacuous: swallowing the error at from_path/ManifestDecl::new/open/current_version caused both new tests to fail with the plan's Ok(VersionPlan{...platform_writes: []...}) printed, proving the tests genuinely exercise the ? propagation and not some unrelated early return.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>76383</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>20</tool_uses><duration_ms>297437</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
