{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:08:42.623Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aa6eef558916d9be3</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_014i1ozCyS3GkmrNtyD8UAAQ</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/aa6eef558916d9be3.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Exit-gate corrected Track 2 spec\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I read the spec fresh, verified every cited code location, and diffed the correction against the committed version. Verdict below.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"artifact_type\": \"spec@1\",\n  \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"retry_count\": 1,\n  \"verdict_summary\": \"The AC-002b correction is directionally right and the new non_goals entry is accurate, but three specific gaps remain: AC-002b lost its owner-bump precondition (vacuously satisfiable), its fixture leaves the member `role` unpinned (making AC-002's Canonical-unconditional clause unfalsifiable), and `purpose` still claims maturin end-to-end. Fix all three and resubmit.\",\n  \"blockers\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"AC-002b\",\n      \"location\": \".claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json acceptance_criteria[AC-002b]; crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:288\",\n      \"finding\": \"The rewrite dropped the original 'Given the AC-001 scenario' anchor and never restated the precondition it carried: the fixture group's owner Package member must receive a real PlannedBump this run. plan_version emits a PlatformWrite only when `bump_by_pkg.get(owner)` is Some (version.rs:288); with no owner bump, `platform_writes` is empty and the assertion 'the resulting VersionPlan's PlatformWrite entry for P has `from` equal to 3.2.1' is vacuously satisfiable by a test that looks for an entry, finds none, and asserts nothing. The criterion also says 'calling commands::version::plan_version on that group', which is not what the API takes — plan_version takes &amp;Workspace, not a group. Required change: restate the setup as 'given a Fixed group whose owner Package member receives a real PlannedBump to Y this run, and which also contains a GroupMember::PlatformManifest member constructed directly in the test's group fixture (not produced by walk.rs discovery) whose path P is a Cargo.toml declaring `version.workspace = true`', and restate the assertion as 'plan_version(&amp;ws, ..) returns Ok and plan.platform_writes contains exactly one entry with manifest == P, from == \\\"3.2.1\\\", and version == Y' so entry existence is asserted rather than presupposed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"AC-002 (the 'ManifestRole::Canonical unconditionally, regardless of the member's own role field' clause) — unfalsifiable after the AC-002b rewrite\",\n      \"location\": \".claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json acceptance_criteria[AC-002] and [AC-002b]; crates/callisto-model/src/package.rs:104-106; crates/callisto-manifests/src/npm.rs:68,229; crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs:213-216\",\n      \"finding\": \"AC-002 asserts plan_version constructs ManifestDecl with ManifestRole::Canonical unconditionally, regardless of the GroupMember::PlatformManifest's own `role`, so a Cargo/TOML platform manifest does not trip the Platform-role-vs-CargoToml rejection at package.rs:104-106. I verified this clause has zero observable consequence in any npm scenario: ManifestDecl::new permits Platform + PackageJson, and PackageJson stores `role` without letting it affect current_version (npm.rs:68, 229), so AC-001/AC-003..AC-007b cannot falsify it. Before the correction, AC-002b's real-discovery scenario would have supplied a member carrying ManifestRole::Platform (the role walk.rs:213-216 stores). The rewrite replaced that with a test-constructed member but did not pin its `role` field, so an implementer who writes `role: ManifestRole::Canonical` into the fixture gets an identical pass whether or not the implementation honors AC-002's rule — the clause becomes unfalsifiable spec-wide. Required change: add to AC-002b that the fixture member's own `role` field is ManifestRole::Platform { .. } (mirroring what walk.rs:213-216 stores for npm platform manifests), and state the consequence explicitly: an implementation that forwarded member.role into ManifestDecl::new instead of hardcoding ManifestRole::Canonical would return Err(ModelError) per package.rs:104-106 and fail this criterion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"purpose (document header, line 3)\",\n      \"location\": \".claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json field `purpose`\",\n      \"finding\": \"purpose still states the track exists 'so a napi-rs/maturin platform package's own manifest gets bumped in lockstep with its owning package' — the exact end-to-end claim the correction retracted. I independently confirmed walk.rs:199-218: the only insert into IdentityIndex.platform sits inside `if *eco == Ecosystem::Npm` with no Cargo branch, and config/groups.rs:161-167 and 202-208 produce GroupMember::PlatformManifest solely from index.platform, so no maturin/Cargo manifest can reach plan_version's platform_writes loop through real discovery. The new non_goals entry says this correctly; purpose contradicts it, and purpose is what a planner reads first when deriving tasks. Required change: rewrite purpose to name npm/napi-rs as the ecosystem this track delivers end-to-end, and add that Cargo-format (maturin) platform manifests are handled by the same format-agnostic machinery (AC-002, AC-002b) but are not reachable through walk.rs discovery today, cross-referencing the walk.rs non_goals entry — mirroring the qualification already added to the `owner: PackageId` non_goals entry.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"reasoning\": \"What I verified independently, not from the summary. (1) walk.rs:184-227 read in full: the platform registration block is `if *eco == Ecosystem::Npm { ... index.platform.insert(...) }` (lines 199-218). No Ecosystem::Cargo branch exists. config/groups.rs:161-167 (fixed) and 202-208 (linked) construct GroupMember::PlatformManifest only from `index.platform.get(name)`. The reported contradiction is real and the new non_goals entry describes it accurately and specifically, naming the exact gate and the exact mechanism. (2) cargo.rs:47-52 is verbatim the inherited_version detection AC-002b cites; cargo.rs:580-587 is verbatim the [workspace.package] version resolution; cargo.rs:178-189 returns Err(ManifestError::WorkspaceInherited) exactly when inherited_version is true and no inheritance context is present; cargo.rs:80,97 confirm CargoToml::open threads ctx.cargo_workspace into the handle. version.rs:264-280 derives OpenContext from the real root exactly as AC-002 describes. So AC-002b's assertion is mechanically meaningful: it distinguishes a correct ctx derivation from a None one. (3) Buildability of the fixture: Workspace fields are pub (lib.rs:55 `pub config`), ResolvedConfig.groups is pub (config/resolve.rs), GroupTable.fixed / GroupDef.members / the GroupMember::PlatformManifest variant are all pub (config/groups.rs:11-34), and the Workspace doc comment at lib.rs:83-85 explicitly blesses hand-constructing a Workspace in tests. A test can `let mut ws = Workspace::load(..)`, push a PlatformManifest member into `ws.config.groups.fixed`, then call plan_version — satisfying the last non_goals testing constraint (plan_version as entry point). So AC-002b is genuinely buildable; my blockers are about what it does and does not pin down, not about reachability. (4) Sweep for missed spots: 'maturin' appears 4x — purpose (blocker 3), the new non_goals entry (correct), AC-002 (rationale about format, not discovery — acceptable), AC-002b (correct). No api_surface text assumes Cargo discovery. AC-008's error scenarios are NOT in the same unreachable class: I read the landed tests at version.rs:803-856 and 863-905, which reach both disjuncts by loading the workspace with a valid npm platform manifest and then deleting/corrupting it before plan_version — a real drift path. (5) AC-007 and the whole rest of the spec: git diff against 24398327 shows exactly three edits — the `owner: PackageId` non_goals entry gained a NOTE, one non_goals entry was added, AC-002b was rewritten, plus reasoning/revision_note. AC-001, AC-003..AC-007b, AC-008..AC-013, scope, and api_surface are byte-identical. AC-007 is genuinely unaffected and the landed producer loop at version.rs:282-302 iterates every PlatformManifest member per group, consistent with it. (6) TBDs: the only 'TBD' substring in the document is the phrase 'No TBDs remain' inside the private reasoning scratchpad. No actual TBDs. (7) Scope fits one planning cycle: three files, one struct field addition, one producer loop, two apply-side fixes. (8) retry_count set to 1: the three prior rounds concluded in a pass and closed that cycle; this is the first gate of the post-implementation correction, so the escalation threshold has not been reached. If this correction cycle itself reaches a fourth failed gate, escalate to human rather than failing again. Note the verdict@1 schema enumerates only pass|fail with additionalProperties false, so escalation must be surfaced in verdict_summary, not as a third enum value.\"\n}\n```\n\nThree things worth flagging to the orchestrator beyond the JSON:\n\n- The correction itself is sound. The contradiction is real (I confirmed `walk.rs:199-218` has no Cargo branch and that `config/groups.rs:161-167` produces `GroupMember::PlatformManifest` only from `index.platform`), option (a) was the right call, and the new non_goals entry is specific enough that a future track can pick up the deferred work without re-investigating.\n- Blocker 2 is the one that matters most. The correction silently made an existing AC-002 clause unfalsifiable. Before the rewrite, AC-002b's real-discovery scenario would have carried `ManifestRole::Platform`; the fixture rewrite left the role unpinned, and no npm scenario can exercise that clause because `ManifestDecl::new` permits `Platform + PackageJson` and `npm.rs` ignores role in `current_version`. One sentence in AC-002b fixes it.\n- All three blockers are text-only edits to `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json`. No code change and no re-planning of landed tasks is implied; TASK-3's implementer can resume as soon as AC-002b is re-issued.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>85234</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>28</tool_uses><duration_ms>314142</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
