{"parentUuid":"69c51653-67f4-4e89-82ec-bb8bee3a4576","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce95q2zHm76qdL9KkmQ3d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011yBJ8GdZZiF3Urn3Bdp4tK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\npython3 << 'PYEOF'\nimport json\n\npath = '.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json'\nwith open(path) as f:\n    d = json.load(f)\n\n# Fix 3: purpose field -- correct maturin end-to-end claim\nd['purpose'] = d['purpose'].replace(\n    \"so a napi-rs/maturin platform package's own manifest gets bumped in lockstep with its \"\n    \"owning package and the owner's optionalDependencies pointer to that platform package \"\n    \"tracks the same target version.\",\n    \"so a napi-rs platform package's own manifest gets bumped in lockstep with its owning \"\n    \"package and the owner's optionalDependencies pointer to that platform package tracks the \"\n    \"same target version. This is delivered end-to-end for npm platform manifests; Cargo-format \"\n    \"(maturin) platform manifests are handled by the same format-agnostic OpenContext/\"\n    \"ManifestRole::Canonical machinery (AC-002, AC-002b) but are not yet reachable through real \"\n    \"workspace discovery (walk.rs's platform-manifest detection is npm-only today -- see \"\n    \"non_goals).\"\n)\n\n# Fix 1+2: AC-002b -- restore owner-bump precondition, assert entry existence, pin role field\nby_id = {c['id']: c for c in d['acceptance_criteria']}\nby_id['AC-002b']['criterion'] = (\n    \"Scoped to the OpenContext/workspace-inheritance resolution logic this track builds \"\n    \"(AC-002), NOT to real-workspace discovery of a Cargo platform manifest -- as of this \"\n    \"spec, crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs:199 (the only site that registers a manifest \"\n    \"into IdentityIndex.platform, which is what allows config/groups.rs::resolve() to \"\n    \"classify a member as GroupMember::PlatformManifest) is gated by `if *eco == \"\n    \"Ecosystem::Npm` with no Ecosystem::Cargo branch, so no Cargo.toml can become a \"\n    \"GroupMember::PlatformManifest through the real, disk-discovered call path today (see \"\n    \"non_goals for the deferred discovery-extension work). This criterion instead verifies \"\n    \"the resolution logic directly: given a Fixed group whose owner Package member receives \"\n    \"a real PlannedBump to version Y this run (the same owner-bump precondition AC-001 \"\n    \"requires -- without a real bump, no PlatformWrite is produced for any member, per \"\n    \"AC-006, and the criterion would be vacuously satisfiable), and which also contains a \"\n    \"GroupMember::PlatformManifest member constructed directly in the test's group/workspace \"\n    \"fixture (via Workspace::load followed by pushing the member into ws.config.groups.fixed, \"\n    \"per lib.rs's documented test-construction pattern -- NOT produced by walk.rs discovery) \"\n    \"whose `role` field is set to ManifestRole::Platform { .. } (mirroring exactly what \"\n    \"walk.rs:213-216 stores for a real npm platform manifest -- this pins AC-002's \"\n    \"'ManifestRole::Canonical unconditionally, regardless of the member's own role field' \"\n    \"clause to something falsifiable: an implementation that forwarded member.role into \"\n    \"ManifestDecl::new instead of hardcoding ManifestRole::Canonical would return \"\n    \"Err(ModelError) per crates/callisto-model/src/package.rs:104-106 and fail this \"\n    \"criterion) and whose path P points at a Cargo.toml with `version.workspace = true` (a \"\n    \"maturin platform crate inheriting its version from the workspace root, per \"\n    \"crates/callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs:47-52's inherited_version detection), and the \"\n    \"workspace's root Cargo.toml declares a `[workspace.package] version` (e.g. \\\"3.2.1\\\", \"\n    \"resolved via WorkspaceInheritance per crates/callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs:580-587), \"\n    \"calling commands::version::plan_version(&ws, ..) on that workspace returns Ok(..) and \"\n    \"the resulting VersionPlan.platform_writes contains EXACTLY ONE entry with manifest == P, \"\n    \"`from` == the resolved workspace version (\\\"3.2.1\\\") -- not an \"\n    \"Err(ManifestError::WorkspaceInherited) and not a missing/empty entry -- and `version` == \"\n    \"Y (the owner's bump target). This confirms plan_version's OpenContext derivation \"\n    \"correctly resolves Cargo workspace-inherited versions and honors the unconditional-\"\n    \"Canonical-role rule for any manifest already classified as GroupMember::PlatformManifest, \"\n    \"regardless of how that classification arose, and that the AC-002 machinery is \"\n    \"format-agnostic. It does NOT confirm that plan_version works end-to-end starting from a \"\n    \"real, disk-discovered Cargo platform manifest -- that requires the walk.rs discovery \"\n    \"extension described in non_goals, which this track does not build.\"\n)\n\nwith open(path, 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(d, f, indent=2)\n\nprint(\"patched\")\nprint(\"purpose has 'maturin' twice:\", d['purpose'].count('maturin'))\nprint(\"AC-002b mentions ManifestRole::Platform:\", 'ManifestRole::Platform' in by_id['AC-002b']['criterion'])\nprint(\"AC-002b mentions EXACTLY ONE:\", 'EXACTLY ONE' in by_id['AC-002b']['criterion'])\nPYEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":430,"cache_read_input_tokens":727059,"output_tokens":1994,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":430,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1994,"cache_read_input_tokens":727059,"cache_creation_input_tokens":430,"cache_creation":{"e