{"parentUuid":"0e2ea386-e8b1-4c3f-a773-b551c2a27ee7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce96r78UbLAzR1JCKKoZu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PKkPFhfYC3pnN96V7Jopzz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/TASK-3-amended.json 2>/dev/null | head -30\necho \"---\"\nls -la /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/TASK-3-amended.json 2>/dev/null"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1555,"cache_read_input_tokens":750841,"output_tokens":281,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":34},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1555,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":281,"cache_read_input_tokens":750841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1555,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1555},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce96r3GJaZbXaiM2HKwj2","type":"assistant","uuid":"0f4c12b6-dcf4-40f0-819f-5f65b8e06103","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:22:26.431Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"0f4c12b6-dcf4-40f0-819f-5f65b8e06103","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01PKkPFhfYC3pnN96V7Jopzz","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"cat /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/TASK-3-amended.json 2>/dev/null | head -30\\necho \\\"---\\\"\\nrtk ls -la /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/TASK-3-amended.json 2>/dev/null\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":16},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1b0ee233-34fe-411b-acf8-48bbea713d46","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:22:26.448Z","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"0f4c12b6-dcf4-40f0-819f-5f65b8e06103","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f6d169e0-a1ab-46f9-9c71-0660b9a04793","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PKkPFhfYC3pnN96V7Jopzz","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"id\": \"TASK-3\",\n  \"title\": \"plan_version platform_writes: workspace-inherited Cargo version (fixture-constructed) + multiple platform siblings\",\n  \"depends_on\": [\n    \"TASK-2\"\n  ],\n  \"files\": [\n    \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\"\n  ],\n  \"reasoning\": \"AMENDED (corrected AC-002b, spec revision_note): TASK-3's lambda-implementer confirmed via walk.rs:199 (IdentityIndex.platform registration gated to `if *eco == Ecosystem::Npm`, no Cargo branch) plus an empirical real-pipeline run that no Cargo.toml can become a GroupMember::PlatformManifest through real, disk-discovered workspace walk today -- a Cargo platform sibling with `version.workspace = true` resolves as an ordinary GroupMember::Package instead. The corrected AC-002b (read verbatim from the spec file, not paraphrased) now verifies plan_version's OpenContext/workspace-inheritance resolution logic directly against a FIXTURE-CONSTRUCTED GroupMember::PlatformManifest: load a real Workspace via Workspace::load, then push a PlatformManifest member directly into ws.config.groups.fixed's GroupDef.members, bypassing walk.rs discovery entirely. The fixture's `role` field must be set to ManifestRole::Platform{..} (mirroring exactly what walk.rs:213-216 stores for a real npm platform manifest) so the test is falsifiable against AC-002's 'ManifestRole::Canonical unconditionally, regardless of the member's own role field' clause -- an implementation that forwarded member.role into ManifestDecl::new instead of hardcoding Canonical would hit the Platform-role-vs-CargoToml-format rejection at callisto-model/src/package.rs:104-106 and fail this test. The owner Package member must receive a real PlannedBump this run (not left unbumped), since AC-002b's own text notes the criterion is otherwise vacuously satisfiable per AC-006. Verified via direct read of the currently landed commands/version.rs (lines 261-334, commits 431feb9 + c3516ba): the platform_writes loop already iterates `group.members(GroupMemberKind::PlatformManifest)` generically -- it has no dependency on how the member entered `ws.config.groups.fixed` (real walk discovery vs. direct fixture construction) -- and already hardcodes `ManifestRole::Canonical` in the `ManifestDecl::new` call at line 300, ignoring the member's own `role` field, and already derives `cargo_workspace`/`open_ctx` from the real workspace root (lines 264-280). So this fixture-based AC-002b test requires zero further implementation changes; it is written purely to pin the behavior AC-002b now describes. AC-007 (unaffected by the correction, confirmed already satisfied by TASK-2's landed producer loop) keeps its original real-discovery test content unchanged, verbatim, per the spec revision_note's own statement that AC-007 required no change.\",\n  \"test\": {\n    \"description\": \"Two tests. AC-002b [REWRITTEN per corrected spec]: fixture-constructed GroupMember::PlatformManifest -- build a real Workspace via Workspace::load (a Cargo owner package plus a separate, ordinary, non-grouped Cargo package acting as the fixture's on-disk platform manifest target), then push a `crate::config::groups::GroupMember::PlatformManifest` literal directly into `ws.config.groups.fixed`'s matching `GroupDef.members`, with `role: callisto_model::ManifestRole::Platform { platform, arch, abi }` set (not default/unpinned) and `path` pointing at a Cargo.toml declaring `version.workspace = true`, whose workspace root `[workspace.package] version` is a distinct, recognizable value (\\\"3.2.1\\\"). The owner Package member must receive a real PlannedBump this run (via a changeset targeting the owner). Call plan_version(&ws, ..) and assert Ok(..) with platform_writes containing exactly one entry: manifest == the fixture path, from == \\\"3.2.1\\\" (the resolved workspace-inherited version, not an Err(ManifestError::WorkspaceInherited) and not missing/empty), version == the owner's real bump target. AC-007 [UNCHANGED, still valid per spec revision_note]: owner with two platform siblings, both real, disk-discovered GroupMember::PlatformManifest members (e.g. linux-x64-gnu and darwin-arm64 targets), both bumped -- plan_version's platform_writes contains one PlatformWrite entry per platform member (two entries total), each with its own manifest path and matching from/version values.\",\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n    \"code\": \"#[test]\\nfn plan_version_platform_write_from_resolves_cargo_workspace_inherited_version() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    git_init_with_commit(root);\\n\\n    // Workspace root Cargo.toml supplying the [workspace.package] version\\n    // that a `version.workspace = true` platform manifest inherits from.\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[workspace]\\\\n\\\\n[workspace.package]\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"3.2.1\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n\\n    // The real owner package -- receives a real PlannedBump this run.\\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\"crates/owner\\\")).unwrap();\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"crates/owner/Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"cargo-owner\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"1.0.0\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n\\n    // The fixture's on-disk platform manifest target -- a maturin-style\\n    // Cargo.toml inheriting its version from [workspace.package]. This is\\n    // an ordinary, real, on-disk Cargo.toml; it is NOT registered as a\\n    // GroupMember::PlatformManifest by walk.rs (per AC-002b, that\\n    // classification is npm-only today) -- it is wired into the group\\n    // fixture manually below.\\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\"platform/plat\\\")).unwrap();\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"platform/plat/Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"cargo-owner-linux-x64-gnu\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion.workspace = true\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"callisto.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[[fixed-group]]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"cargo-owner-group\\\\\\\"\\\\nmembers = [\\\\\\\"cargo-owner\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\".changeset\\\")).unwrap();\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\".changeset/bump.md\\\"),\\n        \\\"---\\\\n\\\\\\\"cargo-owner\\\\\\\": patch\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nfix.\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n    commit_all(root, \\\"add owner and fixture platform crate\\\");\\n\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let runner = NoopRunner;\\n    let mut ws =\\n        Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).expect(\\\"workspace must load\\\");\\n\\n    // Fixture-construct the GroupMember::PlatformManifest, bypassing\\n    // walk.rs discovery entirely (per corrected AC-002b).\\n    let owner = callisto_model::PackageId::Bare(\\\"cargo-owner\\\".to_string());\\n    let group_name = callisto_model::GroupName(\\\"cargo-owner-group\\\".to_string());\\n    let group = ws\\n        .config\\n        .groups\\n        .fixed\\n        .get_mut(&group_name)\\n        .expect(\\\"cargo-owner-group must exist as a real Fixed group after Workspace::load\\\");\\n    group\\n        .members\\n        .push(crate::config::groups::GroupMember::PlatformManifest {\\n            owner: owner.clone(),\\n            role: callisto_model::ManifestRole::Platform {\\n                platform: \\\"linux\\\".to_string(),\\n                arch: \\\"x64\\\".to_string(),\\n                abi: Some(\\\"gnu\\\".to_string()),\\n            },\\n            path: std::path::PathBuf::from(\\\"platform/plat/Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n            name: \\\"cargo-owner-linux-x64-gnu\\\".to_string(),\\n        });\\n\\n    let inference = NoInference;\\n    let opts = VersionOptions {\\n        strict: false,\\n        strict_graph: false,\\n        allow_empty_changesets: true,\\n    };\\n\\n    let plan = plan_version(&ws, &inference, &opts).expect(\\\"plan_version must succeed\\\");\\n\\n    let owner_bump = plan\\n        .bumps\\n        .iter()\\n        .find(|b| b.package == owner)\\n        .expect(\\\"owner must receive a real PlannedBump this run, not a vacuous pass\\\");\\n\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        plan.platform_writes.len(),\\n        1,\\n        \\\"expected exactly one PlatformWrite for the fixture-constructed Cargo platform member, got: {:?}\\\",\\n        plan.platform_writes\\n    );\\n    let pw = &plan.platform_writes[0];\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        pw.manifest,\\n        Path::new(\\\"platform/plat/Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"PlatformWrite.manifest must be the fixture platform manifest's path\\\"\\n    );\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        pw.from.to_string(),\\n        \\\"3.2.1\\\",\\n        \\\"PlatformWrite.from must resolve the Cargo workspace-inherited version.workspace = true \\\\\\n         value from [workspace.package] version, not fail or silently default\\\"\\n    );\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        pw.version, owner_bump.to,\\n        \\\"PlatformWrite.version must equal the owner's real bump target\\\"\\n    );\\n}\",\n    \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_platform_write_from_resolves_cargo_workspace_inherited_version commands::version::tests::plan_version_emits_platform_write_for_each_of_two_platform_siblings\",\n    \"expected_failure\": \"plan_version_platform_write_from_resolves_cargo_workspace_inherited_version: since TASK-2 already landed and its loop is agnostic to how a GroupMember::PlatformManifest entered ws.config.groups.fixed (real walk discovery or direct fixture construction), this test is expected to pass immediately once written. A failure here means TASK-2's loop forwarded `member.role` into `ManifestDecl::new` instead of hardcoding `ManifestRole::Canonical` (commands/version.rs line 300) -- which would surface as `Err(GraphError::Manifest(ManifestError::...))` from the Platform-role-vs-CargoToml-format rejection at callisto-model/src/package.rs:104-106 instead of `Ok(..)` with one PlatformWrite entry. plan_version_emits_platform_write_for_each_of_two_platform_siblings fails before TASK-2's implementation lands (platform_writes hardcoded empty); after TASK-2, it should already pass with zero further implementation changes -- a failure means only one platform member is being processed, or cargo_workspace inheritance isn't reaching the correct WorkspaceInheritance.\"\n  },\n  \"implementation\": {\n    \"description\": \"No new implementation code -- TASK-2's landed loop (commands/version.rs lines 282-330) already iterates every PlatformManifest member per group regardless of how it entered ws.config.groups.fixed, already hardcodes ManifestRole::Canonical unconditionally (line 300, ignoring member.role), and already derives cargo_workspace/open_ctx from the real workspace root (lines 264-280). This task exists purely to pin AC-002b's corrected fixture-based scenario and AC-007's unchanged two-sibling scenario with dedicated tests.\",\n    \"steps\": [\n      \"No production code changes. If plan_version_platform_write_from_resolves_cargo_workspace_inherited_version fails, the bug is TASK-2's loop forwarding member.role into ManifestDecl::new instead of hardcoding ManifestRole::Canonical in commands/version.rs's platform_writes loop -- fix that.\",\n      \"No production code changes. If plan_version_emits_platform_write_for_each_of_two_platform_siblings fails, the bug is TASK-2's loop only processing the first PlatformManifest member found per group, or cargo_workspace being derived as None instead of from WorkspaceCargoResolver -- fix that in commands/version.rs rather than adding new code here.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n  \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass\",\n  \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin corrected AC-002b (fixture-constructed Cargo platform manifest resolution) and AC-007 (multi-sibling platform writes)\",\n  \"covers_criteria\": [\n    \"AC-002b\",\n    \"AC-007\"\n---\n644  /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/TASK-3-amended.json  11.4K","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f1b09bb1-ec94-418d-a955-6bc13c598435","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:22:28.749Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\n  \"id\": \"TASK-3\",\n  \"title\": \"plan_version platform_writes: workspace-inherited Cargo version (fixture-constructed) + multiple platform siblings\",\n  \"depends_on\": [\n    \"TASK-2\"\n  ],\n  \"files\": [\n    \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\"\n  ],\n  \"reasoning\": \"AMENDED (corrected AC-002b, spec revision_note): TASK-3's lambda-implementer confirmed via walk.rs:199 (IdentityIndex.platform registration gated to `if *eco == Ecosystem::Npm`, no Cargo branch) plus an empirical real-pipeline run that no Cargo.toml can become a GroupMember::PlatformManifest through real, disk-discovered workspace walk today -- a Cargo platform sibling with `version.workspace = true` resolves as an ordinary GroupMember::Package instead. The corrected AC-002b (read verbatim from the spec file, not paraphrased) now verifies plan_version's OpenContext/workspace-inheritance resolution logic directly against a FIXTURE-CONSTRUCTED GroupMember::PlatformManifest: load a real Workspace via Workspace::load, then push a PlatformManifest member directly into ws.config.groups.fixed's GroupDef.members, bypassing walk.rs discovery entirely. The fixture's `role` field must be set to ManifestRole::Platform{..} (mirroring exactly what walk.rs:213-216 stores for a real npm platform manifest) so the test is falsifiable against AC-002's 'ManifestRole::Canonical unconditionally, regardless of the member's own role field' clause -- an implementation that forwarded member.role into ManifestDecl::new instead of hardcoding Canonical would hit the Platform-role-vs-CargoToml-format rejection at callisto-model/src/package.rs:104-106 and fail this test. The owner Package member must receive a real PlannedBump this run (not left unbumped), since AC-002b's own text notes the criterion is otherwise vacuously satisfiable per AC-006. Verified via direct read of the currently landed commands/version.rs (lines 261-334, commits 431feb9 + c3516ba): the platform_writes loop already iterates `group.members(GroupMemberKind::PlatformManifest)` generically -- it has no dependency on how the member entered `ws.config.groups.fixed` (real walk discovery vs. direct fixture construction) -- and already hardcodes `ManifestRole::Canonical` in the `ManifestDecl::new` call at line 300, ignoring the member's own `role` field, and already derives `cargo_workspace`/`open_ctx` from the real workspace root (lines 264-280). So this fixture-based AC-002b test requires zero further implementation changes; it is written purely to pin the behavior AC-002b now describes. AC-007 (unaffected by the correction, confirmed already satisfied by TASK-2's landed producer loop) keeps its original real-discovery test content unchanged, verbatim, per the spec revision_note's own statement that AC-007 required no change.\",\n  \"test\": {\n    \"description\": \"Two tests. AC-002b [REWRITTEN per corrected spec]: fixture-constructed GroupMember::PlatformManifest -- build a real Workspace via Workspace::load (a Cargo owner package plus a separate, ordinary, non-grouped Cargo package acting as the fixture's on-disk platform manifest target), then push a `crate::config::groups::GroupMember::PlatformManifest` literal directly into `ws.config.groups.fixed`'s matching `GroupDef.members`, with `role: callisto_model::ManifestRole::Platform { platform, arch, abi }` set (not default/unpinned) and `path` pointing at a Cargo.toml declaring `version.workspace = true`, whose workspace root `[workspace.package] version` is a distinct, recognizable value (\\\"3.2.1\\\"). The owner Package member must receive a real PlannedBump this run (via a changeset targeting the owner). Call plan_version(&ws, ..) and assert Ok(..) with platform_writes containing exactly one entry: manifest == the fixture path, from == \\\"3.2.1\\\" (the resolved workspace-inherited version, not an Err(ManifestError::WorkspaceInherited) and not missing/empty), version == the owner's real bump target. AC-007 [UNCHANGED, still valid per spec revision_note]: owner with two platform siblings, both real, disk-discovered GroupMember::PlatformManifest members (e.g. linux-x64-gnu and darwin-arm64 targets), both bumped -- plan_version's platform_writes contains one PlatformWrite entry per platform member (two entries total), each with its own manifest path and matching from/version values.\",\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n    \"code\": \"#[test]\\nfn plan_version_platform_write_from_resolves_cargo_workspace_inherited_version() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    git_init_with_commit(root);\\n\\n    // Workspace root Cargo.toml supplying the [workspace.package] version\\n    // that a `version.workspace = true` platform manifest inherits from.\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[workspace]\\\\n\\\\n[workspace.package]\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"3.2.1\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n\\n    // The real owner package -- receives a real PlannedBump this run.\\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\"crates/owner\\\")).unwrap();\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"crates/owner/Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"cargo-owner\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"1.0.0\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n\\n    // The fixture's on-disk platform manifest target -- a maturin-style\\n    // Cargo.toml inheriting its version from [workspace.package]. This is\\n    // an ordinary, real, on-disk Cargo.toml; it is NOT registered as a\\n    // GroupMember::PlatformManifest by walk.rs (per AC-002b, that\\n    // classification is npm-only today) -- it is wired into the group\\n    // fixture manually below.\\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\"platform/plat\\\")).unwrap();\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"platform/plat/Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"cargo-owner-linux-x64-gnu\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion.workspace = true\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"callisto.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[[fixed-group]]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"cargo-owner-group\\\\\\\"\\\\nmembers = [\\\\\\\"cargo-owner\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\".changeset\\\")).unwrap();\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\".changeset/bump.md\\\"),\\n        \\\"---\\\\n\\\\\\\"cargo-owner\\\\\\\": patch\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nfix.\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n    commit_all(root, \\\"add owner and fixture platform crate\\\");\\n\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let runner = NoopRunner;\\n    let mut ws =\\n        Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).expect(\\\"workspace must load\\\");\\n\\n    // Fixture-construct the GroupMember::PlatformManifest, bypassing\\n    // walk.rs discovery entirely (per corrected AC-002b).\\n    let owner = callisto_model::PackageId::Bare(\\\"cargo-owner\\\".to_string());\\n    let group_name = callisto_model::GroupName(\\\"cargo-owner-group\\\".to_string());\\n    let group = ws\\n        .config\\n        .groups\\n        .fixed\\n        .get_mut(&group_name)\\n        .expect(\\\"cargo-owner-group must exist as a real Fixed group after Workspace::load\\\");\\n    group\\n        .members\\n        .push(crate::config::groups::GroupMember::PlatformManifest {\\n            owner: owner.clone(),\\n            role: callisto_model::ManifestRole::Platform {\\n                platform: \\\"linux\\\".to_string(),\\n                arch: \\\"x64\\\".to_string(),\\n                abi: Some(\\\"gnu\\\".to_string()),\\n            },\\n            path: std::path::PathBuf::from(\\\"platform/plat/Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n            name: \\\"cargo-owner-linux-x64-gnu\\\".to_string(),\\n        });\\n\\n    let inference = NoInference;\\n    let opts = VersionOptions {\\n        strict: false,\\n        strict_graph: false,\\n        allow_empty_changesets: true,\\n    };\\n\\n    let plan = plan_version(&ws, &inference, &opts).expect(\\\"plan_version must succeed\\\");\\n\\n    let owner_bump = plan\\n        .bumps\\n        .iter()\\n        .find(|b| b.package == owner)\\n        .expect(\\\"owner must receive a real PlannedBump this run, not a vacuous pass\\\");\\n\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        plan.platform_writes.len(),\\n        1,\\n        \\\"expected exactly one PlatformWrite for the fixture-constructed Cargo platform member, got: {:?}\\\",\\n        plan.platform_writes\\n    );\\n    let pw = &plan.platform_writes[0];\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        pw.manifest,\\n        Path::new(\\\"platform/plat/Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"PlatformWrite.manifest must be the fixture platform manifest's path\\\"\\n    );\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        pw.from.to_string(),\\n        \\\"3.2.1\\\",\\n        \\\"PlatformWrite.from must resolve the Cargo workspace-inherited version.workspace = true \\\\\\n         value from [workspace.package] version, not fail or silently default\\\"\\n    );\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        pw.version, owner_bump.to,\\n        \\\"PlatformWrite.version must equal the owner's real bump target\\\"\\n    );\\n}\",\n    \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_platform_write_from_resolves_cargo_workspace_inherited_version commands::version::tests::plan_version_emits_platform_write_for_each_of_two_platform_siblings\",\n    \"expected_failure\": \"plan_version_platform_write_from_resolves_cargo_workspace_inherited_version: since TASK-2 already landed and its loop is agnostic to how a GroupMember::PlatformManifest entered ws.config.groups.fixed (real walk discovery or direct fixture construction), this test is expected to pass immediately once written. A failure here means TASK-2's loop forwarded `member.role` into `ManifestDecl::new` instead of hardcoding `ManifestRole::Canonical` (commands/version.rs line 300) -- which would surface as `Err(GraphError::Manifest(ManifestError::...))` from the Platform-role-vs-CargoToml-format rejection at callisto-model/src/package.rs:104-106 instead of `Ok(..)` with one PlatformWrite entry. plan_version_emits_platform_write_for_each_of_two_platform_siblings fails before TASK-2's implementation lands (platform_writes hardcoded empty); after TASK-2, it should already pass with zero further implementation changes -- a failure means only one platform member is being processed, or cargo_workspace inheritance isn't reaching the correct WorkspaceInheritance.\"\n  },\n  \"implementation\": {\n    \"description\": \"No new implementation code -- TASK-2's landed loop (commands/version.rs lines 282-330) already iterates every PlatformManifest member per group regardless of how it entered ws.config.groups.fixed, already hardcodes ManifestRole::Canonical unconditionally (line 300, ignoring member.role), and already derives cargo_workspace/open_ctx from the real workspace root (lines 264-280). This task exists purely to pin AC-002b's corrected fixture-based scenario and AC-007's unchanged two-sibling scenario with dedicated tests.\",\n    \"steps\": [\n      \"No production code changes. If plan_version_platform_write_from_resolves_cargo_workspace_inherited_version fails, the bug is TASK-2's loop forwarding member.role into ManifestDecl::new instead of hardcoding ManifestRole::Canonical in commands/version.rs's platform_writes loop -- fix that.\",\n      \"No production code changes. If plan_version_emits_platform_write_for_each_of_two_platform_siblings fails, the bug is TASK-2's loop only processing the first PlatformManifest member found per group, or cargo_workspace being derived as None instead of from WorkspaceCargoResolver -- fix that in commands/version.rs rather than adding new code here.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n  \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass\",\n  \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin corrected AC-002b (fixture-constructed Cargo platform manifest resolution) and AC-007 (multi-sibling platform writes)\",\n  \"covers_criteria\": [\n    \"AC-002b\",\n    \"AC-007\"\n---\n644  /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/TASK-3-amended.json  11.4K","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0f4c12b6-dcf4-40f0-819f-5f65b8e06103","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
