{"parentUuid":"38bbce04-2708-4750-ae51-a7eb78d5677e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9swxFqFUg48TanVRcTx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LjSMNBB96pwzMT3nZL6NTb","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/00-design.md","old_string":"Discovery walks the workspace (moon's project graph when available for authoritative\nproject roots, `ignore`-crate walk otherwise — `ProjectLocator`, §0.1/§15); `package-set`\nmatches expand to concrete packages; explicit `[[package]]` entries always win over set\nmatches. A set matching nothing, or two sets claiming the same package, is a hard config\nerror. **Group membership validation, at parse time (P5), not at mutation time**: a package","new_string":"Discovery walks the workspace (moon's project graph when available for authoritative\nproject roots, `ignore`-crate walk otherwise — `ProjectLocator`, §0.1/§15); `package-set`\nmatches expand to concrete packages; explicit `[[package]]` entries always win over set\nmatches. A set matching nothing, or two sets claiming the same package, is a hard config\nerror.\n\n**`match` is a glob against the package's name, not its workspace path.** A bare pattern\n(`\"pkg-*\"`) matches that name in any ecosystem; an `ecosystem:` prefix (`\"cargo:pkg-*\"`,\n`\"npm:pkg-*\"`) scopes it to one ecosystem — this is how `match = \"cargo:*\"` above claims\nevery Cargo package and `match = \"npm:*\"` claims every npm package, mirroring the worked\nexample's earlier path-based phrasing, which described intent, not the shipped mechanism.\nA bare pattern that matches the same name across two ecosystems (a same-named Cargo crate\nand npm package with no `ecosystem:` prefix to disambiguate) is a hard config error\n(`BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems`) — add the prefix. This is deliberately a different\naxis from `[[fixed-group]]`/`[[linked-group]]` `members`, which lists exact package names,\nnot a glob.\n\n**Group membership validation, at parse time (P5), not at mutation time**: a package"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":431,"cache_read_input_tokens":806963,"output_tokens":1162,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":344},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":431,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1162,"cache_read_input_tokens":806963,"cache_creation_input_tokens":431,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":431},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce9swiV7F9DzNQXvFzdzM","type":"assistant","uuid":"f5766bea-dba0-43b8-839b-2cc4a7c3ffa9","timestamp":"2026-08-18T08:14:01.996Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"f5766bea-dba0-43b8-839b-2cc4a7c3ffa9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3f6d3ffe-8d7a-40a5-97d2-978434159727","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LjSMNBB96pwzMT3nZL6NTb","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/00-design.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"ee676946-1924-4829-a81d-1029b4efcbed","timestamp":"2026-08-18T08:14:02.060Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/00-design.md","oldString":"Discovery walks the workspace (moon's project graph when available for authoritative\nproject roots, `ignore`-crate walk otherwise — `ProjectLocator`, §0.1/§15); `package-set`\nmatches expand to concrete packages; explicit `[[package]]` entries always win over set\nmatches. A set matching nothing, or two sets claiming the same package, is a hard config\nerror. **Group membership validation, at parse time (P5), not at mutation time**: a package","newString":"Discovery walks the workspace (moon's project graph when available for authoritative\nproject roots, `ignore`-crate walk otherwise — `ProjectLocator`, §0.1/§15); `package-set`\nmatches expand to concrete packages; explicit `[[package]]` entries always win over set\nmatches. A set matching nothing, or two sets claiming the same package, is a hard config\nerror.\n\n**`match` is a glob against the package's name, not its workspace path.** A bare pattern\n(`\"pkg-*\"`) matches that name in any ecosystem; an `ecosystem:` prefix (`\"cargo:pkg-*\"`,\n`\"npm:pkg-*\"`) scopes it to one ecosystem — this is how `match = \"cargo:*\"` above claims\nevery Cargo package and `match = \"npm:*\"` claims every npm package, mirroring the worked\nexample's earlier path-based phrasing, which described intent, not the shipped mechanism.\nA bare pattern that matches the same name across two ecosystems (a same-named Cargo crate\nand npm package with no `ecosystem:` prefix to disambiguate) is a hard config error\n(`BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems`) — add the prefix. This is deliberately a different\naxis from `[[fixed-group]]`/`[[linked-group]]` `members`, which lists exact package names,\nnot a glob.\n\n**Group membership validation, at parse time (P5), not at mutation time**: a package","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1426,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1426,"newLines":20,"lines":[" project roots, `ignore`-crate walk otherwise — `ProjectLocator`, §0.1/§15); `package-set`"," matches expand to concrete packages; explicit `[[package]]` entries always win over set"," matches. A set matching nothing, or two sets claiming the same package, is a hard config","-error. **Group membership validation, at parse time (P5), not at mutation time**: a package","+error.","+","+**`match` is a glob against the package's name, not its workspace path.** A bare pattern","+(`\"pkg-*\"`) matches that name in any ecosystem; an `ecosystem:` prefix (`\"cargo:pkg-*\"`,","+`\"npm:pkg-*\"`) scopes it to one ecosystem — this is how `match = \"cargo:*\"` above claims","+every Cargo package and `match = \"npm:*\"` claims every npm package, mirroring the worked","+example's earlier path-based phrasing, which described intent, not the shipped mechanism.","+A bare pattern that matches the same name across two ecosystems (a same-named Cargo crate","+and npm package with no `ecosystem:` prefix to disambiguate) is a hard config error","+(`BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems`) — add the prefix. This is deliberately a different","+axis from `[[fixed-group]]`/`[[linked-group]]` `members`, which lists exact package names,","+not a glob.","+","+**Group membership validation, at parse time (P5), not at mutation time**: a package"," must belong to at most one `[[fixed-group]]` and at most one `[[linked-group]]`, and the"," fixed and linked member sets must be disjoint — reject with a clear error listing the"," conflicting groups, rather than letting an ambiguous membership surface as a confusing"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f5766bea-dba0-43b8-839b-2cc4a7c3ffa9","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
