{"parentUuid":"14234141-943a-4c39-b74f-d5cf87ac899f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9wxJjbyxm7KjDqQAqaX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016v8P9cEhk2QQXQhbrQUj2W","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/01-spec.md","offset":7175,"limit":85},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1457,"cache_read_input_tokens":839667,"output_tokens":182,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":64},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1457,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":182,"cache_read_input_tokens":839667,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1457,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1457},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce9wxBS4ZdUXAamjHE5Jd","type":"assistant","uuid":"f6054d09-5c6f-411b-96a2-120e7be45513","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:06:24.087Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"f6054d09-5c6f-411b-96a2-120e7be45513","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"85d31ba4-6f8f-48e6-988f-afee4a454cec","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016v8P9cEhk2QQXQhbrQUj2W","type":"tool_result","content":"7175\t\n7176\t    let (severity, governed_by, escalated) = match (kind, effective) {\n7177\t        // ── row 1 ── Runtime / Optional / Build, spec covers ────────────────── none\n7178\t        (Runtime | Optional | Build, Covers) => (Severity::None, None, false),\n7179\t\n7180\t        // ── row 2 ── Runtime / Optional / Build, spec does not cover ───────────\n7181\t        //             bump + spec rewrite; the severity is `bump-severity`'s value,\n7182\t        //             not a constant (§14: `bump-severity` is HOW HARD, `mode` is WHETHER).\n7183\t        (Runtime | Optional | Build, DoesNotCover) =>\n7184\t            (cfg.bump_severity.as_severity(), Some(ConfigKey::CASCADE_BUMP_SEVERITY), false),\n7185\t\n7186\t        // ── row 3 ── Peer, spec covers ──────────────────────────────────────── none\n7187\t        (Peer, Covers) => (Severity::None, None, false),\n7188\t\n7189\t        // ── row 5 ── Peer, genuinely out of range, non-patch source → MAJOR ────\n7190\t        //             §13 invariant 9. Guarded on `coverage`, not `effective`: the invariant's\n7191\t        //             own condition is \"peer-dep **out-of-range** non-patch,\" so\n7192\t        //             `mode = \"always\"` must not manufacture major bumps out of specs that\n7193\t        //             actually cover. Ordered before row 4 so the guard is the discriminator.\n7194\t        (Peer, DoesNotCover)\n7195\t            if cfg.peer_escalation\n7196\t               && matches!(coverage, DoesNotCover)\n7197\t               && matches!(source, Severity::Minor | Severity::Major) =>\n7198\t            (Severity::Major, Some(ConfigKey::CASCADE_PEER_ESCALATION), true),\n7199\t\n7200\t        // ── row 4 ── Peer, out of range, patch source (or escalation opted out) ─\n7201\t        (Peer, DoesNotCover) =>\n7202\t            (cfg.bump_severity.as_severity(), Some(ConfigKey::CASCADE_BUMP_SEVERITY), false),\n7203\t\n7204\t        // ── row 6 ── Dev, either way ─────────── Severity::None, rewrite only ──\n7205\t        //             §13 invariant 10. Dev never bumps under either `mode`: `mode` decides\n7206\t        //             *whether the coverage test gates the cascade*, and this row's outcome\n7207\t        //             does not depend on the coverage test at all.\n7208\t        (Dev, _) => (Severity::None, None, false),\n7209\t    };\n7210\t\n7211\t    // §13 invariant 28: when the bump happened *only* because `mode = \"always\"` overrode a\n7212\t    // spec that genuinely still covers, `cascade.mode` is the key that caused it, and naming\n7213\t    // `cascade.bump-severity` instead would send the user to the knob that decided how hard,\n7214\t    // not the one that decided at all.\n7215\t    let governed_by = match (cfg.mode, coverage, severity) {\n7216\t        (CascadeMode::Always, Covers | Unknown, s) if s != Severity::None =>\n7217\t            Some(ConfigKey::CASCADE_MODE),\n7218\t        _ => governed_by,\n7219\t    };\n7220\t\n7221\t    CascadeDecision { severity, rewrite, governed_by, escalated,\n7222\t                      unknown_coverage: matches!(coverage, Unknown) }\n7223\t}\n7224\t\n7225\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\n7226\tpub struct CascadeDecision {\n7227\t    /// `Severity::None` means \"no version bump\" — row 6's whole point.\n7228\t    pub severity: Severity,\n7229\t    /// Rewrite this dependent's spec for this edge (§7.6 step 6).\n7230\t    pub rewrite: bool,\n7231\t    /// §13 invariant 28's attribution, computed here so `callisto-cli` renders rather than\n7232\t    /// re-derives (P6, §18 Q5.6 item 2).\n7233\t    pub governed_by: Option<ConfigKey>,\n7234\t    /// Peer escalation fired → `BumpReason::PeerEscalation`, not `BumpReason::Cascade`.\n7235\t    pub escalated: bool,\n7236\t    /// Feeds a `RangeNotRoundTrippable` / `CatalogSpecNotRewritten` diagnostic.\n7237\t    pub unknown_coverage: bool,\n7238\t}\n7239\t```\n7240\t\n7241\tRead as §7.4's table:\n7242\t\n7243\t| Edge kind | Coverage | `severity` | `rewrite` |\n7244\t|---|---|---|---|\n7245\t| `Runtime`/`Optional`/`Build` | `Covers` | `None` (`mode = always` → `bump_severity`, governed by `cascade.mode`) | ✗ |\n7246\t| `Runtime`/`Optional`/`Build` | `DoesNotCover` | `bump_severity` | ✓ |\n7247\t| `Peer` | `Covers` | `None` (`mode = always` → `bump_severity`, governed by `cascade.mode`) | ✗ |\n7248\t| `Peer` | `DoesNotCover`, patch source | `bump_severity` | ✓ |\n7249\t| `Peer` | `DoesNotCover`, non-patch source | `Major`, iff `cfg.peer_escalation` | ✓ |\n7250\t| `Dev` | `Covers` | `None` | ✗ |\n7251\t| `Dev` | `DoesNotCover` | `None` | ✓ |\n7252\t\n7253\t> `[SPEC DECISION, not in 00-design.md: `mode = \"always\"` does **not** trigger peer\n7254\t> escalation.]` §7.4's `always` says \"cascade every dependent regardless of range coverage\" and\n7255\t> §13 invariant 9's condition is literally \"peer-dep **out-of-range** non-patch.\" Reading\n7256\t> `always` as also satisfying invariant 9's out-of-range condition would turn a knob documented\n7257\t> as \"forced downstream re-publishes\" into a knob that produces unrequested major bumps across\n7258\t> the workspace — a surprise §18 Q5.4 flags peer-escalation as *already* the sole sanctioned\n7259\t> instance of. Keeping the guard on real coverage is the smaller reading and the more literal"}]},"uuid":"d1291215-2c84-49ab-91a6-812ad0d5402a","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:06:24.171Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/01-spec.md","content":"\n    let (severity, governed_by, escalated) = match (kind, effective) {\n        // ── row 1 ── Runtime / Optional / Build, spec covers ────────────────── none\n        (Runtime | Optional | Build, Covers) => (Severity::None, None, false),\n\n        // ── row 2 ── Runtime / Optional / Build, spec does not cover ───────────\n        //             bump + spec rewrite; the severity is `bump-severity`'s value,\n        //             not a constant (§14: `bump-severity` is HOW HARD, `mode` is WHETHER).\n        (Runtime | Optional | Build, DoesNotCover) =>\n            (cfg.bump_severity.as_severity(), Some(ConfigKey::CASCADE_BUMP_SEVERITY), false),\n\n        // ── row 3 ── Peer, spec covers ──────────────────────────────────────── none\n        (Peer, Covers) => (Severity::None, None, false),\n\n        // ── row 5 ── Peer, genuinely out of range, non-patch source → MAJOR ────\n        //             §13 invariant 9. Guarded on `coverage`, not `effective`: the invariant's\n        //             own condition is \"peer-dep **out-of-range** non-patch,\" so\n        //             `mode = \"always\"` must not manufacture major bumps out of specs that\n        //             actually cover. Ordered before row 4 so the guard is the discriminator.\n        (Peer, DoesNotCover)\n            if cfg.peer_escalation\n               && matches!(coverage, DoesNotCover)\n               && matches!(source, Severity::Minor | Severity::Major) =>\n            (Severity::Major, Some(ConfigKey::CASCADE_PEER_ESCALATION), true),\n\n        // ── row 4 ── Peer, out of range, patch source (or escalation opted out) ─\n        (Peer, DoesNotCover) =>\n            (cfg.bump_severity.as_severity(), Some(ConfigKey::CASCADE_BUMP_SEVERITY), false),\n\n        // ── row 6 ── Dev, either way ─────────── Severity::None, rewrite only ──\n        //             §13 invariant 10. Dev never bumps under either `mode`: `mode` decides\n        //             *whether the coverage test gates the cascade*, and this row's outcome\n        //             does not depend on the coverage test at all.\n        (Dev, _) => (Severity::None, None, false),\n    };\n\n    // §13 invariant 28: when the bump happened *only* because `mode = \"always\"` overrode a\n    // spec that genuinely still covers, `cascade.mode` is the key that caused it, and naming\n    // `cascade.bump-severity` instead would send the user to the knob that decided how hard,\n    // not the one that decided at all.\n    let governed_by = match (cfg.mode, coverage, severity) {\n        (CascadeMode::Always, Covers | Unknown, s) if s != Severity::None =>\n            Some(ConfigKey::CASCADE_MODE),\n        _ => governed_by,\n    };\n\n    CascadeDecision { severity, rewrite, governed_by, escalated,\n                      unknown_coverage: matches!(coverage, Unknown) }\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct CascadeDecision {\n    /// `Severity::None` means \"no version bump\" — row 6's whole point.\n    pub severity: Severity,\n    /// Rewrite this dependent's spec for this edge (§7.6 step 6).\n    pub rewrite: bool,\n    /// §13 invariant 28's attribution, computed here so `callisto-cli` renders rather than\n    /// re-derives (P6, §18 Q5.6 item 2).\n    pub governed_by: Option<ConfigKey>,\n    /// Peer escalation fired → `BumpReason::PeerEscalation`, not `BumpReason::Cascade`.\n    pub escalated: bool,\n    /// Feeds a `RangeNotRoundTrippable` / `CatalogSpecNotRewritten` diagnostic.\n    pub unknown_coverage: bool,\n}\n```\n\nRead as §7.4's table:\n\n| Edge kind | Coverage | `severity` | `rewrite` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Runtime`/`Optional`/`Build` | `Covers` | `None` (`mode = always` → `bump_severity`, governed by `cascade.mode`) | ✗ |\n| `Runtime`/`Optional`/`Build` | `DoesNotCover` | `bump_severity` | ✓ |\n| `Peer` | `Covers` | `None` (`mode = always` → `bump_severity`, governed by `cascade.mode`) | ✗ |\n| `Peer` | `DoesNotCover`, patch source | `bump_severity` | ✓ |\n| `Peer` | `DoesNotCover`, non-patch source | `Major`, iff `cfg.peer_escalation` | ✓ |\n| `Dev` | `Covers` | `None` | ✗ |\n| `Dev` | `DoesNotCover` | `None` | ✓ |\n\n> `[SPEC DECISION, not in 00-design.md: `mode = \"always\"` does **not** trigger peer\n> escalation.]` §7.4's `always` says \"cascade every dependent regardless of range coverage\" and\n> §13 invariant 9's condition is literally \"peer-dep **out-of-range** non-patch.\" Reading\n> `always` as also satisfying invariant 9's out-of-range condition would turn a knob documented\n> as \"forced downstream re-publishes\" into a knob that produces unrequested major bumps across\n> the workspace — a surprise §18 Q5.4 flags peer-escalation as *already* the sole sanctioned\n> instance of. Keeping the guard on real coverage is the smaller reading and the more literal","numLines":85,"startLine":7175,"totalLines":11439}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f6054d09-5c6f-411b-96a2-120e7be45513","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
