{"parentUuid":"be671989-b444-4e70-b7d6-170ad2416e1c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9xMpint97t8wBKu9rCR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review running now. Meanwhile I'll investigate bug 2's full scope (the rewrite-key issue) since it needs more architectural work than the master plan's \"narrow\" framing suggested."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1563,"cache_read_input_tokens":855524,"output_tokens":1658,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1563,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1658,"cache_read_input_tokens":855524,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1563,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1563},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce9xMhYgozGvtC4bC9t78","type":"assistant","uuid":"0ff533cc-1d58-440f-9f0f-6ddce7fc5110","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:11:42.658Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"0ff533cc-1d58-440f-9f0f-6ddce7fc5110","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9xMpint97t8wBKu9rCR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A73qD6M3yfrDZbdCaj4fy9","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Scope the cross-ecosystem rewrite-key fix","subagent_type":"fork","prompt":"Investigate the full scope of Track 9's second bug in the callisto repo at /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto — read-only investigation, do not edit anything.\n\n**The bug**: `crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs` around line 271 builds a `RewriteKey { name: edge.to.name().to_string(), ... }` using `PackageId::name()` directly. This is wrong for a dual-identity (napi-style) package: when rewriting a cross-ecosystem dependency spec (e.g. a Cargo crate's `Cargo.toml` depending on an npm-identified package, or vice versa), the rewrite key's `name` should be the NATIVE name in the TARGET manifest's ecosystem (already computed as `eco` at line 254), not `edge.to`'s own PackageId name (which may be a different ecosystem's spelling). I already confirmed `IdentityIndex::native_name(&self, id: &PackageId, eco: Ecosystem) -> Option<&str>` exists at `crates/callisto-graph/src/identity.rs:493` and is exactly the right lookup — but `cascade.rs`'s `solve_cascade<D: DependencyResolver>` is generic over the `DependencyResolver` trait (defined in `callisto-model`, Layer 1), which cannot expose `IdentityIndex` (a Layer 2 type in `callisto-graph`) without violating this repo's CLAUDE.md layer-isolation invariant. `ManifestWalkResolver` (the concrete resolver used in production) DOES expose `.identity() -> &IdentityIndex` as an inherent method, not a trait method.\n\n**Your job**: map out exactly what changing this requires, concretely:\n1. Does `CascadeInput` (cascade.rs, already has a `tags: &'a TagIndex` field added by an earlier track) need a new `identity: &'a IdentityIndex` field, following the same pattern? Or is there a simpler path — e.g. is `IdentityIndex` accessible some other way already threaded into `solve_cascade`'s scope?\n2. Find ALL real construction sites of `CascadeInput` in production code (grep for `CascadeInput {` outside test modules) — likely `commands/version.rs` and `commands/snapshot.rs`, per Track 1's recent work. For each, check whether `ws.graph` at that call site is concretely `ManifestWalkResolver` (so `.identity()` would be callable) or a generic `D: DependencyResolver` (so it would NOT be callable without a trait bound change).\n3. Find ALL test-only construction sites of `CascadeInput` (in `#[cfg(test)]` modules across `cascade.rs`, `cascade_tests.rs`, and anywhere else) — estimate how many would need updating to supply a new field, similar to how Track 1's `tags` field addition touched 15 sites (7 in cascade.rs's own tests, 6 in cascade_tests.rs, 2 real sites).\n4. Confirm whether `edge.to`'s type and the exact rewrite-key-construction code path (read cascade.rs's `solve_cascade` around lines 253-280 in full) would need `identity.native_name(&edge.to, eco)` substituted in cleanly, and what the correct fallback should be if `native_name` returns `None` (e.g. a package that only has one manifest and `IdentityIndex.native` was never populated for the target ecosystem) — should it fall back to `edge.to.name()` (current buggy-but-safe behavior) or is that itself wrong?\n5. Try to construct or confirm a concrete failing scenario matching the master plan's claim \"crashes `callisto version` outright on an ordinary Cargo+npm co-located package\" — is this still true today given all the Track 3b1/Track 1/Track 2 work that's landed this session? Read `crates/callisto-manifests` or wherever manifest writes actually consume `RewriteKey.name` as a literal manifest key (e.g. does a wrong name cause a \"dependency not found\" error, silently no-op, or genuinely panic/crash?) to ground this claim.\n\nReport back concisely (under 600 words): a clear scope estimate (how many files/call sites touched, whether this is \"narrow single-function\" or closer to Track 1's CascadeInput-threading scope), the exact fix shape for the rewrite-key construction, and whether the \"crashes outright\" claim is still accurate or has changed."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1563,"cache_read_input_tokens":855524,"output_tokens":1658,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1563,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1658,"cache_read_input_tokens":855524,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1563,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1563},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce9xMhYgozGvtC4bC9t78","type":"assistant","uuid":"dc9e04ec-8e91-4538-9afe-2475bddc097e","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:11:58.375Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
