{"parentUuid":"1367e5e4-b19c-45d8-ba64-e8be81b94f7e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9xXDevqFHG32716Ypkp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PsyXJ6dfPXrY2mPyzFh9yc","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"Track 9's second bug (cross-ecosystem rewrite-key) turns out to need CascadeInput-threading work on par with Track 1 (~16 call sites, a new Workspace field), not the \"narrow, single-function\" fix the master plan assumed. How do you want to handle it?","header":"Rewrite-key scope","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Full canon pipeline, same rigor as Track 1 (Recommended)","description":"Given it touches the same architecture Track 1 just hardened and has a real user-visible failure mode (a hard Err aborting apply_version_plan on a real Cargo+npm co-located package), give it a proper spec → plan → implement cycle rather than rushing a patch into code we just spent significant effort getting right."},{"label":"Lighter multi-task plan, skip formal spec","description":"Use vector-planner directly (no canon spec) to break the already-understood fix (add Workspace.identity field, thread through CascadeInput, fix the 2 real + ~14 test call sites) into small TDD tasks, then implement. Faster, less ceremony, but no adversarial spec review."},{"label":"Just land bug 1 for now, defer bug 2","description":"Commit the peer-escalation fix (already done, pending review) and stop there for this track. Revisit the rewrite-key bug in a future session when there's more room for the bigger effort."}]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1232,"cache_read_input_tokens":861253,"output_tokens":575,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1