{"parentUuid":"548c53cc-11f4-4b21-ae47-272e1b616a54","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9yBfeBMekgzbdyXXbMm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01REypo7fd73gUp5DXpnS1ST","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\ncargo fmt -p callisto-graph\ncargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings 2>&1 | tail -15\necho \"---full suite---\"\ncargo test -p callisto-graph 2>&1 | tail -10"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":387,"cache_read_input_tokens":878444,"output_tokens":150,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":387,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":150,"cache_read_input_tokens":878444,"cache_creation_input_tokens":387,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":387},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce9yBXaFd7GE8uKR22pRv","type":"assistant","uuid":"215e2a97-dfec-435f-88cb-43d417a0f2a3","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:22:31.606Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:23:33.856Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a0c97e6812d46e9f9</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a0c97e6812d46e9f9.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Draft Track 9 spec (cascade correctness), retry\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Now I have full grounding. Producing the spec@1 JSON directly.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK9-CASCADE-REWRITE-KEY-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Fix solve_cascade's dependency-spec rewrite-key construction (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs, RewriteKey.name at the site that currently reads `name: edge.to.name().to_string()`, inside the `if d.rewrite { ... }` block around line 269) so that, when the rewrite target is a dual-identity package registered in IdentityIndex under different native names per ecosystem (e.g. a Cargo crate that is also a napi-rs npm package), the key uses the name actually present in the dependent manifest being rewritten -- looked up via IdentityIndex::native_name(&amp;edge.to, eco) where `eco` is the dependent's own already-computed ecosystem -- instead of PackageId::name(), which is the name registered for the dependency's OWN native ecosystem and can differ from what the cross-ecosystem dependent manifest actually wrote. The wrong key is currently passed to callisto-manifests's update_dependency_spec, which returns Err(ManifestError::DependencyNotFound) when the key does not match a real manifest entry, aborting apply_version_plan for the affected package. This spec threads an `&amp;IdentityIndex` through CascadeInput and Workspace so solve_cascade has the data it needs, following the exact precedent set by Track 1's `tags: &amp;TagIndex` threading (SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS): a new required field on CascadeInput, supplied at both real construction sites, sourced from a new field on Workspace populated once at Workspace::load time from the resolver's already-computed IdentityIndex.\",\n  \"scope\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs (CascadeInput struct, the single RewriteKey-construction site inside solve_cascade's `if d.rewrite` block), crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs (Workspace struct and Workspace::load), crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs (plan_version's CascadeInput construction, line 73), crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs (plan_snapshot's CascadeInput construction, line 54), and every test-only CascadeInput struct-literal construction site in crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs's own `#[cfg(test)]` module and crates/callisto-graph/tests/cascade_tests.rs (8 + 6 = 14 sites confirmed by direct grep count as of this spec). No change to IdentityIndex's internal structure, native_name's signature, callisto-manifests's update_dependency_spec, or cascade_action.\",\n  \"non_goals\": [\n    \"Track 1 (fixed-group cascade correctness, already shipped) and any change to the Fixed-group convergence block or GroupTable::resolve's conflict detection -- unrelated code paths in the same file, out of scope for this spec.\",\n    \"Track 2 (platform-manifest writes, already shipped) and any change to plan_version's platform_writes/optional_dep_updates producer logic -- unrelated.\",\n    \"cascade_action's peer-escalation severity fix -- a separate, narrower Track 9 sub-bug already fixed and committed independently in this same session as a lighter-loop change; this spec covers ONLY the rewrite-key bug.\",\n    \"Redesigning IdentityIndex's own internal structure, native_name's signature, or the Layer 1 (callisto-model) / Layer 2 (callisto-graph) boundary itself -- this spec threads existing, already-implemented identity data through to where it is needed; it does not change how identity resolution works or weaken the layer-isolation invariant (IdentityIndex remains a callisto-graph type; it is never exposed through the generic, callisto-model-defined DependencyResolver trait).\",\n    \"Any change to update_dependency_spec or other callisto-manifests write logic -- that crate already correctly errors on an unmatched key; this spec fixes what key gets constructed, not how a key is consumed.\",\n    \"Constructing or exposing an IdentityIndex for any DependencyResolver implementation other than ManifestWalkResolver. Workspace::load is defined only in the `impl&lt;'a, R: CommandRunner&gt; Workspace&lt;'a, R, ManifestWalkResolver&gt;` block (crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs), which is not generic over D, so `graph.identity()` -- a method defined on ManifestWalkResolver itself, not on the DependencyResolver trait -- is callable there without any trait-bound change. A test double implementing DependencyResolver with no identity() method is unaffected by this spec; such tests supply CascadeInput.identity directly as a struct-literal field, per AC-005.\",\n    \"Deduplicating or otherwise changing IdentityIndex.native's insertion/lookup semantics when the same (PackageId, Ecosystem) pair is registered more than once -- native_name's existing first-match iteration order (BTreeMap iteration, deterministic) is used as-is.\"\n  ],\n  \"api_surface\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"CascadeInput.identity\",\n      \"signature\": \"pub identity: &amp;'a IdentityIndex\",\n      \"description\": \"New required field added to CascadeInput (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs; currently 9 fields: graph, groups, cfg, seed, reasons, named_by, base, pre, tags -- none named identity). IdentityIndex is defined in crates/callisto-graph/src/identity.rs and already derives Clone. Required so the RewriteKey-construction site inside solve_cascade's `if d.rewrite { ... }` block can call `input.identity.native_name(&amp;edge.to, eco)`. Both real construction sites must supply it: commands/version.rs's plan_version (`identity: &amp;ws.graph.index` is not accessible -- use `identity: ws.graph.identity()` via ManifestWalkResolver's public `identity(&amp;self) -&gt; &amp;IdentityIndex` accessor, since `ws.graph` is a `ManifestWalkResolver` there) and commands/snapshot.rs's plan_snapshot (same accessor, `ws.graph.identity()`). Every test-only CascadeInput struct literal (8 sites in cascade.rs's test module, 6 sites in tests/cascade_tests.rs) must add an `identity: &amp;IdentityIndex` field -- either `&amp;IdentityIndex::default()` for tests with no dual-identity fixture, or a populated `IdentityIndex` built via its existing test-construction helpers for tests that need native_name to resolve.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Workspace.identity (via ManifestWalkResolver::identity, no new struct field required)\",\n      \"signature\": \"ws.graph.identity() -&gt; &amp;IdentityIndex, called at CascadeInput-construction sites\",\n      \"description\": \"Verified against live code: ManifestWalkResolver already exposes `pub fn identity(&amp;self) -&gt; &amp;IdentityIndex { &amp;self.index }` (crates/callisto-graph/src/resolver.rs). Workspace::load (crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs, the `impl&lt;'a, R: CommandRunner&gt; Workspace&lt;'a, R, ManifestWalkResolver&gt;` block, not generic over D) already computes `graph.identity()` today and uses it inline for `GroupTable::resolve` and `promoted_siblings`. No new field on the Workspace struct itself is required or added by this spec -- plan_version and plan_snapshot each already hold `ws: &amp;Workspace&lt;'_, R, D&gt;` with `ws.graph: D`; since both call sites are monomorphized through Workspace::load's concrete ManifestWalkResolver in every real (non-test-double) call path, `ws.graph.identity()` is callable at both sites without a trait-bound change. This corrects the requirement's premise of adding a dedicated `Workspace.identity: IdentityIndex` field: the existing `ManifestWalkResolver::identity()` accessor already provides the same data with no duplication, and duplicating it as a second field would risk drift between `ws.graph`'s live index and a stale copy. The two real construction sites (version.rs:73, snapshot.rs:54) pass `identity: ws.graph.identity()` directly as the CascadeInput.identity field.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"cascade::solve_cascade (RewriteKey.name construction, corrected)\",\n      \"signature\": \"Inside solve_cascade's existing `if d.rewrite { ... }` block (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs, `match rewrite_spec(...) { RewriteOutcome::Rewritten(to_spec) =&gt; { let key = RewriteKey { ... } ... } }`). solve_cascade's own public signature is unchanged: `pub fn solve_cascade&lt;D: DependencyResolver&gt;(input: CascadeInput&lt;'_, D&gt;) -&gt; Result&lt;CascadeOutcome, GraphError&gt;`.\",\n      \"description\": \"Replace `name: edge.to.name().to_string(),` with `name: input.identity.native_name(&amp;edge.to, eco).map(str::to_string).unwrap_or_else(|| edge.to.name().to_string()),` -- reusing the `eco` binding already computed two lines above in the same block (`let eco = edge.from.ecosystem().unwrap_or_else(|| { ... });`, itself the dependent (`edge.from`) manifest's own ecosystem, falling back to a Cargo.toml/npm filename heuristic when `edge.from` is a PackageId::Bare with no ecosystem tag). `native_name(&amp;self, id: &amp;PackageId, eco: Ecosystem) -&gt; Option&lt;&amp;str&gt;` (crates/callisto-graph/src/identity.rs:493) looks up the name registered for `edge.to` (the rewrite target's PackageId) specifically under `eco` (the dependent's ecosystem) -- the ecosystem-native name as it would appear as a dependency key in a manifest of that ecosystem. When no such registration exists (the common, non-dual-identity case -- no cross-ecosystem identity link was ever established for this target/ecosystem pairing), `native_name` returns `None` and `unwrap_or_else` falls back to `edge.to.name().to_string()`, byte-for-byte identical to today's unconditional expression. Nothing else in the `RewriteKey` construction (`target`, `kind`) or the surrounding `if d.rewrite` block changes.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-001\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given a workspace where IdentityIndex.native registers a dual-identity package D under two different native names for two different ecosystems (e.g. (Cargo, \\\"my-native-lib\\\") -&gt; D and (Npm, \\\"@scope/my-native-lib\\\") -&gt; D), and a dependent package Dep whose manifest is in the ecosystem OTHER than D's Cargo-native registration (i.e. Dep's manifest ecosystem is Npm) declares an out-of-range dependency spec on D that solve_cascade decides to rewrite (Coverage::DoesNotCover), the RewriteKey produced in CascadeOutcome.rewrites has name == \\\"@scope/my-native-lib\\\" (the name registered for D under Npm, Dep's own manifest ecosystem) -- not \\\"my-native-lib\\\" (D's PackageId::name()).\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-002\",\n      \"criterion\": \"AC-001's scenario is exercised through the real, live call path crate::cascade::run_cascade (which calls solve_cascade internally) -- not solely through a direct, isolated call to IdentityIndex::native_name -- confirming the corrected key reaches CascadeOutcome.rewrites via the full cascade fixpoint loop, including the worklist/dependents-of-edge traversal that reaches the rewrite site.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-003\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given a rewrite target package T for which IdentityIndex::native_name(&amp;T, dependent_manifest_ecosystem) returns None (no cross-ecosystem identity registration exists for that specific (T, ecosystem) pairing -- the common, non-dual-identity case covering every package in this repo's existing cascade/rewrite test fixtures), the resulting RewriteKey.name equals T.name() (PackageId::name()) exactly as it did before this fix.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-004\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given the full existing cascade/rewrite test suite (crates/callisto-graph/tests/cascade_tests.rs and crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs's own test module) exercised against workspaces with no dual-identity package anywhere in the workspace, every test's asserted RewriteKey, SpecRewrite, and resulting manifest write is byte-for-byte identical to its pre-fix value -- confirmed by running the existing suite unmodified except for the mechanical addition of the new `identity` field to each CascadeInput struct literal (populated as `&amp;IdentityIndex::default()` for these non-dual-identity fixtures), with zero assertion changes and zero test failures.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-005\",\n      \"criterion\": \"CascadeInput gains a required `identity: &amp;'a IdentityIndex` field. Both real construction sites -- plan_version in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs and plan_snapshot in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs -- are updated to supply it via `ws.graph.identity()`. The crate fails to compile (a testable, observable proposition: `cargo build -p callisto-graph` and `cargo test -p callisto-graph --no-run`) if either site omits the field.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-006\",\n      \"criterion\": \"The end-to-end scenario named in the originating bug report -- a real, on-disk Cargo+npm co-located dual-identity package with a cross-ecosystem dependent whose spec needs rewriting -- proceeds through apply_version_plan (not solve_cascade in isolation) to a successful completion: no Err(ManifestError::DependencyNotFound) is returned, and the dependent's manifest on disk is mutated to contain the corrected, ecosystem-native dependency key with the new version spec written under that key. Before this fix, the identical scenario is confirmed (by direct reproduction) to abort apply_version_plan with Err(ManifestError::DependencyNotFound) for the affected package.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-007\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Given a rewrite target whose PackageId is a PackageId::Bare (no ecosystem tag) with no IdentityIndex.native registration under the dependent manifest's ecosystem, native_name returns None for every ecosystem argument and the fallback in AC-003 applies -- a PackageId::Bare target never causes a panic, unwrap failure, or a different code path than the None-registration case.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    }\n  ],\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK9-CASCADE-REWRITE-KEY-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Verified all load-bearing claims against live code before drafting: RewriteKey construction at cascade.rs (the `if d.rewrite` block, `name: edge.to.name().to_string()`) confirmed present and unchanged; the `eco` binding used for rewrite_spec's ecosystem argument is computed two lines above the RewriteKey construction and is exactly the dependent (edge.from) manifest's own ecosystem -- the correct second argument for native_name per the requirement's own reasoning. IdentityIndex::native_name(&amp;self, id: &amp;PackageId, eco: Ecosystem) -&gt; Option&lt;&amp;str&gt; confirmed at identity.rs:493, derives Clone confirmed on IdentityIndex at line 338. CascadeInput confirmed to currently have 9 fields (graph, groups, cfg, seed, reasons, named_by, base, pre, tags) with tags added by Track 1 as precedent -- reused that exact struct-field-threading pattern. Both real CascadeInput construction sites confirmed at version.rs:73 and snapshot.rs:54. Workspace::load confirmed defined only in the non-generic-over-D impl block (`impl&lt;'a, R: CommandRunner&gt; Workspace&lt;'a, R, ManifestWalkResolver&gt;`), and `graph.identity()` confirmed already called there today for GroupTable::resolve and promoted_siblings -- so no trait-bound change is needed, matching the requirement's claim. One correction made to the requirement's stated design: the requirement asks for a new `Workspace.identity: IdentityIndex` field populated at load time as a copy of graph.identity(); live-code inspection shows ManifestWalkResolver already exposes `identity(&amp;self) -&gt; &amp;IdentityIndex` and Workspace already holds `graph: D` (concretely ManifestWalkResolver at both real call sites), so `ws.graph.identity()` is directly callable at both CascadeInput construction sites without adding any new field to Workspace -- adding a duplicate field would introduce a second copy of the same data with no synchronization guarantee. This spec's api_surface reflects the simpler, non-duplicating approach; the acceptance criteria (AC-005, AC-006) test the observable outcome (CascadeInput.identity correctly populated, end-to-end apply_version_plan success) rather than the specific internal storage mechanism, so this correction does not narrow what the spec commits to. Test-site count (8 in cascade.rs + 6 in cascade_tests.rs = 14) confirmed by direct grep, matching the requirement's ~14 estimate. DependencyNotFound error-return sites in callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs confirmed at lines 308, 341, 349, 697, matching the requirement's citations closely enough (341/349/697 confirmed, 300 was off-by-a-few but the surrounding DependencyNotFound pattern is real and unambiguous).\"\n}\n```\n\nGrounding notes (all verified directly against live code, not paraphrased from the requirement):\n\n- `crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs`: the buggy `RewriteKey { name: edge.to.name().to_string(), ... }` construction is inside `solve_cascade`'s `if d.rewrite { ... }` block; the `eco` binding used for `rewrite_spec` is computed immediately above it and is exactly the dependent (`edge.from`) manifest's own ecosystem — the correct second argument for `native_name`.\n- `crates/callisto-graph/src/identity.rs:493`: `IdentityIndex::native_name(&amp;self, id: &amp;PackageId, eco: Ecosystem) -&gt; Option&lt;&amp;str&gt;` exists and works as described; `IdentityIndex` derives `Clone`.\n- `CascadeInput` (cascade.rs) currently has 9 fields including `tags: &amp;'a TagIndex` (Track 1's precedent for field-threading, reused here).\n- Real construction sites confirmed at `commands/version.rs:73` and `commands/snapshot.rs:54`; 8 test-site literals in `cascade.rs`'s own test module and 6 in `tests/cascade_tests.rs` (14 total, matching the requirement's estimate).\n- `Workspace::load` is defined only in the non-generic-over-D impl block and already calls `graph.identity()` today — confirmed the requirement's premise is correct, but one correction was made: rather than adding a new duplicate `Workspace.identity` field, the spec has both call sites use the already-public `ws.graph.identity()` (from `ManifestWalkResolver::identity()`), avoiding a second, potentially-stale copy of the same data. This is documented in the `reasoning` field.\n- `ManifestError::DependencyNotFound` return sites in `callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs` confirmed at lines 308, 341, 349, 697.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>65233</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>20</tool_uses><duration_ms>184813</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
