{"parentUuid":"ac953260-bb60-498e-8ad7-811599cd9894","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9yaFQnyWgcj1kNSHDPG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015qa2L9wqszd6tiQcu2m4aQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\ngit add crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix(graph): gate peer-dependency escalation on non-patch source severity\n\ncascade_action's peer-dependency escalation ignored its own source: Severity\nparameter (previously named _source), so every out-of-range peer edge\nescalated to Severity::Major regardless of the real upstream change's\nseverity. Per docs/01-spec.md's §7.4/§13 invariant 9 row 5 (already the\ncorrect reference implementation, just not what the shipped code did): only\na non-patch (Minor or Major) source severity should escalate to Major; a\npatch-severity source falls through to row 4 (cfg.bump_severity), same as\nRuntime/Optional/Build's out-of-range row.\n\nTrack 9 (cascade correctness), first of two sub-bugs -- the second\n(cross-ecosystem rewrite-key names) needs CascadeInput-threading work on\npar with Track 1 and is being spec'd separately.\n\nReviewed via independent read-only agent: confirmed against the spec's\nreference pseudocode for all four Severity variants, no sibling call sites\nduplicate this logic, no unsafe introduced, cascade_action's single\nproduction call site (solve_cascade) verified unaffected in the covering\nintegration test.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HxMVynBHufrDkmRHgmKgcH\nEOF\n)\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":229,"cache_read_input_tokens":894525,"output_tokens":553,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemera