{"parentUuid":"6c65895d-045b-4167-aed9-eb4399cc4f56","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9yhk4fwXFANyA1RauYs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GWzah5AY9YNFP1jeg897Dn","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit Track 9 spec quality","subagent_type":"canon:auditor","prompt":"Adversarially audit the spec@1 at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track9-draft.json (id SPEC-TRACK9-CASCADE-REWRITE-KEY-CORRECTNESS, for the callisto Rust monorepo at /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto — fixes a confirmed-live bug where cascade.rs's solve_cascade builds cross-ecosystem dependency-spec rewrite keys from PackageId::name() instead of the target manifest's ecosystem-native name via IdentityIndex::native_name).\n\nRead the full spec fresh from disk. This spec just went through canon-verifier, which found 6 of 7 criteria directly grounded in the source requirement, and flagged AC-007 (a PackageId::Bare no-panic guarantee) as having no direct textual citation in the requirement -- judge whether this is a legitimate, necessary completeness addition (matching your own \"missing error cases\" audit dimension) given that native_name's real signature takes any PackageId including Bare, or whether it should be trimmed/relaxed. The verifier also confirmed a deliberate, evidence-based deviation from the original requirement's stated design (using the already-existing `ws.graph.identity()` accessor instead of adding a new `Workspace.identity` field) is correct against live code -- do not re-litigate that, it's settled; focus your review elsewhere.\n\nCheck the standard five dimensions: untestable/vague acceptance criteria, ambiguous phrasing admitting two valid interpretations, missing error cases for malformed/out-of-range inputs, scope overlap with other workspace specs (.claude/specs/ directory -- particularly SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS.json, which also touches cascade.rs and CascadeInput; confirm no real overlap between Track 1's Fixed-group convergence block and Track 9's rewrite-key fix, since both are in the same file and both add fields to the same struct), and TBDs/incomplete sections. Pay special attention to whether AC-001's fixture description (a dual-identity package registered under two different native names per ecosystem) is precisely specified enough that two competent implementers would construct the same test scenario -- given this session's established pattern of underspecified fixture-construction mechanisms causing exit-gate failures on Track 1 and Track 2's specs, and given IdentityIndex.native is a private/pub(crate) field that a test would need to populate somehow (directly, via a walk, or via a public constructor) -- verify which mechanism is actually available and whether the spec names it.\n\nAlso verify: does the api_surface's proposed fix line (`name: input.identity.native_name(&edge.to, eco).map(str::to_string).unwrap_or_else(|| edge.to.name().to_string()),`) actually compile against native_name's real return type (Option<&str>) -- read identity.rs:493 yourself to confirm the exact signature and that `.map(str::to_string)` is the correct combinator, not e.g. needing `.map(|s| s.to_string())` or a different method entirely for a &str -> String conversion in this position.\n\nFor every issue found, produce a specific rewritten suggested_fix. Output the standard JSON object with issues array and overall pass/fail verdict."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4028,"cache_read_input_tokens":898252,"output_tokens":1613,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":228},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4028,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_g