{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:48:19.753Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ae5b5a78006f4bae1</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/ae5b5a78006f4bae1.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Exit-gate Track 9 spec\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Verdict: FAIL (retry_count 1, confidence high)\n\nVerdict written to `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/verdict-track9-retry1.json`\n\n### All three claimed fixes landed and are internally consistent\n\n1. **Workspace.identity** is a genuine owned field, coherent across purpose, api_surface, AC-005, non_goals[5]. Independently confirmed legal: `crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs:98` opens `impl&lt;'a, R: CommandRunner&gt; Workspace&lt;'a, R, ManifestWalkResolver&gt;` — genuinely not generic over `D` — and `graph.identity()` is already called there at lines 109 and 116.\n2. **AC-007** now asserts a concrete observable outcome instead of the unfalsifiable \"no panic\" framing.\n3. **CascadeInput.identity** now specifies direct `.native` insertion; confirmed that is the only construction mechanism anywhere in the repo (no builder exists).\n\n**No stale `ws.graph.identity()` claims remain.** All three occurrences are framed as non-compiling or attempted-then-corrected. The bare `graph.identity()` in non_goals[5] refers to `Workspace::load`'s own body, where it genuinely is callable — true, not stale.\n\n**The auditor's compile-error finding is confirmed real.** `plan_version&lt;R, D, I&gt;` (`commands/version.rs:24`) and `plan_snapshot&lt;R, D&gt;` (`commands/snapshot.rs:9`) are both generic over `D`; `identity()` is inherent on `ManifestWalkResolver` (`resolver.rs:41`) and the `DependencyResolver` trait (`callisto-model/src/discovery.rs:36-43`) declares only `packages`/`dependencies_of`/`dependents_of`/`diagnostics`. Also verified: the rewrite site and `eco` binding at `cascade.rs:259-283`, the 8+6=14 CascadeInput literal count (all 8 in cascade.rs fall after `mod tests` at :603), `native` genuinely populated per-ecosystem during walk, and no TBDs.\n\n### Two blockers\n\n**1. Scope omits 18 hand-constructed `Workspace` struct literals across 6 unnamed test files.** `Workspace` derives no `Default` and its literals use no rest pattern — `tests/graph_tests.rs:35-43` spells out all 7 fields — and `lib.rs:83-85` documents `pub` on `tags`/`git` expressly so tests hand-construct them. Sites: `validate_command_tests.rs:112,180`; `snapshot_tests.rs:70,132,183,255`; `matrix_tests.rs:63,101`; `graph_tests.rs:35`; `tags_tests.rs:62,172,333,494`; `publish_tests.rs:167,679,742,974,1342`. All 18 stop compiling the moment the field is added. The spec handled the identical hazard for `CascadeInput` with file names, a grep-confirmed count, and per-case fill values, and gave the equally-broad `Workspace` field none of that. Fix is scope enumeration plus the fill value (`identity: IdentityIndex::default()`) — AC-005's `cargo test --no-run` already catches the breakage, so no new criterion is needed.\n\n**2. AC-004 is unsatisfiable as written and contradicts AC-005.** Its exception clause is exclusive — \"unmodified except for the mechanical addition of the new `identity` field to each CascadeInput struct literal\" — but the crate cannot compile unless the 18 `Workspace` literals are also edited. The state AC-004 describes is unreachable, and at that state AC-005's required `cargo test -p callisto-graph --no-run` fails. Fix is rewording the exception clause to name both mechanical edits; the byte-for-byte invariance assertion itself is correct and should stand.\n\nBoth are mechanical and need no new information from the requirement. AC-002 is weak (a test-methodology constraint, and `run_cascade` is a one-line passthrough to `solve_cascade`) but is precise and binary, so I did not fail on it.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>73523</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>23</tool_uses><duration_ms>350159</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
