{"parentUuid":"3cc3d715-61f7-49c6-9a61-1939ba40ca6c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeA1PQwxQ8bh4YQNLcrqC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No — the retry loop isn't a bug I fixed and it came back; it's the exit-gate genuinely finding a new, real problem each round, same as it did for Track 1 and Track 2. To be concrete about what each retry on Track 9 has actually caught:\n\n- **Retry 1** found a real compile error: the spec's design used `ws.graph.identity()` directly, but `plan_version`/`plan_snapshot` are generic over `D`, and that method only exists on the concrete `ManifestWalkResolver` — it genuinely wouldn't have compiled. Fixed by reverting to an actual `Workspace.identity` field.\n- **Retry 2** (running now) is checking two follow-on gaps from that same fix: 18 other places in the test suite construct a `Workspace` by hand and would *also* stop compiling once that field gets added, and one acceptance criterion's wording became self-contradictory once those 18 sites were accounted for.\n\nEach round is catching something that would have been a real broken build if it had gone to implementation. That's the adversarial pipeline doing its job — expensive in back-and-forth, but it's why Track 1 and Track 2 shipped with zero implementation-time surprises. If you'd rather I stop gating this one and just implement it directly, taking the compile risk myself, I can do that instead — just say so."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":90,"cache_read_input_tokens":926871,"output_tokens":1376,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":941},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":90,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1376,"cache_read_inpu