{"parentUuid":"53de9065-ee0d-4e27-ba87-6533f601e836","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeA44vdDmYW6vwD5M1qKC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X24A1uzLDV6As6RoJdYF7s","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Readability pass on onboarding docs","subagent_type":"fork","prompt":"Do a readability/scannability editorial pass on this repo's onboarding-tier docs, per the user's request just now (scope confirmed via AskUserQuestion as \"onboarding docs only\"). This is a writing/editing task, not a code task — do the actual editing yourself, don't just report findings.\n\nExact file list (9 files total):\n- README.md\n- CONTRIBUTING.md\n- ARCHITECTURE.md\n- docs/06-publishing.md\n- docs/release-paradigms.md\n- crates/callisto-cli/README.md\n- crates/callisto-graph/README.md\n- crates/callisto-changelog/README.md\n- crates/callisto-conventional/README.md\n- crates/callisto-format/README.md\n- crates/callisto-manifests/README.md\n- crates/callisto-model/README.md\n- crates/callisto-vcs/README.md\n- crates/callisto-moon/README.md\n\n(That's 5 top-level/docs files + 9 crate READMEs = 14 files. Explicitly OUT of scope: docs/00-design.md and docs/01-spec.md — those are the formal spec pair (13.6k lines combined) this session has been implementing against; do not touch them, do not even read them for reference beyond what's needed to confirm a cross-reference/link target still exists.)\n\nQuality bar, read each file against this checklist:\n1. No AI slop / word salad / filler — cut hedging (\"it's worth noting that\", \"in order to\"), cut throat-clearing intros, cut restating the obvious, cut corporate-speak. Say the thing directly.\n2. No walls of text — break up paragraphs over ~4-5 lines. Use headers, bullets, numbered steps, and tables where they genuinely aid scanning (not decoratively).\n3. No emojis anywhere (CLAUDE.md's project-wide rule — this repo's docs must stay emoji-free).\n4. Diagrams: only add one (Mermaid or ASCII) where a text description of a flow/architecture genuinely is harder to parse than a diagram would be — e.g. ARCHITECTURE.md's layer-isolation invariant or a pipeline flow, if either doc currently describes one in prose. Don't add a diagram just to have one.\n5. Preserve all technical accuracy — do not change any documented behavior, command, flag, or invariant. This is a prose/structure edit, not a content edit. If you spot something that looks factually stale or wrong while reading (a command that no longer exists, a described behavior that contradicts current code), do NOT silently fix the claim — flag it in your final report instead of editing it, since correcting technical claims needs verification against actual code behavior, which is out of scope for this pass.\n6. Keep each doc's actual voice/purpose intact — a crate README's job is a 30-second orientation, not a tutorial; don't inflate a 15-line README into something long. Brevity in the small READMEs IS the correct scannable form already — check whether it actually needs edits before touching it, several may already be fine as-is.\n\nProcess: read each file, decide if it needs work (several of the tiny crate READMEs may already pass and need zero changes — don't churn a file that's already clean), edit the ones that need it directly, use Edit/Write tools. Do not create new files or restructure the doc set (no splitting/merging files) — this pass is prose-and-structure-within-each-existing-file only.\n\nDo NOT touch, read for editing, or otherwise interact with: crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs, crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs, crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs, crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs, or any file under crates/callisto-graph/tests/ — a separate background implementation task (Track 9 cascade rewrite-key fix) is actively editing and committing to those files right now; touching them would conflict.\n\nDo NOT commit anything — leave changes staged/unstaged in the working tree. The coordinating session will review the diff and commit itself once Track 9's background work is clear of the commit history, so a docs-only commit doesn't get interleaved with Track 9's lambda-implementer commits.\n\nWhen done, report back: which files you edited and a one-line reason per file, which files you left untouched and why, and a list of any stale/questionable technical claims you noticed but did not fix (per rule 5)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1546,"cache_read_input_tokens":120866,"output_tokens":2339,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":792},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1546,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2339,"cache_read_input_tokens":120866,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1546,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1546},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeA44uZDt4DXUueiSQPKR","type":"assistant","uuid":"cd65dd77-edb5-4318-995e-12fd3820683f","timestamp":"2026-08-18T10:26:59.740Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
