{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-08-18T10:36:55.910Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aad78369892b8824d</task-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/aad78369892b8824d.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement Track 9 T1\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Working tree is clean, all test binaries compile, and the full `callisto-graph` suite passed green (exit code 0) before committing. Task T1 is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nExecuted T1 from `.claude/plans/PLAN-TRACK9-CASCADE-REWRITE-KEY-CORRECTNESS.json` via TDD:\n\n1. **RED**: Appended `workspace_load_populates_identity_field_from_graph_identity` to `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/tests/ecosystem_bugs_test.rs`. Confirmed it failed to compile with `error[E0609]: no field 'identity' on type 'Workspace&lt;'_, NoopRunner&gt;'` exactly as the plan predicted.\n\n2. **IMPLEMENT**: Added `pub identity: IdentityIndex` field to `Workspace` in `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs`. One deviation from the plan's literal instructions was necessary: the plan said to add `identity: graph.identity().clone(),` after the `manifest_cache,` line in the struct literal, but that ordering caused `error[E0382]: borrow of moved value: 'graph'` because `graph,` (shorthand, a move) was evaluated earlier in the literal. Fixed by computing `let identity = graph.identity().clone();` before the `Ok(Workspace { ... })` block and placing `identity,` last in the literal — same net effect, compiles cleanly.\n\n3. Confirmed the single-test RED→GREEN transition, then ran `cargo test -p callisto-graph --no-run` to surface all 18 broken struct-literal sites across `validate_command_tests.rs`, `snapshot_tests.rs`, `matrix_tests.rs`, `graph_tests.rs`, `tags_tests.rs`, `publish_tests.rs` — matched the plan's enumerated list exactly. Inserted `identity: callisto_graph::IdentityIndex::default(),` after each literal's `manifest_cache: Default::default(),` line.\n\n4. Verified all test binaries compile (`cargo test -p callisto-graph --no-run`, zero errors), ran the full crate test suite (exit code 0, no failures) and `cargo check --workspace` (clean).\n\n5. Committed only the 8 task-relevant files with the plan's exact commit message, using explicit pathspecs to avoid sweeping in unrelated pre-existing staged changes (`README.md`, `docs/release-paradigms.md`).\n\nFiles touched: `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/tests/{ecosystem_bugs_test,graph_tests,matrix_tests,publish_tests,snapshot_tests,tags_tests,validate_command_tests}.rs`.\n\nCommit: `f265ff0d351bec24021178cdec4f5e4b7c946b24`\n\nOne environment note: immediately after my commit, a second commit `e25b18bd` appeared bearing an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer, reusing my commit message text but actually containing unrelated pre-existing staged changes (`README.md`, `docs/release-paradigms.md`). This appears to be an automatic checkpoint system in this environment, not an action I took — I did not stage or commit those files. Flagging for visibility since it produces a slightly misleading commit message on unrelated content.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"T1\",\n  \"status\": \"done\",\n  \"steps_completed\": [\n    \"RED: added workspace_load_populates_identity_field_from_graph_identity test, confirmed E0609 missing-field compile failure\",\n    \"IMPLEMENT: added pub identity: IdentityIndex field to Workspace struct\",\n    \"IMPLEMENT: populated identity via graph.identity().clone() in Workspace::load (computed before graph move, to fix a plan-literal ordering issue)\",\n    \"GREEN: single new test compiles and passes\",\n    \"Surfaced all 18 E0063 missing-field errors via cargo test -p callisto-graph --no-run, matched plan's enumerated list\",\n    \"Fixed all 18 hand-constructed Workspace struct literals with identity: callisto_graph::IdentityIndex::default()\",\n    \"Confirmed cargo test -p callisto-graph --no-run compiles with zero errors\",\n    \"Ran full cargo test -p callisto-graph suite: all passed, exit code 0\",\n    \"Ran cargo check --workspace: clean\",\n    \"Committed exactly the 8 task files with plan's commit message\"\n  ],\n  \"test_result\": \"pass\",\n  \"commit_sha\": \"f265ff0d351bec24021178cdec4f5e4b7c946b24\",\n  \"concerns\": \"Plan step 4 specified adding `identity: graph.identity().clone(),` after manifest_cache in the struct literal; this ordering fails to compile (E0382 borrow of moved value `graph`) because `graph,` shorthand moves the field earlier in the same literal. Resolved by binding `let identity = graph.identity().clone();` before the Ok(Workspace{...}) construction and placing `identity,` as the last field in the literal instead -- same semantics, compiles cleanly. Also: an automatic checkpoint commit (e25b18bd, tagged Entire-Checkpoint) appeared immediately after my commit, reusing my commit message on unrelated pre-existing staged changes (README.md, docs/release-paradigms.md) that I did not stage or intend to commit -- appears to be an environment-level auto-checkpoint feature, not an action taken by this agent.\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"T1 has covers_criteria: [] per the plan (pure scaffolding task), so no criteria_evidence is required or applicable. Followed plan steps precisely except for the one compile-order fix noted above, which was necessary to make the plan's own specified change compile at all -- verified empirically via the actual E0382 compiler error rather than assumed.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>78218</subagent_tokens><tool_us