{"parentUuid":"45f623ca-7e75-485c-a8e6-c5d32541ace0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeA4s17Ng6MGB9TMqRdDq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Mystery solved — no data was lost or corrupted, but the commit history is mislabeled. Here's exactly what happened:\n\n- T1's background implementer *did* finish and commit correctly as `f265ff0d` (the real code: `lib.rs` + 6 test files) while I was independently re-verifying the same work.\n- By the time my own `git commit` ran, those 7 files were already committed (nothing left to stage for them), but `README.md` and `docs/release-paradigms.md` were still sitting staged in the index from the earlier blocked docs-commit attempt. So my commit went through against *that* diff instead — landing as `e25b18bd`, which carries the docs changes but my Track-9/Workspace.identity commit message.\n\nNet effect: **all content is correct and nothing is lost** — it's purely two commit messages/diffs mismatched. `f265ff0d` (T1's real diff) has only a bare title with no body; `e25b18bd` (the docs diff) has my detailed Track-9 message.\n\nBoth commits are local and unpushed (`main` is 208 ahead of `origin/main`), so fixing this is safe, but it requires amending `e25b18bd` (the most recent commit) — which your standing git-safety rule says I should never do without explicit request."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6005,"cache_read_input_tokens":148424,"output_tokens":3589,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2759},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6005,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3589,"cache_read_input_tokens":148424,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6005,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_