{"parentUuid":"74e297ab-7ffd-4073-a686-a78a76662b3b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCFktBnCChtZzoJwFvvB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GNnamGDhi7ZGPunD4ifwbK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix(graph): use the dependent's ecosystem-native identity for RewriteKey.name in solve_cascade\n\nTrack 9 (rewrite-key correctness) T3/6: solve_cascade's RewriteKey.name\nwas built from PackageId::name() unconditionally, which is the target's\nown native-ecosystem registration -- wrong when the target is a\ndual-identity (napi-style) package registered under different names per\necosystem (e.g. Cargo \"my-native-lib\" vs npm \"@scope/my-native-lib\").\nA cross-ecosystem rewrite onto such a target targeted the wrong manifest\nkey, crashing callisto version on an ordinary Cargo+npm co-located\npackage.\n\nNow looks up input.identity.native_name(&edge.to, eco) first -- the\nname registered for the dependent's own ecosystem -- falling back to\nPackageId::name() when no cross-ecosystem registration exists (the\ncommon case, byte-identical to the old behavior).\n\nCovers AC-001, AC-002. Full callisto-graph suite: 379 passed, 0 failed\n-- no regressions in any existing non-dual-identity fixture.\nEOF\n)\"\ngit log --oneline -6","description":"Commit T3"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":217,"cache_read_input_tokens":177832,"output_tokens":518,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":217,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":518,"cache_read_input_tokens":177832,"cache_creation_input_tokens":