{"parentUuid":"93d986a4-3f78-44d4-8d4e-92c4959e8f2c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCJ2sw5SteENhV7BCRhf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Track 9 is complete.** Both cascade.rs bugs are fixed, tested, and committed:\n\n- **Peer-escalation bug**: fixed earlier this session (`a7007d9`).\n- **Cross-ecosystem rewrite-key bug**: full canon→vector→lambda pipeline just finished — `f265ff0d` through `ca2aa550` (6 tasks), covering all 7 acceptance criteria. Full `callisto-graph` suite: 471 passed / 0 failed. Workspace-wide `clippy` and `fmt` clean.\n\nAlso landed this session: a readability pass on the onboarding docs (`63857f7`) — tightened README's comparison section and a stale \"zero-risk\" claim in release-paradigms.md; the other 12 docs in scope were already clean.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: while resolving T1's commit, I hit a case where an automatic checkpoint system in this environment (visible via `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers) raced with my own commit and briefly mismatched a commit message against its diff — I caught it, confirmed no content was lost, and fixed it with your approval. It resurfaced as a minor note on T4 too (correctly self-diagnosed by that task's implementer, no actual problem). Worth being aware this checkpoint mechanism can interleave with concurrent background commits.\n\n`ACTIVE.md` is updated to reflect Track 9 as done. Ready for next steps whenever you want to point me at the next track."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":750,"cache_read_input_tokens":204833,"output_tokens":493,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":750,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":