{"parentUuid":"e25b6c76-0c1e-479f-96bf-26cda91a6e70","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCMgppxNnCiYQdNEPf89","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have solid, verified evidence for Track 4's Rust-side bugs. Per the master plan, Track 4 gets the full canon pipeline while Track 6-mechanical (7 report field-shape fixes) gets a lighter TDD loop — different rigor tiers, so I'll handle them separately but in parallel: drafting Track 4's spec now, and forking off research into Track 6-mechanical's exact field-shape mismatches concurrently."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1183,"cache_read_input_tokens":227815,"output_tokens":4902,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2191},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1183,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4902,"cache_read_input_tokens":227815,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1183,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1183},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCMgoVarStjFXXrexDVv","type":"assistant","uuid":"b80fa1d5-eb26-47bb-859d-99a3769408c6","timestamp":"2026-08-19T15:39:12.394Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"b80fa1d5-eb26-47bb-859d-99a3769408c6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCMgppxNnCiYQdNEPf89","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W5QrzM9YA938vUGxKVNVH8","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Draft Track 4 canon spec","subagent_type":"canon:drafter","prompt":"Workspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto. Draft a spec@1 for \"Track 4: Release-Pipeline / CI Action Contract Correctness\" from this requirement@1. Do the drafting work yourself and return the spec@1 object directly.\n\nrequirement@1:\n{\n  \"id\": \"REQ-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"statement\": \"Fix four confirmed-live correctness bugs spanning the release pipeline's CLI-to-Action contract, so the shipped GitHub Action actually reaches its release-PR-creation and publish paths on real runs instead of erroring out or silently corrupting reported state.\",\n  \"stakeholder\": \"Users of the callisto-action GitHub Action and the `callisto` CLI's release/tag/publish commands\",\n  \"why\": \"All four bugs were confirmed live against current code this session. Bug 1 is the most severe: it makes the Action's release-PR-creation path unreachable on every real run where it should fire.\",\n  \"done_when\": [\n    \"The shipped Action script (.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml) correctly branches on `callisto status --check`'s real, already-correct CLI contract (1 = pending changesets, 2 = none pending, never 0) instead of its current wrong assumption that exit 0 means 'has pending changesets' -- confirmed live: the current script's `if [[ $STATUS_EXIT -eq 0 ]]; then HAS_CHANGESETS=true` branch is dead code (status --check never returns 0), and the real 'has pending changesets' case (exit 1) instead falls into the script's error-and-abort else-branch, aborting the entire workflow instead of proceeding to release-PR creation.\",\n    \"The Action script's exit-code branching is also robust to clap's own usage-error exit code (2) colliding with 'no changesets pending' (also 2) -- a CLI invocation typo must not be silently reinterpreted as 'workspace clean, proceed to publish'.\",\n    \"crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's top-of-file exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` command is corrected -- it currently reads '0 when no errors and (no --check OR at least one pending changeset)', which contradicts the actual, already-correct implementation in crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/status.rs (check_exit_code_raw: 1 for pending, 2 for none-pending; --check mode never returns 0 regardless of pending state).\",\n    \"`callisto tag` (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs) no longer reports a fabricated `sha` in its CreatedTag output when a tag already exists at a commit different from the requested target -- confirmed live: create_tags_with_options's `if !already_existed { git.create_tag(...) }` branch correctly skips re-tagging, but every push to the `tags` vec (both the already-existed and newly-created paths, e.g. lines ~106 and ~116) unconditionally reports `sha: release.sha.clone()` (the *requested* sha), not the tag's actual real target commit -- so a tag that already existed at a stale/different commit is reported as if it points to the newly-requested sha.\",\n    \"is_error_case: true -- when `callisto tag` finds a tag already existing at a commit that does NOT match the requested release.sha, this must be surfaced as an observable, distinguishable outcome (either the reported sha reflects the tag's true existing target, or an explicit error/warning is surfaced) rather than silently fabricating agreement.\",\n    \"`plan_publish` (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs:427) populates `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` from the package's real CHANGELOG.md content via the already-implemented, already-tested `callisto_changelog::extract_section` function, instead of always hardcoding `None` -- confirmed live via grep: `extract_section` is defined and unit-tested in crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs but has zero call sites anywhere in production code.\",\n    \"is_error_case: true -- when a package's CHANGELOG.md does not exist, or exists but has no section for the version being released, `changelog_section` must remain `None` (not panic, not error the whole plan) -- this is the existing, correct behavior for the not-yet-generated-changelog case and must not regress.\",\n    \"All four fixes are verified against the actual current file/line locations cited above (re-confirm each against live code before implementing, since code may have shifted since this requirement was written).\",\n    \"No JSON wire-format schemaVersion bump is required for any of these four fixes -- none of them change a report type's field shape (add/remove/rename a field); they correct exit-code logic (bugs 1-2), a stale doc comment (folded into bug 1's fix), a misreported value using an already-existing field (bug 3), and populate an already-existing Option<String> field with real data instead of a hardcoded None (bug 4).\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"Track 6-mechanical's JSON report field-shape mismatches (StatusReport, StatusPackageRecord, SnapshotReport, ComposePrBodyReport, CreatedTag's other fields, InitReport, ValidateReport) -- a separate, already-scoped track using a lighter TDD loop, not this spec.\",\n    \"Any change to callisto-model's SCHEMA_VERSION constant or any report type's field shape.\",\n    \"The `callisto publish` command's actual registry-publishing logic (cargo/npm/pypi clients) -- untouched by this track.\",\n    \"Any change to how the Action script handles `plan-publish`'s or `matrix`'s JSON output beyond what's needed for the status-check branching fix -- those are separate `jq` parse sites already confirmed working correctly.\"\n  ]\n}\n\nContext you should verify directly against live code before finalizing acceptance criteria (do not trust the requirement's file:line citations blindly -- they were confirmed moments ago but re-verify): crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/status.rs (check_exit_code_raw, handle), crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs (top-of-file doc comment), .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml (the \"1. Inspecting Workspace Status\" step, lines roughly 75-97), crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs (create_tags_with_options), crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs (plan_publish, changelog_section construction around line 427), crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs (extract_section's actual signature).\n\nThis project's rigor precedent (see .claude/plans/ACTIVE.md for prior tracks' canon-exit-gate history): acceptance criteria must be falsifiable observable-behavior propositions, no internal-implementation-knowledge criteria, error cases carry is_error_case: true, no TBDs. The Action-script fix (bash, not Rust) needs criteria a tester could verify by reading the script's branching logic against the documented exit codes and/or by constructing a repro (mocking `callisto status --check`'s exit code and observing the script's branch taken) -- state clearly how each Action-script criterion is meant to be tested/reviewed, since this isn't cargo-test-shaped like the Rust criteria."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1183,"cache_read_input_tokens":227815,"output_tokens":4902,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2191},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1183,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4902,"cache_read_input_tokens":227815,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1183,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1183},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCMgoVarStjFXXrexDVv","type":"assistant","uuid":"5879e7c0-2c9e-46a4-8c0d-f9fde0ac743b","timestamp":"2026-08-19T15:39:37.498Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
