{"parentUuid":"b6f652cc-971d-4d18-b891-bcd3bed76187","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCMkoEaCDbvgEpDQyfXs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ThfTKtu8fxwEdvntkPCMNd","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Research Track 6-mechanical field mismatches","subagent_type":"fork","prompt":"Research-only task (read-only, no edits) — do this concurrently while a separate agent drafts Track 4's canon spec (different files, no overlap: Track 4 touches status.rs/tag.rs/publish.rs's changelog_section/main.rs/action.yml; you are auditing report.rs's field shapes and each report's construction sites).\n\nTrack 6-mechanical (per the master remediation plan) is: 7 report types in crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs — StatusReport, StatusPackageRecord, SnapshotReport, ComposePrBodyReport, CreatedTag, InitReport, ValidateReport — that an earlier adversarial audit found have field-shape mismatches (missing fields, renamed JSON keys, wrong optionality) against the documented wire contract in docs/01-spec.md. The audit's original artifact isn't available to me directly anymore, so I need you to independently re-derive the actual current mismatches by comparing live code against the live spec doc.\n\nFor EACH of the 7 report types, do this:\n1. Read the struct definition in crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs (exact fields, types, serde attributes — rename/skip_serializing_if/flatten etc).\n2. Find and read every real production construction site (grep for `StatusReport {`, `StatusPackageRecord {`, etc. across crates/callisto-graph/src/ and crates/callisto-cli/src/ — exclude test files) to see what's actually populated at runtime.\n3. Find the corresponding documented JSON contract in docs/01-spec.md (search for the report's name, its field list, any JSON example blocks) — read the actual documented shape/field names/types/optionality.\n4. Diff (2)/(1) against (3): report any field present in the doc but missing from the struct, any field in the struct with a different JSON key (via #[serde(rename)]) than what the doc documents, any field whose documented optionality (required vs optional/nullable) doesn't match the struct's Option<T> vs T, and any field the doc omits entirely that the struct/construction site produces.\n5. Also check the two real jq-consuming sites in .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml (`.platformTargets[].targets[].artifactName` from MatrixReport, `.releases[].tagName` from plan-publish's PublishPlan) — confirm neither of those two paths is affected by any of the 7 report types' mismatches you find (they're a different report type, MatrixReport/PublishPlan, already handled by a separate track/decision — just confirm no accidental overlap).\n\nAlso check the already-resolved wire-format decision from earlier this session: \"Bump schemaVersion for MatrixReport + the plan-publish report (PublishPlan); correctness-fix the rest\" — meaning every mismatch you find in these 7 report types should be fixable as a pure correctness fix (no schemaVersion bump), since none of these 7 are MatrixReport or PublishPlan. If you find a mismatch that seems to genuinely require a breaking field-shape change (not just \"populate an existing field correctly\" or \"rename a field to match docs\"), flag it explicitly as a possible exception to that assumption rather than silently treating it as a simple correctness fix.\n\nReport back, per report type: the specific mismatch(es) found (field name, doc says X, code says Y, file:line for both), or \"no mismatch found, matches docs\" if it's already correct — several of the 7 may already be fine given how much has been fixed this session already. Keep the report structured and concrete (exact field names, exact file:line citations) since this will directly become the input to a lighter-TDD-loop fix pass, one report/field at a time."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5325,"cache_read_input_tokens":228998,"output_tokens":1338,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5325,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1338,"cache_read_input_tokens":228998,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5325},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCMkn67YN9qJ79zjKXas","type":"assistant","uuid":"4d21c298-5f26-44b7-90cf-5bd796250352","timestamp":"2026-08-19T15:39:55.189Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
