{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-19T15:41:37.698Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a205f474396d49247</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01ThfTKtu8fxwEdvntkPCMNd</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a205f474396d49247.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Research Track 6-mechanical field mismatches\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>This is a research-only task: comparing 7 report types (`report.rs`) against their documented wire contract (`docs/01-spec.md` §M.12.4–M.12.6) plus construction-site checks. No edits made.\n\n**Confirmed: no overlap** with MatrixReport/PublishPlan — the Action's only two `jq` sites (`.platformTargets[].targets[].artifactName`, `.releases[]?.tagName`) are untouched by anything below.\n\n**IMPORTANT CROSS-TRACK FINDING:** `TagReport`/`CreatedTag`'s mismatch is the *same underlying defect* as Track 4's \"tag fabricated-sha\" bug — `tag.rs:82` already computes `let already_existed = ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str);` but the value is discarded; the doc's `CreatedTag` shape already specifies the fix (`already_existed: bool`, with explicit rationale: \"An existing tag at a different sha is an error diagnostic, not a silent overwrite\"). Whichever track lands first should own this field; the other must not duplicate it.\n\n---\n\n### StatusReport / StatusPackageRecord — MISMATCH (report.rs:298–336 vs spec:1883–1934)\n- `has_changesets: bool` — **doc says mandatory** (\"§12.5 mandates `.hasChangesets`; the field the Action's mode dispatch reads\") — **entirely missing from the struct**.\n- Doc's `StatusEntry` (renamed `StatusPackageRecord` in code, harmless) is missing `last_released_version: Option&lt;Version&gt;` and `release_trigger: ReleaseTrigger` — both absent from code.\n- `changed_since_last_tag: bool` — doc says \"Mandatory... v0.1 reports the fact\" (always serialized); code has `skip_serializing_if = \"std::ops::Not::not\"`, silently omitting the field from JSON when `false`.\n- Code has an extra field not in the doc: `pending_changesets: Vec&lt;String&gt;`.\n- Construction sites: `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/status.rs:105`, `crates/callisto-cli/src/render/mod.rs:311`.\n\n### SnapshotReport — MAJOR MISMATCH, likely exception (report.rs:339–348 vs spec:1938–1962)\n- Doc: `version: Version` + `packages: Vec&lt;SnapshotPackage{name, ecosystem}&gt;`.\n- Code: `snapshot_tag: String` + `bumps: Vec&lt;BumpRecord&gt;` — **completely different field names, types, and shapes**, not a rename-level fix.\n- **Flagging as likely exception**: this isn't \"populate a field correctly,\" it's two top-level fields with different names *and* different types/semantics. Construction site: `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs:146`.\n\n### ComposePrBodyReport — MISMATCH, borderline exception (report.rs:363–371 vs spec:1971–2018)\n- `body` (doc) vs `pr_body` (code) → JSON key `body` vs `prBody` — a rename, not additive.\n- `metadata: PrBodyMetadata` (labels/managed_labels/overflow — a whole label-tracking subsystem) is **entirely absent** from code.\n- Flagging: the rename is a breaking change; the missing `metadata` object is more than a one-line fix. Construction sites: `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs:74,237`.\n\n### ValidateReport — MISMATCH (report.rs:386–394 vs spec:2035–2045)\n- `ok` (doc) vs `valid` (code) → JSON key rename.\n- `diagnostics` — doc says mandatory/always-present here specifically (\"entire payload *is* its diagnostics\"); code has `skip_serializing_if = \"Vec::is_empty\"`, contradicting that. Construction site: `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/validate.rs:143`.\n\n### TagReport / CreatedTag — MISMATCH, shares root cause with Track 4 (report.rs:409–437 vs spec:2049–2067)\n- `tags` (doc) vs `created_tags` (code) → JSON key rename.\n- `CreatedTag`: doc has `already_existed: bool` (missing from code — see cross-track finding above); code has an extra `package: PackageId` field not in the doc. Construction sites: `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs:65,74,103,113,120`.\n\n### InitReport — MOST DIVERGENT, definite exception (report.rs:440–461 vs spec:2071–2087)\n- Near-zero field overlap beyond `schema_version`/`diagnostics`. Doc: `locator: String`, `packages: Vec&lt;InitPackage&gt;`, `written: Vec&lt;PathBuf&gt;`, `proposed_config: Option&lt;String&gt;`. Code: `initialized: bool`, `config_path: PathBuf`, `diff: InitDiff{new_ecosystems, applied}` — none of these four exist in the other's shape.\n- This reads as a genuine design evolution the docs never caught up with (same category as the Track 3a/6-doc/8-doc precedent), not a mechanical correctness fix — **recommend routing through a doc-correction-first check** (confirm which design actually shipped and is intended) before treating this as \"correctness-fix, no version bump.\" Construction site: `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/init.rs:190`.\n\n**Net assessment against the resolved decision** (\"correctness-fix the rest, no schemaVersion bump for these 7\"): StatusReport's fixes are genuinely additive/correctness-shaped and fit the decision cleanly. SnapshotReport, ComposePrBodyReport's `body` rename, ValidateReport's `ok` rename, TagReport's `tags` rename, and InitReport all involve **renaming or wholesale-replacing existing fields**, not just adding missing ones — each is a real break for any existing consumer parsing the old key. Worth a quick decision-owner check on whether the \"no version bump\" assumption survives contact with these five before implementation starts.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>265209</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>6</tool_uses><duration_ms>98573</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
