{"parentUuid":"0f486a54-f175-4935-b156-2071a4a60d95","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fdaeeb64-6a81-44ef-90ec-7d96be1228b8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a205f474396d49247</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01ThfTKtu8fxwEdvntkPCMNd</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a205f474396d49247.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Research Track 6-mechanical field mismatches\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>This is a research-only task: comparing 7 report types (`report.rs`) against their documented wire contract (`docs/01-spec.md` §M.12.4–M.12.6) plus construction-site checks. No edits made.\n\n**Confirmed: no overlap** with MatrixReport/PublishPlan — the Action's only two `jq` sites (`.platformTargets[].targets[].artifactName`, `.releases[]?.tagName`) are untouched by anything below.\n\n**IMPORTANT CROSS-TRACK FINDING:** `TagReport`/`CreatedTag`'s mismatch is the *same underlying defect* as Track 4's \"tag fabricated-sha\" bug — `tag.rs:82` already computes `let already_existed = ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str);` but the value is discarded; the doc's `CreatedTag` shape already specifies the fix (`already_existed: bool`, with explicit rationale: \"An existing tag at a different sha is an error diagnostic, not a silent overwrite\"). Whichever track lands first should own this field; the other must not duplicate it.\n\n---\n\n### StatusReport / StatusPackageRecord — MISMATCH (report.rs:298–336 vs spec:1883–1934)\n- `has_changesets: bool` — **doc says mandatory** (\"§12.5 mandates `.hasChangesets`; the field the Action's mode dispatch reads\") — **entirely missing from the struct**.\n- Doc's `StatusEntry` (renamed `StatusPackageRecord` in code, harmless) is missing `last_released_version: Option&lt;Version&gt;` and `release_trigger: ReleaseTrigger` — both absent from code.\n- `changed_since_last_tag: bool` — doc says \"Mandatory... v0.1 reports the fact\" (always serialized); code has `skip_serializing_if = \"std::ops::Not::not\"`, silently omitting the field from JSON when `false`.\n- Code has an extra field not in the doc: `pending_changesets: Vec&lt;String&gt;`.\n- Construction sites: `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/status.rs:105`, `crates/callisto-cli/src/render/mod.rs:311`.\n\n### SnapshotReport — MAJOR MISMATCH, likely exception (report.rs:339–348 vs spec:1938–1962)\n- Doc: `version: Version` + `packages: Vec&lt;SnapshotPackage{name, ecosystem}&gt;`.\n- Code: `snapshot_tag: String` + `bumps: Vec&lt;BumpRecord&gt;` — **completely different field names, types, and shapes**, not a rename-level fix.\n- **Flagging as likely exception**: this isn't \"populate a field correctly,\" it's two top-level fields with different names *and* different types/semantics. Construction site: `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs:146`.\n\n### ComposePrBodyReport — MISMATCH, borderline exception (report.rs:363–371 vs spec:1971–2018)\n- `body` (doc) vs `pr_body` (code) → JSON key `body` vs `prBody` — a rename, not additive.\n- `metadata: PrBodyMetadata` (labels/managed_labels/overflow — a whole label-tracking subsystem) is **entirely absent** from code.\n- Flagging: the rename is a breaking change; the missing `metadata` object is more than a one-line fix. Construction sites: `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs:74,237`.\n\n### ValidateReport — MISMATCH (report.rs:386–394 vs spec:2035–2045)\n- `ok` (doc) vs `valid` (code) → JSON key rename.\n- `diagnostics` — doc says mandatory/always-present here specifically (\"entire payload *is* its diagnostics\"); code has `skip_serializing_if = \"Vec::is_empty\"`, contradicting that. Construction site: `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/validate.rs:143`.\n\n### TagReport / CreatedTag — MISMATCH, shares root cause with Track 4 (report.rs:409–437 vs spec:2049–2067)\n- `tags` (doc) vs `created_tags` (code) → JSON key rename.\n- `CreatedTag`: doc has `already_existed: bool` (missing from code — see cross-track finding above); code has an extra `package: PackageId` field not in the doc. Construction sites: `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs:65,74,103,113,120`.\n\n### InitReport — MOST DIVERGENT, definite exception (report.rs:440–461 vs spec:2071–2087)\n- Near-zero field overlap beyond `schema_version`/`diagnostics`. Doc: `locator: String`, `packages: Vec&lt;InitPackage&gt;`, `written: Vec&lt;PathBuf&gt;`, `proposed_config: Option&lt;String&gt;`. Code: `initialized: bool`, `config_path: PathBuf`, `diff: InitDiff{new_ecosystems, applied}` — none of these four exist in the other's shape.\n- This reads as a genuine design evolution the docs never caught up with (same category as the Track 3a/6-doc/8-doc precedent), not a mechanical correctness fix — **recommend routing through a doc-correction-first check** (confirm which design actually shipped and is intended) before treating this as \"correctness-fix, no version bump.\" Construction site: `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/init.rs:190`.\n\n**Net assessment against the resolved decision** (\"correctness-fix the rest, no schemaVersion bump for these 7\"): StatusReport's fixes are genuinely additive/correctness-shaped and fit the decision cleanly. SnapshotReport, ComposePrBodyReport's `body` rename, ValidateReport's `ok` rename, TagReport's `tags` rename, and InitReport all involve **renaming or wholesale-replacing existing fields**, not just adding missing ones — each is a real break for any existing consumer parsing the old key. Worth a quick decision-owner check on whether the \"no version bump\" assumption survives contact with these five before implementation starts.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>265209</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>6</tool_uses><duration_ms>98573</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"7975d995-645f-49cc-8013-11ff2ffb3188","timestamp":"2026-08-19T15:41:37.717Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-19T15:42:42.510Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a2ff2926b141bc427</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Bu3JJHiQbH1ovz4UH7mVKi</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a2ff2926b141bc427.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Draft Track 4 canon spec (redo)\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Now producing the final spec@1 JSON.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Correct four confirmed-live correctness bugs in the release pipeline's CLI-to-Action contract so the shipped GitHub Action reliably reaches release-PR-creation and publish on real runs, instead of erroring out on the normal 'pending changesets' case or silently reporting fabricated state (a stale tag sha, a missing changelog excerpt).\",\n  \"scope\": \"Four fixes, all within the callisto CLI/graph crates and the composite Action script: (1) .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's `callisto status --check` exit-code branching in the 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step; (2) crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's top-of-file exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` subcommand; (3) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs's `create_tags_with_options`, specifically the `sha` field written into every `CreatedTag` pushed to the `tags` vec; (4) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs's `plan_publish`, specifically the `changelog_section` field on `ReleaseEntry` (currently hardcoded `None`), which must be populated via `callisto_changelog::extract_section` (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102) reading each package's `CHANGELOG.md` from its resolved `pkg_dir`.\",\n  \"non_goals\": [\n    \"Track 6-mechanical's JSON report field-shape mismatches (StatusReport, StatusPackageRecord, SnapshotReport, ComposePrBodyReport, CreatedTag's other fields, InitReport, ValidateReport) -- separate track, not touched here.\",\n    \"Any change to callisto-model's SCHEMA_VERSION constant or any report type's field shape -- all four fixes reuse existing fields (CreatedTag.sha, ReleaseEntry.changelog_section) or correct logic/prose, none add, remove, or rename a field.\",\n    \"The `callisto publish` command's actual registry-publishing logic (cargo/npm/pypi clients) -- untouched.\",\n    \"Any change to how the Action script parses `plan-publish`'s or `matrix`'s JSON output via `jq`, beyond the status-check exit-code branching fix -- those jq parse sites are already confirmed working and out of scope.\",\n    \"Adding a dedicated CLI flag or new exit code to distinguish clap usage errors (exit 2) from 'no changesets pending' (exit 2) at the `callisto` binary level -- clap's own exit-code convention is not renegotiated by this track; the fix for the collision lives entirely in the Action script's ability to tell the two apart using information already available to it (stderr content and/or the already-distinct exit code 1 vs 2 contract), not by changing what the CLI emits.\",\n    \"Any change to `callisto status`'s non-`--check` (plain) exit-code behavior -- confirmed correct already (0 on success regardless of pending changesets, 1 on error); only the `--check` branch and its doc comment are in scope.\",\n    \"Resolving what `changelog_section` should contain when a package has a CHANGELOG.md with malformed markdown (e.g. no `##` headings at all) -- `extract_section` already returns `None` for 'heading not found', and that existing not-found behavior is the contract this spec preserves, not a new malformed-input classification to build.\"\n  ],\n  \"api_surface\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"check_exit_code_raw\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn check_exit_code_raw(report: &amp;StatusReport) -&gt; u8 (crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/status.rs:18)\",\n      \"description\": \"Already-correct, unchanged by this spec: returns 1 when any package has a non-empty pending_changesets list, 2 otherwise. `handle` (status.rs:53-54) returns ExitCode::from(this value) when --check is set and there are no diagnostic errors. This is the ground truth the Action script and the main.rs doc comment must both agree with.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"create_tags_with_options\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn create_tags_with_options&lt;R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver&gt;(ws: &amp;Workspace&lt;'_, R, D&gt;, plan: &amp;PublishPlan, opts: &amp;TagOptions, permit: Option&lt;&amp;ApplyPermit&gt;) -&gt; Result&lt;TagReport, GraphError&gt; (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs:30)\",\n      \"description\": \"For each release, checks `ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str)` (tag.rs:82) to decide whether to call `git.create_tag` (skipped when already_existed). Regardless of that branch, currently pushes `CreatedTag { sha: release.sha.clone(), .. }` unconditionally (tag.rs:113-117 and the floating-major push at tag.rs:103-107) -- the fix must make the reported `sha` reflect the tag's true existing target when `already_existed` is true, using `GitDataSource::resolve_commit(&amp;self, refname: &amp;str) -&gt; Result&lt;Option&lt;CommitSha&gt;, VcsError&gt;` (crates/callisto-vcs/src/lib.rs:291 / crates/callisto-vcs/src/access.rs:79), which is already available on the same `git` handle (`ws.git_access()`, tag.rs:48) used elsewhere in this function.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"extract_section\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn extract_section&lt;'a&gt;(changelog: &amp;'a str, version: &amp;Version) -&gt; Option&lt;&amp;'a str&gt; (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102)\",\n      \"description\": \"Already-implemented and already-unit-tested. Finds the `## {version}` heading in `changelog` and returns the slice of content between that heading and the next `## ` heading (or end of file), or `None` if the heading is not found. `plan_publish` must call this with the content of `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` (pkg_dir resolved at publish.rs:290-296) and `ver` (the release version), reading the file only when it exists, and must leave `changelog_section` as `None` when the file is missing or the heading is absent -- it must never panic or error the whole plan on either condition.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-01\",\n      \"criterion\": \"In .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 1 (the documented 'pending changesets' contract), the script sets HAS_CHANGESETS=true and proceeds into the release-PR-creation branch (the `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]` block), rather than falling through to the `echo \\\"::error::...\\\"` / `exit $STATUS_EXIT` else-branch. Verifiable by reading the script's if/elif/else chain against this exit-code table, or by replacing the `callisto status --check` invocation with a stub that exits 1 and observing which branch's echo output appears.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-02\",\n      \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 2 (the documented 'no changesets pending' contract), the script sets HAS_CHANGESETS=false and proceeds into the publish branch (the `else` arm of `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]`). Verifiable the same way as AC-01, substituting an exit-2 stub.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-03\",\n      \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 0, the script does not interpret this as 'has pending changesets' (exit 0 is not a value the real CLI ever returns for `--check`) -- the script's branching logic must not contain a code path that maps exit-code 0 from this invocation to HAS_CHANGESETS=true. Verifiable by reading the script: no comparison in the status-check block equates 0 with a changesets-pending outcome.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-04\",\n      \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with any code other than 1 or 2 (e.g. a clap usage-error exit or an unrelated failure), the script does not silently treat it as either 'has changesets' or 'no changesets' -- it emits an `::error::` annotation identifying the unexpected exit code and terminates the composite action step with a non-zero exit, rather than proceeding into either the release-PR or publish branch. Verifiable by stubbing the invocation to exit with a code outside {1, 2} (e.g. 127) and observing that the workflow step fails with an error annotation rather than continuing.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-05\",\n      \"criterion\": \"crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` command states the `--check` contract as: 1 when at least one package has pending changesets, 2 when no changesets are pending, and does not claim 0 is returned under `--check` for any pending-changeset state. Verifiable by reading the doc comment text at main.rs (currently lines 19-21) and comparing it word-for-word against `check_exit_code_raw`'s actual behavior (status.rs:18-28: 1 for pending, 2 for none-pending, called only when `args.check` is true and there are no diagnostic errors).\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-06\",\n      \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` (create_tags_with_options) processes a release whose tag already exists in the repository (`contains_tag` returns true) and that tag's actual current git target commit differs from `release.sha`, the `CreatedTag` entry pushed for that release reports a `sha` value equal to the tag's real, current target commit (obtained via a live lookup such as `resolve_commit` against the tag ref) -- not `release.sha`. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` against a repository fixture where a tag `pkg@1.0.0` already points at commit A, the release plan requests sha B (A != B), and inspecting the `sha` field of the corresponding entry in the tool's JSON output: it must equal A, not B.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-07\",\n      \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose tag does not yet exist (`contains_tag` returns false), the tag is created at `release.sha` and the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha`. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` against a repository fixture with no pre-existing tag for the release and confirming the reported `sha` matches the requested `release.sha` exactly.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-08\",\n      \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose tag already exists and already points at exactly `release.sha` (the idempotent-rerun case), the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha` and no error or warning is surfaced -- this is a genuine agreement, not a fabricated one, and must continue to report success. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` twice in succession against the same fixture and confirming the second run's reported `sha` for that release still equals `release.sha` with a zero exit code.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-09\",\n      \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` finds a tag already existing at a commit that does not match the requested `release.sha` (the stale-tag case from AC-06), this condition is surfaced as a distinguishable, observable outcome from the same command's output -- either the reported `sha` differs from the requested `release.sha` (satisfying AC-06 alone is sufficient here, since a caller diffing `CreatedTag.sha` against the release plan's requested sha can already detect the mismatch), or an explicit diagnostic entry describing the mismatch appears in the command's diagnostics/output. At minimum, AC-06's corrected `sha` value must never equal the requested `release.sha` when the two differ, so that a caller comparing the two fields can always detect the staleness. Verifiable using the same fixture as AC-06: confirm the tool's output makes the tag/requested-sha mismatch detectable by a caller inspecting only the JSON report (no source-code knowledge required).\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-10\",\n      \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` populates each `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` with `Some(section_text)` when the package's `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` file exists and contains a `## {version}` heading matching the release's version, where `section_text` is the content `extract_section` returns for that heading (the text between that heading and the next `## `-level heading or end of file). Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where a package's CHANGELOG.md contains a `## 1.2.3` section with known body text, releasing version 1.2.3, and confirming the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package equals the known body text.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-11\",\n      \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic, not an empty-string placeholder) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file does not exist at `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md`. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture with a publishable package that has no CHANGELOG.md file, and confirming the command exits 0 and the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package is `null`.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-12\",\n      \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file exists but contains no `## {version}` heading matching the release's version (e.g. the file has other version sections but not this one, or is empty). Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where CHANGELOG.md exists but has no `## {target-version}` heading, and confirming the command exits 0 and the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package is `null`.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-13\",\n      \"criterion\": \"None of the four fixes in this spec change the field names, field types, or presence/absence of any field in StatusReport, CreatedTag, TagReport, ReleaseEntry, or PublishPlan as serialized to JSON -- only the values written into the already-existing `sha` field (CreatedTag) and `changelog_section` field (ReleaseEntry) change, and only script/doc-comment logic changes elsewhere. Verifiable by running `callisto schema` (or diffing the JSON Schema output) before and after the fix and confirming no field is added, removed, renamed, or retyped for these report types.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"All four bugs and the doc-comment mismatch were independently re-confirmed against live code this session (status.rs:18-28, main.rs:19-21, action.yml lines ~89-97, tag.rs:82-117, publish.rs:290-296+423, callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102). AC-09 is deliberately worded to accept AC-06's corrected sha field alone as sufficient evidence of distinguishability, since the requirement's done_when left the exact surfacing mechanism (corrected value vs. explicit warning) as an either/or -- I chose to anchor the falsifiable minimum (mismatch must always be detectable via the two sha fields) rather than mandate a new diagnostic that isn't in any confirmed code path, to avoid inventing an unverified new diagnostic emission point. AC-04's exact clap usage-error exit code (2) intentionally is not hardcoded as literally always distinguishable from 'no changesets pending' (also 2) at the CLI-exit-code level alone, per the requirement's own note that this collision must be handled 'robustly' — I scoped AC-04 to require the script to fail loudly on any unexpected/ambiguous case rather than silently proceed to publish, which is the observable, testable form of 'must not be silently reinterpreted' without requiring a CLI-side exit-code renegotiation that the requirement explicitly did not ask for (see non_goals). Confirmed via grep that resolve_commit is already a stable, tested method on the GitDataSource trait implemented by both GitAccess and the shell fallback, so AC-06's fix is achievable without new VCS surface area.\"\n}\n```\n\nThis spec covers all four confirmed bugs from `REQ-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS`:\n\n- **AC-01 to AC-04**: `.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml` exit-code branching (the dead-code exit-0 branch, the correct exit-1/exit-2 handling, and robustness against unexpected exit codes including clap's usage-error 2).\n- **AC-05**: the stale `main.rs` doc comment.\n- **AC-06 to AC-09**: `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs`'s fabricated-sha bug on already-existing tags, using the already-available `GitDataSource::resolve_commit` (`crates/callisto-vcs/src/lib.rs:291`).\n- **AC-10 to AC-12**: `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs`'s hardcoded `changelog_section: None`, wiring in `extract_section` (`crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102`), with explicit not-found/no-file error cases preserved.\n- **AC-13**: a guard criterion confirming no JSON schema/field-shape changes, matching the requirement's explicit constraint.\n\nAll file:line citations were verified directly against the current working tree before inclusion (none pulled from the requirement text without re-confirmation).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>59565</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>13</tool_uses><duration_ms>101394</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
