{"parentUuid":"bca774ae-c19a-490f-899a-85586c3793bf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCRLYmE2LDspuBBGZf7G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3851,"cache_read_input_tokens":253306,"output_tokens":9058,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3130},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3851,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9058,"cache_read_input_tokens":253306,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3851,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3851},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCRLXYo1f9Sob8thMYck","type":"assistant","uuid":"7fa27413-e9b6-49e1-831c-c4889ed7f243","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:27:16.685Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"7fa27413-e9b6-49e1-831c-c4889ed7f243","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCRLYmE2LDspuBBGZf7G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**On schemaVersion — you're right, and it changes the earlier call.** Checked: `SCHEMA_VERSION` has never been bumped past `1` despite several tagged local releases (`callisto-cli@0.3.2` etc. — self-versioned via git tags), and this session's own Pipeline Protocol explicitly forbids ever invoking `callisto publish` against a real registry. So no external consumer has ever actually pulled a published crate/package and started parsing this JSON shape — the whole point of a schemaVersion bump (warn an existing consumer their parser is now stale) has nothing to protect yet.\n\nThat logic doesn't just apply to the 3 renames — it equally undermines the earlier Decision 3 call to bump for `MatrixReport`/`PublishPlan`. I'm reversing that too: **no schemaVersion bumps anywhere in this pass.** Just fix every field shape to be correct. Once this project does its first real registry publish, schemaVersion discipline starts mattering — not before. Nothing committed so far assumed a bump (verified: `SCHEMA_VERSION` is still `1`, untouched), so there's no rework from this reversal.\n\nNow proceeding on both fronts: Track 4's spec is drafted and needs to go through canon-auditor/exit-gate, and I'm dispatching the case-by-case investigation for SnapshotReport/InitReport."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3851,"cache_read_input_tokens":253306,"output_tokens":9058,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3130},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3851,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9058,"cache_read_input_tokens":253306,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3851,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3851},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCRLXYo1f9Sob8thMYck","type":"assistant","uuid":"3e8f9765-6bbf-4577-bb9b-078cb52f2b3f","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:27:21.548Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"3e8f9765-6bbf-4577-bb9b-078cb52f2b3f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCRLYmE2LDspuBBGZf7G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FkP2Xg8JuPG1PWCWDewJh8","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit Track 4 spec","subagent_type":"canon:auditor","prompt":"Do the audit work yourself directly in this invocation — do not delegate. Audit this spec@1 for \"Track 4: Release-Pipeline / CI Action Contract Correctness\" against your standard five dimensions (untestable/vague criteria, ambiguous phrasing, missing error cases, scope overlap with other workspace specs, TBDs/incomplete sections). Workspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto — check .claude/specs/ for any existing specs this might overlap with (there should be none yet for Track 4, but confirm).\n\nspec@1:\n{\n  \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Correct four confirmed-live correctness bugs in the release pipeline's CLI-to-Action contract so the shipped GitHub Action reliably reaches release-PR-creation and publish on real runs, instead of erroring out on the normal 'pending changesets' case or silently reporting fabricated state (a stale tag sha, a missing changelog excerpt).\",\n  \"scope\": \"Four fixes, all within the callisto CLI/graph crates and the composite Action script: (1) .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's `callisto status --check` exit-code branching in the 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step; (2) crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's top-of-file exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` subcommand; (3) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs's `create_tags_with_options`, specifically the `sha` field written into every `CreatedTag` pushed to the `tags` vec; (4) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs's `plan_publish`, specifically the `changelog_section` field on `ReleaseEntry` (currently hardcoded `None`), which must be populated via `callisto_changelog::extract_section` (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102) reading each package's `CHANGELOG.md` from its resolved `pkg_dir`.\",\n  \"non_goals\": [\n    \"Track 6-mechanical's JSON report field-shape mismatches (StatusReport, StatusPackageRecord, SnapshotReport, ComposePrBodyReport, CreatedTag's other fields, InitReport, ValidateReport) -- separate track, not touched here.\",\n    \"Any change to callisto-model's SCHEMA_VERSION constant or any report type's field shape -- all four fixes reuse existing fields (CreatedTag.sha, ReleaseEntry.changelog_section) or correct logic/prose, none add, remove, or rename a field.\",\n    \"The `callisto publish` command's actual registry-publishing logic (cargo/npm/pypi clients) -- untouched.\",\n    \"Any change to how the Action script parses `plan-publish`'s or `matrix`'s JSON output via `jq`, beyond the status-check exit-code branching fix -- those jq parse sites are already confirmed working and out of scope.\",\n    \"Adding a dedicated CLI flag or new exit code to distinguish clap usage errors (exit 2) from 'no changesets pending' (exit 2) at the `callisto` binary level -- clap's own exit-code convention is not renegotiated by this track; the fix for the collision lives entirely in the Action script's ability to tell the two apart using information already available to it (stderr content and/or the already-distinct exit code 1 vs 2 contract), not by changing what the CLI emits.\",\n    \"Any change to `callisto status`'s non-`--check` (plain) exit-code behavior -- confirmed correct already (0 on success regardless of pending changesets, 1 on error); only the `--check` branch and its doc comment are in scope.\",\n    \"Resolving what `changelog_section` should contain when a package has a CHANGELOG.md with malformed markdown (e.g. no `##` headings at all) -- `extract_section` already returns `None` for 'heading not found', and that existing not-found behavior is the contract this spec preserves, not a new malformed-input classification to build.\"\n  ],\n  \"api_surface\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"check_exit_code_raw\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn check_exit_code_raw(report: &StatusReport) -> u8 (crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/status.rs:18)\",\n      \"description\": \"Already-correct, unchanged by this spec: returns 1 when any package has a non-empty pending_changesets list, 2 otherwise. `handle` (status.rs:53-54) returns ExitCode::from(this value) when --check is set and there are no diagnostic errors. This is the ground truth the Action script and the main.rs doc comment must both agree with.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"create_tags_with_options\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn create_tags_with_options<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(ws: &Workspace<'_, R, D>, plan: &PublishPlan, opts: &TagOptions, permit: Option<&ApplyPermit>) -> Result<TagReport, GraphError> (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs:30)\",\n      \"description\": \"For each release, checks `ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str)` (tag.rs:82) to decide whether to call `git.create_tag` (skipped when already_existed). Regardless of that branch, currently pushes `CreatedTag { sha: release.sha.clone(), .. }` unconditionally (tag.rs:113-117 and the floating-major push at tag.rs:103-107) -- the fix must make the reported `sha` reflect the tag's true existing target when `already_existed` is true, using `GitDataSource::resolve_commit(&self, refname: &str) -> Result<Option<CommitSha>, VcsError>` (crates/callisto-vcs/src/lib.rs:291 / crates/callisto-vcs/src/access.rs:79), which is already available on the same `git` handle (`ws.git_access()`, tag.rs:48) used elsewhere in this function.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"extract_section\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn extract_section<'a>(changelog: &'a str, version: &Version) -> Option<&'a str> (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102)\",\n      \"description\": \"Already-implemented and already-unit-tested. Finds the `## {version}` heading in `changelog` and returns the slice of content between that heading and the next `## ` heading (or end of file), or `None` if the heading is not found. `plan_publish` must call this with the content of `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` (pkg_dir resolved at publish.rs:290-296) and `ver` (the release version), reading the file only when it exists, and must leave `changelog_section` as `None` when the file is missing or the heading is absent -- it must never panic or error the whole plan on either condition.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"AC-01\", \"criterion\": \"In .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 1 (the documented 'pending changesets' contract), the script sets HAS_CHANGESETS=true and proceeds into the release-PR-creation branch (the `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]` block), rather than falling through to the `echo \\\"::error::...\\\"` / `exit $STATUS_EXIT` else-branch. Verifiable by reading the script's if/elif/else chain against this exit-code table, or by replacing the `callisto status --check` invocation with a stub that exits 1 and observing which branch's echo output appears.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-02\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 2 (the documented 'no changesets pending' contract), the script sets HAS_CHANGESETS=false and proceeds into the publish branch (the `else` arm of `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]`). Verifiable the same way as AC-01, substituting an exit-2 stub.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-03\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 0, the script does not interpret this as 'has pending changesets' (exit 0 is not a value the real CLI ever returns for `--check`) -- the script's branching logic must not contain a code path that maps exit-code 0 from this invocation to HAS_CHANGESETS=true. Verifiable by reading the script: no comparison in the status-check block equates 0 with a changesets-pending outcome.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-04\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with any code other than 1 or 2 (e.g. a clap usage-error exit or an unrelated failure), the script does not silently treat it as either 'has changesets' or 'no changesets' -- it emits an `::error::` annotation identifying the unexpected exit code and terminates the composite action step with a non-zero exit, rather than proceeding into either the release-PR or publish branch. Verifiable by stubbing the invocation to exit with a code outside {1, 2} (e.g. 127) and observing that the workflow step fails with an error annotation rather than continuing.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-05\", \"criterion\": \"crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` command states the `--check` contract as: 1 when at least one package has pending changesets, 2 when no changesets are pending, and does not claim 0 is returned under `--check` for any pending-changeset state. Verifiable by reading the doc comment text at main.rs (currently lines 19-21) and comparing it word-for-word against `check_exit_code_raw`'s actual behavior (status.rs:18-28: 1 for pending, 2 for none-pending, called only when `args.check` is true and there are no diagnostic errors).\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-06\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` (create_tags_with_options) processes a release whose tag already exists in the repository (`contains_tag` returns true) and that tag's actual current git target commit differs from `release.sha`, the `CreatedTag` entry pushed for that release reports a `sha` value equal to the tag's real, current target commit (obtained via a live lookup such as `resolve_commit` against the tag ref) -- not `release.sha`. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` against a repository fixture where a tag `pkg@1.0.0` already points at commit A, the release plan requests sha B (A != B), and inspecting the `sha` field of the corresponding entry in the tool's JSON output: it must equal A, not B.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-07\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose tag does not yet exist (`contains_tag` returns false), the tag is created at `release.sha` and the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha`. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` against a repository fixture with no pre-existing tag for the release and confirming the reported `sha` matches the requested `release.sha` exactly.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-08\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose tag already exists and already points at exactly `release.sha` (the idempotent-rerun case), the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha` and no error or warning is surfaced -- this is a genuine agreement, not a fabricated one, and must continue to report success. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` twice in succession against the same fixture and confirming the second run's reported `sha` for that release still equals `release.sha` with a zero exit code.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-09\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` finds a tag already existing at a commit that does not match the requested `release.sha` (the stale-tag case from AC-06), this condition is surfaced as a distinguishable, observable outcome from the same command's output -- either the reported `sha` differs from the requested `release.sha` (satisfying AC-06 alone is sufficient here, since a caller diffing `CreatedTag.sha` against the release plan's requested sha can already detect the mismatch), or an explicit diagnostic entry describing the mismatch appears in the command's diagnostics/output. At minimum, AC-06's corrected `sha` value must never equal the requested `release.sha` when the two differ, so that a caller comparing the two fields can always detect the staleness. Verifiable using the same fixture as AC-06: confirm the tool's output makes the tag/requested-sha mismatch detectable by a caller inspecting only the JSON report (no source-code knowledge required).\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-10\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` populates each `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` with `Some(section_text)` when the package's `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` file exists and contains a `## {version}` heading matching the release's version, where `section_text` is the content `extract_section` returns for that heading (the text between that heading and the next `## `-level heading or end of file). Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where a package's CHANGELOG.md contains a `## 1.2.3` section with known body text, releasing version 1.2.3, and confirming the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package equals the known body text.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-11\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic, not an empty-string placeholder) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file does not exist at `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md`. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture with a publishable package that has no CHANGELOG.md file, and confirming the command exits 0 and the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package is `null`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-12\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file exists but contains no `## {version}` heading matching the release's version (e.g. the file has other version sections but not this one, or is empty). Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where CHANGELOG.md exists but has no `## {target-version}` heading, and confirming the command exits 0 and the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package is `null`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-13\", \"criterion\": \"None of the four fixes in this spec change the field names, field types, or presence/absence of any field in StatusReport, CreatedTag, TagReport, ReleaseEntry, or PublishPlan as serialized to JSON -- only the values written into the already-existing `sha` field (CreatedTag) and `changelog_section` field (ReleaseEntry) change, and only script/doc-comment logic changes elsewhere. Verifiable by running `callisto schema` (or diffing the JSON Schema output) before and after the fix and confirming no field is added, removed, renamed, or retyped for these report types.\", \"is_error_case\": false}\n  ],\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\"\n}\n\nReturn your standard JSON audit output (issues array with criterion_id/type/description/suggested_fix per issue, plus overall pass/fail)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3851,"cache_read_input_tokens":253306,"output_tokens":9058,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3130},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3851,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9058,"cache_read_input_tokens":253306,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3851,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3851},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCRLXYo1f9Sob8thMYck","type":"assistant","uuid":"fcbbd406-d7b3-4034-a7a9-bcf3a1d2a61b","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:28:00.728Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"fcbbd406-d7b3-4034-a7a9-bcf3a1d2a61b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fdaeeb64-6a81-44ef-90ec-7d96be1228b8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FkP2Xg8JuPG1PWCWDewJh8","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: af1db6da68a74765e (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'af1db6da68a74765e', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/af1db6da68a74765e.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"13a76581-d5b7-45b3-aa74-767eb672de92","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:28:03.064Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"af1db6da68a74765e","description":"Audit Track 4 spec","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt":"Do the audit work yourself directly in this invocation — do not delegate. Audit this spec@1 for \"Track 4: Release-Pipeline / CI Action Contract Correctness\" against your standard five dimensions (untestable/vague criteria, ambiguous phrasing, missing error cases, scope overlap with other workspace specs, TBDs/incomplete sections). Workspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto — check .claude/specs/ for any existing specs this might overlap with (there should be none yet for Track 4, but confirm).\n\nspec@1:\n{\n  \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Correct four confirmed-live correctness bugs in the release pipeline's CLI-to-Action contract so the shipped GitHub Action reliably reaches release-PR-creation and publish on real runs, instead of erroring out on the normal 'pending changesets' case or silently reporting fabricated state (a stale tag sha, a missing changelog excerpt).\",\n  \"scope\": \"Four fixes, all within the callisto CLI/graph crates and the composite Action script: (1) .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's `callisto status --check` exit-code branching in the 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step; (2) crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's top-of-file exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` subcommand; (3) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs's `create_tags_with_options`, specifically the `sha` field written into every `CreatedTag` pushed to the `tags` vec; (4) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs's `plan_publish`, specifically the `changelog_section` field on `ReleaseEntry` (currently hardcoded `None`), which must be populated via `callisto_changelog::extract_section` (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102) reading each package's `CHANGELOG.md` from its resolved `pkg_dir`.\",\n  \"non_goals\": [\n    \"Track 6-mechanical's JSON report field-shape mismatches (StatusReport, StatusPackageRecord, SnapshotReport, ComposePrBodyReport, CreatedTag's other fields, InitReport, ValidateReport) -- separate track, not touched here.\",\n    \"Any change to callisto-model's SCHEMA_VERSION constant or any report type's field shape -- all four fixes reuse existing fields (CreatedTag.sha, ReleaseEntry.changelog_section) or correct logic/prose, none add, remove, or rename a field.\",\n    \"The `callisto publish` command's actual registry-publishing logic (cargo/npm/pypi clients) -- untouched.\",\n    \"Any change to how the Action script parses `plan-publish`'s or `matrix`'s JSON output via `jq`, beyond the status-check exit-code branching fix -- those jq parse sites are already confirmed working and out of scope.\",\n    \"Adding a dedicated CLI flag or new exit code to distinguish clap usage errors (exit 2) from 'no changesets pending' (exit 2) at the `callisto` binary level -- clap's own exit-code convention is not renegotiated by this track; the fix for the collision lives entirely in the Action script's ability to tell the two apart using information already available to it (stderr content and/or the already-distinct exit code 1 vs 2 contract), not by changing what the CLI emits.\",\n    \"Any change to `callisto status`'s non-`--check` (plain) exit-code behavior -- confirmed correct already (0 on success regardless of pending changesets, 1 on error); only the `--check` branch and its doc comment are in scope.\",\n    \"Resolving what `changelog_section` should contain when a package has a CHANGELOG.md with malformed markdown (e.g. no `##` headings at all) -- `extract_section` already returns `None` for 'heading not found', and that existing not-found behavior is the contract this spec preserves, not a new malformed-input classification to build.\"\n  ],\n  \"api_surface\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"check_exit_code_raw\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn check_exit_code_raw(report: &StatusReport) -> u8 (crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/status.rs:18)\",\n      \"description\": \"Already-correct, unchanged by this spec: returns 1 when any package has a non-empty pending_changesets list, 2 otherwise. `handle` (status.rs:53-54) returns ExitCode::from(this value) when --check is set and there are no diagnostic errors. This is the ground truth the Action script and the main.rs doc comment must both agree with.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"create_tags_with_options\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn create_tags_with_options<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(ws: &Workspace<'_, R, D>, plan: &PublishPlan, opts: &TagOptions, permit: Option<&ApplyPermit>) -> Result<TagReport, GraphError> (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs:30)\",\n      \"description\": \"For each release, checks `ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str)` (tag.rs:82) to decide whether to call `git.create_tag` (skipped when already_existed). Regardless of that branch, currently pushes `CreatedTag { sha: release.sha.clone(), .. }` unconditionally (tag.rs:113-117 and the floating-major push at tag.rs:103-107) -- the fix must make the reported `sha` reflect the tag's true existing target when `already_existed` is true, using `GitDataSource::resolve_commit(&self, refname: &str) -> Result<Option<CommitSha>, VcsError>` (crates/callisto-vcs/src/lib.rs:291 / crates/callisto-vcs/src/access.rs:79), which is already available on the same `git` handle (`ws.git_access()`, tag.rs:48) used elsewhere in this function.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"extract_section\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn extract_section<'a>(changelog: &'a str, version: &Version) -> Option<&'a str> (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102)\",\n      \"description\": \"Already-implemented and already-unit-tested. Finds the `## {version}` heading in `changelog` and returns the slice of content between that heading and the next `## ` heading (or end of file), or `None` if the heading is not found. `plan_publish` must call this with the content of `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` (pkg_dir resolved at publish.rs:290-296) and `ver` (the release version), reading the file only when it exists, and must leave `changelog_section` as `None` when the file is missing or the heading is absent -- it must never panic or error the whole plan on either condition.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"AC-01\", \"criterion\": \"In .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 1 (the documented 'pending changesets' contract), the script sets HAS_CHANGESETS=true and proceeds into the release-PR-creation branch (the `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]` block), rather than falling through to the `echo \\\"::error::...\\\"` / `exit $STATUS_EXIT` else-branch. Verifiable by reading the script's if/elif/else chain against this exit-code table, or by replacing the `callisto status --check` invocation with a stub that exits 1 and observing which branch's echo output appears.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-02\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 2 (the documented 'no changesets pending' contract), the script sets HAS_CHANGESETS=false and proceeds into the publish branch (the `else` arm of `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]`). Verifiable the same way as AC-01, substituting an exit-2 stub.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-03\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 0, the script does not interpret this as 'has pending changesets' (exit 0 is not a value the real CLI ever returns for `--check`) -- the script's branching logic must not contain a code path that maps exit-code 0 from this invocation to HAS_CHANGESETS=true. Verifiable by reading the script: no comparison in the status-check block equates 0 with a changesets-pending outcome.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-04\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with any code other than 1 or 2 (e.g. a clap usage-error exit or an unrelated failure), the script does not silently treat it as either 'has changesets' or 'no changesets' -- it emits an `::error::` annotation identifying the unexpected exit code and terminates the composite action step with a non-zero exit, rather than proceeding into either the release-PR or publish branch. Verifiable by stubbing the invocation to exit with a code outside {1, 2} (e.g. 127) and observing that the workflow step fails with an error annotation rather than continuing.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-05\", \"criterion\": \"crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` command states the `--check` contract as: 1 when at least one package has pending changesets, 2 when no changesets are pending, and does not claim 0 is returned under `--check` for any pending-changeset state. Verifiable by reading the doc comment text at main.rs (currently lines 19-21) and comparing it word-for-word against `check_exit_code_raw`'s actual behavior (status.rs:18-28: 1 for pending, 2 for none-pending, called only when `args.check` is true and there are no diagnostic errors).\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-06\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` (create_tags_with_options) processes a release whose tag already exists in the repository (`contains_tag` returns true) and that tag's actual current git target commit differs from `release.sha`, the `CreatedTag` entry pushed for that release reports a `sha` value equal to the tag's real, current target commit (obtained via a live lookup such as `resolve_commit` against the tag ref) -- not `release.sha`. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` against a repository fixture where a tag `pkg@1.0.0` already points at commit A, the release plan requests sha B (A != B), and inspecting the `sha` field of the corresponding entry in the tool's JSON output: it must equal A, not B.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-07\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose tag does not yet exist (`contains_tag` returns false), the tag is created at `release.sha` and the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha`. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` against a repository fixture with no pre-existing tag for the release and confirming the reported `sha` matches the requested `release.sha` exactly.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-08\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose tag already exists and already points at exactly `release.sha` (the idempotent-rerun case), the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha` and no error or warning is surfaced -- this is a genuine agreement, not a fabricated one, and must continue to report success. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` twice in succession against the same fixture and confirming the second run's reported `sha` for that release still equals `release.sha` with a zero exit code.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-09\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` finds a tag already existing at a commit that does not match the requested `release.sha` (the stale-tag case from AC-06), this condition is surfaced as a distinguishable, observable outcome from the same command's output -- either the reported `sha` differs from the requested `release.sha` (satisfying AC-06 alone is sufficient here, since a caller diffing `CreatedTag.sha` against the release plan's requested sha can already detect the mismatch), or an explicit diagnostic entry describing the mismatch appears in the command's diagnostics/output. At minimum, AC-06's corrected `sha` value must never equal the requested `release.sha` when the two differ, so that a caller comparing the two fields can always detect the staleness. Verifiable using the same fixture as AC-06: confirm the tool's output makes the tag/requested-sha mismatch detectable by a caller inspecting only the JSON report (no source-code knowledge required).\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-10\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` populates each `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` with `Some(section_text)` when the package's `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` file exists and contains a `## {version}` heading matching the release's version, where `section_text` is the content `extract_section` returns for that heading (the text between that heading and the next `## `-level heading or end of file). Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where a package's CHANGELOG.md contains a `## 1.2.3` section with known body text, releasing version 1.2.3, and confirming the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package equals the known body text.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-11\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic, not an empty-string placeholder) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file does not exist at `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md`. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture with a publishable package that has no CHANGELOG.md file, and confirming the command exits 0 and the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package is `null`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-12\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file exists but contains no `## {version}` heading matching the release's version (e.g. the file has other version sections but not this one, or is empty). Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where CHANGELOG.md exists but has no `## {target-version}` heading, and confirming the command exits 0 and the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package is `null`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-13\", \"criterion\": \"None of the four fixes in this spec change the field names, field types, or presence/absence of any field in StatusReport, CreatedTag, TagReport, ReleaseEntry, or PublishPlan as serialized to JSON -- only the values written into the already-existing `sha` field (CreatedTag) and `changelog_section` field (ReleaseEntry) change, and only script/doc-comment logic changes elsewhere. Verifiable by running `callisto schema` (or diffing the JSON Schema output) before and after the fix and confirming no field is added, removed, renamed, or retyped for these report types.\", \"is_error_case\": false}\n  ],\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\"\n}\n\nReturn your standard JSON audit output (issues array with criterion_id/type/description/suggested_fix per issue, plus overall pass/fail).","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/af1db6da68a74765e.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fcbbd406-d7b3-4034-a7a9-bcf3a1d2a61b","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
