{"parentUuid":"501a7c8b-8869-4e41-928f-584e5f30ba31","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCRSoh51Zg6aCMidnaD1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dispatching a research fork to gather the deciding evidence for SnapshotReport/InitReport before drafting concrete, already-decided acceptance criteria — a \"fix docs or fix code\" spec needs the decision made first; canon specs need falsifiable single outcomes, not open conditionals."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9474,"cache_read_input_tokens":257157,"output_tokens":3804,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2159},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9474,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3804,"cache_read_input_tokens":257157,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9474,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9474},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCRSnT9zV7v8kqfXGyNH","type":"assistant","uuid":"224111a4-0348-4aa8-acd6-2d64abd70b27","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:28:29.414Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"224111a4-0348-4aa8-acd6-2d64abd70b27","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCRSoh51Zg6aCMidnaD1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ApV5D6J5zsPFMNcM4AxTXC","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Investigate SnapshotReport/InitReport doc-vs-code intent","subagent_type":"fork","prompt":"Research-only task (read-only, no edits). This is independent of the two other agents currently running (Track 4 spec audit; unrelated files) — you're investigating SnapshotReport and InitReport specifically, in crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs and docs/01-spec.md.\n\nBackground: an earlier research pass found these two report types have near-total field-shape divergence between the shipped code and docs/01-spec.md's documented wire contract — not a small mismatch like StatusReport's missing field, but two completely different sets of field names/types/semantics:\n\n- SnapshotReport: doc documents `version: Version` + `packages: Vec<SnapshotPackage{name, ecosystem}>`. Code has `snapshot_tag: String` + `bumps: Vec<BumpRecord>`. (report.rs:339-348, docs/01-spec.md around line 1938-1962)\n- InitReport: doc documents `locator: String`, `packages: Vec<InitPackage>`, `written: Vec<PathBuf>`, `proposed_config: Option<String>`. Code has `initialized: bool`, `config_path: PathBuf`, `diff: InitDiff{new_ecosystems, applied}`. (report.rs:440-461, docs/01-spec.md around line 2071-2087)\n\nYour job: for EACH of these two report types, determine which side (docs or code) represents the deliberate, intended, currently-functioning design, and which side is stale. Use these signals:\n\n1. Test coverage: does the current code shape (SnapshotReport's snapshot_tag/bumps, InitReport's initialized/config_path/diff) have real, passing tests exercising it end-to-end (grep tests/ for SnapshotReport, InitReport, snapshot_tag, config_path, InitDiff usage)? A well-tested, exercised shape is evidence of deliberate design; an untested shape is weaker evidence either way.\n2. Git history: `git log --oneline --follow -- crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs` and `git log -p --follow -- crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs` (or targeted `git log -S\"snapshot_tag\"` / `git log -S\"InitDiff\"` / `git log -S\"struct SnapshotReport\"` searches) -- when was the current shape introduced, and does the commit message explain a deliberate redesign? Does docs/01-spec.md's section have any git history showing it was updated around the same time (in sync) or left untouched since a much older commit (evidence of drift)?\n3. Consistency with the rest of the system: does SnapshotReport's `snapshot_tag`/`bumps` shape match how `callisto snapshot`'s actual purpose is described elsewhere in the docs (search docs/00-design.md and docs/01-spec.md's prose sections, not just the JSON contract section, for how snapshot versioning is described conceptually)? Does InitReport's `initialized`/`config_path`/`diff` shape match how `callisto init` is described elsewhere? A shape that matches the surrounding conceptual prose is more likely the intended one; a shape that contradicts the surrounding prose (even though it appears in a JSON-contract subsection) is more likely stale/aspirational.\n4. External consumer check: does .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml, or any other script/doc in the repo, actually construct or parse JSON matching the DOC's documented shape (version/packages for snapshot; locator/packages/written/proposed_config for init)? If nothing anywhere ever produces or consumes the doc's documented shape, that's strong evidence it's aspirational/never-built rather than a real regression.\n5. CLI command construction: read crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs and crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/init.rs in full to understand what real, working functionality currently exists and what data is genuinely available to report at each point.\n\nReport back, per report type: a clear verdict (code is correct/intended, docs are stale OR docs are correct/intended, code is incomplete OR genuinely ambiguous/needs a product decision) with the concrete evidence for each of the 5 signals above, and if code-is-correct, propose the exact corrected doc text (field names/types/JSON example) that should replace the stale documented contract. Be concrete and cite file:line for every claim."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9474,"cache_read_input_tokens":257157,"output_tokens":3804,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2159},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9474,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3804,"cache_read_input_tokens":257157,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9474,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9474},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCRSnT9zV7v8kqfXGyNH","type":"assistant","uuid":"ae26cf65-5eb0-4252-b8d5-33c718763d93","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:28:44.394Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
