{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01HxMVynBHufrDkmRHgmKgcH","lastSequenceNum":6964,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"3fc0fbbd-8745-45b1-9b05-3680f4a41a5c","snapshotMessageId":"e12d0166-9a38-495c-9f28-aabaf5298cda","trackingPath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track4-draft.json","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-08-19T16:31:23.618Z","realParentDir":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad"},"timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:31:23.636Z"}
{"parentUuid":"e24bba2c-c8f3-42ca-b98a-be1f6cadaec9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCReDuf1SpYTLAyQhqf1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015pi5VrXrf9KFfn7BstrAKG","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track4-draft.json","content":"{\n  \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Correct four confirmed-live correctness bugs in the release pipeline's CLI-to-Action contract so the shipped GitHub Action reliably reaches release-PR-creation and publish on real runs, instead of erroring out on the normal 'pending changesets' case or silently reporting fabricated state (a stale tag sha, a missing changelog excerpt).\",\n  \"scope\": \"Four fixes, all within the callisto CLI/graph crates and the composite Action script: (1) .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's `callisto status --check` exit-code branching in the 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step; (2) crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's top-of-file exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` subcommand; (3) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs's `create_tags_with_options`, specifically the `sha` field written into the `CreatedTag` pushed for the per-release tag; (4) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs's `plan_publish`, specifically the `changelog_section` field on `ReleaseEntry` (currently hardcoded `None`), which must be populated via `callisto_changelog::extract_section` (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102) reading each package's `CHANGELOG.md` from its resolved `pkg_dir`.\",\n  \"non_goals\": [\n    \"Track 6-mechanical's JSON report field-shape mismatches (StatusReport, StatusPackageRecord, SnapshotReport, ComposePrBodyReport, CreatedTag's other fields, InitReport, ValidateReport) -- separate track, not touched here.\",\n    \"Any change to callisto-model's SCHEMA_VERSION constant or any report type's field shape -- all four fixes reuse existing fields (CreatedTag.sha, ReleaseEntry.changelog_section) or correct logic/prose, none add, remove, or rename a field.\",\n    \"The `callisto publish` command's actual registry-publishing logic (cargo/npm/pypi clients) -- untouched.\",\n    \"Any change to how the Action script parses `plan-publish`'s or `matrix`'s JSON output via `jq`, beyond the status-check exit-code branching fix -- those jq parse sites are already confirmed working and out of scope.\",\n    \"Adding a dedicated CLI flag or new exit code to distinguish clap usage errors (exit 2) from 'no changesets pending' (exit 2) at the `callisto` binary level -- clap's own exit-code convention is not renegotiated by this track; the fix for the collision lives entirely in the Action script's ability to tell the two apart, not by changing what the CLI emits.\",\n    \"Any change to `callisto status`'s non-`--check` (plain) exit-code behavior -- confirmed correct already (0 on success regardless of pending changesets, 1 on error); only the `--check` branch and its doc comment are in scope.\",\n    \"Resolving what `changelog_section` should contain when a package has a CHANGELOG.md with malformed markdown (e.g. no `##` headings at all) -- `extract_section` already returns `None` for 'heading not found', and that existing not-found behavior is the contract this spec preserves, not a new malformed-input classification to build.\",\n    \"The floating-major alias tag's CreatedTag.sha (tag.rs:103-107) -- it is unconditionally force-moved to release.sha by create_floating_major on every run, so its reported sha is always genuinely correct by construction and is never subject to the staleness bug AC-06/AC-06b fix for the per-release tag; no change needed there.\"\n  ],\n  \"api_surface\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"check_exit_code_raw\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn check_exit_code_raw(report: &StatusReport) -> u8 (crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/status.rs:18)\",\n      \"description\": \"Already-correct, unchanged by this spec: returns 1 when any package has a non-empty pending_changesets list, 2 otherwise. `handle` (status.rs:53-54) returns ExitCode::from(this value) when --check is set and there are no diagnostic errors. This is the ground truth the Action script and the main.rs doc comment must both agree with.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"create_tags_with_options\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn create_tags_with_options<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(ws: &Workspace<'_, R, D>, plan: &PublishPlan, opts: &TagOptions, permit: Option<&ApplyPermit>) -> Result<TagReport, GraphError> (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs:30)\",\n      \"description\": \"For each release, checks `ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str)` (tag.rs:82) to decide whether to call `git.create_tag` (skipped when already_existed). Currently pushes `CreatedTag { sha: release.sha.clone(), .. }` unconditionally for the per-release tag (tag.rs:113-117) -- the fix must make the reported sha reflect the tag's true existing target when already_existed is true, using `GitDataSource::resolve_commit(&self, refname: &str) -> Result<Option<CommitSha>, VcsError>` (crates/callisto-vcs/src/lib.rs:291 / crates/callisto-vcs/src/access.rs:79), already available on the same `git` handle (`ws.git_access()`, tag.rs:48) used elsewhere in this function. When `resolve_commit` returns `Ok(None)` or `Err(VcsError)` for an already-existing tag, `create_tags_with_options` must return `Err(GraphError)` immediately (fail-fast) rather than falling back to `release.sha` -- consistent with this function's existing git-access-failure handling elsewhere and with this spec's purpose of never fabricating reported state. Note: the floating-major alias push at tag.rs:103-107 is out of scope for this fix -- it unconditionally force-moves the alias via git.create_floating_major on every run, so its reported release.sha is always genuinely correct and requires no staleness check.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"extract_section\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn extract_section<'a>(changelog: &'a str, version: &Version) -> Option<&'a str> (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102)\",\n      \"description\": \"Already-implemented and already-unit-tested. Finds the `## {version}` heading in `changelog` and returns the slice of content between that heading and the next `## ` heading (or end of file), or `None` if the heading is not found. `plan_publish` must call this with the content of `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` (pkg_dir resolved at publish.rs:290-298) and `ver` (the release version). `pkg_dir` can legitimately be empty (a package with no manifests) -- in that case no CHANGELOG.md read is attempted at all, and `changelog_section` stays `None`; the function must never fall back to reading a workspace-root or unrelated-package CHANGELOG.md. When `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` exists but fails to read as valid UTF-8 or fails for any reason other than not-found, `changelog_section` stays `None` for that package and a Warning-severity diagnostic naming the package and the read failure is added to the plan's diagnostics -- the whole plan must not error or panic on this path, matching the existing not-found/no-heading non-fatal precedent.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"AC-01\", \"criterion\": \"In .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 1 (the documented 'pending changesets' contract), the script sets HAS_CHANGESETS=true and proceeds into the release-PR-creation branch (the `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]` block), rather than falling through to the `echo \\\"::error::...\\\"` / `exit $STATUS_EXIT` else-branch. Verifiable by reading the script's if/elif/else chain against this exit-code table, or by replacing the `callisto status --check` invocation with a stub that exits 1 and observing which branch's echo output appears.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-02\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 2 (the documented 'no changesets pending' contract), the script sets HAS_CHANGESETS=false and proceeds into the publish branch (the `else` arm of `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]`). Verifiable the same way as AC-01, substituting an exit-2 stub.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-03\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 0, the script does not interpret this as 'has pending changesets' (exit 0 is not a value the real CLI ever returns for `--check`) -- the script's branching logic must not contain a code path that maps exit-code 0 from this invocation to HAS_CHANGESETS=true. Verifiable by reading the script: no comparison in the status-check block equates 0 with a changesets-pending outcome.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-04\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with any code other than 1 or 2 (e.g. a clap usage-error exit or an unrelated failure), the script does not silently treat it as either 'has changesets' or 'no changesets' -- it emits an `::error::` annotation identifying the unexpected exit code and terminates the composite action step with a non-zero exit, rather than proceeding into either the release-PR or publish branch. Verifiable by stubbing the invocation to exit with a code outside {1, 2} (e.g. 127) and observing that the workflow step fails with an error annotation rather than continuing.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-05\", \"criterion\": \"crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` command states the `--check` contract as: 1 when at least one package has pending changesets, 2 when no changesets are pending, and does not claim 0 is returned under `--check` for any pending-changeset state. Verifiable by reading the doc comment text at main.rs (currently lines 19-21) and comparing it word-for-word against `check_exit_code_raw`'s actual behavior (status.rs:18-28: 1 for pending, 2 for none-pending, called only when `args.check` is true and there are no diagnostic errors).\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-06\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` (create_tags_with_options) processes a release whose tag already exists in the repository (`contains_tag` returns true) and that tag's actual current git target commit differs from `release.sha`, the `CreatedTag` entry pushed for that release reports a `sha` value equal to the tag's real, current target commit (obtained via `resolve_commit` against the tag ref) -- not `release.sha` -- such that a caller comparing the reported sha against the release plan's requested sha can detect the mismatch using only the JSON report, without any knowledge of the implementation. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` against a repository fixture where a tag `pkg@1.0.0` already points at commit A, the release plan requests sha B (A != B), and inspecting the `sha` field of the corresponding entry in the tool's JSON output: it must equal A, not B.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-06b\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose tag already exists (`contains_tag` returns true) and `resolve_commit` against that tag's ref returns `Ok(None)` or an `Err(VcsError)`, the command does not fabricate a `sha` value for that release by falling back to `release.sha` -- it returns `Err(GraphError)` immediately and no `TagReport` is produced for that invocation. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` against a fixture where a tag exists per `contains_tag` but its ref cannot be resolved to a commit (e.g. a symbolic ref pointing at a missing object), and confirming the command exits non-zero rather than emitting a `CreatedTag` entry with `release.sha`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-07\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose tag does not yet exist (`contains_tag` returns false), the tag is created at `release.sha` and the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha`. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` against a repository fixture with no pre-existing tag for the release and confirming the reported `sha` matches the requested `release.sha` exactly.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-08\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose tag already exists and already points at exactly `release.sha` (the idempotent-rerun case), the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha` and no error or warning is surfaced -- this is a genuine agreement, not a fabricated one, and must continue to report success. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` twice in succession against the same fixture and confirming the second run's reported `sha` for that release still equals `release.sha` with a zero exit code.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-10\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` populates each `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` with `Some(section_text)` when the package's `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` file exists and contains a `## {version}` heading matching the release's version, where `section_text` is the content `extract_section` returns for that heading. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where a package's CHANGELOG.md contains a `## 1.2.3` section with known body text, releasing version 1.2.3, and confirming the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package equals the known body text.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-11\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic, not an empty-string placeholder) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file does not exist at `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md`. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture with a publishable package that has no CHANGELOG.md file, and confirming the command exits 0 and the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package is `null`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-12\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file exists but contains no `## {version}` heading matching the release's version. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where CHANGELOG.md exists but has no `## {target-version}` heading, and confirming the command exits 0 and the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package is `null`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-12b\", \"criterion\": \"When a publishable package's resolved `pkg_dir` is empty (no manifest to derive a directory from), `plan_publish` treats `changelog_section` as `None` for that package without attempting to read any CHANGELOG.md -- it must not fall back to reading a workspace-root or unrelated-package CHANGELOG.md. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture containing a publishable package with zero manifests and a workspace-root CHANGELOG.md that does contain a matching `## {version}` heading, and confirming that package's `changelogSection` field is `null` (not the root file's content).\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-12c\", \"criterion\": \"When `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` exists but cannot be read as valid UTF-8, or fails to read for a reason other than not-found, `plan_publish` treats `changelog_section` as `None` for that package, adds a Warning-severity diagnostic naming the package and the read failure to the plan's diagnostics, and does not error the whole plan or panic. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a fixture where a package's CHANGELOG.md contains invalid UTF-8 bytes, and confirming the command exits 0, `changelogSection` is `null` for that package, and a diagnostic referencing the package appears in the JSON output's diagnostics.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-13\", \"criterion\": \"None of the four fixes in this spec change the field names, field types, or presence/absence of any field in StatusReport, CreatedTag, TagReport, ReleaseEntry, or PublishPlan as serialized to JSON -- only the values written into the already-existing `sha` field (CreatedTag) and `changelog_section` field (ReleaseEntry) change, and only script/doc-comment logic and error handling change elsewhere. Verifiable by running `callisto schema` (or diffing the JSON Schema output) before and after the fix and confirming no field is added, removed, renamed, or retyped for these report types.\", \"is_error_case\": false}\n  ],\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\"\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1349,"cache_read_input_tokens":276568,"output_tokens":6135,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1349,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6135,"cache_read_input_tokens":276568,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1349,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1349},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCReBqtA5FKms9BPD4H2","type":"assistant","uuid":"3fc0fbbd-8745-45b1-9b05-3680f4a41a5c","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:31:23.605Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"3fc0fbbd-8745-45b1-9b05-3680f4a41a5c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"77a33b11-58ae-4ff8-bdb6-92604a89e081","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015pi5VrXrf9KFfn7BstrAKG","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track4-draft.json (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"cdda5ede-9fc2-4ae1-8b35-3f1743f2e944","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:31:23.691Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track4-draft.json","content":"{\n  \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Correct four confirmed-live correctness bugs in the release pipeline's CLI-to-Action contract so the shipped GitHub Action reliably reaches release-PR-creation and publish on real runs, instead of erroring out on the normal 'pending changesets' case or silently reporting fabricated state (a stale tag sha, a missing changelog excerpt).\",\n  \"scope\": \"Four fixes, all within the callisto CLI/graph crates and the composite Action script: (1) .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's `callisto status --check` exit-code branching in the 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step; (2) crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's top-of-file exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` subcommand; (3) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs's `create_tags_with_options`, specifically the `sha` field written into the `CreatedTag` pushed for the per-release tag; (4) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs's `plan_publish`, specifically the `changelog_section` field on `ReleaseEntry` (currently hardcoded `None`), which must be populated via `callisto_changelog::extract_section` (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102) reading each package's `CHANGELOG.md` from its resolved `pkg_dir`.\",\n  \"non_goals\": [\n    \"Track 6-mechanical's JSON report field-shape mismatches (StatusReport, StatusPackageRecord, SnapshotReport, ComposePrBodyReport, CreatedTag's other fields, InitReport, ValidateReport) -- separate track, not touched here.\",\n    \"Any change to callisto-model's SCHEMA_VERSION constant or any report type's field shape -- all four fixes reuse existing fields (CreatedTag.sha, ReleaseEntry.changelog_section) or correct logic/prose, none add, remove, or rename a field.\",\n    \"The `callisto publish` command's actual registry-publishing logic (cargo/npm/pypi clients) -- untouched.\",\n    \"Any change to how the Action script parses `plan-publish`'s or `matrix`'s JSON output via `jq`, beyond the status-check exit-code branching fix -- those jq parse sites are already confirmed working and out of scope.\",\n    \"Adding a dedicated CLI flag or new exit code to distinguish clap usage errors (exit 2) from 'no changesets pending' (exit 2) at the `callisto` binary level -- clap's own exit-code convention is not renegotiated by this track; the fix for the collision lives entirely in the Action script's ability to tell the two apart, not by changing what the CLI emits.\",\n    \"Any change to `callisto status`'s non-`--check` (plain) exit-code behavior -- confirmed correct already (0 on success regardless of pending changesets, 1 on error); only the `--check` branch and its doc comment are in scope.\",\n    \"Resolving what `changelog_section` should contain when a package has a CHANGELOG.md with malformed markdown (e.g. no `##` headings at all) -- `extract_section` already returns `None` for 'heading not found', and that existing not-found behavior is the contract this spec preserves, not a new malformed-input classification to build.\",\n    \"The floating-major alias tag's CreatedTag.sha (tag.rs:103-107) -- it is unconditionally force-moved to release.sha by create_floating_major on every run, so its reported sha is always genuinely correct by construction and is never subject to the staleness bug AC-06/AC-06b fix for the per-release tag; no change needed there.\"\n  ],\n  \"api_surface\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"check_exit_code_raw\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn check_exit_code_raw(report: &StatusReport) -> u8 (crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/status.rs:18)\",\n      \"description\": \"Already-correct, unchanged by this spec: returns 1 when any package has a non-empty pending_changesets list, 2 otherwise. `handle` (status.rs:53-54) returns ExitCode::from(this value) when --check is set and there are no diagnostic errors. This is the ground truth the Action script and the main.rs doc comment must both agree with.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"create_tags_with_options\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn create_tags_with_options<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(ws: &Workspace<'_, R, D>, plan: &PublishPlan, opts: &TagOptions, permit: Option<&ApplyPermit>) -> Result<TagReport, GraphError> (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs:30)\",\n      \"description\": \"For each release, checks `ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str)` (tag.rs:82) to decide whether to call `git.create_tag` (skipped when already_existed). Currently pushes `CreatedTag { sha: release.sha.clone(), .. }` unconditionally for the per-release tag (tag.rs:113-117) -- the fix must make the reported sha reflect the tag's true existing target when already_existed is true, using `GitDataSource::resolve_commit(&self, refname: &str) -> Result<Option<CommitSha>, VcsError>` (crates/callisto-vcs/src/lib.rs:291 / crates/callisto-vcs/src/access.rs:79), already available on the same `git` handle (`ws.git_access()`, tag.rs:48) used elsewhere in this function. When `resolve_commit` returns `Ok(None)` or `Err(VcsError)` for an already-existing tag, `create_tags_with_options` must return `Err(GraphError)` immediately (fail-fast) rather than falling back to `release.sha` -- consistent with this function's existing git-access-failure handling elsewhere and with this spec's purpose of never fabricating reported state. Note: the floating-major alias push at tag.rs:103-107 is out of scope for this fix -- it unconditionally force-moves the alias via git.create_floating_major on every run, so its reported release.sha is always genuinely correct and requires no staleness check.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"extract_section\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn extract_section<'a>(changelog: &'a str, version: &Version) -> Option<&'a str> (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102)\",\n      \"description\": \"Already-implemented and already-unit-tested. Finds the `## {version}` heading in `changelog` and returns the slice of content between that heading and the next `## ` heading (or end of file), or `None` if the heading is not found. `plan_publish` must call this with the content of `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` (pkg_dir resolved at publish.rs:290-298) and `ver` (the release version). `pkg_dir` can legitimately be empty (a package with no manifests) -- in that case no CHANGELOG.md read is attempted at all, and `changelog_section` stays `None`; the function must never fall back to reading a workspace-root or unrelated-package CHANGELOG.md. When `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` exists but fails to read as valid UTF-8 or fails for any reason other than not-found, `changelog_section` stays `None` for that package and a Warning-severity diagnostic naming the package and the read failure is added to the plan's diagnostics -- the whole plan must not error or panic on this path, matching the existing not-found/no-heading non-fatal precedent.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"AC-01\", \"criterion\": \"In .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 1 (the documented 'pending changesets' contract), the script sets HAS_CHANGESETS=true and proceeds into the release-PR-creation branch (the `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]` block), rather than falling through to the `echo \\\"::error::...\\\"` / `exit $STATUS_EXIT` else-branch. Verifiable by reading the script's if/elif/else chain against this exit-code table, or by replacing the `callisto status --check` invocation with a stub that exits 1 and observing which branch's echo output appears.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-02\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 2 (the documented 'no changesets pending' contract), the script sets HAS_CHANGESETS=false and proceeds into the publish branch (the `else` arm of `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]`). Verifiable the same way as AC-01, substituting an exit-2 stub.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-03\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 0, the script does not interpret this as 'has pending changesets' (exit 0 is not a value the real CLI ever returns for `--check`) -- the script's branching logic must not contain a code path that maps exit-code 0 from this invocation to HAS_CHANGESETS=true. Verifiable by reading the script: no comparison in the status-check block equates 0 with a changesets-pending outcome.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-04\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with any code other than 1 or 2 (e.g. a clap usage-error exit or an unrelated failure), the script does not silently treat it as either 'has changesets' or 'no changesets' -- it emits an `::error::` annotation identifying the unexpected exit code and terminates the composite action step with a non-zero exit, rather than proceeding into either the release-PR or publish branch. Verifiable by stubbing the invocation to exit with a code outside {1, 2} (e.g. 127) and observing that the workflow step fails with an error annotation rather than continuing.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-05\", \"criterion\": \"crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` command states the `--check` contract as: 1 when at least one package has pending changesets, 2 when no changesets are pending, and does not claim 0 is returned under `--check` for any pending-changeset state. Verifiable by reading the doc comment text at main.rs (currently lines 19-21) and comparing it word-for-word against `check_exit_code_raw`'s actual behavior (status.rs:18-28: 1 for pending, 2 for none-pending, called only when `args.check` is true and there are no diagnostic errors).\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-06\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` (create_tags_with_options) processes a release whose tag already exists in the repository (`contains_tag` returns true) and that tag's actual current git target commit differs from `release.sha`, the `CreatedTag` entry pushed for that release reports a `sha` value equal to the tag's real, current target commit (obtained via `resolve_commit` against the tag ref) -- not `release.sha` -- such that a caller comparing the reported sha against the release plan's requested sha can detect the mismatch using only the JSON report, without any knowledge of the implementation. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` against a repository fixture where a tag `pkg@1.0.0` already points at commit A, the release plan requests sha B (A != B), and inspecting the `sha` field of the corresponding entry in the tool's JSON output: it must equal A, not B.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-06b\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose tag already exists (`contains_tag` returns true) and `resolve_commit` against that tag's ref returns `Ok(None)` or an `Err(VcsError)`, the command does not fabricate a `sha` value for that release by falling back to `release.sha` -- it returns `Err(GraphError)` immediately and no `TagReport` is produced for that invocation. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` against a fixture where a tag exists per `contains_tag` but its ref cannot be resolved to a commit (e.g. a symbolic ref pointing at a missing object), and confirming the command exits non-zero rather than emitting a `CreatedTag` entry with `release.sha`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-07\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose tag does not yet exist (`contains_tag` returns false), the tag is created at `release.sha` and the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha`. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` against a repository fixture with no pre-existing tag for the release and confirming the reported `sha` matches the requested `release.sha` exactly.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-08\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose tag already exists and already points at exactly `release.sha` (the idempotent-rerun case), the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha` and no error or warning is surfaced -- this is a genuine agreement, not a fabricated one, and must continue to report success. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` twice in succession against the same fixture and confirming the second run's reported `sha` for that release still equals `release.sha` with a zero exit code.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-10\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` populates each `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` with `Some(section_text)` when the package's `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` file exists and contains a `## {version}` heading matching the release's version, where `section_text` is the content `extract_section` returns for that heading. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where a package's CHANGELOG.md contains a `## 1.2.3` section with known body text, releasing version 1.2.3, and confirming the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package equals the known body text.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-11\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic, not an empty-string placeholder) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file does not exist at `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md`. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture with a publishable package that has no CHANGELOG.md file, and confirming the command exits 0 and the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package is `null`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-12\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file exists but contains no `## {version}` heading matching the release's version. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where CHANGELOG.md exists but has no `## {target-version}` heading, and confirming the command exits 0 and the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package is `null`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-12b\", \"criterion\": \"When a publishable package's resolved `pkg_dir` is empty (no manifest to derive a directory from), `plan_publish` treats `changelog_section` as `None` for that package without attempting to read any CHANGELOG.md -- it must not fall back to reading a workspace-root or unrelated-package CHANGELOG.md. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture containing a publishable package with zero manifests and a workspace-root CHANGELOG.md that does contain a matching `## {version}` heading, and confirming that package's `changelogSection` field is `null` (not the root file's content).\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-12c\", \"criterion\": \"When `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` exists but cannot be read as valid UTF-8, or fails to read for a reason other than not-found, `plan_publish` treats `changelog_section` as `None` for that package, adds a Warning-severity diagnostic naming the package and the read failure to the plan's diagnostics, and does not error the whole plan or panic. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a fixture where a package's CHANGELOG.md contains invalid UTF-8 bytes, and confirming the command exits 0, `changelogSection` is `null` for that package, and a diagnostic referencing the package appears in the JSON output's diagnostics.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-13\", \"criterion\": \"None of the four fixes in this spec change the field names, field types, or presence/absence of any field in StatusReport, CreatedTag, TagReport, ReleaseEntry, or PublishPlan as serialized to JSON -- only the values written into the already-existing `sha` field (CreatedTag) and `changelog_section` field (ReleaseEntry) change, and only script/doc-comment logic and error handling change elsewhere. Verifiable by running `callisto schema` (or diffing the JSON Schema output) before and after the fix and confirming no field is added, removed, renamed, or retyped for these report types.\", \"is_error_case\": false}\n  ],\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3fc0fbbd-8745-45b1-9b05-3680f4a41a5c","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"cdda5ede-9fc2-4ae1-8b35-3f1743f2e944","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Write","toolUseID":"toolu_015pi5VrXrf9KFfn7BstrAKG","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"callisto\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Write\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":46},"type":"attachment","uuid":"201d568a-a3df-4d03-bf06-d5c6425e8d66","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:31:23.691Z","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:31:23.708Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a0535f1647f809b38</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a0535f1647f809b38.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Investigate SnapshotReport/InitReport doc-vs-code intent\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I have decisive evidence for both. Reporting.\n\n**Directive:** determine which side (docs/01-spec.md vs code) is stale for `SnapshotReport` and `InitReport`, per-field, with proposed corrected doc text.\n\n## SnapshotReport — verdict: **code is correct, docs are stale (but flag a design-quality note)**\n\n- **Signal 1 (tests):** code's shape (`snapshot_tag`/`bumps: Vec&lt;BumpRecord&gt;`) is real and wired — consumed by `crates/callisto-cli/src/render/mod.rs`, `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/schema.rs`, and exercised in `crates/callisto-graph/tests/snapshot_tests.rs`. Doc's shape (`version`/`packages: Vec&lt;SnapshotPackage&gt;`) has **zero** consumers anywhere in the repo.\n- **Signal 2 (git history):** struct and doc section were both introduced in the *same* single commit (`1a8f983d`, the giant initial bootstrap) — never touched since. Not drift over time; inconsistent from day one, never reconciled.\n- **Signal 3 (conceptual consistency):** `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs:26-27` computes one identical `snapshot_ver` for every package in the workspace, with an inline comment explicitly stating this (\"every package in the workspace gets this identical... string\") — functionally matching the doc's own stated intent (\"one value for the whole workspace\"). The *behavior* the doc describes is real; only the doc's specific *JSON shape* (`version` + `packages`) was never implemented — the code encodes the same one-shared-version fact via N `BumpRecord`s that all happen to share the same `to`.\n- **Signal 4 (external consumers):** `.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml` has no snapshot-related jq/parsing at all.\n- **Signal 5 (CLI construction):** confirmed via full read of `snapshot.rs` — real, working, single-shared-version logic.\n\n**Design-quality note (not a verdict, just worth flagging to whoever owns doc correction):** the doc's proposed shape is objectively simpler for what this report represents — repeating an identical `to` value and a hardcoded `Patch` severity across every `BumpRecord` is redundant given every entry shares the same target version. Correcting the doc to match code is still the right call (matches this session's established stale-doc-correction precedent), but note the code's shape is more verbose than necessary for the data it carries.\n\n**Proposed corrected doc text** (replace docs/01-spec.md's SnapshotReport block, ~line 1946):\n```rust\npub struct SnapshotReport {\n    pub schema_version: u32,\n    pub snapshot_tag: String,\n    pub bumps: Vec&lt;BumpRecord&gt;,\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Vec::is_empty\")]\n    pub diagnostics: Vec&lt;Diagnostic&gt;,\n}\n```\nDrop the `SnapshotPackage` type and the \"not a published/publishedPackages pair\" framing (accurate in spirit, wrong in shape); replace with prose describing the real one-shared-`to`-value-across-all-`BumpRecord`s behavior.\n\n## InitReport — verdict: **code is correct, docs are stale — strong evidence, not ambiguous**\n\n- **Signal 1 (tests):** dedicated test file `crates/callisto-graph/tests/init_reconcile_test.rs` exists specifically for the reconcile flow `InitDiff` implements. Doc's shape (`locator`/`packages: Vec&lt;InitPackage&gt;`/`written`/`proposed_config`) has no test coverage anywhere.\n- **Signal 2 (git history):** `InitDiff` was added in a **separate, later** commit (`cb92a4c7`, \"publish orchestrator with native-tool pipeline\") after the initial bootstrap (`1a8f983d`) that introduced both the original struct and the doc section — i.e., a genuine, deliberate redesign happened after the doc was written, and the doc was never updated to follow it.\n- **Signal 3 (conceptual consistency) — decisive:** the code's own doc comment (report.rs:450-457) cites `docs/00-design.md §18 Q5.4 mechanism 1` by name. Read directly (docs/00-design.md:1879-1893): §18 Q5.4 mechanism 1 is a fully-developed design section — \"Re-running `callisto init` is the reconcile flow; it re-detects, prints a diff, and applies only with confirmation\" — describing *exactly* the code's `initialized`/`diff: InitDiff{new_ecosystems, applied}` shape. Meanwhile docs/01-spec.md's own M.12.6 section **self-admits** it's provisional: `[SPEC DECISION, not in 00-design.md]... The shapes below are deliberately minimal — each is the smallest thing that lets a wrapper gate on the command's outcome — and each is a candidate for expansion when its milestone lands.` The doc section is an admitted placeholder that was never expanded to match the real, later, richer design that *is* documented elsewhere (00-design.md).\n- **Signal 4 (external consumers):** `crates/callisto-moon/src/extension.rs:270-276` explicitly discusses mapping moon's `InitializeExtensionOutput` onto callisto's real `InitReport` shape, with a comment noting some moon-side fields \"don't map onto cleanly\" — confirming the *current* code shape, not the doc's, is the one real external integration code is written against.\n- **Signal 5 (CLI construction):** not fully read (time-boxed given decisive evidence above), but nothing found contradicts the above.\n\n**Proposed corrected doc text** (replace docs/01-spec.md's InitReport block, ~line 2073, and drop `InitPackage`):\n```rust\npub struct InitReport {\n    pub schema_version: u32,\n    pub initialized: bool,\n    pub config_path: PathBuf,\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub diff: InitDiff,\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Vec::is_empty\")]\n    pub diagnostics: Vec&lt;Diagnostic&gt;,\n}\n\npub struct InitDiff {\n    pub new_ecosystems: Vec&lt;Ecosystem&gt;,\n    pub applied: bool,\n}\n```\nReplace the M.12.6 preamble's \"deliberately minimal placeholder\" framing for InitReport specifically with a cross-reference to §18 Q5.4 mechanism 1 (docs/00-design.md), since that's where the real, authoritative design for this shape already lives.\n\n**Scope note:** M.12.6 also documents `ValidateReport` and `TagReport` in the same section — out of my directive's scope, but worth flagging: `TagReport.CreatedTag` in that same doc block already documents an `already_existed: bool` field that the *current code* is missing (per the separate research thread on Track 6-mechanical/Track 4 overlap) — so M.12.6 isn't uniformly stale, only the `InitReport` portion is.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>293397</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>14</tool_uses><duration_ms>141376</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"parentUuid":"201d568a-a3df-4d03-bf06-d5c6425e8d66","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a0535f1647f809b38</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a0535f1647f809b38.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Investigate SnapshotReport/InitReport doc-vs-code intent\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I have decisive evidence for both. Reporting.\n\n**Directive:** determine which side (docs/01-spec.md vs code) is stale for `SnapshotReport` and `InitReport`, per-field, with proposed corrected doc text.\n\n## SnapshotReport — verdict: **code is correct, docs are stale (but flag a design-quality note)**\n\n- **Signal 1 (tests):** code's shape (`snapshot_tag`/`bumps: Vec&lt;BumpRecord&gt;`) is real and wired — consumed by `crates/callisto-cli/src/render/mod.rs`, `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/schema.rs`, and exercised in `crates/callisto-graph/tests/snapshot_tests.rs`. Doc's shape (`version`/`packages: Vec&lt;SnapshotPackage&gt;`) has **zero** consumers anywhere in the repo.\n- **Signal 2 (git history):** struct and doc section were both introduced in the *same* single commit (`1a8f983d`, the giant initial bootstrap) — never touched since. Not drift over time; inconsistent from day one, never reconciled.\n- **Signal 3 (conceptual consistency):** `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs:26-27` computes one identical `snapshot_ver` for every package in the workspace, with an inline comment explicitly stating this (\"every package in the workspace gets this identical... string\") — functionally matching the doc's own stated intent (\"one value for the whole workspace\"). The *behavior* the doc describes is real; only the doc's specific *JSON shape* (`version` + `packages`) was never implemented — the code encodes the same one-shared-version fact via N `BumpRecord`s that all happen to share the same `to`.\n- **Signal 4 (external consumers):** `.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml` has no snapshot-related jq/parsing at all.\n- **Signal 5 (CLI construction):** confirmed via full read of `snapshot.rs` — real, working, single-shared-version logic.\n\n**Design-quality note (not a verdict, just worth flagging to whoever owns doc correction):** the doc's proposed shape is objectively simpler for what this report represents — repeating an identical `to` value and a hardcoded `Patch` severity across every `BumpRecord` is redundant given every entry shares the same target version. Correcting the doc to match code is still the right call (matches this session's established stale-doc-correction precedent), but note the code's shape is more verbose than necessary for the data it carries.\n\n**Proposed corrected doc text** (replace docs/01-spec.md's SnapshotReport block, ~line 1946):\n```rust\npub struct SnapshotReport {\n    pub schema_version: u32,\n    pub snapshot_tag: String,\n    pub bumps: Vec&lt;BumpRecord&gt;,\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Vec::is_empty\")]\n    pub diagnostics: Vec&lt;Diagnostic&gt;,\n}\n```\nDrop the `SnapshotPackage` type and the \"not a published/publishedPackages pair\" framing (accurate in spirit, wrong in shape); replace with prose describing the real one-shared-`to`-value-across-all-`BumpRecord`s behavior.\n\n## InitReport — verdict: **code is correct, docs are stale — strong evidence, not ambiguous**\n\n- **Signal 1 (tests):** dedicated test file `crates/callisto-graph/tests/init_reconcile_test.rs` exists specifically for the reconcile flow `InitDiff` implements. Doc's shape (`locator`/`packages: Vec&lt;InitPackage&gt;`/`written`/`proposed_config`) has no test coverage anywhere.\n- **Signal 2 (git history):** `InitDiff` was added in a **separate, later** commit (`cb92a4c7`, \"publish orchestrator with native-tool pipeline\") after the initial bootstrap (`1a8f983d`) that introduced both the original struct and the doc section — i.e., a genuine, deliberate redesign happened after the doc was written, and the doc was never updated to follow it.\n- **Signal 3 (conceptual consistency) — decisive:** the code's own doc comment (report.rs:450-457) cites `docs/00-design.md §18 Q5.4 mechanism 1` by name. Read directly (docs/00-design.md:1879-1893): §18 Q5.4 mechanism 1 is a fully-developed design section — \"Re-running `callisto init` is the reconcile flow; it re-detects, prints a diff, and applies only with confirmation\" — describing *exactly* the code's `initialized`/`diff: InitDiff{new_ecosystems, applied}` shape. Meanwhile docs/01-spec.md's own M.12.6 section **self-admits** it's provisional: `[SPEC DECISION, not in 00-design.md]... The shapes below are deliberately minimal — each is the smallest thing that lets a wrapper gate on the command's outcome — and each is a candidate for expansion when its milestone lands.` The doc section is an admitted placeholder that was never expanded to match the real, later, richer design that *is* documented elsewhere (00-design.md).\n- **Signal 4 (external consumers):** `crates/callisto-moon/src/extension.rs:270-276` explicitly discusses mapping moon's `InitializeExtensionOutput` onto callisto's real `InitReport` shape, with a comment noting some moon-side fields \"don't map onto cleanly\" — confirming the *current* code shape, not the doc's, is the one real external integration code is written against.\n- **Signal 5 (CLI construction):** not fully read (time-boxed given decisive evidence above), but nothing found contradicts the above.\n\n**Proposed corrected doc text** (replace docs/01-spec.md's InitReport block, ~line 2073, and drop `InitPackage`):\n```rust\npub struct InitReport {\n    pub schema_version: u32,\n    pub initialized: bool,\n    pub config_path: PathBuf,\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub diff: InitDiff,\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Vec::is_empty\")]\n    pub diagnostics: Vec&lt;Diagnostic&gt;,\n}\n\npub struct InitDiff {\n    pub new_ecosystems: Vec&lt;Ecosystem&gt;,\n    pub applied: bool,\n}\n```\nReplace the M.12.6 preamble's \"deliberately minimal placeholder\" framing for InitReport specifically with a cross-reference to §18 Q5.4 mechanism 1 (docs/00-design.md), since that's where the real, authoritative design for this shape already lives.\n\n**Scope note:** M.12.6 also documents `ValidateReport` and `TagReport` in the same section — out of my directive's scope, but worth flagging: `TagReport.CreatedTag` in that same doc block already documents an `already_existed: bool` field that the *current code* is missing (per the separate research thread on Track 6-mechanical/Track 4 overlap) — so M.12.6 isn't uniformly stale, only the `InitReport` portion is.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>293397</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>14</tool_uses><duration_ms>141376</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","commandMode":"task-notification","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:31:09.675Z"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3f4341da-cf95-46c4-9ef6-9573bd061098","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:31:09.675Z","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
