{"parentUuid":"d502ae92-3a21-4079-978b-2fcbcf36e16a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCRmk7nwiUiZ8nGu15Na","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KbvZ7TETJ6M2miHm7A2Boc","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/01-spec.md","offset":2016,"limit":100},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":943,"cache_read_input_tokens":294748,"output_tokens":238,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":120},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":943,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":238,"cache_read_input_tokens":294748,"cache_creation_input_tokens":943,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":943},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCRmitNetY5UpanSfwbn","type":"assistant","uuid":"dc6f1ec9-2d38-40af-9cce-ce99298c1e65","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:32:23.276Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"dc6f1ec9-2d38-40af-9cce-ce99298c1e65","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"77a33b11-58ae-4ff8-bdb6-92604a89e081","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KbvZ7TETJ6M2miHm7A2Boc","type":"tool_result","content":"2016\t#### M.12.6 `ValidateReport`, `TagReport`, `InitReport`\n2017\t\n2018\t> `[SPEC DECISION, not in 00-design.md: §12.5 enumerates JSON shapes for `status`, `version`,\n2019\t> `plan-publish`, `snapshot`, and `compose-pr-body` only, but §17 v0.2 ships `validate` and\n2020\t> `callisto tag`, and §18 Q5.5 states that `init` supports `--format json` and that its output\n2021\t> is the moon-side payload for `initialize_extension` (§10/§11). §13 invariant 14 requires a\n2022\t> schema version on *every* `--format json` output, so these three cannot be left shapeless.]`\n2023\t> The shapes below are deliberately minimal — each is the smallest thing that lets a wrapper\n2024\t> gate on the command's outcome — and each is a candidate for expansion when its milestone\n2025\t> lands.\n2026\t\n2027\t```rust\n2028\t/// `callisto validate --format json` (v0.2, §17, §18 Q3). Used by the Action's\n2029\t/// `validate-on-pr` gate (§12.2 branch 1), which fails the check on errors.\n2030\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n2031\t#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\n2032\tpub struct ValidateReport {\n2033\t    pub schema_version: u32,\n2034\t    /// `false` iff any diagnostic has `severity == Error` (after `--strict`/`--strict-graph`\n2035\t    /// escalation has been applied). The single field a gate needs to branch on.\n2036\t    pub ok: bool,\n2037\t    /// Mandatory here, unlike every other report — `validate`'s entire payload *is* its\n2038\t    /// diagnostics, so an absent key would leave the command with nothing to say.\n2039\t    pub diagnostics: Vec<Diagnostic>,\n2040\t}\n2041\t\n2042\t/// `callisto tag --format json` (v0.2, §17). Creates **local tags only, never pushes**\n2043\t/// (§9.1); pushing stays the calling workflow's job (§13 invariant 16's push-last rule).\n2044\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n2045\t#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\n2046\tpub struct TagReport {\n2047\t    pub schema_version: u32,\n2048\t    pub tags: Vec<CreatedTag>,\n2049\t    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Vec::is_empty\")]\n2050\t    pub diagnostics: Vec<Diagnostic>,\n2051\t}\n2052\t\n2053\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n2054\t#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\n2055\tpub struct CreatedTag {\n2056\t    pub tag_name: TagName,\n2057\t    pub sha: CommitSha,\n2058\t    /// `true` when the tag already existed at this sha and was left alone — P3's idempotence\n2059\t    /// made observable rather than assumed. An existing tag at a *different* sha is an error\n2060\t    /// diagnostic, not a silent overwrite.\n2061\t    pub already_existed: bool,\n2062\t}\n2063\t\n2064\t/// `callisto init --format json` (v0.1, §18 Q5.5). Also the moon-side payload for\n2065\t/// `initialize_extension` (§10, §11, §MO.2.4).\n2066\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n2067\t#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\n2068\tpub struct InitReport {\n2069\t    pub schema_version: u32,\n2070\t    /// `\"moon\"` or `\"ignore-walk\"` — §18 Q5.5's \"project locator\" line.\n2071\t    pub locator: String,\n2072\t    pub packages: Vec<InitPackage>,\n2073\t    /// Files written, workspace-root-relative.\n2074\t    pub written: Vec<PathBuf>,\n2075\t    /// The proposed `callisto.toml` content when `init` is running as a reconcile/migration\n2076\t    /// flow and is showing a diff for review rather than writing (§5.3, §18 Q4, §13 inv. 21).\n2077\t    /// `null` when `init` wrote directly or had nothing to propose.\n2078\t    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n2079\t    pub proposed_config: Option<String>,\n2080\t    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Vec::is_empty\")]\n2081\t    pub diagnostics: Vec<Diagnostic>,\n2082\t}\n2083\t\n2084\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n2085\t#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\n2086\tpub struct InitPackage {\n2087\t    pub package: PackageId,\n2088\t    pub manifests: Vec<ManifestDecl>,\n2089\t    pub publish_to: Vec<PublishTarget>,\n2090\t    pub release_trigger: ReleaseTrigger,\n2091\t}\n2092\t\n2093\timpl Report for ValidateReport { const COMMAND: &'static str = \"validate\"; /* … */ }\n2094\timpl Report for TagReport      { const COMMAND: &'static str = \"tag\";      /* … */ }\n2095\timpl Report for InitReport     { const COMMAND: &'static str = \"init\";     /* … */ }\n2096\t```\n2097\t\n2098\t#### M.12.7 `MatrixReport` — §19, §G.11 `matrix`, §CLI.6.13\n2099\t\n2100\t`callisto matrix`'s report is keyed by package name rather than shaped as a per-`Package` list\n2101\tlike every other report above, because two packages can independently populate the *same* two\n2102\tmaps without either being \"the\" subject of the report — there is no natural single-array shape\n2103\tthat avoids repeating each package's identity once per contributing field.\n2104\t\n2105\t```rust\n2106\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize, JsonSchema)]\n2107\t#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\n2108\tpub struct MatrixReport {\n2109\t    pub schema_version: u32,\n2110\t    /// Keyed by `PackageId::name()`. `BTreeMap` gives lexicographic key order for free — no\n2111\t    /// separate sort step (AC-009). A package that declares neither `napi.targets` nor\n2112\t    /// `[tool.maturin].targets` contributes no entry; the map is `{}`, not omitted, for a\n2113\t    /// workspace with no platform packages at all (§13 invariant 14's schema-version-on-every-\n2114\t    /// output rule still needs a report to attach to).\n2115\t    pub platform_targets: BTreeMap<String, PlatformTargetGroup>,"}]},"uuid":"bfb3fbc2-e4cc-4efe-9fab-b71872e4acd1","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:32:23.345Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/01-spec.md","content":"#### M.12.6 `ValidateReport`, `TagReport`, `InitReport`\n\n> `[SPEC DECISION, not in 00-design.md: §12.5 enumerates JSON shapes for `status`, `version`,\n> `plan-publish`, `snapshot`, and `compose-pr-body` only, but §17 v0.2 ships `validate` and\n> `callisto tag`, and §18 Q5.5 states that `init` supports `--format json` and that its output\n> is the moon-side payload for `initialize_extension` (§10/§11). §13 invariant 14 requires a\n> schema version on *every* `--format json` output, so these three cannot be left shapeless.]`\n> The shapes below are deliberately minimal — each is the smallest thing that lets a wrapper\n> gate on the command's outcome — and each is a candidate for expansion when its milestone\n> lands.\n\n```rust\n/// `callisto validate --format json` (v0.2, §17, §18 Q3). Used by the Action's\n/// `validate-on-pr` gate (§12.2 branch 1), which fails the check on errors.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\npub struct ValidateReport {\n    pub schema_version: u32,\n    /// `false` iff any diagnostic has `severity == Error` (after `--strict`/`--strict-graph`\n    /// escalation has been applied). The single field a gate needs to branch on.\n    pub ok: bool,\n    /// Mandatory here, unlike every other report — `validate`'s entire payload *is* its\n    /// diagnostics, so an absent key would leave the command with nothing to say.\n    pub diagnostics: Vec<Diagnostic>,\n}\n\n/// `callisto tag --format json` (v0.2, §17). Creates **local tags only, never pushes**\n/// (§9.1); pushing stays the calling workflow's job (§13 invariant 16's push-last rule).\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\npub struct TagReport {\n    pub schema_version: u32,\n    pub tags: Vec<CreatedTag>,\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Vec::is_empty\")]\n    pub diagnostics: Vec<Diagnostic>,\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\npub struct CreatedTag {\n    pub tag_name: TagName,\n    pub sha: CommitSha,\n    /// `true` when the tag already existed at this sha and was left alone — P3's idempotence\n    /// made observable rather than assumed. An existing tag at a *different* sha is an error\n    /// diagnostic, not a silent overwrite.\n    pub already_existed: bool,\n}\n\n/// `callisto init --format json` (v0.1, §18 Q5.5). Also the moon-side payload for\n/// `initialize_extension` (§10, §11, §MO.2.4).\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\npub struct InitReport {\n    pub schema_version: u32,\n    /// `\"moon\"` or `\"ignore-walk\"` — §18 Q5.5's \"project locator\" line.\n    pub locator: String,\n    pub packages: Vec<InitPackage>,\n    /// Files written, workspace-root-relative.\n    pub written: Vec<PathBuf>,\n    /// The proposed `callisto.toml` content when `init` is running as a reconcile/migration\n    /// flow and is showing a diff for review rather than writing (§5.3, §18 Q4, §13 inv. 21).\n    /// `null` when `init` wrote directly or had nothing to propose.\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n    pub proposed_config: Option<String>,\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Vec::is_empty\")]\n    pub diagnostics: Vec<Diagnostic>,\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\npub struct InitPackage {\n    pub package: PackageId,\n    pub manifests: Vec<ManifestDecl>,\n    pub publish_to: Vec<PublishTarget>,\n    pub release_trigger: ReleaseTrigger,\n}\n\nimpl Report for ValidateReport { const COMMAND: &'static str = \"validate\"; /* … */ }\nimpl Report for TagReport      { const COMMAND: &'static str = \"tag\";      /* … */ }\nimpl Report for InitReport     { const COMMAND: &'static str = \"init\";     /* … */ }\n```\n\n#### M.12.7 `MatrixReport` — §19, §G.11 `matrix`, §CLI.6.13\n\n`callisto matrix`'s report is keyed by package name rather than shaped as a per-`Package` list\nlike every other report above, because two packages can independently populate the *same* two\nmaps without either being \"the\" subject of the report — there is no natural single-array shape\nthat avoids repeating each package's identity once per contributing field.\n\n```rust\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize, JsonSchema)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\npub struct MatrixReport {\n    pub schema_version: u32,\n    /// Keyed by `PackageId::name()`. `BTreeMap` gives lexicographic key order for free — no\n    /// separate sort step (AC-009). A package that declares neither `napi.targets` nor\n    /// `[tool.maturin].targets` contributes no entry; the map is `{}`, not omitted, for a\n    /// workspace with no platform packages at all (§13 invariant 14's schema-version-on-every-\n    /// output rule still needs a report to attach to).\n    pub platform_targets: BTreeMap<String, PlatformTargetGroup>,","numLines":100,"startLine":2016,"totalLines":11435}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dc6f1ec9-2d38-40af-9cce-ce99298c1e65","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
