{"parentUuid":"5cea5d51-a920-4be6-8b86-24057a3285c8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"77a33b11-58ae-4ff8-bdb6-92604a89e081","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FeiPP9TsnaQSiZXcoky8Nn","type":"tool_result","content":"442:pub struct InitReport {\n443-    pub schema_version: u32,\n444-    /// `true` only on a first run, when `callisto.toml` did not exist yet and\n445-    /// was written directly. `false` on every re-run (§18 Q5.4 mechanism 1),\n446-    /// including a re-run that applies detected drift — that case is\n447-    /// reported through `diff`, not this flag.\n448-    pub initialized: bool,\n449-    pub config_path: PathBuf,\n450-    /// Drift between the currently-discovered workspace state and what is\n451-    /// already recorded in `callisto.toml`, and whether that drift was\n452-    /// applied this run (docs/00-design.md §18 Q5.4 mechanism 1: re-running\n453-    /// `init` is the reconcile flow — it re-detects, reports a diff, and\n454-    /// applies only with confirmation). Empty/`applied: false` when there is\n455-    /// nothing to reconcile, including on a first run.\n456-    #[serde(default)]\n457-    pub diff: InitDiff,\n--\n481:pub struct InitDiff {\n482-    /// Ecosystems present in the discovered workspace but not yet recorded\n483-    /// against the existing `callisto.toml` (e.g. a `package.json` added to\n484-    /// a previously Cargo-only workspace, or `napi.targets` appearing).\n485-    /// Sorted for determinism. Empty when there is no drift to reconcile.\n486-    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Vec::is_empty\")]\n487-    pub new_ecosystems: Vec<Ecosystem>,\n488-    /// `true` when `new_ecosystems` was non-empty and was written to\n489-    /// `callisto.toml` this run (`InitOptions::yes`). `false` when the diff\n490-    /// was only reported (dry-preview) or when there was no diff to apply.\n491-    #[serde(default)]\n492-    pub applied: bool,\n493-}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d14db39e-9b