{"parentUuid":"768be6f2-8320-45e9-84e9-c7649b782e07","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_014gHwksCdLqBiPMz1GmdmYa","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"rtk grep -n \\\"InitReport\\\\|InitPackage\\\" /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/docs/01-spec.md\",\"description\":\"Recheck remaining InitReport references after edits\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":15},"type":"attachment","uuid":"176c69f0-1e30-43a6-be49-ce50fdf1ecc8","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:32:56.290Z","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"768be6f2-8320-45e9-84e9-c7649b782e07","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"77a33b11-58ae-4ff8-bdb6-92604a89e081","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014gHwksCdLqBiPMz1GmdmYa","type":"tool_result","content":"257:    │                   #   ComposePrBodyReport, ValidateReport, TagReport, InitReport\n2016:#### M.12.6 `ValidateReport`, `TagReport`, `InitReport`\n2025:> when its milestone lands. `InitReport` is not a placeholder: its shape is the reconcile-flow\n2074:pub struct InitReport {\n2109:impl Report for InitReport     { const COMMAND: &'static str = \"init\";     /* … */ }\n5363:`ComposePrBodyReport`, `ValidateReport`, `TagReport`, `InitReport`), `ModelError`,\n8326:pub fn init(ws: &…, opts: &InitOptions) -> Result<InitReport, GraphError>;\n9490:emitted via `log_line` during the call, before the final `InitReport` — `init`'s progress\n10012:/// the payload is **not** `InitReport` (§M.12.6) — moon's real `InitializeExtensionOutput`\n10020:/// as-is. There is no `InitReport` payload here (§M.12.6's report is not moon's wire shape)\n10028:/// moon's own toolchain config and prompts to ask the user — not a callisto `InitReport`.\n10038:`initialize_extension` calls the identical `callisto_graph::commands::init` (§G.11) `callisto-cli` calls — there is no second `init` implementation here, only a second caller of the one that already exists (P6). Its returned `InitReport` (schema version, config path, diagnostics) is intentionally discarded rather than forced into `InitializeExtensionOutput`'s fields, since none of them can carry it faithfully; `init` still runs for its side effects (scaffolding `callisto.toml` / `.changeset`) and to propagate any error. The real wire type also carries no `confirmed`/`--yes`-equivalent flag — there is no host-side prompt surface here to relay a confirm/decline through — so `InitOptions.yes` is set unconditionally to `true`, auto-applying any reconcile drift on a re-run rather than only reporting it (the closest behavior-preserving choice to the old unconditional-write behavior; see `docs/00-design.md` §18 Q5.4 mechanism 1 for what `InitOptions.yes` gates).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"9533bc8a-f866-4d2f-8d2f-beda34608c51","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:32:58.183Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"257:    │                   #   ComposePrBodyReport, ValidateReport, TagReport, InitReport\n2016:#### M.12.6 `ValidateReport`, `TagReport`, `InitReport`\n2025:> when its milestone lands. `InitReport` is not a placeholder: its shape is the reconcile-flow\n2074:pub struct InitReport {\n2109:impl Report for InitReport     { const COMMAND: &'static str = \"init\";     /* … */ }\n5363:`ComposePrBodyReport`, `ValidateReport`, `TagReport`, `InitReport`), `ModelError`,\n8326:pub fn init(ws: &…, opts: &InitOptions) -> Result<InitReport, GraphError>;\n9490:emitted via `log_line` during the call, before the final `InitReport` — `init`'s progress\n10012:/// the payload is **not** `InitReport` (§M.12.6) — moon's real `InitializeExtensionOutput`\n10020:/// as-is. There is no `InitReport` payload here (§M.12.6's report is not moon's wire shape)\n10028:/// moon's own toolchain config and prompts to ask the user — not a callisto `InitReport`.\n10038:`initialize_extension` calls the identical `callisto_graph::commands::init` (§G.11) `callisto-cli` calls — there is no second `init` implementation here, only a second caller of the one that already exists (P6). Its returned `InitReport` (schema version, config path, diagnostics) is intentionally discarded rather than forced into `InitializeExtensionOutput`'s fields, since none of them can carry it faithfully; `init` still runs for its side effects (scaffolding `callisto.toml` / `.changeset`) and to propagate any error. The real wire type also carries no `confirmed`/`--yes`-equivalent flag — there is no host-side prompt surface here to relay a confirm/decline through — so `InitOptions.yes` is set unconditionally to `true`, auto-applying any reconcile drift on a re-run rather than only reporting it (the closest behavior-preserving choice to the old unconditional-write behavior; see `docs/00-design.md` §18 Q5.4 mechanism 1 for what `InitOptions.yes` gates).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"768be6f2-8320-45e9-84e9-c7649b782e07","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
