{"parentUuid":"b3f4a779-5bd0-41f5-a32f-4245c0416d12","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCRq6qooExF542176mme","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V3NQr4WbjA3vWeWiKWrhfh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add docs/01-spec.md\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\ndocs: correct SnapshotReport and InitReport wire-contract sections to match shipped code\n\nBoth sections documented a shape that was never implemented (SnapshotReport:\nversion + packages: Vec<SnapshotPackage>; InitReport: locator + packages +\nwritten + proposed_config) alongside a fully shipped, tested, different\nshape (snapshot_tag + bumps: Vec<BumpRecord>; initialized + config_path +\ndiff: InitDiff). Investigated case-by-case per user request rather than\nassumed, using five independent signals per report type: test coverage,\ngit history (both structs and their doc sections were introduced in the\nsame original bootstrap commit and never reconciled), conceptual\nconsistency with the surrounding prose, real external-consumer code\n(callisto-moon's extension.rs already integrates against InitReport's\nreal shape), and direct CLI command reading.\n\nInitReport's real shape traces to docs/00-design.md's own §18 Q5.4\nmechanism 1 (the reconcile-flow design) -- docs/01-spec.md's M.12.6\npreamble had labeled it a \"deliberately minimal placeholder,\" which was\nitself the stale claim; corrected that framing too, since it's a fully\nimplemented design, not a stub awaiting a milestone.\n\nBoth fixes are doc-only, same category as the earlier Track 3a/6-doc/\n8-doc corrections -- code is correct and already ahead of the docs, no\nRust changes needed. ValidateReport/TagReport in the same M.12.6 section\nare untouched: those are correctly documented already (code needs the\nfix there instead -- separate Track 4/6-mechanical work).\nEOF\n)\"","description":"Commit SnapshotReport/InitReport doc corrections"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"