{"parentUuid":"a81ed8f1-c571-49ea-a155-bc5142db9221","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCSSDUe9hPFksMyE43j5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":465,"cache_read_input_tokens":325290,"output_tokens":8396,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":292},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":465,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8396,"cache_read_input_tokens":325290,"cache_creation_input_tokens":465,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":465},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCSSBmwuzu85fSyMiwA4","type":"assistant","uuid":"68f45899-3e4c-4adb-b3bb-25bf95694ad3","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:41:06.997Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"68f45899-3e4c-4adb-b3bb-25bf95694ad3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCSSDUe9hPFksMyE43j5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XmtsmKo8YzBeNpoLBJi8tD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track4-draft.json","content":"{\n  \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Correct four confirmed-live correctness bugs in the release pipeline's CLI-to-Action contract so the shipped GitHub Action reliably reaches release-PR-creation and publish on real runs, instead of erroring out on the normal 'pending changesets' case or silently reporting fabricated state (a stale tag sha, a missing changelog excerpt) -- in both apply mode and `--dry-run` preview mode.\",\n  \"scope\": \"Four fixes, all within the callisto CLI/graph crates and the composite Action script: (1) .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's `callisto status --check` exit-code branching in the 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step, including the unrecognised-exit-code path (0 included); (2) crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's top-of-file exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` subcommand; (3) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs's `create_tags_with_options`, specifically the `sha` field written into the `CreatedTag` pushed for the per-release tag, in both the apply path (permit granted, tag.rs:82-117) and the `--dry-run` preview path (permit is None, tag.rs:53-80); (4) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs's `plan_publish`, specifically the `changelog_section` field on `ReleaseEntry` (currently hardcoded `None`), which must be populated via `callisto_changelog::extract_section` (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102) reading each package's `CHANGELOG.md` from its resolved `pkg_dir`, plus the two new `DiagnosticCode` cases that surface non-fatal changelog conditions.\",\n  \"non_goals\": [\n    \"Track 6-mechanical's JSON report field-shape mismatches (StatusReport, StatusPackageRecord, SnapshotReport, ComposePrBodyReport, CreatedTag's other fields, InitReport, ValidateReport) -- separate track, not touched here.\",\n    \"Any change to callisto-model's SCHEMA_VERSION constant or any report type's struct fields -- all four fixes reuse existing fields (CreatedTag.sha, ReleaseEntry.changelog_section) or correct logic/prose; the one addition (a new DiagnosticCode variant for AC-12c) extends an already-`#[non_exhaustive]` enum additively and does not require a version bump under this project's current pre-first-publish posture (no real external consumer of this wire format exists yet).\",\n    \"The `callisto publish` command's actual registry-publishing logic (cargo/npm/pypi clients) -- untouched.\",\n    \"Any change to how the Action script parses `plan-publish`'s or `matrix`'s JSON output via `jq`, beyond the status-check exit-code branching fix -- those jq parse sites are already confirmed working and out of scope.\",\n    \"Adding a dedicated CLI flag or new exit code to distinguish clap usage errors (exit 2) from 'no changesets pending' (exit 2) at the `callisto` binary level -- clap's own exit-code convention is not renegotiated by this track; the fix for the collision lives entirely in the Action script's ability to tell the two apart, not by changing what the CLI emits.\",\n    \"Any change to `callisto status`'s non-`--check` (plain) exit-code behavior -- confirmed correct already (0 on success regardless of pending changesets, 1 on error); only the `--check` branch and its doc comment are in scope.\",\n    \"Resolving what `changelog_section` should contain when a package has a CHANGELOG.md with malformed markdown (e.g. no `##` headings at all) -- that is the documented 'heading not found' case already covered by AC-12.\",\n    \"The floating-major alias tag's CreatedTag.sha (tag.rs:99-107 apply path, tag.rs:64-69 dry-run path) -- this is NOT the same bug class as the per-release tag. `create_floating_major` is called unconditionally on every apply run regardless of the alias's prior existence or target (tag.rs:102, no `already_existed`-style gate), so `release.sha` is deterministically what the alias becomes after any real apply run -- there is no 'different real answer' being hidden, unlike the per-release tag which is genuinely left unmoved when it already exists. Reporting `release.sha` for the floating-major alias in BOTH apply mode (where it is now true by construction) and `--dry-run` mode (where it accurately previews what the unconditional apply step will produce) is therefore correct as-is and out of scope for this fix.\"\n  ],\n  \"api_surface\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"check_exit_code_raw\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn check_exit_code_raw(report: &StatusReport) -> u8 (crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/status.rs:18)\",\n      \"description\": \"Already-correct, unchanged by this spec: returns 1 when any package has a non-empty pending_changesets list, 2 otherwise. `handle` (status.rs:53-54) returns ExitCode::from(this value) when --check is set and there are no diagnostic errors. This is the ground truth the Action script and the main.rs doc comment must both agree with.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"create_tags_with_options\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn create_tags_with_options<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(ws: &Workspace<'_, R, D>, plan: &PublishPlan, opts: &TagOptions, permit: Option<&ApplyPermit>) -> Result<TagReport, GraphError> (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs:30)\",\n      \"description\": \"Two structurally parallel paths must both use the same already-existing-tag detection and sha resolution for the PER-RELEASE tag only (not the floating-major alias, see non_goals): the apply path (permit is Some, tag.rs:82-117) currently checks `ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str)` (tag.rs:82) to decide whether to call `git.create_tag`, but unconditionally pushes `CreatedTag { sha: release.sha.clone(), .. }` (tag.rs:113-117) regardless of that check's outcome; the dry-run path (permit is None, tag.rs:53-80) currently performs NO existence check at all and unconditionally pushes `release.sha` (tag.rs:74-78). Both paths must be fixed identically: when the per-release tag already exists at a commit different from `release.sha`, the reported `sha` must be the tag's real current target via `GitDataSource::resolve_commit(&self, refname: &str) -> Result<Option<CommitSha>, VcsError>` (crates/callisto-vcs/src/access.rs:79, reachable via `ws.git_access()`, tag.rs:48) -- not `release.sha` -- in BOTH modes; the dry-run path must perform this check and lookup without mutating any git state (no `git.create_tag` call, matching its existing preview-only contract). When `resolve_commit` returns `Ok(None)` or `Err(VcsError)` for an already-existing tag, in either mode, `create_tags_with_options` must return `Err(GraphError)` immediately (fail-fast, e.g. via `GraphError::Vcs` for the `Err` case and an explicit error construction for the `Ok(None)` case) rather than falling back to `release.sha` -- consistent with this function's existing git-access-failure handling and with this spec's purpose of never fabricating reported state, in a preview or otherwise.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"extract_section\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn extract_section<'a>(changelog: &'a str, version: &Version) -> Option<&'a str> (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102)\",\n      \"description\": \"Already-implemented and already-unit-tested. Finds the `## {version}` heading in `changelog` and returns the slice of content between that heading and the next `## ` heading (or end of file), trimmed, or `None` if the heading is not found OR the matched section's trimmed content is empty (write.rs:131-136: `if raw_section.is_empty() { None } else { Some(raw_section) }`). `plan_publish` must call this with the content of `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` (pkg_dir resolved workspace-root-relative at publish.rs:290-298; joined against the workspace root before reading) and `ver` (the release version). `pkg_dir` can legitimately be empty (a package with no manifests) -- in that case no CHANGELOG.md read is attempted at all, and `changelog_section` stays `None`; the function must never fall back to reading a workspace-root or unrelated-package CHANGELOG.md. Three distinct non-fatal outcomes, each leaving `changelog_section` as `None` and never erroring or panicking the whole plan: (a) no CHANGELOG.md file at `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` (AC-11), (b) file exists but `extract_section` returns `None` -- no matching heading, or a matching heading with empty content (AC-12) -- both add a `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound` (crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs, already exists, currently reserved/unemitted) diagnostic at Info severity naming the package, (c) file exists but fails to read as valid UTF-8 or fails for a reason other than not-found (AC-12c) -- adds a NEW `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError` variant (Warning severity) naming the package and the read failure.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"AC-01\", \"criterion\": \"In .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 1 (the documented 'pending changesets' contract), the script sets HAS_CHANGESETS=true and proceeds into the release-PR-creation branch (the `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]` block), rather than falling through to the unexpected-exit-code branch. Verifiable by reading the script's if/elif/else chain against this exit-code table, or by replacing the `callisto status --check` invocation with a stub that exits 1 and observing which branch's echo output appears.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-02\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 2 (the documented 'no changesets pending' contract), the script sets HAS_CHANGESETS=false and proceeds into the publish branch (the `else` arm of `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]`). Verifiable the same way as AC-01, substituting an exit-2 stub.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-04\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with ANY code other than 1 or 2 -- including 0 (which the real CLI never returns for `--check`), a clap usage-error exit, or any other unrelated failure -- the script does not silently treat it as either 'has changesets' or 'no changesets' and does not fall into a bare `exit $STATUS_EXIT` that could itself be 0 (success). It emits an `::error::` annotation identifying the unexpected exit code and terminates the composite action step with a guaranteed non-zero exit (e.g. `exit 1`, not a passthrough of `$STATUS_EXIT`), rather than proceeding into either the release-PR or publish branch. Verifiable by stubbing the invocation to exit with each of 0 and 127 in turn and confirming, for both, that the workflow step fails with a non-zero exit code and an error annotation, and never reaches the `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]` branch at all (HAS_CHANGESETS must never be read as a truthy or falsy string while unset).\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-05\", \"criterion\": \"crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` command states the `--check` contract as: 1 when at least one package has pending changesets, 2 when no changesets are pending, and does not claim 0 is returned under `--check` for any pending-changeset state. Verifiable by reading the doc comment text at main.rs (currently lines 19-21) and comparing it word-for-word against `check_exit_code_raw`'s actual behavior (status.rs:18-28: 1 for pending, 2 for none-pending, called only when `args.check` is true and there are no diagnostic errors).\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-06\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` (create_tags_with_options), invoked WITHOUT `--dry-run` (permit granted, apply mode), processes a release whose per-release tag already exists in the repository (`contains_tag` returns true) and that tag's actual current git target commit differs from `release.sha`, the `CreatedTag` entry pushed for that release reports a `sha` value equal to the tag's real, current target commit (via `resolve_commit`) -- not `release.sha` -- such that a caller comparing the reported sha against the release plan's requested sha can detect the mismatch using only the JSON report. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` (no --dry-run) against a repository fixture where a tag `pkg@1.0.0` already points at commit A, the release plan requests sha B (A != B), and inspecting the `sha` field of the corresponding entry: it must equal A, not B.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-06b\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag`, invoked WITHOUT `--dry-run`, processes a release whose per-release tag already exists and `resolve_commit` against that tag's ref returns `Ok(None)` or an `Err(VcsError)`, the command does not fabricate a `sha` value by falling back to `release.sha` -- it returns `Err(GraphError)` immediately and no `TagReport` is produced. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` (no --dry-run) against a fixture where a tag exists per `contains_tag` but its ref cannot be resolved to a commit, and confirming the command exits non-zero rather than emitting a `CreatedTag` entry with `release.sha`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-06c\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag --dry-run` previews a release whose per-release tag already exists at a commit different from `release.sha`, the previewed `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` equals the tag's real current target (via `resolve_commit`), not `release.sha` -- identical to AC-06's assertion -- and no git ref is created or moved by the preview. Verifiable by running `callisto tag --dry-run` against the same fixture as AC-06 (tag already at commit A, plan requests B, A != B) and confirming the previewed `sha` equals A, then confirming via `git rev-parse pkg@1.0.0` that the tag ref is still A after the dry-run (unchanged).\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-06d\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag --dry-run` processes a release whose per-release tag already exists and `resolve_commit` against that tag's ref returns `Ok(None)` or an `Err(VcsError)`, the preview does not fabricate a `sha` value by falling back to `release.sha` -- it returns `Err(GraphError)` immediately, identical to AC-06b's behavior. Verifiable using the same unresolvable-ref fixture as AC-06b, invoked with `--dry-run`, confirming the command exits non-zero.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-07\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose per-release tag does not yet exist (`contains_tag` returns false), the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha` -- identically in apply mode (where the tag is also created at `release.sha`) and in `--dry-run` mode (where nothing is created but the same value is correctly previewed, since there is no pre-existing tag to conflict with). Verifiable by running `callisto tag` and separately `callisto tag --dry-run` against a repository fixture with no pre-existing tag for the release, confirming both report `sha` equal to the requested `release.sha`, and confirming (apply mode only) the tag is actually created there while (dry-run mode) no tag is created at all.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-08\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose per-release tag already exists and already points at exactly `release.sha` (the idempotent-rerun case), the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha` and no error or warning is surfaced -- identically in apply mode and `--dry-run` mode, since the existing and requested values already agree and there is nothing to fabricate either way. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` twice in succession (second run is the idempotent case) and separately running `callisto tag --dry-run` against the same post-first-run state, confirming all report `sha` equal to `release.sha` with a zero exit code.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-10\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` populates each `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` with `Some(section_text)` when the package's `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` file exists, contains a `## {version}` heading matching the release's version, AND that heading's section has non-empty content after trimming -- where `section_text` is exactly what `extract_section` returns. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where a package's CHANGELOG.md contains a `## 1.2.3` section with known non-empty body text, releasing version 1.2.3, and confirming the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package equals the known body text.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-10b\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not an empty string) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file exists and has a matching `## {version}` heading, but that section's content is empty or whitespace-only after trimming -- and adds the same `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound` Info-severity diagnostic as AC-12 for that package. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where CHANGELOG.md has a `## 1.2.3` heading immediately followed by only blank lines before the next heading (or end of file), and confirming `changelogSection` is `null` and a `ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic naming the package appears in the JSON output.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-11\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file does not exist at `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md`, and adds a `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic at Info severity naming the package to the plan's diagnostics. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture with a publishable package that has no CHANGELOG.md file, and confirming the command exits 0, `changelogSection` is `null`, and a `ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic naming that package appears in the JSON output's diagnostics.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-12\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file exists but contains no `## {version}` heading matching the release's version, and adds a `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic at Info severity naming the package. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where CHANGELOG.md exists but has no `## {target-version}` heading, and confirming the command exits 0, `changelogSection` is `null`, and a `ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic naming that package appears in the JSON output's diagnostics.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-12b\", \"criterion\": \"When a publishable package's resolved `pkg_dir` is empty (no manifest to derive a directory from), `plan_publish` treats `changelog_section` as `None` for that package without attempting to read any CHANGELOG.md, and without emitting a `ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic (there is no meaningful package directory to name) -- it must not fall back to reading a workspace-root or unrelated-package CHANGELOG.md. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture containing a publishable package with zero manifests and a workspace-root CHANGELOG.md that does contain a matching `## {version}` heading, and confirming that package's `changelogSection` field is `null` (not the root file's content) and no diagnostic for that package is emitted.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-12c\", \"criterion\": \"When `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` exists but cannot be read as valid UTF-8, or fails to read for a reason other than not-found, `plan_publish` treats `changelog_section` as `None` for that package, adds a new `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError` (Warning severity) diagnostic naming the package and the read failure to the plan's diagnostics, and does not error the whole plan or panic. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a fixture where a package's CHANGELOG.md contains invalid UTF-8 bytes, and confirming the command exits 0, `changelogSection` is `null` for that package, and a `ChangelogReadError` diagnostic referencing the package appears in the JSON output's diagnostics.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-13\", \"criterion\": \"None of the fixes in this spec change the field names, field types, or presence/absence of any struct field in StatusReport, CreatedTag, TagReport, ReleaseEntry, or PublishPlan as serialized to JSON -- only the values written into the already-existing `sha` field (CreatedTag) and `changelog_section` field (ReleaseEntry) change, plus script/doc-comment logic and error handling elsewhere. The sole schema-domain addition is one new `DiagnosticCode` enum variant (`ChangelogReadError`, for AC-12c) on the already-`#[non_exhaustive]` `code` field of `Diagnostic` -- an additive enum-variant expansion, not a struct field change, and is explicitly permitted by this criterion. Verifiable by running `callisto schema` (or diffing the JSON Schema output) before and after the fix and confirming no report struct gains, loses, renames, or retypes a field, and that the only diff in the `DiagnosticCode` enum's schema is the new `ChangelogReadError` variant appearing.\", \"is_error_case\": false}\n  ],\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\"\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":465,"cache_read_input_tokens":325290,"output_tokens":8396,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":292},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":465,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8396,"cache_read_input_tokens":325290,"cache_creation_input_tokens":465,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":465},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCSSBmwuzu85fSyMiwA4","type":"assistant","uuid":"ac2e83a9-cfb3-401c-ba0f-6746724fad75","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:42:11.465Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"ac2e83a9-cfb3-401c-ba0f-6746724fad75","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b57dcde8-a197-4c58-90f9-73fff9d7a315","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XmtsmKo8YzBeNpoLBJi8tD","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track4-draft.json has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"ac44f82a-ecf2-4820-9cbe-bcd10bb1eef8","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:42:11.546Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track4-draft.json","content":"{\n  \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Correct four confirmed-live correctness bugs in the release pipeline's CLI-to-Action contract so the shipped GitHub Action reliably reaches release-PR-creation and publish on real runs, instead of erroring out on the normal 'pending changesets' case or silently reporting fabricated state (a stale tag sha, a missing changelog excerpt) -- in both apply mode and `--dry-run` preview mode.\",\n  \"scope\": \"Four fixes, all within the callisto CLI/graph crates and the composite Action script: (1) .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's `callisto status --check` exit-code branching in the 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step, including the unrecognised-exit-code path (0 included); (2) crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's top-of-file exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` subcommand; (3) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs's `create_tags_with_options`, specifically the `sha` field written into the `CreatedTag` pushed for the per-release tag, in both the apply path (permit granted, tag.rs:82-117) and the `--dry-run` preview path (permit is None, tag.rs:53-80); (4) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs's `plan_publish`, specifically the `changelog_section` field on `ReleaseEntry` (currently hardcoded `None`), which must be populated via `callisto_changelog::extract_section` (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102) reading each package's `CHANGELOG.md` from its resolved `pkg_dir`, plus the two new `DiagnosticCode` cases that surface non-fatal changelog conditions.\",\n  \"non_goals\": [\n    \"Track 6-mechanical's JSON report field-shape mismatches (StatusReport, StatusPackageRecord, SnapshotReport, ComposePrBodyReport, CreatedTag's other fields, InitReport, ValidateReport) -- separate track, not touched here.\",\n    \"Any change to callisto-model's SCHEMA_VERSION constant or any report type's struct fields -- all four fixes reuse existing fields (CreatedTag.sha, ReleaseEntry.changelog_section) or correct logic/prose; the one addition (a new DiagnosticCode variant for AC-12c) extends an already-`#[non_exhaustive]` enum additively and does not require a version bump under this project's current pre-first-publish posture (no real external consumer of this wire format exists yet).\",\n    \"The `callisto publish` command's actual registry-publishing logic (cargo/npm/pypi clients) -- untouched.\",\n    \"Any change to how the Action script parses `plan-publish`'s or `matrix`'s JSON output via `jq`, beyond the status-check exit-code branching fix -- those jq parse sites are already confirmed working and out of scope.\",\n    \"Adding a dedicated CLI flag or new exit code to distinguish clap usage errors (exit 2) from 'no changesets pending' (exit 2) at the `callisto` binary level -- clap's own exit-code convention is not renegotiated by this track; the fix for the collision lives entirely in the Action script's ability to tell the two apart, not by changing what the CLI emits.\",\n    \"Any change to `callisto status`'s non-`--check` (plain) exit-code behavior -- confirmed correct already (0 on success regardless of pending changesets, 1 on error); only the `--check` branch and its doc comment are in scope.\",\n    \"Resolving what `changelog_section` should contain when a package has a CHANGELOG.md with malformed markdown (e.g. no `##` headings at all) -- that is the documented 'heading not found' case already covered by AC-12.\",\n    \"The floating-major alias tag's CreatedTag.sha (tag.rs:99-107 apply path, tag.rs:64-69 dry-run path) -- this is NOT the same bug class as the per-release tag. `create_floating_major` is called unconditionally on every apply run regardless of the alias's prior existence or target (tag.rs:102, no `already_existed`-style gate), so `release.sha` is deterministically what the alias becomes after any real apply run -- there is no 'different real answer' being hidden, unlike the per-release tag which is genuinely left unmoved when it already exists. Reporting `release.sha` for the floating-major alias in BOTH apply mode (where it is now true by construction) and `--dry-run` mode (where it accurately previews what the unconditional apply step will produce) is therefore correct as-is and out of scope for this fix.\"\n  ],\n  \"api_surface\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"check_exit_code_raw\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn check_exit_code_raw(report: &StatusReport) -> u8 (crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/status.rs:18)\",\n      \"description\": \"Already-correct, unchanged by this spec: returns 1 when any package has a non-empty pending_changesets list, 2 otherwise. `handle` (status.rs:53-54) returns ExitCode::from(this value) when --check is set and there are no diagnostic errors. This is the ground truth the Action script and the main.rs doc comment must both agree with.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"create_tags_with_options\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn create_tags_with_options<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(ws: &Workspace<'_, R, D>, plan: &PublishPlan, opts: &TagOptions, permit: Option<&ApplyPermit>) -> Result<TagReport, GraphError> (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs:30)\",\n      \"description\": \"Two structurally parallel paths must both use the same already-existing-tag detection and sha resolution for the PER-RELEASE tag only (not the floating-major alias, see non_goals): the apply path (permit is Some, tag.rs:82-117) currently checks `ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str)` (tag.rs:82) to decide whether to call `git.create_tag`, but unconditionally pushes `CreatedTag { sha: release.sha.clone(), .. }` (tag.rs:113-117) regardless of that check's outcome; the dry-run path (permit is None, tag.rs:53-80) currently performs NO existence check at all and unconditionally pushes `release.sha` (tag.rs:74-78). Both paths must be fixed identically: when the per-release tag already exists at a commit different from `release.sha`, the reported `sha` must be the tag's real current target via `GitDataSource::resolve_commit(&self, refname: &str) -> Result<Option<CommitSha>, VcsError>` (crates/callisto-vcs/src/access.rs:79, reachable via `ws.git_access()`, tag.rs:48) -- not `release.sha` -- in BOTH modes; the dry-run path must perform this check and lookup without mutating any git state (no `git.create_tag` call, matching its existing preview-only contract). When `resolve_commit` returns `Ok(None)` or `Err(VcsError)` for an already-existing tag, in either mode, `create_tags_with_options` must return `Err(GraphError)` immediately (fail-fast, e.g. via `GraphError::Vcs` for the `Err` case and an explicit error construction for the `Ok(None)` case) rather than falling back to `release.sha` -- consistent with this function's existing git-access-failure handling and with this spec's purpose of never fabricating reported state, in a preview or otherwise.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"extract_section\",\n      \"signature\": \"fn extract_section<'a>(changelog: &'a str, version: &Version) -> Option<&'a str> (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102)\",\n      \"description\": \"Already-implemented and already-unit-tested. Finds the `## {version}` heading in `changelog` and returns the slice of content between that heading and the next `## ` heading (or end of file), trimmed, or `None` if the heading is not found OR the matched section's trimmed content is empty (write.rs:131-136: `if raw_section.is_empty() { None } else { Some(raw_section) }`). `plan_publish` must call this with the content of `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` (pkg_dir resolved workspace-root-relative at publish.rs:290-298; joined against the workspace root before reading) and `ver` (the release version). `pkg_dir` can legitimately be empty (a package with no manifests) -- in that case no CHANGELOG.md read is attempted at all, and `changelog_section` stays `None`; the function must never fall back to reading a workspace-root or unrelated-package CHANGELOG.md. Three distinct non-fatal outcomes, each leaving `changelog_section` as `None` and never erroring or panicking the whole plan: (a) no CHANGELOG.md file at `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` (AC-11), (b) file exists but `extract_section` returns `None` -- no matching heading, or a matching heading with empty content (AC-12) -- both add a `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound` (crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs, already exists, currently reserved/unemitted) diagnostic at Info severity naming the package, (c) file exists but fails to read as valid UTF-8 or fails for a reason other than not-found (AC-12c) -- adds a NEW `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError` variant (Warning severity) naming the package and the read failure.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"AC-01\", \"criterion\": \"In .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 1 (the documented 'pending changesets' contract), the script sets HAS_CHANGESETS=true and proceeds into the release-PR-creation branch (the `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]` block), rather than falling through to the unexpected-exit-code branch. Verifiable by reading the script's if/elif/else chain against this exit-code table, or by replacing the `callisto status --check` invocation with a stub that exits 1 and observing which branch's echo output appears.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-02\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 2 (the documented 'no changesets pending' contract), the script sets HAS_CHANGESETS=false and proceeds into the publish branch (the `else` arm of `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]`). Verifiable the same way as AC-01, substituting an exit-2 stub.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-04\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with ANY code other than 1 or 2 -- including 0 (which the real CLI never returns for `--check`), a clap usage-error exit, or any other unrelated failure -- the script does not silently treat it as either 'has changesets' or 'no changesets' and does not fall into a bare `exit $STATUS_EXIT` that could itself be 0 (success). It emits an `::error::` annotation identifying the unexpected exit code and terminates the composite action step with a guaranteed non-zero exit (e.g. `exit 1`, not a passthrough of `$STATUS_EXIT`), rather than proceeding into either the release-PR or publish branch. Verifiable by stubbing the invocation to exit with each of 0 and 127 in turn and confirming, for both, that the workflow step fails with a non-zero exit code and an error annotation, and never reaches the `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]` branch at all (HAS_CHANGESETS must never be read as a truthy or falsy string while unset).\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-05\", \"criterion\": \"crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` command states the `--check` contract as: 1 when at least one package has pending changesets, 2 when no changesets are pending, and does not claim 0 is returned under `--check` for any pending-changeset state. Verifiable by reading the doc comment text at main.rs (currently lines 19-21) and comparing it word-for-word against `check_exit_code_raw`'s actual behavior (status.rs:18-28: 1 for pending, 2 for none-pending, called only when `args.check` is true and there are no diagnostic errors).\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-06\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` (create_tags_with_options), invoked WITHOUT `--dry-run` (permit granted, apply mode), processes a release whose per-release tag already exists in the repository (`contains_tag` returns true) and that tag's actual current git target commit differs from `release.sha`, the `CreatedTag` entry pushed for that release reports a `sha` value equal to the tag's real, current target commit (via `resolve_commit`) -- not `release.sha` -- such that a caller comparing the reported sha against the release plan's requested sha can detect the mismatch using only the JSON report. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` (no --dry-run) against a repository fixture where a tag `pkg@1.0.0` already points at commit A, the release plan requests sha B (A != B), and inspecting the `sha` field of the corresponding entry: it must equal A, not B.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-06b\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag`, invoked WITHOUT `--dry-run`, processes a release whose per-release tag already exists and `resolve_commit` against that tag's ref returns `Ok(None)` or an `Err(VcsError)`, the command does not fabricate a `sha` value by falling back to `release.sha` -- it returns `Err(GraphError)` immediately and no `TagReport` is produced. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` (no --dry-run) against a fixture where a tag exists per `contains_tag` but its ref cannot be resolved to a commit, and confirming the command exits non-zero rather than emitting a `CreatedTag` entry with `release.sha`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-06c\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag --dry-run` previews a release whose per-release tag already exists at a commit different from `release.sha`, the previewed `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` equals the tag's real current target (via `resolve_commit`), not `release.sha` -- identical to AC-06's assertion -- and no git ref is created or moved by the preview. Verifiable by running `callisto tag --dry-run` against the same fixture as AC-06 (tag already at commit A, plan requests B, A != B) and confirming the previewed `sha` equals A, then confirming via `git rev-parse pkg@1.0.0` that the tag ref is still A after the dry-run (unchanged).\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-06d\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag --dry-run` processes a release whose per-release tag already exists and `resolve_commit` against that tag's ref returns `Ok(None)` or an `Err(VcsError)`, the preview does not fabricate a `sha` value by falling back to `release.sha` -- it returns `Err(GraphError)` immediately, identical to AC-06b's behavior. Verifiable using the same unresolvable-ref fixture as AC-06b, invoked with `--dry-run`, confirming the command exits non-zero.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-07\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose per-release tag does not yet exist (`contains_tag` returns false), the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha` -- identically in apply mode (where the tag is also created at `release.sha`) and in `--dry-run` mode (where nothing is created but the same value is correctly previewed, since there is no pre-existing tag to conflict with). Verifiable by running `callisto tag` and separately `callisto tag --dry-run` against a repository fixture with no pre-existing tag for the release, confirming both report `sha` equal to the requested `release.sha`, and confirming (apply mode only) the tag is actually created there while (dry-run mode) no tag is created at all.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-08\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose per-release tag already exists and already points at exactly `release.sha` (the idempotent-rerun case), the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha` and no error or warning is surfaced -- identically in apply mode and `--dry-run` mode, since the existing and requested values already agree and there is nothing to fabricate either way. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` twice in succession (second run is the idempotent case) and separately running `callisto tag --dry-run` against the same post-first-run state, confirming all report `sha` equal to `release.sha` with a zero exit code.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-10\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` populates each `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` with `Some(section_text)` when the package's `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` file exists, contains a `## {version}` heading matching the release's version, AND that heading's section has non-empty content after trimming -- where `section_text` is exactly what `extract_section` returns. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where a package's CHANGELOG.md contains a `## 1.2.3` section with known non-empty body text, releasing version 1.2.3, and confirming the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package equals the known body text.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-10b\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not an empty string) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file exists and has a matching `## {version}` heading, but that section's content is empty or whitespace-only after trimming -- and adds the same `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound` Info-severity diagnostic as AC-12 for that package. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where CHANGELOG.md has a `## 1.2.3` heading immediately followed by only blank lines before the next heading (or end of file), and confirming `changelogSection` is `null` and a `ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic naming the package appears in the JSON output.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-11\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file does not exist at `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md`, and adds a `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic at Info severity naming the package to the plan's diagnostics. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture with a publishable package that has no CHANGELOG.md file, and confirming the command exits 0, `changelogSection` is `null`, and a `ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic naming that package appears in the JSON output's diagnostics.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-12\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file exists but contains no `## {version}` heading matching the release's version, and adds a `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic at Info severity naming the package. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where CHANGELOG.md exists but has no `## {target-version}` heading, and confirming the command exits 0, `changelogSection` is `null`, and a `ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic naming that package appears in the JSON output's diagnostics.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-12b\", \"criterion\": \"When a publishable package's resolved `pkg_dir` is empty (no manifest to derive a directory from), `plan_publish` treats `changelog_section` as `None` for that package without attempting to read any CHANGELOG.md, and without emitting a `ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic (there is no meaningful package directory to name) -- it must not fall back to reading a workspace-root or unrelated-package CHANGELOG.md. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture containing a publishable package with zero manifests and a workspace-root CHANGELOG.md that does contain a matching `## {version}` heading, and confirming that package's `changelogSection` field is `null` (not the root file's content) and no diagnostic for that package is emitted.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-12c\", \"criterion\": \"When `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` exists but cannot be read as valid UTF-8, or fails to read for a reason other than not-found, `plan_publish` treats `changelog_section` as `None` for that package, adds a new `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError` (Warning severity) diagnostic naming the package and the read failure to the plan's diagnostics, and does not error the whole plan or panic. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a fixture where a package's CHANGELOG.md contains invalid UTF-8 bytes, and confirming the command exits 0, `changelogSection` is `null` for that package, and a `ChangelogReadError` diagnostic referencing the package appears in the JSON output's diagnostics.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-13\", \"criterion\": \"None of the fixes in this spec change the field names, field types, or presence/absence of any struct field in StatusReport, CreatedTag, TagReport, ReleaseEntry, or PublishPlan as serialized to JSON -- only the values written into the already-existing `sha` field (CreatedTag) and `changelog_section` field (ReleaseEntry) change, plus script/doc-comment logic and error handling elsewhere. The sole schema-domain addition is one new `DiagnosticCode` enum variant (`ChangelogReadError`, for AC-12c) on the already-`#[non_exhaustive]` `code` field of `Diagnostic` -- an additive enum-variant expansion, not a struct field change, and is explicitly permitted by this criterion. Verifiable by running `callisto schema` (or diffing the JSON Schema output) before and after the fix and confirming no report struct gains, loses, renames, or retypes a field, and that the only diff in the `DiagnosticCode` enum's schema is the new `ChangelogReadError` variant appearing.\", \"is_error_case\": false}\n  ],\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":16,"newStart":1,"newLines":16,"lines":[" {","   \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\",","-  \"purpose\": \"Correct four confirmed-live correctness bugs in the release pipeline's CLI-to-Action contract so the shipped GitHub Action reliably reaches release-PR-creation and publish on real runs, instead of erroring out on the normal 'pending changesets' case or silently reporting fabricated state (a stale tag sha, a missing changelog excerpt).\",","-  \"scope\": \"Four fixes, all within the callisto CLI/graph crates and the composite Action script: (1) .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's `callisto status --check` exit-code branching in the 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step; (2) crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's top-of-file exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` subcommand; (3) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs's `create_tags_with_options`, specifically the `sha` field written into the `CreatedTag` pushed for the per-release tag; (4) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs's `plan_publish`, specifically the `changelog_section` field on `ReleaseEntry` (currently hardcoded `None`), which must be populated via `callisto_changelog::extract_section` (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102) reading each package's `CHANGELOG.md` from its resolved `pkg_dir`.\",","+  \"purpose\": \"Correct four confirmed-live correctness bugs in the release pipeline's CLI-to-Action contract so the shipped GitHub Action reliably reaches release-PR-creation and publish on real runs, instead of erroring out on the normal 'pending changesets' case or silently reporting fabricated state (a stale tag sha, a missing changelog excerpt) -- in both apply mode and `--dry-run` preview mode.\",","+  \"scope\": \"Four fixes, all within the callisto CLI/graph crates and the composite Action script: (1) .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's `callisto status --check` exit-code branching in the 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step, including the unrecognised-exit-code path (0 included); (2) crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's top-of-file exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` subcommand; (3) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs's `create_tags_with_options`, specifically the `sha` field written into the `CreatedTag` pushed for the per-release tag, in both the apply path (permit granted, tag.rs:82-117) and the `--dry-run` preview path (permit is None, tag.rs:53-80); (4) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs's `plan_publish`, specifically the `changelog_section` field on `ReleaseEntry` (currently hardcoded `None`), which must be populated via `callisto_changelog::extract_section` (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102) reading each package's `CHANGELOG.md` from its resolved `pkg_dir`, plus the two new `DiagnosticCode` cases that surface non-fatal changelog conditions.\",","   \"non_goals\": [","     \"Track 6-mechanical's JSON report field-shape mismatches (StatusReport, StatusPackageRecord, SnapshotReport, ComposePrBodyReport, CreatedTag's other fields, InitReport, ValidateReport) -- separate track, not touched here.\",","-    \"Any change to callisto-model's SCHEMA_VERSION constant or any report type's field shape -- all four fixes reuse existing fields (CreatedTag.sha, ReleaseEntry.changelog_section) or correct logic/prose, none add, remove, or rename a field.\",","+    \"Any change to callisto-model's SCHEMA_VERSION constant or any report type's struct fields -- all four fixes reuse existing fields (CreatedTag.sha, ReleaseEntry.changelog_section) or correct logic/prose; the one addition (a new DiagnosticCode variant for AC-12c) extends an already-`#[non_exhaustive]` enum additively and does not require a version bump under this project's current pre-first-publish posture (no real external consumer of this wire format exists yet).\",","     \"The `callisto publish` command's actual registry-publishing logic (cargo/npm/pypi clients) -- untouched.\",","     \"Any change to how the Action script parses `plan-publish`'s or `matrix`'s JSON output via `jq`, beyond the status-check exit-code branching fix -- those jq parse sites are already confirmed working and out of scope.\",","     \"Adding a dedicated CLI flag or new exit code to distinguish clap usage errors (exit 2) from 'no changesets pending' (exit 2) at the `callisto` binary level -- clap's own exit-code convention is not renegotiated by this track; the fix for the collision lives entirely in the Action script's ability to tell the two apart, not by changing what the CLI emits.\",","     \"Any change to `callisto status`'s non-`--check` (plain) exit-code behavior -- confirmed correct already (0 on success regardless of pending changesets, 1 on error); only the `--check` branch and its doc comment are in scope.\",","-    \"Resolving what `changelog_section` should contain when a package has a CHANGELOG.md with malformed markdown (e.g. no `##` headings at all) -- `extract_section` already returns `None` for 'heading not found', and that existing not-found behavior is the contract this spec preserves, not a new malformed-input classification to build.\",","-    \"The floating-major alias tag's CreatedTag.sha (tag.rs:103-107) -- it is unconditionally force-moved to release.sha by create_floating_major on every run, so its reported sha is always genuinely correct by construction and is never subject to the staleness bug AC-06/AC-06b fix for the per-release tag; no change needed there.\"","+    \"Resolving what `changelog_section` should contain when a package has a CHANGELOG.md with malformed markdown (e.g. no `##` headings at all) -- that is the documented 'heading not found' case already covered by AC-12.\",","+    \"The floating-major alias tag's CreatedTag.sha (tag.rs:99-107 apply path, tag.rs:64-69 dry-run path) -- this is NOT the same bug class as the per-release tag. `create_floating_major` is called unconditionally on every apply run regardless of the alias's prior existence or target (tag.rs:102, no `already_existed`-style gate), so `release.sha` is deterministically what the alias becomes after any real apply run -- there is no 'different real answer' being hidden, unlike the per-release tag which is genuinely left unmoved when it already exists. Reporting `release.sha` for the floating-major alias in BOTH apply mode (where it is now true by construction) and `--dry-run` mode (where it accurately previews what the unconditional apply step will produce) is therefore correct as-is and out of scope for this fix.\"","   ],","   \"api_surface\": [","     {"]},{"oldStart":21,"oldLines":30,"newStart":21,"newLines":32,"lines":["     {","       \"name\": \"create_tags_with_options\",","       \"signature\": \"fn create_tags_with_options<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(ws: &Workspace<'_, R, D>, plan: &PublishPlan, opts: &TagOptions, permit: Option<&ApplyPermit>) -> Result<TagReport, GraphError> (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs:30)\",","-      \"description\": \"For each release, checks `ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str)` (tag.rs:82) to decide whether to call `git.create_tag` (skipped when already_existed). Currently pushes `CreatedTag { sha: release.sha.clone(), .. }` unconditionally for the per-release tag (tag.rs:113-117) -- the fix must make the reported sha reflect the tag's true existing target when already_existed is true, using `GitDataSource::resolve_commit(&self, refname: &str) -> Result<Option<CommitSha>, VcsError>` (crates/callisto-vcs/src/lib.rs:291 / crates/callisto-vcs/src/access.rs:79), already available on the same `git` handle (`ws.git_access()`, tag.rs:48) used elsewhere in this function. When `resolve_commit` returns `Ok(None)` or `Err(VcsError)` for an already-existing tag, `create_tags_with_options` must return `Err(GraphError)` immediately (fail-fast) rather than falling back to `release.sha` -- consistent with this function's existing git-access-failure handling elsewhere and with this spec's purpose of never fabricating reported state. Note: the floating-major alias push at tag.rs:103-107 is out of scope for this fix -- it unconditionally force-moves the alias via git.create_floating_major on every run, so its reported release.sha is always genuinely correct and requires no staleness check.\"","+      \"description\": \"Two structurally parallel paths must both use the same already-existing-tag detection and sha resolution for the PER-RELEASE tag only (not the floating-major alias, see non_goals): the apply path (permit is Some, tag.rs:82-117) currently checks `ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str)` (tag.rs:82) to decide whether to call `git.create_tag`, but unconditionally pushes `CreatedTag { sha: release.sha.clone(), .. }` (tag.rs:113-117) regardless of that check's outcome; the dry-run path (permit is None, tag.rs:53-80) currently performs NO existence check at all and unconditionally pushes `release.sha` (tag.rs:74-78). Both paths must be fixed identically: when the per-release tag already exists at a commit different from `release.sha`, the reported `sha` must be the tag's real current target via `GitDataSource::resolve_commit(&self, refname: &str) -> Result<Option<CommitSha>, VcsError>` (crates/callisto-vcs/src/access.rs:79, reachable via `ws.git_access()`, tag.rs:48) -- not `release.sha` -- in BOTH modes; the dry-run path must perform this check and lookup without mutating any git state (no `git.create_tag` call, matching its existing preview-only contract). When `resolve_commit` returns `Ok(None)` or `Err(VcsError)` for an already-existing tag, in either mode, `create_tags_with_options` must return `Err(GraphError)` immediately (fail-fast, e.g. via `GraphError::Vcs` for the `Err` case and an explicit error construction for the `Ok(None)` case) rather than falling back to `release.sha` -- consistent with this function's existing git-access-failure handling and with this spec's purpose of never fabricating reported state, in a preview or otherwise.\"","     },","     {","       \"name\": \"extract_section\",","       \"signature\": \"fn extract_section<'a>(changelog: &'a str, version: &Version) -> Option<&'a str> (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102)\",","-      \"description\": \"Already-implemented and already-unit-tested. Finds the `## {version}` heading in `changelog` and returns the slice of content between that heading and the next `## ` heading (or end of file), or `None` if the heading is not found. `plan_publish` must call this with the content of `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` (pkg_dir resolved at publish.rs:290-298) and `ver` (the release version). `pkg_dir` can legitimately be empty (a package with no manifests) -- in that case no CHANGELOG.md read is attempted at all, and `changelog_section` stays `None`; the function must never fall back to reading a workspace-root or unrelated-package CHANGELOG.md. When `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` exists but fails to read as valid UTF-8 or fails for any reason other than not-found, `changelog_section` stays `None` for that package and a Warning-severity diagnostic naming the package and the read failure is added to the plan's diagnostics -- the whole plan must not error or panic on this path, matching the existing not-found/no-heading non-fatal precedent.\"","+      \"description\": \"Already-implemented and already-unit-tested. Finds the `## {version}` heading in `changelog` and returns the slice of content between that heading and the next `## ` heading (or end of file), trimmed, or `None` if the heading is not found OR the matched section's trimmed content is empty (write.rs:131-136: `if raw_section.is_empty() { None } else { Some(raw_section) }`). `plan_publish` must call this with the content of `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` (pkg_dir resolved workspace-root-relative at publish.rs:290-298; joined against the workspace root before reading) and `ver` (the release version). `pkg_dir` can legitimately be empty (a package with no manifests) -- in that case no CHANGELOG.md read is attempted at all, and `changelog_section` stays `None`; the function must never fall back to reading a workspace-root or unrelated-package CHANGELOG.md. Three distinct non-fatal outcomes, each leaving `changelog_section` as `None` and never erroring or panicking the whole plan: (a) no CHANGELOG.md file at `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` (AC-11), (b) file exists but `extract_section` returns `None` -- no matching heading, or a matching heading with empty content (AC-12) -- both add a `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound` (crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs, already exists, currently reserved/unemitted) diagnostic at Info severity naming the package, (c) file exists but fails to read as valid UTF-8 or fails for a reason other than not-found (AC-12c) -- adds a NEW `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError` variant (Warning severity) naming the package and the read failure.\"","     }","   ],","   \"acceptance_criteria\": [","-    {\"id\": \"AC-01\", \"criterion\": \"In .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 1 (the documented 'pending changesets' contract), the script sets HAS_CHANGESETS=true and proceeds into the release-PR-creation branch (the `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]` block), rather than falling through to the `echo \\\"::error::...\\\"` / `exit $STATUS_EXIT` else-branch. Verifiable by reading the script's if/elif/else chain against this exit-code table, or by replacing the `callisto status --check` invocation with a stub that exits 1 and observing which branch's echo output appears.\", \"is_error_case\": false},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-01\", \"criterion\": \"In .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 1 (the documented 'pending changesets' contract), the script sets HAS_CHANGESETS=true and proceeds into the release-PR-creation branch (the `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]` block), rather than falling through to the unexpected-exit-code branch. Verifiable by reading the script's if/elif/else chain against this exit-code table, or by replacing the `callisto status --check` invocation with a stub that exits 1 and observing which branch's echo output appears.\", \"is_error_case\": false},","     {\"id\": \"AC-02\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 2 (the documented 'no changesets pending' contract), the script sets HAS_CHANGESETS=false and proceeds into the publish branch (the `else` arm of `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]`). Verifiable the same way as AC-01, substituting an exit-2 stub.\", \"is_error_case\": false},","-    {\"id\": \"AC-03\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with code 0, the script does not interpret this as 'has pending changesets' (exit 0 is not a value the real CLI ever returns for `--check`) -- the script's branching logic must not contain a code path that maps exit-code 0 from this invocation to HAS_CHANGESETS=true. Verifiable by reading the script: no comparison in the status-check block equates 0 with a changesets-pending outcome.\", \"is_error_case\": true},","-    {\"id\": \"AC-04\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with any code other than 1 or 2 (e.g. a clap usage-error exit or an unrelated failure), the script does not silently treat it as either 'has changesets' or 'no changesets' -- it emits an `::error::` annotation identifying the unexpected exit code and terminates the composite action step with a non-zero exit, rather than proceeding into either the release-PR or publish branch. Verifiable by stubbing the invocation to exit with a code outside {1, 2} (e.g. 127) and observing that the workflow step fails with an error annotation rather than continuing.\", \"is_error_case\": true},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-04\", \"criterion\": \"In the same step, when `callisto status --check` exits with ANY code other than 1 or 2 -- including 0 (which the real CLI never returns for `--check`), a clap usage-error exit, or any other unrelated failure -- the script does not silently treat it as either 'has changesets' or 'no changesets' and does not fall into a bare `exit $STATUS_EXIT` that could itself be 0 (success). It emits an `::error::` annotation identifying the unexpected exit code and terminates the composite action step with a guaranteed non-zero exit (e.g. `exit 1`, not a passthrough of `$STATUS_EXIT`), rather than proceeding into either the release-PR or publish branch. Verifiable by stubbing the invocation to exit with each of 0 and 127 in turn and confirming, for both, that the workflow step fails with a non-zero exit code and an error annotation, and never reaches the `if [[ \\\"$HAS_CHANGESETS\\\" == \\\"true\\\" ]]` branch at all (HAS_CHANGESETS must never be read as a truthy or falsy string while unset).\", \"is_error_case\": true},","     {\"id\": \"AC-05\", \"criterion\": \"crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` command states the `--check` contract as: 1 when at least one package has pending changesets, 2 when no changesets are pending, and does not claim 0 is returned under `--check` for any pending-changeset state. Verifiable by reading the doc comment text at main.rs (currently lines 19-21) and comparing it word-for-word against `check_exit_code_raw`'s actual behavior (status.rs:18-28: 1 for pending, 2 for none-pending, called only when `args.check` is true and there are no diagnostic errors).\", \"is_error_case\": false},","-    {\"id\": \"AC-06\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` (create_tags_with_options) processes a release whose tag already exists in the repository (`contains_tag` returns true) and that tag's actual current git target commit differs from `release.sha`, the `CreatedTag` entry pushed for that release reports a `sha` value equal to the tag's real, current target commit (obtained via `resolve_commit` against the tag ref) -- not `release.sha` -- such that a caller comparing the reported sha against the release plan's requested sha can detect the mismatch using only the JSON report, without any knowledge of the implementation. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` against a repository fixture where a tag `pkg@1.0.0` already points at commit A, the release plan requests sha B (A != B), and inspecting the `sha` field of the corresponding entry in the tool's JSON output: it must equal A, not B.\", \"is_error_case\": false},","-    {\"id\": \"AC-06b\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose tag already exists (`contains_tag` returns true) and `resolve_commit` against that tag's ref returns `Ok(None)` or an `Err(VcsError)`, the command does not fabricate a `sha` value for that release by falling back to `release.sha` -- it returns `Err(GraphError)` immediately and no `TagReport` is produced for that invocation. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` against a fixture where a tag exists per `contains_tag` but its ref cannot be resolved to a commit (e.g. a symbolic ref pointing at a missing object), and confirming the command exits non-zero rather than emitting a `CreatedTag` entry with `release.sha`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},","-    {\"id\": \"AC-07\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose tag does not yet exist (`contains_tag` returns false), the tag is created at `release.sha` and the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha`. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` against a repository fixture with no pre-existing tag for the release and confirming the reported `sha` matches the requested `release.sha` exactly.\", \"is_error_case\": false},","-    {\"id\": \"AC-08\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose tag already exists and already points at exactly `release.sha` (the idempotent-rerun case), the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha` and no error or warning is surfaced -- this is a genuine agreement, not a fabricated one, and must continue to report success. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` twice in succession against the same fixture and confirming the second run's reported `sha` for that release still equals `release.sha` with a zero exit code.\", \"is_error_case\": false},","-    {\"id\": \"AC-10\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` populates each `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` with `Some(section_text)` when the package's `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` file exists and contains a `## {version}` heading matching the release's version, where `section_text` is the content `extract_section` returns for that heading. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where a package's CHANGELOG.md contains a `## 1.2.3` section with known body text, releasing version 1.2.3, and confirming the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package equals the known body text.\", \"is_error_case\": false},","-    {\"id\": \"AC-11\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic, not an empty-string placeholder) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file does not exist at `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md`. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture with a publishable package that has no CHANGELOG.md file, and confirming the command exits 0 and the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package is `null`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},","-    {\"id\": \"AC-12\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file exists but contains no `## {version}` heading matching the release's version. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where CHANGELOG.md exists but has no `## {target-version}` heading, and confirming the command exits 0 and the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package is `null`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},","-    {\"id\": \"AC-12b\", \"criterion\": \"When a publishable package's resolved `pkg_dir` is empty (no manifest to derive a directory from), `plan_publish` treats `changelog_section` as `None` for that package without attempting to read any CHANGELOG.md -- it must not fall back to reading a workspace-root or unrelated-package CHANGELOG.md. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture containing a publishable package with zero manifests and a workspace-root CHANGELOG.md that does contain a matching `## {version}` heading, and confirming that package's `changelogSection` field is `null` (not the root file's content).\", \"is_error_case\": true},","-    {\"id\": \"AC-12c\", \"criterion\": \"When `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` exists but cannot be read as valid UTF-8, or fails to read for a reason other than not-found, `plan_publish` treats `changelog_section` as `None` for that package, adds a Warning-severity diagnostic naming the package and the read failure to the plan's diagnostics, and does not error the whole plan or panic. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a fixture where a package's CHANGELOG.md contains invalid UTF-8 bytes, and confirming the command exits 0, `changelogSection` is `null` for that package, and a diagnostic referencing the package appears in the JSON output's diagnostics.\", \"is_error_case\": true},","-    {\"id\": \"AC-13\", \"criterion\": \"None of the four fixes in this spec change the field names, field types, or presence/absence of any field in StatusReport, CreatedTag, TagReport, ReleaseEntry, or PublishPlan as serialized to JSON -- only the values written into the already-existing `sha` field (CreatedTag) and `changelog_section` field (ReleaseEntry) change, and only script/doc-comment logic and error handling change elsewhere. Verifiable by running `callisto schema` (or diffing the JSON Schema output) before and after the fix and confirming no field is added, removed, renamed, or retyped for these report types.\", \"is_error_case\": false}","+    {\"id\": \"AC-06\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` (create_tags_with_options), invoked WITHOUT `--dry-run` (permit granted, apply mode), processes a release whose per-release tag already exists in the repository (`contains_tag` returns true) and that tag's actual current git target commit differs from `release.sha`, the `CreatedTag` entry pushed for that release reports a `sha` value equal to the tag's real, current target commit (via `resolve_commit`) -- not `release.sha` -- such that a caller comparing the reported sha against the release plan's requested sha can detect the mismatch using only the JSON report. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` (no --dry-run) against a repository fixture where a tag `pkg@1.0.0` already points at commit A, the release plan requests sha B (A != B), and inspecting the `sha` field of the corresponding entry: it must equal A, not B.\", \"is_error_case\": false},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-06b\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag`, invoked WITHOUT `--dry-run`, processes a release whose per-release tag already exists and `resolve_commit` against that tag's ref returns `Ok(None)` or an `Err(VcsError)`, the command does not fabricate a `sha` value by falling back to `release.sha` -- it returns `Err(GraphError)` immediately and no `TagReport` is produced. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` (no --dry-run) against a fixture where a tag exists per `contains_tag` but its ref cannot be resolved to a commit, and confirming the command exits non-zero rather than emitting a `CreatedTag` entry with `release.sha`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-06c\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag --dry-run` previews a release whose per-release tag already exists at a commit different from `release.sha`, the previewed `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` equals the tag's real current target (via `resolve_commit`), not `release.sha` -- identical to AC-06's assertion -- and no git ref is created or moved by the preview. Verifiable by running `callisto tag --dry-run` against the same fixture as AC-06 (tag already at commit A, plan requests B, A != B) and confirming the previewed `sha` equals A, then confirming via `git rev-parse pkg@1.0.0` that the tag ref is still A after the dry-run (unchanged).\", \"is_error_case\": false},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-06d\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag --dry-run` processes a release whose per-release tag already exists and `resolve_commit` against that tag's ref returns `Ok(None)` or an `Err(VcsError)`, the preview does not fabricate a `sha` value by falling back to `release.sha` -- it returns `Err(GraphError)` immediately, identical to AC-06b's behavior. Verifiable using the same unresolvable-ref fixture as AC-06b, invoked with `--dry-run`, confirming the command exits non-zero.\", \"is_error_case\": true},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-07\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose per-release tag does not yet exist (`contains_tag` returns false), the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha` -- identically in apply mode (where the tag is also created at `release.sha`) and in `--dry-run` mode (where nothing is created but the same value is correctly previewed, since there is no pre-existing tag to conflict with). Verifiable by running `callisto tag` and separately `callisto tag --dry-run` against a repository fixture with no pre-existing tag for the release, confirming both report `sha` equal to the requested `release.sha`, and confirming (apply mode only) the tag is actually created there while (dry-run mode) no tag is created at all.\", \"is_error_case\": false},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-08\", \"criterion\": \"When `callisto tag` processes a release whose per-release tag already exists and already points at exactly `release.sha` (the idempotent-rerun case), the `CreatedTag` entry's `sha` field equals `release.sha` and no error or warning is surfaced -- identically in apply mode and `--dry-run` mode, since the existing and requested values already agree and there is nothing to fabricate either way. Verifiable by running `callisto tag` twice in succession (second run is the idempotent case) and separately running `callisto tag --dry-run` against the same post-first-run state, confirming all report `sha` equal to `release.sha` with a zero exit code.\", \"is_error_case\": false},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-10\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` populates each `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` with `Some(section_text)` when the package's `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` file exists, contains a `## {version}` heading matching the release's version, AND that heading's section has non-empty content after trimming -- where `section_text` is exactly what `extract_section` returns. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where a package's CHANGELOG.md contains a `## 1.2.3` section with known non-empty body text, releasing version 1.2.3, and confirming the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package equals the known body text.\", \"is_error_case\": false},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-10b\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not an empty string) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file exists and has a matching `## {version}` heading, but that section's content is empty or whitespace-only after trimming -- and adds the same `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound` Info-severity diagnostic as AC-12 for that package. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where CHANGELOG.md has a `## 1.2.3` heading immediately followed by only blank lines before the next heading (or end of file), and confirming `changelogSection` is `null` and a `ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic naming the package appears in the JSON output.\", \"is_error_case\": true},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-11\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file does not exist at `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md`, and adds a `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic at Info severity naming the package to the plan's diagnostics. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture with a publishable package that has no CHANGELOG.md file, and confirming the command exits 0, `changelogSection` is `null`, and a `ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic naming that package appears in the JSON output's diagnostics.\", \"is_error_case\": true},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-12\", \"criterion\": \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic) when the package's CHANGELOG.md file exists but contains no `## {version}` heading matching the release's version, and adds a `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic at Info severity naming the package. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where CHANGELOG.md exists but has no `## {target-version}` heading, and confirming the command exits 0, `changelogSection` is `null`, and a `ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic naming that package appears in the JSON output's diagnostics.\", \"is_error_case\": true},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-12b\", \"criterion\": \"When a publishable package's resolved `pkg_dir` is empty (no manifest to derive a directory from), `plan_publish` treats `changelog_section` as `None` for that package without attempting to read any CHANGELOG.md, and without emitting a `ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic (there is no meaningful package directory to name) -- it must not fall back to reading a workspace-root or unrelated-package CHANGELOG.md. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture containing a publishable package with zero manifests and a workspace-root CHANGELOG.md that does contain a matching `## {version}` heading, and confirming that package's `changelogSection` field is `null` (not the root file's content) and no diagnostic for that package is emitted.\", \"is_error_case\": true},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-12c\", \"criterion\": \"When `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md` exists but cannot be read as valid UTF-8, or fails to read for a reason other than not-found, `plan_publish` treats `changelog_section` as `None` for that package, adds a new `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError` (Warning severity) diagnostic naming the package and the read failure to the plan's diagnostics, and does not error the whole plan or panic. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a fixture where a package's CHANGELOG.md contains invalid UTF-8 bytes, and confirming the command exits 0, `changelogSection` is `null` for that package, and a `ChangelogReadError` diagnostic referencing the package appears in the JSON output's diagnostics.\", \"is_error_case\": true},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-13\", \"criterion\": \"None of the fixes in this spec change the field names, field types, or presence/absence of any struct field in StatusReport, CreatedTag, TagReport, ReleaseEntry, or PublishPlan as serialized to JSON -- only the values written into the already-existing `sha` field (CreatedTag) and `changelog_section` field (ReleaseEntry) change, plus script/doc-comment logic and error handling elsewhere. The sole schema-domain addition is one new `DiagnosticCode` enum variant (`ChangelogReadError`, for AC-12c) on the already-`#[non_exhaustive]` `code` field of `Diagnostic` -- an additive enum-variant expansion, not a struct field change, and is explicitly permitted by this criterion. Verifiable by running `callisto schema` (or diffing the JSON Schema output) before and after the fix and confirming no report struct gains, loses, renames, or retypes a field, and that the only diff in the `DiagnosticCode` enum's schema is the new `ChangelogReadError` variant appearing.\", \"is_error_case\": false}","   ],","   \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\""," }"]}],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ac2e83a9-cfb3-401c-ba0f-6746724fad75","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
