{"parentUuid":"40e43e0a-64dd-48a4-a9d3-74bcce6ff9c7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCSXqYhHXSP7PChtbbzF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Resubmitting the revised spec to canon-exit-gate."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":356,"cache_read_input_tokens":334292,"output_tokens":1368,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":356,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1368,"cache_read_input_tokens":334292,"cache_creation_input_tokens":356,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":356},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCSXn1s8bpnALV8D5X64","type":"assistant","uuid":"d5694eb7-ed9b-49e1-a02a-3fd8769eb095","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:42:20.280Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"d5694eb7-ed9b-49e1-a02a-3fd8769eb095","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCSXqYhHXSP7PChtbbzF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011JrHpkXfp7v1hUQoochkRY","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Re-exit-gate Track 4 spec (round 3)","subagent_type":"canon:exit-gate","prompt":"Do the gate review yourself directly in this invocation, do not delegate. Workspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto. Read the spec@1 from /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track4-draft.json (read it from disk, it's a valid JSON file).\n\nThis is retry_count: 2 (third submission). The prior round (retry_count 1) found six blockers, all addressed in this revision:\n1. The `--dry-run` path bypassed the whole tag-sha fix entirely (no existence check at all) -- added AC-06c/AC-06d as dry-run twins of AC-06/AC-06b, and rewrote the create_tags_with_options api_surface entry to describe both paths.\n2. The non_goals claim about the floating-major alias being \"always correct by construction\" was false for the dry-run path -- corrected by explaining WHY the floating-major alias is fundamentally not the same bug class (create_floating_major is called unconditionally on every apply run with no already-existed gate, so release.sha is deterministically correct in both modes, unlike the per-release tag which is genuinely left unmoved when it already exists) rather than claiming a apply-path-only fact.\n3. Exit-code-0 could silently fall through the Action script's bare `exit $STATUS_EXIT` and reach the publish branch with HAS_CHANGESETS unset -- AC-03 was deleted and merged into a rewritten AC-04 requiring a guaranteed non-zero exit (not a passthrough of $STATUS_EXIT) for ANY code other than 1/2, with both 0 and 127 as explicit test stubs.\n4. AC-12c's diagnostic code was unnamed and conflicted with a stale ChangelogSectionNotFound description -- named a new DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError variant (Warning severity) for the genuine read-failure case, distinct from ChangelogSectionNotFound (Info severity, reused for the not-found cases).\n5. AC-11/AC-12 were silent on whether a diagnostic is emitted -- now explicit: both emit DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound at Info severity.\n6. AC-10 was falsified by extract_section's real empty-content-returns-None behavor -- reworded to require non-empty trimmed content, and added AC-10b for the empty-section case (treated like AC-12: None + ChangelogSectionNotFound diagnostic).\n7. AC-13 was updated to explicitly permit the one additive DiagnosticCode enum variant while still prohibiting any report struct field change.\n\nVerify these fixes actually close what was found, re-verify every file:line citation against live code yourself (do not trust the spec or my summary), and check for any NEW issues these edits might have introduced -- particularly: does AC-06c's claim that resolve_commit lookup can happen in dry-run mode without mutating git state actually hold given the real code structure at tag.rs:53-80? Does the DiagnosticCode addition genuinely not require touching any report struct? Is Info the right severity tier for ChangelogSectionNotFound given how Severity/DiagnosticSeverity works elsewhere in this codebase (check crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs for the actual severity enum and how other Info-tier diagnostics are used, if any exist, to confirm Info is a real, used tier and not something I invented)?\n\nIf retry_count exceeds 3 this should escalate to human review rather than another gate cycle -- but this is retry 2, so proceed with a normal verdict."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":356,"cache_read_input_tokens":334292,"output_tokens":1368,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":356,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1368,"cache_read_input_tokens":334292,"cache_creation_input_tokens":356,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":356},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCSXn1s8bpnALV8D5X64","type":"assistant","uuid":"aaba0e82-4f72-4f68-966e-b3c008403801","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:42:34.181Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"aaba0e82-4f72-4f68-966e-b3c008403801","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b57dcde8-a197-4c58-90f9-73fff9d7a315","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011JrHpkXfp7v1hUQoochkRY","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: ac51f537d076f5d28 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'ac51f537d076f5d28', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/ac51f537d076f5d28.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"74af7b47-dea3-4557-b85b-4a2d3515af8f","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:42:36.772Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"ac51f537d076f5d28","description":"Re-exit-gate Track 4 spec (round 3)","resolvedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","prompt":"Do the gate review yourself directly in this invocation, do not delegate. Workspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto. Read the spec@1 from /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track4-draft.json (read it from disk, it's a valid JSON file).\n\nThis is retry_count: 2 (third submission). The prior round (retry_count 1) found six blockers, all addressed in this revision:\n1. The `--dry-run` path bypassed the whole tag-sha fix entirely (no existence check at all) -- added AC-06c/AC-06d as dry-run twins of AC-06/AC-06b, and rewrote the create_tags_with_options api_surface entry to describe both paths.\n2. The non_goals claim about the floating-major alias being \"always correct by construction\" was false for the dry-run path -- corrected by explaining WHY the floating-major alias is fundamentally not the same bug class (create_floating_major is called unconditionally on every apply run with no already-existed gate, so release.sha is deterministically correct in both modes, unlike the per-release tag which is genuinely left unmoved when it already exists) rather than claiming a apply-path-only fact.\n3. Exit-code-0 could silently fall through the Action script's bare `exit $STATUS_EXIT` and reach the publish branch with HAS_CHANGESETS unset -- AC-03 was deleted and merged into a rewritten AC-04 requiring a guaranteed non-zero exit (not a passthrough of $STATUS_EXIT) for ANY code other than 1/2, with both 0 and 127 as explicit test stubs.\n4. AC-12c's diagnostic code was unnamed and conflicted with a stale ChangelogSectionNotFound description -- named a new DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError variant (Warning severity) for the genuine read-failure case, distinct from ChangelogSectionNotFound (Info severity, reused for the not-found cases).\n5. AC-11/AC-12 were silent on whether a diagnostic is emitted -- now explicit: both emit DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound at Info severity.\n6. AC-10 was falsified by extract_section's real empty-content-returns-None behavor -- reworded to require non-empty trimmed content, and added AC-10b for the empty-section case (treated like AC-12: None + ChangelogSectionNotFound diagnostic).\n7. AC-13 was updated to explicitly permit the one additive DiagnosticCode enum variant while still prohibiting any report struct field change.\n\nVerify these fixes actually close what was found, re-verify every file:line citation against live code yourself (do not trust the spec or my summary), and check for any NEW issues these edits might have introduced -- particularly: does AC-06c's claim that resolve_commit lookup can happen in dry-run mode without mutating git state actually hold given the real code structure at tag.rs:53-80? Does the DiagnosticCode addition genuinely not require touching any report struct? Is Info the right severity tier for ChangelogSectionNotFound given how Severity/DiagnosticSeverity works elsewhere in this codebase (check crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs for the actual severity enum and how other Info-tier diagnostics are used, if any exist, to confirm Info is a real, used tier and not something I invented)?\n\nIf retry_count exceeds 3 this should escalate to human review rather than another gate cycle -- but this is retry 2, so proceed with a normal verdict.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/ac51f537d076f5d28.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"aaba0e82-4f72-4f68-966e-b3c008403801","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
