{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01HxMVynBHufrDkmRHgmKgcH","lastSequenceNum":6964,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"51bbaacc-0444-4534-8c20-60e34d1bf6a5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track4-draft.json","snippet":"1\t{\n2\t  \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\",\n3\t  \"purpose\": \"Correct four confirmed-live correctness bugs in the release pipeline's CLI-to-Action contract so the shipped GitHub Action reliably reaches release-PR-creation and publish on real runs, instead of erroring out on the normal 'pending changesets' case or silently reporting fabricated state (a stale tag sha, a missing changelog excerpt) -- in both apply mode and `--dry-run` preview mode.\",\n4\t  \"scope\": \"Four fixes, all within the callisto CLI/graph crates and the composite Action script: (1) .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's `callisto status --check` exit-code branching in the 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step, including the unrecognised-exit-code path (0 included); (2) crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's top-of-file exit-code-contract doc comment for the `status` subcommand; (3) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs's `create_tags_with_options`, specifically the `sha` field written into the `CreatedTag` pushed for the per-release tag, in both the apply path (permit granted, tag.rs:82-117) and the `--dry-run` preview path (permit is None, tag.rs:53-80); (4) crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs's `plan_publish`, specifically the `changelog_section` field on `ReleaseEntry` (currently hardcoded `None`), which must be populated via `callisto_changelog::extract_section` (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102) reading each package's `CHANGELOG.md` from its resolved `pkg_dir`, plus the two new `DiagnosticCode` cases that surface non-fatal changelog conditions.\",\n5\t  \"non_goals\": [\n6\t    \"Track 6-mechanical's JSON report field-shape mismatches (StatusReport, StatusPackageRecord, SnapshotReport, ComposePrBodyReport, CreatedTag's other fields, InitReport, ValidateReport) -- separate track, not touched here.\",\n7\t    \"Any change to callisto-model's SCHEMA_VERSION constant or any report type's struct fields -- all four fixes reuse existing fields (CreatedTag.sha, ReleaseEntry.changelog_section) or correct logic/prose; the one addition (a new DiagnosticCode variant for AC-12c) extends an already-`#[non_exhaustive]` enum additively and does not require a version bump under this project's current pre-first-publish posture (no real external consumer of this wire format exists yet).\",\n8\t    \"The `callisto publish` command's actual registry-publishing logic (cargo/npm/pypi clients) -- untouched.\",\n9\t    \"Any change to how the Action script parses `plan-publish`'s or `matrix`'s JSON output via `jq`, beyond the status-check exit-code branching fix -- those jq parse sites are already confirmed working and out of scope.\",\n10\t    \"Adding a dedicated CLI flag or new exit code to distinguish clap usage errors (exit 2) from 'no changesets pending' (exit 2) at the `callisto` binary level -- clap's own exit-code convention is not renegotiated by this track; the fix for the collision lives entirely in the Action script's ability to tell the two apart, not by changing what the CLI emits.\",\n11\t    \"Any change to `callisto status`'s non-`--check` (plain) exit-code behavior -- confirmed correct already (0 on success regardless of pending changesets, 1 on error); only the `--check` branch and its doc comment are in scope.\",\n12\t    \"Resolving what `changelog_section` should contain when a package has a CHANGELOG.md with malformed markdown (e.g. no `##` headings at all) -- that is the documented 'heading not found' case already covered by AC-12.\",\n13\t    \"The floating-major alias tag's CreatedTag.sha (tag.rs:99-107 apply path, tag.rs:64-69 dry-run path) -- this is NOT the same bug class as the per-release tag. `create_floating_major` is called unconditionally on every apply run regardless of the alias's prior existence or target (tag.rs:102, no `already_existed`-style gate), so `release.sha` is deterministically what the alias becomes after any real apply run -- there is no 'different real answer' being hidden, unlike the per-release tag which is genuinely left unmoved when it already exists. Reporting `release.sha` for the floating-major alias in BOTH apply mode (where it is now true by construction) and `--dry-run` mode (where it accurately previews what the unconditional apply step will produce) is therefore correct as-is and out of scope for this fix.\"\n14\t  ],\n15\t  \"api_surface\": [\n16\t    {\n17\t      \"name\": \"check_exit_code_raw\",\n18\t      \"signature\": \"fn check_exit_code_raw(report: &StatusReport) -> u8 (crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/status.rs:18)\",\n19\t      \"description\": \"Already-correct, unchanged by this spec: returns 1 when any package has a non-empty pending_changesets list, 2 otherwise. `handle` (status.rs:53-54) returns ExitCode::from(this value) when --check is set and there are no diagnostic errors. This is the ground truth the Action script and the main.rs doc comment must both agree with.\"\n20\t    },\n21\t    {\n22\t      \"name\": \"create_tags_with_options\",\n23\t      \"signature\": \"fn create_tags_with_options<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(ws: &Workspace<'_, R, D>, plan: &PublishPlan, opts: &TagOptions, permit: Option<&ApplyPermit>) -> Result<TagReport, GraphError> (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs:30)\",\n24\t      \"description\": \"Two structurally parallel paths must both use the same already-existing-tag detection and sha resolution for the PER-RELEASE tag only (not the floating-major alias, see non_goals): the apply path (permit is Some, tag.rs:82-117) currently checks `ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str)` (tag.rs:82) to decide whether to call `git.create_tag`, but unconditionally pushes `CreatedTag { sha: release.sha.clone(), .. }` (tag.rs:113-117) regardless of that check's outcome; the dry-run path (permit is None, tag.rs:53-80) currently performs NO existence check at all and unconditionally pushes `release.sha` (tag.rs:74-78). Both paths must be fixed identically: when the per-release tag already exists at a commit different from `release.sha`, the reported `sha` must be the tag's real current target via `GitDataSource::resolve_commit(&self, refname: &str) -> Result<Option<CommitSha>, VcsError>` (crates/callisto-vcs/src/access.rs:79, reachable via `ws.git_access()`, tag.rs:48) -- not `release.sha` -- in BOTH modes; the dry-run path must perform this check and lookup without mutating any git state (no `git.create_tag` call, matching its existing preview-only contract). When `resolve_commit` returns `Ok(None)` or `Err(VcsError)` for an already-existing tag, in either mode, `create_tags_with_options` must return `Err(GraphError)` immediately (fail-fast, e.g. via `GraphError::Vcs` for the `Err` case and an explicit error construction for the `Ok(None)` case) rather than falling back to `release.sha` -- consistent with this function's existing git-access-failure handling and with this spec's purpose of never fabricating reported state, in a preview or otherwise.\"\n25\t    },\n26\t    {\n27\t      \"name\": \"extract_section\",\n28\t      \"signature\": \"fn extract_section<'a>(changelog: &'a str, version: &Version) -> Option<&'a str> (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102)\",\n\n... [92 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f422575c-3b87-437c-9b25-28db293ef9e8","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:47:12.835Z","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
