{"parentUuid":"6655e5d9-90c7-49ac-95e8-fc4a50a4a656","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCcw2vryxtVucJiradLY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Rwby7hS1SvZkL1LfXSVLo5","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Re-exit-gate Track 4 spec (round 4 retry)","subagent_type":"canon:exit-gate","prompt":"Do the gate review yourself directly in this invocation, do not delegate. Workspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto. Read the spec@1 from /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track4-draft.json (read it from disk).\n\nThis is retry_count: 3 (fourth submission — a prior verdict on an earlier draft said a fourth fail must escalate to human review, so this needs to be a genuinely thorough final check). A prior gate round (retry_count 2, on an earlier version of this same spec) found three blockers, all addressed in the version now on disk:\n\n1. BLK-01 (critical): AC-10b/AC-11/AC-12 and the extract_section api_surface entry specified a nonexistent \"Info\" severity tier -- DiagnosticSeverity only has Warning/Error. Fixed: all three (plus AC-12c, which had the identical latent bug even though the prior gate didn't explicitly flag it) now specify Warning severity throughout.\n2. BLK-02 (major): AC-10b/AC-11/AC-12/AC-12b's verification language said \"confirming changelogSection is null\", but ReleaseEntry.changelog_section carries skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\" (plan.rs:116), so a None value is OMITTED from the JSON, never serialized as null. Fixed: all four (plus AC-12c, same underlying field/bug, proactively fixed) now say \"confirming the changelogSection key is absent from that release entry... not present as null\".\n3. BLK-03 (major): AC-06b/AC-06d described a fixture (\"a tag exists per contains_tag but its ref cannot be resolved\") that cannot be constructed via the real CLI/git, since any tag list_tags returns will also resolve under resolve_commit for a real repository. Fixed: both now explicitly name the actual seam -- constructing a Workspace over a stub CommandRunner whose tag-listing reports the tag exists while its `git rev-parse --verify --quiet <ref>^{commit}` invocation is made to fail/error, at the callisto-graph level, not via the CLI.\n\nVerify all three fixes actually hold against live code:\n- Re-check DiagnosticSeverity's real variants (crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs, search for \"pub enum DiagnosticSeverity\").\n- Re-check plan.rs:116's serde attribute on ReleaseEntry.changelog_section.\n- Re-check whether a stub-CommandRunner-based fixture is actually constructible for create_tags_with_options given its real signature -- grep for existing stub/mock CommandRunner test patterns in crates/callisto-graph/tests/ or src/cascade.rs's test module to confirm this is a real, already-used testing pattern in this codebase, not something invented.\n\nAlso do a genuinely fresh full pass over every other acceptance criterion (AC-01 through AC-13, all of them, not just the three that changed) checking for anything else missed across the three prior rounds -- this is meant to be the final, most thorough pass before human escalation would be needed.\n\nWork efficiently -- read files directly with targeted greps/reads rather than broad exploration, and produce your verdict JSON as soon as you have enough evidence. If this passes, that's the end of Track 4's canon pipeline stage -- it moves to vector:planner next."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":352115,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1567,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":218},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":352115,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_avail