op as the pkg_dir code at `publish.rs:289-298`). That resolves the override bug and dissolves AC-12b's empty-directory case entirely.\n\n## On escalation\n\nThe `verdict@1` schema admits only `pass|fail` with `additionalProperties: false`, so `escalate` is not representable — the verdict field is `fail` and the escalation is carried in `verdict_summary`. I recommend human review before a fifth round. Not because the blockers are unfixable — both are precisely actionable — but because the pattern has not converged: four rounds have each surfaced a *different* criterion contradicting live code. That recurrence points at a process defect (criteria composed without reading the implementation) rather than something a fifth patch cycle fixes.\n\nNon-blocking note: AC-03 and AC-09 are absent from the criteria list. Numbering gaps are not a gate condition and AC-04 appears to absorb the exit-0 case, but downstream planning shouldn't read the gaps as missing input.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>82918</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>28</tool_uses><duration_ms>330962</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"e3ba217a-485f-471f-af79-f53a70a26216","timestamp":"2026-08-19T19:04:36.794Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
