{"parentUuid":"fafaa640-065f-4903-a825-d15c117a6819","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCe1uvRyoA3qQorFPxQh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B9L89B96L6TWt8HALSCeCy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad\npython3 << 'PYEOF'\nimport json\n\nwith open('spec-track4-draft.json') as f:\n    spec = json.load(f)\n\n# Fix scope field\nspec['scope'] = spec['scope'].replace(\n    \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs's `plan_publish`, specifically the `changelog_section` field on `ReleaseEntry` (currently hardcoded `None`), which must be populated via `callisto_changelog::extract_section` (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102) reading each package's `CHANGELOG.md` from its resolved `pkg_dir`, plus the two new `DiagnosticCode` cases that surface non-fatal changelog conditions.\",\n    \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs's `plan_publish`, specifically the `changelog_section` field on `ReleaseEntry` (currently hardcoded `None`), which must be populated via `callisto_changelog::extract_section` (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102) reading the package's already-resolved changelog file at `pkg.changelog` (`Package.changelog: Option<PathBuf>`, always `Some`, workspace-root-relative -- the same field `callisto version`'s changelog-rendering step already uses at commands/version.rs:148, honoring any `[[package]] changelog = \\\"...\\\"` override), plus the two new `DiagnosticCode` cases that surface non-fatal changelog conditions.\"\n)\n\n# Fix extract_section api_surface entry\nfor entry in spec['api_surface']:\n    if entry['name'] == 'extract_section':\n        entry['description'] = (\n            \"Already-implemented and already-unit-tested. Finds the `## {version}` heading in `changelog` and returns the slice of content between that heading and the next `## ` heading (or end of file), trimmed, or `None` if the heading is not found OR the matched section's trimmed content is empty (write.rs:131-136: `if raw_section.is_empty() { None } else { Some(raw_section) }`). \"\n            \"`plan_publish` must call this with the content of the package's resolved changelog file at `pkg.changelog` (crates/callisto-model/src/package.rs:17, `Option<PathBuf>` but always `Some` by construction -- populated in walk.rs:387-392 as either a `[[package]] changelog = \\\"...\\\"` override path or the default co-located `CHANGELOG.md`, workspace-root-relative) and `ver` (the release version) -- the identical field `plan_version` already reads at commands/version.rs:148 to decide where to render changelog entries, so the read and write sides always agree on which file is 'the' changelog for a package. \"\n            \"Three distinct non-fatal outcomes, each leaving `changelog_section` as `None` and never erroring or panicking the whole plan: (a) no file exists yet at the `pkg.changelog` path (AC-11) -- the common case before a package's first release, since `callisto version` creates the file on first write, (b) file exists but `extract_section` returns `None` -- no matching heading, or a matching heading with empty content (AC-12) -- both add a `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound` (crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs, already exists, currently reserved/unemitted) diagnostic at Warning severity naming the package, (c) file exists but fails to read as valid UTF-8 or fails for a reason other than not-found (AC-12c) -- adds a NEW `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError` variant (Warning severity) naming the package and the read failure.\"\n        )\n\n# Update AC-10, AC-10b, AC-11, AC-12, AC-12c wording from pkg_dir/CHANGELOG.md to pkg.changelog\nac_map = {ac['id']: ac for ac in spec['acceptance_criteria']}\n\nac_map['AC-10']['criterion'] = (\n    \"`plan_publish` populates each `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` with `Some(section_text)` when the file at the package's resolved `pkg.changelog` path exists, contains a `## {version}` heading matching the release's version, AND that heading's section has non-empty content after trimming -- where `section_text` is exactly what `extract_section` returns. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where a package's changelog file (at its resolved `pkg.changelog` path, e.g. co-located `CHANGELOG.md`) contains a `## 1.2.3` section with known non-empty body text, releasing version 1.2.3, and confirming the JSON output's `changelogSection` field for that package equals the known body text.\"\n)\n\nac_map['AC-10b']['criterion'] = (\n    \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not an empty string) when the file at the package's resolved `pkg.changelog` path exists and has a matching `## {version}` heading, but that section's content is empty or whitespace-only after trimming -- and adds a `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound` Warning-severity diagnostic as AC-12 for that package. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where the package's changelog file has a `## 1.2.3` heading immediately followed by only blank lines before the next heading (or end of file), and confirming the `changelogSection` key is absent from that release entry (per plan.rs:116's `skip_serializing_if`, not present as `null`) and a `ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic naming the package appears in the JSON output's diagnostics.\"\n)\n\nac_map['AC-11']['criterion'] = (\n    \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic) when no file exists yet at the package's resolved `pkg.changelog` path (the common case before a package's first release), and adds a `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic at Warning severity naming the package to the plan's diagnostics. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture with a publishable package whose resolved changelog file does not exist on disk, and confirming the command exits 0, the `changelogSection` key is absent from that release entry (per plan.rs:116's `skip_serializing_if`, not present as `null`), and a `ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic naming that package appears in the JSON output's diagnostics.\"\n)\n\nac_map['AC-12']['criterion'] = (\n    \"`plan_publish` leaves `ReleaseEntry.changelog_section` as `None` (not an error, not a panic) when the file at the package's resolved `pkg.changelog` path exists but contains no `## {version}` heading matching the release's version, and adds a `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic at Warning severity naming the package. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a workspace fixture where the package's changelog file exists but has no `## {target-version}` heading, and confirming the command exits 0, the `changelogSection` key is absent from that release entry (per plan.rs:116's `skip_serializing_if`, not present as `null`), and a `ChangelogSectionNotFound` diagnostic naming that package appears in the JSON output's diagnostics.\"\n)\n\nac_map['AC-12c']['criterion'] = (\n    \"When the file at the package's resolved `pkg.changelog` path exists but cannot be read as valid UTF-8, or fails to read for a reason other than not-found, `plan_publish` treats `changelog_section` as `None` for that package, adds a new `DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError` (Warning severity) diagnostic naming the package and the read failure to the plan's diagnostics, and does not error the whole plan or panic. Verifiable by running `callisto plan-publish --format json` against a fixture where a package's changelog file contains invalid UTF-8 bytes, and confirming the command exits 0, the `changelogSection` key is absent from that release entry (per plan.rs:116's `skip_serializing_if`, not present as `null`), and a `ChangelogReadError` diagnostic referencing the package appears in the JSON output's diagnostics.\"\n)\n\n# Delete AC-12b entirely -- its concern (avoiding an accidental fallback read from an\n# empty/wrong directory) is structurally moot once pkg.changelog (an already-resolved,\n# always-Some, purpose-built field) is used instead of deriving a path from pkg_dir.\ndel ac_map['AC-12b']\n\nspec['acceptance_criteria'] = list(ac_map.values())\n\n# Update AC-13's guard criterion: no longer needs to mention pkg_dir-derived empty case\nfor ac in spec['acceptance_criteria']:\n    if ac['id'] == 'AC-13':\n        pass  # AC-13's text doesn't reference pkg_dir/AC-12b specifically, leave as-is\n\nwith open('spec-track4-draft.json', 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(spec, f, indent=2)\n\nprint(\"done, AC count:\", len(spec['acceptance_criteria']))\nPYEOF\npython3 -c \"import json; s=json.load(open('spec-track4-draft.json')); print([a['id'] for a in s['acceptance_criteria']])\"","description":"Apply Package.changelog fix and remove moot AC-12b"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":910,"cache_read_input_tokens":360629,"output_tokens":4661,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1192},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":910,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4661,"cache_read_input_tokens":360629,"cache_creation_input_tokens":910,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":910},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCe1tMvN31gvb4vkYPSy","type":"assistant","uuid":"3897e155-053b-4a7b-8757-2fca6b13f59c","timestamp":"2026-08-19T19:13:34.498Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","