{"parentUuid":"da8793ba-b087-4e8a-bdb3-91566d015dcc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCe648QtMsEziAkMHCbc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016gvYJLcwTQTbQBgCsVUWco","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Exit-gate Track 4 spec (final round)","subagent_type":"canon:exit-gate","prompt":"Do the gate review yourself directly in this invocation, do not delegate. Workspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto. Read the spec@1 from /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track4-draft.json (read it from disk).\n\nThis is retry_count: 3, submitted as this track's final round -- a prior verdict (retry_count 3, on an earlier version of this spec) recommended human escalation rather than a fifth automated cycle, finding two new blockers on top of three already-fixed ones from earlier rounds. The user was consulted and explicitly chose to attempt one more, well-targeted fix rather than escalate, since both blockers traced to a single, now precisely-diagnosed root cause. Both are fixed in the version now on disk:\n\n1. (was critical) The changelog-read side (AC-10/10b/11/12/12c) previously derived a path as `{pkg_dir}/CHANGELOG.md`, ignoring `Package.changelog: Option<PathBuf>` -- the already-resolved, user-overridable changelog path that `callisto version`'s write side already uses (commands/version.rs:148, `if let Some(ch_path) = &pkg.changelog`). Verified via walk.rs:387-392 that `pkg.changelog` is ALWAYS `Some` (either a `[[package]] changelog = \"...\"` override path or a default, both wrapped in Some, no None branch exists). Fixed: every affected criterion, the `extract_section` api_surface entry, and the `scope` field now reference `pkg.changelog` directly instead of deriving a path from `pkg_dir`.\n\n2. (was major) AC-12b's fixture (\"a publishable package with zero manifests\") was unconstructible, and its underlying concern (avoiding a fallback read from an empty/wrong directory) is now structurally moot once `pkg.changelog` -- an already-resolved, purpose-built, always-`Some` field -- replaces the `pkg_dir`-derivation approach entirely. Fixed: AC-12b is deleted outright, not patched. The spec now has 16 acceptance criteria: AC-01, AC-02, AC-04, AC-05, AC-06, AC-06b, AC-06c, AC-06d, AC-07, AC-08, AC-10, AC-10b, AC-11, AC-12, AC-12c, AC-13.\n\nDo a genuinely fresh, thorough pass:\n1. Verify Package.changelog's field and its always-Some population logic yourself (crates/callisto-model/src/package.rs:17, crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs:387-392).\n2. Verify commands/version.rs:148's usage matches the spec's claim that read and write sides now agree on which file is \"the\" changelog.\n3. Confirm AC-12b's deletion doesn't leave any orphaned reference elsewhere in the document (non_goals, scope, other criteria).\n4. Re-verify every one of the three previously-fixed blockers from round 2 still holds in this version (DiagnosticSeverity has only Warning/Error; the changelogSection key-absent-not-null language; the stub-CommandRunner fixture for AC-06b/AC-06d is real and constructible) -- don't assume they're untouched by this round's edits, confirm directly.\n5. Do a full fresh read of every remaining acceptance criterion (AC-01, AC-02, AC-04 through AC-13) against live code, not just the changed ones.\n\nWork efficiently -- targeted greps/reads, not broad exploration. Produce your verdict as soon as you have sufficient evidence rather than exhaustively re-deriving everything from zero."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":383,"cache_read_input_tokens":367199,"output_tokens":1391,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":383,"ephemeral