{"parentUuid":"fe0d5f9b-e4a7-474b-90e2-2d44919c8bd7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCeZdfGvW64LxQeTTTYb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015mv7ENhvNENk43eLS6d1tg","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Plan Track 4 implementation","subagent_type":"vector:planner","prompt":"Produce a plan@1 for the spec at .claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS.json (workspace root /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto, read spec_file_path from disk). Do the planning work YOURSELF in this invocation and return the plan@1 JSON object directly as your final output — do not describe a plan to produce it, and do not delegate to another agent.\n\nThis spec passed canon-exit-gate on its 5th attempt after unusually heavy adversarial review (5 rounds, escalating from a compile-error-class design flaw through a missing dry-run path, an invented severity tier, a serde null-vs-absent mismatch, an unconstructible test fixture, to a changelog-path derivation that ignored an existing resolved field). Trust the spec's 16 acceptance criteria and its api_surface section's mechanism descriptions as precisely accurate — every file:line citation was independently re-verified against live code in the final passing round — but still verify each claim yourself against the live code before writing each task's failing test, since code can drift even between a passing gate and planning, and this spec in particular has a well-established history of small drifts.\n\nFour independent fixes covered by the 16 criteria, which should become roughly 4 task clusters (dependency order: none of these four fixes depend on each other, they touch entirely disjoint files — you can sequence them in any order, but each fix internally has its own small dependency chain):\n\n1. **Action script exit-code branching** (AC-01, AC-02, AC-04) + **stale doc comment** (AC-05): .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step needs its if/elif/else chain rewritten so exit 1 → HAS_CHANGESETS=true, exit 2 → HAS_CHANGESETS=false, and anything else (including 0) → guaranteed non-zero step failure with an ::error:: annotation, never a passthrough `exit $STATUS_EXIT`. main.rs's doc comment (lines ~19-21) needs correcting to match the already-correct status.rs contract. Since this is bash, not Rust, plan the test/verification as: read the script's branching logic against the exit-code table, and/or construct stub invocations (replacing the callisto binary call with a shell stub exiting a given code) and assert which branch's output appears — the spec's own AC verification methods describe this precisely, follow them.\n\n2. **Tag fabricated-sha fix, apply mode** (AC-06, AC-06b) + **dry-run mode** (AC-06c, AC-06d) + **regression proofs** (AC-07, AC-08): crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs's create_tags_with_options needs both its apply path (permit Some, tag.rs:82-117) and dry-run path (permit None, tag.rs:53-80) to check contains_tag and, when true and the real target differs from release.sha, use GitDataSource::resolve_commit to report the true sha instead — fail-fast (Err(GraphError)) when resolve_commit returns Ok(None) or Err in either mode. AC-06b/AC-06d's tests need a stub CommandRunner fixture (the spec's api_surface and AC text describe the exact seam: stub git tag-listing to report the tag exists while stubbing `git rev-parse --verify --quiet <ref>^{commit}` to fail — cite crates/callisto-graph/tests/tags_laziness_test.rs and crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs's FakeRevParseRunner as existing precedent for this exact stubbing pattern in this codebase, use them as a model).\n\n3. **changelog_section population**: crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs's plan_publish needs to read `pkg.changelog` (Package.changelog: Option<PathBuf>, always Some by construction per walk.rs:387-392) via callisto_changelog::extract_section (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs:102) instead of hardcoding None, covering: found-with-content (AC-10), found-but-empty-section (AC-10b), file-doesn't-exist (AC-11), file-exists-no-matching-heading (AC-12), file-exists-unreadable/non-UTF8 (AC-12c) — the last two needing DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound (already exists, reserved, unemitted) at Warning severity for AC-10b/AC-11/AC-12, and a NEW DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError variant (Warning severity, needs adding to crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs's #[non_exhaustive] enum) for AC-12c.\n\n4. **Guard/regression proof** (AC-13): confirm via `callisto schema` diffing that no report struct field changed shape, and that the only schema delta is the new ChangelogReadError enum variant.\n\nNo task should exceed 15 minutes. Every one of the 16 acceptance criteria must appear in at least one task's covers_criteria. Output the plan@1 object directly (the calling process will persist it to .claude/plans/ and route it through vector:challenger next)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1557,"cache_read_input_tokens":371723,"output_tokens":1873,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1557,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1873,"cache_read_input_tokens":371723,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1557,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1557},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCeZbb1Z8urwKpuHvYde","type":"assistant","uuid":"6d7da069-130e-4038-a88e-9cd10679ddf8","timestamp":"2026-08-19T19:20:25.011Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gab