{"parentUuid":"bc4ac8e2-cbe9-4642-b639-136119a99511","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCftsoj2Jg8iGD4o63qq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1735,"cache_read_input_tokens":405781,"output_tokens":29003,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":373},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1735,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":29003,"cache_read_input_tokens":405781,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1735,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1735},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCftrBFNBsRXMN5f26xG","type":"assistant","uuid":"5dafa0dc-cd67-49b3-b1ec-b399bf296872","timestamp":"2026-08-19T19:37:38.616Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"5dafa0dc-cd67-49b3-b1ec-b399bf296872","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCftsoj2Jg8iGD4o63qq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ugati5vviURe6jYtnx8SfS","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/plan-track4-draft.json","content":"{\n  \"artifact_type\": \"plan@1\",\n  \"id\": \"PLAN-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"spec_file_path\": \".claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS.json\",\n  \"spec_hash\": \"sha256:26502a95f78494d2c1759752e86543a70d0a22588ef4dbec18f2324752e52255\",\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Verified every api_surface claim against live code before writing tasks (all citations held: action.yml lines 90-97 have exactly the described exit-0-true/exit-2-false/else-passthrough bug with no exit-1 branch at all; main.rs:19-21 wrongly claims 0 under --check with pending changesets; tag.rs:82-117/53-80 unconditionally push release.sha; publish.rs:427 hardcodes None; DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound exists unemitted at diagnostic.rs:144, ChangelogReadError does not exist yet; ReleaseEntry.changelog_section already has skip_serializing_if at plan.rs:116-117; Package.changelog is workspace-root-relative, always Some, set at walk.rs:323/387-392). Four disjoint clusters, sequenced arbitrarily since none depend on each other, but each cluster's internal tasks are ordered (foundation before use, e.g. the new DiagnosticCode variant before the code that emits it). Two tasks (T5, T8/T9) are pure regression-proof tasks whose assertions pass immediately because the single cohesive fix in the preceding task already satisfies them -- documented explicitly per task rather than forcing an artificial red phase that would require temporarily breaking working code. Stub CommandRunner fixtures for tag.rs (T3/T4) follow the exact pattern of FakeRevParseRunner in aggregate.rs and CountingTagListRunner in tags_laziness_test.rs: a non-git-discoverable tempdir forces GitAccess through the CommandRunner shell fallback deterministically, and TagIndex::build's contains_tag check is satisfied by stubbing `git tag --list` while resolve_commit's three outcomes (Some/None/Err) are satisfied by stubbing `git rev-parse --verify --quiet <tag>^{commit}`. AC-07/AC-08 regression (T5) instead uses a real git repo, since those scenarios exercise the actual tag-creation write path and native gix idempotent-read path that a stub would have to reimplement pointlessly. The AC-13 schema guard (T10) uses field/variant sets captured directly from the live, unmodified binary via `callisto schema --type <X>` before any code in this plan was written, so the expected sets are the true pre-fix baseline, not a guess.\",\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T1\",\n      \"cluster\": \"action-script-exit-code\",\n      \"description\": \"Fix action.yml's 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step so exit 1 -> HAS_CHANGESETS=true, exit 2 -> HAS_CHANGESETS=false, and any other exit code (including 0) fails the step with an ::error:: annotation and a guaranteed non-zero exit, never a passthrough of $STATUS_EXIT.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-01\", \"AC-02\", \"AC-04\"],\n      \"files\": [\".github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml\", \".github/actions/callisto-action/tests/test_status_check_branching.sh\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Current code (action.yml:90-97) has no branch for exit 1 at all -- exit 0 is wrongly mapped to HAS_CHANGESETS=true, and the else branch does `exit $STATUS_EXIT` which is a passthrough that could itself be 0. Composite-action bash isn't unit-testable via cargo, so this task adds a small, self-contained bash test that extracts the exact run-body text between the step's `::group::1. Inspecting Workspace Status` and its matching `::endgroup::` markers straight out of action.yml (so the test can never drift from the real file) and executes it with a stubbed `callisto` shell function standing in for the binary, for exit codes 1, 2, 0, and 127.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"create\",\n        \"file_path\": \".github/actions/callisto-action/tests/test_status_check_branching.sh\",\n        \"content\": \"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Regression test for the \\\"Inspecting Workspace Status\\\" step's exit-code\\n# branching in action.yml (AC-01, AC-02, AC-04). Extracts the exact run-body\\n# text between the step's ::group::1. Inspecting Workspace Status marker and\\n# its matching ::endgroup:: marker directly out of action.yml, so this test\\n# always exercises the file's current real logic -- it cannot drift from it.\\nset -u\\nACTION_YML=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\\\")/..\\\" && pwd)/action.yml\\\"\\n\\nextract_snippet() {\\n  sed -n '/::group::1\\\\. Inspecting Workspace Status/,/::endgroup::/p' \\\"$ACTION_YML\\\" | sed '1d;$d'\\n}\\n\\nrun_case() {\\n  local stub_exit=\\\"$1\\\"\\n  local tmp_script\\n  tmp_script=\\\"$(mktemp)\\\"\\n  {\\n    echo \\\"callisto() { exit ${stub_exit}; }\\\"\\n    extract_snippet\\n    echo 'echo \\\"__HAS_CHANGESETS=${HAS_CHANGESETS-<unset>}__\\\"'\\n  } > \\\"$tmp_script\\\"\\n  bash \\\"$tmp_script\\\"\\n  local code=$?\\n  rm -f \\\"$tmp_script\\\"\\n  return $code\\n}\\n\\nfail=0\\n\\n# AC-01: exit 1 -> HAS_CHANGESETS=true, step must not fail.\\nout=$(run_case 1); code=$?\\nif [[ $code -ne 0 ]] || [[ \\\"$out\\\" != *\\\"__HAS_CHANGESETS=true__\\\"* ]]; then\\n  echo \\\"FAIL AC-01: exit 1 case: code=$code out=$out\\\"; fail=1\\nelse\\n  echo \\\"PASS AC-01\\\"\\nfi\\n\\n# AC-02: exit 2 -> HAS_CHANGESETS=false, step must not fail.\\nout=$(run_case 2); code=$?\\nif [[ $code -ne 0 ]] || [[ \\\"$out\\\" != *\\\"__HAS_CHANGESETS=false__\\\"* ]]; then\\n  echo \\\"FAIL AC-02: exit 2 case: code=$code out=$out\\\"; fail=1\\nelse\\n  echo \\\"PASS AC-02\\\"\\nfi\\n\\n# AC-04: exit 0 -> step must fail (non-zero), HAS_CHANGESETS never read.\\nout=$(run_case 0); code=$?\\nif [[ $code -eq 0 ]] || [[ \\\"$out\\\" == *\\\"__HAS_CHANGESETS=true__\\\"* ]] || [[ \\\"$out\\\" == *\\\"__HAS_CHANGESETS=false__\\\"* ]]; then\\n  echo \\\"FAIL AC-04 (exit 0): code=$code out=$out\\\"; fail=1\\nelse\\n  echo \\\"PASS AC-04 (exit 0)\\\"\\nfi\\n\\n# AC-04: exit 127 -> same requirement, a different unrecognised code.\\nout=$(run_case 127); code=$?\\nif [[ $code -eq 0 ]] || [[ \\\"$out\\\" == *\\\"__HAS_CHANGESETS=true__\\\"* ]] || [[ \\\"$out\\\" == *\\\"__HAS_CHANGESETS=false__\\\"* ]]; then\\n  echo \\\"FAIL AC-04 (exit 127): code=$code out=$out\\\"; fail=1\\nelse\\n  echo \\\"PASS AC-04 (exit 127)\\\"\\nfi\\n\\nexit $fail\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"bash .github/actions/callisto-action/tests/test_status_check_branching.sh; echo \\\"exit=$?\\\"\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"FAIL AC-01: exit 1 case: code=1 out=__HAS_CHANGESETS=<unset>__ (current code has no branch for exit 1, so it falls through to the else arm and `exit 1`, never setting HAS_CHANGESETS at all)\\nPASS AC-02\\nFAIL AC-04 (exit 0): code=0 out=__HAS_CHANGESETS=true__ (current code wrongly treats exit 0 as HAS_CHANGESETS=true and exits 0)\\nPASS AC-04 (exit 127)\\nexit=1\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \".github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml\",\n        \"old_string\": \"        echo \\\"::group::1. Inspecting Workspace Status\\\"\\n        set +e\\n        callisto status --check\\n        STATUS_EXIT=$?\\n        set -e\\n        if [[ $STATUS_EXIT -eq 0 ]]; then\\n          HAS_CHANGESETS=true\\n        elif [[ $STATUS_EXIT -eq 2 ]]; then\\n          HAS_CHANGESETS=false\\n        else\\n          echo \\\"::error::callisto status --check failed with exit code $STATUS_EXIT\\\"\\n          exit $STATUS_EXIT\\n        fi\\n        echo \\\"::endgroup::\\\"\",\n        \"new_string\": \"        echo \\\"::group::1. Inspecting Workspace Status\\\"\\n        set +e\\n        callisto status --check\\n        STATUS_EXIT=$?\\n        set -e\\n        if [[ $STATUS_EXIT -eq 1 ]]; then\\n          HAS_CHANGESETS=true\\n        elif [[ $STATUS_EXIT -eq 2 ]]; then\\n          HAS_CHANGESETS=false\\n        else\\n          echo \\\"::error::callisto status --check exited with unexpected code $STATUS_EXIT (expected 1 for pending changesets or 2 for none pending)\\\"\\n          exit 1\\n        fi\\n        echo \\\"::endgroup::\\\"\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"bash .github/actions/callisto-action/tests/test_status_check_branching.sh; echo \\\"exit=$?\\\"\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"PASS AC-01\\nPASS AC-02\\nPASS AC-04 (exit 0)\\nPASS AC-04 (exit 127)\\nexit=0\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"fix(action): correct callisto status --check exit-code branching\\n\\nExit 1 (pending changesets) previously had no branch and fell through\\nto a passthrough `exit $STATUS_EXIT`; exit 0 was wrongly treated as\\n\\\"has changesets\\\". Any unrecognised exit code (including 0) now emits\\nan ::error:: annotation and fails the step with a guaranteed non-zero\\nexit instead of ever proceeding into the release-PR or publish branch.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T2\",\n      \"cluster\": \"action-script-exit-code\",\n      \"description\": \"Correct crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's status exit-code-contract doc comment, which currently claims 0 is returned under --check when at least one pending changeset exists (contradicting check_exit_code_raw at status.rs:18-28, which returns 1 in that case).\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-05\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs\", \"crates/callisto-cli/tests/status_doc_comment_test.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"The doc comment is prose, not executable logic, so its 'test' is a mechanical source-text pin: assert the old wrong claim is gone and the corrected claim is present, using include_str! on main.rs itself so the test reads the real file, not a copy.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"create\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-cli/tests/status_doc_comment_test.rs\",\n        \"content\": \"//! Pins the wording of main.rs's `status` exit-code-contract doc comment\\n//! against check_exit_code_raw's actual behavior (AC-05).\\n\\nconst MAIN_RS: &str = include_str!(\\\"../src/main.rs\\\");\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn status_exit_code_doc_comment_does_not_claim_zero_for_check_with_pending_changesets() {\\n    assert!(\\n        !MAIN_RS.contains(\\\"0 when no errors and (no --check OR at least one pending changeset)\\\"),\\n        \\\"main.rs's status exit-code doc comment must not claim 0 is returned under --check \\\\\\n         when changesets are pending; check_exit_code_raw (status.rs) returns 1 in that case\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn status_exit_code_doc_comment_states_correct_check_contract() {\\n    assert!(\\n        MAIN_RS.contains(\\\"OR when --check is set and at least one package has pending changesets\\\"),\\n        \\\"main.rs's status exit-code doc comment must state --check returns 1 when at least \\\\\\n         one package has pending changesets\\\"\\n    );\\n    assert!(\\n        MAIN_RS.contains(\\\"when --check is set, there are no diagnostic\\\"),\\n        \\\"main.rs's status exit-code doc comment must state --check returns 2 only when there \\\\\\n         are no diagnostic errors and no changesets are pending\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-cli --test status_doc_comment_test\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"test status_exit_code_doc_comment_states_correct_check_contract ... FAILED\\nassertion failed: MAIN_RS.contains(\\\"OR when --check is set and at least one package has pending changesets\\\")\\ntest status_exit_code_doc_comment_does_not_claim_zero_for_check_with_pending_changesets ... ok\\ntest result: FAILED. 1 passed; 1 failed\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs\",\n        \"old_string\": \"//   status         0 when no errors and (no --check OR at least one pending changeset)\\n//                  1 when any diagnostic is Error-severity (or Warning under --strict)\\n//                  2 (ExitCode::from(2)) when --check is set and no changesets are pending\",\n        \"new_string\": \"//   status         0 when no errors and --check is not set\\n//                  1 when any diagnostic is Error-severity (or Warning under --strict),\\n//                    OR when --check is set and at least one package has pending changesets\\n//                  2 (ExitCode::from(2)) when --check is set, there are no diagnostic\\n//                    errors, and no changesets are pending\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-cli --test status_doc_comment_test\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test status_exit_code_doc_comment_does_not_claim_zero_for_check_with_pending_changesets ... ok\\ntest status_exit_code_doc_comment_states_correct_check_contract ... ok\\ntest result: ok. 2 passed\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"docs(cli): correct status --check exit-code contract doc comment\\n\\nThe doc comment claimed 0 is returned under --check whenever a\\nchangeset is pending; check_exit_code_raw actually returns 1 in that\\ncase. Corrects the comment to match the implementation exactly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T3\",\n      \"cluster\": \"tag-sha-fabrication\",\n      \"description\": \"Fix create_tags_with_options's apply path (permit Some, tag.rs:82-117) so that when the per-release tag already exists at a commit different from release.sha, the reported CreatedTag.sha is the tag's real target via GitDataSource::resolve_commit, not release.sha -- and fail-fast with Err(GraphError::Vcs) when resolve_commit returns Ok(None) or Err.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-06\", \"AC-06b\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs\", \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Stub CommandRunner fixture follows aggregate.rs's FakeRevParseRunner / tags_laziness_test.rs's non-repo-dir pattern: a tempdir gix cannot discover forces GitAccess through the CommandRunner shell fallback deterministically for both `git tag --list` (contains_tag) and `git rev-parse --verify --quiet <tag>^{commit}` (resolve_commit).\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"create\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs\",\n        \"content\": \"//! Regression tests for tag.rs's per-release-tag sha fabrication fix\\n//! (AC-06, AC-06b, AC-06c, AC-06d, AC-07, AC-08). This file is built up\\n//! across three tasks (T3: apply path, T4: dry-run path); each task adds\\n//! its own #[test] functions to the shared fixtures below.\\n\\nuse std::path::Path;\\n\\nuse callisto_graph::commands::{create_tags_with_options, TagOptions};\\nuse callisto_graph::locate::IgnoreWalkLocator;\\nuse callisto_graph::{GraphError, Workspace};\\nuse callisto_model::{\\n    ApplyPermit, CommandError, CommandOutput, CommandRunner, CommitSha, PackageId, PublishPlan,\\n    ReleaseEntry, TagName, SCHEMA_VERSION,\\n};\\n\\nfn write_minimal_workspace(root: &Path) {\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[workspace]\\\\nmembers = [\\\\\\\"crates/*\\\\\\\"]\\\\nresolver = \\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n    let pkg_dir = root.join(\\\"crates/my-app\\\");\\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(&pkg_dir).unwrap();\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        pkg_dir.join(\\\"Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"my-app\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"0.1.0\\\\\\\"\\\\nedition = \\\\\\\"2021\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n}\\n\\nenum RevParse {\\n    Sha(String),\\n    NotFound,\\n    CommandErr,\\n}\\n\\n/// A `CommandRunner` double answering `git tag --list` (whether the\\n/// per-release tag exists) and `git rev-parse --verify --quiet <tag>^{commit}`\\n/// (the tag's real current target, or a failure) so the apply and dry-run\\n/// paths' existing-tag-sha-resolution logic can be tested without a real\\n/// diverging git repository.\\nstruct StubTagRunner {\\n    tag_exists: bool,\\n    tag_name: String,\\n    rev_parse: RevParse,\\n}\\n\\nimpl CommandRunner for StubTagRunner {\\n    fn run(\\n        &self,\\n        program: &str,\\n        args: &[&str],\\n        _cwd: &Path,\\n    ) -> Result<CommandOutput, CommandError> {\\n        assert_eq!(program, \\\"git\\\", \\\"only `git` should be shelled out to here\\\");\\n        match args {\\n            [\\\"tag\\\", \\\"--list\\\"] => Ok(CommandOutput {\\n                exit_code: Some(0),\\n                stdout: if self.tag_exists {\\n                    format!(\\\"{}\\\\n\\\", self.tag_name)\\n                } else {\\n                    String::new()\\n                },\\n                stderr: String::new(),\\n            }),\\n            [\\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"--verify\\\", \\\"--quiet\\\", rev] => {\\n                let expected = format!(\\\"{}^{{commit}}\\\", self.tag_name);\\n                assert_eq!(*rev, expected.as_str());\\n                match &self.rev_parse {\\n                    RevParse::Sha(s) => Ok(CommandOutput {\\n                        exit_code: Some(0),\\n                        stdout: format!(\\\"{s}\\\\n\\\"),\\n                        stderr: String::new(),\\n                    }),\\n                    RevParse::NotFound => Ok(CommandOutput {\\n                        exit_code: Some(1),\\n                        stdout: String::new(),\\n                        stderr: String::new(),\\n                    }),\\n                    RevParse::CommandErr => Err(CommandError::NotFound {\\n                        program: \\\"git\\\".to_string(),\\n                    }),\\n                }\\n            }\\n            other => panic!(\\\"unexpected git invocation: {other:?}\\\"),\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn assert_non_repo(root: &Path) {\\n    assert!(\\n        callisto_vcs::GitRepository::discover(root).is_err(),\\n        \\\"test fixture must not be discoverable as a Git repo\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\\nfn release_entry(tag_name: &str, sha: &str) -> ReleaseEntry {\\n    ReleaseEntry {\\n        package: PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap(),\\n        tag_name: TagName(tag_name.to_string()),\\n        sha: CommitSha::parse(sha).unwrap(),\\n        changelog_section: None,\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn plan_with_release(entry: ReleaseEntry) -> PublishPlan {\\n    PublishPlan {\\n        schema_version: SCHEMA_VERSION,\\n        rust_crates: vec![],\\n        npm_main_packages: vec![],\\n        npm_platform_packages: vec![],\\n        pypi_packages: vec![],\\n        releases: vec![entry],\\n        diagnostics: vec![],\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n// ---- T3: apply path (permit Some) ----\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn apply_mode_reports_real_target_when_tag_exists_and_differs_from_release_sha() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_minimal_workspace(root);\\n    assert_non_repo(root);\\n\\n    let real_sha = \\\"a\\\".repeat(40);\\n    let requested_sha = \\\"b\\\".repeat(40);\\n    let runner = StubTagRunner {\\n        tag_exists: true,\\n        tag_name: \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\".to_string(),\\n        rev_parse: RevParse::Sha(real_sha.clone()),\\n    };\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n    let plan = plan_with_release(release_entry(\\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &requested_sha));\\n    let permit = ApplyPermit::force_for_tests();\\n\\n    let report = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), Some(&permit))\\n        .expect(\\\"create_tags_with_options must succeed\\\");\\n\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        report.created_tags[0].sha.as_str(),\\n        real_sha,\\n        \\\"apply mode must report the tag's real current target, not release.sha, when the tag \\\\\\n         already exists at a different commit\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn apply_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_returns_ok_none_for_existing_tag() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_minimal_workspace(root);\\n    assert_non_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = StubTagRunner {\\n        tag_exists: true,\\n        tag_name: \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\".to_string(),\\n        rev_parse: RevParse::NotFound,\\n    };\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n    let plan = plan_with_release(release_entry(\\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &\\\"b\\\".repeat(40)));\\n    let permit = ApplyPermit::force_for_tests();\\n\\n    let result = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), Some(&permit));\\n\\n    assert!(\\n        matches!(result, Err(GraphError::Vcs(_))),\\n        \\\"must return Err(GraphError::Vcs) when resolve_commit returns Ok(None) for an \\\\\\n         already-existing tag, not fabricate release.sha; got {result:?}\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn apply_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_errors_for_existing_tag() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_minimal_workspace(root);\\n    assert_non_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = StubTagRunner {\\n        tag_exists: true,\\n        tag_name: \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\".to_string(),\\n        rev_parse: RevParse::CommandErr,\\n    };\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n    let plan = plan_with_release(release_entry(\\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &\\\"b\\\".repeat(40)));\\n    let permit = ApplyPermit::force_for_tests();\\n\\n    let result = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), Some(&permit));\\n\\n    assert!(\\n        matches!(result, Err(GraphError::Vcs(_))),\\n        \\\"must return Err(GraphError::Vcs) when resolve_commit itself errors for an \\\\\\n         already-existing tag, not fabricate release.sha; got {result:?}\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test tag_sha_fabrication_test\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"test apply_mode_reports_real_target_when_tag_exists_and_differs_from_release_sha ... FAILED\\nassertion `left == right` failed: apply mode must report the tag's real current target, not release.sha, when the tag already exists at a different commit\\n  left: \\\"bbbb...\\\" (release.sha, currently pushed unconditionally)\\n right: \\\"aaaa...\\\"\\ntest apply_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_returns_ok_none_for_existing_tag ... FAILED (returns Ok(TagReport) today, never calls resolve_commit)\\ntest apply_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_errors_for_existing_tag ... FAILED (same)\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs\",\n        \"old_string\": \"use callisto_model::{\\n    ApplyPermit, CommandRunner, CreatedTag, PublishPlan, TagReport, SCHEMA_VERSION,\\n};\\nuse callisto_vcs::GitDataSource;\",\n        \"new_string\": \"use callisto_model::{\\n    ApplyPermit, CommandRunner, CreatedTag, PublishPlan, TagReport, SCHEMA_VERSION,\\n};\\nuse callisto_vcs::{GitDataSource, VcsError};\"\n      },\n      \"implementation_2\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs\",\n        \"old_string\": \"        let already_existed = ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str);\\n\\n        if !already_existed {\\n            let msg = format!(\\\"Release {}\\\", tag_str);\\n            git.create_tag(tag_str, &release.sha, Some(&msg), permit)?;\\n        }\\n\\n        if opts.floating_major {\",\n        \"new_string\": \"        let already_existed = ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str);\\n\\n        let sha = if already_existed {\\n            match git.resolve_commit(tag_str)? {\\n                Some(actual) => actual,\\n                None => {\\n                    return Err(GraphError::Vcs(VcsError::RefNotFound {\\n                        ref_name: tag_str.to_string(),\\n                    }))\\n                }\\n            }\\n        } else {\\n            let msg = format!(\\\"Release {}\\\", tag_str);\\n            git.create_tag(tag_str, &release.sha, Some(&msg), permit)?;\\n            release.sha.clone()\\n        };\\n\\n        if opts.floating_major {\"\n      },\n      \"implementation_3\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs\",\n        \"old_string\": \"        tags.push(CreatedTag {\\n            package: release.package.clone(),\\n            tag_name: release.tag_name.clone(),\\n            sha: release.sha.clone(),\\n        });\\n    }\\n\\n    Ok(TagReport {\",\n        \"new_string\": \"        tags.push(CreatedTag {\\n            package: release.package.clone(),\\n            tag_name: release.tag_name.clone(),\\n            sha,\\n        });\\n    }\\n\\n    Ok(TagReport {\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test tag_sha_fabrication_test\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test apply_mode_reports_real_target_when_tag_exists_and_differs_from_release_sha ... ok\\ntest apply_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_returns_ok_none_for_existing_tag ... ok\\ntest apply_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_errors_for_existing_tag ... ok\\ntest result: ok. 3 passed\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"fix(graph): stop fabricating CreatedTag.sha in apply-mode tag creation\\n\\ncreate_tags_with_options's apply path pushed release.sha unconditionally\\neven when the per-release tag already existed at a different commit.\\nNow resolves the tag's real target via GitDataSource::resolve_commit\\nwhen it already exists, and fails fast (Err(GraphError::Vcs)) rather\\nthan fabricating a sha when resolution comes back empty or errors.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T4\",\n      \"cluster\": \"tag-sha-fabrication\",\n      \"description\": \"Apply the identical fix to create_tags_with_options's dry-run path (permit None, tag.rs:53-80): add the existing-tag check and resolve_commit lookup it currently lacks entirely, without performing any git write.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-06c\", \"AC-06d\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs\", \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Same StubTagRunner fixture from T3, reused via `mod` sharing since this appends to the same test file. The stub's `other => panic!` arm on any unexpected git invocation doubles as proof that dry-run never calls a write op (no `git tag -a...`), satisfying AC-06c's 'no git ref created or moved' requirement structurally.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"append\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs\",\n        \"content\": \"\\n// ---- T4: dry-run path (permit None) ----\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn dry_run_mode_reports_real_target_when_tag_exists_and_differs_from_release_sha() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_minimal_workspace(root);\\n    assert_non_repo(root);\\n\\n    let real_sha = \\\"a\\\".repeat(40);\\n    let requested_sha = \\\"b\\\".repeat(40);\\n    let runner = StubTagRunner {\\n        tag_exists: true,\\n        tag_name: \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\".to_string(),\\n        rev_parse: RevParse::Sha(real_sha.clone()),\\n    };\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n    let plan = plan_with_release(release_entry(\\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &requested_sha));\\n\\n    let report = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), None)\\n        .expect(\\\"create_tags_with_options (dry-run) must succeed\\\");\\n\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        report.created_tags[0].sha.as_str(),\\n        real_sha,\\n        \\\"dry-run mode must preview the tag's real current target, not release.sha, when the \\\\\\n         tag already exists at a different commit\\\"\\n    );\\n    // StubTagRunner panics on any git invocation other than `tag --list` and\\n    // `rev-parse --verify --quiet ...` -- reaching this point without a panic\\n    // proves no write op (e.g. `git tag -a`) was ever attempted.\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn dry_run_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_returns_ok_none_for_existing_tag() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_minimal_workspace(root);\\n    assert_non_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = StubTagRunner {\\n        tag_exists: true,\\n        tag_name: \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\".to_string(),\\n        rev_parse: RevParse::NotFound,\\n    };\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n    let plan = plan_with_release(release_entry(\\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &\\\"b\\\".repeat(40)));\\n\\n    let result = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), None);\\n\\n    assert!(\\n        matches!(result, Err(GraphError::Vcs(_))),\\n        \\\"dry-run must return Err(GraphError::Vcs) when resolve_commit returns Ok(None) for an \\\\\\n         already-existing tag, not fabricate release.sha; got {result:?}\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn dry_run_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_errors_for_existing_tag() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_minimal_workspace(root);\\n    assert_non_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = StubTagRunner {\\n        tag_exists: true,\\n        tag_name: \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\".to_string(),\\n        rev_parse: RevParse::CommandErr,\\n    };\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n    let plan = plan_with_release(release_entry(\\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &\\\"b\\\".repeat(40)));\\n\\n    let result = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), None);\\n\\n    assert!(\\n        matches!(result, Err(GraphError::Vcs(_))),\\n        \\\"dry-run must return Err(GraphError::Vcs) when resolve_commit itself errors for an \\\\\\n         already-existing tag, not fabricate release.sha; got {result:?}\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test tag_sha_fabrication_test\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"test dry_run_mode_reports_real_target_when_tag_exists_and_differs_from_release_sha ... FAILED\\nassertion `left == right` failed: dry-run mode must preview the tag's real current target, not release.sha, when the tag already exists at a different commit\\n  left: \\\"bbbb...\\\" (release.sha, currently pushed unconditionally, no existing-tag check at all in dry-run today)\\n right: \\\"aaaa...\\\"\\ntest dry_run_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_returns_ok_none_for_existing_tag ... FAILED (returns Ok(TagReport) today, never checks contains_tag or resolve_commit in dry-run)\\ntest dry_run_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_errors_for_existing_tag ... FAILED (same)\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs\",\n        \"old_string\": \"                }\\n            }\\n            tags.push(CreatedTag {\\n                package: release.package.clone(),\\n                tag_name: release.tag_name.clone(),\\n                sha: release.sha.clone(),\\n            });\\n            continue;\\n        };\",\n        \"new_string\": \"                }\\n            }\\n\\n            let already_existed = ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str);\\n            let sha = if already_existed {\\n                match git.resolve_commit(tag_str)? {\\n                    Some(actual) => actual,\\n                    None => {\\n                        return Err(GraphError::Vcs(VcsError::RefNotFound {\\n                            ref_name: tag_str.to_string(),\\n                        }))\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            } else {\\n                release.sha.clone()\\n            };\\n\\n            tags.push(CreatedTag {\\n                package: release.package.clone(),\\n                tag_name: release.tag_name.clone(),\\n                sha,\\n            });\\n            continue;\\n        };\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test tag_sha_fabrication_test\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test result: ok. 6 passed (all T3 + T4 tests)\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"fix(graph): stop fabricating CreatedTag.sha in dry-run tag preview\\n\\ncreate_tags_with_options's dry-run path performed no existing-tag check\\nat all and always previewed release.sha. Now mirrors the apply path:\\nresolves the tag's real target via resolve_commit when it already\\nexists, without any git write, and fails fast rather than fabricating\\na sha when resolution is empty or errors.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T5\",\n      \"cluster\": \"tag-sha-fabrication\",\n      \"description\": \"Regression proof that the T3/T4 fix does not change behavior for the two cases where the reported sha was already correct: tag does not exist yet (AC-07), and tag already exists at exactly release.sha -- the idempotent rerun case (AC-08). Uses a real git repository fixture (not a stub) so the create_tag write path and native gix resolve_commit path are both exercised for real, in both apply and dry-run mode.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-07\", \"AC-08\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"No new implementation: T3/T4 already implemented the complete logic. This task only adds regression tests, so both are expected to pass on first run -- proving the fix introduced no regression in the two cases it must leave unchanged.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"append\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs\",\n        \"content\": \"\\n// ---- T5: regression proofs (real git repo, no stubbing) ----\\n\\nstruct PanicRunner;\\nimpl CommandRunner for PanicRunner {\\n    fn run(&self, program: &str, args: &[&str], _cwd: &Path) -> Result<CommandOutput, CommandError> {\\n        panic!(\\\"unexpected CommandRunner invocation ({program} {args:?}) -- a real .git repo is present, so GitAccess must use native gix, never the shell fallback\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn init_git_repo(dir: &Path) {\\n    let run = |args: &[&str]| {\\n        let status = std::process::Command::new(\\\"git\\\")\\n            .args(args)\\n            .current_dir(dir)\\n            .status()\\n            .expect(\\\"git should run\\\");\\n        assert!(status.success(), \\\"git {args:?} failed\\\");\\n    };\\n    run(&[\\\"init\\\", \\\"-q\\\"]);\\n    run(&[\\\"config\\\", \\\"user.email\\\", \\\"test@example.com\\\"]);\\n    run(&[\\\"config\\\", \\\"user.name\\\", \\\"Test\\\"]);\\n    run(&[\\\"add\\\", \\\".\\\"]);\\n    run(&[\\\"commit\\\", \\\"-q\\\", \\\"-m\\\", \\\"init\\\"]);\\n}\\n\\nfn git_head_sha(dir: &Path) -> String {\\n    let out = std::process::Command::new(\\\"git\\\")\\n        .args([\\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"HEAD\\\"])\\n        .current_dir(dir)\\n        .output()\\n        .unwrap();\\n    String::from_utf8(out.stdout).unwrap().trim().to_string()\\n}\\n\\nfn git_tag_exists_at(dir: &Path, tag: &str, expected_sha: &str) -> bool {\\n    let out = std::process::Command::new(\\\"git\\\")\\n        .args([\\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"--verify\\\", \\\"--quiet\\\", &format!(\\\"{tag}^{{commit}}\\\")])\\n        .current_dir(dir)\\n        .output()\\n        .unwrap();\\n    out.status.success() && String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout).trim() == expected_sha\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn tag_not_existing_reports_release_sha_in_both_modes_and_apply_creates_it() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_minimal_workspace(root);\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n    let head = git_head_sha(root);\\n\\n    let runner = PanicRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n    let plan = plan_with_release(release_entry(\\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &head));\\n\\n    // Dry-run first, while the tag genuinely does not exist yet.\\n    let dry_report = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), None)\\n        .expect(\\\"dry-run must succeed\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(dry_report.created_tags[0].sha.as_str(), head, \\\"AC-07 dry-run\\\");\\n    assert!(\\n        !git_tag_exists_at(root, \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &head),\\n        \\\"dry-run must not create the tag\\\"\\n    );\\n\\n    // Apply: tag still does not exist -> gets created at release.sha.\\n    let permit = ApplyPermit::force_for_tests();\\n    let apply_report = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), Some(&permit))\\n        .expect(\\\"apply must succeed\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(apply_report.created_tags[0].sha.as_str(), head, \\\"AC-07 apply\\\");\\n    assert!(\\n        git_tag_exists_at(root, \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &head),\\n        \\\"apply must create the tag at release.sha\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn tag_existing_at_release_sha_reports_release_sha_with_no_error_in_both_modes() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_minimal_workspace(root);\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n    let head = git_head_sha(root);\\n\\n    // Pre-create the tag directly via git, at exactly the sha the plan will request.\\n    let status = std::process::Command::new(\\\"git\\\")\\n        .args([\\\"tag\\\", \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &head])\\n        .current_dir(root)\\n        .status()\\n        .unwrap();\\n    assert!(status.success());\\n\\n    let runner = PanicRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n    let plan = plan_with_release(release_entry(\\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &head));\\n\\n    let permit = ApplyPermit::force_for_tests();\\n    let apply_report = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), Some(&permit))\\n        .expect(\\\"idempotent apply rerun must succeed with no error\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(apply_report.created_tags[0].sha.as_str(), head, \\\"AC-08 apply\\\");\\n\\n    let dry_report = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), None)\\n        .expect(\\\"dry-run against already-tagged state must succeed with no error\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(dry_report.created_tags[0].sha.as_str(), head, \\\"AC-08 dry-run\\\");\\n}\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test tag_sha_fabrication_test tag_not_existing_reports_release_sha_in_both_modes_and_apply_creates_it tag_existing_at_release_sha_reports_release_sha_with_no_error_in_both_modes\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"N/A -- pure regression-proof task: T3/T4 already implement the complete apply-path and dry-run-path logic these tests exercise, so both are expected to pass immediately (no red phase). If either fails, it means T3/T4's fix broke a case it was required to leave unchanged.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"none\",\n        \"note\": \"No code change. T3/T4 already implemented the full logic these tests verify.\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test tag_sha_fabrication_test\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test result: ok. 8 passed (all T3 + T4 + T5 tests)\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin AC-07/AC-08 no-regression behavior for tag sha resolution\\n\\nProves the AC-06/AC-06b/AC-06c/AC-06d fix does not change reported sha\\nfor the two cases it must leave alone: tag not yet existing, and an\\nidempotent rerun where the existing tag already matches release.sha --\\nin both apply and --dry-run mode, against a real git repository.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T6\",\n      \"cluster\": \"changelog-section\",\n      \"description\": \"Add the new DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError variant to the already-#[non_exhaustive] enum, needed by plan_publish's changelog-read-failure path (AC-12c).\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-12c\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Purely additive foundation step, done first so the next task can reference the variant. Mirrors the file's existing kebab-case round-trip test pattern exactly.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs\",\n        \"old_string\": \"    /// `callisto matrix` found the same platform triple declared more than once within one\\n    /// package's own `napi.targets`/`[tool.maturin].targets` -- the duplicate is dropped\\n    /// (first occurrence wins) rather than treated as a hard error.\\n    DuplicatePlatformTriple,\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::DiagnosticCode;\",\n        \"new_string\": \"    /// `callisto matrix` found the same platform triple declared more than once within one\\n    /// package's own `napi.targets`/`[tool.maturin].targets` -- the duplicate is dropped\\n    /// (first occurrence wins) rather than treated as a hard error.\\n    DuplicatePlatformTriple,\\n    /// A changelog file exists at the package's resolved `pkg.changelog` path but could not\\n    /// be read -- invalid UTF-8, permission denied, or any I/O failure other than \\\"file does\\n    /// not exist\\\" (that case is `ChangelogSectionNotFound` instead). `changelog_section` is\\n    /// left `None` for the package; `plan_publish` is not aborted.\\n    ChangelogReadError,\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::DiagnosticCode;\\n\\n    /// AC-12c: DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError must serialize to the kebab-case string\\n    /// \\\"changelog-read-error\\\" and deserialize back to the same variant.\\n    #[test]\\n    fn changelog_read_error_serializes_to_kebab_case() {\\n        let code = DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError;\\n        let json = serde_json::to_string(&code).unwrap();\\n        assert_eq!(\\n            json,\\n            r#\\\"\\\"changelog-read-error\\\"\\\"#,\\n            \\\"DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError must serialize to \\\\\\\"changelog-read-error\\\\\\\"\\\",\\n        );\\n        let roundtrip: DiagnosticCode = serde_json::from_str(&json).unwrap();\\n        assert_eq!(\\n            roundtrip, code,\\n            \\\"deserialized value must equal the original variant\\\",\\n        );\\n    }\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-model --lib diagnostic::tests::changelog_read_error_serializes_to_kebab_case\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"error[E0599]: no variant or associated item named `ChangelogReadError` found for enum `DiagnosticCode`\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"none\",\n        \"note\": \"The single edit above adds both the variant and its test in one change (the variant cannot compile without the test referencing it, and vice versa is not applicable here since this is a pure additive enum variant) -- run the test command again after the edit to confirm green.\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-model --lib diagnostic::tests::changelog_read_error_serializes_to_kebab_case\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test diagnostic::tests::changelog_read_error_serializes_to_kebab_case ... ok\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"feat(model): add DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError variant\\n\\nAdditive #[non_exhaustive] enum variant for plan_publish to report when\\na package's changelog file exists but fails to read (invalid UTF-8 or\\nany I/O error other than not-found) rather than silently treating it\\nthe same as a missing file.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T7\",\n      \"cluster\": \"changelog-section\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement changelog_section population in plan_publish: replace the hardcoded None (publish.rs:427) with a call through a new resolve_changelog_section helper that reads pkg.changelog and calls callisto_changelog::extract_section, covering the happy path (AC-10) and the file-does-not-exist path (AC-11) with new tests. The helper's implementation also handles the empty-section, no-heading, and unreadable-file cases in the same pass (proved by T8/T9's regression tests).\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-10\", \"AC-11\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs\", \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Reuses this file's existing fixture idioms (init_git_repo, DummyRunner) so a package with no changeset and no matching tag is naturally a release candidate (is_release=true via the untagged cur_ver path), letting the test drive plan_publish end-to-end rather than unit-testing the helper in isolation.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"append\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs\",\n        \"content\": \"\\n// ---- changelog_section population (AC-10, AC-11) ----\\n\\nfn write_release_candidate_pkg(root: &std::path::Path, version: &str) {\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n        format!(\\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"pkg\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"{version}\\\\\\\"\\\\nedition = \\\\\\\"2021\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\"),\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_populates_changelog_section_when_heading_has_content() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_release_candidate_pkg(root, \\\"1.2.3\\\");\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"CHANGELOG.md\\\"),\\n        \\\"# Changelog\\\\n\\\\n## 1.2.3\\\\n\\\\nSome release notes here.\\\\n\\\\n## 1.2.2\\\\n\\\\nOlder notes.\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let release = plan\\n        .releases\\n        .iter()\\n        .find(|r| r.package == pkg_id)\\n        .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\\\"expected a ReleaseEntry for pkg, got: {:?}\\\", plan.releases));\\n\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        release.changelog_section.as_deref(),\\n        Some(\\\"Some release notes here.\\\"),\\n        \\\"changelog_section must equal extract_section's trimmed output for the matching heading\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_file_does_not_exist() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_release_candidate_pkg(root, \\\"1.2.3\\\");\\n    // Deliberately no CHANGELOG.md written.\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let release = plan\\n        .releases\\n        .iter()\\n        .find(|r| r.package == pkg_id)\\n        .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\\\"expected a ReleaseEntry for pkg, got: {:?}\\\", plan.releases));\\n\\n    assert_eq!(release.changelog_section, None, \\\"AC-11: no changelog file on disk\\\");\\n    assert!(\\n        plan.diagnostics.iter().any(|d| d.code\\n            == callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound\\n            && d.package.as_ref() == Some(&pkg_id)),\\n        \\\"expected a ChangelogSectionNotFound diagnostic naming pkg; got {:?}\\\",\\n        plan.diagnostics\\n    );\\n}\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_populates_changelog_section_when_heading_has_content plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_file_does_not_exist\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"test plan_publish_populates_changelog_section_when_heading_has_content ... FAILED\\nassertion `left == right` failed: changelog_section must equal extract_section's trimmed output for the matching heading\\n  left: None\\n right: Some(\\\"Some release notes here.\\\")\\ntest plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_file_does_not_exist ... FAILED\\nassertion failed: expected a ChangelogSectionNotFound diagnostic naming pkg; got []\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs\",\n        \"old_string\": \"pub fn plan_publish<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(\",\n        \"new_string\": \"/// Resolves a package's `changelog_section` for `plan_publish`: reads the file at\\n/// `ws_root.join(changelog_rel_path)` and extracts the `## {ver}` section via\\n/// `callisto_changelog::extract_section`. Every non-fatal outcome (file not found, no\\n/// matching heading, empty matched section, or an unreadable file) leaves the return value\\n/// `None` and pushes exactly one Warning diagnostic into `diagnostics` rather than aborting\\n/// the plan -- `ChangelogSectionNotFound` for the first three (AC-10b, AC-11, AC-12），\\n/// `ChangelogReadError` for a read failure that is not \\\"file does not exist\\\" (AC-12c).\\nfn resolve_changelog_section(\\n    ws_root: &std::path::Path,\\n    changelog_rel_path: &std::path::Path,\\n    pkg_id: &callisto_model::PackageId,\\n    ver: &callisto_model::Version,\\n    diagnostics: &mut Vec<callisto_model::Diagnostic>,\\n) -> Option<String> {\\n    let full_path = ws_root.join(changelog_rel_path);\\n    let content = match std::fs::read_to_string(&full_path) {\\n        Ok(c) => c,\\n        Err(e) if e.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound => {\\n            diagnostics.push(callisto_model::Diagnostic {\\n                code: callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound,\\n                severity: callisto_model::DiagnosticSeverity::Warning,\\n                message: format!(\\n                    \\\"no changelog file found at `{}` for package `{}`\\\",\\n                    changelog_rel_path.display(),\\n                    pkg_id.display_name()\\n                ),\\n                package: Some(pkg_id.clone()),\\n                path: Some(changelog_rel_path.to_path_buf()),\\n                escalated_by: None,\\n                governed_by: None,\\n            });\\n            return None;\\n        }\\n        Err(e) => {\\n            diagnostics.push(callisto_model::Diagnostic {\\n                code: callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError,\\n                severity: callisto_model::DiagnosticSeverity::Warning,\\n                message: format!(\\n                    \\\"could not read changelog at `{}` for package `{}`: {e}\\\",\\n                    changelog_rel_path.display(),\\n                    pkg_id.display_name()\\n                ),\\n                package: Some(pkg_id.clone()),\\n                path: Some(changelog_rel_path.to_path_buf()),\\n                escalated_by: None,\\n                governed_by: None,\\n            });\\n            return None;\\n        }\\n    };\\n\\n    match callisto_changelog::extract_section(&content, ver) {\\n        Some(section) => Some(section.to_string()),\\n        None => {\\n            diagnostics.push(callisto_model::Diagnostic {\\n                code: callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound,\\n                severity: callisto_model::DiagnosticSeverity::Warning,\\n                message: format!(\\n                    \\\"no `## {}` section found in `{}` for package `{}`\\\",\\n                    ver.render(),\\n                    changelog_rel_path.display(),\\n                    pkg_id.display_name()\\n                ),\\n                package: Some(pkg_id.clone()),\\n                path: Some(changelog_rel_path.to_path_buf()),\\n                escalated_by: None,\\n                governed_by: None,\\n            });\\n            None\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn plan_publish<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(\"\n      },\n      \"implementation_2\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs\",\n        \"old_string\": \"                if let (Some(ref sha), Some(idx)) = (&head_sha, tag_index) {\\n                    releases.push(ReleaseEntry {\\n                        package: pkg.id.clone(),\\n                        tag_name: idx.template(&pkg.id).render(&ver),\\n                        sha: sha.clone(),\\n                        changelog_section: None,\\n                    });\\n                }\",\n        \"new_string\": \"                if let (Some(ref sha), Some(idx)) = (&head_sha, tag_index) {\\n                    let changelog_section = pkg.changelog.as_ref().and_then(|ch_path| {\\n                        resolve_changelog_section(\\n                            &ws.root,\\n                            ch_path,\\n                            &pkg.id,\\n                            &ver,\\n                            &mut diagnostics,\\n                        )\\n                    });\\n                    releases.push(ReleaseEntry {\\n                        package: pkg.id.clone(),\\n                        tag_name: idx.template(&pkg.id).render(&ver),\\n                        sha: sha.clone(),\\n                        changelog_section,\\n                    });\\n                }\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_populates_changelog_section_when_heading_has_content plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_file_does_not_exist\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test plan_publish_populates_changelog_section_when_heading_has_content ... ok\\ntest plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_file_does_not_exist ... ok\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"fix(graph): populate ReleaseEntry.changelog_section from the package's changelog\\n\\nplan_publish hardcoded changelog_section to None. Now reads the file\\nat the package's resolved pkg.changelog path (the same field callisto\\nversion's changelog-rendering step already uses) and extracts the\\nrelease's `## {version}` section via callisto_changelog::extract_section,\\nwarning via a ChangelogSectionNotFound/ChangelogReadError diagnostic\\nrather than erroring the plan when the file or section is unavailable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T8\",\n      \"cluster\": \"changelog-section\",\n      \"description\": \"Regression proof that resolve_changelog_section (T7) also correctly handles the empty-section case (AC-10b) and the no-matching-heading case (AC-12) -- both already flow through the same extract_section call and ChangelogSectionNotFound diagnostic T7 implemented.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-10b\", \"AC-12\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"No new implementation: extract_section (write.rs:131-136) already returns None uniformly for both an empty matched section and a missing heading, and T7's helper already reports both via ChangelogSectionNotFound. Both tests are expected to pass on first run.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"append\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs\",\n        \"content\": \"\\n// ---- regression: AC-10b (empty section), AC-12 (no matching heading) ----\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_matched_heading_section_is_empty() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_release_candidate_pkg(root, \\\"1.2.3\\\");\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"CHANGELOG.md\\\"),\\n        \\\"# Changelog\\\\n\\\\n## 1.2.3\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n## 1.2.2\\\\n\\\\nOlder notes.\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let release = plan.releases.iter().find(|r| r.package == pkg_id).unwrap();\\n\\n    assert_eq!(release.changelog_section, None, \\\"AC-10b: matched heading has empty content\\\");\\n    assert!(\\n        plan.diagnostics.iter().any(|d| d.code\\n            == callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound\\n            && d.package.as_ref() == Some(&pkg_id)),\\n        \\\"expected a ChangelogSectionNotFound diagnostic naming pkg; got {:?}\\\",\\n        plan.diagnostics\\n    );\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_no_matching_heading() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_release_candidate_pkg(root, \\\"1.2.3\\\");\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"CHANGELOG.md\\\"),\\n        \\\"# Changelog\\\\n\\\\n## 1.2.2\\\\n\\\\nOlder notes only, no 1.2.3 section.\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let release = plan.releases.iter().find(|r| r.package == pkg_id).unwrap();\\n\\n    assert_eq!(release.changelog_section, None, \\\"AC-12: no `## 1.2.3` heading in the file\\\");\\n    assert!(\\n        plan.diagnostics.iter().any(|d| d.code\\n            == callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound\\n            && d.package.as_ref() == Some(&pkg_id)),\\n        \\\"expected a ChangelogSectionNotFound diagnostic naming pkg; got {:?}\\\",\\n        plan.diagnostics\\n    );\\n}\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_matched_heading_section_is_empty plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_no_matching_heading\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"N/A -- pure regression-proof task: T7's resolve_changelog_section already calls extract_section, which already returns None uniformly for an empty matched section and for no matching heading. Both tests are expected to pass on first run.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"none\",\n        \"note\": \"No code change. T7 already implements the logic these tests verify.\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_matched_heading_section_is_empty plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_no_matching_heading\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_matched_heading_section_is_empty ... ok\\ntest plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_no_matching_heading ... ok\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin AC-10b/AC-12 changelog_section no-regression behavior\\n\\nProves resolve_changelog_section correctly leaves changelog_section as\\nNone (with a ChangelogSectionNotFound diagnostic, no error) both when a\\nmatched ## {version} heading's section is empty and when no heading\\nmatches the release version at all.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T9\",\n      \"cluster\": \"changelog-section\",\n      \"description\": \"Regression proof that resolve_changelog_section distinguishes an unreadable changelog file (invalid UTF-8) from a missing one, reporting ChangelogReadError rather than ChangelogSectionNotFound (AC-12c).\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-12c\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"No new implementation: T7's helper already has a distinct match arm for a read error other than NotFound, using the ChangelogReadError variant T6 added. This test is expected to pass on first run.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"append\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs\",\n        \"content\": \"\\n// ---- regression: AC-12c (unreadable / invalid UTF-8 changelog file) ----\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_and_emits_read_error_for_invalid_utf8() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_release_candidate_pkg(root, \\\"1.2.3\\\");\\n    std::fs::write(root.join(\\\"CHANGELOG.md\\\"), [0x23, 0x20, 0xFF, 0xFE, 0x0A]).unwrap();\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let release = plan.releases.iter().find(|r| r.package == pkg_id).unwrap();\\n\\n    assert_eq!(release.changelog_section, None, \\\"AC-12c: file exists but is not valid UTF-8\\\");\\n    assert!(\\n        plan.diagnostics.iter().any(|d| d.code\\n            == callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError\\n            && d.package.as_ref() == Some(&pkg_id)),\\n        \\\"expected a ChangelogReadError diagnostic naming pkg; got {:?}\\\",\\n        plan.diagnostics\\n    );\\n    assert!(\\n        !plan.diagnostics.iter().any(|d| d.code\\n            == callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound\\n            && d.package.as_ref() == Some(&pkg_id)),\\n        \\\"an unreadable file must not also be reported as ChangelogSectionNotFound\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_and_emits_read_error_for_invalid_utf8\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"N/A -- pure regression-proof task: T7's resolve_changelog_section already distinguishes ErrorKind::NotFound (ChangelogSectionNotFound) from any other read error (ChangelogReadError, added in T6). Expected to pass on first run.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"none\",\n        \"note\": \"No code change. T6 (variant) + T7 (helper's Err(e) arm) already implement the logic this test verifies.\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_and_emits_read_error_for_invalid_utf8\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_and_emits_read_error_for_invalid_utf8 ... ok\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin AC-12c changelog read-error diagnostic behavior\\n\\nProves an unreadable (invalid UTF-8) changelog file is reported via\\nDiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError, distinct from the not-found case,\\nand does not also fire ChangelogSectionNotFound for the same package.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T10\",\n      \"cluster\": \"schema-guard\",\n      \"description\": \"Guard/regression proof for AC-13: confirm via `callisto schema` that no report struct (StatusReport, CreatedTag, TagReport, ReleaseEntry, PublishPlan) gained, lost, renamed, or retyped a field, and that the only DiagnosticCode schema delta is the new changelog-read-error variant.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-13\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-cli/tests/schema_guard_test.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Expected field/variant sets below were captured directly from `callisto schema --type <X>` run against the live, unmodified repository before any task in this plan was implemented, so they are the true pre-fix baseline -- this task's assertions are a real diff, not a guess. Run last, after every other task, so it also functions as the plan's final integration guard.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"create\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-cli/tests/schema_guard_test.rs\",\n        \"content\": \"//! AC-13 guard: none of this track's fixes may change any report struct's field shape.\\n//! The only permitted schema delta is the additive DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError\\n//! variant. Expected sets below were captured from `callisto schema` against the live,\\n//! unmodified repository before this track's fixes were implemented.\\n\\nuse std::collections::BTreeSet;\\nuse std::process::Command;\\n\\nfn run_schema(target: &str) -> serde_json::Value {\\n    let bin = env!(\\\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_callisto\\\");\\n    let out = Command::new(bin)\\n        .args([\\\"schema\\\", \\\"--type\\\", target])\\n        .output()\\n        .expect(\\\"callisto schema must run\\\");\\n    assert!(\\n        out.status.success(),\\n        \\\"callisto schema --type {target} failed: {}\\\",\\n        String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stderr)\\n    );\\n    serde_json::from_slice(&out.stdout).expect(\\\"schema output must be valid JSON\\\")\\n}\\n\\nfn required_and_props(schema: &serde_json::Value) -> (BTreeSet<String>, BTreeSet<String>) {\\n    let required: BTreeSet<String> = schema[\\\"required\\\"]\\n        .as_array()\\n        .unwrap()\\n        .iter()\\n        .map(|v| v.as_str().unwrap().to_string())\\n        .collect();\\n    let props: BTreeSet<String> = schema[\\\"properties\\\"]\\n        .as_object()\\n        .unwrap()\\n        .keys()\\n        .cloned()\\n        .collect();\\n    (required, props)\\n}\\n\\nfn set(items: &[&str]) -> BTreeSet<String> {\\n    items.iter().map(|s| s.to_string()).collect()\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn ac13_report_struct_field_shapes_are_unchanged() {\\n    let tag_schema = run_schema(\\\"tag\\\");\\n    let (req, props) = required_and_props(&tag_schema);\\n    assert_eq!(req, set(&[\\\"createdTags\\\", \\\"schemaVersion\\\"]));\\n    assert_eq!(props, set(&[\\\"createdTags\\\", \\\"diagnostics\\\", \\\"schemaVersion\\\"]));\\n\\n    let created_tag = &tag_schema[\\\"definitions\\\"][\\\"CreatedTag\\\"];\\n    let (req, props) = required_and_props(created_tag);\\n    assert_eq!(req, set(&[\\\"package\\\", \\\"sha\\\", \\\"tagName\\\"]));\\n    assert_eq!(props, req);\\n\\n    let status_schema = run_schema(\\\"status\\\");\\n    let (req, props) = required_and_props(&status_schema);\\n    assert_eq!(req, set(&[\\\"packages\\\", \\\"schemaVersion\\\"]));\\n    assert_eq!(props, set(&[\\\"diagnostics\\\", \\\"packages\\\", \\\"schemaVersion\\\"]));\\n\\n    let plan_schema = run_schema(\\\"plan-publish\\\");\\n    let (req, props) = required_and_props(&plan_schema);\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        req,\\n        set(&[\\\"npmMainPackages\\\", \\\"npmPlatformPackages\\\", \\\"releases\\\", \\\"rustCrates\\\", \\\"schemaVersion\\\"])\\n    );\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        props,\\n        set(&[\\n            \\\"diagnostics\\\", \\\"npmMainPackages\\\", \\\"npmPlatformPackages\\\", \\\"pypiPackages\\\", \\\"releases\\\",\\n            \\\"rustCrates\\\", \\\"schemaVersion\\\"\\n        ])\\n    );\\n\\n    let release_entry = &plan_schema[\\\"definitions\\\"][\\\"ReleaseEntry\\\"];\\n    let (req, props) = required_and_props(release_entry);\\n    assert_eq!(req, set(&[\\\"package\\\", \\\"sha\\\", \\\"tagName\\\"]));\\n    assert_eq!(props, set(&[\\\"changelogSection\\\", \\\"package\\\", \\\"sha\\\", \\\"tagName\\\"]));\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn ac13_diagnostic_code_enum_gains_only_changelog_read_error() {\\n    let tag_schema = run_schema(\\\"tag\\\");\\n    let variants: BTreeSet<String> = tag_schema[\\\"definitions\\\"][\\\"DiagnosticCode\\\"][\\\"oneOf\\\"]\\n        .as_array()\\n        .unwrap()\\n        .iter()\\n        .map(|v| v[\\\"enum\\\"][0].as_str().unwrap().to_string())\\n        .collect();\\n\\n    let expected = set(&[\\n        \\\"empty-changeset\\\", \\\"empty-summary\\\", \\\"unknown-package\\\", \\\"invalid-package-name\\\",\\n        \\\"napi-target-added-not-in-members\\\", \\\"napi-target-removed-still-on-disk\\\",\\n        \\\"napi-coordination-not-yet-supported\\\", \\\"graph-edge-disagreement\\\",\\n        \\\"range-not-round-trippable\\\", \\\"catalog-spec-not-rewritten\\\", \\\"tag-glob-non-version-match\\\",\\n        \\\"changesets-config-key-dropped\\\", \\\"pre-major-inference-inert\\\", \\\"changelog-section-not-found\\\",\\n        \\\"changeset-read-error\\\", \\\"git-discovery-failed\\\", \\\"bare-rule-matches-multiple-ecosystems\\\",\\n        \\\"unrecognised-platform-triple\\\", \\\"publish-target-not-implemented\\\", \\\"package-set-matched-nothing\\\",\\n        \\\"duplicate-platform-triple\\\", \\\"changelog-read-error\\\",\\n    ]);\\n\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        variants, expected,\\n        \\\"DiagnosticCode schema must gain exactly one new variant: changelog-read-error\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-cli --test schema_guard_test\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"test ac13_diagnostic_code_enum_gains_only_changelog_read_error ... FAILED\\nassertion `left == right` failed: DiagnosticCode schema must gain exactly one new variant: changelog-read-error\\n(fails until T6 adds the variant; ac13_report_struct_field_shapes_are_unchanged passes throughout since T3-T9 never change any struct's field shape, only field values and enum membership)\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"none\",\n        \"note\": \"No code change. This task only adds the guard test; it becomes green once T6 (adds the enum variant) is in place, and stays green through every other task since none of them change a struct's field shape. Run last.\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-cli --test schema_guard_test\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test ac13_report_struct_field_shapes_are_unchanged ... ok\\ntest ac13_diagnostic_code_enum_gains_only_changelog_read_error ... ok\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(cli): add AC-13 schema guard against report struct field drift\\n\\nAsserts callisto schema output for tag/status/plan-publish reports has\\nan unchanged field shape after this track's fixes, and that the only\\nDiagnosticCode delta is the new additive changelog-read-error variant.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1735,"cache_read_input_tokens":405781,"output_tokens":29003,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":373},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1735,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":29003,"cache_read_input_tokens":405781,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1735,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1735},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCftrBFNBsRXMN5f26xG","type":"assistant","uuid":"ba9e9487-021a-4691-8098-efc9203b79de","timestamp":"2026-08-19T19:40:37.331Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"ba9e9487-021a-4691-8098-efc9203b79de","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6b9b446f-d94d-4cb1-afc5-4b460f415034","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ugati5vviURe6jYtnx8SfS","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/plan-track4-draft.json (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"f82274dc-5420-4107-9c63-7cabdc83df7f","timestamp":"2026-08-19T19:40:37.438Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/plan-track4-draft.json","content":"{\n  \"artifact_type\": \"plan@1\",\n  \"id\": \"PLAN-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"spec_file_path\": \".claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS.json\",\n  \"spec_hash\": \"sha256:26502a95f78494d2c1759752e86543a70d0a22588ef4dbec18f2324752e52255\",\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Verified every api_surface claim against live code before writing tasks (all citations held: action.yml lines 90-97 have exactly the described exit-0-true/exit-2-false/else-passthrough bug with no exit-1 branch at all; main.rs:19-21 wrongly claims 0 under --check with pending changesets; tag.rs:82-117/53-80 unconditionally push release.sha; publish.rs:427 hardcodes None; DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound exists unemitted at diagnostic.rs:144, ChangelogReadError does not exist yet; ReleaseEntry.changelog_section already has skip_serializing_if at plan.rs:116-117; Package.changelog is workspace-root-relative, always Some, set at walk.rs:323/387-392). Four disjoint clusters, sequenced arbitrarily since none depend on each other, but each cluster's internal tasks are ordered (foundation before use, e.g. the new DiagnosticCode variant before the code that emits it). Two tasks (T5, T8/T9) are pure regression-proof tasks whose assertions pass immediately because the single cohesive fix in the preceding task already satisfies them -- documented explicitly per task rather than forcing an artificial red phase that would require temporarily breaking working code. Stub CommandRunner fixtures for tag.rs (T3/T4) follow the exact pattern of FakeRevParseRunner in aggregate.rs and CountingTagListRunner in tags_laziness_test.rs: a non-git-discoverable tempdir forces GitAccess through the CommandRunner shell fallback deterministically, and TagIndex::build's contains_tag check is satisfied by stubbing `git tag --list` while resolve_commit's three outcomes (Some/None/Err) are satisfied by stubbing `git rev-parse --verify --quiet <tag>^{commit}`. AC-07/AC-08 regression (T5) instead uses a real git repo, since those scenarios exercise the actual tag-creation write path and native gix idempotent-read path that a stub would have to reimplement pointlessly. The AC-13 schema guard (T10) uses field/variant sets captured directly from the live, unmodified binary via `callisto schema --type <X>` before any code in this plan was written, so the expected sets are the true pre-fix baseline, not a guess.\",\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T1\",\n      \"cluster\": \"action-script-exit-code\",\n      \"description\": \"Fix action.yml's 'Inspecting Workspace Status' step so exit 1 -> HAS_CHANGESETS=true, exit 2 -> HAS_CHANGESETS=false, and any other exit code (including 0) fails the step with an ::error:: annotation and a guaranteed non-zero exit, never a passthrough of $STATUS_EXIT.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-01\", \"AC-02\", \"AC-04\"],\n      \"files\": [\".github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml\", \".github/actions/callisto-action/tests/test_status_check_branching.sh\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Current code (action.yml:90-97) has no branch for exit 1 at all -- exit 0 is wrongly mapped to HAS_CHANGESETS=true, and the else branch does `exit $STATUS_EXIT` which is a passthrough that could itself be 0. Composite-action bash isn't unit-testable via cargo, so this task adds a small, self-contained bash test that extracts the exact run-body text between the step's `::group::1. Inspecting Workspace Status` and its matching `::endgroup::` markers straight out of action.yml (so the test can never drift from the real file) and executes it with a stubbed `callisto` shell function standing in for the binary, for exit codes 1, 2, 0, and 127.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"create\",\n        \"file_path\": \".github/actions/callisto-action/tests/test_status_check_branching.sh\",\n        \"content\": \"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Regression test for the \\\"Inspecting Workspace Status\\\" step's exit-code\\n# branching in action.yml (AC-01, AC-02, AC-04). Extracts the exact run-body\\n# text between the step's ::group::1. Inspecting Workspace Status marker and\\n# its matching ::endgroup:: marker directly out of action.yml, so this test\\n# always exercises the file's current real logic -- it cannot drift from it.\\nset -u\\nACTION_YML=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\\\")/..\\\" && pwd)/action.yml\\\"\\n\\nextract_snippet() {\\n  sed -n '/::group::1\\\\. Inspecting Workspace Status/,/::endgroup::/p' \\\"$ACTION_YML\\\" | sed '1d;$d'\\n}\\n\\nrun_case() {\\n  local stub_exit=\\\"$1\\\"\\n  local tmp_script\\n  tmp_script=\\\"$(mktemp)\\\"\\n  {\\n    echo \\\"callisto() { exit ${stub_exit}; }\\\"\\n    extract_snippet\\n    echo 'echo \\\"__HAS_CHANGESETS=${HAS_CHANGESETS-<unset>}__\\\"'\\n  } > \\\"$tmp_script\\\"\\n  bash \\\"$tmp_script\\\"\\n  local code=$?\\n  rm -f \\\"$tmp_script\\\"\\n  return $code\\n}\\n\\nfail=0\\n\\n# AC-01: exit 1 -> HAS_CHANGESETS=true, step must not fail.\\nout=$(run_case 1); code=$?\\nif [[ $code -ne 0 ]] || [[ \\\"$out\\\" != *\\\"__HAS_CHANGESETS=true__\\\"* ]]; then\\n  echo \\\"FAIL AC-01: exit 1 case: code=$code out=$out\\\"; fail=1\\nelse\\n  echo \\\"PASS AC-01\\\"\\nfi\\n\\n# AC-02: exit 2 -> HAS_CHANGESETS=false, step must not fail.\\nout=$(run_case 2); code=$?\\nif [[ $code -ne 0 ]] || [[ \\\"$out\\\" != *\\\"__HAS_CHANGESETS=false__\\\"* ]]; then\\n  echo \\\"FAIL AC-02: exit 2 case: code=$code out=$out\\\"; fail=1\\nelse\\n  echo \\\"PASS AC-02\\\"\\nfi\\n\\n# AC-04: exit 0 -> step must fail (non-zero), HAS_CHANGESETS never read.\\nout=$(run_case 0); code=$?\\nif [[ $code -eq 0 ]] || [[ \\\"$out\\\" == *\\\"__HAS_CHANGESETS=true__\\\"* ]] || [[ \\\"$out\\\" == *\\\"__HAS_CHANGESETS=false__\\\"* ]]; then\\n  echo \\\"FAIL AC-04 (exit 0): code=$code out=$out\\\"; fail=1\\nelse\\n  echo \\\"PASS AC-04 (exit 0)\\\"\\nfi\\n\\n# AC-04: exit 127 -> same requirement, a different unrecognised code.\\nout=$(run_case 127); code=$?\\nif [[ $code -eq 0 ]] || [[ \\\"$out\\\" == *\\\"__HAS_CHANGESETS=true__\\\"* ]] || [[ \\\"$out\\\" == *\\\"__HAS_CHANGESETS=false__\\\"* ]]; then\\n  echo \\\"FAIL AC-04 (exit 127): code=$code out=$out\\\"; fail=1\\nelse\\n  echo \\\"PASS AC-04 (exit 127)\\\"\\nfi\\n\\nexit $fail\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"bash .github/actions/callisto-action/tests/test_status_check_branching.sh; echo \\\"exit=$?\\\"\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"FAIL AC-01: exit 1 case: code=1 out=__HAS_CHANGESETS=<unset>__ (current code has no branch for exit 1, so it falls through to the else arm and `exit 1`, never setting HAS_CHANGESETS at all)\\nPASS AC-02\\nFAIL AC-04 (exit 0): code=0 out=__HAS_CHANGESETS=true__ (current code wrongly treats exit 0 as HAS_CHANGESETS=true and exits 0)\\nPASS AC-04 (exit 127)\\nexit=1\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \".github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml\",\n        \"old_string\": \"        echo \\\"::group::1. Inspecting Workspace Status\\\"\\n        set +e\\n        callisto status --check\\n        STATUS_EXIT=$?\\n        set -e\\n        if [[ $STATUS_EXIT -eq 0 ]]; then\\n          HAS_CHANGESETS=true\\n        elif [[ $STATUS_EXIT -eq 2 ]]; then\\n          HAS_CHANGESETS=false\\n        else\\n          echo \\\"::error::callisto status --check failed with exit code $STATUS_EXIT\\\"\\n          exit $STATUS_EXIT\\n        fi\\n        echo \\\"::endgroup::\\\"\",\n        \"new_string\": \"        echo \\\"::group::1. Inspecting Workspace Status\\\"\\n        set +e\\n        callisto status --check\\n        STATUS_EXIT=$?\\n        set -e\\n        if [[ $STATUS_EXIT -eq 1 ]]; then\\n          HAS_CHANGESETS=true\\n        elif [[ $STATUS_EXIT -eq 2 ]]; then\\n          HAS_CHANGESETS=false\\n        else\\n          echo \\\"::error::callisto status --check exited with unexpected code $STATUS_EXIT (expected 1 for pending changesets or 2 for none pending)\\\"\\n          exit 1\\n        fi\\n        echo \\\"::endgroup::\\\"\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"bash .github/actions/callisto-action/tests/test_status_check_branching.sh; echo \\\"exit=$?\\\"\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"PASS AC-01\\nPASS AC-02\\nPASS AC-04 (exit 0)\\nPASS AC-04 (exit 127)\\nexit=0\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"fix(action): correct callisto status --check exit-code branching\\n\\nExit 1 (pending changesets) previously had no branch and fell through\\nto a passthrough `exit $STATUS_EXIT`; exit 0 was wrongly treated as\\n\\\"has changesets\\\". Any unrecognised exit code (including 0) now emits\\nan ::error:: annotation and fails the step with a guaranteed non-zero\\nexit instead of ever proceeding into the release-PR or publish branch.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T2\",\n      \"cluster\": \"action-script-exit-code\",\n      \"description\": \"Correct crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs's status exit-code-contract doc comment, which currently claims 0 is returned under --check when at least one pending changeset exists (contradicting check_exit_code_raw at status.rs:18-28, which returns 1 in that case).\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-05\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs\", \"crates/callisto-cli/tests/status_doc_comment_test.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"The doc comment is prose, not executable logic, so its 'test' is a mechanical source-text pin: assert the old wrong claim is gone and the corrected claim is present, using include_str! on main.rs itself so the test reads the real file, not a copy.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"create\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-cli/tests/status_doc_comment_test.rs\",\n        \"content\": \"//! Pins the wording of main.rs's `status` exit-code-contract doc comment\\n//! against check_exit_code_raw's actual behavior (AC-05).\\n\\nconst MAIN_RS: &str = include_str!(\\\"../src/main.rs\\\");\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn status_exit_code_doc_comment_does_not_claim_zero_for_check_with_pending_changesets() {\\n    assert!(\\n        !MAIN_RS.contains(\\\"0 when no errors and (no --check OR at least one pending changeset)\\\"),\\n        \\\"main.rs's status exit-code doc comment must not claim 0 is returned under --check \\\\\\n         when changesets are pending; check_exit_code_raw (status.rs) returns 1 in that case\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn status_exit_code_doc_comment_states_correct_check_contract() {\\n    assert!(\\n        MAIN_RS.contains(\\\"OR when --check is set and at least one package has pending changesets\\\"),\\n        \\\"main.rs's status exit-code doc comment must state --check returns 1 when at least \\\\\\n         one package has pending changesets\\\"\\n    );\\n    assert!(\\n        MAIN_RS.contains(\\\"when --check is set, there are no diagnostic\\\"),\\n        \\\"main.rs's status exit-code doc comment must state --check returns 2 only when there \\\\\\n         are no diagnostic errors and no changesets are pending\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-cli --test status_doc_comment_test\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"test status_exit_code_doc_comment_states_correct_check_contract ... FAILED\\nassertion failed: MAIN_RS.contains(\\\"OR when --check is set and at least one package has pending changesets\\\")\\ntest status_exit_code_doc_comment_does_not_claim_zero_for_check_with_pending_changesets ... ok\\ntest result: FAILED. 1 passed; 1 failed\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs\",\n        \"old_string\": \"//   status         0 when no errors and (no --check OR at least one pending changeset)\\n//                  1 when any diagnostic is Error-severity (or Warning under --strict)\\n//                  2 (ExitCode::from(2)) when --check is set and no changesets are pending\",\n        \"new_string\": \"//   status         0 when no errors and --check is not set\\n//                  1 when any diagnostic is Error-severity (or Warning under --strict),\\n//                    OR when --check is set and at least one package has pending changesets\\n//                  2 (ExitCode::from(2)) when --check is set, there are no diagnostic\\n//                    errors, and no changesets are pending\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-cli --test status_doc_comment_test\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test status_exit_code_doc_comment_does_not_claim_zero_for_check_with_pending_changesets ... ok\\ntest status_exit_code_doc_comment_states_correct_check_contract ... ok\\ntest result: ok. 2 passed\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"docs(cli): correct status --check exit-code contract doc comment\\n\\nThe doc comment claimed 0 is returned under --check whenever a\\nchangeset is pending; check_exit_code_raw actually returns 1 in that\\ncase. Corrects the comment to match the implementation exactly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T3\",\n      \"cluster\": \"tag-sha-fabrication\",\n      \"description\": \"Fix create_tags_with_options's apply path (permit Some, tag.rs:82-117) so that when the per-release tag already exists at a commit different from release.sha, the reported CreatedTag.sha is the tag's real target via GitDataSource::resolve_commit, not release.sha -- and fail-fast with Err(GraphError::Vcs) when resolve_commit returns Ok(None) or Err.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-06\", \"AC-06b\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs\", \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Stub CommandRunner fixture follows aggregate.rs's FakeRevParseRunner / tags_laziness_test.rs's non-repo-dir pattern: a tempdir gix cannot discover forces GitAccess through the CommandRunner shell fallback deterministically for both `git tag --list` (contains_tag) and `git rev-parse --verify --quiet <tag>^{commit}` (resolve_commit).\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"create\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs\",\n        \"content\": \"//! Regression tests for tag.rs's per-release-tag sha fabrication fix\\n//! (AC-06, AC-06b, AC-06c, AC-06d, AC-07, AC-08). This file is built up\\n//! across three tasks (T3: apply path, T4: dry-run path); each task adds\\n//! its own #[test] functions to the shared fixtures below.\\n\\nuse std::path::Path;\\n\\nuse callisto_graph::commands::{create_tags_with_options, TagOptions};\\nuse callisto_graph::locate::IgnoreWalkLocator;\\nuse callisto_graph::{GraphError, Workspace};\\nuse callisto_model::{\\n    ApplyPermit, CommandError, CommandOutput, CommandRunner, CommitSha, PackageId, PublishPlan,\\n    ReleaseEntry, TagName, SCHEMA_VERSION,\\n};\\n\\nfn write_minimal_workspace(root: &Path) {\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[workspace]\\\\nmembers = [\\\\\\\"crates/*\\\\\\\"]\\\\nresolver = \\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n    let pkg_dir = root.join(\\\"crates/my-app\\\");\\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(&pkg_dir).unwrap();\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        pkg_dir.join(\\\"Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n        \\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"my-app\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"0.1.0\\\\\\\"\\\\nedition = \\\\\\\"2021\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n}\\n\\nenum RevParse {\\n    Sha(String),\\n    NotFound,\\n    CommandErr,\\n}\\n\\n/// A `CommandRunner` double answering `git tag --list` (whether the\\n/// per-release tag exists) and `git rev-parse --verify --quiet <tag>^{commit}`\\n/// (the tag's real current target, or a failure) so the apply and dry-run\\n/// paths' existing-tag-sha-resolution logic can be tested without a real\\n/// diverging git repository.\\nstruct StubTagRunner {\\n    tag_exists: bool,\\n    tag_name: String,\\n    rev_parse: RevParse,\\n}\\n\\nimpl CommandRunner for StubTagRunner {\\n    fn run(\\n        &self,\\n        program: &str,\\n        args: &[&str],\\n        _cwd: &Path,\\n    ) -> Result<CommandOutput, CommandError> {\\n        assert_eq!(program, \\\"git\\\", \\\"only `git` should be shelled out to here\\\");\\n        match args {\\n            [\\\"tag\\\", \\\"--list\\\"] => Ok(CommandOutput {\\n                exit_code: Some(0),\\n                stdout: if self.tag_exists {\\n                    format!(\\\"{}\\\\n\\\", self.tag_name)\\n                } else {\\n                    String::new()\\n                },\\n                stderr: String::new(),\\n            }),\\n            [\\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"--verify\\\", \\\"--quiet\\\", rev] => {\\n                let expected = format!(\\\"{}^{{commit}}\\\", self.tag_name);\\n                assert_eq!(*rev, expected.as_str());\\n                match &self.rev_parse {\\n                    RevParse::Sha(s) => Ok(CommandOutput {\\n                        exit_code: Some(0),\\n                        stdout: format!(\\\"{s}\\\\n\\\"),\\n                        stderr: String::new(),\\n                    }),\\n                    RevParse::NotFound => Ok(CommandOutput {\\n                        exit_code: Some(1),\\n                        stdout: String::new(),\\n                        stderr: String::new(),\\n                    }),\\n                    RevParse::CommandErr => Err(CommandError::NotFound {\\n                        program: \\\"git\\\".to_string(),\\n                    }),\\n                }\\n            }\\n            other => panic!(\\\"unexpected git invocation: {other:?}\\\"),\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn assert_non_repo(root: &Path) {\\n    assert!(\\n        callisto_vcs::GitRepository::discover(root).is_err(),\\n        \\\"test fixture must not be discoverable as a Git repo\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\\nfn release_entry(tag_name: &str, sha: &str) -> ReleaseEntry {\\n    ReleaseEntry {\\n        package: PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap(),\\n        tag_name: TagName(tag_name.to_string()),\\n        sha: CommitSha::parse(sha).unwrap(),\\n        changelog_section: None,\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn plan_with_release(entry: ReleaseEntry) -> PublishPlan {\\n    PublishPlan {\\n        schema_version: SCHEMA_VERSION,\\n        rust_crates: vec![],\\n        npm_main_packages: vec![],\\n        npm_platform_packages: vec![],\\n        pypi_packages: vec![],\\n        releases: vec![entry],\\n        diagnostics: vec![],\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n// ---- T3: apply path (permit Some) ----\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn apply_mode_reports_real_target_when_tag_exists_and_differs_from_release_sha() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_minimal_workspace(root);\\n    assert_non_repo(root);\\n\\n    let real_sha = \\\"a\\\".repeat(40);\\n    let requested_sha = \\\"b\\\".repeat(40);\\n    let runner = StubTagRunner {\\n        tag_exists: true,\\n        tag_name: \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\".to_string(),\\n        rev_parse: RevParse::Sha(real_sha.clone()),\\n    };\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n    let plan = plan_with_release(release_entry(\\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &requested_sha));\\n    let permit = ApplyPermit::force_for_tests();\\n\\n    let report = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), Some(&permit))\\n        .expect(\\\"create_tags_with_options must succeed\\\");\\n\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        report.created_tags[0].sha.as_str(),\\n        real_sha,\\n        \\\"apply mode must report the tag's real current target, not release.sha, when the tag \\\\\\n         already exists at a different commit\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn apply_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_returns_ok_none_for_existing_tag() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_minimal_workspace(root);\\n    assert_non_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = StubTagRunner {\\n        tag_exists: true,\\n        tag_name: \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\".to_string(),\\n        rev_parse: RevParse::NotFound,\\n    };\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n    let plan = plan_with_release(release_entry(\\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &\\\"b\\\".repeat(40)));\\n    let permit = ApplyPermit::force_for_tests();\\n\\n    let result = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), Some(&permit));\\n\\n    assert!(\\n        matches!(result, Err(GraphError::Vcs(_))),\\n        \\\"must return Err(GraphError::Vcs) when resolve_commit returns Ok(None) for an \\\\\\n         already-existing tag, not fabricate release.sha; got {result:?}\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn apply_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_errors_for_existing_tag() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_minimal_workspace(root);\\n    assert_non_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = StubTagRunner {\\n        tag_exists: true,\\n        tag_name: \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\".to_string(),\\n        rev_parse: RevParse::CommandErr,\\n    };\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n    let plan = plan_with_release(release_entry(\\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &\\\"b\\\".repeat(40)));\\n    let permit = ApplyPermit::force_for_tests();\\n\\n    let result = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), Some(&permit));\\n\\n    assert!(\\n        matches!(result, Err(GraphError::Vcs(_))),\\n        \\\"must return Err(GraphError::Vcs) when resolve_commit itself errors for an \\\\\\n         already-existing tag, not fabricate release.sha; got {result:?}\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test tag_sha_fabrication_test\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"test apply_mode_reports_real_target_when_tag_exists_and_differs_from_release_sha ... FAILED\\nassertion `left == right` failed: apply mode must report the tag's real current target, not release.sha, when the tag already exists at a different commit\\n  left: \\\"bbbb...\\\" (release.sha, currently pushed unconditionally)\\n right: \\\"aaaa...\\\"\\ntest apply_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_returns_ok_none_for_existing_tag ... FAILED (returns Ok(TagReport) today, never calls resolve_commit)\\ntest apply_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_errors_for_existing_tag ... FAILED (same)\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs\",\n        \"old_string\": \"use callisto_model::{\\n    ApplyPermit, CommandRunner, CreatedTag, PublishPlan, TagReport, SCHEMA_VERSION,\\n};\\nuse callisto_vcs::GitDataSource;\",\n        \"new_string\": \"use callisto_model::{\\n    ApplyPermit, CommandRunner, CreatedTag, PublishPlan, TagReport, SCHEMA_VERSION,\\n};\\nuse callisto_vcs::{GitDataSource, VcsError};\"\n      },\n      \"implementation_2\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs\",\n        \"old_string\": \"        let already_existed = ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str);\\n\\n        if !already_existed {\\n            let msg = format!(\\\"Release {}\\\", tag_str);\\n            git.create_tag(tag_str, &release.sha, Some(&msg), permit)?;\\n        }\\n\\n        if opts.floating_major {\",\n        \"new_string\": \"        let already_existed = ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str);\\n\\n        let sha = if already_existed {\\n            match git.resolve_commit(tag_str)? {\\n                Some(actual) => actual,\\n                None => {\\n                    return Err(GraphError::Vcs(VcsError::RefNotFound {\\n                        ref_name: tag_str.to_string(),\\n                    }))\\n                }\\n            }\\n        } else {\\n            let msg = format!(\\\"Release {}\\\", tag_str);\\n            git.create_tag(tag_str, &release.sha, Some(&msg), permit)?;\\n            release.sha.clone()\\n        };\\n\\n        if opts.floating_major {\"\n      },\n      \"implementation_3\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs\",\n        \"old_string\": \"        tags.push(CreatedTag {\\n            package: release.package.clone(),\\n            tag_name: release.tag_name.clone(),\\n            sha: release.sha.clone(),\\n        });\\n    }\\n\\n    Ok(TagReport {\",\n        \"new_string\": \"        tags.push(CreatedTag {\\n            package: release.package.clone(),\\n            tag_name: release.tag_name.clone(),\\n            sha,\\n        });\\n    }\\n\\n    Ok(TagReport {\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test tag_sha_fabrication_test\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test apply_mode_reports_real_target_when_tag_exists_and_differs_from_release_sha ... ok\\ntest apply_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_returns_ok_none_for_existing_tag ... ok\\ntest apply_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_errors_for_existing_tag ... ok\\ntest result: ok. 3 passed\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"fix(graph): stop fabricating CreatedTag.sha in apply-mode tag creation\\n\\ncreate_tags_with_options's apply path pushed release.sha unconditionally\\neven when the per-release tag already existed at a different commit.\\nNow resolves the tag's real target via GitDataSource::resolve_commit\\nwhen it already exists, and fails fast (Err(GraphError::Vcs)) rather\\nthan fabricating a sha when resolution comes back empty or errors.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T4\",\n      \"cluster\": \"tag-sha-fabrication\",\n      \"description\": \"Apply the identical fix to create_tags_with_options's dry-run path (permit None, tag.rs:53-80): add the existing-tag check and resolve_commit lookup it currently lacks entirely, without performing any git write.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-06c\", \"AC-06d\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs\", \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Same StubTagRunner fixture from T3, reused via `mod` sharing since this appends to the same test file. The stub's `other => panic!` arm on any unexpected git invocation doubles as proof that dry-run never calls a write op (no `git tag -a...`), satisfying AC-06c's 'no git ref created or moved' requirement structurally.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"append\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs\",\n        \"content\": \"\\n// ---- T4: dry-run path (permit None) ----\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn dry_run_mode_reports_real_target_when_tag_exists_and_differs_from_release_sha() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_minimal_workspace(root);\\n    assert_non_repo(root);\\n\\n    let real_sha = \\\"a\\\".repeat(40);\\n    let requested_sha = \\\"b\\\".repeat(40);\\n    let runner = StubTagRunner {\\n        tag_exists: true,\\n        tag_name: \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\".to_string(),\\n        rev_parse: RevParse::Sha(real_sha.clone()),\\n    };\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n    let plan = plan_with_release(release_entry(\\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &requested_sha));\\n\\n    let report = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), None)\\n        .expect(\\\"create_tags_with_options (dry-run) must succeed\\\");\\n\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        report.created_tags[0].sha.as_str(),\\n        real_sha,\\n        \\\"dry-run mode must preview the tag's real current target, not release.sha, when the \\\\\\n         tag already exists at a different commit\\\"\\n    );\\n    // StubTagRunner panics on any git invocation other than `tag --list` and\\n    // `rev-parse --verify --quiet ...` -- reaching this point without a panic\\n    // proves no write op (e.g. `git tag -a`) was ever attempted.\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn dry_run_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_returns_ok_none_for_existing_tag() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_minimal_workspace(root);\\n    assert_non_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = StubTagRunner {\\n        tag_exists: true,\\n        tag_name: \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\".to_string(),\\n        rev_parse: RevParse::NotFound,\\n    };\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n    let plan = plan_with_release(release_entry(\\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &\\\"b\\\".repeat(40)));\\n\\n    let result = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), None);\\n\\n    assert!(\\n        matches!(result, Err(GraphError::Vcs(_))),\\n        \\\"dry-run must return Err(GraphError::Vcs) when resolve_commit returns Ok(None) for an \\\\\\n         already-existing tag, not fabricate release.sha; got {result:?}\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn dry_run_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_errors_for_existing_tag() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_minimal_workspace(root);\\n    assert_non_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = StubTagRunner {\\n        tag_exists: true,\\n        tag_name: \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\".to_string(),\\n        rev_parse: RevParse::CommandErr,\\n    };\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n    let plan = plan_with_release(release_entry(\\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &\\\"b\\\".repeat(40)));\\n\\n    let result = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), None);\\n\\n    assert!(\\n        matches!(result, Err(GraphError::Vcs(_))),\\n        \\\"dry-run must return Err(GraphError::Vcs) when resolve_commit itself errors for an \\\\\\n         already-existing tag, not fabricate release.sha; got {result:?}\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test tag_sha_fabrication_test\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"test dry_run_mode_reports_real_target_when_tag_exists_and_differs_from_release_sha ... FAILED\\nassertion `left == right` failed: dry-run mode must preview the tag's real current target, not release.sha, when the tag already exists at a different commit\\n  left: \\\"bbbb...\\\" (release.sha, currently pushed unconditionally, no existing-tag check at all in dry-run today)\\n right: \\\"aaaa...\\\"\\ntest dry_run_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_returns_ok_none_for_existing_tag ... FAILED (returns Ok(TagReport) today, never checks contains_tag or resolve_commit in dry-run)\\ntest dry_run_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_errors_for_existing_tag ... FAILED (same)\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs\",\n        \"old_string\": \"                }\\n            }\\n            tags.push(CreatedTag {\\n                package: release.package.clone(),\\n                tag_name: release.tag_name.clone(),\\n                sha: release.sha.clone(),\\n            });\\n            continue;\\n        };\",\n        \"new_string\": \"                }\\n            }\\n\\n            let already_existed = ws.tags()?.contains_tag(tag_str);\\n            let sha = if already_existed {\\n                match git.resolve_commit(tag_str)? {\\n                    Some(actual) => actual,\\n                    None => {\\n                        return Err(GraphError::Vcs(VcsError::RefNotFound {\\n                            ref_name: tag_str.to_string(),\\n                        }))\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            } else {\\n                release.sha.clone()\\n            };\\n\\n            tags.push(CreatedTag {\\n                package: release.package.clone(),\\n                tag_name: release.tag_name.clone(),\\n                sha,\\n            });\\n            continue;\\n        };\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test tag_sha_fabrication_test\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test result: ok. 6 passed (all T3 + T4 tests)\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"fix(graph): stop fabricating CreatedTag.sha in dry-run tag preview\\n\\ncreate_tags_with_options's dry-run path performed no existing-tag check\\nat all and always previewed release.sha. Now mirrors the apply path:\\nresolves the tag's real target via resolve_commit when it already\\nexists, without any git write, and fails fast rather than fabricating\\na sha when resolution is empty or errors.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T5\",\n      \"cluster\": \"tag-sha-fabrication\",\n      \"description\": \"Regression proof that the T3/T4 fix does not change behavior for the two cases where the reported sha was already correct: tag does not exist yet (AC-07), and tag already exists at exactly release.sha -- the idempotent rerun case (AC-08). Uses a real git repository fixture (not a stub) so the create_tag write path and native gix resolve_commit path are both exercised for real, in both apply and dry-run mode.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-07\", \"AC-08\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"No new implementation: T3/T4 already implemented the complete logic. This task only adds regression tests, so both are expected to pass on first run -- proving the fix introduced no regression in the two cases it must leave unchanged.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"append\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs\",\n        \"content\": \"\\n// ---- T5: regression proofs (real git repo, no stubbing) ----\\n\\nstruct PanicRunner;\\nimpl CommandRunner for PanicRunner {\\n    fn run(&self, program: &str, args: &[&str], _cwd: &Path) -> Result<CommandOutput, CommandError> {\\n        panic!(\\\"unexpected CommandRunner invocation ({program} {args:?}) -- a real .git repo is present, so GitAccess must use native gix, never the shell fallback\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn init_git_repo(dir: &Path) {\\n    let run = |args: &[&str]| {\\n        let status = std::process::Command::new(\\\"git\\\")\\n            .args(args)\\n            .current_dir(dir)\\n            .status()\\n            .expect(\\\"git should run\\\");\\n        assert!(status.success(), \\\"git {args:?} failed\\\");\\n    };\\n    run(&[\\\"init\\\", \\\"-q\\\"]);\\n    run(&[\\\"config\\\", \\\"user.email\\\", \\\"test@example.com\\\"]);\\n    run(&[\\\"config\\\", \\\"user.name\\\", \\\"Test\\\"]);\\n    run(&[\\\"add\\\", \\\".\\\"]);\\n    run(&[\\\"commit\\\", \\\"-q\\\", \\\"-m\\\", \\\"init\\\"]);\\n}\\n\\nfn git_head_sha(dir: &Path) -> String {\\n    let out = std::process::Command::new(\\\"git\\\")\\n        .args([\\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"HEAD\\\"])\\n        .current_dir(dir)\\n        .output()\\n        .unwrap();\\n    String::from_utf8(out.stdout).unwrap().trim().to_string()\\n}\\n\\nfn git_tag_exists_at(dir: &Path, tag: &str, expected_sha: &str) -> bool {\\n    let out = std::process::Command::new(\\\"git\\\")\\n        .args([\\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"--verify\\\", \\\"--quiet\\\", &format!(\\\"{tag}^{{commit}}\\\")])\\n        .current_dir(dir)\\n        .output()\\n        .unwrap();\\n    out.status.success() && String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout).trim() == expected_sha\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn tag_not_existing_reports_release_sha_in_both_modes_and_apply_creates_it() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_minimal_workspace(root);\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n    let head = git_head_sha(root);\\n\\n    let runner = PanicRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n    let plan = plan_with_release(release_entry(\\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &head));\\n\\n    // Dry-run first, while the tag genuinely does not exist yet.\\n    let dry_report = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), None)\\n        .expect(\\\"dry-run must succeed\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(dry_report.created_tags[0].sha.as_str(), head, \\\"AC-07 dry-run\\\");\\n    assert!(\\n        !git_tag_exists_at(root, \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &head),\\n        \\\"dry-run must not create the tag\\\"\\n    );\\n\\n    // Apply: tag still does not exist -> gets created at release.sha.\\n    let permit = ApplyPermit::force_for_tests();\\n    let apply_report = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), Some(&permit))\\n        .expect(\\\"apply must succeed\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(apply_report.created_tags[0].sha.as_str(), head, \\\"AC-07 apply\\\");\\n    assert!(\\n        git_tag_exists_at(root, \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &head),\\n        \\\"apply must create the tag at release.sha\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn tag_existing_at_release_sha_reports_release_sha_with_no_error_in_both_modes() {\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_minimal_workspace(root);\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n    let head = git_head_sha(root);\\n\\n    // Pre-create the tag directly via git, at exactly the sha the plan will request.\\n    let status = std::process::Command::new(\\\"git\\\")\\n        .args([\\\"tag\\\", \\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &head])\\n        .current_dir(root)\\n        .status()\\n        .unwrap();\\n    assert!(status.success());\\n\\n    let runner = PanicRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n    let plan = plan_with_release(release_entry(\\\"pkg@1.0.0\\\", &head));\\n\\n    let permit = ApplyPermit::force_for_tests();\\n    let apply_report = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), Some(&permit))\\n        .expect(\\\"idempotent apply rerun must succeed with no error\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(apply_report.created_tags[0].sha.as_str(), head, \\\"AC-08 apply\\\");\\n\\n    let dry_report = create_tags_with_options(&ws, &plan, &TagOptions::default(), None)\\n        .expect(\\\"dry-run against already-tagged state must succeed with no error\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(dry_report.created_tags[0].sha.as_str(), head, \\\"AC-08 dry-run\\\");\\n}\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test tag_sha_fabrication_test tag_not_existing_reports_release_sha_in_both_modes_and_apply_creates_it tag_existing_at_release_sha_reports_release_sha_with_no_error_in_both_modes\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"N/A -- pure regression-proof task: T3/T4 already implement the complete apply-path and dry-run-path logic these tests exercise, so both are expected to pass immediately (no red phase). If either fails, it means T3/T4's fix broke a case it was required to leave unchanged.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"none\",\n        \"note\": \"No code change. T3/T4 already implemented the full logic these tests verify.\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test tag_sha_fabrication_test\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test result: ok. 8 passed (all T3 + T4 + T5 tests)\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin AC-07/AC-08 no-regression behavior for tag sha resolution\\n\\nProves the AC-06/AC-06b/AC-06c/AC-06d fix does not change reported sha\\nfor the two cases it must leave alone: tag not yet existing, and an\\nidempotent rerun where the existing tag already matches release.sha --\\nin both apply and --dry-run mode, against a real git repository.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T6\",\n      \"cluster\": \"changelog-section\",\n      \"description\": \"Add the new DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError variant to the already-#[non_exhaustive] enum, needed by plan_publish's changelog-read-failure path (AC-12c).\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-12c\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Purely additive foundation step, done first so the next task can reference the variant. Mirrors the file's existing kebab-case round-trip test pattern exactly.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs\",\n        \"old_string\": \"    /// `callisto matrix` found the same platform triple declared more than once within one\\n    /// package's own `napi.targets`/`[tool.maturin].targets` -- the duplicate is dropped\\n    /// (first occurrence wins) rather than treated as a hard error.\\n    DuplicatePlatformTriple,\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::DiagnosticCode;\",\n        \"new_string\": \"    /// `callisto matrix` found the same platform triple declared more than once within one\\n    /// package's own `napi.targets`/`[tool.maturin].targets` -- the duplicate is dropped\\n    /// (first occurrence wins) rather than treated as a hard error.\\n    DuplicatePlatformTriple,\\n    /// A changelog file exists at the package's resolved `pkg.changelog` path but could not\\n    /// be read -- invalid UTF-8, permission denied, or any I/O failure other than \\\"file does\\n    /// not exist\\\" (that case is `ChangelogSectionNotFound` instead). `changelog_section` is\\n    /// left `None` for the package; `plan_publish` is not aborted.\\n    ChangelogReadError,\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::DiagnosticCode;\\n\\n    /// AC-12c: DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError must serialize to the kebab-case string\\n    /// \\\"changelog-read-error\\\" and deserialize back to the same variant.\\n    #[test]\\n    fn changelog_read_error_serializes_to_kebab_case() {\\n        let code = DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError;\\n        let json = serde_json::to_string(&code).unwrap();\\n        assert_eq!(\\n            json,\\n            r#\\\"\\\"changelog-read-error\\\"\\\"#,\\n            \\\"DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError must serialize to \\\\\\\"changelog-read-error\\\\\\\"\\\",\\n        );\\n        let roundtrip: DiagnosticCode = serde_json::from_str(&json).unwrap();\\n        assert_eq!(\\n            roundtrip, code,\\n            \\\"deserialized value must equal the original variant\\\",\\n        );\\n    }\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-model --lib diagnostic::tests::changelog_read_error_serializes_to_kebab_case\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"error[E0599]: no variant or associated item named `ChangelogReadError` found for enum `DiagnosticCode`\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"none\",\n        \"note\": \"The single edit above adds both the variant and its test in one change (the variant cannot compile without the test referencing it, and vice versa is not applicable here since this is a pure additive enum variant) -- run the test command again after the edit to confirm green.\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-model --lib diagnostic::tests::changelog_read_error_serializes_to_kebab_case\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test diagnostic::tests::changelog_read_error_serializes_to_kebab_case ... ok\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"feat(model): add DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError variant\\n\\nAdditive #[non_exhaustive] enum variant for plan_publish to report when\\na package's changelog file exists but fails to read (invalid UTF-8 or\\nany I/O error other than not-found) rather than silently treating it\\nthe same as a missing file.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T7\",\n      \"cluster\": \"changelog-section\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement changelog_section population in plan_publish: replace the hardcoded None (publish.rs:427) with a call through a new resolve_changelog_section helper that reads pkg.changelog and calls callisto_changelog::extract_section, covering the happy path (AC-10) and the file-does-not-exist path (AC-11) with new tests. The helper's implementation also handles the empty-section, no-heading, and unreadable-file cases in the same pass (proved by T8/T9's regression tests).\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-10\", \"AC-11\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs\", \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Reuses this file's existing fixture idioms (init_git_repo, DummyRunner) so a package with no changeset and no matching tag is naturally a release candidate (is_release=true via the untagged cur_ver path), letting the test drive plan_publish end-to-end rather than unit-testing the helper in isolation.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"append\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs\",\n        \"content\": \"\\n// ---- changelog_section population (AC-10, AC-11) ----\\n\\nfn write_release_candidate_pkg(root: &std::path::Path, version: &str) {\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n        format!(\\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"pkg\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"{version}\\\\\\\"\\\\nedition = \\\\\\\"2021\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\"),\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_populates_changelog_section_when_heading_has_content() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_release_candidate_pkg(root, \\\"1.2.3\\\");\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"CHANGELOG.md\\\"),\\n        \\\"# Changelog\\\\n\\\\n## 1.2.3\\\\n\\\\nSome release notes here.\\\\n\\\\n## 1.2.2\\\\n\\\\nOlder notes.\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let release = plan\\n        .releases\\n        .iter()\\n        .find(|r| r.package == pkg_id)\\n        .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\\\"expected a ReleaseEntry for pkg, got: {:?}\\\", plan.releases));\\n\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        release.changelog_section.as_deref(),\\n        Some(\\\"Some release notes here.\\\"),\\n        \\\"changelog_section must equal extract_section's trimmed output for the matching heading\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_file_does_not_exist() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_release_candidate_pkg(root, \\\"1.2.3\\\");\\n    // Deliberately no CHANGELOG.md written.\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let release = plan\\n        .releases\\n        .iter()\\n        .find(|r| r.package == pkg_id)\\n        .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\\\"expected a ReleaseEntry for pkg, got: {:?}\\\", plan.releases));\\n\\n    assert_eq!(release.changelog_section, None, \\\"AC-11: no changelog file on disk\\\");\\n    assert!(\\n        plan.diagnostics.iter().any(|d| d.code\\n            == callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound\\n            && d.package.as_ref() == Some(&pkg_id)),\\n        \\\"expected a ChangelogSectionNotFound diagnostic naming pkg; got {:?}\\\",\\n        plan.diagnostics\\n    );\\n}\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_populates_changelog_section_when_heading_has_content plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_file_does_not_exist\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"test plan_publish_populates_changelog_section_when_heading_has_content ... FAILED\\nassertion `left == right` failed: changelog_section must equal extract_section's trimmed output for the matching heading\\n  left: None\\n right: Some(\\\"Some release notes here.\\\")\\ntest plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_file_does_not_exist ... FAILED\\nassertion failed: expected a ChangelogSectionNotFound diagnostic naming pkg; got []\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs\",\n        \"old_string\": \"pub fn plan_publish<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(\",\n        \"new_string\": \"/// Resolves a package's `changelog_section` for `plan_publish`: reads the file at\\n/// `ws_root.join(changelog_rel_path)` and extracts the `## {ver}` section via\\n/// `callisto_changelog::extract_section`. Every non-fatal outcome (file not found, no\\n/// matching heading, empty matched section, or an unreadable file) leaves the return value\\n/// `None` and pushes exactly one Warning diagnostic into `diagnostics` rather than aborting\\n/// the plan -- `ChangelogSectionNotFound` for the first three (AC-10b, AC-11, AC-12），\\n/// `ChangelogReadError` for a read failure that is not \\\"file does not exist\\\" (AC-12c).\\nfn resolve_changelog_section(\\n    ws_root: &std::path::Path,\\n    changelog_rel_path: &std::path::Path,\\n    pkg_id: &callisto_model::PackageId,\\n    ver: &callisto_model::Version,\\n    diagnostics: &mut Vec<callisto_model::Diagnostic>,\\n) -> Option<String> {\\n    let full_path = ws_root.join(changelog_rel_path);\\n    let content = match std::fs::read_to_string(&full_path) {\\n        Ok(c) => c,\\n        Err(e) if e.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound => {\\n            diagnostics.push(callisto_model::Diagnostic {\\n                code: callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound,\\n                severity: callisto_model::DiagnosticSeverity::Warning,\\n                message: format!(\\n                    \\\"no changelog file found at `{}` for package `{}`\\\",\\n                    changelog_rel_path.display(),\\n                    pkg_id.display_name()\\n                ),\\n                package: Some(pkg_id.clone()),\\n                path: Some(changelog_rel_path.to_path_buf()),\\n                escalated_by: None,\\n                governed_by: None,\\n            });\\n            return None;\\n        }\\n        Err(e) => {\\n            diagnostics.push(callisto_model::Diagnostic {\\n                code: callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError,\\n                severity: callisto_model::DiagnosticSeverity::Warning,\\n                message: format!(\\n                    \\\"could not read changelog at `{}` for package `{}`: {e}\\\",\\n                    changelog_rel_path.display(),\\n                    pkg_id.display_name()\\n                ),\\n                package: Some(pkg_id.clone()),\\n                path: Some(changelog_rel_path.to_path_buf()),\\n                escalated_by: None,\\n                governed_by: None,\\n            });\\n            return None;\\n        }\\n    };\\n\\n    match callisto_changelog::extract_section(&content, ver) {\\n        Some(section) => Some(section.to_string()),\\n        None => {\\n            diagnostics.push(callisto_model::Diagnostic {\\n                code: callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound,\\n                severity: callisto_model::DiagnosticSeverity::Warning,\\n                message: format!(\\n                    \\\"no `## {}` section found in `{}` for package `{}`\\\",\\n                    ver.render(),\\n                    changelog_rel_path.display(),\\n                    pkg_id.display_name()\\n                ),\\n                package: Some(pkg_id.clone()),\\n                path: Some(changelog_rel_path.to_path_buf()),\\n                escalated_by: None,\\n                governed_by: None,\\n            });\\n            None\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn plan_publish<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(\"\n      },\n      \"implementation_2\": {\n        \"action\": \"edit\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/publish.rs\",\n        \"old_string\": \"                if let (Some(ref sha), Some(idx)) = (&head_sha, tag_index) {\\n                    releases.push(ReleaseEntry {\\n                        package: pkg.id.clone(),\\n                        tag_name: idx.template(&pkg.id).render(&ver),\\n                        sha: sha.clone(),\\n                        changelog_section: None,\\n                    });\\n                }\",\n        \"new_string\": \"                if let (Some(ref sha), Some(idx)) = (&head_sha, tag_index) {\\n                    let changelog_section = pkg.changelog.as_ref().and_then(|ch_path| {\\n                        resolve_changelog_section(\\n                            &ws.root,\\n                            ch_path,\\n                            &pkg.id,\\n                            &ver,\\n                            &mut diagnostics,\\n                        )\\n                    });\\n                    releases.push(ReleaseEntry {\\n                        package: pkg.id.clone(),\\n                        tag_name: idx.template(&pkg.id).render(&ver),\\n                        sha: sha.clone(),\\n                        changelog_section,\\n                    });\\n                }\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_populates_changelog_section_when_heading_has_content plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_file_does_not_exist\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test plan_publish_populates_changelog_section_when_heading_has_content ... ok\\ntest plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_file_does_not_exist ... ok\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"fix(graph): populate ReleaseEntry.changelog_section from the package's changelog\\n\\nplan_publish hardcoded changelog_section to None. Now reads the file\\nat the package's resolved pkg.changelog path (the same field callisto\\nversion's changelog-rendering step already uses) and extracts the\\nrelease's `## {version}` section via callisto_changelog::extract_section,\\nwarning via a ChangelogSectionNotFound/ChangelogReadError diagnostic\\nrather than erroring the plan when the file or section is unavailable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T8\",\n      \"cluster\": \"changelog-section\",\n      \"description\": \"Regression proof that resolve_changelog_section (T7) also correctly handles the empty-section case (AC-10b) and the no-matching-heading case (AC-12) -- both already flow through the same extract_section call and ChangelogSectionNotFound diagnostic T7 implemented.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-10b\", \"AC-12\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"No new implementation: extract_section (write.rs:131-136) already returns None uniformly for both an empty matched section and a missing heading, and T7's helper already reports both via ChangelogSectionNotFound. Both tests are expected to pass on first run.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"append\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs\",\n        \"content\": \"\\n// ---- regression: AC-10b (empty section), AC-12 (no matching heading) ----\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_matched_heading_section_is_empty() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_release_candidate_pkg(root, \\\"1.2.3\\\");\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"CHANGELOG.md\\\"),\\n        \\\"# Changelog\\\\n\\\\n## 1.2.3\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n## 1.2.2\\\\n\\\\nOlder notes.\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let release = plan.releases.iter().find(|r| r.package == pkg_id).unwrap();\\n\\n    assert_eq!(release.changelog_section, None, \\\"AC-10b: matched heading has empty content\\\");\\n    assert!(\\n        plan.diagnostics.iter().any(|d| d.code\\n            == callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound\\n            && d.package.as_ref() == Some(&pkg_id)),\\n        \\\"expected a ChangelogSectionNotFound diagnostic naming pkg; got {:?}\\\",\\n        plan.diagnostics\\n    );\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_no_matching_heading() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_release_candidate_pkg(root, \\\"1.2.3\\\");\\n    std::fs::write(\\n        root.join(\\\"CHANGELOG.md\\\"),\\n        \\\"# Changelog\\\\n\\\\n## 1.2.2\\\\n\\\\nOlder notes only, no 1.2.3 section.\\\\n\\\",\\n    )\\n    .unwrap();\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let release = plan.releases.iter().find(|r| r.package == pkg_id).unwrap();\\n\\n    assert_eq!(release.changelog_section, None, \\\"AC-12: no `## 1.2.3` heading in the file\\\");\\n    assert!(\\n        plan.diagnostics.iter().any(|d| d.code\\n            == callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound\\n            && d.package.as_ref() == Some(&pkg_id)),\\n        \\\"expected a ChangelogSectionNotFound diagnostic naming pkg; got {:?}\\\",\\n        plan.diagnostics\\n    );\\n}\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_matched_heading_section_is_empty plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_no_matching_heading\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"N/A -- pure regression-proof task: T7's resolve_changelog_section already calls extract_section, which already returns None uniformly for an empty matched section and for no matching heading. Both tests are expected to pass on first run.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"none\",\n        \"note\": \"No code change. T7 already implements the logic these tests verify.\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_matched_heading_section_is_empty plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_no_matching_heading\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_matched_heading_section_is_empty ... ok\\ntest plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_when_no_matching_heading ... ok\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin AC-10b/AC-12 changelog_section no-regression behavior\\n\\nProves resolve_changelog_section correctly leaves changelog_section as\\nNone (with a ChangelogSectionNotFound diagnostic, no error) both when a\\nmatched ## {version} heading's section is empty and when no heading\\nmatches the release version at all.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T9\",\n      \"cluster\": \"changelog-section\",\n      \"description\": \"Regression proof that resolve_changelog_section distinguishes an unreadable changelog file (invalid UTF-8) from a missing one, reporting ChangelogReadError rather than ChangelogSectionNotFound (AC-12c).\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-12c\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"No new implementation: T7's helper already has a distinct match arm for a read error other than NotFound, using the ChangelogReadError variant T6 added. This test is expected to pass on first run.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"append\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-graph/tests/publish_tests.rs\",\n        \"content\": \"\\n// ---- regression: AC-12c (unreadable / invalid UTF-8 changelog file) ----\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_and_emits_read_error_for_invalid_utf8() {\\n    use callisto_graph::commands::{plan_publish, PublishOptions};\\n\\n    let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n    let root = tmp.path();\\n    write_release_candidate_pkg(root, \\\"1.2.3\\\");\\n    std::fs::write(root.join(\\\"CHANGELOG.md\\\"), [0x23, 0x20, 0xFF, 0xFE, 0x0A]).unwrap();\\n    init_git_repo(root);\\n\\n    let runner = DummyRunner;\\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n    let ws = callisto_graph::Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &locator, &runner).unwrap();\\n\\n    let plan = plan_publish(&ws, &PublishOptions::default()).expect(\\\"plan_publish must succeed\\\");\\n    let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg\\\").unwrap();\\n    let release = plan.releases.iter().find(|r| r.package == pkg_id).unwrap();\\n\\n    assert_eq!(release.changelog_section, None, \\\"AC-12c: file exists but is not valid UTF-8\\\");\\n    assert!(\\n        plan.diagnostics.iter().any(|d| d.code\\n            == callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError\\n            && d.package.as_ref() == Some(&pkg_id)),\\n        \\\"expected a ChangelogReadError diagnostic naming pkg; got {:?}\\\",\\n        plan.diagnostics\\n    );\\n    assert!(\\n        !plan.diagnostics.iter().any(|d| d.code\\n            == callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::ChangelogSectionNotFound\\n            && d.package.as_ref() == Some(&pkg_id)),\\n        \\\"an unreadable file must not also be reported as ChangelogSectionNotFound\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_and_emits_read_error_for_invalid_utf8\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"N/A -- pure regression-proof task: T7's resolve_changelog_section already distinguishes ErrorKind::NotFound (ChangelogSectionNotFound) from any other read error (ChangelogReadError, added in T6). Expected to pass on first run.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"none\",\n        \"note\": \"No code change. T6 (variant) + T7 (helper's Err(e) arm) already implement the logic this test verifies.\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --test publish_tests plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_and_emits_read_error_for_invalid_utf8\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test plan_publish_leaves_changelog_section_none_and_emits_read_error_for_invalid_utf8 ... ok\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin AC-12c changelog read-error diagnostic behavior\\n\\nProves an unreadable (invalid UTF-8) changelog file is reported via\\nDiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError, distinct from the not-found case,\\nand does not also fire ChangelogSectionNotFound for the same package.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T10\",\n      \"cluster\": \"schema-guard\",\n      \"description\": \"Guard/regression proof for AC-13: confirm via `callisto schema` that no report struct (StatusReport, CreatedTag, TagReport, ReleaseEntry, PublishPlan) gained, lost, renamed, or retyped a field, and that the only DiagnosticCode schema delta is the new changelog-read-error variant.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-13\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-cli/tests/schema_guard_test.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Expected field/variant sets below were captured directly from `callisto schema --type <X>` run against the live, unmodified repository before any task in this plan was implemented, so they are the true pre-fix baseline -- this task's assertions are a real diff, not a guess. Run last, after every other task, so it also functions as the plan's final integration guard.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"action\": \"create\",\n        \"file_path\": \"crates/callisto-cli/tests/schema_guard_test.rs\",\n        \"content\": \"//! AC-13 guard: none of this track's fixes may change any report struct's field shape.\\n//! The only permitted schema delta is the additive DiagnosticCode::ChangelogReadError\\n//! variant. Expected sets below were captured from `callisto schema` against the live,\\n//! unmodified repository before this track's fixes were implemented.\\n\\nuse std::collections::BTreeSet;\\nuse std::process::Command;\\n\\nfn run_schema(target: &str) -> serde_json::Value {\\n    let bin = env!(\\\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_callisto\\\");\\n    let out = Command::new(bin)\\n        .args([\\\"schema\\\", \\\"--type\\\", target])\\n        .output()\\n        .expect(\\\"callisto schema must run\\\");\\n    assert!(\\n        out.status.success(),\\n        \\\"callisto schema --type {target} failed: {}\\\",\\n        String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stderr)\\n    );\\n    serde_json::from_slice(&out.stdout).expect(\\\"schema output must be valid JSON\\\")\\n}\\n\\nfn required_and_props(schema: &serde_json::Value) -> (BTreeSet<String>, BTreeSet<String>) {\\n    let required: BTreeSet<String> = schema[\\\"required\\\"]\\n        .as_array()\\n        .unwrap()\\n        .iter()\\n        .map(|v| v.as_str().unwrap().to_string())\\n        .collect();\\n    let props: BTreeSet<String> = schema[\\\"properties\\\"]\\n        .as_object()\\n        .unwrap()\\n        .keys()\\n        .cloned()\\n        .collect();\\n    (required, props)\\n}\\n\\nfn set(items: &[&str]) -> BTreeSet<String> {\\n    items.iter().map(|s| s.to_string()).collect()\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn ac13_report_struct_field_shapes_are_unchanged() {\\n    let tag_schema = run_schema(\\\"tag\\\");\\n    let (req, props) = required_and_props(&tag_schema);\\n    assert_eq!(req, set(&[\\\"createdTags\\\", \\\"schemaVersion\\\"]));\\n    assert_eq!(props, set(&[\\\"createdTags\\\", \\\"diagnostics\\\", \\\"schemaVersion\\\"]));\\n\\n    let created_tag = &tag_schema[\\\"definitions\\\"][\\\"CreatedTag\\\"];\\n    let (req, props) = required_and_props(created_tag);\\n    assert_eq!(req, set(&[\\\"package\\\", \\\"sha\\\", \\\"tagName\\\"]));\\n    assert_eq!(props, req);\\n\\n    let status_schema = run_schema(\\\"status\\\");\\n    let (req, props) = required_and_props(&status_schema);\\n    assert_eq!(req, set(&[\\\"packages\\\", \\\"schemaVersion\\\"]));\\n    assert_eq!(props, set(&[\\\"diagnostics\\\", \\\"packages\\\", \\\"schemaVersion\\\"]));\\n\\n    let plan_schema = run_schema(\\\"plan-publish\\\");\\n    let (req, props) = required_and_props(&plan_schema);\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        req,\\n        set(&[\\\"npmMainPackages\\\", \\\"npmPlatformPackages\\\", \\\"releases\\\", \\\"rustCrates\\\", \\\"schemaVersion\\\"])\\n    );\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        props,\\n        set(&[\\n            \\\"diagnostics\\\", \\\"npmMainPackages\\\", \\\"npmPlatformPackages\\\", \\\"pypiPackages\\\", \\\"releases\\\",\\n            \\\"rustCrates\\\", \\\"schemaVersion\\\"\\n        ])\\n    );\\n\\n    let release_entry = &plan_schema[\\\"definitions\\\"][\\\"ReleaseEntry\\\"];\\n    let (req, props) = required_and_props(release_entry);\\n    assert_eq!(req, set(&[\\\"package\\\", \\\"sha\\\", \\\"tagName\\\"]));\\n    assert_eq!(props, set(&[\\\"changelogSection\\\", \\\"package\\\", \\\"sha\\\", \\\"tagName\\\"]));\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn ac13_diagnostic_code_enum_gains_only_changelog_read_error() {\\n    let tag_schema = run_schema(\\\"tag\\\");\\n    let variants: BTreeSet<String> = tag_schema[\\\"definitions\\\"][\\\"DiagnosticCode\\\"][\\\"oneOf\\\"]\\n        .as_array()\\n        .unwrap()\\n        .iter()\\n        .map(|v| v[\\\"enum\\\"][0].as_str().unwrap().to_string())\\n        .collect();\\n\\n    let expected = set(&[\\n        \\\"empty-changeset\\\", \\\"empty-summary\\\", \\\"unknown-package\\\", \\\"invalid-package-name\\\",\\n        \\\"napi-target-added-not-in-members\\\", \\\"napi-target-removed-still-on-disk\\\",\\n        \\\"napi-coordination-not-yet-supported\\\", \\\"graph-edge-disagreement\\\",\\n        \\\"range-not-round-trippable\\\", \\\"catalog-spec-not-rewritten\\\", \\\"tag-glob-non-version-match\\\",\\n        \\\"changesets-config-key-dropped\\\", \\\"pre-major-inference-inert\\\", \\\"changelog-section-not-found\\\",\\n        \\\"changeset-read-error\\\", \\\"git-discovery-failed\\\", \\\"bare-rule-matches-multiple-ecosystems\\\",\\n        \\\"unrecognised-platform-triple\\\", \\\"publish-target-not-implemented\\\", \\\"package-set-matched-nothing\\\",\\n        \\\"duplicate-platform-triple\\\", \\\"changelog-read-error\\\",\\n    ]);\\n\\n    assert_eq!(\\n        variants, expected,\\n        \\\"DiagnosticCode schema must gain exactly one new variant: changelog-read-error\\\"\\n    );\\n}\\n\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-cli --test schema_guard_test\",\n        \"expected_failure_output\": \"test ac13_diagnostic_code_enum_gains_only_changelog_read_error ... FAILED\\nassertion `left == right` failed: DiagnosticCode schema must gain exactly one new variant: changelog-read-error\\n(fails until T6 adds the variant; ac13_report_struct_field_shapes_are_unchanged passes throughout since T3-T9 never change any struct's field shape, only field values and enum membership)\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"action\": \"none\",\n        \"note\": \"No code change. This task only adds the guard test; it becomes green once T6 (adds the enum variant) is in place, and stays green through every other task since none of them change a struct's field shape. Run last.\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-cli --test schema_guard_test\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test ac13_report_struct_field_shapes_are_unchanged ... ok\\ntest ac13_diagnostic_code_enum_gains_only_changelog_read_error ... ok\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(cli): add AC-13 schema guard against report struct field drift\\n\\nAsserts callisto schema output for tag/status/plan-publish reports has\\nan unchanged field shape after this track's fixes, and that the only\\nDiagnosticCode delta is the new additive changelog-read-error variant.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ba9e9487-021a-4691-8098-efc9203b79de","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/U