{"parentUuid":"0ed23553-00c1-474d-ac4b-3c5c6aaa440a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeChMQMbRqug53uqEkwmo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xrt1nJhwgimknDNCHdcWLb","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement Track 4 T1","subagent_type":"lambda:implementer","prompt":"Workspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto (Rust cargo workspace, moon-managed). Execute exactly task T1 from the plan at .claude/plans/PLAN-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS.json — read the plan from disk and pull T1's exact steps from there (test content, implementation old_string/new_string, run/verify commands) rather than relying on any paraphrase.\n\nWorkspace manifest from recon (baseline confirmed green: callisto-graph 381 tests, callisto-cli 48 tests, callisto-model 86 tests, all passing; spec hash matches plan's spec_hash, no drift):\n{\n  \"workspace_root\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\",\n  \"language\": \"rust\",\n  \"test_runner\": \"cargo test\",\n  \"build_tool\": \"cargo\",\n  \"spec_file_path\": \".claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK4-RELEASE-PIPELINE-CONTRACT-CORRECTNESS.json\"\n}\n\nT1 in one sentence: fix .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml's \"Inspecting Workspace Status\" step so exit code 1 (pending changesets) sets HAS_CHANGESETS=true, exit 2 (none pending) sets HAS_CHANGESETS=false, and any other exit code (including 0, which the CLI never actually returns for --check) fails the step with a guaranteed non-zero exit and an ::error:: annotation rather than a passthrough `exit $STATUS_EXIT`. This is bash, not Rust — the plan's test approach is a new self-contained bash script (.github/actions/callisto-action/tests/test_status_check_branching.sh) that mechanically extracts the exact run-body text between the step's `::group::1. Inspecting Workspace Status` and `::endgroup::` markers directly out of action.yml (so the test can never drift from the real file) and executes it against a stubbed `callisto` shell function for exit codes 1, 2, 0, and 127, then checks step exit code and the HAS_CHANGESETS value observed.\n\nFollow the plan's RED step first: create the test script exactly as specified, run it against the CURRENT (buggy) action.yml, confirm it fails exactly as predicted (AC-01 and AC-04's exit-0 case fail, AC-02 and AC-04's exit-127 case pass — since exit 127 already happens to fall into the current unconditional else-branch's `exit $STATUS_EXIT`, which is non-zero for 127). Then apply the plan's exact action.yml edit, confirm all 4 cases pass. Commit with the plan's exact commit message when green.\n\nSince this task has no cargo compile step, standard `just ci`-style checks don't fully apply — but do run `cargo fmt --check` and confirm no Rust files were touched unexpectedly (this task should ONLY touch action.yml and the new test script). Single, self-contained task — do not start T2 or any other task."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1673,"cache_read_input_tokens":444977,"output_tokens":1854,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":672},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1673,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1854,"cache_read_input_tokens":444977,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1673,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1673},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeChMMD5xNomcv4cwyd9c","type":"assistant","uuid":"6ffb868d-434d-4678-ae68-f7ec0ff005ed","timestamp":"2026-08-19T19:56:57.800Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061