ner and crates/callisto-graph/tests/tags_laziness_test.rs.\n\nFollow the plan's RED step first: create the test file with T3's three tests (apply_mode_reports_real_target_when_tag_exists_and_differs_from_release_sha, apply_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_returns_ok_none_for_existing_tag, apply_mode_fails_fast_when_resolve_commit_errors_for_existing_tag) plus the shared fixture helpers (write_minimal_workspace, StubTagRunner, assert_non_repo, release_entry, plan_with_release) exactly as the plan specifies, confirm RED against the current buggy tag.rs. Then apply the plan's three implementation edits (import change, the sha-resolution logic replacing the unconditional push, and using the new `sha` binding in the final CreatedTag push) in order, confirm GREEN.\n\nBefore committing, run the full `cargo test -p callisto-graph` suite (0 failed required — this task edits tag.rs, a file with substantial existing test coverage, so regressions matter), `cargo fmt -p callisto-graph -- --check`, and `cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings`, and actually observe each command's real output. Commit with the plan's exact commit message when everything is clean. Single, self-contained task — do not start T4 or T5 (they build on this same test file but are separate tasks)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":884,"cache_read_input_tokens":460068,"output_tokens":1382,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":69},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":884,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1382,"cache_read_input_tokens":460068,"cache_creation_input_tokens":884,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":884},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standa