{"parentUuid":"da08b982-85f1-44fd-9d2f-0d32a1fac347","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeCoT2qQQKdqincevnAxn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019xVjK3Rv12rS9fK9iq8Wc8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix(graph): stop fabricating CreatedTag.sha in apply-mode tag creation\n\nTrack 4 (release-pipeline contract correctness) T3/10: create_tags_with_options's\napply path pushed release.sha unconditionally even when the per-release\ntag already existed at a different commit. Now resolves the tag's real\ntarget via GitDataSource::resolve_commit when it already exists, and\nfails fast (Err(GraphError::Vcs)) rather than fabricating a sha when\nresolution comes back empty or errors.\n\nFixes two sibling regressions surfaced by full-suite verification:\ntags_tests.rs's AlreadyTaggedTestRunner and CountingTagListRunner stub\nCommandRunners simulated an already-existing tag via `git tag --list`\nbut had no response for the new `git rev-parse --verify --quiet\n<tag>^{commit}` call resolve_commit now makes -- both now answer it\nwith the tag's simulated sha, matching their existing fixture intent.\nEOF\n)\"\ngit log --oneline -3","description":"Commit T3 with the sibling regression fix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":356,"cache_read_input_tokens":497747,"output_tokens":466,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":356,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":466,"cache_read_input_tokens":497747,"cache_creation_input_tokens":356,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":356},