{"parentUuid":"395f84fc-f6ed-4f6b-900b-2f9dcc982c36","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeD64aGc1C9t85eu1Zf7c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QmAcLcikh2y3hWGGRjgW72","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix StatusReport field mismatches","subagent_type":"lambda:implementer","prompt":"Workspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto (Rust cargo workspace, moon-managed). This is a Track 6-mechanical fix — lighter TDD loop tier (no formal spec/plan, this task IS the full scope), matching the established pattern in .claude/plans/ACTIVE.md for narrow, well-scoped correctness fixes. Do the work directly: red test → minimal fix → green → full suite → fmt → clippy → commit. Do not batch unrelated report types into this commit — this task is StatusReport/StatusPackageRecord ONLY.\n\nContext: an earlier research pass found StatusReport/StatusPackageRecord (crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs, roughly lines 298-336) has field-shape mismatches against the documented wire contract in docs/01-spec.md §M.12.4 area (search for \"StatusReport\" and \"StatusEntry\"/\"StatusPackageRecord\" in that doc). Reported findings (RE-VERIFY every one against live code and the live doc before acting — this research is from earlier in a long session and code may have drifted):\n1. `has_changesets: bool` — the doc mandates this field (used by the Action's mode dispatch), but the current struct is missing it entirely.\n2. The doc's package-record type is missing from the current struct: `last_released_version: Option<Version>` and `release_trigger: ReleaseTrigger` fields the doc documents but the code doesn't have.\n3. `changed_since_last_tag: bool` — doc says this is mandatory/always-serialized; current code has `#[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"std::ops::Not::not\")]`, which omits the field from JSON when false, contradicting \"always present.\"\n4. Code may have an extra field not in the doc: `pending_changesets: Vec<String>` — if so, this is presumably fine to keep (additive, not a doc violation) unless it's actually meant to be renamed/removed; use judgment, don't remove real data-carrying fields without strong evidence the doc explicitly says NOT to have it.\n5. Construction sites likely at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/status.rs and crates/callisto-cli/src/render/mod.rs — find and update all real (non-test) construction sites.\n\nIMPORTANT constraint from a resolved decision earlier this session: NO SCHEMA_VERSION bump for any of these fixes — this project has never done a real registry publish, so there's no external consumer to protect from a wire-format change yet. Just fix the struct/construction sites to be correct.\n\nProcess: 1) Read docs/01-spec.md's actual current StatusReport/StatusEntry documentation section in full. 2) Read report.rs's actual current StatusReport/StatusPackageRecord struct. 3) Diff them yourself, confirm or correct the findings above. 4) For each genuine mismatch, write a failing test first (either a unit test on the struct's serde behavior, or an integration test on `callisto status --format json`'s real output, whichever fits the existing test file conventions in this codebase — check crates/callisto-graph/tests/ and crates/callisto-cli/tests/ for precedent), confirm it fails, then fix it, confirm green. 5) Update every real construction site so the new/changed fields are actually populated with correct data, not just added as always-None/always-default placeholders — has_changesets should reflect whether any package has pending changesets, last_released_version/release_trigger should be populated from real data already available in the command's existing logic (check what data is already computed nearby).\n\nBefore committing: run the full `cargo test -p callisto-model` and `cargo test -p callisto-graph` and `cargo test -p callisto-cli` suites (this touches all three), `cargo fmt --check` on each touched crate, and `cargo clippy --all