{"parentUuid":"db99c129-21ac-4fc8-a79c-94f9207abc8d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeEN8ndESTCyk69EjXebz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015v16KWyJp7C7zp8818F8br","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix ValidateReport field rename","subagent_type":"lambda:implementer","prompt":"Workspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto (Rust cargo workspace, moon-managed). This is a Track 6-mechanical fix — lighter TDD loop tier (no formal spec/plan, this task IS the full scope). Do the work directly: red test → minimal fix → green → full suite → fmt → clippy → commit. Do not batch unrelated report types into this commit — this task is ValidateReport ONLY.\n\nContext: an earlier research pass found ValidateReport (crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs) has a field-name mismatch against the documented wire contract in docs/01-spec.md (search for \"ValidateReport\" — it's in the M.12.6 section alongside TagReport/InitReport). Reported findings (RE-VERIFY every one against live code and the live doc before acting):\n1. The doc documents the field as `ok: bool`; the current struct has `valid: bool` instead — a JSON key rename needed (camelCase: `ok` not `valid`).\n2. The doc says `diagnostics` is mandatory here specifically (\"validate's entire payload *is* its diagnostics\" — read the actual doc prose for the exact framing), but the current code has `#[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Vec::is_empty\")]` on it, which would omit the field when there are no diagnostics — contradicting \"always present.\"\n\nIMPORTANT constraint from a resolved decision earlier this session: NO SCHEMA_VERSION bump for any of these fixes — this project has never done a real registry publish, so there's no external consumer to protect from a wire-format change yet. Also note: Track 4 (already shipped, commit 926c2af4) added an AC-13 schema guard test at crates/callisto-cli/tests/schema_guard_test.rs that hardcodes expected field sets for tag/status/plan-publish schemas — this test does NOT currently check ValidateReport's schema at all, so it should not need updating for this task, but confirm that yourself by reading the test file.\n\nProcess: 1) Read docs/01-spec.md's actual current ValidateReport documentation in full (the M.12.6 section). 2) Read report.rs's actual current ValidateReport struct. 3) Diff them yourself, confirm or correct the findings above. 4) Find every real (non-test) construction site of ValidateReport (likely crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/validate.rs) and every real consumption site (grep for `.valid` field access anywhere in the workspace, including any render/output code in callisto-cli). 5) Write a failing test first proving the current `valid` key (wrong) vs expected `ok` key, and proving diagnostics is always serialized even when empty, confirm both fail, then rename the field and fix the serde attribute, confirm green. Update every real construction/consumption site to use the renamed field.\n\nBefore committing: run the full `cargo test -p callisto-model`, `cargo test -p callisto-graph`, and `cargo test -p callisto-cli` suites, `cargo fmt --check` on each touched crate, and `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` on each touched crate. If you find the doc and code disagree in a way that suggests the CODE might be the intended design (not the doc) — stop and report the contradiction rather than guessing. Commit with a clear conventional commit message when everything is clean and verified."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1414,"cache_read_input_tokens":612522,"output_tokens":1660,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":275},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1414,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"n