{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-20T17:24:08.230Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a3b55c5311841c59d</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_015v16KWyJp7C7zp8818F8br</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/08ccaac1-3846-4134-8b06-140e5b9c22f2/tasks/a3b55c5311841c59d.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Fix ValidateReport field rename\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Summary\n\nTDD cycle completed for the `ValidateReport` field-mismatch fix (Track 6-mechanical, scoped to ValidateReport only).\n\n**Verification of findings** (both confirmed against live doc/code):\n1. `docs/01-spec.md` M.12.6 documents `ok: bool`; code had `valid: bool` — confirmed and fixed.\n2. Doc explicitly states diagnostics is mandatory (\"validate's entire payload *is* its diagnostics\"); code had `#[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Vec::is_empty\")]` — confirmed and removed.\n3. `crates/callisto-cli/tests/schema_guard_test.rs` does not reference `ValidateReport` at all — confirmed, no change needed there.\n\n**Red phase**: Added `crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs:497-543` (`validate_report_tests` module) referencing a not-yet-existing `ok` field — compile failure confirmed the test was red before any implementation change.\n\n**Green phase**: Renamed `valid` → `ok` and removed the `skip_serializing_if` attribute at `crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs:477-486`. Updated every real (non-test) construction/consumption site:\n- `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/validate.rs:145` (construction)\n- `crates/callisto-cli/src/render/mod.rs:140` (consumption)\n- `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/validate.rs:30` (consumption/exit code)\n- `crates/callisto-moon/src/extension.rs:203` (consumption/exit code)\n- `crates/callisto-graph/tests/validate_command_tests.rs:203` (pre-existing test, updated to compile/pass)\n\n**Verification**: `cargo test -p callisto-model` (92 passed), `cargo test -p callisto-graph` (all passed), `cargo test -p callisto-cli` (all passed, e2e output confirmed `{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"ok\":true,\"diagnostics\":[]}`), `cargo fmt --check` clean on all four touched crates, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n**Commit**: `c277c561` — `fix(model): align ValidateReport wire shape with docs/01-spec.md M.12.6`\n\nNo schema_version bump, per the resolved constraint. No contradiction found — doc and intended code agreed; only the code was out of sync.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>77048</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>50</tool_uses><duration_ms>1076667</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
