 — this project has never done a real registry publish, so there's no external consumer to protect yet.\n\nIMPORTANT — if you find that `metadata`'s underlying data (which labels were applied, overflow state) is NOT actually computed anywhere in the current pr_body command logic, this is a scope question, not something to guess your way through: STOP and report back what's missing and what it would take, rather than either (a) fabricating placeholder/always-empty metadata that doesn't reflect reality, or (b) silently skipping the metadata field and only doing the rename. A partial, honest fix (rename only, metadata explicitly deferred with a clear reason) is fine and expected if the underlying data genuinely isn't there yet — this project has precedent this session for narrowing scope with an honest non_goals-style note rather than faking a field. Do not spend more than a reasonable investigation budget chasing this before reporting back.\n\nProcess: 1) Read docs/01-spec.md's actual current ComposePrBodyReport documentation in full, including PrBodyMetadata's exact fields. 2) Read report.rs's actual current ComposePrBodyReport struct. 3) Diff them yourself. 4) Find every real (non-test) construction/consumption site (likely crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs and consumption in callisto-cli). 5) Write failing tests first for whatever you determine is genuinely fixable, confirm red, then implement, confirm green.\n\nBefore committing: run the full `cargo test -p callisto-model`, `cargo test -p callisto-graph`, `cargo test -p callisto-cli`, and `cargo test -p callisto-moon` suites (callisto-moon may also consume this report — check), `cargo fmt --check` on each touched crate, and `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` on each touched crate. Commit with a clear conventional commit message when everything is clean and verified, or report back without committing if you hit the metadata-data-doesn't-exist scope question above."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":707,"cache_read_input_tokens":619273,"output_tokens":1506,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":75},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":707,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1506,"cache_read_input_tokens":619273,"cache_creation_input_tokens":707,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":707},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeEPvhXnmjRv2ynA9yg7c","type":"assistant","uuid":"2acdd7a2-3ada-4397-8ee3-0d7ecedbc8a0","timestamp":"2026-08-20T17:29:36.551Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
