{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-20T17:49:36.559Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>acfee8fec46cb2a22</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_019sAbGHGJMfh6hXohX5bv5f</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/08ccaac1-3846-4134-8b06-140e5b9c22f2/tasks/acfee8fec46cb2a22.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Fix ComposePrBodyReport field mismatches\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Task complete. Summary:\n\n**Findings (re-verified against live code and live doc):**\n1. `docs/01-spec.md` §M.12.5 documents `ComposePrBodyReport.body: String`; the struct at `crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs` had `pr_body: String` — a real wire-key mismatch (`prBody` vs `body`). Fixed via rename.\n2. The doc also documents `metadata: PrBodyMetadata` (labels / managed_labels / overflow). Investigated `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs` and all consumers (callisto-cli, callisto-moon — moon has no direct reference at all): only `labels` (\"labels callisto wants applied now\") has a real data source (`opts.labels`). `managed_labels` requires round-tripping previously-applied labels from the existing PR body — no such parsing exists anywhere. `overflow` requires detecting a body that exceeds GitHub's size limit and pushing to a notes branch — no size-limit/notes-branch logic exists anywhere in the codebase (confirmed via grep for \"overflow\", \"notes branch\", size-limit constants). Since 2 of 3 subfields have zero backing computation, I did not add the `metadata` field — that would require fabricating placeholder data for `managedLabels`/`overflow`. This is documented explicitly, not silently dropped, per the resolved-decision precedent for this session.\n\n**TDD cycle:**\n- Red: added `compose_pr_body_report_json_uses_body_key_not_pr_body` test in `crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs` (function at line 498, assertion at line 504) — confirmed failing via compile error (`E0560: no field named 'body'`) before any implementation change.\n- Green: renamed the field (`crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs:463`), updated all construction sites (`crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs`, two `Ok(ComposePrBodyReport{...})` sites) and all consumption sites (`crates/callisto-cli/src/render/mod.rs:167`, plus test assertions in `crates/callisto-cli/tests/lifecycle_e2e_tests.rs` and `crates/callisto-graph/tests/graph_tests.rs`).\n\n**Verification:** `cargo test` green on `callisto-model` (93 passed), `callisto-graph`, `callisto-cli`, and `callisto-moon` (built + tested, no direct field references). `cargo fmt --check` clean on all touched crates. `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean on `callisto-model`, `callisto-graph`, `callisto-cli`. No `SCHEMA_VERSION` bump, per the resolved constraint.\n\n**Commit:** `d6714eec` — `fix(model): rename ComposePrBodyReport.pr_body to body per spec`, scoped to exactly the 5 files touched by `ComposePrBodyReport` (no other report types included).\n\nNo blockers — the metadata gap is documented as an explicit deferral in both the struct's doc comment and the commit message, not a silent omission, matching the pre-authorized \"partial, honest fix\" outcome.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>85874</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>49</tool_uses><duration_ms>1195894</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
