{"parentUuid":"3891a55a-2d3e-4dbe-9c43-92f44e4e5506","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fd8061b6-67bb-4944-9bfe-d6fcd4b7c4ef","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rapn9U8qwA2B9gGM5KeiLf","type":"tool_result","content":"commit d6714eec52a46716a1c381cd6362769b64393b69\nAuthor: Gabe Castro <gabe@techworx.dev>\nDate:   Thu Aug 20 10:48:59 2026 -0700\n\n    fix(model): rename ComposePrBodyReport.pr_body to body per spec\n    \n    docs/01-spec.md §M.12.5 documents the composed PR body field as `body`,\n    serialized camelCase as \"body\" -- the struct instead had `pr_body`,\n    producing \"prBody\" on the wire. Renamed field and updated all\n    construction/consumption sites (callisto-graph::commands::pr_body,\n    callisto-cli::render, and their tests).\n    \n    The spec also documents a `metadata: PrBodyMetadata` field\n    (labels/managedLabels/overflow). That is intentionally NOT added here:\n    managedLabels requires round-tripping the previous run's applied\n    labels from the existing PR body, and overflow requires notes-branch\n    overflow detection -- neither is computed anywhere in the current\n    compose-pr-body command logic. Adding the field would mean fabricating\n    placeholder data, so it is left out of scope with an explicit note on\n    the struct and the covering test, rather than silently dropped.\n    \n    No SCHEMA_VERSION bump (no external registry consumer yet).\n    \n    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M0G4MQSD0ZHHE5KFB8439QE0\n\n crates/callisto-cli/src/render/mod.rs            |  2 +-\n crates/callisto-cli/tests/lifecycle_e2e_tests.rs | 10 +++---\n crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs    |  8 ++---\n crates/callisto-graph/tests/graph_tests.rs       |  2 +-\n crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs              | 44 +++++++++++++++++++++++-\n 5 files changed, 54 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a740dc3e-77ba-4fc3-970b-47f66974a55c","timestamp":"2026-08-20T17:49:48.616Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"commit d6714eec52a46716a1c381cd6362769b64393b69\nAuthor: Gabe Castro <gabe@techworx.dev>\nDate:   Thu Aug 20 10:48:59 2026 -0700\n\n    fix(model): rename ComposePrBodyReport.pr_body to body per spec\n    \n    docs/01-spec.md §M.12.5 documents the composed PR body field as `body`,\n    serialized camelCase as \"body\" -- the struct instead had `pr_body`,\n    producing \"prBody\" on the wire. Renamed field and updated all\n    construction/consumption sites (callisto-graph::commands::pr_body,\n    callisto-cli::render, and their tests).\n    \n    The spec also documents a `metadata: PrBodyMetadata` field\n    (labels/managedLabels/overflow). That is intentionally NOT added here:\n    managedLabels requires round-tripping the previous run's applied\n    labels from the existing PR body, and overflow requires notes-branch\n    overflow detection -- neither is computed anywhere in the current\n    compose-pr-body command logic. Adding the field would mean fabricating\n    placeholder data, so it is left out of scope with an explicit note on\n    the struct and the covering test, rather than silently dropped.\n    \n    No SCHEMA_VERSION bump (no external registry consumer yet).\n    \n    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M0G4MQSD0ZHHE5KFB8439QE0\n\n crates/callisto-cli/src/render/mod.rs            |  2 +-\n crates/callisto-cli/tests/lifecycle_e2e_tests.rs | 10 +++---\n crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs    |  8 ++---\n crates/callisto-graph/tests/graph_tests.rs       |  2 +-\n crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs              | 44 +++++++++++++++++++++++-\n 5 files changed, 54 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3891a55a-2d3e-4dbe-9c43-92f44e4e5506","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBran