{"parentUuid":"c61db0f2-3176-4a6c-a811-9a6e1dd08872","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeEVph4JDESLGnbXCJfhU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011VSn4QkfiCHUQ4UzyAVy6k","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\ngit add crates/callisto-cli/src/render/mod.rs crates/callisto-cli/tests/schema_guard_test.rs crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs crates/callisto-graph/tests/tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs crates/callisto-graph/tests/tags_tests.rs crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix(model): align TagReport/CreatedTag wire shape with docs/01-spec.md M.12.6\n\nRenames TagReport.created_tags to tags (JSON key \"tags\", not\n\"createdTags\") and adds CreatedTag.already_existed: bool -- true when\nthe tag already existed at this sha and was left alone, making Track\n4's idempotence fix (commits 5166d601/3bcc91e2) observable on the wire\nrather than only inferable from unchanged state.\n\nAll four CreatedTag construction sites in create_tags_with_options\n(the per-release tag and the floating-major alias, in both apply and\n--dry-run mode) already computed an `already_existed`/`major_already_existed`\nlocal via contains_tag() for their own sha-resolution logic -- this\njust threads that existing value into the struct instead of computing\nit a second time.\n\nUpdates Track 4's AC-13 schema guard baseline (crates/callisto-cli/\ntests/schema_guard_test.rs) to reflect this intentional shape change --\nthat guard's purpose is catching drift, and this is the task whose\nexplicit scope is changing CreatedTag's shape.\n\nThis closes out Track 6-mechanical's report-field-shape work: all four\nJSON report types with confirmed mismatches (StatusReport, ValidateReport,\nComposePrBodyReport, TagReport/CreatedTag) are now aligned with\ndocs/01-spec.md. No SCHEMA_VERSION bump (no external registry consumer\nyet).\nEOF\n)\"\ngit log --oneline -6","descri