{"parentUuid":"f8d40a13-9b1c-4d8a-a1e4-128bab60a3ef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeEWz6gyUHLjpHreHTp4d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`BumpReason::Inference` only tracks `commits: usize` (a count) — not per-commit sha/subject data that `ChangeSource::Commit` would need. This might be the same \"can't fabricate, data doesn't exist\" situation Track 6 hit with `ComposePrBodyReport`. Let me investigate before drafting the requirement, rather than assume."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1262,"cache_read_input_tokens":664805,"output_tokens":2179,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":485},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1262,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2179,"cache_read_input_tokens":664805,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1262,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1262},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeEWz3mbw4nvdyN6P1fJR","type":"assistant","uuid":"e1ac27fa-fb32-403f-94c3-e710484882e3","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:02:00.885Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"e1ac27fa-fb32-403f-94c3-e710484882e3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeEWz6gyUHLjpHreHTp4d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MRpji7Chgs4u1ZzC1QY3yw","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Investigate Track 5 data availability","subagent_type":"fork","prompt":"Research-only task (read-only, no edits). This grounds a canon requirement I'm about to draft for Track 5 (changelog/PR-body rendering consolidation, full canon pipeline per explicit user choice).\n\nThree components, investigate each for real data availability before I draft acceptance criteria:\n\n1. **pr_body.rs hand-rolled Markdown vs render_section.** Read crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs in full. Confirm it never calls `callisto_changelog::render_section` (or any function from callisto-changelog) and instead builds Markdown by hand. Read `callisto_changelog::render_section`'s full implementation (crates/callisto-changelog/src/render.rs) and `ChangelogInput`/`ChangelogEntry`/`ChangeSource` (crates/callisto-changelog/src/input.rs) to understand what render_section actually produces and what input shape it needs. Determine: does pr_body.rs currently have access to data shaped like ChangelogInput (per-package entries with severity+source), or does it work from a fundamentally different data source (e.g. raw ReleaseEntry/VersionReport data) that would need real transformation work to feed render_section? Is this a mechanical \"call the existing function instead\" fix, or does it require building a new data-marshaling layer?\n\n2. **ChangeSource::Commit's real data availability.** `BumpReason::Inference` (crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs, search \"enum BumpReason\") only carries `commits: usize` (a count) and `remapped: bool` -- no per-commit sha/subject. But `ChangeSource::Commit` (crates/callisto-changelog/src/input.rs) needs `sha: CommitSha, subject: String` for ONE commit (singular, not a list). Trace where inference-driven bumps are actually computed -- search for wherever `BumpReason::Inference` is constructed (likely in commit-severity-inference logic, check crates/callisto-graph/src/ for \"Inference\" and inference-related files) and determine: is real per-commit sha/subject data available at or near that computation site (even if it's currently being thrown away and only a count is kept), or would surfacing it require re-architecting the inference pipeline to track individual commits instead of just a count? If ChangeSource::Commit is meant to represent ONE representative commit when N commits contributed, is there evidence in the code/docs of which commit that should be (e.g. the most severe, the first, the last)?\n\n3. **ChangeSource::NewGroupMember's real data availability.** Trace where a \"new group member\" event is currently detected -- this session's Track 1 work (already shipped) added `pre_mutation_checks` divergence/napi-drift detection to groups.rs, which may be the relevant mechanism, or may be unrelated. Search crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs and crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs for anything related to detecting a package newly joining a fixed/linked group. Is `group: GroupName` (the only field ChangeSource::NewGroupMember needs) available wherever this detection happens?\n\n4. **ChangelogInput.entries union bug.** Find where `ChangelogInput`/`ChangelogEntry` values are actually constructed for a real `callisto version` run (likely in commands/version.rs, search for \"ChangelogInput\" or \"changelog_inputs\"). Confirm whether, when one package has multiple real contributing causes in one run (e.g. both a changeset AND a cascade-driven bump), only one ChangelogEntry ends up in the Vec (data loss) versus multiple entries being unioned. Read the actual construction logic and characterize precisely what happens today -- is it \"last write wins\", \"first write wins\", \"changeset always wins over other sources\", or something else? Cite exact file:line.\n\nReport back per component: confirmed/refuted, with exact file:line evidence, and for each of the two \"is the data available\" questions (Commit, NewGroupMember), a clear verdict on whether the fix is \"real data already exists, just needs wiring\" or \"data doesn't exist yet, would require new tracking/architecture work\" -- this determines whether Track 5's spec can require full ChangeSource::Commit construction or must scope it down/defer it, mirroring the ComposePrBodyReport precedent from earlier this session where 2 of 3 documented subfields had zero backing computation and were explicitly deferred rather than fabricated."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1262,"cache_read_input_tokens":664805,"output_tokens":2179,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":485},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1262,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2179,"cache_read_input_tokens":664805,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1262,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1262},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeEWz3mbw4nvdyN6P1fJR","type":"assistant","uuid":"e5c9b346-8c89-4fc4-b27c-877d54fc61b0","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:02:16.707Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
