{"parentUuid":"b0f944b8-ba7c-448b-b8a6-ae79127ed1e9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeEX8ciULtkZ5g5XEcZQh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three \"missing\" pieces have real backing data — no fabrication needed anywhere, unlike `ComposePrBodyReport`. Drafting the canon requirement now."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2550,"cache_read_input_tokens":668662,"output_tokens":4856,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1325},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2550,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4856,"cache_read_input_tokens":668662,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2550,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2550},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeEX8ZAuGwp9sKtj9EQKz","type":"assistant","uuid":"c0637872-2254-4f56-aec0-b79983d4c829","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:04:06.014Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"c0637872-2254-4f56-aec0-b79983d4c829","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeEX8ciULtkZ5g5XEcZQh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WR9iLGY1VvgQEWm36XfWVL","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Draft Track 5 canon spec","subagent_type":"canon:drafter","prompt":"IMPORTANT: You are the canon:drafter agent. Do the spec-drafting work YOURSELF, directly, in this single invocation. Do NOT delegate or dispatch to another agent — you ARE the drafter. Verify every cited file:line against live code yourself using Read/Grep, then return the complete spec@1 JSON object as your final text output.\n\nWorkspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto. Draft a spec@1 for \"Track 5: Changelog/PR-body Rendering Consolidation\" from this requirement@1.\n\nrequirement@1:\n{\n  \"id\": \"REQ-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION\",\n  \"statement\": \"Make callisto's changelog and PR-body rendering accurately reflect every real cause of a version bump, and consolidate PR-body composition to reuse the shared changelog renderer instead of hand-rolling its own Markdown -- closing four confirmed gaps where either the rendering logic is duplicated, or real underlying cause data is computed and then discarded before it reaches the reader.\",\n  \"stakeholder\": \"Anyone reading a callisto-generated CHANGELOG.md entry or release-PR body to understand why a package's version changed\",\n  \"why\": \"All four gaps were confirmed live this session via direct code reading (not assumed from stale docs). Three of the four have real backing data sitting one hop away from where it's silently discarded -- this is a wiring gap, not missing functionality requiring new architecture.\",\n  \"done_when\": [\n    \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs stops hand-building its own Markdown structure and instead calls callisto_changelog::render_section (crates/callisto-changelog/src/render.rs:5) to render each bumped package's changelog section, reusing the BumpReason-to-ChangeSource mapping logic that already exists at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:157-195 rather than duplicating it -- confirmed live: pr_body.rs (322 lines) currently has zero imports from callisto_changelog and hand-matches BumpReason inline at roughly lines 104-123 and 185-225 to build a summary table plus collapsible-details Markdown structure. This is real integration work (marshaling VersionPlan.bumps data into ChangelogInput per package, embedding each rendered section inside pr_body.rs's existing table/details wrapper), not a one-line swap -- scope it accordingly.\",\n    \"ChangeSource::Commit (crates/callisto-changelog/src/input.rs, fields: sha: CommitSha, subject: String) is actually constructed for inference-driven bumps, using real per-commit data. Confirmed live: InferenceOutcome (crates/callisto-graph/src/infer.rs:29-34) already carries commits: Vec<(CommitSha, String)> -- full per-commit sha+subject -- but at BumpReason::Inference's only construction site (crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs:224-229), only outcome.commit_count (a usize) is kept; outcome.commits is computed and discarded on the spot, never stored. Since ChangeSource::Commit takes exactly ONE commit (not a list) but N commits may have contributed, the implementer must pick a single representative commit and apply that choice consistently -- verify InferenceOutcome.commits' actual natural ordering (chronological ascending or descending, or another order) against live code before deciding whether 'first' or 'last' in the Vec is the more recent/most-representative commit, and document the choice in a code comment since no existing precedent establishes it.\",\n    \"ChangeSource::NewGroupMember (crates/callisto-changelog/src/input.rs, field: group: GroupName) is actually constructed when a package newly joins a fixed/linked group. Confirmed live: GroupCheckOutcome.new_members: BTreeMap<GroupName, Vec<PackageId>> (crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:14,85) is already computed in plan_version as group_check (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:87-93) -- but only group_check.diagnostics is ever read (line 219); group_check.new_members is computed and never consumed anywhere in the function.\",\n    \"When a package's bump in one callisto version run has both a changeset-sourced cause AND a genuine non-changeset cause (cascade, peer-escalation, or group-union) recorded in outcome.reasons for the same package, ChangelogInput.entries for that package contains BOTH corresponding ChangelogEntry values, not just the changeset-sourced one. Confirmed live at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:148-154: the changeset-sourced branch (`if let Some(mut agg_input) = agg.changelog_inputs.get(id).cloned()`) is a hard if/else against the non-changeset synthesis branch (lines 156-195) -- when a changeset entry exists, the synthesis branch never runs at all, silently dropping any real non-changeset cause for the same package in the same run. Fix scope: append a second synthesized ChangelogEntry to agg_input.entries when both a changeset-sourced entry AND a genuine outcome.reasons value exist for the same package -- outcome.reasons remains readable inside the changeset branch since it's a separate map from agg.changelog_inputs.\",\n    \"is_error_case: true -- when a package's bump has no changeset AND no synthesizable reason in outcome.reasons (e.g. a bump whose cause genuinely can't be attributed), ChangelogInput.entries for that package must not panic, error the whole command, or silently omit the package from the changelog entirely -- the existing fallback behavior for this case (verify what it currently is) must be preserved.\",\n    \"is_error_case: true -- render_section (already implemented) returns Err(ChangelogError::EmptyInput) when given a ChangelogInput with zero entries; pr_body.rs's new integration with render_section must handle this without crashing the whole PR-body composition for one package's empty-entries edge case (verify whether this case is actually reachable given done_when's other criteria, and handle it gracefully either way).\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"A FULL multi-cause union covering more than one non-changeset reason per package (e.g. two independent cascade paths, or a cascade plus a peer-escalation, both non-changeset, contributing to the same package in the same run) -- outcome.reasons/agg.reasons are single-valued (BTreeMap<PackageId, BumpReason>, not BTreeMap<PackageId, Vec<BumpReason>>) all the way up through cascade.rs's severity/reason bookkeeping. Fixing this fully would require changing that data model throughout cascade.rs -- a genuinely separate, larger track. This spec's scope is exactly the changeset-plus-one-other-reason case, which is confirmed to already be fixable without touching the single-valued reasons maps.\",\n    \"Any change to callisto_changelog::render_section's own rendering logic, grouping, or output format -- it is already implemented and correct; this track only changes what calls it and what data it's fed.\",\n    \"Any change to how CHANGELOG.md itself is written to disk (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs) -- untouched, already correct.\",\n    \"Choosing which single commit is 'representative' when multiple commits drove an inference-based bump is a real design decision this spec authorizes the implementer to make (with the ordering-verification requirement above) -- it does not mandate a specific commit-selection algorithm beyond 'pick one consistently and document why'.\",\n    \"Any change to inference's own severity-computation logic, or to when inference fires at all -- only what data survives from InferenceOutcome to ChangeSource::Commit is in scope.\"\n  ]\n}\n\nAlso verify directly against live code (do not trust the requirement's citations blindly -- re-confirm each, since even this investigation happened minutes ago and this session has precedent for drift between investigation and drafting):\n- crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs (full file)\n- crates/callisto-changelog/src/render.rs (render_section, full function)\n- crates/callisto-changelog/src/input.rs (ChangelogInput, ChangelogEntry, ChangeSource -- full enum)\n- crates/callisto-graph/src/infer.rs (InferenceOutcome, lines ~29-34 and wherever it's constructed)\n- crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs (BumpReason::Inference construction, ~lines 224-229)\n- crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs (GroupCheckOutcome.new_members, ~lines 14, 85)\n- crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs (group_check construction ~87-93, its diagnostics-only consumption ~219, the changelog_inputs if/else ~148-195)\n- crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs (BumpReason enum, all variants -- to see exactly what data each variant carries, for accurately mapping to ChangeSource in the pr_body.rs integration)\n\nThis project's rigor precedent (see .claude/plans/ACTIVE.md, especially the Track 4 and Track 9 entries): acceptance criteria must be falsifiable observable-behavior propositions, no internal-implementation-knowledge-only criteria (each should be verifiable via a test that constructs a real scenario and checks real output), error cases carry is_error_case: true, no TBDs anywhere. This spec is entering the SAME full canon->vector->lambda pipeline that took Track 4 five exit-gate rounds and Track 9 three rounds -- write acceptance criteria precisely enough to survive that level of adversarial scrutiny the first time: cite exact types, exact field names, exact file:line, and state exactly how each criterion would be tested (unit test on the render/mapping function directly, or integration test through the real `callisto version`/`callisto compose-pr-body` command against an on-disk fixture)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2550,"cache_read_input_tokens":668662,"output_tokens":4856,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1325},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2550,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4856,"cache_read_input_tokens":668662,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2550,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2550},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeEX8ZAuGwp9sKtj9EQKz","type":"assistant","uuid":"29d65fbf-06e9-444b-8006-222d509451de","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:04:38.307Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"29d65fbf-06e9-444b-8006-222d509451de","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"03524286-9ace-407b-a119-62766f323323","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WR9iLGY1VvgQEWm36XfWVL","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a59eaa49606c1572c (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a59eaa49606c1572c', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/08ccaac1-3846-4134-8b06-140e5b9c22f2/tasks/a59eaa49606c1572c.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"b13294e6-97d5-4d00-9741-b15898854e6b","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:04:44.371Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a59eaa49606c1572c","description":"Draft Track 5 canon spec","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt":"IMPORTANT: You are the canon:drafter agent. Do the spec-drafting work YOURSELF, directly, in this single invocation. Do NOT delegate or dispatch to another agent — you ARE the drafter. Verify every cited file:line against live code yourself using Read/Grep, then return the complete spec@1 JSON object as your final text output.\n\nWorkspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto. Draft a spec@1 for \"Track 5: Changelog/PR-body Rendering Consolidation\" from this requirement@1.\n\nrequirement@1:\n{\n  \"id\": \"REQ-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION\",\n  \"statement\": \"Make callisto's changelog and PR-body rendering accurately reflect every real cause of a version bump, and consolidate PR-body composition to reuse the shared changelog renderer instead of hand-rolling its own Markdown -- closing four confirmed gaps where either the rendering logic is duplicated, or real underlying cause data is computed and then discarded before it reaches the reader.\",\n  \"stakeholder\": \"Anyone reading a callisto-generated CHANGELOG.md entry or release-PR body to understand why a package's version changed\",\n  \"why\": \"All four gaps were confirmed live this session via direct code reading (not assumed from stale docs). Three of the four have real backing data sitting one hop away from where it's silently discarded -- this is a wiring gap, not missing functionality requiring new architecture.\",\n  \"done_when\": [\n    \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs stops hand-building its own Markdown structure and instead calls callisto_changelog::render_section (crates/callisto-changelog/src/render.rs:5) to render each bumped package's changelog section, reusing the BumpReason-to-ChangeSource mapping logic that already exists at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:157-195 rather than duplicating it -- confirmed live: pr_body.rs (322 lines) currently has zero imports from callisto_changelog and hand-matches BumpReason inline at roughly lines 104-123 and 185-225 to build a summary table plus collapsible-details Markdown structure. This is real integration work (marshaling VersionPlan.bumps data into ChangelogInput per package, embedding each rendered section inside pr_body.rs's existing table/details wrapper), not a one-line swap -- scope it accordingly.\",\n    \"ChangeSource::Commit (crates/callisto-changelog/src/input.rs, fields: sha: CommitSha, subject: String) is actually constructed for inference-driven bumps, using real per-commit data. Confirmed live: InferenceOutcome (crates/callisto-graph/src/infer.rs:29-34) already carries commits: Vec<(CommitSha, String)> -- full per-commit sha+subject -- but at BumpReason::Inference's only construction site (crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs:224-229), only outcome.commit_count (a usize) is kept; outcome.commits is computed and discarded on the spot, never stored. Since ChangeSource::Commit takes exactly ONE commit (not a list) but N commits may have contributed, the implementer must pick a single representative commit and apply that choice consistently -- verify InferenceOutcome.commits' actual natural ordering (chronological ascending or descending, or another order) against live code before deciding whether 'first' or 'last' in the Vec is the more recent/most-representative commit, and document the choice in a code comment since no existing precedent establishes it.\",\n    \"ChangeSource::NewGroupMember (crates/callisto-changelog/src/input.rs, field: group: GroupName) is actually constructed when a package newly joins a fixed/linked group. Confirmed live: GroupCheckOutcome.new_members: BTreeMap<GroupName, Vec<PackageId>> (crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:14,85) is already computed in plan_version as group_check (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:87-93) -- but only group_check.diagnostics is ever read (line 219); group_check.new_members is computed and never consumed anywhere in the function.\",\n    \"When a package's bump in one callisto version run has both a changeset-sourced cause AND a genuine non-changeset cause (cascade, peer-escalation, or group-union) recorded in outcome.reasons for the same package, ChangelogInput.entries for that package contains BOTH corresponding ChangelogEntry values, not just the changeset-sourced one. Confirmed live at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:148-154: the changeset-sourced branch (`if let Some(mut agg_input) = agg.changelog_inputs.get(id).cloned()`) is a hard if/else against the non-changeset synthesis branch (lines 156-195) -- when a changeset entry exists, the synthesis branch never runs at all, silently dropping any real non-changeset cause for the same package in the same run. Fix scope: append a second synthesized ChangelogEntry to agg_input.entries when both a changeset-sourced entry AND a genuine outcome.reasons value exist for the same package -- outcome.reasons remains readable inside the changeset branch since it's a separate map from agg.changelog_inputs.\",\n    \"is_error_case: true -- when a package's bump has no changeset AND no synthesizable reason in outcome.reasons (e.g. a bump whose cause genuinely can't be attributed), ChangelogInput.entries for that package must not panic, error the whole command, or silently omit the package from the changelog entirely -- the existing fallback behavior for this case (verify what it currently is) must be preserved.\",\n    \"is_error_case: true -- render_section (already implemented) returns Err(ChangelogError::EmptyInput) when given a ChangelogInput with zero entries; pr_body.rs's new integration with render_section must handle this without crashing the whole PR-body composition for one package's empty-entries edge case (verify whether this case is actually reachable given done_when's other criteria, and handle it gracefully either way).\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"A FULL multi-cause union covering more than one non-changeset reason per package (e.g. two independent cascade paths, or a cascade plus a peer-escalation, both non-changeset, contributing to the same package in the same run) -- outcome.reasons/agg.reasons are single-valued (BTreeMap<PackageId, BumpReason>, not BTreeMap<PackageId, Vec<BumpReason>>) all the way up through cascade.rs's severity/reason bookkeeping. Fixing this fully would require changing that data model throughout cascade.rs -- a genuinely separate, larger track. This spec's scope is exactly the changeset-plus-one-other-reason case, which is confirmed to already be fixable without touching the single-valued reasons maps.\",\n    \"Any change to callisto_changelog::render_section's own rendering logic, grouping, or output format -- it is already implemented and correct; this track only changes what calls it and what data it's fed.\",\n    \"Any change to how CHANGELOG.md itself is written to disk (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs) -- untouched, already correct.\",\n    \"Choosing which single commit is 'representative' when multiple commits drove an inference-based bump is a real design decision this spec authorizes the implementer to make (with the ordering-verification requirement above) -- it does not mandate a specific commit-selection algorithm beyond 'pick one consistently and document why'.\",\n    \"Any change to inference's own severity-computation logic, or to when inference fires at all -- only what data survives from InferenceOutcome to ChangeSource::Commit is in scope.\"\n  ]\n}\n\nAlso verify directly against live code (do not trust the requirement's citations blindly -- re-confirm each, since even this investigation happened minutes ago and this session has precedent for drift between investigation and drafting):\n- crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs (full file)\n- crates/callisto-changelog/src/render.rs (render_section, full function)\n- crates/callisto-changelog/src/input.rs (ChangelogInput, ChangelogEntry, ChangeSource -- full enum)\n- crates/callisto-graph/src/infer.rs (InferenceOutcome, lines ~29-34 and wherever it's constructed)\n- crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs (BumpReason::Inference construction, ~lines 224-229)\n- crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs (GroupCheckOutcome.new_members, ~lines 14, 85)\n- crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs (group_check construction ~87-93, its diagnostics-only consumption ~219, the changelog_inputs if/else ~148-195)\n- crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs (BumpReason enum, all variants -- to see exactly what data each variant carries, for accurately mapping to ChangeSource in the pr_body.rs integration)\n\nThis project's rigor precedent (see .claude/plans/ACTIVE.md, especially the Track 4 and Track 9 entries): acceptance criteria must be falsifiable observable-behavior propositions, no internal-implementation-knowledge-only criteria (each should be verifiable via a test that constructs a real scenario and checks real output), error cases carry is_error_case: true, no TBDs anywhere. This spec is entering the SAME full canon->vector->lambda pipeline that took Track 4 five exit-gate rounds and Track 9 three rounds -- write acceptance criteria precisely enough to survive that level of adversarial scrutiny the first time: cite exact types, exact field names, exact file:line, and state exactly how each criterion would be tested (unit test on the render/mapping function directly, or integration test through the real `callisto version`/`callisto compose-pr-body` command against an on-disk fixture).","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/08ccaac1-3846-4134-8b06-140e5b9c22f2/tasks/a59eaa49606c1572c.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"29d65fbf-06e9-444b-8006-222d509451de","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
