{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:08:23.663Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a59eaa49606c1572c</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01WR9iLGY1VvgQEWm36XfWVL</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/08ccaac1-3846-4134-8b06-140e5b9c22f2/tasks/a59eaa49606c1572c.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Draft Track 5 canon spec\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I have enough grounding now. Producing the spec@1.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Make callisto's changelog and PR-body rendering accurately reflect every real cause of a version bump, by (1) making crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs reuse callisto_changelog::render_section and the already-built ChangelogInput data in VersionPlan.changelog_writes instead of hand-rolling its own Markdown from BumpReason, and (2) wiring three confirmed pieces of real, already-computed cause data -- InferenceOutcome.commits, GroupCheckOutcome.new_members, and a package's non-changeset outcome.reasons entry that co-occurs with a changeset entry -- through to ChangelogInput.entries instead of letting them be silently discarded.\",\n  \"scope\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs (Release Reason collapsible-details rendering only, not the Executive Summary table); crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs (BumpReason::Inference construction site, ~lines 223-236); crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs (the changelog_inputs if/else at ~lines 148-215, and group_check consumption at ~line 219); crates/callisto-changelog/src/input.rs is read but not modified (ChangeSource variants already exist and are sufficient). No change to callisto_changelog::render_section, callisto-changelog/src/write.rs, or inference's own severity computation.\",\n  \"non_goals\": [\n    \"A full multi-cause union covering more than one non-changeset reason per package in the same run (e.g. two independent cascades, or a cascade plus a peer-escalation, both non-changeset, for the same package). outcome.reasons and agg.reasons are BTreeMap&lt;PackageId, BumpReason&gt; (single-valued), not BTreeMap&lt;PackageId, Vec&lt;BumpReason&gt;&gt;, all the way through cascade.rs's severity/reason bookkeeping. This spec's scope is exactly changeset-plus-one-other-reason; a full N-reason union requires changing that data model throughout cascade.rs and is a separate, larger track.\",\n    \"Any change to callisto_changelog::render_section's rendering logic, grouping, section ordering, or Markdown output format -- it is already implemented and correct; this track only changes what calls it and what ChangelogInput data it is fed.\",\n    \"Any change to how CHANGELOG.md is written to disk (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs) -- untouched.\",\n    \"Any change to inference's own severity-computation logic, or to when inference fires at all -- only what data survives from InferenceOutcome to the resulting ChangeSource is in scope.\",\n    \"The exact Rust data-modeling mechanism used to carry a representative (CommitSha, String) pair from InferenceOutcome through to ChangeSource::Commit (e.g. a new field on BumpReason::Inference vs. a side-channel map in AggregateOutcome) is left to the implementer -- this spec constrains only the observable output (which commit's sha/subject appears in the rendered changelog entry), not the internal storage shape.\",\n    \"pr_body.rs's Executive Summary table (### Release Summary, the `| Package | Ecosystem | ... | Reason |` table built at pr_body.rs:82-136) is unchanged by this track. Its one-line `reason_str` per bump is a compact table-cell label, not a rendered changelog section, and render_section has no one-line output mode -- consolidating that table is out of scope; only the collapsible '#### Release Reason' block inside each package's `&lt;details&gt;` (pr_body.rs:175-218) is replaced with reused ChangelogInput + render_section output.\",\n    \"Constructing BumpReason::NewGroupMember (or any new BumpReason variant) is not required by this spec -- the NewGroupMember gap can be closed by directly constructing ChangeSource::NewGroupMember in version.rs's changelog-entry synthesis without necessarily threading a corresponding BumpReason through outcome.reasons; the implementer may choose either path as long as AC-004's observable behavior holds.\"\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-001\",\n      \"criterion\": \"For every bump in VersionPlan.bumps whose package has a matching entry `w` in VersionPlan.changelog_writes (i.e. some `w` where `w.input.package == bump.package`), the '#### Release Reason' block inside that package's `&lt;details&gt;` element in ComposePrBodyReport.body contains, verbatim, the exact string returned by `callisto_changelog::render_section(&amp;w.input)` (including render_section's own '## &lt;version&gt;' or '## Unreleased' heading line) -- not a hand-matched reconstruction. After this change, crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs contains no `match` arm on `BumpReason::Cascade`, `BumpReason::PeerEscalation`, `BumpReason::FixedGroupUnion`, or `BumpReason::LinkedGroupUnion` that independently builds descriptive Markdown text (the block previously at pr_body.rs:184-216 is deleted, not duplicated) -- verified by `grep -c 'BumpReason::Cascade\\\\|BumpReason::PeerEscalation\\\\|BumpReason::FixedGroupUnion\\\\|BumpReason::LinkedGroupUnion' crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs` returning 0. Test method: a new unit test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs's `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` constructs a VersionPlan with one PlannedBump and one matching ChangelogWrite (built the same way version.rs builds it, with a real ChangeSource::Changeset entry), calls `render_pr_body_from_plan`, independently calls `callisto_changelog::render_section` on the same ChangelogInput in the test body, and asserts `report.body.contains(&amp;expected_section)` where `expected_section` is that independently-computed render_section output.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-002\",\n      \"criterion\": \"For a bump whose package has no entry in VersionPlan.changelog_writes (the package declares no changelog file, i.e. `pkg.changelog` is `None` in the versioning pipeline, so version.rs's changelog-write loop at ~lines 148-215 never runs for it), that package's `&lt;details&gt;` block in ComposePrBodyReport.body still contains a non-empty '#### Release Reason' section (the pre-existing per-BumpReason descriptive text is preserved for this case) -- render_pr_body_from_plan does not error, panic, or emit an empty '#### Release Reason' heading with no following text for such a package. Test method: unit test in pr_body.rs constructing a VersionPlan with one PlannedBump whose `reason` is `Some(BumpReason::Cascade{..})` and an empty `changelog_writes` Vec (simulating no changelog file for that package); assert `render_pr_body_from_plan` returns `Ok` and `report.body` contains '#### Release Reason' followed by non-whitespace content before the next `&lt;/details&gt;`.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-003\",\n      \"criterion\": \"When a package's bump in a `plan_version` run is driven by `BumpReason::Inference` (i.e. `outcome.reasons.get(id) == Some(BumpReason::Inference{..})`) and the `InferenceOutcome` returned by the `SeverityInference` implementation for that package has a non-empty `commits: Vec&lt;(CommitSha, String)&gt;`, the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package in the resulting `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains a `ChangeSource::Commit { sha, subject }` entry where `sha` and `subject` equal `commits[0]`'s `CommitSha` and `String` respectively -- `commits[0]` because `callisto-vcs`'s `commits_since` (crates/callisto-vcs/src/shell.rs:141-174, and the native gix path it documents itself as matching field-for-field) shells `git log --no-merges` without a reversing flag, which is git's default newest-first order, so index 0 is the most recent commit. This choice is documented with a code comment at the construction site explaining why index 0 (not the last index) was chosen. Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module supplies a fake `SeverityInference` impl whose `infer()` returns `Ok(Some(InferenceOutcome { severity: Severity::Minor, commit_count: 2, remapped: false, commits: vec![(sha_recent, \\\"feat: recent\\\".into()), (sha_older, \\\"fix: older\\\".into())] }))` for a fixture package with no pending changeset, calls `plan_version`, and asserts the resulting `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package contains a `ChangeSource::Commit` entry with `sha == sha_recent` and `subject == \\\"feat: recent\\\"` (not `sha_older`).\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-004\",\n      \"criterion\": \"When a package ID appears in `GroupCheckOutcome.new_members`'s `Vec&lt;PackageId&gt;` for some `GroupName` key (computed by `pre_mutation_checks` at crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:85, exposed to `plan_version` as `group_check.new_members` at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:87-93) AND that package has a bump this run (i.e. `outcome.severities.get(id)` is `Some(sev)` with `sev != Severity::None`), the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package in `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains a `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group }` entry where `group` equals that `GroupName` key. Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module constructs a fixture workspace with a fixed group containing one already-released member and one fresh (never-tagged) member, drives a bump for the fresh member (e.g. via a changeset or the group's fixed-union bump), calls `plan_version`, and asserts the fresh member's `ChangelogInput.entries` contains `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group: &lt;the fixed group's GroupName&gt; }`.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-005\",\n      \"criterion\": \"When a package `id` with a bump this run has BOTH a changeset-sourced entry (`agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)` is `Some`) AND a genuine non-changeset reason recorded for the same run (`outcome.reasons.get(id)` is `Some(reason)` where `reason` is one of `Cascade`, `PeerEscalation`, `FixedGroupUnion`, or `LinkedGroupUnion` -- the variants version.rs's synthesis branch already maps to a `ChangeSource` at ~lines 158-187), the resulting `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package contains: (a) every entry from `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)`'s `entries`, verbatim and in original order, followed by (b) exactly one additional `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is the `ChangeSource` variant that version.rs's existing mapping (lines 158-187) produces for `reason`, with `severity` equal to the package's resolved bump `severity` for this run. Total `entries.len()` equals the changeset-only entry count plus 1. Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module constructs a fixture where a package has one pending changeset AND is also a cascade target this run (both `agg.changelog_inputs` and `outcome.reasons` populated for the same package ID), calls `plan_version`, and asserts `changelog_writes` for that package has `entries.len() == 2`, with the first entry's `source` matching `ChangeSource::Changeset{..}` and the second matching `ChangeSource::DependencyUpdate{..}` (the mapping for `BumpReason::Cascade`).\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-006\",\n      \"criterion\": \"When a package has a bump this run (severity &gt; None), `pkg.changelog` is `Some`, `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)` is `None` (no changeset), AND `outcome.reasons.get(id)` is either `None` or a variant with no direct `ChangeSource` mapping (falls to the catch-all currently at version.rs:188-199), `plan_version` does not panic and does not return `Err` attributable to this condition -- `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains exactly one `ChangelogWrite` for that package whose `input.entries.len() &gt;= 1`, preserving the existing fallback: a single `ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: String::new(), summary: format!(\\\"Version bump ({})\\\", &lt;severity as major|minor|patch|none&gt;) }` entry. Test method: integration test in version.rs's test module constructs a fixture package with a bump whose `reason` is `None` and no pending changeset, calls `plan_version`, asserts it returns `Ok`, and asserts the package's `ChangelogWrite.input.entries` has exactly 1 entry matching `ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: \\\"\\\", summary }` where `summary` starts with `\\\"Version bump (\\\"`.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-007\",\n      \"criterion\": \"render_pr_body_from_plan's call to `callisto_changelog::render_section` for a given package never causes the overall `compose_pr_body`/`render_pr_body_from_plan` call to panic or return `Err` because that one package's `ChangelogInput.entries` was empty (which would make `render_section` return `Err(ChangelogError::EmptyInput)`) -- on such an error for one package, that package's `&lt;details&gt;` block still renders (falling back to the AC-002 pre-existing per-BumpReason text, or if no `reason` is available either, a literal fallback line `_No changelog entries available._`) and every other package's block in the same PR body renders normally and completely. Note: this scenario is confirmed unreachable through the normal `plan_version` -&gt; `pr_body` pipeline as of AC-006 (changelog_writes entries are never empty), so this criterion is tested by calling `render_pr_body_from_plan`'s per-package rendering path directly with a hand-constructed `VersionPlan` whose matching `ChangelogWrite.input.entries` is an empty `Vec` (bypassing `plan_version`), and asserting the call returns `Ok` with a body containing both the fallback text for that package and the normally-rendered block for a second, unaffected package in the same plan.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    }\n  ],\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"All four requirement gaps were re-confirmed live against current code (not trusted from the requirement's citations): pr_body.rs (322 lines, verified full read) has zero callisto_changelog imports and hand-matches BumpReason at lines 99-124 (summary table, deliberately left out of scope -- render_section has no one-line mode) and 175-218 (Release Reason block, the actual AC-001 target). Crucially, I found VersionPlan.changelog_writes (plan.rs:19, populated at version.rs:148-215) ALREADY carries a fully-built ChangelogInput per package via the exact BumpReason-to-ChangeSource mapping the requirement wants reused -- so pr_body.rs's real fix is simpler than 'marshal VersionPlan.bumps into ChangelogInput': it's 'look up the already-built ChangelogWrite by package and call render_section on it', for packages where one exists (AC-001), with the pre-existing fallback preserved for packages with no changelog file (AC-002, not covered by the requirement's done_when but necessary since pkg.changelog can be None for a bumped package). InferenceOutcome.commits ordering was resolved by reading callisto-vcs/src/shell.rs:141-174's doc comment and args ('git log --no-merges', no reversing flag) -- git's default is newest-first, so index 0 is most recent; the native gix path is documented as matching the shell path field-for-field. GroupCheckOutcome.new_members (groups.rs:13-14, populated at line 85) is confirmed never consumed beyond diagnostics at version.rs:219; BumpReason::NewGroupMember is confirmed constructed nowhere in the graph crate (only matched defensively in pr_body.rs), so AC-004 is scoped to observable ChangeSource output rather than mandating a BumpReason variant be populated, since the implementer could wire ChangeSource::NewGroupMember directly from group_check.new_members without touching BumpReason at all -- left as an implementation choice in non_goals. The dual-cause union (AC-005) is confirmed as a hard if/else at version.rs:148-154; verified agg.reasons/outcome.reasons remain a separate, still-readable map inside the changeset branch, so appending a second entry is mechanically straightforward without touching the single-valued reasons maps (out of scope per requirement). AC-006/AC-007 error cases were scoped by tracing the actual current fallback code (the `_ =&gt;` catch-all at version.rs:188-199) to state precisely what 'preserved' means rather than leaving it vague.\"\n}\n```\n\nSummary of files verified directly against live code (all citations above are re-confirmed, not trusted from the requirement):\n\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs` (full 322-line file read)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-changelog/src/render.rs` (full `render_section`)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-changelog/src/input.rs` (full `ChangelogInput`/`ChangelogEntry`/`ChangeSource`)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/infer.rs` (full `InferenceOutcome`/construction)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs:190-249` (`BumpReason::Inference` construction, confirmed `outcome.commits` discarded)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs` (full file — `GroupCheckOutcome.new_members` at lines 13-14, populated line 85)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:1-260` (`group_check` construction ~87-93, diagnostics-only consumption ~219, the `changelog_inputs` if/else ~148-215, and the discovery that `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` already carries built `ChangelogInput`s)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs:253-286` (full `BumpReason` enum)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs:454-513` (`ComposePrBodyReport`)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/plan.rs:14-62` (`VersionPlan`, `PlannedBump`, `ChangelogWrite` — confirms the reuse path)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-vcs/src/shell.rs:127-174` and `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-vcs/src/access.rs:88-99` (commit ordering evidence for AC-003)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-conventional/src/infer.rs`, `window.rs` (commit fetch pipeline, no reordering)\n\nNote one correction to the requirement's own framing, called out in `reasoning`: `pr_body.rs`'s real integration point is reusing the already-built `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` (populated by `version.rs`'s existing mapping), not re-deriving `ChangelogInput` from `VersionPlan.bumps` — this is a simpler, more accurate wiring path than the requirement described, and AC-001/AC-002 are written against it.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>85626</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>19</tool_uses><duration_ms>218266</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
