{"parentUuid":"50b96aa9-9c23-4f8a-826b-83433000694f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeEXUwgJDsER45pvNVFj3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good — the drafter even found a simpler, more accurate integration path than my requirement described. Dispatching the audit round now."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7640,"cache_read_input_tokens":676483,"output_tokens":5709,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":117},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7640,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5709,"cache_read_input_tokens":676483,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7640,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7640},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeEXUtChCLfozcWbE5eMT","type":"assistant","uuid":"66d75266-6dd6-499e-b015-d454a2a9ead2","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:08:27.965Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"66d75266-6dd6-499e-b015-d454a2a9ead2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeEXUwgJDsER45pvNVFj3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0153HWMPQUskbztDU8gXmkgB","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit Track 5 spec","subagent_type":"canon:auditor","prompt":"Do the audit work yourself directly in this invocation — do not delegate. Audit this spec@1 for \"Track 5: Changelog/PR-body Rendering Consolidation\" against your standard five dimensions (untestable/vague criteria, ambiguous phrasing, missing error cases, scope overlap with other workspace specs, TBDs/incomplete sections). Workspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto — check .claude/specs/ for any existing specs this might overlap with.\n\nThis spec is entering the same full canon->vector->lambda pipeline that took Track 4 five exit-gate rounds and Track 9 three rounds this session — the common failure classes to watch for specifically: invented API/field names not actually present in live code, criteria whose test method describes an unconstructible fixture, criteria that assert on internal implementation details rather than observable behavior, and criteria that silently assume data is available when it might not be. Re-verify every file:line citation and every type/field/method name against live code yourself — do not trust the spec's citations.\n\nspec@1:\n{\n  \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Make callisto's changelog and PR-body rendering accurately reflect every real cause of a version bump, by (1) making crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs reuse callisto_changelog::render_section and the already-built ChangelogInput data in VersionPlan.changelog_writes instead of hand-rolling its own Markdown from BumpReason, and (2) wiring three confirmed pieces of real, already-computed cause data -- InferenceOutcome.commits, GroupCheckOutcome.new_members, and a package's non-changeset outcome.reasons entry that co-occurs with a changeset entry -- through to ChangelogInput.entries instead of letting them be silently discarded.\",\n  \"scope\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs (Release Reason collapsible-details rendering only, not the Executive Summary table); crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs (BumpReason::Inference construction site, ~lines 223-236); crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs (the changelog_inputs if/else at ~lines 148-215, and group_check consumption at ~line 219); crates/callisto-changelog/src/input.rs is read but not modified (ChangeSource variants already exist and are sufficient). No change to callisto_changelog::render_section, callisto-changelog/src/write.rs, or inference's own severity computation.\",\n  \"non_goals\": [\n    \"A full multi-cause union covering more than one non-changeset reason per package in the same run (e.g. two independent cascades, or a cascade plus a peer-escalation, both non-changeset, for the same package). outcome.reasons and agg.reasons are BTreeMap<PackageId, BumpReason> (single-valued), not BTreeMap<PackageId, Vec<BumpReason>>, all the way through cascade.rs's severity/reason bookkeeping. This spec's scope is exactly changeset-plus-one-other-reason; a full N-reason union requires changing that data model throughout cascade.rs and is a separate, larger track.\",\n    \"Any change to callisto_changelog::render_section's rendering logic, grouping, section ordering, or Markdown output format -- it is already implemented and correct; this track only changes what calls it and what ChangelogInput data it is fed.\",\n    \"Any change to how CHANGELOG.md is written to disk (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs) -- untouched.\",\n    \"Any change to inference's own severity-computation logic, or to when inference fires at all -- only what data survives from InferenceOutcome to the resulting ChangeSource is in scope.\",\n    \"The exact Rust data-modeling mechanism used to carry a representative (CommitSha, String) pair from InferenceOutcome through to ChangeSource::Commit (e.g. a new field on BumpReason::Inference vs. a side-channel map in AggregateOutcome) is left to the implementer -- this spec constrains only the observable output (which commit's sha/subject appears in the rendered changelog entry), not the internal storage shape.\",\n    \"pr_body.rs's Executive Summary table (### Release Summary, the `| Package | Ecosystem | ... | Reason |` table built at pr_body.rs:82-136) is unchanged by this track. Its one-line `reason_str` per bump is a compact table-cell label, not a rendered changelog section, and render_section has no one-line output mode -- consolidating that table is out of scope; only the collapsible '#### Release Reason' block inside each package's `<details>` (pr_body.rs:175-218) is replaced with reused ChangelogInput + render_section output.\",\n    \"Constructing BumpReason::NewGroupMember (or any new BumpReason variant) is not required by this spec -- the NewGroupMember gap can be closed by directly constructing ChangeSource::NewGroupMember in version.rs's changelog-entry synthesis without necessarily threading a corresponding BumpReason through outcome.reasons; the implementer may choose either path as long as AC-004's observable behavior holds.\"\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"AC-001\", \"criterion\": \"For every bump in VersionPlan.bumps whose package has a matching entry `w` in VersionPlan.changelog_writes (i.e. some `w` where `w.input.package == bump.package`), the '#### Release Reason' block inside that package's `<details>` element in ComposePrBodyReport.body contains, verbatim, the exact string returned by `callisto_changelog::render_section(&w.input)` (including render_section's own '## <version>' or '## Unreleased' heading line) -- not a hand-matched reconstruction. After this change, crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs contains no `match` arm on `BumpReason::Cascade`, `BumpReason::PeerEscalation`, `BumpReason::FixedGroupUnion`, or `BumpReason::LinkedGroupUnion` that independently builds descriptive Markdown text (the block previously at pr_body.rs:184-216 is deleted, not duplicated) -- verified by `grep -c 'BumpReason::Cascade\\\\|BumpReason::PeerEscalation\\\\|BumpReason::FixedGroupUnion\\\\|BumpReason::LinkedGroupUnion' crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs` returning 0. Test method: a new unit test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs's `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` constructs a VersionPlan with one PlannedBump and one matching ChangelogWrite (built the same way version.rs builds it, with a real ChangeSource::Changeset entry), calls `render_pr_body_from_plan`, independently calls `callisto_changelog::render_section` on the same ChangelogInput in the test body, and asserts `report.body.contains(&expected_section)` where `expected_section` is that independently-computed render_section output.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-002\", \"criterion\": \"For a bump whose package has no entry in VersionPlan.changelog_writes (the package declares no changelog file, i.e. `pkg.changelog` is `None` in the versioning pipeline, so version.rs's changelog-write loop at ~lines 148-215 never runs for it), that package's `<details>` block in ComposePrBodyReport.body still contains a non-empty '#### Release Reason' section (the pre-existing per-BumpReason descriptive text is preserved for this case) -- render_pr_body_from_plan does not error, panic, or emit an empty '#### Release Reason' heading with no following text for such a package. Test method: unit test in pr_body.rs constructing a VersionPlan with one PlannedBump whose `reason` is `Some(BumpReason::Cascade{..})` and an empty `changelog_writes` Vec (simulating no changelog file for that package); assert `render_pr_body_from_plan` returns `Ok` and `report.body` contains '#### Release Reason' followed by non-whitespace content before the next `</details>`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-003\", \"criterion\": \"When a package's bump in a `plan_version` run is driven by `BumpReason::Inference` (i.e. `outcome.reasons.get(id) == Some(BumpReason::Inference{..})`) and the `InferenceOutcome` returned by the `SeverityInference` implementation for that package has a non-empty `commits: Vec<(CommitSha, String)>`, the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package in the resulting `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains a `ChangeSource::Commit { sha, subject }` entry where `sha` and `subject` equal `commits[0]`'s `CommitSha` and `String` respectively -- `commits[0]` because `callisto-vcs`'s `commits_since` (crates/callisto-vcs/src/shell.rs:141-174, and the native gix path it documents itself as matching field-for-field) shells `git log --no-merges` without a reversing flag, which is git's default newest-first order, so index 0 is the most recent commit. This choice is documented with a code comment at the construction site explaining why index 0 (not the last index) was chosen. Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module supplies a fake `SeverityInference` impl whose `infer()` returns `Ok(Some(InferenceOutcome { severity: Severity::Minor, commit_count: 2, remapped: false, commits: vec![(sha_recent, \\\"feat: recent\\\".into()), (sha_older, \\\"fix: older\\\".into())] }))` for a fixture package with no pending changeset, calls `plan_version`, and asserts the resulting `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package contains a `ChangeSource::Commit` entry with `sha == sha_recent` and `subject == \\\"feat: recent\\\"` (not `sha_older`).\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-004\", \"criterion\": \"When a package ID appears in `GroupCheckOutcome.new_members`'s `Vec<PackageId>` for some `GroupName` key (computed by `pre_mutation_checks` at crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:85, exposed to `plan_version` as `group_check.new_members` at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:87-93) AND that package has a bump this run (i.e. `outcome.severities.get(id)` is `Some(sev)` with `sev != Severity::None`), the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package in `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains a `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group }` entry where `group` equals that `GroupName` key. Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module constructs a fixture workspace with a fixed group containing one already-released member and one fresh (never-tagged) member, drives a bump for the fresh member (e.g. via a changeset or the group's fixed-union bump), calls `plan_version`, and asserts the fresh member's `ChangelogInput.entries` contains `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group: <the fixed group's GroupName> }`.\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-005\", \"criterion\": \"When a package `id` with a bump this run has BOTH a changeset-sourced entry (`agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)` is `Some`) AND a genuine non-changeset reason recorded for the same run (`outcome.reasons.get(id)` is `Some(reason)` where `reason` is one of `Cascade`, `PeerEscalation`, `FixedGroupUnion`, or `LinkedGroupUnion` -- the variants version.rs's synthesis branch already maps to a `ChangeSource` at ~lines 158-187), the resulting `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package contains: (a) every entry from `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)`'s `entries`, verbatim and in original order, followed by (b) exactly one additional `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is the `ChangeSource` variant that version.rs's existing mapping (lines 158-187) produces for `reason`, with `severity` equal to the package's resolved bump `severity` for this run. Total `entries.len()` equals the changeset-only entry count plus 1. Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module constructs a fixture where a package has one pending changeset AND is also a cascade target this run (both `agg.changelog_inputs` and `outcome.reasons` populated for the same package ID), calls `plan_version`, and asserts `changelog_writes` for that package has `entries.len() == 2`, with the first entry's `source` matching `ChangeSource::Changeset{..}` and the second matching `ChangeSource::DependencyUpdate{..}` (the mapping for `BumpReason::Cascade`).\", \"is_error_case\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-006\", \"criterion\": \"When a package has a bump this run (severity > None), `pkg.changelog` is `Some`, `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)` is `None` (no changeset), AND `outcome.reasons.get(id)` is either `None` or a variant with no direct `ChangeSource` mapping (falls to the catch-all currently at version.rs:188-199), `plan_version` does not panic and does not return `Err` attributable to this condition -- `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains exactly one `ChangelogWrite` for that package whose `input.entries.len() >= 1`, preserving the existing fallback: a single `ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: String::new(), summary: format!(\\\"Version bump ({})\\\", <severity as major|minor|patch|none>) }` entry. Test method: integration test in version.rs's test module constructs a fixture package with a bump whose `reason` is `None` and no pending changeset, calls `plan_version`, asserts it returns `Ok`, and asserts the package's `ChangelogWrite.input.entries` has exactly 1 entry matching `ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: \\\"\\\", summary }` where `summary` starts with `\\\"Version bump (\\\"`.\", \"is_error_case\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-007\", \"criterion\": \"render_pr_body_from_plan's call to `callisto_changelog::render_section` for a given package never causes the overall `compose_pr_body`/`render_pr_body_from_plan` call to panic or return `Err` because that one package's `ChangelogInput.entries` was empty (which would make `render_section` return `Err(ChangelogError::EmptyInput)`) -- on such an error for one package, that package's `<details>` block still renders (falling back to the AC-002 pre-existing per-BumpReason text, or if no `reason` is available either, a literal fallback line `_No changelog entries available._`) and every other package's block in the same PR body renders normally and completely. Note: this scenario is confirmed unreachable through the normal `plan_version` -> `pr_body` pipeline as of AC-006 (changelog_writes entries are never empty), so this criterion is tested by calling `render_pr_body_from_plan`'s per-package rendering path directly with a hand-constructed `VersionPlan` whose matching `ChangelogWrite.input.entries` is an empty `Vec` (bypassing `plan_version`), and asserting the call returns `Ok` with a body containing both the fallback text for that package and the normally-rendered block for a second, unaffected package in the same plan.\", \"is_error_case\": true}\n  ],\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION\"\n}\n\nReturn the challenger's standard JSON output (issues array with criterion_id/type/description/suggested_fix per issue, plus overall pass/fail)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7640,"cache_read_input_tokens":676483,"output_tokens":5709,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":117},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7640,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5709,"cache_read_input_tokens":676483,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7640,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7640},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeEXUtChCLfozcWbE5eMT","type":"assistant","uuid":"60b24856-dab8-45a1-8871-c59657fd9470","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:09:08.690Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType