{"parentUuid":"c268c9cb-fcf6-4fa1-a017-d8beeb5d9eb3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeEXwdwCwn7y6uhMg4zJJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016Wat3vrmz64zPingzY5WeK","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Exit-gate Track 5 spec","subagent_type":"canon:exit-gate","prompt":"Do the gate review yourself directly in this invocation, do not delegate. Workspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto. Read the spec@1 from /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/08ccaac1-3846-4134-8b06-140e5b9c22f2/scratchpad/spec-track5-draft.json (read it from disk).\n\nThis is retry_count: 1 (second submission). The first audit round found six issues, all fixed in this version:\n1. AC-001's grep-based verification was self-contradicting the spec's own non_goals -- it greped for BumpReason enum variant names that the (intentionally preserved, out-of-scope) Executive Summary table also matches on, so the grep could never return 0. Fixed: grep target changed to the literal Markdown fragments the deleted collapsible-details block produced (\"Automatic dependency cascade triggered by\" etc.), which don't appear in the Summary table's one-line labels.\n2. AC-002 falsely claimed universal fallback-text coverage, but pr_body.rs's pre-existing match has no arm for BumpReason::Inference/PreRelease/NewGroupMember (they fall to a catch-all producing an empty section) -- and this track's own AC-003/AC-004 newly make those variants reachable in the no-changelog-file case. Fixed: AC-002 now explicitly requires fallback text for all three, with example wording, and its test method covers all four variants (Cascade + the three gaps) instead of just Cascade.\n3. AC-007 was missing a test scenario for the \"no reason AND no entries\" case (literal fallback line), only covering the \"reason present, entries empty\" case. Fixed: AC-007 now specifies both sub-cases explicitly with two separate test scenarios.\n4. AC-007's phrase \"per-package rendering path directly\" was ambiguous (could imply a new internal function). Fixed: clarified as calling the existing public render_pr_body_from_plan function, no new function introduced; also added to non_goals.\n5+6. AC-003 and AC-004 left the synthesized ChangelogEntry's required `severity` field completely unconstrained/untested. Fixed: both now require severity to equal the package's resolved bump severity (outcome.severities.get(id)), with test methods updated to assert it.\n\nVerify all six fixes hold against live code, and do a genuinely fresh full pass over every other acceptance criterion (AC-001 through AC-007) checking for anything else missed. Specifically re-verify: pr_body.rs's actual match arms and line numbers (both the Executive Summary table ~99-124 and the collapsible-details block ~178-216) to confirm the new grep target strings are accurate and won't collide with anything unintended; ChangelogEntry's actual field requirements (severity + source, both required) in crates/callisto-changelog/src/input.rs; BumpReason's full variant list in crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs to confirm Inference/PreRelease/NewGroupMember are indeed the only three variants missing from pr_body.rs's existing match.\n\nIf this passes, it moves to vector:planner next."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":234,"cache_read_input_tokens":702702,"output_tokens":1178,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":234,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1178,"cache_read_input_tokens":702702,"cache_creation_input_tokens":234,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":234},"type":"message"}],"s