{"parentUuid":"8216df13-0da7-416b-b6b4-d495ded09050","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeEYPeYdviEX2Y6j9eqVB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3537,"cache_read_input_tokens":706315,"output_tokens":1606,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1487},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3537,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1606,"cache_read_input_tokens":706315,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3537,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3537},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeEYPXnbKwUgYTFDxSpf5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a5bd0e7e-5031-40ac-aebc-88709faaeb8a","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:20:36.924Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"a5bd0e7e-5031-40ac-aebc-88709faaeb8a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeEYPeYdviEX2Y6j9eqVB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015eENGQegidtVN9uTnMV98y","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/08ccaac1-3846-4134-8b06-140e5b9c22f2/scratchpad/spec-track5-draft.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3537,"cache_read_input_tokens":706315,"output_tokens":1606,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1487},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3537,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1606,"cache_read_input_tokens":706315,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3537,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3537},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeEYPXnbKwUgYTFDxSpf5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5b762ca1-f6e2-46fd-81af-7c4aa44b8a99","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:20:38.214Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"5b762ca1-f6e2-46fd-81af-7c4aa44b8a99","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"629ff530-1437-4686-829d-1f8152b6d488","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015eENGQegidtVN9uTnMV98y","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION\",\n3\t  \"purpose\": \"Make callisto's changelog and PR-body rendering accurately reflect every real cause of a version bump, by (1) making crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs reuse callisto_changelog::render_section and the already-built ChangelogInput data in VersionPlan.changelog_writes instead of hand-rolling its own Markdown from BumpReason, and (2) wiring three confirmed pieces of real, already-computed cause data -- InferenceOutcome.commits, GroupCheckOutcome.new_members, and a package's non-changeset outcome.reasons entry that co-occurs with a changeset entry -- through to ChangelogInput.entries instead of letting them be silently discarded.\",\n4\t  \"scope\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs (Release Reason collapsible-details rendering only, not the Executive Summary table); crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs (BumpReason::Inference construction site, ~lines 223-236); crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs (the changelog_inputs if/else at ~lines 148-215, and group_check consumption at ~line 219); crates/callisto-changelog/src/input.rs is read but not modified (ChangeSource variants already exist and are sufficient). No change to callisto_changelog::render_section, callisto-changelog/src/write.rs, or inference's own severity computation.\",\n5\t  \"non_goals\": [\n6\t    \"A full multi-cause union covering more than one non-changeset reason per package in the same run (e.g. two independent cascades, or a cascade plus a peer-escalation, both non-changeset, for the same package). outcome.reasons and agg.reasons are BTreeMap<PackageId, BumpReason> (single-valued), not BTreeMap<PackageId, Vec<BumpReason>>, all the way through cascade.rs's severity/reason bookkeeping. This spec's scope is exactly changeset-plus-one-other-reason; a full N-reason union requires changing that data model throughout cascade.rs and is a separate, larger track.\",\n7\t    \"Any change to callisto_changelog::render_section's rendering logic, grouping, section ordering, or Markdown output format -- it is already implemented and correct; this track only changes what calls it and what ChangelogInput data it is fed.\",\n8\t    \"Any change to how CHANGELOG.md is written to disk (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs) -- untouched.\",\n9\t    \"Any change to inference's own severity-computation logic, or to when inference fires at all -- only what data survives from InferenceOutcome to the resulting ChangeSource is in scope.\",\n10\t    \"The exact Rust data-modeling mechanism used to carry a representative (CommitSha, String) pair from InferenceOutcome through to ChangeSource::Commit (e.g. a new field on BumpReason::Inference vs. a side-channel map in AggregateOutcome) is left to the implementer -- this spec constrains only the observable output (which commit's sha/subject appears in the rendered changelog entry), not the internal storage shape.\",\n11\t    \"pr_body.rs's Executive Summary table (### Release Summary, the `| Package | Ecosystem | ... | Reason |` table built at pr_body.rs:82-136) is unchanged by this track, INCLUDING its own existing match arms on BumpReason::Cascade/PeerEscalation/FixedGroupUnion/LinkedGroupUnion at lines 99-124 -- these are one-line table-cell labels, not rendered changelog sections, and remain in the file untouched after this track. Its one-line `reason_str` per bump is a compact table-cell label, not a rendered changelog section, and render_section has no one-line output mode -- consolidating that table is out of scope; only the collapsible '#### Release Reason' block inside each package's `<details>` (pr_body.rs:175-218) is replaced with reused ChangelogInput + render_section output.\",\n12\t    \"Constructing BumpReason::NewGroupMember (or any new BumpReason variant) is not required by this spec -- the NewGroupMember gap can be closed by directly constructing ChangeSource::NewGroupMember in version.rs's changelog-entry synthesis without necessarily threading a corresponding BumpReason through outcome.reasons; the implementer may choose either path as long as AC-004's observable behavior holds.\",\n13\t    \"Introducing any new public or private function beyond what's needed to delete the old per-BumpReason Markdown-building code and call render_section instead -- AC-007's test method calls the existing public render_pr_body_from_plan function; no new 'per-package rendering' function is introduced by this spec.\"\n14\t  ],\n15\t  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n16\t    {\n17\t      \"id\": \"AC-001\",\n18\t      \"criterion\": \"For every bump in VersionPlan.bumps whose package has a matching entry `w` in VersionPlan.changelog_writes (i.e. some `w` where `w.input.package == bump.package`), the '#### Release Reason' block inside that package's `<details>` element in ComposePrBodyReport.body contains, verbatim, the exact string returned by `callisto_changelog::render_section(&w.input)` (including render_section's own '## <version>' or '## Unreleased' heading line) -- not a hand-matched reconstruction. After this change, the collapsible-details block previously at pr_body.rs:184-216 (the per-BumpReason Markdown-building code driving the '#### Release Reason' section) is deleted, not duplicated -- verified by `grep -c 'Automatic dependency cascade triggered by\\\\|Peer dependency escalation triggered by\\\\|Fixed group synchronization for group\\\\|Linked group version alignment for group' crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs` returning 0 (these are the literal Markdown fragments the deleted block produced; they do not appear anywhere else in the file, including the untouched Executive Summary table, so this grep cannot be satisfied by anything other than genuinely deleting the old block). The Executive Summary table's own match arms on BumpReason::Cascade/PeerEscalation/FixedGroupUnion/LinkedGroupUnion (pr_body.rs:99-124) are explicitly out of scope per this spec's non_goals and are NOT required to be removed or to return 0 on any grep. Test method: a new unit test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs's `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` constructs a VersionPlan with one PlannedBump and one matching ChangelogWrite (built the same way version.rs builds it, with a real ChangeSource::Changeset entry), calls `render_pr_body_from_plan`, independently calls `callisto_changelog::render_section` on the same ChangelogInput in the test body, and asserts `report.body.contains(&expected_section)` where `expected_section` is that independently-computed render_section output.\",\n19\t      \"is_error_case\": false\n20\t    },\n21\t    {\n22\t      \"id\": \"AC-002\",\n23\t      \"criterion\": \"For a bump whose package has no entry in VersionPlan.changelog_writes (the package declares no changelog file, i.e. `pkg.changelog` is `None` in the versioning pipeline, so version.rs's changelog-write loop at ~lines 148-215 never runs for it), that package's `<details>` block in ComposePrBodyReport.body still contains a non-empty '#### Release Reason' section, for every BumpReason variant -- render_pr_body_from_plan does not error, panic, or emit an empty '#### Release Reason' heading with no following text for such a package. This explicitly includes BumpReason::Inference, BumpReason::PreRelease, and BumpReason::NewGroupMember, which pr_body.rs's pre-existing match (lines 178-216) does NOT currently handle (they fall to the `_ => {}` catch-all at line 216 today, rendering an empty heading with no content) -- confirmed live as an existing gap that this track's own AC-003/AC-004 additions make newly reachable in practice (packages bumped via Inference or newly joining a group can now have a no-changelog-file case). This track must add fallback text for these three variants inside the same match, e.g.: `BumpReason::Inference { commits, .. } => format!(\\\"- Inferred from {} commit(s) since the last release.\\\\n\\\\n\\\", commits)`, `BumpReason::PreRelease { tag } => format!(\\\"- Pre-release finalization (tag `{}`).\\\\n\\\\n\\\", tag)`, `BumpReason::NewGroupMember { group } => format!(\\\"- New member of group `{}`.\\\\n\\\\n\\\", group.as_str())` (exact wording is the implementer's choice; the requirement is non-empty, non-panicking content). Test method: unit tests in pr_body.rs constructing a VersionPlan with one PlannedBump and an empty `changelog_writes` Vec (simulating no changelog file for that package), once each for `reason: Some(BumpReason::Cascade{..})` (pre-existing coverage), `Some(BumpReason::Inference{..})`, `Some(BumpReason::PreRelease{..})`, and `Some(BumpReason::NewGroupMember{..})` -- asserting for each that `render_pr_body_from_plan` returns `Ok` and `report.body` contains '#### Release Reason' followed by non-whitespace content before the next `</details>`.\",\n24\t      \"is_error_case\": true\n25\t    },\n26\t    {\n27\t      \"id\": \"AC-003\",\n28\t      \"criterion\": \"When a package's bump in a `plan_version` run is driven by `BumpReason::Inference` (i.e. `outcome.reasons.get(id) == Some(BumpReason::Inference{..})`) and the `InferenceOutcome` returned by the `SeverityInference` implementation for that package has a non-empty `commits: Vec<(CommitSha, String)>`, the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package in the resulting `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains a `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is `ChangeSource::Commit { sha, subject }` with `sha` and `subject` equal to `commits[0]`'s `CommitSha` and `String` respectively (`commits[0]` because `callisto-vcs`'s `commits_since` shells `git log --no-merges` without a reversing flag -- git's default newest-first order -- so index 0 is the most recent commit; this choice is documented with a code comment at the construction site), AND whose `severity` field equals the package's resolved bump severity for this run (`outcome.severities.get(id)`, i.e. the same severity value used to construct the corresponding `PlannedBump`). Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module supplies a fake `SeverityInference` impl whose `infer()` returns `Ok(Some(InferenceOutcome { severity: Severity::Minor, commit_count: 2, remapped: false, commits: vec![(sha_recent, \\\"feat: recent\\\".into()), (sha_older, \\\"fix: older\\\".into())] }))` for a fixture package with no pending changeset, calls `plan_version`, and asserts the resulting `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package contains a `ChangelogEntry` with `source` matching `ChangeSource::Commit { sha: sha_recent, subject: \\\"feat: recent\\\".to_string() }` (not `sha_older`) and `severity == Severity::Minor`.\",\n29\t      \"is_error_case\": false\n30\t    },\n31\t    {\n32\t      \"id\": \"AC-004\",\n33\t      \"criterion\": \"When a package ID appears in `GroupCheckOutcome.new_members`'s `Vec<PackageId>` for some `GroupName` key (computed by `pre_mutation_checks` at crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:85, exposed to `plan_version` as `group_check.new_members` at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:87-93) AND that package has a bump this run (i.e. `outcome.severities.get(id)` is `Some(sev)` with `sev != Severity::None`), the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package in `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains a `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group }` with `group` equal to that `GroupName` key, AND whose `severity` field equals the package's resolved bump severity for this run (`outcome.severities.get(id)`, i.e. the same severity value used for the package's `PlannedBump`). Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module constructs a fixture workspace with a fixed group containing one already-released member and one fresh (never-tagged) member, drives a bump for the fresh member (e.g. via a changeset or the group's fixed-union bump) with a known severity, calls `plan_version`, and asserts the fresh member's `ChangelogInput.entries` contains a `ChangelogEntry` with `source` matching `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group: <the fixed group's GroupName> }` and `severity` matching the fixture's driven bump severity.\",\n34\t      \"is_error_case\": false\n35\t    },\n36\t    {\n37\t      \"id\": \"AC-005\",\n38\t      \"criterion\": \"When a package `id` with a bump this run has BOTH a changeset-sourced entry (`agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)` is `Some`) AND a genuine non-changeset reason recorded for the same run (`outcome.reasons.get(id)` is `Some(reason)` where `reason` is one of `Cascade`, `PeerEscalation`, `FixedGroupUnion`, or `LinkedGroupUnion` -- the variants version.rs's synthesis branch already maps to a `ChangeSource` at ~lines 158-187), the resulting `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package contains: (a) every entry from `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)`'s `entries`, verbatim and in original order, followed by (b) exactly one additional `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is the `ChangeSource` variant that version.rs's existing mapping (lines 158-187) produces for `reason`, with `severity` equal to the package's resolved bump `severity` for this run. Total `entries.len()` equals the changeset-only entry count plus 1. Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module constructs a fixture where a package has one pending changeset AND is also a cascade target this run (both `agg.changelog_inputs` and `outcome.reasons` populated for the same package ID), calls `plan_version`, and asserts `changelog_writes` for that package has `entries.len() == 2`, with the first entry's `source` matching `ChangeSource::Changeset{..}` and the second matching `ChangeSource::DependencyUpdate{..}` (the mapping for `BumpReason::Cascade`).\",\n39\t      \"is_error_case\": false\n40\t    },\n41\t    {\n42\t      \"id\": \"AC-006\",\n43\t      \"criterion\": \"When a package has a bump this run (severity > None), `pkg.changelog` is `Some`, `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)` is `None` (no changeset), AND `outcome.reasons.get(id)` is either `None` or a variant with no direct `ChangeSource` mapping (falls to the catch-all currently at version.rs:188-199), `plan_version` does not panic and does not return `Err` attributable to this condition -- `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains exactly one `ChangelogWrite` for that package whose `input.entries.len() >= 1`, preserving the existing fallback: a single `ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: String::new(), summary: format!(\\\"Version bump ({})\\\", <severity as major|minor|patch|none>) }` entry. Test method: integration test in version.rs's test module constructs a fixture package with a bump whose `reason` is `None` and no pending changeset, calls `plan_version`, asserts it returns `Ok`, and asserts the package's `ChangelogWrite.input.entries` has exactly 1 entry matching `ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: \\\"\\\", summary }` where `summary` starts with `\\\"Version bump (\\\"`.\",\n44\t      \"is_error_case\": true\n45\t    },\n46\t    {\n47\t      \"id\": \"AC-007\",\n48\t      \"criterion\": \"render_pr_body_from_plan's call to `callisto_changelog::render_section` for a given package never causes the overall render_pr_body_from_plan call to panic or return `Err` because that one package's `ChangelogInput.entries` was empty (which would make `render_section` return `Err(ChangelogError::EmptyInput)`) -- on such an error for one package, that package's `<details>` block still renders and every other package's block in the same PR body renders normally and completely. Two fallback sub-cases: (a) when the package's `bump.reason` is `Some(..)`, the block falls back to AC-002's per-BumpReason text; (b) when `bump.reason` is `None` (no reason available either), the block falls back to the literal line `_No changelog entries available._`. Note: this scenario is confirmed unreachable through the normal `plan_version` -> `pr_body` pipeline as of AC-006 (changelog_writes entries are never empty when reached via plan_version), so this criterion is tested by calling the existing public function `render_pr_body_from_plan` (no new function is introduced) with a hand-constructed `VersionPlan` whose matching `ChangelogWrite.input.entries` is an empty `Vec` (bypassing `plan_version`). Test method: two unit tests -- (1) constructs a VersionPlan with one PlannedBump whose `reason` is `Some(BumpReason::Cascade{..})` and a matching ChangelogWrite whose `input.entries` is an empty Vec, plus a second, unaffected PlannedBump with normal data; asserts `render_pr_body_from_plan` returns `Ok` and the body contains both the AC-002 fallback text for the first package and the normally-rendered render_section output for the second. (2) constructs a VersionPlan with one PlannedBump whose `reason` is `None` and a matching ChangelogWrite whose `input.entries` is an empty Vec; asserts `render_pr_body_from_plan` returns `Ok` and the body contains the literal line `_No changelog entries available._` inside that package's `<details>` block.\",\n49\t      \"is_error_case\": true\n50\t    }\n51\t  ],\n52\t  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION\"\n53\t}\n54\t"}]},"uuid":"c642c494-9bdf-4a12-b605-69705a96f9ec","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:20:38.559Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/08ccaac1-3846-4134-8b06-140e5b9c22f2/scratchpad/spec-track5-draft.json","content":"{\n  \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Make callisto's changelog and PR-body rendering accurately reflect every real cause of a version bump, by (1) making crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs reuse callisto_changelog::render_section and the already-built ChangelogInput data in VersionPlan.changelog_writes instead of hand-rolling its own Markdown from BumpReason, and (2) wiring three confirmed pieces of real, already-computed cause data -- InferenceOutcome.commits, GroupCheckOutcome.new_members, and a package's non-changeset outcome.reasons entry that co-occurs with a changeset entry -- through to ChangelogInput.entries instead of letting them be silently discarded.\",\n  \"scope\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs (Release Reason collapsible-details rendering only, not the Executive Summary table); crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs (BumpReason::Inference construction site, ~lines 223-236); crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs (the changelog_inputs if/else at ~lines 148-215, and group_check consumption at ~line 219); crates/callisto-changelog/src/input.rs is read but not modified (ChangeSource variants already exist and are sufficient). No change to callisto_changelog::render_section, callisto-changelog/src/write.rs, or inference's own severity computation.\",\n  \"non_goals\": [\n    \"A full multi-cause union covering more than one non-changeset reason per package in the same run (e.g. two independent cascades, or a cascade plus a peer-escalation, both non-changeset, for the same package). outcome.reasons and agg.reasons are BTreeMap<PackageId, BumpReason> (single-valued), not BTreeMap<PackageId, Vec<BumpReason>>, all the way through cascade.rs's severity/reason bookkeeping. This spec's scope is exactly changeset-plus-one-other-reason; a full N-reason union requires changing that data model throughout cascade.rs and is a separate, larger track.\",\n    \"Any change to callisto_changelog::render_section's rendering logic, grouping, section ordering, or Markdown output format -- it is already implemented and correct; this track only changes what calls it and what ChangelogInput data it is fed.\",\n    \"Any change to how CHANGELOG.md is written to disk (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs) -- untouched.\",\n    \"Any change to inference's own severity-computation logic, or to when inference fires at all -- only what data survives from InferenceOutcome to the resulting ChangeSource is in scope.\",\n    \"The exact Rust data-modeling mechanism used to carry a representative (CommitSha, String) pair from InferenceOutcome through to ChangeSource::Commit (e.g. a new field on BumpReason::Inference vs. a side-channel map in AggregateOutcome) is left to the implementer -- this spec constrains only the observable output (which commit's sha/subject appears in the rendered changelog entry), not the internal storage shape.\",\n    \"pr_body.rs's Executive Summary table (### Release Summary, the `| Package | Ecosystem | ... | Reason |` table built at pr_body.rs:82-136) is unchanged by this track, INCLUDING its own existing match arms on BumpReason::Cascade/PeerEscalation/FixedGroupUnion/LinkedGroupUnion at lines 99-124 -- these are one-line table-cell labels, not rendered changelog sections, and remain in the file untouched after this track. Its one-line `reason_str` per bump is a compact table-cell label, not a rendered changelog section, and render_section has no one-line output mode -- consolidating that table is out of scope; only the collapsible '#### Release Reason' block inside each package's `<details>` (pr_body.rs:175-218) is replaced with reused ChangelogInput + render_section output.\",\n    \"Constructing BumpReason::NewGroupMember (or any new BumpReason variant) is not required by this spec -- the NewGroupMember gap can be closed by directly constructing ChangeSource::NewGroupMember in version.rs's changelog-entry synthesis without necessarily threading a corresponding BumpReason through outcome.reasons; the implementer may choose either path as long as AC-004's observable behavior holds.\",\n    \"Introducing any new public or private function beyond what's needed to delete the old per-BumpReason Markdown-building code and call render_section instead -- AC-007's test method calls the existing public render_pr_body_from_plan function; no new 'per-package rendering' function is introduced by this spec.\"\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-001\",\n      \"criterion\": \"For every bump in VersionPlan.bumps whose package has a matching entry `w` in VersionPlan.changelog_writes (i.e. some `w` where `w.input.package == bump.package`), the '#### Release Reason' block inside that package's `<details>` element in ComposePrBodyReport.body contains, verbatim, the exact string returned by `callisto_changelog::render_section(&w.input)` (including render_section's own '## <version>' or '## Unreleased' heading line) -- not a hand-matched reconstruction. After this change, the collapsible-details block previously at pr_body.rs:184-216 (the per-BumpReason Markdown-building code driving the '#### Release Reason' section) is deleted, not duplicated -- verified by `grep -c 'Automatic dependency cascade triggered by\\\\|Peer dependency escalation triggered by\\\\|Fixed group synchronization for group\\\\|Linked group version alignment for group' crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs` returning 0 (these are the literal Markdown fragments the deleted block produced; they do not appear anywhere else in the file, including the untouched Executive Summary table, so this grep cannot be satisfied by anything other than genuinely deleting the old block). The Executive Summary table's own match arms on BumpReason::Cascade/PeerEscalation/FixedGroupUnion/LinkedGroupUnion (pr_body.rs:99-124) are explicitly out of scope per this spec's non_goals and are NOT required to be removed or to return 0 on any grep. Test method: a new unit test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs's `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` constructs a VersionPlan with one PlannedBump and one matching ChangelogWrite (built the same way version.rs builds it, with a real ChangeSource::Changeset entry), calls `render_pr_body_from_plan`, independently calls `callisto_changelog::render_section` on the same ChangelogInput in the test body, and asserts `report.body.contains(&expected_section)` where `expected_section` is that independently-computed render_section output.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-002\",\n      \"criterion\": \"For a bump whose package has no entry in VersionPlan.changelog_writes (the package declares no changelog file, i.e. `pkg.changelog` is `None` in the versioning pipeline, so version.rs's changelog-write loop at ~lines 148-215 never runs for it), that package's `<details>` block in ComposePrBodyReport.body still contains a non-empty '#### Release Reason' section, for every BumpReason variant -- render_pr_body_from_plan does not error, panic, or emit an empty '#### Release Reason' heading with no following text for such a package. This explicitly includes BumpReason::Inference, BumpReason::PreRelease, and BumpReason::NewGroupMember, which pr_body.rs's pre-existing match (lines 178-216) does NOT currently handle (they fall to the `_ => {}` catch-all at line 216 today, rendering an empty heading with no content) -- confirmed live as an existing gap that this track's own AC-003/AC-004 additions make newly reachable in practice (packages bumped via Inference or newly joining a group can now have a no-changelog-file case). This track must add fallback text for these three variants inside the same match, e.g.: `BumpReason::Inference { commits, .. } => format!(\\\"- Inferred from {} commit(s) since the last release.\\\\n\\\\n\\\", commits)`, `BumpReason::PreRelease { tag } => format!(\\\"- Pre-release finalization (tag `{}`).\\\\n\\\\n\\\", tag)`, `BumpReason::NewGroupMember { group } => format!(\\\"- New member of group `{}`.\\\\n\\\\n\\\", group.as_str())` (exact wording is the implementer's choice; the requirement is non-empty, non-panicking content). Test method: unit tests in pr_body.rs constructing a VersionPlan with one PlannedBump and an empty `changelog_writes` Vec (simulating no changelog file for that package), once each for `reason: Some(BumpReason::Cascade{..})` (pre-existing coverage), `Some(BumpReason::Inference{..})`, `Some(BumpReason::PreRelease{..})`, and `Some(BumpReason::NewGroupMember{..})` -- asserting for each that `render_pr_body_from_plan` returns `Ok` and `report.body` contains '#### Release Reason' followed by non-whitespace content before the next `</details>`.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-003\",\n      \"criterion\": \"When a package's bump in a `plan_version` run is driven by `BumpReason::Inference` (i.e. `outcome.reasons.get(id) == Some(BumpReason::Inference{..})`) and the `InferenceOutcome` returned by the `SeverityInference` implementation for that package has a non-empty `commits: Vec<(CommitSha, String)>`, the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package in the resulting `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains a `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is `ChangeSource::Commit { sha, subject }` with `sha` and `subject` equal to `commits[0]`'s `CommitSha` and `String` respectively (`commits[0]` because `callisto-vcs`'s `commits_since` shells `git log --no-merges` without a reversing flag -- git's default newest-first order -- so index 0 is the most recent commit; this choice is documented with a code comment at the construction site), AND whose `severity` field equals the package's resolved bump severity for this run (`outcome.severities.get(id)`, i.e. the same severity value used to construct the corresponding `PlannedBump`). Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module supplies a fake `SeverityInference` impl whose `infer()` returns `Ok(Some(InferenceOutcome { severity: Severity::Minor, commit_count: 2, remapped: false, commits: vec![(sha_recent, \\\"feat: recent\\\".into()), (sha_older, \\\"fix: older\\\".into())] }))` for a fixture package with no pending changeset, calls `plan_version`, and asserts the resulting `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package contains a `ChangelogEntry` with `source` matching `ChangeSource::Commit { sha: sha_recent, subject: \\\"feat: recent\\\".to_string() }` (not `sha_older`) and `severity == Severity::Minor`.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-004\",\n      \"criterion\": \"When a package ID appears in `GroupCheckOutcome.new_members`'s `Vec<PackageId>` for some `GroupName` key (computed by `pre_mutation_checks` at crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:85, exposed to `plan_version` as `group_check.new_members` at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:87-93) AND that package has a bump this run (i.e. `outcome.severities.get(id)` is `Some(sev)` with `sev != Severity::None`), the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package in `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains a `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group }` with `group` equal to that `GroupName` key, AND whose `severity` field equals the package's resolved bump severity for this run (`outcome.severities.get(id)`, i.e. the same severity value used for the package's `PlannedBump`). Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module constructs a fixture workspace with a fixed group containing one already-released member and one fresh (never-tagged) member, drives a bump for the fresh member (e.g. via a changeset or the group's fixed-union bump) with a known severity, calls `plan_version`, and asserts the fresh member's `ChangelogInput.entries` contains a `ChangelogEntry` with `source` matching `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group: <the fixed group's GroupName> }` and `severity` matching the fixture's driven bump severity.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-005\",\n      \"criterion\": \"When a package `id` with a bump this run has BOTH a changeset-sourced entry (`agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)` is `Some`) AND a genuine non-changeset reason recorded for the same run (`outcome.reasons.get(id)` is `Some(reason)` where `reason` is one of `Cascade`, `PeerEscalation`, `FixedGroupUnion`, or `LinkedGroupUnion` -- the variants version.rs's synthesis branch already maps to a `ChangeSource` at ~lines 158-187), the resulting `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package contains: (a) every entry from `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)`'s `entries`, verbatim and in original order, followed by (b) exactly one additional `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is the `ChangeSource` variant that version.rs's existing mapping (lines 158-187) produces for `reason`, with `severity` equal to the package's resolved bump `severity` for this run. Total `entries.len()` equals the changeset-only entry count plus 1. Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module constructs a fixture where a package has one pending changeset AND is also a cascade target this run (both `agg.changelog_inputs` and `outcome.reasons` populated for the same package ID), calls `plan_version`, and asserts `changelog_writes` for that package has `entries.len() == 2`, with the first entry's `source` matching `ChangeSource::Changeset{..}` and the second matching `ChangeSource::DependencyUpdate{..}` (the mapping for `BumpReason::Cascade`).\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-006\",\n      \"criterion\": \"When a package has a bump this run (severity > None), `pkg.changelog` is `Some`, `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)` is `None` (no changeset), AND `outcome.reasons.get(id)` is either `None` or a variant with no direct `ChangeSource` mapping (falls to the catch-all currently at version.rs:188-199), `plan_version` does not panic and does not return `Err` attributable to this condition -- `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains exactly one `ChangelogWrite` for that package whose `input.entries.len() >= 1`, preserving the existing fallback: a single `ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: String::new(), summary: format!(\\\"Version bump ({})\\\", <severity as major|minor|patch|none>) }` entry. Test method: integration test in version.rs's test module constructs a fixture package with a bump whose `reason` is `None` and no pending changeset, calls `plan_version`, asserts it returns `Ok`, and asserts the package's `ChangelogWrite.input.entries` has exactly 1 entry matching `ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: \\\"\\\", summary }` where `summary` starts with `\\\"Version bump (\\\"`.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-007\",\n      \"criterion\": \"render_pr_body_from_plan's call to `callisto_changelog::render_section` for a given package never causes the overall render_pr_body_from_plan call to panic or return `Err` because that one package's `ChangelogInput.entries` was empty (which would make `render_section` return `Err(ChangelogError::EmptyInput)`) -- on such an error for one package, that package's `<details>` block still renders and every other package's block in the same PR body renders normally and completely. Two fallback sub-cases: (a) when the package's `bump.reason` is `Some(..)`, the block falls back to AC-002's per-BumpReason text; (b) when `bump.reason` is `None` (no reason available either), the block falls back to the literal line `_No changelog entries available._`. Note: this scenario is confirmed unreachable through the normal `plan_version` -> `pr_body` pipeline as of AC-006 (changelog_writes entries are never empty when reached via plan_version), so this criterion is tested by calling the existing public function `render_pr_body_from_plan` (no new function is introduced) with a hand-constructed `VersionPlan` whose matching `ChangelogWrite.input.entries` is an empty `Vec` (bypassing `plan_version`). Test method: two unit tests -- (1) constructs a VersionPlan with one PlannedBump whose `reason` is `Some(BumpReason::Cascade{..})` and a matching ChangelogWrite whose `input.entries` is an empty Vec, plus a second, unaffected PlannedBump with normal data; asserts `render_pr_body_from_plan` returns `Ok` and the body contains both the AC-002 fallback text for the first package and the normally-rendered render_section output for the second. (2) constructs a VersionPlan with one PlannedBump whose `reason` is `None` and a matching ChangelogWrite whose `input.entries` is an empty Vec; asserts `render_pr_body_from_plan` returns `Ok` and the body contains the literal line `_No changelog entries available._` inside that package's `<details>` block.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    }\n  ],\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION\"\n}\n","numLines":54,"startLine":1,"totalLines":54}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5b762ca1-f6e2-46fd-81af-7c4aa44b8a99","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
