{"parentUuid":"78b12ca2-634a-4930-b244-ef0e59cf6c24","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeEYWDL2QNTkxtv7ZNkj5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EvVMx7qZ3Sci5aYgGtn5hH","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Exit-gate Track 5 spec round 3","subagent_type":"canon:exit-gate","prompt":"Do the gate review yourself directly in this invocation, do not delegate. Workspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto. Read the spec@1 from /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/08ccaac1-3846-4134-8b06-140e5b9c22f2/scratchpad/spec-track5-draft.json (read it from disk).\n\nThis is retry_count: 2 (third submission — your own protocol escalates to human review after 3 retries, so treat this as needing to be thorough). Round 2 found five defects, all addressed in this version:\n\n1. AC-001 vs AC-002 contradicted each other: AC-001 required deleting the per-BumpReason fallback match (grep to 0); AC-002 required the SAME match retained and extended with 3 new arms. Fixed via real restructuring: the match is now explicitly RETAINED (stated in non_goals) as a fallback path, not deleted. AC-001 was rewritten from a structural \"delete the code\" claim to a DISPATCH PRIORITY claim: when a ChangelogWrite exists, render_section's output must be used INSTEAD OF the fallback text, even when both are reachable for the same package -- tested by constructing a case where both paths are available and asserting the fallback's distinctive literal text does NOT appear in the output.\n\n2. AC-004 (NewGroupMember) vs AC-005 (changeset+one-other-reason) had an arithmetic contradiction when both applied to the same package (AC-005 claimed an absolute total entries.len(), AC-004 could add one more on top) and AC-004's entry position was unspecified. Fixed: AC-005 now only describes its own N+1 entries as a prefix, explicitly disclaiming any total-length claim since AC-004 is independent/additive. AC-004 now specifies its entry is always appended LAST, and its own test fixture deliberately combines with a changeset to exercise this ordering. AC-006 and AC-005's test fixtures were adjusted to explicitly NOT be new-group-members, so their exact-length assertions stay valid.\n\n3. AC-003 (Inference) left the case of InferenceOutcome.commits being empty (while commit_count is nonzero -- the type doesn't prevent this) completely unhandled, and this was no longer covered by AC-006 once AC-003 claimed the Inference reason. Fixed: AC-003 now has an explicit second clause for the empty-commits case, falling back to a ChangeSource::Changeset with a commit-count-based summary (mirroring AC-006's pattern), with a second test case.\n\n4. AC-003 and AC-004 didn't state the `pkg.changelog.is_some()` precondition that version.rs:148 actually gates changelog-write construction on (AC-006 already had it), making both technically unsatisfiable as written on a no-changelog fixture. Fixed: both now explicitly require `pkg.changelog` is `Some(..)`.\n\n5. AC-007 only covered ChangelogError::EmptyInput, but render_section's group_entries call can also return ChangelogError::SeverityNoneEntry via the same hand-constructed-VersionPlan test route AC-007 itself mandates. Fixed: AC-007 now covers \"any Err(..)\" generically, with an explicit second test case for SeverityNoneEntry alongside the original EmptyInput case and the no-reason-either case (now three test cases total).\n\nVerify all five fixes hold against live code and are internally consistent with each other (the AC-001/AC-002/AC-004/AC-005 restructuring in particular touches multiple criteria that must now cohere as a single dispatch/accumulation model -- trace through a realistic scenario yourself: a package with a matching ChangelogWrite, a changeset, a cascade reason, AND being a new group member, and confirm the spec's criteria taken together produce one unambiguous, non-contradictory expected outcome for it). Re-verify ChangelogError's actual variant list, ChangelogEntry's field requirements, GroupCheckOutcome/InferenceOutcome's actual field types, and every file:line citation against live code -- do not trust the spec's own citations or my summary above.\n\nDo a genuinely fresh full pass over every criterion, not just the five that changed. If this passes, it moves to vector:planner next -- this is likely the last automated round before either a pass or human escalation, so be thorough rather than fast."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":230,"cache_read_input_tokens":725461,"output_tokens":1631,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":230,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1631,"cache_read_input_tokens":725461,"cache_creation_input_tokens":230,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":230},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeEYWAkVzLrNR9Bjp4C6F","type":"assistant","uuid":"a23cdd60-47cb-4460-a7a7-47391c61013b","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:22:06.262Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
