k pattern rather than leaving this state unhandled. Test method: two integration tests in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module. (1) supplies a fake `SeverityInference` impl whose `infer()` returns `Ok(Some(InferenceOutcome { severity: Severity::Minor, commit_count: 2, remapped: false, commits: vec![(sha_recent, \\\"feat: recent\\\".into()), (sha_older, \\\"fix: older\\\".into())] }))` for a fixture package with `pkg.changelog` set and no pending changeset, calls `plan_version`, and asserts the resulting `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package contains a `ChangelogEntry` with `source` matching `ChangeSource::Commit { sha: sha_recent, subject: \\\"feat: recent\\\".to_string() }` (not `sha_older`) and `severity == Severity::Minor`. (2) same fixture but `InferenceOutcome { commit_count: 2, commits: vec![], .. }` (empty commits, nonzero count), asserting the entry instead matches `ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: \\\"\\\", summary }` where `summary == \\\"Inferred version bump (2 commit(s))\\\"`.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-004\",\n      \"criterion\": \"When a package ID appears in `GroupCheckOutcome.new_members`'s `Vec<PackageId>` for some `GroupName` key (computed by `pre_mutation_checks` at crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:85, exposed to `plan_version` as `group_check.new_members` at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:87-93) AND that package has a bump this run (i.e. `outcome.severities.get(id)` is `Some(sev)` with `sev != Severity::None`) AND `pkg.changelog` is `Some(..)`, the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package in `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains, as its LAST entry (appended after any entries AC-003/AC-005/AC-006 already contributed for the same package -- this criterion is always additive, never a replacement, since GroupCheckOutcome.new_members is a separate structure from the single-valued outcome.reasons map and is not subject to AC-005's non_goals limitation), a `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group }` with `group` equal to that `GroupName` key, AND whose `severity` field equals the package's resolved bump severity for this run (`outcome.severities.get(id)`, i.e. the same severity value used for the package's `PlannedBump`). Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module constructs a fixture workspace with a fixed group containing one already-released member and one fresh (never-tagged) member with `pkg.changelog` set, drives a bump for the fresh member via a changeset (so AC-005's changeset-sourced entry also applies, exercising the additive-ordering requirement) with a known severity, calls `plan_version`, and asserts the fresh member's `ChangelogInput.entries` has the changeset entry first and, as its last element, a `ChangelogEntry` with `source` matching `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group: <the fixed group's GroupName> }` and `severity` matching the fixture's driven bump severity.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-005\",\n      \"criterion\": \"When a package `id` with a bump this run has BOTH a changeset-sourced entry (`agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)` is `Some`) AND a genuine non-changeset reason recorded for the same run (`outcome.reasons.get(id)` is `Some(reason)` where `reason` is one of `Cascade`, `PeerEscalation`, `FixedGroupUnion`, or `LinkedGroupUnion` -- the variants version.rs's synthesis branch already maps to a `ChangeSource` at ~lines 158-187), the resulting `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package contains, as its first N entries (N = the changeset-sourced entry count): every entry from `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)`'s `entries`, verbatim and in original order, immediately followed by exactly one additional `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is the `ChangeSource` variant that version.rs's existing mapping (lines 158-187) produces for `reason`, with `severity` equal to the package's resolved bump `severity` for this run. This criterion describes ONLY these N+1 entries; it does not claim `entries.len()` in total, since AC-004's NewGroupMember entry (when also applicable to the same package) is independently appended afterward per AC-004's own ordering rule. Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module constructs a fixture where a package has one pending changeset AND is also a cascade target this run, but is NOT a new group member (so AC-004 does not apply and entries.len() is exactly determinable), calls `plan_version`, and asserts `changelog_writes` for that package has `entries.len() == 2`, with the first entry's `source` matching `ChangeSource::Changeset{..}` and the second matching `ChangeSource::DependencyUpdate{..}` (the mapping for `BumpReason::Cascade`).\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false","new_string":"      \"id\": \"AC-003\",\n      \"criterion\": \"When a package's bump in a `plan_version` run has `pkg.changelog` equal to `Some(..)`, is driven by `BumpReason::Inference` (i.e. `outcome.reasons.get(id) == Some(BumpReason::Inference{..})`), AND `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)` is `None` (no pending changeset for this package -- the changeset-present case is covered by AC-005, not here, since {changelog_inputs: Some, reason: Inference} is a reachable state where a changeset and an inference-driven reason coexist): if the `InferenceOutcome` returned by the `SeverityInference` implementation for that package has a non-empty `commits: Vec<(CommitSha, String)>`, the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package in the resulting `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains EXACTLY ONE entry, a `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is `ChangeSource::Commit { sha, subject }` with `sha` and `subject` equal to `commits[0]`'s `CommitSha` and `String` respectively (`commits[0]` because `callisto-vcs`'s `commits_since` shells `git log --no-merges` without a reversing flag -- git's default newest-first order -- so index 0 is the most recent commit; this choice is documented with a code comment at the construction site), AND whose `severity` field equals the package's resolved bump severity for this run (`outcome.severities.get(id)`, i.e. the same severity value used to construct the corresponding `PlannedBump`). If instead `commits` is empty (a state `InferenceOutcome`'s type does not itself prevent, even though `commit_count` is nonzero), `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package contains EXACTLY ONE entry, a `ChangelogEntry` with `source` matching `ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: String::new(), summary: format!(\\\"Inferred version bump ({} commit(s))\\\", commit_count) }` and `severity` equal to the resolved bump severity -- mirroring AC-006's fallback pattern rather than leaving this state unhandled. Test method: two integration tests in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module. (1) supplies a fake `SeverityInference` impl whose `infer()` returns `Ok(Some(InferenceOutcome { severity: Severity::Minor, commit_count: 2, remapped: false, commits: vec![(sha_recent, \\\"feat: recent\\\".into()), (sha_older, \\\"fix: older\\\".into())] }))` for a fixture package with `pkg.changelog` set and no pending changeset, calls `plan_version`, and asserts the resulting `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package has `entries.len() == 1` with `source` matching `ChangeSource::Commit { sha: sha_recent, subject: \\\"feat: recent\\\".to_string() }` (not `sha_older`) and `severity == Severity::Minor`. (2) same fixture but `InferenceOutcome { commit_count: 2, commits: vec![], .. }` (empty commits, nonzero count), asserting `entries.len() == 1` with the entry matching `ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: \\\"\\\", summary }` where `summary == \\\"Inferred version bump (2 commit(s))\\\"`.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-004\",\n      \"criterion\": \"When a package ID appears in `GroupCheckOutcome.new_members`'s `Vec<PackageId>` for some `GroupName` key (computed by `pre_mutation_checks` at crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:85, exposed to `plan_version` as `group_check.new_members` at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:87-93) AND that package has a bump this run (i.e. `outcome.severities.get(id)` is `Some(sev)` with `sev != Severity::None`) AND `pkg.changelog` is `Some(..)`, the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package in `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains, as its LAST entry (appended after any entries AC-003/AC-005/AC-006 already contributed for the same package -- this criterion is always additive, never a replacement, since GroupCheckOutcome.new_members is a separate structure from the single-valued outcome.reasons map and is not subject to AC-005's non_goals limitation), a `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group }` with `group` equal to that `GroupName` key, AND whose `severity` field equals the package's resolved bump severity for this run (`outcome.severities.get(id)`, i.e. the same severity value used for the package's `PlannedBump`). Test method: two integration tests in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module. (1) constructs a fixture workspace with a fixed group containing one already-released member and one fresh (never-tagged) member with `pkg.changelog` set, drives a bump for the fresh member via a changeset with no other reason for the same package this run (so `outcome.reasons.get(id)` is `None` or a Changeset-derived reason with no AC-005 mapping, and AC-005 does not independently contribute a second entry), calls `plan_version`, and asserts `entries.len() == 2`: the changeset entry first (arriving via the pre-existing `agg.changelog_inputs` branch at version.rs:149, NOT via AC-005, since AC-005 requires a genuine non-changeset `outcome.reasons` value which this fixture does not have), and the `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember` entry last. (2) same fixture, but the fresh member is ALSO a cascade target this run with a cascade-