y: Severity::Minor, commit_count: 2, remapped: false, commits: vec![(sha_recent, \\\"feat: recent\\\".into()), (sha_older, \\\"fix: older\\\".into())] }))` for a fixture package with `pkg.changelog` set and no pending changeset, calls `plan_version`, and asserts the resulting `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package has `entries.len() == 1` with `source` matching `ChangeSource::Commit { sha: sha_recent, subject: \\\"feat: recent\\\".to_string() }` (not `sha_older`) and `severity == Severity::Minor`. (2) same fixture but `InferenceOutcome { commit_count: 2, commits: vec![], .. }` (empty commits, nonzero count), asserting `entries.len() == 1` with the entry matching `ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: \\\"\\\", summary }` where `summary == \\\"Inferred version bump (2 commit(s))\\\"`.\",","       \"is_error_case\": false","     },","     {","       \"id\": \"AC-004\",","-      \"criterion\": \"When a package ID appears in `GroupCheckOutcome.new_members`'s `Vec<PackageId>` for some `GroupName` key (computed by `pre_mutation_checks` at crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:85, exposed to `plan_version` as `group_check.new_members` at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:87-93) AND that package has a bump this run (i.e. `outcome.severities.get(id)` is `Some(sev)` with `sev != Severity::None`) AND `pkg.changelog` is `Some(..)`, the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package in `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains, as its LAST entry (appended after any entries AC-003/AC-005/AC-006 already contributed for the same package -- this criterion is always additive, never a replacement, since GroupCheckOutcome.new_members is a separate structure from the single-valued outcome.reasons map and is not subject to AC-005's non_goals limitation), a `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group }` with `group` equal to that `GroupName` key, AND whose `severity` field equals the package's resolved bump severity for this run (`outcome.severities.get(id)`, i.e. the same severity value used for the package's `PlannedBump`). Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module constructs a fixture workspace with a fixed group containing one already-released member and one fresh (never-tagged) member with `pkg.changelog` set, drives a bump for the fresh member via a changeset (so AC-005's changeset-sourced entry also applies, exercising the additive-ordering requirement) with a known severity, calls `plan_version`, and asserts the fresh member's `ChangelogInput.entries` has the changeset entry first and, as its last element, a `ChangelogEntry` with `source` matching `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group: <the fixed group's GroupName> }` and `severity` matching the fixture's driven bump severity.\",","+      \"criterion\": \"When a package ID appears in `GroupCheckOutcome.new_members`'s `Vec<PackageId>` for some `GroupName` key (computed by `pre_mutation_checks` at crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:85, exposed to `plan_version` as `group_check.new_members` at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:87-93) AND that package has a bump this run (i.e. `outcome.severities.get(id)` is `Some(sev)` with `sev != Severity::None`) AND `pkg.changelog` is `Some(..)`, the `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package in `VersionPlan.changelog_writes` contains, as its LAST entry (appended after any entries AC-003/AC-005/AC-006 already contributed for the same package -- this criterion is always additive, never a replacement, since GroupCheckOutcome.new_members is a separate structure from the single-valued outcome.reasons map and is not subject to AC-005's non_goals limitation), a `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group }` with `group` equal to that `GroupName` key, AND whose `severity` field equals the package's resolved bump severity for this run (`outcome.severities.get(id)`, i.e. the same severity value used for the package's `PlannedBump`). Test method: two integration tests in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module. (1) constructs a fixture workspace with a fixed group containing one already-released member and one fresh (never-tagged) member with `pkg.changelog` set, drives a bump for the fresh member via a changeset with no other reason for the same package this run (so `outcome.reasons.get(id)` is `None` or a Changeset-derived reason with no AC-005 mapping, and AC-005 does not independently contribute a second entry), calls `plan_version`, and asserts `entries.len() == 2`: the changeset entry first (arriving via the pre-existing `agg.changelog_inputs` branch at version.rs:149, NOT via AC-005, since AC-005 requires a genuine non-changeset `outcome.reasons` value which this fixture does not have), and the `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember` entry last. (2) same fixture, but the fresh member is ALSO a cascade target this run with a cascade-driven severity strictly greater than the changeset's own severity (satisfying cascade.rs:501's `target > cur_sev` gate so the cascade path actually fires and `outcome.reasons.get(id)` becomes `Some(BumpReason::Cascade{..})` without being overwritten back), exercising AC-005's additive entry too; asserts `entries.len() == 3` in order: `ChangeSource::Changeset{..}`, `ChangeSource::DependencyUpdate{..}` (AC-005's Cascade mapping), `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember{..}` (this criterion, appended last).\",","       \"is_error_case\": false","     },","     {","       \"id\": \"AC-005\",","-      \"criterion\": \"When a package `id` with a bump this run has BOTH a changeset-sourced entry (`agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)` is `Some`) AND a genuine non-changeset reason recorded for the same run (`outcome.reasons.get(id)` is `Some(reason)` where `reason` is one of `Cascade`, `PeerEscalation`, `FixedGroupUnion`, or `LinkedGroupUnion` -- the variants version.rs's synthesis branch already maps to a `ChangeSource` at ~lines 158-187), the resulting `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package contains, as its first N entries (N = the changeset-sourced entry count): every entry from `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)`'s `entries`, verbatim and in original order, immediately followed by exactly one additional `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is the `ChangeSource` variant that version.rs's existing mapping (lines 158-187) produces for `reason`, with `severity` equal to the package's resolved bump `severity` for this run. This criterion describes ONLY these N+1 entries; it does not claim `entries.len()` in total, since AC-004's NewGroupMember entry (when also applicable to the same package) is independently appended afterward per AC-004's own ordering rule. Test method: an integration test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module constructs a fixture where a package has one pending changeset AND is also a cascade target this run, but is NOT a new group member (so AC-004 does not apply and entries.len() is exactly determinable), calls `plan_version`, and asserts `changelog_writes` for that package has `entries.len() == 2`, with the first entry's `source` matching `ChangeSource::Changeset{..}` and the second matching `ChangeSource::DependencyUpdate{..}` (the mapping for `BumpReason::Cascade`).\",","+      \"criterion\": \"When a package `id` with a bump this run has BOTH a changeset-sourced entry (`agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)` is `Some`) AND a genuine non-changeset reason recorded for the same run (`outcome.reasons.get(id)` is `Some(reason)` where `reason` is one of `Cascade`, `PeerEscalation`, `FixedGroupUnion`, `LinkedGroupUnion`, or `Inference` -- the first four are the variants version.rs's synthesis branch already maps to a `ChangeSource` at ~lines 158-187; `Inference` maps per AC-003's own Commit-or-empty-commits-fallback logic, reused here rather than duplicated), the resulting `ChangelogInput.entries` for that package contains, as its first N entries (N = the changeset-sourced entry count): every entry from `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)`'s `entries`, verbatim and in original order, immediately followed by exactly one additional `ChangelogEntry` whose `source` is the `ChangeSource` variant that mapping produces for `reason` (AC-003's mapping when `reason` is `Inference`, version.rs's existing mapping otherwise), with `severity` equal to the package's resolved bump `severity` for this run. This criterion describes ONLY these N+1 entries; it does not claim `entries.len()` in total, since AC-004's NewGroupMember entry (when also applicable to the same package) is independently appended afterward per AC-004's own ordering rule. Test method: two integration tests in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module. (1) constructs a fixture where a package has one pending changeset AND is also a cascade target this run with cascade severity strictly greater than the changeset's severity (satisfying cascade.rs:501's `target > cur_sev` gate), and is NOT a new group member, calls `plan_version`, and asserts `changelog_writes` for that package has `entries.len() == 2`, with the first entry's `source` matching `ChangeSource::Changeset{..}` and the second matching `ChangeSource::DependencyUpdate{..}` (the mapping for `BumpReason::Cascade`). (2) same shape but the package's `outcome.reasons.get(id)` is `Some(BumpReason::Inference{..})` instead of Cascade (a real inference-then-changeset-both-present state), asserts `entries.len() == 2` with the second entry matching AC-003's Commit-or-fallback mapping for that Inference reason.\",","       \"is_error_case\": false","     },","     {"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d40cc7f9-3978-45a3-99a2-322781b2f0c7","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
