 that `GroupName` key, AND whose `severity` field equals the package's resolved bump severity for this run (`outcome.severities.get(id)`, i.e. the same severity value used for the package's `PlannedBump`). Test method: two integration tests in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs's test module. (1) constructs a fixture workspace with a fixed group containing one already-released member and one fresh (never-tagged) member with `pkg.changelog` set, drives a bump for the fresh member via a changeset with no other reason for the same package this run (so `outcome.reasons.get(id)` is `None` or a Changeset-derived reason with no AC-005 mapping, and AC-005 does not independently contribute a second entry), calls `plan_version`, and asserts `entries.len() == 2`: the changeset entry first (arriving via the pre-existing `agg.changelog_inputs` branch at version.rs:149, NOT via AC-005, since AC-005 requires a genuine non-changeset `outcome.reasons` value which this fixture does not have), and the `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember` entry last. (2) same fixture, but the fresh member is ALSO a cascade target this run with a cascade-driven severity strictly greater than the changeset's own severity (satisfying cascade.rs:501's `target > cur_sev` gate so the cascade path actually fires and `outcome.reasons.get(id)` becomes `Some(BumpReason::Cascade{..})` without being overwritten back), exercising AC-005's additive entry too; asserts `entries.len() == 3` in order: `ChangeSource::Changeset{..}`, `ChangeSource::DependencyUpdate{..}` (AC-005's Cascade mapping), `ChangeSource::NewGroupMember{..}` (this criterion, appended last).\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c980ef07-59de-480a-91b4-d64c0a752dd6","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"m