{"parentUuid":"6af4e4e2-8d6f-4c80-bab3-79ef2daf47a7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01FjDF3uiYGERFc5bAhSvu6n","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"callisto\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":47},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9da01f61-c3ff-4460-b99e-8f9181585b41","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:31:05.683Z","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"9da01f61-c3ff-4460-b99e-8f9181585b41","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/08ccaac1-3846-4134-8b06-140e5b9c22f2/scratchpad/spec-track5-draft.json","snippet":"1\t{\n2\t  \"id\": \"SPEC-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION\",\n3\t  \"purpose\": \"Make callisto's changelog and PR-body rendering accurately reflect every real cause of a version bump, by (1) making crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs prioritize callisto_changelog::render_section and the already-built ChangelogInput data in VersionPlan.changelog_writes over its own hand-rolled per-BumpReason Markdown (retained as a fallback, not deleted) whenever a matching ChangelogWrite exists, and (2) wiring three confirmed pieces of real, already-computed cause data -- InferenceOutcome.commits, GroupCheckOutcome.new_members, and a package's non-changeset outcome.reasons entry that co-occurs with a changeset entry -- through to ChangelogInput.entries instead of letting them be silently discarded.\",\n4\t  \"scope\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs (Release Reason collapsible-details rendering only, not the Executive Summary table); crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs (BumpReason::Inference construction site, ~lines 223-236); crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs (the changelog_inputs if/else at ~lines 148-215, and group_check consumption at ~line 219); crates/callisto-changelog/src/input.rs is read but not modified (ChangeSource variants already exist and are sufficient). No change to callisto_changelog::render_section, callisto-changelog/src/write.rs, or inference's own severity computation.\",\n5\t  \"non_goals\": [\n6\t    \"A full multi-cause union covering more than one non-changeset reason per package in the same run (e.g. two independent cascades, or a cascade plus a peer-escalation, both non-changeset, for the same package). outcome.reasons and agg.reasons are BTreeMap<PackageId, BumpReason> (single-valued), not BTreeMap<PackageId, Vec<BumpReason>>, all the way through cascade.rs's severity/reason bookkeeping. This spec's scope is exactly changeset-plus-one-other-reason (AC-005); a full N-reason union requires changing that data model throughout cascade.rs and is a separate, larger track. ChangeSource::NewGroupMember (AC-004) is independent of this limitation -- it is always additive on top of whatever AC-005/AC-006 already produced for the package, never subject to the single-valued outcome.reasons constraint, since new_members is tracked in a separate structure (GroupCheckOutcome).\",\n7\t    \"Any change to callisto_changelog::render_section's rendering logic, grouping, section ordering, or Markdown output format -- it is already implemented and correct; this track only changes what calls it and what ChangelogInput data it is fed.\",\n8\t    \"Any change to how CHANGELOG.md is written to disk (crates/callisto-changelog/src/write.rs) -- untouched.\",\n9\t    \"Any change to inference's own severity-computation logic, or to when inference fires at all -- only what data survives from InferenceOutcome to the resulting ChangeSource is in scope.\",\n10\t    \"The exact Rust data-modeling mechanism used to carry a representative (CommitSha, String) pair from InferenceOutcome through to ChangeSource::Commit (e.g. a new field on BumpReason::Inference vs. a side-channel map in AggregateOutcome) is left to the implementer -- this spec constrains only the observable output (which commit's sha/subject appears in the rendered changelog entry), not the internal storage shape.\",\n11\t    \"pr_body.rs's Executive Summary table (### Release Summary, the `| Package | Ecosystem | ... | Reason |` table built at pr_body.rs:82-136) is unchanged by this track, INCLUDING its own existing match arms on BumpReason::Cascade/PeerEscalation/FixedGroupUnion/LinkedGroupUnion at lines 99-124 -- these are one-line table-cell labels, not rendered changelog sections, and remain in the file untouched after this track. render_section has no one-line output mode -- consolidating that table is out of scope; only the collapsible '#### Release Reason' block inside each package's `<details>` (pr_body.rs:175-218) changes, and only in its dispatch logic (see AC-001/AC-002), not by deleting the existing per-BumpReason match.\",\n12\t    \"Constructing BumpReason::NewGroupMember (or any new BumpReason variant) is not required by this spec -- the NewGroupMember gap can be closed by directly constructing ChangeSource::NewGroupMember in version.rs's changelog-entry synthesis without necessarily threading a corresponding BumpReason through outcome.reasons; the implementer may choose either path as long as AC-004's observable behavior holds.\",\n13\t    \"Introducing any new public or private function beyond what's needed to add the render_section-priority dispatch and call render_section instead of the fallback when applicable -- AC-007's test method calls the existing public render_pr_body_from_plan function; no new 'per-package rendering' function is introduced by this spec.\",\n14\t    \"The pre-existing per-BumpReason match in pr_body.rs (lines 178-216, covering Changeset/Cascade/PeerEscalation/FixedGroupUnion/LinkedGroupUnion, extended by this spec to also cover Inference/PreRelease/NewGroupMember per AC-002) is explicitly RETAINED in the file, not deleted -- it becomes the fallback path used when no matching ChangelogWrite exists (AC-002) or when render_section errors on an existing ChangelogWrite (AC-007), rather than the sole rendering path it is today.\"\n15\t  ],\n16\t  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n17\t    {\n18\t      \"id\": \"AC-001\",\n19\t      \"criterion\": \"For every bump in VersionPlan.bumps whose package has a matching entry `w` in VersionPlan.changelog_writes (i.e. some `w` where `w.input.package == bump.package`) AND `render_section(&w.input)` returns `Ok(section)`, the '#### Release Reason' block inside that package's `<details>` element in ComposePrBodyReport.body contains, verbatim, `section` -- and does NOT contain the per-BumpReason fallback text AC-002 describes, even when the bump's `reason` field is also `Some(..)` and would independently produce non-empty fallback text. render_section's output takes dispatch priority over the fallback match whenever both are available for the same package; the fallback match (retained per non_goals, not deleted) is reached only under the conditions AC-002 and AC-007 describe. Test method: a new unit test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs's `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` constructs a VersionPlan with one PlannedBump whose `reason` is `Some(BumpReason::Cascade{ via, dep_kind, spec, dependency_to })` (so the fallback match's Cascade arm, if reached, would produce text containing the literal fragment \\\"Automatic dependency cascade triggered by\\\") AND a matching ChangelogWrite (built the same way version.rs builds it, with a real ChangeSource::Changeset entry, independent of the bump's `reason`), calls `render_pr_body_from_plan`, independently calls `callisto_changelog::render_section` on the same ChangelogInput in the test body to compute `expected_section`, and asserts `report.body.contains(&expected_section)` AND `!report.body.contains(\\\"Automatic dependency cascade triggered by\\\")` -- proving render_section's output was used and the fallback text was not, despite both being reachable inputs for the same package.\",\n20\t      \"is_error_case\": false\n21\t    },\n22\t    {\n23\t      \"id\": \"AC-002\",\n\n... [31 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c7156e25-7912-4559-bb4d-38447237b091","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:31:05.891Z","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
