{"parentUuid":"aee73f53-f42a-4bdf-8a65-5c6468b2f96b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeEZDKmNTkZAMkydgrhm9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LBqE4417Up1eB92xYUArfk","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Exit-gate Track 5 spec final round","subagent_type":"canon:exit-gate","prompt":"Do the gate review yourself directly in this invocation, do not delegate. Workspace root: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto. Read the spec@1 from /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/08ccaac1-3846-4134-8b06-140e5b9c22f2/scratchpad/spec-track5-draft.json (read it from disk).\n\nThis is retry_count: 2, submitted as this spec's final round -- your own protocol escalates to human review after 3 retries, and round 3's own verdict said \"the next submission is the last automated round.\" Round 3 found two blockers, both fixed in this version:\n\n1. AC-003 (Inference synthesis) left the state {agg.changelog_inputs.get(id) == Some (changeset present), reason == Inference} completely unconstrained -- neither AC-003, AC-005 (which only listed Cascade/PeerEscalation/FixedGroupUnion/LinkedGroupUnion), nor AC-006 (which requires changelog_inputs == None) covered it, and this state is genuinely reachable (aggregate.rs's inference loop runs first and sets reasons[P] = Inference; the later changeset loop only overwrites the reason when severity is strictly greater, but always pushes into changelog_inputs when severity != None). Fixed: AC-003 now has an explicit `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id) is None` precondition (scoping it to the no-changeset case, parallel to AC-006's structure) and pins entries.len() == 1 for both its Commit and empty-commits-fallback branches. AC-005's reason list now explicitly includes Inference, mapped via AC-003's own Commit-or-fallback logic (reused, not duplicated), with a second test case covering changeset+Inference co-occurrence.\n\n2. AC-004's own test-method rationale was factually wrong: it claimed the fixture's changeset entry \"also applies\" via AC-005, but in that specific fixture (fresh group member bumped via changeset, no cascade/peer-escalation involved) the reason is Changeset-derived with no AC-005 mapping, so the changeset entry actually arrives via the pre-existing version.rs:149 branch, not AC-005 -- meaning the original fixture never exercised AC-004's additive-ordering interaction with a spec-added entry at all. Fixed: AC-004's test method corrected to state the accurate mechanism (case 1, entries.len()==2, changeset-then-NewGroupMember, explicitly NOT via AC-005) and a NEW second case added where the same fresh member is ALSO a cascade target with cascade severity exceeding the changeset severity (satisfying cascade.rs:501's target > cur_sev gate), producing a genuine 3-entry sequence [Changeset, DependencyUpdate, NewGroupMember] that actually exercises AC-004's additive-append-after-AC-005 ordering claim.\n\nAlso fixed: a trivial line-citation nit (version.rs:87-93 -> 87-94 to include the closing paren line) in AC-004.\n\nVerify both fixes hold against live code, paying special attention to: (a) re-derive the full state table (changelog_inputs {Some,None} x reason {all BumpReason variants}) yourself and confirm every cell is now covered by exactly one of AC-003/AC-005/AC-006 with no gaps and no double-coverage; (b) actually trace through cascade.rs:501's real gate condition and confirm a cascade with severity strictly exceeding a changeset's severity for the same package genuinely produces reason == Cascade without being overwritten back to Changeset, i.e. confirm AC-004's new second test case is genuinely constructible; (c) re-verify every other criterion (AC-001, AC-002, AC-006, AC-007) fresh, since round 3 confirmed these already held but you should not simply take that on faith three rounds later -- read the live code yourself.\n\nIf this passes, it moves to vector:planner next. If it fails a third time, say so plainly and recommend escalation rather than proposing a fourth round yourself."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3284,"cache_read_input_tokens":741691,"output_tokens":1502,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3284,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1502,"cache_read_input_tokens":741691,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3284,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3284},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeEZDH8NjCVFktDupyuPi","type":"assistant","uuid":"acf3aef5-029e-404f-8b30-9c4a55e0ba86","timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:31:23.334Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
