{"parentUuid":"45641695-ed58-494b-bfa4-1a24c2a815d5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c130550b-7276-470a-8fe3-0aa3d1f5a26a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X9JveSpLduBmEXLrVwX6qU","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n    \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"artifact_type\": \"spec@1\",\n    \"retry_count\": 3,\n    \"verdict_summary\": \"Round 3's two blockers are genuinely fixed and AC-001/002/006/007 re-verified clean against live code. Two new blockers found in the corrected text: AC-003 now contradicts AC-004 on a reachable state, and AC-004's new fixture is not constructible as described. Retry budget exhausted \\u2014 escalate to human.\",\n    \"blockers\": [\n        {\n            \"criterion\": \"AC-003\",\n            \"location\": \"spec AC-003 (both branches); crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:148-215; crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:84-86\",\n            \"finding\": \"AC-003's newly added 'contains EXACTLY ONE entry' claim (stated unqualified in both the Commit branch and the empty-commits fallback branch) directly contradicts AC-004 on a reachable state. State: a never-tagged member of a fixed group, pkg.changelog Some, no pending changeset, bumped by inference. groups.rs:84-86 puts it in GroupCheckOutcome.new_members (fresh = last_tag None), aggregate.rs:227-233 sets reasons[id] = Inference, and agg.changelog_inputs.get(id) is None \\u2014 so AC-003 applies AND AC-004 applies. AC-003 demands entries.len() == 1; AC-004 demands the NewGroupMember entry be appended last, giving 2. An implementer cannot satisfy both and must make a judgment call about which criterion wins. AC-005 and AC-006 both already carry the needed carve-out; AC-003 is the only one missing it. Exact fix: in both AC-003 branches, replace 'contains EXACTLY ONE entry' with 'contains exactly one entry before AC-004's independent NewGroupMember append (if applicable)', mirroring AC-006's existing wording ('input.entries.len() >= 1 before AC-004's independent NewGroupMember append (if applicable)'), and add to each of AC-003's two test methods the fixture constraint that the package is not a member of any fixed group (so entries.len() == 1 is the correct assertion for those two tests specifically).\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"criterion\": \"AC-004\",\n            \"location\": \"spec AC-004 test method, cases (1) and (2); crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:400-446 (overwrite at 435); crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:97-142\",\n            \"finding\": \"AC-004's fixture is under-constrained and its non-overwrite claim names the wrong gate, so neither test case is constructible as described. Because GroupCheckOutcome.new_members is populated only from groups.fixed (groups.rs:28), any AC-004 fixture is necessarily a fixed group, so solve_cascade's fixed-group convergence block (cascade.rs:400-446) always runs (max_sev > None). That block computes winner = fixed_group_target(...), which bumps aligned_base = base[released[0]] (groups.rs:129-141) \\u2014 the ALREADY-RELEASED member's manifest version \\u2014 and then, at cascade.rs:433-440, for every member whose out.targets != winner it overwrites out.reasons with BumpReason::FixedGroupUnion. The fresh member's own target came from bump_target on ITS base (cascade.rs:526 via raise, or 208 via seed). So whenever the fresh member's manifest version differs from the released member's manifest version \\u2014 the natural reading of 'one already-released member and one fresh (never-tagged) member' \\u2014 reasons[fresh] is overwritten to FixedGroupUnion AFTER the cascade sets it. Consequences: case (1)'s premise 'outcome.reasons.get(id) is None or a Changeset-derived reason with no AC-005 mapping' becomes false (FixedGroupUnion IS in AC-005's list), so AC-005 contributes a GroupUnion entry and entries.len() is 3, not the asserted 2; case (2)'s asserted middle entry is ChangeSource::GroupUnion, not ChangeSource::DependencyUpdate, and its explicit claim that the reason becomes Cascade 'without being overwritten back' is false. Case (2) also cites 'cascade.rs:501's target > cur_sev gate' \\u2014 line 501 is 'if sev <= cur_sev { return Ok(false); }' (identifier is sev, not target); that gate is real and correctly characterized, but it is not the gate that threatens the reason here, so the rationale checks the wrong site. Exact fix: (a) add to BOTH cases the fixture constraint that the fresh member's and the released member's manifest base versions are identical (e.g. both 1.0.0, with only the released member carrying a git tag), so bump_target(fresh, sev) equals fixed_group_target's winner and the cascade.rs:433 branch is never taken; (b) rewrite case (2)'s parenthetical to cite both gates: cascade severity must strictly exceed the seeded severity to pass cascade.rs:501, AND the fixed-group targets must already equal the group winner so cascade.rs:435 does not overwrite reasons[fresh] with FixedGroupUnion; (c) correct 'cascade.rs:501's target > cur_sev gate' to 'cascade.rs:501's sev > cur_sev gate' in both AC-004 and AC-005, where the same phrasing appears.\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"reasoning\": \"Round 3's two blockers verified fixed against live code. (1) State-table gap: aggregate.rs:297 gates the reason overwrite on entry.severity > cur_sev while aggregate.rs:309 pushes into changelog_inputs whenever severity != None, so {changelog_inputs: Some, reason: Inference} is genuinely reachable \\u2014 AC-003's new 'changelog_inputs is None' precondition plus AC-005's expanded reason list now cover it with no double-coverage. Re-derived full table: {Some, Cascade/PeerEscalation/FixedGroupUnion/LinkedGroupUnion/Inference} -> AC-005 only; {None, Inference} -> AC-003 only (AC-006 excluded since Inference now has a mapping); {None, None-or-Changeset} -> AC-006 only; {Some, Changeset} -> pre-existing version.rs:149 passthrough, no criterion, unchanged behavior; {None, Cascade/PeerEscalation/FixedGroupUnion/LinkedGroupUnion} -> uncovered by all three (AC-006 excludes mapped variants, AC-005 requires changelog_inputs Some) but is pre-existing untouched behavior at version.rs:158-187 \\u2014 noted, not blocking. (2) AC-004's mechanism claim now correct on the changeset side: aggregate union_fixed leaves reasons[fresh] = Changeset since it holds the group max, so the changeset entry does arrive via version.rs:149 and not via AC-005, as the corrected text says. Line citations re-checked: version.rs:87-94 (pre_mutation_checks call incl. closing paren) correct; groups.rs:85 exact; version.rs:148-215/149/158-187/188-199 correct; pr_body.rs:82-136, 99-124, 175-218, 178-216, 216 catch-all all correct; aggregate.rs:223-236 correct. AC-001 fallback fragment 'Automatic dependency cascade triggered by' verified at pr_body.rs:191. AC-002's gap claim verified: Inference/PreRelease/NewGroupMember all fall to '_ => {}' at pr_body.rs:216 while the heading is pushed unconditionally at 176; all three BumpReason variants exist (report.rs:260-285). AC-006's fallback text matches version.rs:188-199 verbatim. AC-007: ChangelogError::EmptyInput (error.rs:8) and SeverityNoneEntry (group.rs:19) both exist and are reachable from render_section (render.rs:5-7); render_pr_body_from_plan is public (pr_body.rs:29). AC-003's commits[0]-is-newest rationale verified: shell.rs:141-160 builds 'git log --no-merges --format=...' with no --reverse. InferenceOutcome.commits is Vec<(CommitSha, String)> (infer.rs:35). No TBDs anywhere; error cases carry is_error_case: true on AC-002/AC-006/AC-007; scope (3 files, ~11 tests) fits one planning cycle. The two blockers above are both new, both introduced or left by round 3's own corrections, and both are the same class round 3 caught: an absolute claim that is false on a reachable state. Retry budget is exhausted (this is the third gate pass); recommending human review rather than a fourth automated round. Schema note: verdict@1 has no 'escalate' enum value, so verdict is 'fail' with retry_count 3 and the escalation recommendation carried in verdict_summary.\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"051f28fc-fbbe-43a5-89c5-25ff914f4078","timestamp":"2026-08-20T21:04:53.484Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\n    \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"artifact_type\": \"spec@1\",\n    \"retry_count\": 3,\n    \"verdict_summary\": \"Round 3's two blockers are genuinely fixed and AC-001/002/006/007 re-verified clean against live code. Two new blockers found in the corrected text: AC-003 now contradicts AC-004 on a reachable state, and AC-004's new fixture is not constructible as described. Retry budget exhausted \\u2014 escalate to human.\",\n    \"blockers\": [\n        {\n            \"criterion\": \"AC-003\",\n            \"location\": \"spec AC-003 (both branches); crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:148-215; crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:84-86\",\n            \"finding\": \"AC-003's newly added 'contains EXACTLY ONE entry' claim (stated unqualified in both the Commit branch and the empty-commits fallback branch) directly contradicts AC-004 on a reachable state. State: a never-tagged member of a fixed group, pkg.changelog Some, no pending changeset, bumped by inference. groups.rs:84-86 puts it in GroupCheckOutcome.new_members (fresh = last_tag None), aggregate.rs:227-233 sets reasons[id] = Inference, and agg.changelog_inputs.get(id) is None \\u2014 so AC-003 applies AND AC-004 applies. AC-003 demands entries.len() == 1; AC-004 demands the NewGroupMember entry be appended last, giving 2. An implementer cannot satisfy both and must make a judgment call about which criterion wins. AC-005 and AC-006 both already carry the needed carve-out; AC-003 is the only one missing it. Exact fix: in both AC-003 branches, replace 'contains EXACTLY ONE entry' with 'contains exactly one entry before AC-004's independent NewGroupMember append (if applicable)', mirroring AC-006's existing wording 