{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-20T21:16:01.566Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a629ea8be840011b5</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01WxDXv15RX4NMzW4cBNMvQj</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/08ccaac1-3846-4134-8b06-140e5b9c22f2/tasks/a629ea8be840011b5.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Exit-gate Track 5 spec round 5\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I verified every claim against live code. Two prior blockers are genuinely fixed; a third, previously unflagged defect blocks.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"artifact_type\": \"spec@1\",\n  \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"retry_count\": 4,\n  \"verdict_summary\": \"Both prior blockers verified fixed against live code. A distinct, previously unflagged defect blocks: AC-006's test fixture (a bump with reason None) is unreachable through plan_version. retry_count is now 4 and exceeds the threshold: human escalation, no further automated rounds.\",\n  \"blockers\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"AC-006\",\n      \"location\": \"spec AC-006 test_method; crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:105-146, aggregate.rs:226/298/447/527, cascade.rs:505/520/533-539, snapshot.rs:44-51\",\n      \"finding\": \"AC-006's test method requires a fixture where a package has a bump (severity &gt; None) and `reason` is `None`, driven through plan_version. That state is unreachable. Every site that inserts into a severities map on the plan_version path pairs the insert with a reason insert in the same guarded block (aggregate.rs:226/227 inference, 298/299 changeset, 447/448 union_fixed, 527/528 union_linked, version.rs:62-67 PreMode::Exit, cascade.rs:505/520 raise, cascade.rs:533-539 fixed siblings). The only two unpaired severity inserts (cascade.rs:349 and 420, the linked/fixed levelling loops) are immediately followed by the target loops at 380-392 and 432-444, where an unseeded member's `out.targets.get(&amp;id)` is None and therefore never equals `Some(&amp;winner)`, so a LinkedGroupUnion/FixedGroupUnion reason is always inserted. Nothing anywhere removes from `reasons`, and plan_version (version.rs:42-50) unconditionally runs aggregate with no bypass option. So `PlannedBump.reason == None` cannot occur and the test cannot be written. EXACT FIX: leave AC-006's criterion text unchanged (its disjunction correctly describes the `_ =&gt;` guard at version.rs:188), and replace only its test method with the reachable disjunct, mirroring the reachability note AC-007 already carries for itself: \\\"Test method: integration test in version.rs's test module. Because a bump with `reason: None` is unreachable through plan_version (every severity insertion on that path pairs with a reason insertion), this criterion is tested via the reachable no-mapping variant: construct a fixture workspace containing `.changeset/pre.json` with `mode: \\\\\\\"exit\\\\\\\"` and a tag, one package whose canonical manifest version is a pre-release (e.g. `1.1.0-alpha.1`) with `pkg.changelog` set, no pending changeset files on disk, not a member of any fixed or linked group, and pass `crate::infer::NoInference` as the SeverityInference impl so no Inference reason is recorded. version.rs:58-70 then injects `Severity::Patch` and `BumpReason::PreRelease { tag }`, `agg.changelog_inputs.get(id)` is None, and the catch-all at version.rs:188-199 is reached. Call `plan_version` with `VersionOptions::default()`, assert it returns `Ok`, and assert the package's `ChangelogWrite.input.entries` has exactly 1 entry matching `ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\", summary }` where `summary == \\\\\\\"Version bump (patch)\\\\\\\"`.\\\"\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"reasoning\": \"Everything else re-verified fresh against live code this round, not on prior verdicts. Prior fix 1 (AC-003): the {changelog_inputs: None, reason: Inference, is-fixed-group-member} state is now covered jointly rather than contradictorily — AC-003 scopes its single-entry claim to the pre-append snapshot (same wording AC-006 already used) and AC-004 owns the appended entry; the fixture's explicit non-membership makes the literal entries.len()==1 assertion correct rather than merely relocating the collision. Full state table over {changelog_inputs, reason, new-member} has no remaining contradiction or gap: A=Some/B=Changeset|None is untouched pre-existing behavior (version.rs:149 branch), correctly left unpinned. Prior fix 2 (AC-004): traced concretely. Case 1 — group {R tagged 1.0.0, F fresh 1.0.0}, F gets a Patch changeset. aggregate union_fixed (aggregate.rs:447) raises only R (target &gt; cur fails for F), so agg.reasons[F] stays Changeset. Seeding (cascade.rs:207-210) gives targets[F]=bump(1.0.0,Patch)=1.0.1. Fixed block: max_sev=Patch, fixed_group_target uses aligned_base=base[R]=1.0.0 and SemVerVersioning → winner 1.0.1 == targets[F], so 433-440 is not taken and reason stays Changeset (not in AC-005's list) → entries [Changeset, NewGroupMember], len 2, exactly as asserted. Case 2 — F additionally raised to Minor by a cascade (cascade.rs:501 `sev &lt;= cur_sev` early-returns, so Minor &gt; Patch fires); raise sets targets[F]=1.1.0 and reason Cascade, and its sibling block (530-543) pulls R to Minor/1.1.0; the fixed block then computes winner bump(1.0.0,Minor)=1.1.0 == targets[F], so 433-440 is again not taken → entries [Changeset, DependencyUpdate, NewGroupMember], len 3, as asserted. Version equality is safe: bump.rs:97-106 constructs a fresh canonical `Version::semver(...)` so raw-string provenance from two different manifests cannot make equal versions compare unequal. The gate-identifier correction to `sev &gt; cur_sev` matches line 501. Other re-verifications: pr_body.rs table 82-136 and match arms 99-124, details block 175-218, per-BumpReason match 178-216 with `_ =&gt; {}` at 216 and the literal 'Automatic dependency cascade triggered by' at 191 — all exactly as the spec cites; Inference/PreRelease/NewGroupMember do fall to the catch-all today. BumpReason field shapes (report.rs:256-286) make AC-002's proposed fallback snippets compile. ChangeSource::Commit/NewGroupMember already exist (input.rs:23-42). InferenceOutcome's four fields (infer.rs:31-36) match AC-003's literal exactly, and `commits` is genuinely discarded at aggregate.rs:227-233. The commits[0]=newest claim is correct end-to-end: shell.rs:147-155 runs `git log --no-merges` with no --reverse, the gix path walks outward from HEAD, commit.rs:72 documents newest-first, and infer.rs:95-99 plus callisto-conventional/src/infer.rs:26-40 preserve order. AC-005's Inference sub-case is reachable because aggregate runs inference before changesets and the changeset overwrite is gated on `entry.severity &gt; cur_sev`, so any changeset severity &lt;= the inferred severity leaves reason=Inference while still pushing the changelog entry. render_section (render.rs:5-9) and group.rs:19 confirm both AC-007 error triggers are real. Scope fits one planning cycle. No TBDs. Note: the schema's verdict enum admits only pass|fail, so escalation is carried in verdict_summary and retry_count rather than a verdict value.\"\n}\n```\n\n## What I confirmed fixed\n\n**Prior blocker 1 (AC-003 exclusivity).** Closed, not relocated. AC-003's claim is now scoped to the pre-append snapshot, so on the `{changelog_inputs: None, reason: Inference, is-fixed-group-member}` state AC-003 and AC-004 make complementary claims instead of contradictory ones. The added fixture exclusion independently makes the literal `entries.len() == 1` assertion correct for those two tests. I re-derived the full state table; no gap and no remaining collision.\n\n**Prior blocker 2 (AC-004 fixture).** Traced concretely for both cases with two members at 1.0.0, one tagged. `fixed_group_target`'s winner (aligned to `base[R]` = 1.0.0) equals `bump_target(F, sev)` in both configurations — 1.0.1 for the changeset-Patch case, 1.1.0 for the cascade-Minor case — so `cascade.rs:433-440`'s overwrite branch is genuinely never taken and F keeps `Changeset` / `Cascade` respectively. Both asserted outcomes (len 2 and len 3, in the stated order) hold. Version equality is safe because `bump.rs:97-106` builds a fresh canonical `Version`, so manifest raw-string provenance can't break it. The `sev &gt; cur_sev` identifier correction matches `cascade.rs:501`.\n\n## What blocks\n\nAC-006's test method asks for a fixture whose `PlannedBump.reason` is `None`. I enumerated every severity-insertion site on the `plan_version` path and every reason-insertion site, plus confirmed nothing removes from `reasons` and `plan_version` has no aggregate bypass: a bump always carries a reason. The fixture cannot be built. Notably, AC-007 already documents exactly this class of problem for itself and routes around it — AC-006 does not. The exact replacement test-method text is in the blocker above; it uses the reachable `PreMode::Exit` → `BumpReason::PreRelease` path, which lands on the same catch-all at `version.rs:188-199` and yields `\"Version bump (patch)\"`.\n\n## Disposition\n\nretry_count is now 4, which exceeds the threshold of 3. **This must go to human escalation. I am not recommending another automated round.** It does not proceed to vector:planner.\n\nOne thing the human should weigh: this is not a persistent blocker. The two blockers from round 3 were fixed correctly and I verified both against live code. What surfaced is a distinct, single-fixture defect in a criterion that three prior rounds passed, with a one-paragraph replacement already written. The schema's `verdict` enum admits only `pass`/`fail`, so I emitted `fail`; the escalation is carried in `verdict_summary` and `retry_count`.\n\nFiles read: `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/infer.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-changelog/src/input.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-changelog/src/render.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-changelog/src/error.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-changelog/src/group.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-model/src/version.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-model/src/commit.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-format/src/bump.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-vcs/src/shell.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-vcs/src/access.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-vcs/src/lib.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-conventional/src/infer.rs`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>121695</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>33</tool_uses><duration_ms>572022</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
