{"parentUuid":"ed1e8074-168a-4c18-bdfe-2d9e42e7b2d1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeEhLPvHPJjXqGKYofXYf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TksJmPiabfhdyFRNVwbWC4","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Plan Track 5 implementation","subagent_type":"vector:planner","prompt":"Produce a plan@1 for the spec at .claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION.json (workspace root /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto, read spec_file_path from disk). Do the planning work YOURSELF in this invocation and return the plan@1 JSON object directly as your final output — do not describe a plan to produce it, and do not delegate to another agent.\n\nThis spec passed canon-exit-gate on its 5th attempt after unusually heavy adversarial review — five full rounds tracing real cascade.rs/groups.rs/aggregate.rs convergence logic, catching contradictions between criteria, unconstructible test fixtures, and unreachable states. Trust the spec's 7 acceptance criteria as precisely accurate on the specific claims each round's adversarial review actually exercised (the state-coverage table, the fixed-group convergence trace, the commits[0]-is-newest ordering, the ChangelogError variant list) — every file:line citation was independently re-verified against live code in the final passing round. But still verify each claim yourself against the live code before writing each task's failing test, since code can drift even between a passing gate and planning, and this spec in particular has an established history of criteria interactions that looked fine in isolation but broke when combined (AC-001/002, AC-003/004/005, AC-004/006 all had real interaction bugs caught across rounds) — so when sequencing tasks, pay special attention to any task whose test fixture involves MORE than one of: a changeset, a cascade/peer-escalation/group-union reason, group membership (new_members), or inference, since that's exactly where this spec's own drafting repeatedly went wrong.\n\nSeven acceptance criteria, roughly in this dependency order (read the spec directly for the authoritative text — this is your orientation, not a substitute):\n1. AC-006 (fallback/catch-all preservation, uses a PreRelease-exit-mode fixture per the spec's own final-round correction) — foundational, no new logic, just a regression pin.\n2. AC-003 (Inference synthesis: ChangeSource::Commit from InferenceOutcome.commits, currently discarded at aggregate.rs's BumpReason::Inference construction site — two branches, non-empty commits and empty-commits fallback).\n3. AC-004 (ChangeSource::NewGroupMember from GroupCheckOutcome.new_members, computed but never consumed at version.rs — appended last, additive).\n4. AC-005 (changeset + one other reason union, including Inference reusing AC-003's mapping — this is where the spec's real architectural fix to version.rs's hard if/else at ~148-154 happens).\n5. AC-001 + AC-002 (pr_body.rs: add render_section-priority dispatch when a matching ChangelogWrite exists, keep the existing per-BumpReason match as fallback, extend that fallback match with 3 new arms for Inference/PreRelease/NewGroupMember).\n6. AC-007 (render_section error resilience in pr_body.rs — depends on AC-001/002's dispatch logic existing first).\n\nNo task should exceed 15 minutes. Every one of the 7 acceptance criteria must appear in at least one task's covers_criteria. Given this spec's history of criteria-interaction bugs, where a task's fixture combines multiple conditions (e.g. AC-004's two-case test method, or AC-005's Inference sub-case), make sure the task's steps include constructing the EXACT fixture the spec's test method describes (matching manifest versions where specified, NoInference where specified, etc.) rather than a simplified approximation — re-verify each fixture's constructibility against live cascade.rs/aggregate.rs/groups.rs logic yourself before finalizing that task's steps, the same way the exit-gate rounds did.\n\nOutput the plan@1 object directly (the calling process will persist it to .claude/plans/ and route it through vector:challenger next)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2101,"cache_read_input_tokens":770683,"output_tokens":1517,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":36},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2101,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1517,"cache_read_input_tokens":770683,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2101,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2101},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeEhLLYNwitFmBFXkjkMq","type":"assistant","uuid":"b28e44f3-89a7-48be-b9a7-438cedd3d860","timestamp":"2026-08-20T21:17:55.354Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.236","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
