{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-20T21:27:11.384Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>af91279aaed022599</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/08ccaac1-3846-4134-8b06-140e5b9c22f2/tasks/af91279aaed022599.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Plan Track 5 implementation\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Here is the `plan@1` for SPEC-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"PLAN-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION\",\n  \"spec_file_path\": \".claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION.json\",\n  \"spec_hash\": \"sha256:879f6e3a48fb875864fb5f7b4fe0de9154fae745295073539f0b63ce3d031417\",\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK5-CHANGELOG-PR-BODY-CONSOLIDATION\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Live-code verification (2026-08-20) confirmed every spec citation: aggregate.rs:223-236 constructs BumpReason::Inference from InferenceOutcome without ever retaining outcome.commits (Vec&lt;(CommitSha,String)&gt;); BumpReason::Inference itself only carries commits:usize + remapped:bool, so the (CommitSha,String) pairs are structurally unreachable from version.rs today -- confirming AC-003's non_goals note that a carrier mechanism must be chosen. I chose a side-channel map (Aggregation.inference_commits: BTreeMap&lt;PackageId, Vec&lt;(CommitSha,String)&gt;&gt;) over adding a field to BumpReason::Inference, because BumpReason is also rendered in pr_body.rs's Executive Summary table match (out of scope, non_goals) and in VersionReport/BumpRecord (public API surface) -- widening it would touch out-of-scope call sites, whereas a private field on Aggregation (already version.rs-local via `agg`) does not. version.rs:149 confirmed as the exact `if let Some(agg_input) = agg.changelog_inputs...` branch; the else-branch match at 155-199 confirmed with `_ =&gt; ChangeSource::Changeset` catch-all at line 188 producing 'Version bump ({severity})' -- this is BOTH the AC-006 fallback (already correct today, since PreRelease has no arm) AND the mapping AC-005 must reuse. groups.rs:85 pre_mutation_checks confirmed producing GroupCheckOutcome.new_members: BTreeMap&lt;GroupName, Vec&lt;PackageId&gt;&gt;, computed at version.rs:87 before run_cascade (line ~94), so it is in scope for the changelog_writes loop starting ~line 106. pr_body.rs's fallback match confirmed at the `if let Some(ref reason) = bump.reason { body.push_str(\\\"#### Release Reason\\\"); match reason {...} }` block with `_ =&gt; {}` catch-all -- Inference/PreRelease/NewGroupMember silently produce an empty heading today, exactly as AC-002 states. render_section (callisto-changelog/src/render.rs) confirmed to emit its own '## &lt;version&gt;' heading, never a '#### Release Reason' heading -- so the dispatch path must still emit '#### Release Reason' itself before pushing render_section's raw output, exactly as AC-001 requires ('contains, verbatim, section' under our own heading). ChangelogError::EmptyInput/SeverityNoneEntry confirmed in callisto-changelog/src/error.rs. Found a reusable, already-working real-git cascade fixture at crates/callisto-graph/tests/version_tests.rs (pkg-app depends on pkg-core via caret '1.0.0'; pkg-core major bump cascades pkg-app) -- reused its shape for AC-005/AC-004's cascade sub-cases. Found CascadeBumpSeverity config knob (crates/callisto-graph/src/config/resolve.rs:106, raw.rs:50 '[cascade] bump-severity') defaulting to Patch -- AC-005/AC-004(2)'s requirement that cascade severity be strictly greater than a Patch changeset requires setting 'bump-severity = \\\"minor\\\"' in callisto.toml, otherwise cascade severity (default Patch) never exceeds a Patch changeset and cascade.rs's raise() sev&gt;cur_sev gate (~line 496) never fires -- this is exactly the kind of interaction the adversarial rounds warned about, so I made this explicit rather than leaving fixture severities ambiguous. CRITICAL RE-SEQUENCING: the user's rough orientation ordered AC-004 (step 3) before AC-005 (step 4), but AC-004's own second test method requires entries.len()==3 with a DependencyUpdate entry in the middle -- that entry only exists once AC-005's changeset+cascade union logic is implemented. Sequencing AC-004 before AC-005 would make AC-004's task 2 test unimplementable (referencing behavior that does not exist yet), which is exactly the AC-004/AC-006-class interaction bug the adversarial rounds caught repeatedly. I resequenced to AC-003 -&gt; AC-005 -&gt; AC-004 so every task's fixture only exercises already-implemented behavior. Split AC-001+AC-002 into two tasks (AC-002 first, additive fallback arms; AC-001 second, dispatch priority) and split AC-003 into a scaffold task (aggregate.rs field+population, unit-testable in isolation) and a consumption task (version.rs mapping arm) to keep every task under 15 minutes and independently compilable. AC-007 is deliberately last since it restructures the exact dispatch block AC-001 introduces (adding an `Option&lt;&amp;BumpReason&gt;`-aware else-arm with a None case) -- doing it before AC-001 exists would mean editing code that isn't there yet.\"\n  ,\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T1\",\n      \"title\": \"AC-006: pin the existing PreRelease/no-mapping changelog fallback behavior\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Verified live: version.rs's else-branch match (no changeset) at ~155-199 has arms only for FixedGroupUnion/LinkedGroupUnion/Cascade/PeerEscalation; BumpReason::PreRelease falls to the `_ =&gt;` catch-all at line 188, which already produces `ChangeSource::Changeset{filename:String::new(), summary:format!(\\\"Version bump ({sev})\\\")}`. No production code change is required for this criterion -- it is already correct. Per the spec's own characterization ('foundational, no new logic, just a regression pin'), this task has no true red phase: the test is written first and is expected to pass immediately, proving the current fallback is correct before later tasks touch this same match. This is intentional, not a shortcut -- later tasks (T4) restructure this exact match, so a passing pin test here is the regression guard that would fail if T4 broke the no-mapping fallback.\",\n      \"files_to_create_or_modify\": [\n        \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\"\n      ],\n      \"test_first\": {\n        \"description\": \"Add a new #[test] inside `mod tests` in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs, in the same style as the existing `version_merges_group_check_diagnostics_into_plan` test (reuses git_init_with_commit/NoopRunner/IgnoreWalkLocator/Workspace::load/NoInference already defined in that module).\",\n        \"test_code\": \"    /// AC-006: a package with a bump this run, `pkg.changelog` set, no pending\\n    /// changeset, and a BumpReason with no direct ChangeSource mapping\\n    /// (PreRelease) must still produce exactly one ChangelogWrite entry via\\n    /// the generic 'Version bump ({severity})' fallback -- plan_version must\\n    /// not panic or error.\\n    #[test]\\n    fn version_prerelease_exit_falls_back_to_generic_changeset_summary() {\\n        let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n        let root = tmp.path();\\n        git_init_with_commit(root);\\n\\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\"pkg-a\\\")).unwrap();\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\"pkg-a/Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n            \\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"pkg-a\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"1.1.0-alpha.1\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\".changeset\\\")).unwrap();\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\".changeset/pre.json\\\"),\\n            r#\\\"{\\\"mode\\\":\\\"exit\\\",\\\"tag\\\":\\\"alpha\\\",\\\"initialVersions\\\":{},\\\"changesets\\\":[]}\\\"#,\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n        commit_all(root, \\\"add package\\\");\\n\\n        let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n        let runner = NoopRunner;\\n        let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &amp;locator, &amp;runner).expect(\\\"workspace must load\\\");\\n\\n        let inference = NoInference;\\n        let opts = VersionOptions {\\n            strict: false,\\n            strict_graph: false,\\n            allow_empty_changesets: true,\\n        };\\n\\n        let plan = plan_version(&amp;ws, &amp;inference, &amp;opts).expect(\\\"plan_version must succeed\\\");\\n\\n        let pkg_a = callisto_model::PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-a\\\").unwrap();\\n        let write = plan\\n            .changelog_writes\\n            .iter()\\n            .find(|w| w.input.package == pkg_a)\\n            .expect(\\\"pkg-a must have a ChangelogWrite\\\");\\n\\n        assert_eq!(write.input.entries.len(), 1, \\\"expected exactly 1 entry, got {:?}\\\", write.input.entries);\\n        match &amp;write.input.entries[0].source {\\n            callisto_changelog::ChangeSource::Changeset { filename, summary } =&gt; {\\n                assert_eq!(filename, \\\"\\\");\\n                assert_eq!(summary, \\\"Version bump (patch)\\\");\\n            }\\n            other =&gt; panic!(\\\"expected ChangeSource::Changeset fallback, got {other:?}\\\"),\\n        }\\n    }\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::version_prerelease_exit_falls_back_to_generic_changeset_summary\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"error[E0433]: failed to resolve: use of undeclared crate or module `callisto_changelog` -- OR the test does not yet exist, so `cargo test` reports 'test ... not found'. Either way, before this task's test is added there is no test named version_prerelease_exit_falls_back_to_generic_changeset_summary in the binary to run.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"No production code change. The existing catch-all at version.rs's else-branch match (`_ =&gt; ChangeSource::Changeset { filename: String::new(), summary: format!(\\\"Version bump ({})\\\", ...) }`) already satisfies AC-006. Add `use callisto_model::PackageId;` is unnecessary since `callisto_model::PackageId::parse` is already used fully-qualified elsewhere in this test module (see `version_merges_group_check_diagnostics_into_plan`'s sibling tests for the pattern); add `use callisto_changelog::ChangeSource;` is likewise unnecessary since the test above references it fully-qualified as `callisto_changelog::ChangeSource`.\",\n        \"code\": \"(no changes to non-test code)\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::version_prerelease_exit_falls_back_to_generic_changeset_summary\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test commands::version::tests::version_prerelease_exit_falls_back_to_generic_changeset_summary ... ok\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin AC-006 PreRelease-exit no-mapping changelog fallback\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-006\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T2\",\n      \"title\": \"AC-003 scaffold: retain InferenceOutcome.commits on Aggregation\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"BumpReason::Inference (callisto-model/src/report.rs:256-286) only carries `commits: usize` and `remapped: bool` -- the (CommitSha,String) pairs InferenceOutcome.commits holds are discarded the instant aggregate.rs:223-236 constructs the reason. AC-003 requires those pairs to survive to version.rs. Per the spec's own non_goals, the carrier mechanism is an implementer choice; I add a side-channel map on Aggregation (already threaded into version.rs as `agg` and still in scope when changelog_writes are built) rather than widening BumpReason, since BumpReason is also read by pr_body.rs's out-of-scope Executive Summary table and by the public VersionReport/BumpRecord API.\",\n      \"files_to_create_or_modify\": [\n        \"crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs\"\n      ],\n      \"test_first\": {\n        \"description\": \"Add a new #[test] inside `mod tests` in crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs, reusing the `init_repo`/`run_git`/`SinglePackageGraph`/`RealGitRunner` helpers already defined there (see `test_aggregate_scopes_inference_window_to_last_tag` for the exact pattern).\",\n        \"test_code\": \"    struct FixedCommitsInference {\\n        commits: Vec&lt;(CommitSha, String)&gt;,\\n    }\\n\\n    impl SeverityInference for FixedCommitsInference {\\n        fn infer(\\n            &amp;self,\\n            _pkg: &amp;Package,\\n            _git: &amp;GitAccess&lt;'_&gt;,\\n            _window: InferenceWindowSpec&lt;'_&gt;,\\n        ) -&gt; Result&lt;Option&lt;InferenceOutcome&gt;, GraphError&gt; {\\n            Ok(Some(InferenceOutcome {\\n                severity: Severity::Minor,\\n                commit_count: self.commits.len(),\\n                remapped: false,\\n                commits: self.commits.clone(),\\n            }))\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// AC-003 scaffold: aggregate() must retain InferenceOutcome.commits\\n    /// on Aggregation.inference_commits keyed by package, not discard it\\n    /// after constructing BumpReason::Inference (which only carries a count).\\n    #[test]\\n    fn test_aggregate_retains_inference_commits_on_aggregation() {\\n        let ws_dir = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n        let root = ws_dir.path();\\n        init_repo(root);\\n        std::fs::write(root.join(\\\"README.md\\\"), \\\"hello\\\\n\\\").unwrap();\\n        run_git(root, &amp;[\\\"add\\\", \\\".\\\"]);\\n        run_git(root, &amp;[\\\"commit\\\", \\\"-q\\\", \\\"-m\\\", \\\"initial commit\\\"]);\\n\\n        let pkg_id = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-a\\\").unwrap();\\n        let manifest = ManifestDecl::new(\\n            \\\"Cargo.toml\\\",\\n            ManifestRole::Canonical,\\n            ManifestFormat::CargoToml,\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n        let graph = SinglePackageGraph {\\n            pkg: Package {\\n                id: pkg_id.clone(),\\n                manifests: vec![manifest],\\n                changelog: None,\\n                release_trigger: callisto_model::ReleaseTrigger::Changeset,\\n                publish_to: Vec::new(),\\n                tag_template: None,\\n            },\\n        };\\n        let runner = RealGitRunner;\\n        let git = GitAccess::discover(root, &amp;runner);\\n        let cfg = crate::config::load(root).unwrap();\\n        let tags = TagIndex::build(&amp;git, &amp;graph, &amp;cfg).unwrap();\\n\\n        let mut base_versions = BTreeMap::new();\\n        base_versions.insert(pkg_id.clone(), callisto_model::Version::semver(1, 0, 0));\\n\\n        let sha_recent = CommitSha::parse(&amp;\\\"a\\\".repeat(40)).unwrap();\\n        let inference = FixedCommitsInference {\\n            commits: vec![(sha_recent.clone(), \\\"feat: recent\\\".to_string())],\\n        };\\n\\n        let agg = aggregate(&amp;graph, &amp;cfg, &amp;git, &amp;tags, &amp;base_versions, None, &amp;inference).unwrap();\\n\\n        assert_eq!(\\n            agg.inference_commits.get(&amp;pkg_id),\\n            Some(&amp;vec![(sha_recent, \\\"feat: recent\\\".to_string())]),\\n            \\\"Aggregation.inference_commits must retain InferenceOutcome.commits for the package\\\"\\n        );\\n    }\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib aggregate::tests::test_aggregate_retains_inference_commits_on_aggregation\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"error[E0609]: no field `inference_commits` on type `Aggregation` (compile failure, since the field does not exist yet)\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"Add a new field to the Aggregation struct (aggregate.rs, the `#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default)] pub struct Aggregation` block) and populate it at the existing Inference-outcome insertion site (aggregate.rs:223-236, inside `Ok(Some(outcome)) =&gt; { if outcome.severity &gt; cur_sev { ... } }`), right alongside the existing `agg.named_by.insert(...)` line.\",\n        \"code\": \"// In `pub struct Aggregation { ... }`, add:\\n    pub inference_commits: BTreeMap&lt;PackageId, Vec&lt;(CommitSha, String)&gt;&gt;,\\n\\n// In the aggregate() loop, inside `Ok(Some(outcome)) =&gt; { if outcome.severity &gt; cur_sev {`,\\n// immediately after the existing `agg.named_by.insert(pkg.id.clone(), NamedBy::Inference);` line, add:\\n                    agg.inference_commits\\n                        .insert(pkg.id.clone(), outcome.commits.clone());\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib aggregate::tests::test_aggregate_retains_inference_commits_on_aggregation\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test aggregate::tests::test_aggregate_retains_inference_commits_on_aggregation ... ok\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"feat(graph): retain InferenceOutcome.commits on Aggregation.inference_commits\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T3\",\n      \"title\": \"AC-003: map Inference reason to ChangeSource::Commit (or Changeset fallback) in version.rs's no-changeset synthesis\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"version.rs's else-branch match (no agg.changelog_inputs entry) has no arm for BumpReason::Inference today, so Inference-driven bumps fall to the same generic 'Version bump ({sev})' catch-all as PreRelease -- discarding both the commit_count and (via T2's new field) the actual commit data. Add a dedicated arm reading agg.inference_commits (populated by T2) and picking commits[0] (git log --no-merges default newest-first order, per spec) or falling back to a Changeset-shaped summary when empty.\",\n      \"files_to_create_or_modify\": [\n        \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\"\n      ],\n      \"test_first\": {\n        \"description\": \"Add two #[test]s inside `mod tests` in version.rs. Both need a fake SeverityInference forcing a fixed InferenceOutcome; define it once above the tests it's used in.\",\n        \"test_code\": \"    struct FixedInference {\\n        outcome: crate::infer::InferenceOutcome,\\n    }\\n\\n    impl crate::infer::SeverityInference for FixedInference {\\n        fn infer(\\n            &amp;self,\\n            _pkg: &amp;callisto_model::Package,\\n            _git: &amp;callisto_vcs::GitAccess&lt;'_&gt;,\\n            _window: crate::infer::InferenceWindowSpec&lt;'_&gt;,\\n        ) -&gt; Result&lt;Option&lt;crate::infer::InferenceOutcome&gt;, GraphError&gt; {\\n            Ok(Some(self.outcome.clone()))\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// AC-003 (non-empty commits): Inference-driven bump with a real,\\n    /// non-empty InferenceOutcome.commits must produce exactly one\\n    /// ChangelogEntry with ChangeSource::Commit from commits[0] (newest,\\n    /// since callisto-vcs shells `git log --no-merges` with no reversing\\n    /// flag -- git's default newest-first order).\\n    #[test]\\n    fn plan_version_inference_reason_maps_to_most_recent_commit() {\\n        let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n        let root = tmp.path();\\n        git_init_with_commit(root);\\n\\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\"pkg-a\\\")).unwrap();\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\"pkg-a/Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n            \\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"pkg-a\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"1.0.0\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n        commit_all(root, \\\"add package\\\");\\n\\n        let sha_recent = callisto_model::CommitSha::parse(&amp;\\\"a\\\".repeat(40)).unwrap();\\n        let sha_older = callisto_model::CommitSha::parse(&amp;\\\"b\\\".repeat(40)).unwrap();\\n        let inference = FixedInference {\\n            outcome: crate::infer::InferenceOutcome {\\n                severity: callisto_model::Severity::Minor,\\n                commit_count: 2,\\n                remapped: false,\\n                commits: vec![\\n                    (sha_recent.clone(), \\\"feat: recent\\\".to_string()),\\n                    (sha_older, \\\"fix: older\\\".to_string()),\\n                ],\\n            },\\n        };\\n\\n        let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n        let runner = NoopRunner;\\n        let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &amp;locator, &amp;runner).expect(\\\"workspace must load\\\");\\n        let opts = VersionOptions {\\n            strict: false,\\n            strict_graph: false,\\n            allow_empty_changesets: true,\\n        };\\n\\n        let plan = plan_version(&amp;ws, &amp;inference, &amp;opts).expect(\\\"plan_version must succeed\\\");\\n\\n        let pkg_a = callisto_model::PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-a\\\").unwrap();\\n        let write = plan\\n            .changelog_writes\\n            .iter()\\n            .find(|w| w.input.package == pkg_a)\\n            .expect(\\\"pkg-a must have a ChangelogWrite\\\");\\n\\n        assert_eq!(write.input.entries.len(), 1);\\n        assert_eq!(write.input.entries[0].severity, callisto_model::Severity::Minor);\\n        match &amp;write.input.entries[0].source {\\n            callisto_changelog::ChangeSource::Commit { sha, subject } =&gt; {\\n                assert_eq!(sha, &amp;sha_recent);\\n                assert_eq!(subject, \\\"feat: recent\\\");\\n            }\\n            other =&gt; panic!(\\\"expected ChangeSource::Commit, got {other:?}\\\"),\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// AC-003 (empty commits): an InferenceOutcome with empty `commits` but\\n    /// nonzero `commit_count` must fall back to a ChangeSource::Changeset\\n    /// entry summarizing the count, mirroring AC-006's fallback pattern.\\n    #[test]\\n    fn plan_version_inference_reason_falls_back_when_commits_empty() {\\n        let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n        let root = tmp.path();\\n        git_init_with_commit(root);\\n\\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\"pkg-a\\\")).unwrap();\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\"pkg-a/Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n            \\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"pkg-a\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"1.0.0\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n        commit_all(root, \\\"add package\\\");\\n\\n        let inference = FixedInference {\\n            outcome: crate::infer::InferenceOutcome {\\n                severity: callisto_model::Severity::Minor,\\n                commit_count: 2,\\n                remapped: false,\\n                commits: vec![],\\n            },\\n        };\\n\\n        let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n        let runner = NoopRunner;\\n        let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &amp;locator, &amp;runner).expect(\\\"workspace must load\\\");\\n        let opts = VersionOptions {\\n            strict: false,\\n            strict_graph: false,\\n            allow_empty_changesets: true,\\n        };\\n\\n        let plan = plan_version(&amp;ws, &amp;inference, &amp;opts).expect(\\\"plan_version must succeed\\\");\\n\\n        let pkg_a = callisto_model::PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-a\\\").unwrap();\\n        let write = plan\\n            .changelog_writes\\n            .iter()\\n            .find(|w| w.input.package == pkg_a)\\n            .expect(\\\"pkg-a must have a ChangelogWrite\\\");\\n\\n        assert_eq!(write.input.entries.len(), 1);\\n        match &amp;write.input.entries[0].source {\\n            callisto_changelog::ChangeSource::Changeset { filename, summary } =&gt; {\\n                assert_eq!(filename, \\\"\\\");\\n                assert_eq!(summary, \\\"Inferred version bump (2 commit(s))\\\");\\n            }\\n            other =&gt; panic!(\\\"expected ChangeSource::Changeset fallback, got {other:?}\\\"),\\n        }\\n    }\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_inference_reason_maps_to_most_recent_commit commands::version::tests::plan_version_inference_reason_falls_back_when_commits_empty\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"assertion `left == right` failed (or panic 'expected ChangeSource::Commit, got Changeset { filename: \\\"\\\", summary: \\\"Version bump (minor)\\\" }') -- both tests currently fall to the generic catch-all since no Inference arm exists in version.rs's else-branch match.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"In version.rs's else-branch match (the `match outcome.reasons.get(id) { ... }` block, ~lines 155-199), insert a new arm for `Some(BumpReason::Inference { commits, .. })` before the `_ =&gt;` catch-all, using agg.inference_commits (T2) to pick commits[0] or fall back.\",\n        \"code\": \"                    Some(BumpReason::Inference { commits, .. }) =&gt; {\\n                        match agg.inference_commits.get(id).and_then(|c| c.first()) {\\n                            Some((sha, subject)) =&gt; ChangeSource::Commit {\\n                                sha: sha.clone(),\\n                                subject: subject.clone(),\\n                            },\\n                            None =&gt; ChangeSource::Changeset {\\n                                filename: String::new(),\\n                                summary: format!(\\\"Inferred version bump ({commits} commit(s))\\\"),\\n                            },\\n                        }\\n                    }\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_inference_reason_maps_to_most_recent_commit commands::version::tests::plan_version_inference_reason_falls_back_when_commits_empty\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test commands::version::tests::plan_version_inference_reason_maps_to_most_recent_commit ... ok\\ntest commands::version::tests::plan_version_inference_reason_falls_back_when_commits_empty ... ok\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"feat(graph): map Inference reason to ChangeSource::Commit in changelog synthesis\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-003\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T4\",\n      \"title\": \"AC-005: union a changeset entry with the reason-mapped entry for the same package\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"version.rs:149's `if let Some(mut agg_input) = agg.changelog_inputs.get(id).cloned() { agg_input.from = ...; agg_input.to = ...; agg_input }` branch currently ignores outcome.reasons entirely -- a package with both a pending changeset and a genuine non-changeset reason (Cascade/PeerEscalation/FixedGroupUnion/LinkedGroupUnion/Inference) silently drops the second cause. Extract the else-branch's reason-to-ChangeSource match (now including T3's Inference arm) into a standalone helper reusable from both branches, then call it from the if-branch to append one additional entry. This is the exact architectural fix the spec calls out at version.rs's if/else ~148-215.\",\n      \"files_to_create_or_modify\": [\n        \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\"\n      ],\n      \"test_first\": {\n        \"description\": \"Add two #[test]s inside `mod tests` in version.rs, reusing the pkg-core/pkg-app cascade fixture shape confirmed working in crates/callisto-graph/tests/version_tests.rs's test_plan_version_produces_correct_bumps_in_cascade. `[cascade]\\\\nbump-severity = \\\"minor\\\"` is required in callisto.toml so the cascade severity (Minor) is strictly greater than the changeset severity (Patch), satisfying cascade.rs's raise() `sev &gt; cur_sev` gate.\",\n        \"test_code\": \"    /// AC-005 (Cascade sub-case): a package with a pending changeset AND a\\n    /// genuine Cascade reason this run must get its changeset entries\\n    /// followed by exactly one additional DependencyUpdate entry.\\n    #[test]\\n    fn plan_version_unions_changeset_with_cascade_reason() {\\n        let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n        let root = tmp.path();\\n        git_init_with_commit(root);\\n\\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\"pkg-core\\\")).unwrap();\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\"pkg-core/Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n            \\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"pkg-core\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"1.0.0\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n\\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\"pkg-app\\\")).unwrap();\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\"pkg-app/Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n            \\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"pkg-app\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"1.0.0\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n[dependencies]\\\\npkg-core = \\\\\\\"1.0.0\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\"callisto.toml\\\"),\\n            \\\"[cascade]\\\\nbump-severity = \\\\\\\"minor\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n\\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\".changeset\\\")).unwrap();\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\".changeset/core-break.md\\\"),\\n            \\\"---\\\\n\\\\\\\"pkg-core\\\\\\\": major\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nBreaking API change.\\\\n\\\",\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\".changeset/app-patch.md\\\"),\\n            \\\"---\\\\n\\\\\\\"pkg-app\\\\\\\": patch\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nUnrelated small fix.\\\\n\\\",\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n        commit_all(root, \\\"add packages and changesets\\\");\\n\\n        let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n        let runner = NoopRunner;\\n        let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &amp;locator, &amp;runner).expect(\\\"workspace must load\\\");\\n        let inference = crate::infer::NoInference;\\n        let opts = VersionOptions {\\n            strict: false,\\n            strict_graph: false,\\n            allow_empty_changesets: true,\\n        };\\n\\n        let plan = plan_version(&amp;ws, &amp;inference, &amp;opts).expect(\\\"plan_version must succeed\\\");\\n\\n        let pkg_app = callisto_model::PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-app\\\").unwrap();\\n        let write = plan\\n            .changelog_writes\\n            .iter()\\n            .find(|w| w.input.package == pkg_app)\\n            .expect(\\\"pkg-app must have a ChangelogWrite\\\");\\n\\n        assert_eq!(write.input.entries.len(), 2, \\\"got: {:?}\\\", write.input.entries);\\n        assert!(matches!(\\n            write.input.entries[0].source,\\n            callisto_changelog::ChangeSource::Changeset { .. }\\n        ));\\n        assert!(matches!(\\n            write.input.entries[1].source,\\n            callisto_changelog::ChangeSource::DependencyUpdate { .. }\\n        ));\\n    }\\n\\n    /// AC-005 (Inference sub-case, reusing T3's mapping): a package with\\n    /// both a pending changeset and outcome.reasons == Some(Inference{..})\\n    /// must get its changeset entries followed by one Inference-mapped\\n    /// entry (AC-003's Commit-or-fallback logic).\\n    #[test]\\n    fn plan_version_unions_changeset_with_inference_reason() {\\n        let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n        let root = tmp.path();\\n        git_init_with_commit(root);\\n\\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\"pkg-a\\\")).unwrap();\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\"pkg-a/Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n            \\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"pkg-a\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"1.0.0\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\".changeset\\\")).unwrap();\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\".changeset/pkg-a-patch.md\\\"),\\n            \\\"---\\\\n\\\\\\\"pkg-a\\\\\\\": patch\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nSmall fix.\\\\n\\\",\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n        commit_all(root, \\\"add package and changeset\\\");\\n\\n        let sha = callisto_model::CommitSha::parse(&amp;\\\"c\\\".repeat(40)).unwrap();\\n        let inference = FixedInference {\\n            outcome: crate::infer::InferenceOutcome {\\n                severity: callisto_model::Severity::Minor,\\n                commit_count: 1,\\n                remapped: false,\\n                commits: vec![(sha.clone(), \\\"feat: bigger change\\\".to_string())],\\n            },\\n        };\\n\\n        let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n        let runner = NoopRunner;\\n        let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &amp;locator, &amp;runner).expect(\\\"workspace must load\\\");\\n        let opts = VersionOptions {\\n            strict: false,\\n            strict_graph: false,\\n            allow_empty_changesets: true,\\n        };\\n\\n        let plan = plan_version(&amp;ws, &amp;inference, &amp;opts).expect(\\\"plan_version must succeed\\\");\\n\\n        let pkg_a = callisto_model::PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-a\\\").unwrap();\\n        let write = plan\\n            .changelog_writes\\n            .iter()\\n            .find(|w| w.input.package == pkg_a)\\n            .expect(\\\"pkg-a must have a ChangelogWrite\\\");\\n\\n        assert_eq!(write.input.entries.len(), 2, \\\"got: {:?}\\\", write.input.entries);\\n        assert!(matches!(\\n            write.input.entries[0].source,\\n            callisto_changelog::ChangeSource::Changeset { .. }\\n        ));\\n        match &amp;write.input.entries[1].source {\\n            callisto_changelog::ChangeSource::Commit { sha: got_sha, subject } =&gt; {\\n                assert_eq!(got_sha, &amp;sha);\\n                assert_eq!(subject, \\\"feat: bigger change\\\");\\n            }\\n            other =&gt; panic!(\\\"expected ChangeSource::Commit, got {other:?}\\\"),\\n        }\\n    }\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_unions_changeset_with_cascade_reason commands::version::tests::plan_version_unions_changeset_with_inference_reason\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"assertion `left == right` failed: left: 1, right: 2 -- the if-branch currently only carries agg.changelog_inputs's own entries through unchanged, never appending a reason-mapped entry.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"Extract the else-branch's `source` match (now including T3's Inference arm) into a standalone function `map_reason_to_change_source`, taking `&amp;BumpReason`, the package `id`, the resolved `to` Version, `&amp;outcome` (for PeerEscalation's dependency target lookup), and `&amp;agg` (for Inference's commits lookup). Change the `let input = if let Some(mut agg_input) = ...` binding to `let mut input = if let Some(mut agg_input) = ...` (needed by T5 too) and call the helper from the if-branch to append. Rewire the else-branch to call the same helper, falling back to the existing generic Changeset summary (AC-006, unchanged) when the helper returns None.\",\n        \"code\": \"// New free function, placed above `pub fn plan_version` or below it in the same module:\\nfn map_reason_to_change_source(\\n    reason: &amp;BumpReason,\\n    id: &amp;callisto_model::PackageId,\\n    to: &amp;callisto_model::Version,\\n    outcome: &amp;crate::cascade::CascadeOutcome,\\n    agg: &amp;crate::aggregate::Aggregation,\\n) -&gt; Option&lt;ChangeSource&gt; {\\n    match reason {\\n        BumpReason::FixedGroupUnion { group } =&gt; Some(ChangeSource::GroupUnion {\\n            group: group.clone(),\\n            kind: GroupKind::Fixed,\\n        }),\\n        BumpReason::LinkedGroupUnion { group } =&gt; Some(ChangeSource::GroupUnion {\\n            group: group.clone(),\\n            kind: GroupKind::Linked,\\n        }),\\n        BumpReason::Cascade {\\n            via,\\n            dep_kind,\\n            dependency_to,\\n            ..\\n        } =&gt; Some(ChangeSource::DependencyUpdate {\\n            dependency: via.clone(),\\n            dep_kind: *dep_kind,\\n            to: dependency_to.clone(),\\n        }),\\n        BumpReason::PeerEscalation { via, .. } =&gt; {\\n            let dep_to = outcome.targets.get(via).cloned().unwrap_or_else(|| to.clone());\\n            Some(ChangeSource::PeerEscalation {\\n                dependency: via.clone(),\\n                to: dep_to,\\n            })\\n        }\\n        BumpReason::Inference { commits, .. } =&gt; {\\n            match agg.inference_commits.get(id).and_then(|c| c.first()) {\\n                Some((sha, subject)) =&gt; Some(ChangeSource::Commit {\\n                    sha: sha.clone(),\\n                    subject: subject.clone(),\\n                }),\\n                None =&gt; Some(ChangeSource::Changeset {\\n                    filename: String::new(),\\n                    summary: format!(\\\"Inferred version bump ({commits} commit(s))\\\"),\\n                }),\\n            }\\n        }\\n        _ =&gt; None,\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n// Replace the existing `let input = if let Some(mut agg_input) = agg.changelog_inputs.get(id).cloned() { ... } else { ... };`\\n// block with:\\n            let mut input = if let Some(mut agg_input) = agg.changelog_inputs.get(id).cloned() {\\n                agg_input.from = from.clone();\\n                agg_input.to = Some(to.clone());\\n                if let Some(reason) = outcome.reasons.get(id) {\\n                    if let Some(source) = map_reason_to_change_source(reason, id, &amp;to, &amp;outcome, &amp;agg) {\\n                        agg_input.entries.push(ChangelogEntry { severity: sev, source });\\n                    }\\n                }\\n                agg_input\\n            } else {\\n                let source = outcome\\n                    .reasons\\n                    .get(id)\\n                    .and_then(|r| map_reason_to_change_source(r, id, &amp;to, &amp;outcome, &amp;agg))\\n                    .unwrap_or_else(|| ChangeSource::Changeset {\\n                        filename: String::new(),\\n                        summary: format!(\\n                            \\\"Version bump ({})\\\",\\n                            match sev {\\n                                Severity::Major =&gt; \\\"major\\\",\\n                                Severity::Minor =&gt; \\\"minor\\\",\\n                                Severity::Patch =&gt; \\\"patch\\\",\\n                                Severity::None =&gt; \\\"none\\\",\\n                            }\\n                        ),\\n                    });\\n                ChangelogInput {\\n                    package: id.clone(),\\n                    from: from.clone(),\\n                    to: Some(to.clone()),\\n                    entries: vec![ChangelogEntry { severity: sev, source }],\\n                }\\n            };\\n// (the subsequent `changelog_writes.push(crate::plan::ChangelogWrite { changelog_path: ch_path.clone(), input });`\\n// line is unaffected -- `input` is still the same binding, now declared `mut`.)\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_unions_changeset_with_cascade_reason commands::version::tests::plan_version_unions_changeset_with_inference_reason commands::version::tests::plan_version_inference_reason_maps_to_most_recent_commit commands::version::tests::version_prerelease_exit_falls_back_to_generic_changeset_summary\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test commands::version::tests::plan_version_unions_changeset_with_cascade_reason ... ok\\ntest commands::version::tests::plan_version_unions_changeset_with_inference_reason ... ok\\ntest commands::version::tests::plan_version_inference_reason_maps_to_most_recent_commit ... ok\\ntest commands::version::tests::version_prerelease_exit_falls_back_to_generic_changeset_summary ... ok\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"feat(graph): union changeset entries with the reason-mapped entry for the same package\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-005\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T5\",\n      \"title\": \"AC-004: append a NewGroupMember entry as the last changelog entry for fresh group members\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"GroupCheckOutcome.new_members (groups.rs:85, exposed to plan_version as `group_check` at version.rs:87-94, computed before run_cascade) is never consulted when building changelog_writes. Append a ChangeSource::NewGroupMember entry as the LAST entry (always additive, per non_goals -- new_members is a separate structure from the single-valued outcome.reasons map) whenever the package id appears in any group's new_members list. Verified live: cascade.rs's fixed-group convergence block (~416-442) only overwrites a member's `reason` when `out.targets.get(&amp;id) != Some(&amp;winner)` -- with both group members starting at an identical base version, `winner` (computed via fixed_group_target's aligned_base = the released member's base version) equals the fresh member's own already-computed target, so the convergence loop's overwrite branch is never taken and the fresh member's changeset-or-cascade reason survives untouched, exactly as the spec's test method requires.\",\n      \"files_to_create_or_modify\": [\n        \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\"\n      ],\n      \"test_first\": {\n        \"description\": \"Add two #[test]s inside `mod tests` in version.rs. Test (2) requires T4's cascade-union logic to already exist (it asserts on the DependencyUpdate entry T4 introduced), which is why this task is sequenced after T4.\",\n        \"test_code\": \"    /// AC-004 (changeset-only sub-case): a fixed group with one released\\n    /// member and one fresh (never-tagged) member at the identical base\\n    /// version; the fresh member gets a changeset-driven bump with no other\\n    /// reason. Entries must be [Changeset, NewGroupMember] in that order.\\n    #[test]\\n    fn plan_version_appends_new_group_member_entry_after_changeset() {\\n        let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n        let root = tmp.path();\\n        git_init_with_commit(root);\\n\\n        for name in [\\\"pkg-released\\\", \\\"pkg-fresh\\\"] {\\n            std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(name)).unwrap();\\n            std::fs::write(\\n                root.join(name).join(\\\"Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n                format!(\\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"{name}\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"1.0.0\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\"),\\n            )\\n            .unwrap();\\n        }\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\"callisto.toml\\\"),\\n            \\\"[[fixed-group]]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"grp\\\\\\\"\\\\nmembers = [\\\\\\\"pkg-released\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"pkg-fresh\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\",\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\".changeset\\\")).unwrap();\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\".changeset/fresh-patch.md\\\"),\\n            \\\"---\\\\n\\\\\\\"pkg-fresh\\\\\\\": patch\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nfix.\\\\n\\\",\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n        commit_all(root, \\\"add packages\\\");\\n        tag(root, \\\"pkg-released@1.0.0\\\");\\n\\n        let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n        let runner = NoopRunner;\\n        let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &amp;locator, &amp;runner).expect(\\\"workspace must load\\\");\\n        let inference = crate::infer::NoInference;\\n        let opts = VersionOptions {\\n            strict: false,\\n            strict_graph: false,\\n            allow_empty_changesets: true,\\n        };\\n\\n        let plan = plan_version(&amp;ws, &amp;inference, &amp;opts).expect(\\\"plan_version must succeed\\\");\\n\\n        let pkg_fresh = callisto_model::PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-fresh\\\").unwrap();\\n        let write = plan\\n            .changelog_writes\\n            .iter()\\n            .find(|w| w.input.package == pkg_fresh)\\n            .expect(\\\"pkg-fresh must have a ChangelogWrite\\\");\\n\\n        assert_eq!(write.input.entries.len(), 2, \\\"got: {:?}\\\", write.input.entries);\\n        assert!(matches!(\\n            write.input.entries[0].source,\\n            callisto_changelog::ChangeSource::Changeset { .. }\\n        ));\\n        assert!(matches!(\\n            write.input.entries[1].source,\\n            callisto_changelog::ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { .. }\\n        ));\\n    }\\n\\n    /// AC-004 (additive-on-top-of-AC-005 sub-case): same fixed-group\\n    /// fixture, but pkg-fresh is ALSO a cascade target this run (via a\\n    /// third driver package), so it has both a changeset entry and a\\n    /// cascade-mapped entry (T4) before the NewGroupMember append.\\n    #[test]\\n    fn plan_version_new_group_member_entry_is_additive_after_cascade_union() {\\n        let tmp = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\\n        let root = tmp.path();\\n        git_init_with_commit(root);\\n\\n        for name in [\\\"pkg-released\\\", \\\"pkg-fresh\\\"] {\\n            std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(name)).unwrap();\\n            std::fs::write(\\n                root.join(name).join(\\\"Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n                format!(\\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"{name}\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"1.0.0\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\"),\\n            )\\n            .unwrap();\\n        }\\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\"pkg-driver\\\")).unwrap();\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\"pkg-driver/Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n            \\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"pkg-driver\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"1.0.0\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\"pkg-fresh/Cargo.toml\\\"),\\n            \\\"[package]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"pkg-fresh\\\\\\\"\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\"1.0.0\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n[dependencies]\\\\npkg-driver = \\\\\\\"1.0.0\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\"callisto.toml\\\"),\\n            \\\"[[fixed-group]]\\\\nname = \\\\\\\"grp\\\\\\\"\\\\nmembers = [\\\\\\\"pkg-released\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"pkg-fresh\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n[cascade]\\\\nbump-severity = \\\\\\\"minor\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(root.join(\\\".changeset\\\")).unwrap();\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\".changeset/fresh-patch.md\\\"),\\n            \\\"---\\\\n\\\\\\\"pkg-fresh\\\\\\\": patch\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nfix.\\\\n\\\",\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n        std::fs::write(\\n            root.join(\\\".changeset/driver-major.md\\\"),\\n            \\\"---\\\\n\\\\\\\"pkg-driver\\\\\\\": major\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nBreaking.\\\\n\\\",\\n        )\\n        .unwrap();\\n        commit_all(root, \\\"add packages\\\");\\n        tag(root, \\\"pkg-released@1.0.0\\\");\\n\\n        let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(root);\\n        let runner = NoopRunner;\\n        let ws = Workspace::load(root.to_path_buf(), &amp;locator, &amp;runner).expect(\\\"workspace must load\\\");\\n        let inference = crate::infer::NoInference;\\n        let opts = VersionOptions {\\n            strict: false,\\n            strict_graph: false,\\n            allow_empty_changesets: true,\\n        };\\n\\n        let plan = plan_version(&amp;ws, &amp;inference, &amp;opts).expect(\\\"plan_version must succeed\\\");\\n\\n        let pkg_fresh = callisto_model::PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-fresh\\\").unwrap();\\n        let write = plan\\n            .changelog_writes\\n            .iter()\\n            .find(|w| w.input.package == pkg_fresh)\\n            .expect(\\\"pkg-fresh must have a ChangelogWrite\\\");\\n\\n        assert_eq!(write.input.entries.len(), 3, \\\"got: {:?}\\\", write.input.entries);\\n        assert!(matches!(\\n            write.input.entries[0].source,\\n            callisto_changelog::ChangeSource::Changeset { .. }\\n        ));\\n        assert!(matches!(\\n            write.input.entries[1].source,\\n            callisto_changelog::ChangeSource::DependencyUpdate { .. }\\n        ));\\n        assert!(matches!(\\n            write.input.entries[2].source,\\n            callisto_changelog::ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { .. }\\n        ));\\n    }\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_appends_new_group_member_entry_after_changeset commands::version::tests::plan_version_new_group_member_entry_is_additive_after_cascade_union\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"assertion `left == right` failed: left: 1, right: 2 (and left: 2, right: 3 for the second test) -- group_check.new_members is never consulted when building changelog_writes today.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"After T4's `let mut input = ...` block and before `changelog_writes.push(...)`, look up whether `id` appears in any group's `group_check.new_members` list and, if so, push a NewGroupMember entry as the last entry.\",\n        \"code\": \"            if let Some(group_name) = group_check\\n                .new_members\\n                .iter()\\n                .find(|(_, members)| members.contains(id))\\n                .map(|(name, _)| name.clone())\\n            {\\n                input.entries.push(ChangelogEntry {\\n                    severity: sev,\\n                    source: ChangeSource::NewGroupMember { group: group_name },\\n                });\\n            }\\n\\n            changelog_writes.push(crate::plan::ChangelogWrite {\\n                changelog_path: ch_path.clone(),\\n                input,\\n            });\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test result: ok. (all tests in commands::version::tests pass, including the two new AC-004 tests and all previously-added AC-003/AC-005/AC-006 tests)\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"feat(graph): append NewGroupMember changelog entry for fresh fixed-group members\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-004\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T6\",\n      \"title\": \"AC-002: extend pr_body.rs's per-BumpReason fallback match with Inference/PreRelease/NewGroupMember arms\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"pr_body.rs's fallback match (`if let Some(ref reason) = bump.reason { body.push_str(\\\"#### Release Reason\\\\n\\\"); match reason { ... _ =&gt; {} } }`) has no arms for Inference/PreRelease/NewGroupMember -- confirmed live, they fall to the `_ =&gt; {}` catch-all, producing an empty '#### Release Reason' heading with no content. T3/T5's version.rs changes make these reasons newly reachable for no-changelog-file packages (AC-004's group case, AC-003's inference case), so this gap is now live, not theoretical.\",\n      \"files_to_create_or_modify\": [\n        \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs\"\n      ],\n      \"test_first\": {\n        \"description\": \"Add three #[test]s inside `mod tests` in pr_body.rs, following the exact VersionPlan-construction shape of the existing `test_compose_pr_body_snapshot` test (empty `changelog_writes: vec![]` simulates 'no changelog file for that package').\",\n        \"test_code\": \"    fn plan_with_single_bump(reason: BumpReason) -&gt; VersionPlan {\\n        VersionPlan {\\n            bumps: vec![PlannedBump {\\n                package: PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-a\\\").unwrap(),\\n                from: Version::semver(1, 0, 0),\\n                to: Version::semver(1, 1, 0),\\n                severity: Severity::Minor,\\n                governed_by: None,\\n                reason: Some(reason),\\n                writes: vec![],\\n            }],\\n            rewrites: vec![],\\n            platform_writes: vec![],\\n            optional_dep_updates: vec![],\\n            changelog_writes: vec![],\\n            consumed_changesets: vec![],\\n            pre_state_update: None,\\n            delete_pre_json: None,\\n            pre_cursor_updates: vec![],\\n            observed_versions: std::collections::BTreeMap::new(),\\n            diagnostics: vec![],\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn assert_release_reason_has_content(body: &amp;str) {\\n        let start = body.find(\\\"#### Release Reason\\\").expect(\\\"must contain '#### Release Reason'\\\");\\n        let after_heading = &amp;body[start + \\\"#### Release Reason\\\".len()..];\\n        let end = after_heading.find(\\\"&lt;/details&gt;\\\").unwrap_or(after_heading.len());\\n        let section = after_heading[..end].trim();\\n        assert!(!section.is_empty(), \\\"'#### Release Reason' section must have non-whitespace content, got body: {body}\\\");\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn ac002_inference_fallback_is_non_empty() {\\n        let plan = plan_with_single_bump(BumpReason::Inference { commits: 3, remapped: false });\\n        let report = render_pr_body_from_plan(&amp;plan, &amp;PrBodyOptions::default()).unwrap();\\n        assert_release_reason_has_content(&amp;report.body);\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn ac002_prerelease_fallback_is_non_empty() {\\n        let plan = plan_with_single_bump(BumpReason::PreRelease { tag: \\\"alpha\\\".to_string() });\\n        let report = render_pr_body_from_plan(&amp;plan, &amp;PrBodyOptions::default()).unwrap();\\n        assert_release_reason_has_content(&amp;report.body);\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn ac002_new_group_member_fallback_is_non_empty() {\\n        let plan = plan_with_single_bump(BumpReason::NewGroupMember {\\n            group: callisto_model::GroupName(\\\"grp\\\".to_string()),\\n        });\\n        let report = render_pr_body_from_plan(&amp;plan, &amp;PrBodyOptions::default()).unwrap();\\n        assert_release_reason_has_content(&amp;report.body);\\n    }\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::pr_body::tests::ac002_inference_fallback_is_non_empty commands::pr_body::tests::ac002_prerelease_fallback_is_non_empty commands::pr_body::tests::ac002_new_group_member_fallback_is_non_empty\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"thread panicked at 'must contain '#### Release Reason'' -- wait, the heading IS pushed today (guarded by `if let Some(ref reason)`), so the panic is instead: 'called `Option::expect()` on a `None` value' is NOT hit, but assert_release_reason_has_content panics with ''#### Release Reason' section must have non-whitespace content' since Inference/PreRelease/NewGroupMember hit the `_ =&gt; {}` catch-all and push nothing after the heading.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"Add three new match arms to pr_body.rs's fallback match (inside `if let Some(ref reason) = bump.reason { body.push_str(\\\"#### Release Reason\\\\n\\\"); match reason { ... } }`), before the `_ =&gt; {}` catch-all.\",\n        \"code\": \"                callisto_model::BumpReason::Inference { commits, .. } =&gt; {\\n                    body.push_str(&amp;format!(\\n                        \\\"- Inferred from {commits} commit(s) since the last release.\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n                    ));\\n                }\\n                callisto_model::BumpReason::PreRelease { tag } =&gt; {\\n                    body.push_str(&amp;format!(\\n                        \\\"- Pre-release finalization (tag `{tag}`).\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n                    ));\\n                }\\n                callisto_model::BumpReason::NewGroupMember { group } =&gt; {\\n                    body.push_str(&amp;format!(\\n                        \\\"- New member of group `{}`.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\n                        group.as_str()\\n                    ));\\n                }\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::pr_body::tests\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test result: ok. (ac002_inference_fallback_is_non_empty, ac002_prerelease_fallback_is_non_empty, ac002_new_group_member_fallback_is_non_empty, and the pre-existing test_compose_pr_body_snapshot/test_compose_pr_body_custom_branch_override all pass)\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"feat(graph): extend pr_body fallback with Inference/PreRelease/NewGroupMember arms\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-002\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T7\",\n      \"title\": \"AC-001: dispatch to render_section when a matching ChangelogWrite renders successfully, falling back otherwise\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"pr_body.rs currently always uses its own hand-rolled per-BumpReason match, never calling callisto_changelog::render_section, even though VersionPlan.changelog_writes already carries a fully-built ChangelogInput for every package with a changelog file. render_section itself emits a '## &lt;version&gt;' heading (not '#### Release Reason'), so the dispatch path must still push '#### Release Reason' as our own heading before pushing render_section's raw output, to satisfy AC-001's 'contains, verbatim, section' requirement while still producing a well-formed collapsible block.\",\n      \"files_to_create_or_modify\": [\n        \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs\"\n      ],\n      \"test_first\": {\n        \"description\": \"Add one #[test] inside `mod tests` in pr_body.rs, per AC-001's exact test method: a bump whose `reason` is `Some(BumpReason::Cascade{..})` (so the fallback Cascade arm, if reached, would produce 'Automatic dependency cascade triggered by') AND a matching ChangelogWrite built the same way version.rs builds it.\",\n        \"test_code\": \"    #[test]\\n    fn ac001_render_section_takes_priority_over_fallback_when_both_available() {\\n        let pkg_a = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-a\\\").unwrap();\\n        let bump = PlannedBump {\\n            package: pkg_a.clone(),\\n            from: Version::semver(1, 0, 0),\\n            to: Version::semver(1, 1, 0),\\n            severity: Severity::Minor,\\n            governed_by: None,\\n            reason: Some(BumpReason::Cascade {\\n                via: PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-core\\\").unwrap(),\\n                dep_kind: callisto_model::DepKind::Runtime,\\n                spec: \\\"^1.0.0\\\".to_string(),\\n                dependency_to: Version::semver(2, 0, 0),\\n            }),\\n            writes: vec![],\\n        };\\n\\n        let input = callisto_changelog::ChangelogInput {\\n            package: pkg_a.clone(),\\n            from: Version::semver(1, 0, 0),\\n            to: Some(Version::semver(1, 1, 0)),\\n            entries: vec![callisto_changelog::ChangelogEntry {\\n                severity: Severity::Minor,\\n                source: callisto_changelog::ChangeSource::Changeset {\\n                    filename: \\\"swift-foxes.md\\\".to_string(),\\n                    summary: \\\"A real changeset summary.\\\".to_string(),\\n                },\\n            }],\\n        };\\n        let expected_section = callisto_changelog::render_section(&amp;input).unwrap();\\n\\n        let plan = VersionPlan {\\n            bumps: vec![bump],\\n            rewrites: vec![],\\n            platform_writes: vec![],\\n            optional_dep_updates: vec![],\\n            changelog_writes: vec![crate::plan::ChangelogWrite {\\n                changelog_path: std::path::PathBuf::from(\\\"CHANGELOG.md\\\"),\\n                input,\\n            }],\\n            consumed_changesets: vec![],\\n            pre_state_update: None,\\n            delete_pre_json: None,\\n            pre_cursor_updates: vec![],\\n            observed_versions: std::collections::BTreeMap::new(),\\n            diagnostics: vec![],\\n        };\\n\\n        let report = render_pr_body_from_plan(&amp;plan, &amp;PrBodyOptions::default()).unwrap();\\n\\n        assert!(\\n            report.body.contains(&amp;expected_section),\\n            \\\"body must contain render_section's verbatim output; body: {}\\\",\\n            report.body\\n        );\\n        assert!(\\n            !report.body.contains(\\\"Automatic dependency cascade triggered by\\\"),\\n            \\\"body must NOT contain the fallback Cascade text when render_section succeeded; body: {}\\\",\\n            report.body\\n        );\\n    }\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::pr_body::tests::ac001_render_section_takes_priority_over_fallback_when_both_available\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"thread panicked at 'body must contain render_section's verbatim output' -- render_pr_body_from_plan never calls render_section today; the fallback Cascade arm text 'Automatic dependency cascade triggered by' is present instead.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"Before the existing `if let Some(ref reason) = bump.reason { body.push_str(\\\"#### Release Reason\\\\n\\\"); match reason {...} }` block in the package-details loop, look up a matching ChangelogWrite by package id and try render_section; on success, push the heading + verbatim section and skip the fallback. Guard the existing fallback block with `if !rendered`.\",\n        \"code\": \"        let matching_write = plan\\n            .changelog_writes\\n            .iter()\\n            .find(|w| w.input.package == bump.package);\\n\\n        let mut rendered = false;\\n        if let Some(w) = matching_write {\\n            if let Ok(section) = callisto_changelog::render_section(&amp;w.input) {\\n                body.push_str(\\\"#### Release Reason\\\\n\\\");\\n                body.push_str(&amp;section);\\n                body.push('\\\\n');\\n                rendered = true;\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        if !rendered {\\n            if let Some(ref reason) = bump.reason {\\n                body.push_str(\\\"#### Release Reason\\\\n\\\");\\n                match reason {\\n                    // ...existing 5 arms plus T6's 3 new arms, unchanged...\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::pr_body::tests\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test result: ok. (ac001_render_section_takes_priority_over_fallback_when_both_available passes; test_compose_pr_body_snapshot's insta snapshot is unaffected since that test's plan.changelog_writes is empty, so matching_write is always None for it, taking the unchanged fallback path)\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"feat(graph): dispatch to render_section ahead of the per-BumpReason fallback in pr_body\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-001\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T8\",\n      \"title\": \"AC-007: render_section errors and reason:None both fall through to a working fallback\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"T7's `if !rendered { if let Some(ref reason) = bump.reason { ... } }` already handles render_section Err(..) correctly (rendered stays false, fallback match runs) -- but when `bump.reason` is also None, nothing is pushed at all today (no heading, no content), which fails AC-007(3)'s requirement of the literal '_No changelog entries available._' line. Restructure the inner block to always push the heading once the fallback path is reached, and handle reason:None explicitly.\",\n      \"files_to_create_or_modify\": [\n        \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs\"\n      ],\n      \"test_first\": {\n        \"description\": \"Add three #[test]s inside `mod tests` in pr_body.rs per AC-007's exact test method, using deliberately-invalid ChangelogWrite inputs to trigger EmptyInput and SeverityNoneEntry.\",\n        \"test_code\": \"    #[test]\\n    fn ac007_empty_entries_falls_back_and_other_package_renders_normally() {\\n        let pkg_a = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-a\\\").unwrap();\\n        let pkg_b = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-b\\\").unwrap();\\n\\n        let bump_a = PlannedBump {\\n            package: pkg_a.clone(),\\n            from: Version::semver(1, 0, 0),\\n            to: Version::semver(1, 1, 0),\\n            severity: Severity::Minor,\\n            governed_by: None,\\n            reason: Some(BumpReason::Cascade {\\n                via: PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-core\\\").unwrap(),\\n                dep_kind: callisto_model::DepKind::Runtime,\\n                spec: \\\"^1.0.0\\\".to_string(),\\n                dependency_to: Version::semver(2, 0, 0),\\n            }),\\n            writes: vec![],\\n        };\\n        let bump_b = PlannedBump {\\n            package: pkg_b.clone(),\\n            from: Version::semver(1, 0, 0),\\n            to: Version::semver(1, 0, 1),\\n            severity: Severity::Patch,\\n            governed_by: None,\\n            reason: Some(BumpReason::Changeset { changesets: vec![\\\"fix-1\\\".to_string()] }),\\n            writes: vec![],\\n        };\\n\\n        let good_input = callisto_changelog::ChangelogInput {\\n            package: pkg_b.clone(),\\n            from: Version::semver(1, 0, 0),\\n            to: Some(Version::semver(1, 0, 1)),\\n            entries: vec![callisto_changelog::ChangelogEntry {\\n                severity: Severity::Patch,\\n                source: callisto_changelog::ChangeSource::Changeset {\\n                    filename: \\\"fix-1.md\\\".to_string(),\\n                    summary: \\\"A fix.\\\".to_string(),\\n                },\\n            }],\\n        };\\n        let expected_section = callisto_changelog::render_section(&amp;good_input).unwrap();\\n\\n        let plan = VersionPlan {\\n            bumps: vec![bump_a, bump_b],\\n            rewrites: vec![],\\n            platform_writes: vec![],\\n            optional_dep_updates: vec![],\\n            changelog_writes: vec![\\n                crate::plan::ChangelogWrite {\\n                    changelog_path: std::path::PathBuf::from(\\\"CHANGELOG.md\\\"),\\n                    input: callisto_changelog::ChangelogInput {\\n                        package: pkg_a.clone(),\\n                        from: Version::semver(1, 0, 0),\\n                        to: Some(Version::semver(1, 1, 0)),\\n                        entries: vec![],\\n                    },\\n                },\\n                crate::plan::ChangelogWrite {\\n                    changelog_path: std::path::PathBuf::from(\\\"CHANGELOG.md\\\"),\\n                    input: good_input,\\n                },\\n            ],\\n            consumed_changesets: vec![],\\n            pre_state_update: None,\\n            delete_pre_json: None,\\n            pre_cursor_updates: vec![],\\n            observed_versions: std::collections::BTreeMap::new(),\\n            diagnostics: vec![],\\n        };\\n\\n        let report = render_pr_body_from_plan(&amp;plan, &amp;PrBodyOptions::default()).unwrap();\\n        assert!(\\n            report.body.contains(\\\"Automatic dependency cascade triggered by\\\"),\\n            \\\"pkg-a must use the AC-002 fallback text since its ChangelogWrite has empty entries; body: {}\\\",\\n            report.body\\n        );\\n        assert!(\\n            report.body.contains(&amp;expected_section),\\n            \\\"pkg-b must still render normally via render_section; body: {}\\\",\\n            report.body\\n        );\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn ac007_severity_none_entry_falls_back() {\\n        let pkg_a = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-a\\\").unwrap();\\n        let bump_a = PlannedBump {\\n            package: pkg_a.clone(),\\n            from: Version::semver(1, 0, 0),\\n            to: Version::semver(1, 1, 0),\\n            severity: Severity::Minor,\\n            governed_by: None,\\n            reason: Some(BumpReason::Cascade {\\n                via: PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-core\\\").unwrap(),\\n                dep_kind: callisto_model::DepKind::Runtime,\\n                spec: \\\"^1.0.0\\\".to_string(),\\n                dependency_to: Version::semver(2, 0, 0),\\n            }),\\n            writes: vec![],\\n        };\\n        let plan = VersionPlan {\\n            bumps: vec![bump_a],\\n            rewrites: vec![],\\n            platform_writes: vec![],\\n            optional_dep_updates: vec![],\\n            changelog_writes: vec![crate::plan::ChangelogWrite {\\n                changelog_path: std::path::PathBuf::from(\\\"CHANGELOG.md\\\"),\\n                input: callisto_changelog::ChangelogInput {\\n                    package: pkg_a.clone(),\\n                    from: Version::semver(1, 0, 0),\\n                    to: Some(Version::semver(1, 1, 0)),\\n                    entries: vec![callisto_changelog::ChangelogEntry {\\n                        severity: Severity::None,\\n                        source: callisto_changelog::ChangeSource::Changeset {\\n                            filename: \\\"x.md\\\".to_string(),\\n                            summary: \\\"whatever\\\".to_string(),\\n                        },\\n                    }],\\n                },\\n            }],\\n            consumed_changesets: vec![],\\n            pre_state_update: None,\\n            delete_pre_json: None,\\n            pre_cursor_updates: vec![],\\n            observed_versions: std::collections::BTreeMap::new(),\\n            diagnostics: vec![],\\n        };\\n\\n        let report = render_pr_body_from_plan(&amp;plan, &amp;PrBodyOptions::default()).unwrap();\\n        assert!(\\n            report.body.contains(\\\"Automatic dependency cascade triggered by\\\"),\\n            \\\"body: {}\\\",\\n            report.body\\n        );\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn ac007_empty_entries_and_no_reason_uses_no_changelog_entries_literal() {\\n        let pkg_a = PackageId::parse(\\\"pkg-a\\\").unwrap();\\n        let bump_a = PlannedBump {\\n            package: pkg_a.clone(),\\n            from: Version::semver(1, 0, 0),\\n            to: Version::semver(1, 1, 0),\\n            severity: Severity::Minor,\\n            governed_by: None,\\n            reason: None,\\n            writes: vec![],\\n        };\\n        let plan = VersionPlan {\\n            bumps: vec![bump_a],\\n            rewrites: vec![],\\n            platform_writes: vec![],\\n            optional_dep_updates: vec![],\\n            changelog_writes: vec![crate::plan::ChangelogWrite {\\n                changelog_path: std::path::PathBuf::from(\\\"CHANGELOG.md\\\"),\\n                input: callisto_changelog::ChangelogInput {\\n                    package: pkg_a.clone(),\\n                    from: Version::semver(1, 0, 0),\\n                    to: Some(Version::semver(1, 1, 0)),\\n                    entries: vec![],\\n                },\\n            }],\\n            consumed_changesets: vec![],\\n            pre_state_update: None,\\n            delete_pre_json: None,\\n            pre_cursor_updates: vec![],\\n            observed_versions: std::collections::BTreeMap::new(),\\n            diagnostics: vec![],\\n        };\\n\\n        let report = render_pr_body_from_plan(&amp;plan, &amp;PrBodyOptions::default()).unwrap();\\n        assert!(\\n            report.body.contains(\\\"_No changelog entries available._\\\"),\\n            \\\"body: {}\\\",\\n            report.body\\n        );\\n    }\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::pr_body::tests::ac007_empty_entries_falls_back_and_other_package_renders_normally commands::pr_body::tests::ac007_severity_none_entry_falls_back commands::pr_body::tests::ac007_empty_entries_and_no_reason_uses_no_changelog_entries_literal\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"thread panicked at 'body: ...' (ac007_empty_entries_and_no_reason_uses_no_changelog_entries_literal fails: today the block is entirely skipped when bump.reason is None, so no '#### Release Reason' heading and no '_No changelog entries available._' line appear at all). The first two tests pass already once T7 lands (documented here to lock the Err(..) fallback behavior against regression before restructuring).\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"Replace T7's `if !rendered { if let Some(ref reason) = bump.reason { body.push_str(\\\"#### Release Reason\\\\n\\\"); match reason {...} } }` with a version that always pushes the heading in the fallback path and explicitly handles `bump.reason == None`.\",\n        \"code\": \"        if !rendered {\\n            body.push_str(\\\"#### Release Reason\\\\n\\\");\\n            match &amp;bump.reason {\\n                Some(reason) =&gt; match reason {\\n                    // ...existing 5 arms plus T6's 3 new arms, unchanged...\\n                },\\n                None =&gt; {\\n                    body.push_str(\\\"_No changelog entries available._\\\\n\\\\n\\\");\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\"\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::pr_body::tests\",\n      \"expected_pass_output\": \"test result: ok. (all pr_body::tests pass: ac007_empty_entries_falls_back_and_other_package_renders_normally, ac007_severity_none_entry_falls_back, ac007_empty_entries_and_no_reason_uses_no_changelog_entries_literal, ac001_render_section_takes_priority_over_fallback_when_both_available, ac002_inference_fallback_is_non_empty, ac002_prerelease_fallback_is_non_empty, ac002_new_group_member_fallback_is_non_empty, test_compose_pr_body_snapshot, test_compose_pr_body_custom_branch_override)\",\n      \"verify_full_suite_command\": \"just ci\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"fix(graph): fall through to fallback rendering on render_section errors and reason:None\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-007\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nSummary of what I verified against live code before writing each task (all under `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto`):\n\n- `crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs:223-236` — confirmed `BumpReason::Inference` construction discards `outcome.commits`.\n- `crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs:256-286` — confirmed `BumpReason::Inference` has no field for commit data, forcing the side-channel design in T2.\n- `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:87-94,148-215` — confirmed the exact if/else, catch-all (line 188), and `group_check` availability before the changelog-writes loop.\n- `crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:17-89` — confirmed `GroupCheckOutcome.new_members` shape.\n- `crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:416-442,489-500` — confirmed the fixed-group convergence overwrite condition and the `sev &gt; cur_sev` raise gate.\n- `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/pr_body.rs` — confirmed the fallback match's `_ =&gt; {}` catch-all and the absence of any `render_section` call.\n- `crates/callisto-changelog/src/render.rs`, `error.rs` — confirmed `render_section`'s heading behavior and `ChangelogError::{EmptyInput, SeverityNoneEntry}`.\n- `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/resolve.rs:106,289-294`, `raw.rs:50` — confirmed `[cascade] bump-severity` config knob, used to force cascade severity above a Patch changeset in T4/T5's fixtures.\n- `crates/callisto-graph/tests/version_tests.rs:52-127` — reused this already-working real-git cascade fixture pattern for T4/T5.\n\nKey deviation from the user's rough ordering: I moved AC-004 after AC-005 (not before), because AC-004's own second test method asserts a `DependencyUpdate` entry that only exists once AC-005's changeset+cascade union logic is implemented — sequencing them as originally suggested would have made that test unimplementable, exactly the kind of AC-004/AC-005 interaction bug this spec's adversarial rounds caught repeatedly.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>122424</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>42</tool_uses><duration_ms>551640</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
