{"parentUuid":"0f3ff029-eb57-45ef-9bad-9bc349f84982","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeFBnZ5gQuv4d4MPxtCNQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Given 341 commits across 9 crates spanning ~15 tracks, I'll delegate the drafting to a fork — it can read the full commit history without cluttering this session, and it already has this conversation's context (including everything in `ACTIVE.md`)."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":432,"cache_read_input_tokens":288796,"output_tokens":5085,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2730},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":432,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5085,"cache_read_input_tokens":288796,"cache_creation_input_tokens":432,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":432},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeFBnXCKUPCci6ypfRbjt","type":"assistant","uuid":"4a8d8c81-8e30-4ad6-8971-5a19b27ab762","timestamp":"2026-08-21T03:31:18.244Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"4a8d8c81-8e30-4ad6-8971-5a19b27ab762","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeFBnZ5gQuv4d4MPxtCNQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RWgEqoxqRkpMpz8wUbE9vF","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"fork","name":"changeset-draft","description":"Draft comprehensive changeset for unreleased work","prompt":"The user asked to make sure there's an appropriate changeset covering ALL unreleased work in this repo (they confirmed via AskUserQuestion: \"Everything since last release (Recommended)\" — comprehensive, not scoped to just Track 4/5/6).\n\n## Background you already have\nYou've inherited this full conversation, which includes `.claude/plans/ACTIVE.md`'s full content read earlier in this session — it has detailed, already-written track-by-track summaries for: Track B, Track E, Track F, Track G, Spec A (manifest persist split), Spec B (apply write-batching), post-Track-G 8-bug remediation, Track 3a/3b1, Track 3a, Track 6-doc/8-doc, Track 1 (fixed-group cascade), Track 2 (platform-manifest writes), Track 9 (cascade rewrite keys), Track 4 (release-pipeline contract), Track 6-mechanical (JSON report shapes), Track 5 (changelog/PR-body consolidation, just completed). Use those descriptions as your primary source — they're already accurate and reviewed; you don't need to re-derive every fact from scratch, but DO verify specifics you're unsure about by reading the actual diffs/commits.\n\n## Task\n1. The last real release commit is `f40d87b8` (\"chore(release): version packages (#4)\"). Everything after it (341 commits, `git log --oneline f40d87b8..HEAD`) is unreleased.\n2. Touched crates (confirmed via `git diff --stat f40d87b8..HEAD -- crates/`): callisto-model, callisto-graph, callisto-cli, callisto-manifests, callisto-changelog, callisto-format, callisto-conventional, callisto-vcs, callisto-moon. NOT callisto-fixtures (untouched).\n3. Read `git log --oneline --no-merges f40d87b8..HEAD` in full and skim diffs/commit bodies as needed to fill in anything ACTIVE.md doesn't cover (ACTIVE.md is thorough but covers the *canon-pipeline* tracks in detail — there are also many smaller ungated fixes in the log, e.g. commits like `fix(cli): status --check returns exit code 1 when changesets pending`, `fix(graph): honor pre-release flag and bare-name config in aggregate`, `fix(model): correct PEP 440 is_prerelease and VersionReq normalization`, `feat(publish): package filter, registry resolution, subprocess hardening`, security fixes like `fix(ci): prevent shell injection in callisto-action`, etc. — these need to be captured too, not just the big canon tracks).\n4. Note: `version.workspace = true` is used by every crate (all share one workspace version number in `Cargo.toml`'s `[workspace.package] version = \"0.3.3\"`), so the actual emitted version will be governed by the single highest severity across all changeset entries — but changesets are still declared per-package (matching this repo's own existing changeset format), so assign per-package severity based on that package's own actual changes, not a pre-decided uniform level.\n5. Determine per-package severity (major/minor/patch) for: callisto-model, callisto-graph, callisto-cli, callisto-manifests, callisto-changelog, callisto-format, callisto-conventional, callisto-vcs, callisto-moon. Use real semver judgment:\n   - MAJOR: breaking public API changes (e.g. `CascadeInput` gained a required field per Track 9 — ACTIVE.md flags this explicitly as \"a semver-breaking public API change, expected and accepted\"; `Manifest::persist` promoted to a required trait method per Spec A; JSON report field renames — `valid`→`ok`, `pr_body`→`body`, `created_tags`→`tags` — which are breaking for any consumer of that JSON shape, e.g. the shipped GitHub Action).\n   - MINOR: new features/additive capability (e.g. the new `callisto matrix` command and its full napi/maturin discovery pipeline — Track G; new diagnostic codes; new report fields that are purely additive).\n   - PATCH: bug fixes, correctness fixes, performance improvements, hardening that don't change the public contract.\n   Note this repo's OWN prior changeset (`git show 37d2d93e -- .changeset` — read it for exact format/tone reference) used uniform \"patch\" across all 5 touched crates for a batch of security+correctness+performance fixes with NO new features and NO breaking changes — that's the calibration baseline for what counts as \"patch\" here. This session's work includes real new features (matrix command) and real breaking API/wire-format changes, so do NOT default to uniform patch — use real judgment per package.\n6. Write ONE changeset file at `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.changeset/<kebab-case-slug>.md` in this exact format (frontmatter block of `package: bump-level` pairs for every touched package, blank line, then a Markdown body with a top-level `# <title>` and `##` category sections — mirror `37d2d93e`'s style: Security / Correctness / Performance / Features / Housekeeping / Breaking Changes as applicable, each bullet bolded-lead-in with the crate name in parens, written for a human reader of CHANGELOG.md, not a commit-message dump). Do NOT create multiple changeset files — one comprehensive file covering everything, matching how the prior real release did it.\n7. Before finalizing, sanity-check the frontmatter package list against `crates/*/Cargo.toml`'s `[package] name = \"...\"` values (changeset package keys must match the real Cargo package names exactly, not directory names, in case they differ).\n8. Do NOT run `callisto version`, `callisto publish`, or any other callisto command against this repo — this session's own Pipeline Protocol (in ACTIVE.md and CLAUDE.md) forbids running callisto commands against itself. Just write the changeset markdown file directly with the Write tool.\n9. Verify the file's frontmatter is valid YAML-ish (matches the exact `---\\npkg: level\\n---\\n` format from the reference example) by reading it back after writing.\n\n## Report back\nEnd with a concise summary (under 250 words): the file path, the per-package severity you assigned and one-line why for each, and any commit(s) you found that ACTIVE.md didn't already cover and had to research directly."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":432,"cache_read_input_tokens":288796,"output_tokens":5085,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2730},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":432,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5085,"cache_read_input_tokens":288796,"cache_creation_input_tokens":432,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":432},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeFBnXCKUPCci6ypfRbjt","type":"assistant","uuid":"96975970-bd8f-46e0-940a-ffe61012fd84","timestamp":"2026-08-21T03:31:41.421Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
