{"parentUuid":"faae3c9c-9090-4ceb-aa7e-4e176e901a22","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeFC8iqrsN1B1qeo6kwBo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V54RDvAurd2j7q8fzWYWNx","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.changeset/release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1493,"cache_read_input_tokens":294779,"output_tokens":167,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":63},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1493,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":167,"cache_read_input_tokens":294779,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1493,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1493},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeFC8gj7eddakyWrGQ6Jj","type":"assistant","uuid":"f10c3245-4d68-4f73-bc55-ea62bdb8c345","timestamp":"2026-08-21T03:35:19.154Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"f10c3245-4d68-4f73-bc55-ea62bdb8c345","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"83900f18-e6bb-498c-b6ae-80718baa4f9c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V54RDvAurd2j7q8fzWYWNx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tcallisto-model: major\n3\tcallisto-graph: major\n4\tcallisto-cli: major\n5\tcallisto-manifests: major\n6\tcallisto-conventional: major\n7\tcallisto-vcs: minor\n8\tcallisto-moon: patch\n9\tcallisto-changelog: patch\n10\tcallisto-format: patch\n11\t---\n12\t\n13\t# Release pipeline correctness, `callisto matrix`, and cross-ecosystem identity hardening\n14\t\n15\tA large batch of work spanning version/cascade correctness, a new platform-target discovery\n16\tcommand, JSON wire-contract fixes, security hardening, and cross-ecosystem identity resolution.\n17\t\n18\t## Breaking Changes\n19\t\n20\t- **`CascadeInput` gained two new required fields** (`callisto-graph`): `tags: &TagIndex` and\n21\t  `identity: &IdentityIndex`. Any external construction site must supply both.\n22\t- **`Manifest::persist` promoted to a required trait method** (`callisto-manifests`): manifest\n23\t  mutation methods (`write_version`, `update_dependency_spec`, `update_optional_dependencies`) are\n24\t  now pure in-memory mutations; callers must invoke `persist()` explicitly. Any external `Manifest`\n25\t  implementor must now provide `persist`.\n26\t- **JSON report field renames** (`callisto-model`, surfaced through `callisto-cli --format json`):\n27\t  `ValidateReport.valid` → `ok`, `ComposePrBodyReport.pr_body` → `body`,\n28\t  `TagReport.created_tags` → `tags` (plus a new `already_existed: bool` field). `StatusReport` gained\n29\t  `hasChangesets`, `lastReleasedVersion`, and `releaseTrigger`. Consumers parsing these JSON shapes\n30\t  (including the shipped GitHub Action) must update field references.\n31\t- **`callisto-conventional` decoupled from `callisto-vcs`**: `fetch_commits`/`infer_severity` now\n32\t  take `&dyn callisto_model::CommitWalker` instead of `(&dyn CommandRunner, &Path)`;\n33\t  `ConventionalError::Vcs` renamed to `ConventionalError::CommitWalk`.\n34\t- **`PublishTarget::Npm.restricted: bool` replaced with `access: Option<NpmAccess>`**\n35\t  (`callisto-model`): npm's real 3-valued `publishConfig.access` (absent / public / restricted) was\n36\t  previously collapsed into a boolean, silently dropping explicit `\"public\"` on unscoped packages.\n37\t- **`PackageIdParseError` gained a new `LeadingHyphen` variant** (`callisto-model`), split out from\n38\t  the previously inaccurate `PathTraversal` error reported for inputs with no `..` at all.\n39\t\n40\t## Features\n41\t\n42\t- **New `callisto matrix [--package <name>]` command** (`callisto-cli`, `callisto-graph`,\n43\t  `callisto-model`): discovers napi and maturin platform targets from `package.json`/`pyproject.toml`,\n44\t  produces a per-triple CI table (host runner, cross-compilation flag, artifact name), and reports\n45\t  `engines.node`/`requires-python` runtime versions, with diagnostics for conflicting or unrecognised\n46\t  targets.\n47\t- **Real platform-manifest and `optionalDependencies` planning** (`callisto-graph`): `plan_version`\n48\t  now computes real `PlatformWrite`/`OptionalDepUpdate` entries for a bumped owner's platform-manifest\n49\t  siblings in a Fixed group, instead of leaving those fields silently empty.\n50\t- **Fixed-group cascade convergence** (`callisto-graph`): siblings in a Fixed group now converge on a\n51\t  shared group-aligned target instead of bumping independently from their own base version, closing a\n52\t  silent version-divergence bug.\n53\t- **Cross-ecosystem and workspace-membership-aware package discovery** (`callisto-graph`): Cargo/npm/\n54\t  pnpm workspace membership globs are now honored (previously-excluded fuzz targets/scratch examples\n55\t  are no longer discovered as release-managed packages); same-named packages in different ecosystems\n56\t  (e.g. a Rust crate and its Python binding) resolve via promotion instead of erroring; `cargo:foo`/\n57\t  `npm:foo` ecosystem-prefixed group-member spellings now work.\n58\t- **Changelog/PR-body rendering consolidation** (`callisto-graph`): PR bodies now reuse the same\n59\t  `render_section` renderer CHANGELOG.md uses; inference-driven and new-fixed-group-member bumps get\n60\t  real changelog entries instead of a generic fallback; a package with multiple contributing causes\n61\t  (e.g. a changeset plus a cascade) now gets a union of entries instead of dropping all but one.\n62\t\n63\t## Security\n64\t\n65\t- Package names are validated before being passed to `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish`,\n66\t  closing an argument-injection vector (`callisto-graph`).\n67\t- `publishConfig.registry` for npm packages is now validated against an approved allowlist,\n68\t  preventing SSRF via a malicious registry URL (`callisto-graph`).\n69\t- The shipped GitHub Action no longer interpolates untrusted expressions directly into shell steps.\n70\t- Credentials are now redacted from git/registry-CLI subprocess stderr before being embedded in error\n71\t  messages (`callisto-vcs`, `callisto-model`, `callisto-graph`).\n72\t- Subprocess stdout/stderr capture is now bounded, preventing a memory-exhaustion DoS from a\n73\t  misbehaving child process (`callisto-cli`).\n74\t- Tag names with a leading hyphen are now rejected and shelled tag refs are qualified, closing a\n75\t  git-argument-injection vector (`callisto-vcs`, `callisto-model`).\n76\t\n77\t## Correctness\n78\t\n79\t- `callisto tag` no longer fabricates `CreatedTag.sha` when a tag already exists at a different\n80\t  commit — the real target is resolved via `git rev-parse`, in both apply and `--dry-run` modes.\n81\t- The shipped GitHub Action's `status --check` exit-code branching now matches the CLI's real\n82\t  contract (1 = pending, 2 = none pending) — the release-PR creation path was previously unreachable\n83\t  on every real run.\n84\t- `plan_publish` now reads back `CHANGELOG.md`'s real section instead of hardcoding\n85\t  `changelog_section: None`.\n86\t- A topological git revwalk crossing the `since` boundary before visiting all merged-branch commits\n87\t  no longer silently drops those commits from `commits_since_with_pathspec` (`callisto-vcs`).\n88\t- `apply_version_plan` is now idempotent, stages an npm lockfile refresh, and persists manifest writes\n89\t  correctly per loop instead of risking a lost write.\n90\t- Same-path manifest writes are now batched into one open/mutate/persist cycle with strict per-group\n91\t  sequential processing, closing a stale-handle-clobber data-loss hazard.\n92\t- Peer-dependency escalation now respects the real cascading severity instead of always escalating to\n93\t  Major.\n94\t- PEP 440 `is_prerelease`/`VersionReq` normalization corrected (`callisto-model`); Cargo caret-range\n95\t  coverage now correctly excludes pre-release versions (`callisto-format`).\n96\t- Duplicate diagnostic codes resolved across `callisto-model`/`callisto-format`/`callisto-graph` —\n97\t  several distinct error conditions previously shared the same machine-readable code.\n98\t- `GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership` is now actually detected when two differently-spelled\n99\t  group-member strings resolve to the same package across two groups.\n100\t- Numerous smaller fixes: BREAKING CHANGE commit-footer parsing, Python dependency-name PEP 503\n101\t  normalization, npm workspace package-manager auto-detection (pnpm/yarn/bun/npm), Cargo compound\n102\t  dependency-range rewriting, workspace-inherited-version publish guard, and more.\n103\t\n104\t## Performance\n105\t\n106\t- A single shared `GitAccess` is now reused across `status`, `plan_snapshot`, `plan_publish`, and\n107\t  `plan_version` instead of rediscovering the repository per package or per command.\n108\t- Tag existence checks now use the cached `TagIndex` instead of a per-release lookup.\n109\t- Each platform manifest is now parsed once and shared across extraction paths in `callisto matrix`.\n110\t\n111\t## Housekeeping\n112\t\n113\t- Numerous documentation corrections (design/spec docs, ARCHITECTURE.md, README.md) to match shipped\n114\t  behavior, including error-code completeness and previously-stale \"not implemented\" claims.\n115\t- Workspace dependency hygiene: several dependencies centralized to `workspace.dependencies`; an\n116\t  unused AGPL dev-dependency removed from Layer 1 crates.\n117\t"}]},"uuid":"c9707047-538f-4602-b4c1-8bc90ed26725","timestamp":"2026-08-21T03:35:19.208Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.changeset/release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening.md","content":"---\ncallisto-model: major\ncallisto-graph: major\ncallisto-cli: major\ncallisto-manifests: major\ncallisto-conventional: major\ncallisto-vcs: minor\ncallisto-moon: patch\ncallisto-changelog: patch\ncallisto-format: patch\n---\n\n# Release pipeline correctness, `callisto matrix`, and cross-ecosystem identity hardening\n\nA large batch of work spanning version/cascade correctness, a new platform-target discovery\ncommand, JSON wire-contract fixes, security hardening, and cross-ecosystem identity resolution.\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\n- **`CascadeInput` gained two new required fields** (`callisto-graph`): `tags: &TagIndex` and\n  `identity: &IdentityIndex`. Any external construction site must supply both.\n- **`Manifest::persist` promoted to a required trait method** (`callisto-manifests`): manifest\n  mutation methods (`write_version`, `update_dependency_spec`, `update_optional_dependencies`) are\n  now pure in-memory mutations; callers must invoke `persist()` explicitly. Any external `Manifest`\n  implementor must now provide `persist`.\n- **JSON report field renames** (`callisto-model`, surfaced through `callisto-cli --format json`):\n  `ValidateReport.valid` → `ok`, `ComposePrBodyReport.pr_body` → `body`,\n  `TagReport.created_tags` → `tags` (plus a new `already_existed: bool` field). `StatusReport` gained\n  `hasChangesets`, `lastReleasedVersion`, and `releaseTrigger`. Consumers parsing these JSON shapes\n  (including the shipped GitHub Action) must update field references.\n- **`callisto-conventional` decoupled from `callisto-vcs`**: `fetch_commits`/`infer_severity` now\n  take `&dyn callisto_model::CommitWalker` instead of `(&dyn CommandRunner, &Path)`;\n  `ConventionalError::Vcs` renamed to `ConventionalError::CommitWalk`.\n- **`PublishTarget::Npm.restricted: bool` replaced with `access: Option<NpmAccess>`**\n  (`callisto-model`): npm's real 3-valued `publishConfig.access` (absent / public / restricted) was\n  previously collapsed into a boolean, silently dropping explicit `\"public\"` on unscoped packages.\n- **`PackageIdParseError` gained a new `LeadingHyphen` variant** (`callisto-model`), split out from\n  the previously inaccurate `PathTraversal` error reported for inputs with no `..` at all.\n\n## Features\n\n- **New `callisto matrix [--package <name>]` command** (`callisto-cli`, `callisto-graph`,\n  `callisto-model`): discovers napi and maturin platform targets from `package.json`/`pyproject.toml`,\n  produces a per-triple CI table (host runner, cross-compilation flag, artifact name), and reports\n  `engines.node`/`requires-python` runtime versions, with diagnostics for conflicting or unrecognised\n  targets.\n- **Real platform-manifest and `optionalDependencies` planning** (`callisto-graph`): `plan_version`\n  now computes real `PlatformWrite`/`OptionalDepUpdate` entries for a bumped owner's platform-manifest\n  siblings in a Fixed group, instead of leaving those fields silently empty.\n- **Fixed-group cascade convergence** (`callisto-graph`): siblings in a Fixed group now converge on a\n  shared group-aligned target instead of bumping independently from their own base version, closing a\n  silent version-divergence bug.\n- **Cross-ecosystem and workspace-membership-aware package discovery** (`callisto-graph`): Cargo/npm/\n  pnpm workspace membership globs are now honored (previously-excluded fuzz targets/scratch examples\n  are no longer discovered as release-managed packages); same-named packages in different ecosystems\n  (e.g. a Rust crate and its Python binding) resolve via promotion instead of erroring; `cargo:foo`/\n  `npm:foo` ecosystem-prefixed group-member spellings now work.\n- **Changelog/PR-body rendering consolidation** (`callisto-graph`): PR bodies now reuse the same\n  `render_section` renderer CHANGELOG.md uses; inference-driven and new-fixed-group-member bumps get\n  real changelog entries instead of a generic fallback; a package with multiple contributing causes\n  (e.g. a changeset plus a cascade) now gets a union of entries instead of dropping all but one.\n\n## Security\n\n- Package names are validated before being passed to `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish`,\n  closing an argument-injection vector (`callisto-graph`).\n- `publishConfig.registry` for npm packages is now validated against an approved allowlist,\n  preventing SSRF via a malicious registry URL (`callisto-graph`).\n- The shipped GitHub Action no longer interpolates untrusted expressions directly into shell steps.\n- Credentials are now redacted from git/registry-CLI subprocess stderr before being embedded in error\n  messages (`callisto-vcs`, `callisto-model`, `callisto-graph`).\n- Subprocess stdout/stderr capture is now bounded, preventing a memory-exhaustion DoS from a\n  misbehaving child process (`callisto-cli`).\n- Tag names with a leading hyphen are now rejected and shelled tag refs are qualified, closing a\n  git-argument-injection vector (`callisto-vcs`, `callisto-model`).\n\n## Correctness\n\n- `callisto tag` no longer fabricates `CreatedTag.sha` when a tag already exists at a different\n  commit — the real target is resolved via `git rev-parse`, in both apply and `--dry-run` modes.\n- The shipped GitHub Action's `status --check` exit-code branching now matches the CLI's real\n  contract (1 = pending, 2 = none pending) — the release-PR creation path was previously unreachable\n  on every real run.\n- `plan_publish` now reads back `CHANGELOG.md`'s real section instead of hardcoding\n  `changelog_section: None`.\n- A topological git revwalk crossing the `since` boundary before visiting all merged-branch commits\n  no longer silently drops those commits from `commits_since_with_pathspec` (`callisto-vcs`).\n- `apply_version_plan` is now idempotent, stages an npm lockfile refresh, and persists manifest writes\n  correctly per loop instead of risking a lost write.\n- Same-path manifest writes are now batched into one open/mutate/persist cycle with strict per-group\n  sequential processing, closing a stale-handle-clobber data-loss hazard.\n- Peer-dependency escalation now respects the real cascading severity instead of always escalating to\n  Major.\n- PEP 440 `is_prerelease`/`VersionReq` normalization corrected (`callisto-model`); Cargo caret-range\n  coverage now correctly excludes pre-release versions (`callisto-format`).\n- Duplicate diagnostic codes resolved across `callisto-model`/`callisto-format`/`callisto-graph` —\n  several distinct error conditions previously shared the same machine-readable code.\n- `GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership` is now actually detected when two differently-spelled\n  group-member strings resolve to the same package across two groups.\n- Numerous smaller fixes: BREAKING CHANGE commit-footer parsing, Python dependency-name PEP 503\n  normalization, npm workspace package-manager auto-detection (pnpm/yarn/bun/npm), Cargo compound\n  dependency-range rewriting, workspace-inherited-version publish guard, and more.\n\n## Performance\n\n- A single shared `GitAccess` is now reused across `status`, `plan_snapshot`, `plan_publish`, and\n  `plan_version` instead of rediscovering the repository per package or per command.\n- Tag existence checks now use the cached `TagIndex` instead of a per-release lookup.\n- Each platform manifest is now parsed once and shared across extraction paths in `callisto matrix`.\n\n## Housekeeping\n\n- Numerous documentation corrections (design/spec docs, ARCHITECTURE.md, README.md) to match shipped\n  behavior, including error-code completeness and previously-stale \"not implemented\" claims.\n- Workspace dependency hygiene: several dependencies centralized to `workspace.dependencies`; an\n  unused AGPL dev-dependency removed from Layer 1 crates.\n","numLines":117,"startLine":1,"totalLines":117}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f10c3245-4d68-4f73-bc55-ea62bdb8c345","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
