{"parentUuid":"2457ee26-0caa-4589-98bf-777bbeeee695","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeFD3f7Mi8Aw9JcaM5HQr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013wixH8XtKgtc5xgRzjHqDL","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.changeset/release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening.md","content":"---\ncallisto-model: major\ncallisto-graph: major\ncallisto-cli: major\ncallisto-manifests: major\ncallisto-conventional: major\ncallisto-vcs: minor\ncallisto-moon: patch\ncallisto-changelog: patch\ncallisto-format: patch\n---\n\n# Release pipeline correctness, `callisto matrix`, and cross-ecosystem identity fixes\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\n- **`CascadeInput` needs two new fields** (`callisto-graph`): `tags: &TagIndex` and `identity: &IdentityIndex`. Update any code that constructs it directly.\n- **`Manifest::persist` is now required** (`callisto-manifests`): mutation methods (`write_version`, `update_dependency_spec`, `update_optional_dependencies`) only mutate in memory now — call `persist()` to write. Custom `Manifest` implementors must add it.\n- **JSON report fields renamed** (`callisto-model`, visible via `callisto-cli --format json`): `ValidateReport.valid` → `ok`, `ComposePrBodyReport.pr_body` → `body`, `TagReport.created_tags` → `tags` (plus a new `already_existed: bool`). `StatusReport` gained `hasChangesets`, `lastReleasedVersion`, `releaseTrigger`. Update anything parsing this JSON, including the shipped GitHub Action.\n- **`callisto-conventional` no longer depends on `callisto-vcs`**: `fetch_commits`/`infer_severity` take `&dyn callisto_model::CommitWalker` instead of `(&dyn CommandRunner, &Path)`. `ConventionalError::Vcs` is now `ConventionalError::CommitWalk`.\n- **`PublishTarget::Npm.restricted: bool` is now `access: Option<NpmAccess>`** (`callisto-model`): npm's `publishConfig.access` has three real states (unset, public, restricted) that a bool couldn't represent — explicit `\"public\"` on an unscoped package was silently dropped.\n- **New `PackageIdParseError::LeadingHyphen` variant** (`callisto-model`), split out from `PathTraversal`, which was previously reported for inputs that had no `..` at all.\n\n## Features\n\n- **New `callisto matrix [--package <name>]` command**: discovers napi and maturin platform targets from `package.json`/`pyproject.toml`, builds a per-triple CI table (host runner, cross-compile flag, artifact name), and reports `engines.node`/`requires-python` versions.\n- **Platform-manifest and `optionalDependencies` planning actually works now** (`callisto-graph`): `plan_version` computes real writes for a bumped owner's platform siblings in a Fixed group — previously these fields were always empty.\n- **Fixed groups converge correctly** (`callisto-graph`): siblings in a Fixed group now bump to a shared target instead of drifting independently from their own base version.\n- **Better cross-ecosystem package discovery** (`callisto-graph`): Cargo/npm/pnpm workspace membership is now honored (fuzz targets and scratch examples stop showing up as release-managed packages); same-named packages in different ecosystems (a Rust crate and its Python binding, say) resolve correctly instead of erroring; `cargo:foo`/`npm:foo` prefixed group-member names work.\n- **One changelog renderer, everywhere** (`callisto-graph`): PR bodies now render through the same code CHANGELOG.md uses. Inference-driven and new-group-member bumps get real entries instead of a generic placeholder, and a bump with multiple causes (changeset + cascade, say) now lists all of them instead of just one.\n\n## Security\n\n- Package names are validated before hitting `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish`, closing an argument-injection hole (`callisto-graph`).\n- `publishConfig.registry` for npm packages is checked against an allowlist, blocking SSRF via a malicious registry URL (`callisto-graph`).\n- The shipped GitHub Action no longer interpolates untrusted input directly into shell steps.\n- Credentials are redacted from git/registry-CLI stderr before it lands in error messages (`callisto-vcs`, `callisto-model`, `callisto-graph`).\n- Subprocess output capture is now bounded, so a runaway child process can't exhaust memory (`callisto-cli`).\n- Tag names with a leading hyphen are rejected and shelled refs are qualified, closing a git argument-injection hole (`callisto-vcs`, `callisto-model`).\n\n## Fixes\n\n- `callisto tag` no longer fabricates a sha when a tag already exists at a different commit — it resolves the real target via `git rev-parse`, in both apply and `--dry-run` modes.\n- The shipped GitHub Action's `status --check` branching now matches the CLI's real exit codes (1 = pending, 2 = none pending) — the release-PR step was unreachable before this.\n- `plan_publish` reads the real `CHANGELOG.md` section instead of always leaving it blank.\n- Merged-branch commits that cross the `since` boundary are no longer dropped from `commits_since_with_pathspec` (`callisto-vcs`).\n- `apply_version_plan` is now idempotent, refreshes the npm lockfile, and persists writes correctly instead of risking a lost write.\n- Manifest writes to the same file are batched into one open/mutate/persist cycle, processed strictly in order — closing a stale-handle data-loss bug.\n- Peer-dependency escalation respects the actual cascading severity instead of always jumping to Major.\n- PEP 440 `is_prerelease`/`VersionReq` normalization is fixed (`callisto-model`); Cargo caret-range coverage now correctly excludes pre-release versions (`callisto-format`).\n- Several duplicate diagnostic codes — different error conditions that shared one machine-readable code — now have their own.\n- `GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership` is actually detected now, when two differently-spelled group-member strings resolve to the same package across two groups.\n- Smaller fixes: BREAKING CHANGE footer parsing, Python dependency-name normalization (PEP 503), npm package-manager auto-detection (pnpm/yarn/bun/npm), Cargo compound dependency-range rewriting, workspace-inherited-version publish guard.\n\n## Performance\n\n- `status`, `plan_snapshot`, `plan_publish`, and `plan_version` now share one `GitAccess` instead of rediscovering the repo per package or command.\n- Tag existence checks use the cached `TagIndex` instead of a lookup per release.\n- `callisto matrix` parses each platform manifest once and reuses it across extraction paths.\n\n## Housekeeping\n\n- Docs (design/spec, ARCHITECTURE.md, README.md) updated to match shipped behavior.\n- Dependency cleanup: several deps centralized to `workspace.dependencies`; an unused AGPL dev-dependency removed from Layer 1 crates.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":382,"cache_read_input_tokens":301042,"output_tokens":2833,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":334},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":382,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2833,"cache_read_input_tokens":301042,"cache_creation_input_tokens":382,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":382},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeFD3dmzAiFGv7CpfB88o","type":"assistant","uuid":"dfa15fa7-b209-4283-ad31-a8ddfc478b95","timestamp":"2026-08-21T03:47:40.143Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"dfa15fa7-b209-4283-ad31-a8ddfc478b95","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"958ceb8a-0f83-404e-a78d-95392eca0b44","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013wixH8XtKgtc5xgRzjHqDL","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.changeset/release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"7498a27f-7f8c-4ce1-83e0-d3c634f56065","timestamp":"2026-08-21T03:47:40.230Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.changeset/release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening.md","content":"---\ncallisto-model: major\ncallisto-graph: major\ncallisto-cli: major\ncallisto-manifests: major\ncallisto-conventional: major\ncallisto-vcs: minor\ncallisto-moon: patch\ncallisto-changelog: patch\ncallisto-format: patch\n---\n\n# Release pipeline correctness, `callisto matrix`, and cross-ecosystem identity fixes\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\n- **`CascadeInput` needs two new fields** (`callisto-graph`): `tags: &TagIndex` and `identity: &IdentityIndex`. Update any code that constructs it directly.\n- **`Manifest::persist` is now required** (`callisto-manifests`): mutation methods (`write_version`, `update_dependency_spec`, `update_optional_dependencies`) only mutate in memory now — call `persist()` to write. Custom `Manifest` implementors must add it.\n- **JSON report fields renamed** (`callisto-model`, visible via `callisto-cli --format json`): `ValidateReport.valid` → `ok`, `ComposePrBodyReport.pr_body` → `body`, `TagReport.created_tags` → `tags` (plus a new `already_existed: bool`). `StatusReport` gained `hasChangesets`, `lastReleasedVersion`, `releaseTrigger`. Update anything parsing this JSON, including the shipped GitHub Action.\n- **`callisto-conventional` no longer depends on `callisto-vcs`**: `fetch_commits`/`infer_severity` take `&dyn callisto_model::CommitWalker` instead of `(&dyn CommandRunner, &Path)`. `ConventionalError::Vcs` is now `ConventionalError::CommitWalk`.\n- **`PublishTarget::Npm.restricted: bool` is now `access: Option<NpmAccess>`** (`callisto-model`): npm's `publishConfig.access` has three real states (unset, public, restricted) that a bool couldn't represent — explicit `\"public\"` on an unscoped package was silently dropped.\n- **New `PackageIdParseError::LeadingHyphen` variant** (`callisto-model`), split out from `PathTraversal`, which was previously reported for inputs that had no `..` at all.\n\n## Features\n\n- **New `callisto matrix [--package <name>]` command**: discovers napi and maturin platform targets from `package.json`/`pyproject.toml`, builds a per-triple CI table (host runner, cross-compile flag, artifact name), and reports `engines.node`/`requires-python` versions.\n- **Platform-manifest and `optionalDependencies` planning actually works now** (`callisto-graph`): `plan_version` computes real writes for a bumped owner's platform siblings in a Fixed group — previously these fields were always empty.\n- **Fixed groups converge correctly** (`callisto-graph`): siblings in a Fixed group now bump to a shared target instead of drifting independently from their own base version.\n- **Better cross-ecosystem package discovery** (`callisto-graph`): Cargo/npm/pnpm workspace membership is now honored (fuzz targets and scratch examples stop showing up as release-managed packages); same-named packages in different ecosystems (a Rust crate and its Python binding, say) resolve correctly instead of erroring; `cargo:foo`/`npm:foo` prefixed group-member names work.\n- **One changelog renderer, everywhere** (`callisto-graph`): PR bodies now render through the same code CHANGELOG.md uses. Inference-driven and new-group-member bumps get real entries instead of a generic placeholder, and a bump with multiple causes (changeset + cascade, say) now lists all of them instead of just one.\n\n## Security\n\n- Package names are validated before hitting `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish`, closing an argument-injection hole (`callisto-graph`).\n- `publishConfig.registry` for npm packages is checked against an allowlist, blocking SSRF via a malicious registry URL (`callisto-graph`).\n- The shipped GitHub Action no longer interpolates untrusted input directly into shell steps.\n- Credentials are redacted from git/registry-CLI stderr before it lands in error messages (`callisto-vcs`, `callisto-model`, `callisto-graph`).\n- Subprocess output capture is now bounded, so a runaway child process can't exhaust memory (`callisto-cli`).\n- Tag names with a leading hyphen are rejected and shelled refs are qualified, closing a git argument-injection hole (`callisto-vcs`, `callisto-model`).\n\n## Fixes\n\n- `callisto tag` no longer fabricates a sha when a tag already exists at a different commit — it resolves the real target via `git rev-parse`, in both apply and `--dry-run` modes.\n- The shipped GitHub Action's `status --check` branching now matches the CLI's real exit codes (1 = pending, 2 = none pending) — the release-PR step was unreachable before this.\n- `plan_publish` reads the real `CHANGELOG.md` section instead of always leaving it blank.\n- Merged-branch commits that cross the `since` boundary are no longer dropped from `commits_since_with_pathspec` (`callisto-vcs`).\n- `apply_version_plan` is now idempotent, refreshes the npm lockfile, and persists writes correctly instead of risking a lost write.\n- Manifest writes to the same file are batched into one open/mutate/persist cycle, processed strictly in order — closing a stale-handle data-loss bug.\n- Peer-dependency escalation respects the actual cascading severity instead of always jumping to Major.\n- PEP 440 `is_prerelease`/`VersionReq` normalization is fixed (`callisto-model`); Cargo caret-range coverage now correctly excludes pre-release versions (`callisto-format`).\n- Several duplicate diagnostic codes — different error conditions that shared one machine-readable code — now have their own.\n- `GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership` is actually detected now, when two differently-spelled group-member strings resolve to the same package across two groups.\n- Smaller fixes: BREAKING CHANGE footer parsing, Python dependency-name normalization (PEP 503), npm package-manager auto-detection (pnpm/yarn/bun/npm), Cargo compound dependency-range rewriting, workspace-inherited-version publish guard.\n\n## Performance\n\n- `status`, `plan_snapshot`, `plan_publish`, and `plan_version` now share one `GitAccess` instead of rediscovering the repo per package or command.\n- Tag existence checks use the cached `TagIndex` instead of a lookup per release.\n- `callisto matrix` parses each platform manifest once and reuses it across extraction paths.\n\n## Housekeeping\n\n- Docs (design/spec, ARCHITECTURE.md, README.md) updated to match shipped behavior.\n- Dependency cleanup: several deps centralized to `workspace.dependencies`; an unused AGPL dev-dependency removed from Layer 1 crates.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":10,"oldLines":107,"newStart":10,"newLines":55,"lines":[" callisto-format: patch"," ---"," ","-# Release pipeline correctness, `callisto matrix`, and cross-ecosystem identity hardening","+# Release pipeline correctness, `callisto matrix`, and cross-ecosystem identity fixes"," ","-A large batch of work spanning version/cascade correctness, a new platform-target discovery","-command, JSON wire-contract fixes, security hardening, and cross-ecosystem identity resolution.","-"," ## Breaking Changes"," ","-- **`CascadeInput` gained two new required fields** (`callisto-graph`): `tags: &TagIndex` and","-  `identity: &IdentityIndex`. Any external construction site must supply both.","-- **`Manifest::persist` promoted to a required trait method** (`callisto-manifests`): manifest","-  mutation methods (`write_version`, `update_dependency_spec`, `update_optional_dependencies`) are","-  now pure in-memory mutations; callers must invoke `persist()` explicitly. Any external `Manifest`","-  implementor must now provide `persist`.","-- **JSON report field renames** (`callisto-model`, surfaced through `callisto-cli --format json`):","-  `ValidateReport.valid` → `ok`, `ComposePrBodyReport.pr_body` → `body`,","-  `TagReport.created_tags` → `tags` (plus a new `already_existed: bool` field). `StatusReport` gained","-  `hasChangesets`, `lastReleasedVersion`, and `releaseTrigger`. Consumers parsing these JSON shapes","-  (including the shipped GitHub Action) must update field references.","-- **`callisto-conventional` decoupled from `callisto-vcs`**: `fetch_commits`/`infer_severity` now","-  take `&dyn callisto_model::CommitWalker` instead of `(&dyn CommandRunner, &Path)`;","-  `ConventionalError::Vcs` renamed to `ConventionalError::CommitWalk`.","-- **`PublishTarget::Npm.restricted: bool` replaced with `access: Option<NpmAccess>`**","-  (`callisto-model`): npm's real 3-valued `publishConfig.access` (absent / public / restricted) was","-  previously collapsed into a boolean, silently dropping explicit `\"public\"` on unscoped packages.","-- **`PackageIdParseError` gained a new `LeadingHyphen` variant** (`callisto-model`), split out from","-  the previously inaccurate `PathTraversal` error reported for inputs with no `..` at all.","+- **`CascadeInput` needs two new fields** (`callisto-graph`): `tags: &TagIndex` and `identity: &IdentityIndex`. Update any code that constructs it directly.","+- **`Manifest::persist` is now required** (`callisto-manifests`): mutation methods (`write_version`, `update_dependency_spec`, `update_optional_dependencies`) only mutate in memory now — call `persist()` to write. Custom `Manifest` implementors must add it.","+- **JSON report fields renamed** (`callisto-model`, visible via `callisto-cli --format json`): `ValidateReport.valid` → `ok`, `ComposePrBodyReport.pr_body` → `body`, `TagReport.created_tags` → `tags` (plus a new `already_existed: bool`). `StatusReport` gained `hasChangesets`, `lastReleasedVersion`, `releaseTrigger`. Update anything parsing this JSON, including the shipped GitHub Action.","+- **`callisto-conventional` no longer depends on `callisto-vcs`**: `fetch_commits`/`infer_severity` take `&dyn callisto_model::CommitWalker` instead of `(&dyn CommandRunner, &Path)`. `ConventionalError::Vcs` is now `ConventionalError::CommitWalk`.","+- **`PublishTarget::Npm.restricted: bool` is now `access: Option<NpmAccess>`** (`callisto-model`): npm's `publishConfig.access` has three real states (unset, public, restricted) that a bool couldn't represent — explicit `\"public\"` on an unscoped package was silently dropped.","+- **New `PackageIdParseError::LeadingHyphen` variant** (`callisto-model`), split out from `PathTraversal`, which was previously reported for inputs that had no `..` at all."," "," ## Features"," ","-- **New `callisto matrix [--package <name>]` command** (`callisto-cli`, `callisto-graph`,","-  `callisto-model`): discovers napi and maturin platform targets from `package.json`/`pyproject.toml`,","-  produces a per-triple CI table (host runner, cross-compilation flag, artifact name), and reports","-  `engines.node`/`requires-python` runtime versions, with diagnostics for conflicting or unrecognised","-  targets.","-- **Real platform-manifest and `optionalDependencies` planning** (`callisto-graph`): `plan_version`","-  now computes real `PlatformWrite`/`OptionalDepUpdate` entries for a bumped owner's platform-manifest","-  siblings in a Fixed group, instead of leaving those fields silently empty.","-- **Fixed-group cascade convergence** (`callisto-graph`): siblings in a Fixed group now converge on a","-  shared group-aligned target instead of bumping independently from their own base version, closing a","-  silent version-divergence bug.","-- **Cross-ecosystem and workspace-membership-aware package discovery** (`callisto-graph`): Cargo/npm/","-  pnpm workspace membership globs are now honored (previously-excluded fuzz targets/scratch examples","-  are no longer discovered as release-managed packages); same-named packages in different ecosystems","-  (e.g. a Rust crate and its Python binding) resolve via promotion instead of erroring; `cargo:foo`/","-  `npm:foo` ecosystem-prefixed group-member spellings now work.","-- **Changelog/PR-body rendering consolidation** (`callisto-graph`): PR bodies now reuse the same","-  `render_section` renderer CHANGELOG.md uses; inference-driven and new-fixed-group-member bumps get","-  real changelog entries instead of a generic fallback; a package with multiple contributing causes","-  (e.g. a changeset plus a cascade) now gets a union of entries instead of dropping all but one.","+- **New `callisto matrix [--package <name>]` command**: discovers napi and maturin platform targets from `package.json`/`pyproject.toml`, builds a per-triple CI table (host runner, cross-compile flag, artifact name), and reports `engines.node`/`requires-python` versions.","+- **Platform-manifest and `optionalDependencies` planning actually works now** (`callisto-graph`): `plan_version` computes real writes for a bumped owner's platform siblings in a Fixed group — previously these fields were always empty.","+- **Fixed groups converge correctly** (`callisto-graph`): siblings in a Fixed group now bump to a shared target instead of drifting independently from their own base version.","+- **Better cross-ecosystem package discovery** (`callisto-graph`): Cargo/npm/pnpm workspace membership is now honored (fuzz targets and scratch examples stop showing up as release-managed packages); same-named packages in different ecosystems (a Rust crate and its Python binding, say) resolve correctly instead of erroring; `cargo:foo`/`npm:foo` prefixed group-member names work.","+- **One changelog renderer, everywhere** (`callisto-graph`): PR bodies now render through the same code CHANGELOG.md uses. Inference-driven and new-group-member bumps get real entries instead of a generic placeholder, and a bump with multiple causes (changeset + cascade, say) now lists all of them instead of just one."," "," ## Security"," ","-- Package names are validated before being passed to `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish`,","-  closing an argument-injection vector (`callisto-graph`).","-- `publishConfig.registry` for npm packages is now validated against an approved allowlist,","-  preventing SSRF via a malicious registry URL (`callisto-graph`).","-- The shipped GitHub Action no longer interpolates untrusted expressions directly into shell steps.","-- Credentials are now redacted from git/registry-CLI subprocess stderr before being embedded in error","-  messages (`callisto-vcs`, `callisto-model`, `callisto-graph`).","-- Subprocess stdout/stderr capture is now bounded, preventing a memory-exhaustion DoS from a","-  misbehaving child process (`callisto-cli`).","-- Tag names with a leading hyphen are now rejected and shelled tag refs are qualified, closing a","-  git-argument-injection vector (`callisto-vcs`, `callisto-model`).","+- Package names are validated before hitting `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish`, closing an argument-injection hole (`callisto-graph`).","+- `publishConfig.registry` for npm packages is checked against an allowlist, blocking SSRF via a malicious registry URL (`callisto-graph`).","+- The shipped GitHub Action no longer interpolates untrusted input directly into shell steps.","+- Credentials are redacted from git/registry-CLI stderr before it lands in error messages (`callisto-vcs`, `callisto-model`, `callisto-graph`).","+- Subprocess output capture is now bounded, so a runaway child process can't exhaust memory (`callisto-cli`).","+- Tag names with a leading hyphen are rejected and shelled refs are qualified, closing a git argument-injection hole (`callisto-vcs`, `callisto-model`)."," ","-## Correctness","+## Fixes"," ","-- `callisto tag` no longer fabricates `CreatedTag.sha` when a tag already exists at a different","-  commit — the real target is resolved via `git rev-parse`, in both apply and `--dry-run` modes.","-- The shipped GitHub Action's `status --check` exit-code branching now matches the CLI's real","-  contract (1 = pending, 2 = none pending) — the release-PR creation path was previously unreachable","-  on every real run.","-- `plan_publish` now reads back `CHANGELOG.md`'s real section instead of hardcoding","-  `changelog_section: None`.","-- A topological git revwalk crossing the `since` boundary before visiting all merged-branch commits","-  no longer silently drops those commits from `commits_since_with_pathspec` (`callisto-vcs`).","-- `apply_version_plan` is now idempotent, stages an npm lockfile refresh, and persists manifest writes","-  correctly per loop instead of risking a lost write.","-- Same-path manifest writes are now batched into one open/mutate/persist cycle with strict per-group","-  sequential processing, closing a stale-handle-clobber data-loss hazard.","-- Peer-dependency escalation now respects the real cascading severity instead of always escalating to","-  Major.","-- PEP 440 `is_prerelease`/`VersionReq` normalization corrected (`callisto-model`); Cargo caret-range","-  coverage now correctly excludes pre-release versions (`callisto-format`).","-- Duplicate diagnostic codes resolved across `callisto-model`/`callisto-format`/`callisto-graph` —","-  several distinct error conditions previously shared the same machine-readable code.","-- `GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership` is now actually detected when two differently-spelled","-  group-member strings resolve to the same package across two groups.","-- Numerous smaller fixes: BREAKING CHANGE commit-footer parsing, Python dependency-name PEP 503","-  normalization, npm workspace package-manager auto-detection (pnpm/yarn/bun/npm), Cargo compound","-  dependency-range rewriting, workspace-inherited-version publish guard, and more.","+- `callisto tag` no longer fabricates a sha when a tag already exists at a different commit — it resolves the real target via `git rev-parse`, in both apply and `--dry-run` modes.","+- The shipped GitHub Action's `status --check` branching now matches the CLI's real exit codes (1 = pending, 2 = none pending) — the release-PR step was unreachable before this.","+- `plan_publish` reads the real `CHANGELOG.md` section instead of always leaving it blank.","+- Merged-branch commits that cross the `since` boundary are no longer dropped from `commits_since_with_pathspec` (`callisto-vcs`).","+- `apply_version_plan` is now idempotent, refreshes the npm lockfile, and persists writes correctly instead of risking a lost write.","+- Manifest writes to the same file are batched into one open/mutate/persist cycle, processed strictly in order — closing a stale-handle data-loss bug.","+- Peer-dependency escalation respects the actual cascading severity instead of always jumping to Major.","+- PEP 440 `is_prerelease`/`VersionReq` normalization is fixed (`callisto-model`); Cargo caret-range coverage now correctly excludes pre-release versions (`callisto-format`).","+- Several duplicate diagnostic codes — different error conditions that shared one machine-readable code — now have their own.","+- `GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership` is actually detected now, when two differently-spelled group-member strings resolve to the same package across two groups.","+- Smaller fixes: BREAKING CHANGE footer parsing, Python dependency-name normalization (PEP 503), npm package-manager auto-detection (pnpm/yarn/bun/npm), Cargo compound dependency-range rewriting, workspace-inherited-version publish guard."," "," ## Performance"," ","-- A single shared `GitAccess` is now reused across `status`, `plan_snapshot`, `plan_publish`, and","-  `plan_version` instead of rediscovering the repository per package or per command.","-- Tag existence checks now use the cached `TagIndex` instead of a per-release lookup.","-- Each platform manifest is now parsed once and shared across extraction paths in `callisto matrix`.","+- `status`, `plan_snapshot`, `plan_publish`, and `plan_version` now share one `GitAccess` instead of rediscovering the repo per package or command.","+- Tag existence checks use the cached `TagIndex` instead of a lookup per release.","+- `callisto matrix` parses each platform manifest once and reuses it across extraction paths."," "," ## Housekeeping"," ","-- Numerous documentation corrections (design/spec docs, ARCHITECTURE.md, README.md) to match shipped","-  behavior, including error-code completeness and previously-stale \"not implemented\" claims.","-- Workspace dependency hygiene: several dependencies centralized to `workspace.dependencies`; an","-  unused AGPL dev-dependency removed from Layer 1 crates.","+- Docs (design/spec, ARCHITECTURE.md, README.md) updated to match shipped behavior.","+- Dependency cleanup: several deps centralized to `workspace.dependencies`; an unused AGPL dev-dependency removed from Layer 1 crates."]}],"originalFile":"---\ncallisto-model: major\ncallisto-graph: major\ncallisto-cli: major\ncallisto-manifests: major\ncallisto-conventional: major\ncallisto-vcs: minor\ncallisto-moon: patch\ncallisto-changelog: patch\ncallisto-format: patch\n---\n\n# Release pipeline correctness, `callisto matrix`, and cross-ecosystem identity hardening\n\nA large batch of work spanning version/cascade correctness, a new platform-target discovery\ncommand, JSON wire-contract fixes, security hardening, and cross-ecosystem identity resolution.\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\n- **`CascadeInput` gained two new required fields** (`callisto-graph`): `tags: &TagIndex` and\n  `identity: &IdentityIndex`. Any external construction site must supply both.\n- **`Manifest::persist` promoted to a required trait method** (`callisto-manifests`): manifest\n  mutation methods (`write_version`, `update_dependency_spec`, `update_optional_dependencies`) are\n  now pure in-memory mutations; callers must invoke `persist()` explicitly. Any external `Manifest`\n  implementor must now provide `persist`.\n- **JSON report field renames** (`callisto-model`, surfaced through `callisto-cli --format json`):\n  `ValidateReport.valid` → `ok`, `ComposePrBodyReport.pr_body` → `body`,\n  `TagReport.created_tags` → `tags` (plus a new `already_existed: bool` field). `StatusReport` gained\n  `hasChangesets`, `lastReleasedVersion`, and `releaseTrigger`. Consumers parsing these JSON shapes\n  (including the shipped GitHub Action) must update field references.\n- **`callisto-conventional` decoupled from `callisto-vcs`**: `fetch_commits`/`infer_severity` now\n  take `&dyn callisto_model::CommitWalker` instead of `(&dyn CommandRunner, &Path)`;\n  `ConventionalError::Vcs` renamed to `ConventionalError::CommitWalk`.\n- **`PublishTarget::Npm.restricted: bool` replaced with `access: Option<NpmAccess>`**\n  (`callisto-model`): npm's real 3-valued `publishConfig.access` (absent / public / restricted) was\n  previously collapsed into a boolean, silently dropping explicit `\"public\"` on unscoped packages.\n- **`PackageIdParseError` gained a new `LeadingHyphen` variant** (`callisto-model`), split out from\n  the previously inaccurate `PathTraversal` error reported for inputs with no `..` at all.\n\n## Features\n\n- **New `callisto matrix [--package <name>]` command** (`callisto-cli`, `callisto-graph`,\n  `callisto-model`): discovers napi and maturin platform targets from `package.json`/`pyproject.toml`,\n  produces a per-triple CI table (host runner, cross-compilation flag, artifact name), and reports\n  `engines.node`/`requires-python` runtime versions, with diagnostics for conflicting or unrecognised\n  targets.\n- **Real platform-manifest and `optionalDependencies` planning** (`callisto-graph`): `plan_version`\n  now computes real `PlatformWrite`/`OptionalDepUpdate` entries for a bumped owner's platform-manifest\n  siblings in a Fixed group, instead of leaving those fields silently empty.\n- **Fixed-group cascade convergence** (`callisto-graph`): siblings in a Fixed group now converge on a\n  shared group-aligned target instead of bumping independently from their own base version, closing a\n  silent version-divergence bug.\n- **Cross-ecosystem and workspace-membership-aware package discovery** (`callisto-graph`): Cargo/npm/\n  pnpm workspace membership globs are now honored (previously-excluded fuzz targets/scratch examples\n  are no longer discovered as release-managed packages); same-named packages in different ecosystems\n  (e.g. a Rust crate and its Python binding) resolve via promotion instead of erroring; `cargo:foo`/\n  `npm:foo` ecosystem-prefixed group-member spellings now work.\n- **Changelog/PR-body rendering consolidation** (`callisto-graph`): PR bodies now reuse the same\n  `render_section` renderer CHANGELOG.md uses; inference-driven and new-fixed-group-member bumps get\n  real changelog entries instead of a generic fallback; a package with multiple contributing causes\n  (e.g. a changeset plus a cascade) now gets a union of entries instead of dropping all but one.\n\n## Security\n\n- Package names are validated before being passed to `cargo publish`/`npm publish`/`pypi publish`,\n  closing an argument-injection vector (`callisto-graph`).\n- `publishConfig.registry` for npm packages is now validated against an approved allowlist,\n  preventing SSRF via a malicious registry URL (`callisto-graph`).\n- The shipped GitHub Action no longer interpolates untrusted expressions directly into shell steps.\n- Credentials are now redacted from git/registry-CLI subprocess stderr before being embedded in error\n  messages (`callisto-vcs`, `callisto-model`, `callisto-graph`).\n- Subprocess stdout/stderr capture is now bounded, preventing a memory-exhaustion DoS from a\n  misbehaving child process (`callisto-cli`).\n- Tag names with a leading hyphen are now rejected and shelled tag refs are qualified, closing a\n  git-argument-injection vector (`callisto-vcs`, `callisto-model`).\n\n## Correctness\n\n- `callisto tag` no longer fabricates `CreatedTag.sha` when a tag already exists at a different\n  commit — the real target is resolved via `git rev-parse`, in both apply and `--dry-run` modes.\n- The shipped GitHub Action's `status --check` exit-code branching now matches the CLI's real\n  contract (1 = pending, 2 = none pending) — the release-PR creation path was previously unreachable\n  on every real run.\n- `plan_publish` now reads back `CHANGELOG.md`'s real section instead of hardcoding\n  `changelog_section: None`.\n- A topological git revwalk crossing the `since` boundary before visiting all merged-branch commits\n  no longer silently drops those commits from `commits_since_with_pathspec` (`callisto-vcs`).\n- `apply_version_plan` is now idempotent, stages an npm lockfile refresh, and persists manifest writes\n  correctly per loop instead of risking a lost write.\n- Same-path manifest writes are now batched into one open/mutate/persist cycle with strict per-group\n  sequential processing, closing a stale-handle-clobber data-loss hazard.\n- Peer-dependency escalation now respects the real cascading severity instead of always escalating to\n  Major.\n- PEP 440 `is_prerelease`/`VersionReq` normalization corrected (`callisto-model`); Cargo caret-range\n  coverage now correctly excludes pre-release versions (`callisto-format`).\n- Duplicate diagnostic codes resolved across `callisto-model`/`callisto-format`/`callisto-graph` —\n  several distinct error conditions previously shared the same machine-readable code.\n- `GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership` is now actually detected when two differently-spelled\n  group-member strings resolve to the same package across two groups.\n- Numerous smaller fixes: BREAKING CHANGE commit-footer parsing, Python dependency-name PEP 503\n  normalization, npm workspace package-manager auto-detection (pnpm/yarn/bun/npm), Cargo compound\n  dependency-range rewriting, workspace-inherited-version publish guard, and more.\n\n## Performance\n\n- A single shared `GitAccess` is now reused across `status`, `plan_snapshot`, `plan_publish`, and\n  `plan_version` instead of rediscovering the repository per package or per command.\n- Tag existence checks now use the cached `TagIndex` instead of a per-release lookup.\n- Each platform manifest is now parsed once and shared across extraction paths in `callisto matrix`.\n\n## Housekeeping\n\n- Numerous documentation corrections (design/spec docs, ARCHITECTURE.md, README.md) to match shipped\n  behavior, including error-code completeness and previously-stale \"not implemented\" claims.\n- Workspace dependency hygiene: several dependencies centralized to `workspace.dependencies`; an\n  unused AGPL dev-dependency removed from Layer 1 crates.\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dfa15fa7-b209-4283-ad31-a8ddfc478b95","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
