{"parentUuid":"42b21c97-a64e-4c3f-a0ea-59a5ce0d6586","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeFDui2cu1cFXMzsnEV7Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Working tree is clean apart from the new changeset. Let me fork out a check of README/ARCHITECTURE against the current CLI surface and feature set, while I check a few other release-readiness basics directly."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1864,"cache_read_input_tokens":310310,"output_tokens":1438,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1864,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1438,"cache_read_input_tokens":310310,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1864,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1864},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeFDughzSs4w1aD8fT2S5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8c9aae40-e20b-4d12-bdc3-39a924a4553b","timestamp":"2026-08-21T03:58:35.666Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"8c9aae40-e20b-4d12-bdc3-39a924a4553b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeFDui2cu1cFXMzsnEV7Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EhG5yMkyv7eMYufhHFPtvQ","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"fork","name":"docs-release-audit","description":"Check README/ARCHITECTURE accuracy for release","prompt":"The user is prepping this repo (callisto, a release/versioning CLI tool) for its next release, after a very large batch of work landed (the changeset you'll find at `.changeset/release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening.md` — read it first, it's a comprehensive, already-reviewed summary of everything that changed since the last release, including a brand-new `callisto matrix` command and several breaking API/JSON changes).\n\n## Task\nCheck whether `README.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` (repo root) are accurate against the CURRENT code, not stale. Specifically:\n\n1. Read `README.md` in full. Cross-check every claim against real code:\n   - Does it list all real CLI commands? Compare against `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/` or the clap command definitions (find the clap `Subcommand` enum or equivalent) — does it mention the new `callisto matrix` command? If README has a command list/table, is it complete and accurate (right flags, right descriptions)?\n   - Do installation instructions, usage examples, and any JSON output examples match reality (e.g. if it shows sample JSON output for `status`/`validate`/`tag`, check the field names match the CURRENT report shapes in `crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs` — the changeset notes `ValidateReport.valid`→`ok`, `ComposePrBodyReport.pr_body`→`body`, `TagReport.created_tags`→`tags`, new `StatusReport` fields — if README shows old field names in examples, that's now stale and must be flagged).\n   - Are there broken links, wrong badge URLs, or references to files that no longer exist?\n2. Read `ARCHITECTURE.md` in full. Cross-check against real code:\n   - Does its crate list match the actual crates in `crates/` (there are 10: callisto-model, callisto-graph, callisto-cli, callisto-manifests, callisto-changelog, callisto-format, callisto-conventional, callisto-vcs, callisto-moon, callisto-fixtures)?\n   - Does it describe the Layer 1/Layer 2 isolation invariant correctly (per `CLAUDE.md`: Layer 1 = callisto-model, callisto-format, must stay MIT OR Apache-2.0, no AGPL deps)?\n   - Does it mention `callisto matrix` and its napi/maturin discovery pipeline if it documents the command surface?\n   - Are there any claims contradicted by things fixed in this release batch (check the changeset's Breaking Changes / Fixes sections for anything ARCHITECTURE.md might describe incorrectly — e.g. does it describe `CascadeInput`'s fields, `Manifest::persist`, or the JSON report shapes in a way that's now wrong)?\n   - Check for the same \"demand-gated\"/stale-claim pattern this project has hit before (see git log for \"Track 6-doc\"/\"Track 8-doc\"/\"Track 3a\" commits if curious — this repo has a history of docs drifting from shipped code).\n3. Do NOT read the full docs/00-design.md or docs/01-spec.md in depth (separate, larger docs, out of scope for this pass) — but if you happen to notice something egregious while cross-referencing, note it briefly.\n4. Do NOT edit any files. This is a read-only audit — report findings only.\n\n## Report back (under 400 words)\nA punch list: for each of README.md and ARCHITECTURE.md, either \"accurate, no changes needed\" or a specific list of stale/incorrect claims with the exact line/section and what's wrong. Prioritize anything a new user or contributor would hit first (install instructions, command list, JSON examples) over deep architectural nuance."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1864,"cache_read_input_tokens":310310,"output_tokens":1438,"output_tokens_detai