{"parentUuid":"6c98e8e0-0aac-4e24-bea7-98bd50a89d10","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5a846dc1-2e04-43fc-9830-bb9087b1af8d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EhG5yMkyv7eMYufhHFPtvQ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: ad872a76320bd5028 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'ad872a76320bd5028', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/ad872a76320bd5028.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"e825582b-080e-4e10-83d1-c27c68bbe33c","timestamp":"2026-08-21T03:58:54.506Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"ad872a76320bd5028","description":"Check README/ARCHITECTURE accuracy for release","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt":"The user is prepping this repo (callisto, a release/versioning CLI tool) for its next release, after a very large batch of work landed (the changeset you'll find at `.changeset/release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening.md` — read it first, it's a comprehensive, already-reviewed summary of everything that changed since the last release, including a brand-new `callisto matrix` command and several breaking API/JSON changes).\n\n## Task\nCheck whether `README.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` (repo root) are accurate against the CURRENT code, not stale. Specifically:\n\n1. Read `README.md` in full. Cross-check every claim against real code:\n   - Does it list all real CLI commands? Compare against `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/` or the clap command definitions (find the clap `Subcommand` enum or equivalent) — does it mention the new `callisto matrix` command? If README has a command list/table, is it complete and accurate (right flags, right descriptions)?\n   - Do installation instructions, usage examples, and any JSON output examples match reality (e.g. if it shows sample JSON output for `status`/`validate`/`tag`, check the field names match the CURRENT report shapes in `crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs` — the changeset notes `ValidateReport.valid`→`ok`, `ComposePrBodyReport.pr_body`→`body`, `TagReport.created_tags`→`tags`, new `StatusReport` fields — if README shows old field names in examples, that's now stale and must be flagged).\n   - Are there broken links, wrong badge URLs, or references to files that no longer exist?\n2. Read `ARCHITECTURE.md` in full. Cross-check against real code:\n   - Does its crate list match the actual crates in `crates/` (there are 10: callisto-model, callisto-graph, callisto-cli, callisto-manifests, callisto-changelog, callisto-format, callisto-conventional, callisto-vcs, callisto-moon, callisto-fixtures)?\n   - Does it describe the Layer 1/Layer 2 isolation invariant correctly (per `CLAUDE.md`: Layer 1 = callisto-model, callisto-format, must stay MIT OR Apache-2.0, no AGPL deps)?\n   - Does it mention `callisto matrix` and its napi/maturin discovery pipeline if it documents the command surface?\n   - Are there any claims contradicted by things fixed in this release batch (check the changeset's Breaking Changes / Fixes sections for anything ARCHITECTURE.md might describe incorrectly — e.g. does it describe `CascadeInput`'s fields, `Manifest::persist`, or the JSON report shapes in a way that's now wrong)?\n   - Check for the same \"demand-gated\"/stale-claim pattern this project has hit before (see git log for \"Track 6-doc\"/\"Track 8-doc\"/\"Track 3a\" commits if curious — this repo has a history of docs drifting from shipped code).\n3. Do NOT read the full docs/00-design.md or docs/01-spec.md in depth (separate, larger docs, out of scope for this pass) — but if you happen to notice something egregious while cross-referencing, note it briefly.\n4. Do NOT edit any files. This is a read-only audit — report findings only.\n\n## Report back (under 400 words)\nA punch list: for each of README.md and ARCHITECTURE.md, either \"accurate, no changes needed\" or a specific list of stale/incorrect claims with the exact line/section and what's wrong. Prioritize anything a new user or contributor would hit first (install instructions, command list, JSON examples) over deep architectural nuance.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/ad872a76320bd5028.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6c98e8e0-0aac-4e24-bea7-98bd50a89d10","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
