{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-21T04:00:04.258Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ad872a76320bd5028</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01EhG5yMkyv7eMYufhHFPtvQ</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/ad872a76320bd5028.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Check README/ARCHITECTURE accuracy for release\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## README.md / ARCHITECTURE.md audit\n\n**Checked**: `.changeset/release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening.md` for context; cross-referenced both docs against `crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs` (real command list), `crates/callisto-cli/src/render/mod.rs` (real text output), and every crate's `Cargo.toml` `license` field.\n\n### README.md — 2 concrete errors found\n\n1. **Quick Start sample output is fabricated, not real** (lines 43-53). The shown `callisto status`/`callisto version` output doesn't match what the code actually prints.\n   - Real `render_status` (mod.rs:24-39): `  {name} {version} (pending: {severity})` — no `-&gt;` target version, no changeset filename, no `[cascade: X]` annotation.\n   - Real `render_version` (mod.rs:42-53): `  {name} {from} → {to}` — no \"Updated N package manifests\", no \"Appended changelog entries\", no \"Consumed N changeset\" lines.\n   - This is the first thing a new user sees. Needs to be replaced with real captured output, not aspirational prose.\n\n2. **License table error** (line 230): lists `callisto-vcs` as `AGPL-3.0`. Its real `Cargo.toml` says `license = \"MIT OR Apache-2.0\"` — confirmed, and ARCHITECTURE.md's own table (line 125) already has this crate correct. This is a license-compliance-relevant error, worth fixing before release. Every other crate's license row in README's table checks out against its real `Cargo.toml`.\n\nEverything else checked out: `callisto matrix` is documented (Key Capabilities section), install instructions, badges, and links look fine, no broken references found. README isn't meant to be an exhaustive command reference (it covers init/add/status/version/compose-pr-body/matrix, not pre/validate/snapshot/plan-publish/publish/tag/completions/schema) — that's a scoping choice, not staleness, so not flagged as an error.\n\n### ARCHITECTURE.md — accurate, no changes needed\n\n- Crate list/count (10), Layer 1/2 licensing invariant, and the `callisto-vcs` license are all correct and already match code.\n- `callisto matrix` is documented with an explicit `[partially implemented]` status callout (§12) that accurately describes what's live (napi/maturin/npm/PyPI) vs. planned (Java, .NET, `publish-target` subcommand) — this is honest, not a stale claim.\n- Nothing in the changeset's Breaking Changes contradicts anything ARCHITECTURE.md claims (it doesn't describe `CascadeInput`'s exact fields, `Manifest::persist`'s pre-change signature, or JSON report field names in enough detail to be wrong).\n\nDid not deep-read docs/00-design.md or docs/01-spec.md (out of scope) — no red flags noticed in passing.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>344526</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>10</tool_uses><duration_ms>68652</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
