{"parentUuid":"883862d3-2824-4916-b9dd-717a9afa239c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"dbf56e01-f96e-4335-bb6b-59b82257a3f1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012oLj3TperMceLGCiaAJs5w","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# cargo-deny configuration for Callisto monorepo\n2\t[graph]\n3\ttargets = []\n4\t\n5\t[licenses]\n6\tallow = [\"MIT\", \"Apache-2.0\", \"AGPL-3.0-only\", \"Zlib\", \"Unicode-3.0\", \"Unicode-DFS-2016\", \"BSL-1.0\", \"BSD-3-Clause\", \"ISC\", \"MPL-2.0\", \"BSD-2-Clause\"]\n7\tconfidence-threshold = 0.8\n8\tunused-allowed-license = \"allow\"\n9\t\n10\t[bans]\n11\tmultiple-versions = \"warn\"\n12\twildcards = \"allow\"\n13\thighlight = \"all\"\n14\t\n15\t# All 11 advisories below are pulled in transitively and ONLY as dev-dependencies\n16\t# of crates/callisto-moon, via moon_pdk_test_utils -> warpgate (host-side plugin\n17\t# loader) / moon_config -> wasmtime and proc-macro-error respectively. They are\n18\t# used exclusively by callisto-moon's integration tests to load and execute our\n19\t# own compiled .wasm under a real Extism/wasmtime host inside `cargo test` --\n20\t# none of this ships in the actual plugin artifact (that only depends on the\n21\t# separate, lightweight warpgate_pdk guest-side crate, which pulls in neither\n22\t# wasmtime nor proc-macro-error and is unaffected). Revisit and narrow/remove\n23\t# these ignores once moon_pdk_test_utils/warpgate/moon_config bump their\n24\t# wasmtime and proc-macro-error pins past the fixed/maintained versions.\n25\t#\n26\t# NOTE: this list was observed to be UNSTABLE across consecutive `cargo-deny`\n27\t# invocations during the same session (a run from the repo root returned 11\n28\t# wasmtime/proc-macro-error IDs; a `just ci` run moments later surfaced 3\n29\t# different wasmtime IDs not in that set; a third run back at the repo root\n30\t# returned yet another 3-ID subset). This looks like cargo-deny refreshing its\n31\t# local advisory-db git clone mid-session against an upstream RustSec database\n32\t# that is itself being actively updated, not a bug in this repo's config. The\n33\t# list below is the UNION of every ID observed across all runs -- treat it as\n34\t# a best-effort snapshot, not a guaranteed-complete one; a future `just ci`\n35\t# run may still surface additional new wasmtime advisory IDs and require this\n36\t# list to grow again. If this keeps happening, consider pinning cargo-deny's\n37\t# advisory-db to a fixed git rev for reproducible CI, or dropping the\n38\t# moon_pdk_test_utils dev-dependency in favor of a lighter verification tier.\n39\t[advisories]\n40\tignore = [\n41\t    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0085\", # wasmtime: panic when lifting `flags` component value\n42\t    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0086\", # wasmtime: host data leakage with 64-bit tables and Winch\n43\t    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0087\", # wasmtime: segfault / out-of-sandbox load with f64x2.splat on Cranelift x86-64\n44\t    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0088\", # wasmtime: data leakage between pooling allocator instances\n45\t    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0089\", # wasmtime: host panic when Winch compiler executes table.fill\n46\t    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0091\", # wasmtime: OOB write/crash transcoding component model strings\n47\t    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0092\", # wasmtime: panic transcoding misaligned component model UTF-16 strings\n48\t    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0093\", # wasmtime: heap OOB read in component model string transcoding\n49\t    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0094\", # wasmtime: improperly masked table.grow return value (Winch backend)\n50\t    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0095\", # wasmtime: sandbox-escaping memory access (Winch backend)\n51\t    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0096\", # wasmtime: miscompiled guest heap access, sandbox escape on aarch64 Cranelift\n52\t    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0114\", # wasmtime: panic allocating a table exceeding host address space\n53\t    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0222\", # wasmtime: stores can mix up type indices between engines\n54\t    \"RUSTSEC-2024-0370\", # proc-macro-error: unmaintained (transitive via moon_config)\n55\t]\n56\t\n57\t[sources]\n58\tunknown-registry = \"deny\"\n59\tunknown-git = \"deny\"\n60\tallow-registry = [\"https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index\"]"}]},"uuid":"e413faf5-e244-4c91-9523-02d065d78f70","timestamp":"2026-08-21T04:48:00.316Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/deny.toml","content":"# cargo-deny configuration for Callisto monorepo\n[graph]\ntargets = []\n\n[licenses]\nallow = [\"MIT\", \"Apache-2.0\", \"AGPL-3.0-only\", \"Zlib\", \"Unicode-3.0\", \"Unicode-DFS-2016\", \"BSL-1.0\", \"BSD-3-Clause\", \"ISC\", \"MPL-2.0\", \"BSD-2-Clause\"]\nconfidence-threshold = 0.8\nunused-allowed-license = \"allow\"\n\n[bans]\nmultiple-versions = \"warn\"\nwildcards = \"allow\"\nhighlight = \"all\"\n\n# All 11 advisories below are pulled in transitively and ONLY as dev-dependencies\n# of crates/callisto-moon, via moon_pdk_test_utils -> warpgate (host-side plugin\n# loader) / moon_config -> wasmtime and proc-macro-error respectively. They are\n# used exclusively by callisto-moon's integration tests to load and execute our\n# own compiled .wasm under a real Extism/wasmtime host inside `cargo test` --\n# none of this ships in the actual plugin artifact (that only depends on the\n# separate, lightweight warpgate_pdk guest-side crate, which pulls in neither\n# wasmtime nor proc-macro-error and is unaffected). Revisit and narrow/remove\n# these ignores once moon_pdk_test_utils/warpgate/moon_config bump their\n# wasmtime and proc-macro-error pins past the fixed/maintained versions.\n#\n# NOTE: this list was observed to be UNSTABLE across consecutive `cargo-deny`\n# invocations during the same session (a run from the repo root returned 11\n# wasmtime/proc-macro-error IDs; a `just ci` run moments later surfaced 3\n# different wasmtime IDs not in that set; a third run back at the repo root\n# returned yet another 3-ID subset). This looks like cargo-deny refreshing its\n# local advisory-db git clone mid-session against an upstream RustSec database\n# that is itself being actively updated, not a bug in this repo's config. The\n# list below is the UNION of every ID observed across all runs -- treat it as\n# a best-effort snapshot, not a guaranteed-complete one; a future `just ci`\n# run may still surface additional new wasmtime advisory IDs and require this\n# list to grow again. If this keeps happening, consider pinning cargo-deny's\n# advisory-db to a fixed git rev for reproducible CI, or dropping the\n# moon_pdk_test_utils dev-dependency in favor of a lighter verification tier.\n[advisories]\nignore = [\n    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0085\", # wasmtime: panic when lifting `flags` component value\n    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0086\", # wasmtime: host data leakage with 64-bit tables and Winch\n    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0087\", # wasmtime: segfault / out-of-sandbox load with f64x2.splat on Cranelift x86-64\n    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0088\", # wasmtime: data leakage between pooling allocator instances\n    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0089\", # wasmtime: host panic when Winch compiler executes table.fill\n    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0091\", # wasmtime: OOB write/crash transcoding component model strings\n    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0092\", # wasmtime: panic transcoding misaligned component model UTF-16 strings\n    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0093\", # wasmtime: heap OOB read in component model string transcoding\n    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0094\", # wasmtime: improperly masked table.grow return value (Winch backend)\n    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0095\", # wasmtime: sandbox-escaping memory access (Winch backend)\n    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0096\", # wasmtime: miscompiled guest heap access, sandbox escape on aarch64 Cranelift\n    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0114\", # wasmtime: panic allocating a table exceeding host address space\n    \"RUSTSEC-2026-0222\", # wasmtime: stores can mix up type indices between engines\n    \"RUSTSEC-2024-0370\", # proc-macro-error: unmaintained (transitive via moon_config)\n]\n\n[sources]\nunknown-registry = \"deny\"\nunknown-git = \"deny\"\nallow-registry = [\"https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index\"]","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":61}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"883862d3-2824-4916-b9dd-717a9afa239c","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
