{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:17:46.345Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a7cfc1cb431b253df</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_016tL8piYokJvwntfHjj55gE</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/a7cfc1cb431b253df.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review manifests diff for cleanup\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Good, confirmed line numbers. Reporting findings now.\n\n**Directive: review manifests diff (cargo.rs/npm.rs/python.rs/lib.rs) for reuse/simplification/efficiency issues.**\n\nThe mutate/persist split (write_version/update_dependency_spec no longer call persist directly) is a deliberate, well-tested refactor — not flagged. The three `*_package_name` free functions are legitimately distinct per-ecosystem parsers with an explicit doc comment justifying the duplication of pattern (not logic) — not flagged.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs\",\n    \"line\": 373,\n    \"summary\": \"The 'else return Err(UnrecognizedDependencyValue{path,name})' fallback (added by this diff) is repeated 4 times near-verbatim: CargoToml::update_dependency_spec (lines 373, 390) and WorkspaceCargoResolver::write_dependency (lines 719, 736), which is itself a near-duplicate of update_dependency_spec.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Same 6-line error-construction block duplicated 4x; a future change to the error shape (e.g. adding a 'shape' field describing what was found) requires editing 4 call sites instead of one shared helper like `fn unrecognized_dependency_value(path: &amp;Path, name: &amp;str) -&gt; ManifestError`.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-manifests/src/python.rs\",\n    \"line\": 452,\n    \"summary\": \"PEP 503 name-equivalence comparison `normalize_pypi_package_name(a) == normalize_pypi_package_name(b)` (introduced by this diff) is duplicated between update_dependency_spec (line 325) and update_optional_dependencies (line 452).\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Two independent copies of the same 'PEP-503-equal' predicate; if the equivalence rule is ever refined (e.g. case-folding), one copy is easy to miss. A single `fn pep503_names_match(a: &amp;str, b: &amp;str) -&gt; bool` would remove the duplication.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-manifests/src/npm.rs\",\n    \"line\": 908,\n    \"summary\": \"PublishTarget::Npm's access field is now computed with `.and_then(...).and_then(|s| match s {...})` chained off a single `.as_str()` — fine — but note WorkspaceCargoResolver::write_dependency (cargo.rs) duplicates CargoToml::update_dependency_spec's entire body (as_value_mut/as_table_mut branching) with only the persist-call and path differing; this pre-dates the diff but the diff added the new error branches to both copies in lockstep, doubling the size of the duplication rather than factoring it out now that both branches diverge in one new way (persist timing).\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"The two ~40-line dependency-value-rewrite bodies in cargo.rs now need to be kept in sync by hand for every future edge case (this diff already had to add the same 2 new error arms to both); a shared `fn rewrite_dependency_value(item: &amp;mut Item, new: DepSpec, ...) -&gt; Result&lt;(), ManifestError&gt;` would collapse both copies into one call site each.\"\n  }\n]\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>91879</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>4</tool_uses><duration_ms>46289</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
