{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:18:31.128Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aabd10440529965be</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_011ALoMWaYPEvKA6UusNrs2X</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/aabd10440529965be.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review locate/walk diff for cleanup\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I have enough to finalize my findings for this scope.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs\",\n    \"line\": 256,\n    \"summary\": \"read_npm_membership reads and JSON-parses package.json twice per call: once in package_json_declares_name(root) (line 245), then again in read_package_json_workspaces(root) (line 288) when no pnpm-workspace.yaml governs.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Every call to read_npm_membership() — which runs once per IgnoreWalkLocator::projects() invocation, itself on the hot path for every graph/matrix command — does two separate fs::read_to_string + serde_json::from_str passes over the same file. The parsed serde_json::Value from the first read is discarded and re-derived instead of being threaded through to read_package_json_workspaces, doubling I/O and JSON-parse cost for no reason.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs\",\n    \"line\": 146,\n    \"summary\": \"this_set is re-fetched from claiming_ecosystems via a BTreeMap::get(...).cloned() right after the identical value (this_claiming) was computed and inserted into that same map a few lines above (line 140), while this_claiming is still in scope.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Adds a redundant map lookup + BTreeSet clone per package during graph construction when the already-owned this_claiming local could be reused directly (e.g. this_claiming.clone()), avoiding the extra map traversal on every processed manifest.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs\",\n    \"line\": 59,\n    \"summary\": \"is_promoted_bare_name is a #[cfg(test)]-only reimplementation of the same disjoint-ecosystem promotion predicate that the production code path in build() already implements inline (via claiming_sets_disjoint against promoted_siblings), rather than the tests exercising the real production branch directly.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Two separate implementations of 'is this bare name promoted' now exist — one executes in production, one only in tests — so a future change to the real promotion logic in build() can silently diverge from is_promoted_bare_name without any test catching it, since the tests only prove the standalone copy is correct, not the inline logic that actually runs.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs\",\n    \"line\": 658,\n    \"summary\": \"napi_linux_abi_from_package_name allocates a new String via format!(\\\"-{abi}\\\") on every loop iteration (up to 3 per call) just to test a suffix, instead of matching against static string literals.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Runs once per npm platform-role manifest detected during every workspace walk; each call does up to 3 heap allocations purely to build a suffix pattern for ends_with, when \\\"-gnu\\\"/\\\"-musl\\\"/\\\"-gnueabihf\\\" could be compared directly with zero allocation.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs\",\n    \"line\": 545,\n    \"summary\": \"mod ac09e_probe contains two tests (probe_unparseable_package_json_before_04e, probe_pnpm_non_string_seq_before_04e) that are near-verbatim duplicates of read_npm_membership_falls_back_to_absent_when_root_package_json_syntax_is_invalid and read_npm_membership_falls_back_to_absent_when_pnpm_packages_sequence_has_non_string_element already in npm_membership_tests above.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Leftover development-scaffolding test module duplicates coverage already provided elsewhere in the same file, adding dead maintenance surface (two places to update if the behavior changes) with no additional signal over the existing tests.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nFork complete — reporting to parent.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>119203</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>11</tool_uses><duration_ms>82563</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
