{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:18:58.026Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a020417a5f929108b</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01NerLUYEPjLR1jiPuyxg2Xi</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/a020417a5f929108b.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review model/vcs diff for cleanup\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Task**: Review callisto-model/src and callisto-vcs/src diff for REUSE/SIMPLIFICATION/EFFICIENCY issues, return ≤5 JSON findings.\n\nReviewed all changed files in both crates (registry.rs new file, report.rs, exec.rs, path.rs, identity.rs, ecosystem.rs, lib.rs, diagnostic.rs, error.rs, tag.rs, matrix.rs, Cargo.toml; vcs shell.rs, lib.rs, access.rs, Cargo.toml). Most of the diff is well-tested bug fixes with good doc comments (git-version semver parsing, POSIX backslash path handling, PackageId leading-hyphen error, tag-template leading-hyphen rejection). Only one significant cross-file duplication surfaced within this scope; the rest of the diff introduces no meaningful waste, dead code, or over-capturing closures.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-vcs/src/shell.rs\",\n    \"line\": 37,\n    \"summary\": \"New `redact_git_stderr` wrapper (`callisto_model::redact_known_secrets(text, &amp;callisto_model::known_credential_env_values(std::env::vars()))`) is a verbatim copy of functions added by this same diff in at least 3-4 other files (`callisto-cli/src/commands/pre.rs:25`, `callisto-graph/src/apply.rs:509`, `callisto-conventional/src/pre_cursor.rs:18`, and `callisto-graph/src/commands/publish_client.rs:710` as `redact_stderr`)\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"The same 4-line body (call known_credential_env_values(std::env::vars()) then redact_known_secrets) is hand-copied into 5 places instead of being a single `callisto_model::redact_process_stderr(text)` helper. Any future change to the redaction call convention (e.g. caching the env snapshot instead of re-reading it on every error, or adding another credential source) has to be made in 5 files instead of 1, and it's easy for a 6th call site to reinvent it again rather than notice the existing one.\"\n  }\n]\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>94631</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>15</tool_uses><duration_ms>95514</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
