{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:19:28.229Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aebbb3597a2f05730</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01FbAn82eNR5DzakDtwkDm7b</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/aebbb3597a2f05730.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Audit config/resolve.rs and identity.rs diff for regressions\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Confirmed intentional and covered. My scoped review found no genuine regressions.\n\n**Report: Config/Identity audit** — scoped to `config/resolve.rs`, `identity.rs` (graph + model), `lib.rs`, `config_resolve_tests.rs`.\n\nNo confirmed regressions found in this scope. Checked and ruled out:\n- `resolve_package_config`: signature changed `Option&lt;&amp;PackageConfig&gt;` → `Result&lt;Option&lt;&amp;PackageConfig&gt;, GraphError&gt;` to add promoted-sibling ambiguity detection. Both call sites (`aggregate.rs:212`, `walk.rs:353`) propagate the error via `?`. Two-pass matching logic (prefixed-first, then bare) unchanged.\n- `PreMajorInferencePolicy` struct→enum conversion: all three variants (`Off`/`Conservative`/`ConservativeFeat`) correctly consumed in `aggregate.rs::apply_pre_major`, no dropped combination.\n- `PublishTarget::Npm { restricted: bool }` → `{ access: Option&lt;NpmAccess&gt; }`: intentional refinement, `None` correctly documented/handled downstream in `publish_client.rs`/`publish.rs` as \"defer to npm's own ecosystem default.\"\n- `PackageIdParseError::PathTraversal` split into `PathTraversal` + `LeadingHyphen`: both `..` and leading-`-` rejection paths still enforced (verified for bare and both prefixed forms); no caller matches on the old specific variant.\n- `IdentityIndex::resolve_native_with_fallback` lost a `1 =&gt; Some(...)` arm (now always warns + returns `None` on any cross-ecosystem miss, even unambiguous single-candidate). Initially looked like a real finding (feeds `DepEdge` construction in `walk.rs:540`, so it affects cascade-graph edges), but it's a deliberate, tested tightening from commit `de83f6f5` (T13a) with an explicit end-to-end regression test (T13b) — not an accidental deletion.\n- `error.rs`: removed unused `ConfigError::ParseYaml` (dead code, no callers) and fixed a duplicate `E117` diagnostic code collision by renumbering one to `E113` — a bug fix, not a regression.\n\nNo candidate findings to report from this scope.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>101379</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>26</tool_uses><duration_ms>150789</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
