n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n    \"line\": 314,\n    \"summary\": \"plan_version re-derives the OpenContext from scratch (Cargo.toml exists check, WorkspaceCargoResolver::load, detect_npm_workspace_kind) instead of reusing the equivalent discovery logic already present in walk.rs, apply.rs, and lib.rs.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A 4th independent copy of ~15 lines of workspace-inheritance-detection logic; a future fix (e.g. supporting a new npm workspace kind) must be patched in four places, and missing this one silently reintroduces stale behavior only in the version-planning path.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n    \"line\": 351,\n    \"summary\": \"Platform-manifest and owner-manifest handles are opened via the raw callisto_manifests::open() call instead of the Workspace's manifest_cache::open_cached (defined in callisto-graph/src/lib.rs and already used by Workspace::base_versions, lib.rs:209).\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Bypasses the per-command-run manifest cache that lib.rs documents as existing precisely so a given manifest is opened at most once per command run; any manifest already opened elsewhere in the same run (e.g. by base_versions) is read from disk and re-parsed a second time here.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n    \"line\": 367,\n    \"summary\": \"Inside the per-platform-member loop, the owner package's canonical manifest is opened and parsed fresh for every platform sibling that owner has, rather than once per owner.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"For an owner with N platform-manifest siblings (the new test plan_version_merges_two_platform_siblings_optional_dep_updates_into_one_entry exercises this), the same owner Cargo.toml/package.json is read and re-parsed N times within a single plan_version call instead of once, hoisted out of the loop.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs\",\n    \"line\": 244,\n    \"summary\": \"read_npm_membership reads and JSON-parses root package.json twice per call: once in package_json_declares_name(root) (line ~244), then again in read_package_json_workspaces(root) (line ~283) whenever no pnpm-workspace.yaml governs.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"read_npm_membership runs once per IgnoreWalkLocator::projects() invocation, which is on the hot path for every graph/matrix command. The parsed serde_json::Value from the first read is discarded and re-derived rather than threaded through, doubling I/O and JSON-parse cost on every npm-ecosystem workspace scan for no behavioral gain.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs\",\n    \"line\": 132,\n    \"summary\": \"Workspace::load now stores `let identity = graph.identity().clone();` — a full clone of the IdentityIndex — purely so version.rs can pass `identity: &amp;ws.identity` into CascadeInput, duplicating data already reachable via `ws.graph.identity()` (the pattern used everywhere else, e.g. walk.rs).\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Every Workspace::load (i.e. every command invocation) now pays to clone the entire IdentityIndex (bare/native/prefixed/platform BTreeMaps) instead of passing through the existing reference, adding an unnecessary allocation on the startup path of every command.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\n**Notable non-findings**: the manifests fork confirmed the mutate/persist split and the three ecosystem `*_package_name` functions are deliberate, well-justified duplication (doc comments explain why) — not flagged. The graph-core fork confirmed matrix.rs and tags.rs already implement the efficiency improvements an audit would otherwise ask for. Runner-up candidates not included in the final 6 (available on request): a 4x-duplicated error-fallback block in `cargo.rs` (~line 373), a duplicated PEP-503 name-equivalence check in `python.rs` (~line 452), a redundant map lookup in `walk.rs` (~line 146), a per-iteration allocation in `napi_linux_abi_from_package_name` (`walk.rs:658`), and a leftover duplicate test module in `membership.rs` (~line 545).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>61591</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>16</tool_uses><duration_ms>238675</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
