n; `check_git_version` and its tests remain intact in `callisto-model`.\n- **walk.rs**: the large identity-promotion addition (disjoint-claiming-ecosystem-sets test before promoting vs. erroring `DuplicatePackage`) is internally consistent across all 5 documented \"STALE-KEY REWRITE\" locations and matches its extensive dedicated test suite.\n- **matrix.rs**: `read_napi_targets`/`read_maturin_targets`/etc. were split into parse-once + extract, same error/AC semantics preserved, plus a new duplicate-triple diagnostic.\n- **config/resolve.rs**: `resolve_package_config` gained a `Result` return (new `AmbiguousName` error for promoted siblings) — both production callers (`aggregate.rs:212`, `walk.rs:353`) propagate it via `?`, no swallowing. `PreMajorInferencePolicy` bool-pair → enum conversion has no lingering field access anywhere.\n- **callisto-vcs/shell.rs**: additive credential-redaction and `--` flag-injection hardening, well tested.\n- **callisto-model/path.rs**: `.replace('\\\\','/')` → `path_slash` is a genuine POSIX-filename-corruption fix; traversal/absolute-path containment logic untouched.\n- **deny.toml**: 3 new ignored RUSTSEC advisories, all `unmaintained` (not vulnerability) transitive-via-wasmtime crates (`im-rc`, `sized-chunks`, `bitmaps`), each with an inline justification comment — consistent with the commit message.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>197816</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>56</tool_uses><duration_ms>351793</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
