{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:23:10.010Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a948e31392bc7bc7a</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/a948e31392bc7bc7a.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Audit callisto-model and callisto-vcs diff for regressions\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Audit complete. Here are the confirmed candidate findings from `crates/callisto-graph/{locate,walk.rs,matrix.rs,config,identity.rs}`, `crates/callisto-manifests/`, `crates/callisto-vcs/src/shell.rs`, and `deny.toml`:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-model/src/exec.rs\",\n    \"line\": 153,\n    \"summary\": \"The git-version compatibility gate (`probe_git`, formerly `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/git.rs`) was deleted wholesale in this diff, along with its `pub use git::probe_git` re-export in `locate/mod.rs`. `check_git_version` itself survives in `callisto-model` but is now called from nowhere in production code — grep across `callisto-graph`, `callisto-vcs`, and `callisto-moon` shows zero call sites outside `exec.rs`'s own unit tests. `docs/01-spec.md` (§G.2.4, §P7, §9930) still documents this as running once per invocation before the first real `git` call, producing `CommandError::IncompatibleVersion`.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A user or CI runner on git &lt; 2.20 (the documented floor, `REQUIRED_GIT`) now gets no upfront, clear 'incompatible git version' error. Instead the tool proceeds straight into `GitAccess::discover`/`ShellGit` calls and fails later with whatever raw, less-diagnosable error the actual git subcommand happens to produce (or, for git flag/behavior differences that don't hard-fail, may silently misbehave). The unit tests for `check_git_version` still pass, giving false confidence the version gate is enforced when it is unreachable at runtime.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"deny.toml\",\n    \"line\": 55,\n    \"summary\": \"Three new RUSTSEC unmaintained-crate advisories (RUSTSEC-2026-0250 im-rc, -0251 sized-chunks, -0247 bitmaps, all transitive via `wasm-compose -&gt; wasmtime`) were added to the `ignore` list. Justification is only a one-line inline comment per entry; there is no corresponding upgrade, vendoring, or removal of the wasmtime-chain dependency, and no evidence in the diff of an attempt to drop the transitive dependency instead of silencing the advisory.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"If any of these transitive crates later gets a real (non-`unmaintained`) vulnerability advisory under a similarly-worded RUSTSEC ID, `cargo deny` will keep passing silently unless someone notices the ignore list needs re-auditing — the ignore list has no expiry/review mechanism, so this is a standing gap rather than a point-in-time judgment call.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\n**Note:** a separate background fork is still auditing `callisto-model`'s `lib.rs`, `path.rs`, `registry.rs`, `report.rs`, `tag.rs`, `ecosystem.rs`, and `callisto-vcs`'s `access.rs`/`lib.rs` — I directly spot-checked `shell.rs` (secret redaction + `--` arg-injection hardening, both net-positive, no regressions) and `report.rs`'s field renames (`pr_body`→`body`, `valid`→`ok`, `created_tags`→`tags` — all intentional spec-alignment changes guarded by a dedicated schema-drift test, not silent regressions) myself and found nothing beyond the two items above. I couldn't spawn a second parallel fork for the graph-core files (walk.rs/matrix.rs/config/resolve.rs/identity.rs) due to a subagent nesting limit, so I audited those directly — the large diffs there (dual-identity \"promotion\" logic, `PreMajorInferencePolicy` bool→enum, npm `access` field) are all deliberate, well-tested changes with no unguarded deleted invariants found. I'll let you know if the outstanding fork surfaces anything once it returns.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>152684</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>51</tool_uses><duration_ms>355799</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:23:15.291Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a948e31392bc7bc7a</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/a948e31392bc7bc7a.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Audit callisto-model and callisto-vcs diff for regressions\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Audit complete. Here are the confirmed candidate findings from `crates/callisto-graph/{locate,walk.rs,matrix.rs,config,identity.rs}`, `crates/callisto-manifests/`, `crates/callisto-vcs/src/shell.rs`, and `deny.toml`:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-model/src/exec.rs\",\n    \"line\": 153,\n    \"summary\": \"The git-version compatibility gate (`probe_git`, formerly `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/git.rs`) was deleted wholesale in this diff, along with its `pub use git::probe_git` re-export in `locate/mod.rs`. `check_git_version` itself survives in `callisto-model` but is now called from nowhere in production code — grep across `callisto-graph`, `callisto-vcs`, and `callisto-moon` shows zero call sites outside `exec.rs`'s own unit tests. `docs/01-spec.md` (§G.2.4, §P7, §9930) still documents this as running once per invocation before the first real `git` call, producing `CommandError::IncompatibleVersion`.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A user or CI runner on git &lt; 2.20 (the documented floor, `REQUIRED_GIT`) now gets no upfront, clear 'incompatible git version' error. Instead the tool proceeds straight into `GitAccess::discover`/`ShellGit` calls and fails later with whatever raw, less-diagnosable error the actual git subcommand happens to produce (or, for git flag/behavior differences that don't hard-fail, may silently misbehave). The unit tests for `check_git_version` still pass, giving false confidence the version gate is enforced when it is unreachable at runtime.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"deny.toml\",\n    \"line\": 55,\n    \"summary\": \"Three new RUSTSEC unmaintained-crate advisories (RUSTSEC-2026-0250 im-rc, -0251 sized-chunks, -0247 bitmaps, all transitive via `wasm-compose -&gt; wasmtime`) were added to the `ignore` list. Justification is only a one-line inline comment per entry; there is no corresponding upgrade, vendoring, or removal of the wasmtime-chain dependency, and no evidence in the diff of an attempt to drop the transitive dependency instead of silencing the advisory.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"If any of these transitive crates later gets a real (non-`unmaintained`) vulnerability advisory under a similarly-worded RUSTSEC ID, `cargo deny` will keep passing silently unless someone notices the ignore list needs re-auditing — the ignore list has no expiry/review mechanism, so this is a standing gap rather than a point-in-time judgment call.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\n**Note:** a separate background fork is still auditing `callisto-model`'s `lib.rs`, `path.rs`, `registry.rs`, `report.rs`, `tag.rs`, `ecosystem.rs`, and `callisto-vcs`'s `access.rs`/`lib.rs` — I directly spot-checked `shell.rs` (secret redaction + `--` arg-injection hardening, both net-positive, no regressions) and `report.rs`'s field renames (`pr_body`→`body`, `valid`→`ok`, `created_tags`→`tags` — all intentional spec-alignment changes guarded by a dedicated schema-drift test, not silent regressions) myself and found nothing beyond the two items above. I couldn't spawn a second parallel fork for the graph-core files (walk.rs/matrix.rs/config/resolve.rs/identity.rs) due to a subagent nesting limit, so I audited those directly — the large diffs there (dual-identity \"promotion\" logic, `PreMajorInferencePolicy` bool→enum, npm `access` field) are all deliberate, well-tested changes with no unguarded deleted invariants found. I'll let you know if the outstanding fork surfaces anything once it returns.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>152684</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>51</tool_uses><duration_ms>355799</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:24:08.407Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a6ef258d15287d3f4</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/a6ef258d15287d3f4.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Angle A2: line-by-line scan of graph identity/aggregate/commands\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Based on my review of the diff between `origin/main` and this branch across the specified `callisto-graph` files, here are my findings.\n\n## Summary\n\nI read every hunk in the diff (`identity.rs`, `infer.rs`, `tags.rs`, `apply.rs`, `cascade.rs`, `changed.rs`, `aggregate.rs`, `lib.rs`, `plan.rs`, `error.rs`, `config/groups.rs`, `config/raw.rs`, `commands/pr_body.rs`, `commands/publish.rs`, `commands/publish_client.rs`, `commands/snapshot.rs`, `commands/status.rs`, `commands/tag.rs`, `commands/validate.rs`, `commands/version.rs`) and the full enclosing functions for each touched hunk. Most of the diff is a large, well-tested \"share one `GitAccess`/`TagIndex` across a command\" refactor plus several already-landed hardening fixes (credential redaction, tag-SHA fabrication fix for the primary tag, `E117` diagnostic-code collision fix, npm `access` bool→enum fix, cascade peer-escalation source gating). Three real gaps stood out:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/identity.rs\",\n    \"line\": 446,\n    \"summary\": \"IdentityIndex::resolve_native_with_fallback dropped its `1 =&gt; Some(candidates[0])` match arm, so it now pushes an ambiguity diagnostic and returns None even when exactly one cross-ecosystem candidate exists — contradicting its own doc comment (\\\"Like resolve_native but pushes a Diagnostic when cross-ecosystem ambiguity is detected (two packages...)\\\") and its sibling resolve_native, which still returns Some for a single match (per the new resolve_native_unchanged_still_returns_cross_ecosystem_match test in the same file).\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"walk.rs's ManifestWalkResolver::build (crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs:538-543) is the sole caller: an npm package that depends by bare name on a uniquely-named Cargo crate in the same workspace (no name collision with any other ecosystem) previously resolved to a single cross-ecosystem candidate and got a real DepEdge in the dependency graph. After this change, resolve_native_with_fallback returns None for that same single-candidate case, so no edge is created — only a warning diagnostic is pushed. The dependency is silently dropped from the graph, so cascade.rs never sees it and a version bump in the Cargo crate will not cascade to the npm dependent, with only a warning (not an error) as the trace.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs\",\n    \"line\": 65,\n    \"summary\": \"In create_tags_with_options's dry-run/preview branch (permit is None), the floating-major-tag block computes major_already_existed via ws.tags()?.contains_tag(...) but then unconditionally reports sha: release.sha.clone() instead of resolving the tag's actual current SHA when it already exists — unlike the primary tag's handling 12 lines below in the same branch, which correctly calls git.resolve_commit(tag_str) when already_existed is true.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A repo where the floating major tag (e.g. `v2`) already exists pointing at an older release commit (e.g. v2.3.0's SHA) and a new patch release v2.3.1 is being previewed with --floating-major and no ApplyPermit (dry-run/what-would-happen report). The CreatedTag entry for `v2` in the report will claim already_existed: true but sha: &lt;v2.3.1's new sha&gt; — fabricating the SHA the floating tag currently points to, exactly the class of bug tag_sha_fabrication_test.rs was written to catch for the primary tag, but left unfixed for the floating-major tag in the preview path.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/validate.rs\",\n    \"line\": 103,\n    \"summary\": \"validate()'s per-changeset package-existence check uses the raw, permissive PackageId::matches(&amp;id) inside `.any(...)`, which returns true if the bare name matches a package in ANY ecosystem (matches's own semantics: `(None, _) | (_, None) =&gt; true`) — it never detects that two different packages (e.g. a Cargo crate and an npm package) both match the same bare name, unlike aggregate.rs's dedicated resolve_target_package/resolve_unique helper (aggregate.rs:291), which hard-errors on that exact ambiguity via `?`.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A changeset file names a bare package like `serde` in a workspace containing both a Cargo package `serde` and an npm package `serde`. `callisto validate` (e.g. run as a CI gate on the PR) reports no diagnostic at all for this changeset — `.any()` is satisfied by either match. Later, `callisto version`/`plan_version` consumes the same changeset through `aggregate()`, which calls `resolve_target_package` and hard-errors with `GraphError::AmbiguousName`. The release pipeline breaks at the version-planning step on a changeset that `validate` already approved as clean.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nFiles read in full during this review (for reference): `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/identity.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/tag.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/validate.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/napi.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs` (relevant sections), plus diffs of every file in the requested list.\n\nI did not write anything to `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto-findings/FINDINGS.md` per instructions (read-only investigation; that ledger is maintained by the orchestrating process, not by me in this pass) — the three findings above are new and not already logged there as `CONFIRMED`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>181354</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>51</tool_uses><duration_ms>497674</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
