{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:24:13.474Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a639f4e513986ece1</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/a639f4e513986ece1.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Angle A1: line-by-line scan of graph locate/walk/matrix\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Good, I have exact line numbers. Now I'll finalize the findings.\n\n## Findings\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs\",\n    \"line\": 68,\n    \"summary\": \"IgnoreWalkLocator::projects() decides directory-hood with Path::is_dir() (which follows symlinks) instead of the walker's own file_type, so a symlink under the workspace pointing at an external directory is treated as a real project directory and its Cargo.toml/package.json/pyproject.toml is read and later re-opened for writes through the same symlink.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A repo contains `vendor/link -&gt; /some/external/path` (a symlink to a directory outside the git working tree) whose target has a Cargo.toml with `[package]`. The `ignore` crate's WalkBuilder (follow_links defaults to false) still yields this symlink DirEntry to the callback rather than silently dropping it (confirmed in ignore-0.4.33 src/walk.rs: `if work.is_symlink() || !work.is_dir() { return self.visitor.visit(Ok(work.dent)) }`). `path.is_dir()` at line 68 then resolves the symlink and returns true, so the code proceeds to `path.join(\\\"Cargo.toml\\\")`, reads through the symlink, and registers a ProjectRoot with `path: \\\"vendor/link\\\"`. Any later apply/version-bump step reconstructs `root.join(\\\"vendor/link\\\").join(\\\"Cargo.toml\\\")` and writes through the same symlink, silently mutating a file entirely outside the intended workspace root/git repo.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs\",\n    \"line\": 120,\n    \"summary\": \"The pyproject.toml discovery branch has no workspace-membership filter at all, unlike the Cargo and Npm branches this same PR just added `cargo_membership.admits(...)`/`npm_membership.admits(...)` guards to — every reachable pyproject.toml with a resolvable name is unconditionally included as a package.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A repo has a root `pyproject.toml` with `[tool.uv.workspace] members = [\\\"packages/*\\\"]` excluding `examples/demo`, but `examples/demo/pyproject.toml` still exists (e.g. a sample project not meant to be a release-managed package). `projects()` returns an Ecosystem::Pypi entry for `examples/demo` anyway because no PypiMembership type/check exists, in contrast to the newly-enforced Cargo `[workspace] members/exclude` and npm `workspaces`/`pnpm-workspace.yaml` filters landed in this same PR.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs\",\n    \"line\": 158,\n    \"summary\": \"When two same-bare-name packages conflict on overlapping ecosystems, the DuplicatePackage error's offending_path is looked up via `.find(...).unwrap_or_default()`, so a lookup miss silently reports an empty PathBuf as one of the conflicting paths instead of surfacing an internal-invariant violation.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"If `promoted_siblings`'s recorded conflicting_id ever fails to match a key in `package_manifest_decls` (e.g. due to a future refactor that reorders when entries are inserted/removed relative to when this branch runs), `GraphError::DuplicatePackage` is still returned but with `paths: vec![PathBuf::new(), rel_path]` — a confusing, silently-wrong diagnostic (empty path) instead of a loud panic/assertion pointing at the real bug.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nFiles reviewed (all read in full, not just diff hunks): `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/git.rs` (deleted), `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/mod.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/root.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/matrix.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/resolve.rs`. Also cross-referenced `crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs` and `crates/callisto-model/src/ecosystem.rs` to confirm the `PreMajorInferencePolicy` enum migration and `PublishTarget::Npm.access` rename in `resolve.rs` are correctly consumed elsewhere (no bug found there), and inspected the vendored `ignore-0.4.33` crate source (`~/.cargo/registry/.../ignore-0.4.33/src/walk.rs`) to confirm the symlink-yielding behavior underlying finding #1.\n\nNote: none of these three findings are recorded as `CONFIRMED` in `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto-findings/FINDINGS.md`, so none were skipped as already-logged. Per this agent's instructions, no findings file was written to the callisto-findings repo — these are reported directly in this response for the orchestrating agent to log/triage.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>173256</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>38</tool_uses><duration_ms>512357</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:24:14.515Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a639f4e513986ece1</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/a639f4e513986ece1.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Angle A1: line-by-line scan of graph locate/walk/matrix\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Good, I have exact line numbers. Now I'll finalize the findings.\n\n## Findings\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs\",\n    \"line\": 68,\n    \"summary\": \"IgnoreWalkLocator::projects() decides directory-hood with Path::is_dir() (which follows symlinks) instead of the walker's own file_type, so a symlink under the workspace pointing at an external directory is treated as a real project directory and its Cargo.toml/package.json/pyproject.toml is read and later re-opened for writes through the same symlink.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A repo contains `vendor/link -&gt; /some/external/path` (a symlink to a directory outside the git working tree) whose target has a Cargo.toml with `[package]`. The `ignore` crate's WalkBuilder (follow_links defaults to false) still yields this symlink DirEntry to the callback rather than silently dropping it (confirmed in ignore-0.4.33 src/walk.rs: `if work.is_symlink() || !work.is_dir() { return self.visitor.visit(Ok(work.dent)) }`). `path.is_dir()` at line 68 then resolves the symlink and returns true, so the code proceeds to `path.join(\\\"Cargo.toml\\\")`, reads through the symlink, and registers a ProjectRoot with `path: \\\"vendor/link\\\"`. Any later apply/version-bump step reconstructs `root.join(\\\"vendor/link\\\").join(\\\"Cargo.toml\\\")` and writes through the same symlink, silently mutating a file entirely outside the intended workspace root/git repo.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs\",\n    \"line\": 120,\n    \"summary\": \"The pyproject.toml discovery branch has no workspace-membership filter at all, unlike the Cargo and Npm branches this same PR just added `cargo_membership.admits(...)`/`npm_membership.admits(...)` guards to — every reachable pyproject.toml with a resolvable name is unconditionally included as a package.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A repo has a root `pyproject.toml` with `[tool.uv.workspace] members = [\\\"packages/*\\\"]` excluding `examples/demo`, but `examples/demo/pyproject.toml` still exists (e.g. a sample project not meant to be a release-managed package). `projects()` returns an Ecosystem::Pypi entry for `examples/demo` anyway because no PypiMembership type/check exists, in contrast to the newly-enforced Cargo `[workspace] members/exclude` and npm `workspaces`/`pnpm-workspace.yaml` filters landed in this same PR.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs\",\n    \"line\": 158,\n    \"summary\": \"When two same-bare-name packages conflict on overlapping ecosystems, the DuplicatePackage error's offending_path is looked up via `.find(...).unwrap_or_default()`, so a lookup miss silently reports an empty PathBuf as one of the conflicting paths instead of surfacing an internal-invariant violation.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"If `promoted_siblings`'s recorded conflicting_id ever fails to match a key in `package_manifest_decls` (e.g. due to a future refactor that reorders when entries are inserted/removed relative to when this branch runs), `GraphError::DuplicatePackage` is still returned but with `paths: vec![PathBuf::new(), rel_path]` — a confusing, silently-wrong diagnostic (empty path) instead of a loud panic/assertion pointing at the real bug.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nFiles reviewed (all read in full, not just diff hunks): `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/git.rs` (deleted), `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/mod.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/root.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/matrix.rs`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/resolve.rs`. Also cross-referenced `crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs` and `crates/callisto-model/src/ecosystem.rs` to confirm the `PreMajorInferencePolicy` enum migration and `PublishTarget::Npm.access` rename in `resolve.rs` are correctly consumed elsewhere (no bug found there), and inspected the vendored `ignore-0.4.33` crate source (`~/.cargo/registry/.../ignore-0.4.33/src/walk.rs`) to confirm the symlink-yielding behavior underlying finding #1.\n\nNote: none of these three findings are recorded as `CONFIRMED` in `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto-findings/FINDINGS.md`, so none were skipped as already-logged. Per this agent's instructions, no findings file was written to the callisto-findings repo — these are reported directly in this response for the orchestrating agent to log/triage.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>173256</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>38</tool_uses><duration_ms>512357</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
