eeds to `path.join(\"Cargo.toml\")`/`package.json`/`pyproject.toml` and reads the manifest through the symlink, registering it as a `ProjectRoot` with a workspace-relative path computed via `strip_prefix` (line 161) that only strips the *symlink's own* location, not its target. No guard exists to reject this before the `is_dir()` check.\n\n### CANDIDATE 2 — pyproject.toml branch missing membership check\n\n**Verdict: CONFIRMED**\n\nThe full `projects()` body confirms this asymmetry directly. The Cargo branch (lines 72-97) computes `let rel = to_workspace_relative(...)` then gates inclusion with `if cargo_membership.admits(&amp;rel, is_root) { ... }` (line 84). The Npm branch (lines 99-118) does the same with `npm_membership.admits(&amp;rel, is_root)` (line 106). The pyproject.toml branch (lines 120-146) has no equivalent: it parses the TOML, extracts `name` from `[project]` or `[tool.poetry]`, computes `rel`, and unconditionally does `results.push(ProjectRoot { ... })` (lines 138-142) — no `admits`/membership call of any kind. `membership.rs` (`crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs`) only exports `CargoMembership` (line 34) and `NpmMembership` (line 222); grep for `Membership` in that file shows no `PythonMembership`/`PyMembership` type exists at all. So every reachable `pyproject.toml` with a resolvable name is included regardless of any Python workspace configuration.\n\n### CANDIDATE 3 — `ShellGit::list_tags` missing success-check\n\n**Verdict: CONFIRMED**\n\nI read the entire `impl GitDataSource for ShellGit&lt;'_&gt;` block (`crates/callisto-vcs/src/shell.rs:75-227`). `list_tags` (lines 97-107) runs `self.runner.run(\"git\", &amp;[\"tag\", \"--list\"], &amp;self.root)?` and immediately does `let all = output.stdout_lines().map(|s| s.to_string());`, then filters/maps into `Vec&lt;TagName&gt;` and returns `Ok(...)` — there is no `if !output.success() { ... }` check anywhere in this function. Every sibling method in the same impl block does check: `head_sha` (lines 78-84), `commits_since` (lines 165-171), `create_tag` (lines 197-203), and `create_floating_major` (lines 218-224) all guard with `if !output.success() { return Err(VcsError::Git(...redact_git_stderr(&amp;output.stderr)...)) }`. (`resolve_commit` intentionally treats failure as `Ok(None)`, which is a documented, different design choice, not a silent-swallow bug.) So a failing `git tag --list` (e.g., not a git repo, corrupted repo) with empty/non-empty stderr and empty stdout falls through `stdout_lines()` on empty stdout and returns `Ok(vec![])` — indistinguishable from \"repository has zero tags\" — with no error surfaced and no stderr redaction/reporting path exercised at all.\n\n**Files read (absolute paths):**\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-vcs/src/shell.rs`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto-findings/FINDINGS.md` (checked — none of these three are already logged as CONFIRMED)</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>53255</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>9</tool_uses><duration_ms>52544</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
