walk.rs` (lines 1-460, plus grep across the whole file for `STALE-KEY`, `index.`, `promoted_siblings.`, and promotion-related test names), `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/identity.rs` (`IdentityIndex` struct definition, lines 339-352).\n\nNote: the `index.platform` staleness-on-promotion gap I found while tracing this is a plausible latent bug in its own right (untested, matches the same hazard class), but it is not yet in `FINDINGS.md` — flagging it here for the parent agent's awareness rather than logging it myself, since this task was scoped as read-only verification of the specific candidate.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>48080</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>15</tool_uses><duration_ms>135501</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:30:54.498Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>abfe17342ab38ec24</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_014N6qt2RAay1kkcHFdqk7Wm</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/c0ad64b2-6440-4937-8328-8d9fd9db278c/tasks/abfe17342ab38ec24.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Verify batch 3: runner buffer/cargo persist/duplicate-path bugs\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Verification Results\n\nI read `.agents/subagents/bug-hunter.md`, `.agents/skills/bug-hunter/SKILL.md`, and the external findings ledger at `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto-findings/FINDINGS.md` first. None of the three candidates below appear in that ledger, so none are pre-logged duplicates. This was read-only investigation; no files were modified, and no findings were written into the callisto repo itself.\n\n### Candidate 1 — `pending_line` unbounded growth in stderr reader thread\n**Verdict: CONFIRMED**\n\nFile: `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-cli/src/runner.rs`, `run_with_timeout_impl`'s stderr thread (lines 165-214).\n\n- `captured: Vec&lt;u8&gt;` (line 167) is capped against `MAX_CAPTURED_OUTPUT_BYTES` (line 189-196) exactly as the doc comment at lines 8-14 promises.\n- `pending_line: Vec&lt;u8&gt;` (line 169) is used purely to buffer bytes for live `eprintln!` echo per line (lines 176-188) and is only ever `.clear()`'d when a `b'\\n'` is seen (line 184). There is no size check or truncation anywhere on `pending_line` — every non-newline byte is unconditionally `.push()`'d (line 186), even after `captured` has already hit its cap and `truncated` is `true`.\n- Concretely: a subprocess that writes many megabytes to stderr with zero `\\n` bytes will have `captured` correctly bounded at 10 MiB, but `pending_line` will grow to the full size of the flood, unbounded — defeating the memory-bounding purpose the surrounding code (and its own doc comment at lines 156-164) explicitly claims to guarantee. The existing test `run_with_timeout_caps_accumulated_stderr_with_no_newlines_and_still_drains_the_pipe` (lines 489-517) only asserts on the returned `CommandOutput.stderr` field (i.e. `captured`), so it does not catch this — it doesn't observe `pending_line`'s in-thread memory footprint at all.\n\n### Candidate 2 — Redundant/wasted `atomic_write` when `update_dependency_spec` delegates to `WorkspaceCargoResolver`\n**Verdict: CONFIRMED**\n\nFiles: `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs`.\n\n- `CargoToml::update_dependency_spec` (cargo.rs:300-328): when the dependency is workspace-inherited and this manifest isn't the root itself, it does `let mut ws_res = WorkspaceCargoResolver::load(&amp;root_cargo)?; return ws_res.write_dependency(name, new, permit);` (lines 326-327). `WorkspaceCargoResolver::write_dependency` (lines 671-743) mutates its own `self.document` and calls its own `self.persist(permit)` at line 742, which does `atomic_write(&amp;self.absolute_path, ...)` (line 747) — this is the **root** `Cargo.toml`, written immediately. Nothing in this branch touches the calling `CargoToml`'s own `self.document`.\n- Callers unconditionally persist afterward: `apply.rs:227-234` does `handle.update_dependency_spec(...)?; handle.persist(permit)?;` with no branch distinguishing the delegation case; the earlier rewrites-loop (`apply.rs:164-176`) sets `mutated = true` unconditionally after calling `update_dependency_spec` and later does `if mutated { handle.persist(permit)?; }` — same effect.\n- `Manifest::persist` for `CargoToml` (cargo.rs:118-131) always calls `crate::atomic::atomic_write(&amp;self.absolute, &amp;text, permit)`, and `atomic_write` itself (`callisto-model/src/atomic.rs:42-69`) has no content-equality short-circuit — it unconditionally creates a temp file, writes, flushes, `sync_all`s, renames, and fsyncs the parent/grandparent directories every time. So every delegation call causes one genuine, unnecessary full atomic-write-plus-fsync cycle of the member's byte-identical `Cargo.toml`.\n\n### Candidate 3 — `unwrap_or_default()` on `offending_path` lookup in `DuplicatePackage` error path\n**Verdict: REFUTED** (as a reachable bug — the code pattern exists exactly as described, but I traced a proof that the lookup miss cannot actually occur under current invariants)\n\nFile: `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs:144-163`.\n\n- The pattern exists verbatim: `let offending_path = package_manifest_decls.iter().find(|(id, _)| *id == conflicting_id).map(|(_, (p, _))| p.clone()).unwrap_or_default();` (lines 154-158), feeding directly into `GraphError::DuplicatePackage { paths: vec![offending_path, rel_path], .. }`.\n- However, tracing the invariants: `conflicting_id` values only ever originate from `promoted_siblings` entries, and every entry ever pushed into `promoted_siblings` (both the initial-pair promotion at lines 305-308, and the branch-ii join at lines 168-171) is paired, in the very same code path, with an insert of the identical `PackageId` key into `package_manifest_decls` (lines 263-266 and line 231 respectively). The only removal from `package_manifest_decls` (line 267, `.remove(&amp;primary_id)`) targets the pre-promotion bare id, never a promoted `Prefixed` id. Further, `compute_claiming_ecosystems_and_native_keys` (lines 29-43) guarantees a path's own primary ecosystem is always a member of its own claiming set (since `list[0].1 == primary_id` trivially satisfies the `id.name() == primary_id.name()` filter), so two paths whose claiming sets are disjoint (the precondition for reaching branch-ii's promotion instead of erroring) necessarily have different primary ecosystems, and therefore different `PackageId::Prefixed{ecosystem, ..}` values — so a later path's freshly-computed `promoted_id` can never silently collide with (overwrite) an earlier sibling's key in `package_manifest_decls`. Given this, every `conflicting_id` drawn from `promoted_siblings` is provably still present in `package_manifest_decls` at the moment of the `.find()` call, so `unwrap_or_default()` is unreachable dead-code fallback rather than a live silent-corruption path.\n- Note: this is a fragile style inconsistency worth flagging separately (the surrounding code explicitly documents, in its own \"STALE-KEY REWRITE\" comment at lines 248-254, that it deliberately avoided this exact anti-pattern elsewhere in the same function by using captured values instead of a post-hoc `.get()`/`.find()` lookup — yet left this instance as a `.find()`+`unwrap_or_default()`). But as a \"silently corrupts the reported error\" claim, it is refuted by the disjointness-invariant trace above.\n\n**Relevant files read:**\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-cli/src/runner.rs`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-model/src/atomic.rs`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs`</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>68269</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>18</tool_uses><duration_ms>145865</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
