c::atomic_write(&amp;self.absolute, &amp;text, permit)`, and `atomic_write` itself (`callisto-model/src/atomic.rs:42-69`) has no content-equality short-circuit — it unconditionally creates a temp file, writes, flushes, `sync_all`s, renames, and fsyncs the parent/grandparent directories every time. So every delegation call causes one genuine, unnecessary full atomic-write-plus-fsync cycle of the member's byte-identical `Cargo.toml`.\n\n### Candidate 3 — `unwrap_or_default()` on `offending_path` lookup in `DuplicatePackage` error path\n**Verdict: REFUTED** (as a reachable bug — the code pattern exists exactly as described, but I traced a proof that the lookup miss cannot actually occur under current invariants)\n\nFile: `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs:144-163`.\n\n- The pattern exists verbatim: `let offending_path = package_manifest_decls.iter().find(|(id, _)| *id == conflicting_id).map(|(_, (p, _))| p.clone()).unwrap_or_default();` (lines 154-158), feeding directly into `GraphError::DuplicatePackage { paths: vec![offending_path, rel_path], .. }`.\n- However, tracing the invariants: `conflicting_id` values only ever originate from `promoted_siblings` entries, and every entry ever pushed into `promoted_siblings` (both the initial-pair promotion at lines 305-308, and the branch-ii join at lines 168-171) is paired, in the very same code path, with an insert of the identical `PackageId` key into `package_manifest_decls` (lines 263-266 and line 231 respectively). The only removal from `package_manifest_decls` (line 267, `.remove(&amp;primary_id)`) targets the pre-promotion bare id, never a promoted `Prefixed` id. Further, `compute_claiming_ecosystems_and_native_keys` (lines 29-43) guarantees a path's own primary ecosystem is always a member of its own claiming set (since `list[0].1 == primary_id` trivially satisfies the `id.name() == primary_id.name()` filter), so two paths whose claiming sets are disjoint (the precondition for reaching bra