{"parentUuid":"b3d5d398-f969-4bf8-9dbd-68b54a69779c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeFN5yUGRRzwmi9QUXCtz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2493,"cache_read_input_tokens":388815,"output_tokens":1433,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":881},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2493,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1433,"cache_read_input_tokens":388815,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2493,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2493},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeFN5v4NsYn6APHyyGvyV","type":"assistant","uuid":"5083b44e-a766-47f9-bb07-05d8d5d00bba","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:45:58.462Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"5083b44e-a766-47f9-bb07-05d8d5d00bba","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeFN5yUGRRzwmi9QUXCtz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You're right to push on this — it's not simply \"the code should reject symlinks.\" I checked `to_workspace_relative` (line 154): it only does a lexical `starts_with` check, so a path like `<root>/vendor/link` looks completely fine even when it's a symlink to `/external/path` — the walker itself never reports anything outside the workspace.\n\nThe actual situation:\n\n- `WalkBuilder` here has no `.follow_links(...)` call, so it uses the `ignore` crate's default: **don't traverse into symlinked directories**. That's a real, if implicit, decision already baked into this code.\n- `path.is_dir()` at line 68 uses `stat()` semantics, which follows the symlink and returns `true` anyway — silently overriding that decision. So today's behavior (a manifest inside a symlinked dir gets picked up) is an *accident* of `is_dir()`'s behavior, not a deliberate, tested choice.\n- The real risk isn't discovery — it's that once that manifest is registered as a package root at path `vendor/link`, later version bumps/changelog writes go through `fs::write`/`atomic_write`, which also follow the symlink. So a release tool could end up mutating files at `/external/path`, outside the repo, without anyone deciding that should happen.\n\nSo the actual choice is: do you want callisto to explicitly support symlinked workspace members (vendor-link style monorepos), or explicitly reject them? Either is defensible — right now it's neither, it's just unintentional. If you want to support it, the fix is enabling `.follow_links(true)` deliberately (plus a test); if not, the fix is skipping symlinks at line 68. Which way do you want it?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2493,"cache_read_input_tokens":388815,"output_tokens":1433,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":881},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2493,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1433,"cache_read_input_tokens":388815,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2493,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2493},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeFN5v4NsYn6APHyyGvyV","type":"assistant","uuid":"90bfeac9-57e3-4919-baf1-21d31b2ea654","timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:46:04.650Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
