{"parentUuid":"eb9f0661-853d-4f2f-82a9-4d5a1bad892f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeFzwNJkijiwfNj7T2M71","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016tMydAGuw4gwWXGEX6yEKa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/validate.rs && git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix(graph): detect ambiguous bare package names in validate\n\nvalidate() used the permissive PackageId::matches (a bare name matches\nany ecosystem) via .any() for its unknown-package check, so a\nchangeset entry naming a bare package that exists in two or more\necosystems silently passed. aggregate()/plan_version hard-error on the\nidentical input via resolve_target_package's collect-and-error\npattern. validate now uses the same PackageId::resolve_unique method\nand reports a new DiagnosticCode::AmbiguousPackageName, so the\npre-flight check users run before `version` actually catches this.\nEOF\n)\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_read_input_tokens":455145,"output_tokens":331,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":331,"cache_read_input_tokens":455145,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeFzwKwd9zJ2jENQAt8br","type":"assistant","uuid":"749bec24-73fb-431c-9380-1c099c96c436","timestamp":"2026-08-21T13:49:07.291Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli"