{"parentUuid":"1852319c-bb27-438c-8bf3-512bba480d20","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeG11bgXeqKmpVhdnQgsG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5600,"cache_read_input_tokens":460741,"output_tokens":1099,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":670},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5600,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1099,"cache_read_input_tokens":460741,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5600,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5600},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeG11ZRMVMWT6gkCBQgkr","type":"assistant","uuid":"168a2e4e-9737-45c1-a47f-d484ccadd6f1","timestamp":"2026-08-21T13:50:09.654Z","effort":"high","session_id":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"release-pipeline-and-matrix-hardening","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"168a2e4e-9737-45c1-a47f-d484ccadd6f1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeG11bgXeqKmpVhdnQgsG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Investigated finding #3 and it doesn't hold up — this one's a false positive, not a real bug.\n\n`create_floating_major` shells out to `git tag -f` (force flag) — it **always** re-points the floating major tag to `release.sha`, regardless of whether it existed before. That's the whole point of a \"floating\" tag (unlike a per-release tag, which is immutable once created). Apply-mode's own code (line 135) already reports `sha: release.sha.clone()` unconditionally too — so both branches agree, correctly, that the floating tag will point at `release.sha` after this run either way. \"Fabricating\" a sha here would only be a bug if the tag were supposed to stay immutable, which floating major tags explicitly aren't.\n\nSkipping this one — applying the review's suggested fix would actually make dry-run *disagree* with what apply-mode really does. Moving to finding #4: `list_tags` swallowing git failures."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5600,"cache_read_input_tokens":460741,"output_tokens":1099,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":670},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5600,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1099,"cache_read_input_tokens":460741,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5600,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5600},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeG11ZRMVMWT6gkCBQgkr","type":"assistant","uuid":"1eabc087-3931-498a-ae70-590631ae3390","timestamp":"2026-08-21T13:50:12.513Z","effort":"high","session