{"parentUuid":"b68d8d43-0861-43c6-b9b4-678e861dd061","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"70114f87-e957-4ebe-a1f1-479e2d3bda05","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JWciycbjNaUXBpy5WsYWEv","type":"tool_result","content":"83:    fn list_tags(&self, glob_pattern: Option<&str>) -> Result<Vec<TagName>, VcsError>;\n84-}\n85-\n86-/// Unified git-data access surface covering every operation callisto's\n87-/// release-graph logic needs, independent of *how* the data is sourced.\n88-///\n89-/// Two backends implement this trait:\n90-///\n91-/// - [`GitRepository`] -- native, backed by `gix`. Fast and side-effect-free\n92-///   for reads, but entirely unavailable on `wasm32` (gix is excluded from\n93-///   that target's dependency set, so [`GitRepository::discover`] always\n94-///   returns `Err` there).\n95-/// - [`ShellGit`] -- shells out to the real `git` binary via a\n96-///   [`callisto_model::CommandRunner`], so it works everywhere a `git`\n97-///   binary is reachable, including through the `wasm32`/Extism host\n98-///   bridge.\n99-///\n100-/// Callers should not implement or select between these directly; use\n101-/// [`GitAccess::discover`], which tries native `gix` first and transparently\n102-/// falls back to the `CommandRunner` shell-out, applying the correct\n103-/// per-operation fallback policy (see [`GitAccess`]'s docs).\n--\n112:    fn list_tags(&self, glob: Option<&str>) -> Result<Vec<TagName>, VcsError>;\n113-\n114-    /// Resolves `refname` (tag, branch, or partial/full SHA) to the commit\n115-    /// it points at. An unresolvable ref is *not* an error -- it resolves\n116-    /// to `Ok(None)`, which callers typically treat as \"no bound\" / \"infer\n117-    /// over full history\".\n118-    fn resolve_commit(&self, refname: &str) -> Result<Option<CommitSha>, VcsError>;\n119-","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"bad1b4f4-cf27-44e5-b877-bdfdecc9159d","timestamp":"2026-08-21T13:50:18.893Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"83:    fn list_t